ction privately to your teacher."}},{"k":"mailbox_submit_info","v":{"s":"Drafts stay on this device. Submit sends your reflection to your teacher’s Class Mailbox."}},{"k":"download_submit_info","v":{"s":"Submit downloads your reflection for you to share with your teacher."}},{"k":"progress_info","v":{"s":" Your live progress is updated too."}},{"k":"local_info","v":{"s":"Local practice — your reflection stays on this device."}},{"k":"kwl_guidance","v":{"s":"Submit your current thinking; you can return to Learned and submit a revision later. Blank sections are allowed."}},{"k":"reasoning_guidance","v":{"s":"Before submitting, check that you explained your choices and named supporting evidence. This is not automatically scored."}},{"k":"storage_failed","v":{"s":"This browser could not save your draft. Keep this page open and copy your writing before leaving."}},{"k":"draft_changes","v":{"s":"You have changes that have not been submitted."}},{"k":"submitting","v":{"s":"Submitting…"}},{"k":"save_reflection","v":{"s":"Save reflection"}},{"k":"submit_revision","v":{"s":"Submit revision"}},{"k":"submit_reflection","v":{"s":"Submit reflection"}},{"k":"version_saved","v":{"s":"This version is saved. You can keep revising."}},{"k":"import_info","v":{"s":"Earlier KWL notes for this topic are saved on this device. Import them if they are yours."}},{"k":"import_notes","v":{"s":"Import my earlier KWL notes"}},{"k":"preview_saved","v":{"s":"Preview saved on this device. It was not submitted as student work."}},{"k":"submit_failed","v":{"s":"Your reflection could not be submitted. Your draft is still here; try again."}},{"k":"submitted_ungraded","v":{"s":"Reflection submitted. Your words have not been automatically graded."}},{"k":"submission_failed","v":{"s":"Submission failed. Your draft is still here."}},{"k":"local_no_connection","v":{"s":"Saved on this device. No live submission connection is available."}},{"k":"practice_reflection","v":{"s":"Practice reflection"}},{"k":"start_reflection","v":{"s":"Start reflection for students"}},{"k":"starting_reflection","v":{"s":"Starting reflection…"}},{"k":"stop_reflection","v":{"s":"Stop reflection for students"}},{"k":"reflection_live","v":{"s":"Reflection is live for students."}},{"k":"reflection_controls","v":{"s":"Reflection activity controls"}},{"k":"feedback_sent","v":{"s":"Feedback sent to this learner."}},{"k":"feedback_failed","v":{"s":"Feedback could not be saved. Your draft is still here."}},{"k":"teacher_feedback","v":{"s":"Teacher feedback"}},{"k":"feedback_scope","v":{"s":"Feedback applies to this revision and is visible only to this learner and the teacher."}},{"k":"feedback_changed","v":{"s":"Saved feedback has changed. Your draft has been kept."}},{"k":"load_feedback","v":{"s":"Load saved feedback"}},{"k":"sending","v":{"s":"Sending…"}},{"k":"send_feedback","v":{"s":"Send feedback"}},{"k":"review_title","v":{"s":"Review organizer reflections"}},{"k":"review_intro","v":{"s":"Read learner thinking beside the diagram, compare revisions, and send feedback. Reflections are not automatically scored."}},{"k":"export_reminder","v":{"s":"Export before ending the class. This inbox is kept on the teacher’s device until the session expires, is deleted, or the desktop runtime closes."}},{"k":"refresh","v":{"s":"Refresh"}},{"k":"export","v":{"s":"Export reflections"}},{"k":"loading","v":{"s":"Loading reflections…"}},{"k":"empty","v":{"s":"No reflections submitted yet."}},{"k":"learner_activity","v":{"s":"Learner and activity"}},{"k":"revision","v":{"s":"Revision"}},{"k":"diagram_reference","v":{"s":"Diagram when activity started"}},{"k":"learner_writing","v":{"s":"Learner writing"}},{"k":"changed","v":{"s":"Changed since the previous revision"}},{"k":"blank","v":{"s":"Not yet answered"}},{"k":"previous","v":{"s":"Previous response"}},{"k":"your_feedback","v":{"s":"Feedback on your reflections"}},{"k":"refresh_feedback","v":{"s":"Refresh feedback"}},{"k":"no_feedback","v":{"s":"No teacher feedback yet. You can keep revising your draft."}},{"k":"kwl_chart_know_label","v":{"s":"What I know"}},{"k":"kwl_chart_know_prompt","v":{"s":"Describe your own prior knowledge. It is okay to be unsure."}},{"k":"kwl_chart_want_label","v":{"s":"What I want to know"}},{"k":"kwl_chart_want_prompt","v":{"s":"Ask a question you would like to investigate."}},{"k":"kwl_chart_learned_label","v":{"s":"What I learned or revised"}},{"k":"kwl_chart_learned_prompt","v":{"s":"Return after learning. What changed, and what evidence helped?"}},{"k":"claim_evidence_reasoning_claim_label","v":{"s":"My claim"}},{"k":"claim_evidence_reasoning_claim_prompt","v":{"s":"Answer the question in your own words."}},{"k":"claim_evidence_reasoning_evidence_label","v":{"s":"My evidence"}},{"k":"claim_evidence_reasoning_evidence_prompt","v":{"s":"Give specific observations, data, or a quotation and its source location."}},{"k":"claim_evidence_reasoning_reasoning_label","v":{"s":"My reasoning"}},{"k":"claim_evidence_reasoning_reasoning_prompt","v":{"s":"Explain why your evidence supports the claim. Consider another explanation."}},{"k":"cause_and_effect_cause_label","v":{"s":"Cause and linked effect"}},{"k":"cause_and_effect_cause_prompt","v":{"s":"Pair a cause with its effect from the diagram, or propose a supported alternative."}},{"k":"cause_and_effect_mechanism_label","v":{"s":"How they are connected"}},{"k":"cause_and_effect_mechanism_prompt","v":{"s":"Explain what happens between the cause and the effect."}},{"k":"cause_and_effect_evidence_label","v":{"s":"Evidence and limits"}},{"k":"cause_and_effect_evidence_prompt","v":{"s":"Name your source or observation. Could something else explain the effect?"}},{"k":"frayer_model_example_label","v":{"s":"My own example"}},{"k":"frayer_model_example_prompt","v":{"s":"Give a new example of the term."}},{"k":"frayer_model_nonexample_label","v":{"s":"My own non-example"}},{"k":"frayer_model_nonexample_prompt","v":{"s":"Give something that does not fit the term."}},{"k":"frayer_model_reasoning_label","v":{"s":"Why they fit or do not fit"}},{"k":"frayer_model_reasoning_prompt","v":{"s":"Use the defining characteristics to explain both choices."}},{"k":"see_think_wonder_see_label","v":{"s":"I observe"}},{"k":"see_think_wonder_see_prompt","v":{"s":"Record what you can directly observe."}},{"k":"see_think_wonder_think_label","v":{"s":"I infer"}},{"k":"see_think_wonder_think_prompt","v":{"s":"Explain your interpretation and the observations that support it."}},{"k":"see_think_wonder_wonder_label","v":{"s":"I wonder"}},{"k":"see_think_wonder_wonder_prompt","v":{"s":"Ask a question that could help you learn more."}}],"id":8}},{"k":"live_connection","v":{"o":[{"k":"connecting","v":{"s":"Connecting to the class…"}},{"k":"retrying","v":{"s":"Class updates paused. Reconnecting automatically…"}},{"k":"failed","v":{"s":"Class updates are disconnected. Check your connection and try reconnecting."}},{"k":"access","v":{"s":"Class access was denied. Ask your teacher to check access, then reconnect."}},{"k":"sign_in","v":{"s":"Sign in again to restore class access, then reconnect."}},{"k":"reconnect","v":{"s":"Reconnect"}}],"id":9}},{"k":"tour","v":{"o":[{"k":"exit","v":{"s":"Exit tour"}},{"k":"guided_workflow_title","v":{"s":"Build your first lesson with Guided Mode"}},{"k":"guided_workflow_text","v":{"s":"Build a lesson step by step from Start & setup → Guided Mode. Choose Adapt a reading for a focused path, another preset, or Plan with AI and review the proposed steps. Add source text, review each result, write or draft student directions, then open the current lesson in Document Builder. Preview the learner experience and complete the readiness checks before teaching. Resume later saves your place on this device."}},{"k":"input_panel_title","v":{"s":"Input Panel"}},{"k":"tool_finder_title","v":{"s":"Find the tool you need"}},{"k":"tool_finder_text","v":{"s":"This panel narrows the list of tools below. Pick a purpose, such as Make accessible or Assess, or type what you are looking for. It does not create anything by itself: it just makes the list shorter so the tool you want is easier to find. While this tour is running every tool is shown, so you can see the whole set."}},{"k":"directions_title","v":{"s":"Prepare student directions"}},{"k":"directions_text","v":{"s":"Write student directions yourself, or use Draft for me to start from your lesson plan and resource pack. Review and edit the steps, learning goal, due date, and success criteria for your class, then save. Read the directions as a learner before assigning them."}},{"k":"upload_accessibility_title","v":{"s":"Check and improve document accessibility"}},{"k":"upload_accessibility_text","v":{"s":"Upload a PDF, Word, or PowerPoint file to check for accessibility barriers. Make Accessible runs the available audit and repair steps; review the results, unresolved issues, and exported document before sharing. Available output formats depend on the source and processing options. Batch tools are also available in the Educator Hub."}},{"k":"udl_guide_title","v":{"s":"Build a lesson by talking"}},{"k":"udl_guide_text","v":{"s":"Build a whole lesson by talking to AlloBot instead of configuring tools one at a time. Describe what you are teaching and the guide proposes a plan you can review, edit, and run.\n### How It Works\n• **Describe the lesson**: Say the topic, grade, and any standards — answer with the suggestion pills or type your own.\n• **Review the plan**: AlloBot proposes a numbered Lesson Blueprint: which resources, in what order, with an instruction for each.\n• **Change anything first**: Reorder steps by drag or keyboard, swap a tool, rewrite an instruction, or remove a step before a single resource is generated.\n• **Ask questions**: \"Why a Venn diagram here?\" gets an answer — asking never rewrites your plan.\n• **Run it**: Each row reports its own status as it lands, so you can watch the pack build.\n### After The Run\n• **Rebuild one step**: Regenerate a single resource without re-running the whole pack.\n• **Preview in place**: Check what landed beside its plan row, without leaving the panel.\n• **Save as a template**: Keep the shape of a lesson that worked and start from it next time.\n• **Previous plans**: A finished plan is filed away with its history, so replacing it does not lose it.\n### Pro Tip\nClick the \"?\" on any plan row to see what that resource actually does before you generate it — useful when the guide suggests a tool you have not used.\n### Important\nMost steps need source material. Add or generate a source first, or the plan will run and produce nothing.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Action & Expression**: Supports planning and strategy development (Guideline 6.2) by making the whole instructional sequence visible and editable before committing to it."}},{"k":"universal_settings_title","v":{"s":"Universal Settings"}},{"k":"universal_settings_text","v":{"s":"One place to set the grade level and language that every generator inherits. Change it here instead of per tool.\n### What It Controls\n• **Grade Level**: The reading and complexity target applied to newly generated resources.\n• **Language**: The target language for generated content and translations.\n• **Shared Defaults**: Settings apply across tools, so a Quiz and a Glossary made afterwards agree with each other.\n### Why It Matters\n• **Consistency**: A pack whose parts target different grades reads as inconsistent to students.\n• **Fewer clicks**: Set it once at the start of a lesson rather than adjusting each panel.\n### Pro Tip\nSet this BEFORE generating. It applies to new work — resources you already made keep the settings they were built with, so check the header summary if a pack looks mismatched.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Representation**: Offers ways of customizing the display of information (Guideline 1) at the workspace level, so every resource starts at the learner's level."}},{"k":"input_panel_text","v":{"s":"Start with the passage or topic you want to teach. Most resource tools use this source material.\n### Add your source\n• Paste or type text, upload a supported file, import a URL, or use the source-generation tools.\n• Check imported or generated text for completeness and accuracy before continuing. Some websites restrict extraction.\n### Set the context\n• Open Universal Settings to review grade, language, and instructional preferences.\n• Choose a focused Guided Mode path if you want one step at a time. Review each result against the source and your learning goal."}},{"k":"analysis_title","v":{"s":"Start Analysis"}},{"k":"analysis_text","v":{"s":"Review the AI's deep understanding of your content. This analysis ensures accuracy before generating student materials by breaking down the text into its atomic pedagogical components.\n### Panel Options\n• **Check Accuracy**: Enable web grounding to verify factual claims and identify potential inaccuracies in your source text.\n### Analysis Components\n• **Executive Summary**: A concise overview of the input text's main ideas and purpose.\n• **Key Themes**: Identifies core concepts and 'Big Ideas' for instruction.\n• **Vocabulary Extraction**: Categorizes terms into Tier 2 (Academic) and Tier 3 (Domain-Specific) vocabulary.\n### Pro Tip\nEnable 'Check Accuracy' before running the analysis to catch potential misinformation early. The AI will cross-reference claims with current web sources.\n### Important\nWhen you run the analysis, the AI-processed version becomes the 'Analyzed Source'. This Analyzed Source replaces the original input as the source of truth for all other generated resources.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Engagement**: Minimizes threats and distractions (Guideline 7.3) by ensuring content is thematically clear and age-appropriate before instruction begins."}},{"k":"glossary_title","v":{"s":"Smart Glossary"}},{"k":"glossary_text","v":{"s":"Generate a comprehensive Visual Glossary with strong vocabulary support, multi-language capabilities, and interactive games.\n### Panel Options\n• **Tier 2/Tier 3 Counts**: Specify academic vs domain-specific term counts.\n• **Definition Level**: Kindergarten to College complexity.\n• **Bilingual Support**: Add up to 4 target languages for multilingual glossaries.\n• **Custom Instructions**: Guide term selection or definitions.\n### Generated Resources\n• **Visual Terms**: AI-generated images for each word with TTS pronunciation.\n• **Multi-Language Definitions**: View definitions in multiple languages side-by-side.\n• **Flashcards**: Standard and Bilingual sets with front/back audio.\n• **Audio Support**: Downloadable audio files for offline study.\n### Vocabulary Games\n• **Word Search**: Printable puzzles with answer keys.\n• **Bingo**: Auto-caller mode with speed control and printable cards.\n• **Memory Match**: Anti-cheat mode hides definitions during gameplay.\n• **Crossword**: AI-generated clues with keyboard navigation.\n• **Word Scramble**: Unscramble vocabulary terms for spelling practice.\n• **Syntax Scramble**: Reconstruct sentences using glossary terms.\n### Export Options\n• **PDF Export**: High-quality printable glossary sheets.\n• **Flashcard Slides**: PowerPoint export for classroom projection.\n• **Audio Downloads**: Individual or batch audio file downloads.\n### Pro Tip\nLink to the **Word Sounds Studio** to practice phonemic awareness and phonics with your glossary terms•perfect for early readers!\n### UDL Connection\n• **Representation**: Clarifies vocabulary and symbols (Guideline 2) via visual, auditory, and interactive formats."}},{"k":"simplified_title","v":{"s":"Adapted Text"}},{"k":"simplified_text","v":{"s":"Differentiate your text for diverse learners. This tool rewrites content to specific proficiency levels and provides a rich Immersive Reader with literacy supports.\n### Panel Options\n• **Grade Goal**: Scale complexity from Kindergarten to College level.\n• **Mode Selection**: Standard Rewrite, Explain & Expand, or Summarize.\n• **Language**: Translate the adapted text into a target language.\n### Immersive Reader Features\n• **Focus Reader**: View one word or a short group at your own pace, with pause and Previous/Next controls.\n• **Karaoke Mode**: Sentence-by-sentence TTS with active highlighting.\n• **Bionic Reading**: Bolds word beginnings as an optional visual preference.\n• **Grammar Highlighting**: Color-code Nouns, Verbs, and Adjectives.\n• **Cloze Activity**: Interactive fill-in-the-blank comprehension game.\n• **Focus view**: Hide the header and sidebar using Focus view beside the reading controls. Choose Exit focus view to return.\n### Oral Reading Fluency (ORF)\n• **Listen to Read-Alouds**: Students read text aloud while the system records and analyzes.\n• **WCPM Scoring**: Automatic Words Correct Per Minute calculation.\n• **Color-Coded Feedback**: Green (correct), Yellow (hesitation), Red (missed) highlighting.\n• **Accuracy Tracking**: Percentage of correctly read words with fluency data persistence.\n### Pro Tip\nToggle 'Grammar Highlighting' to identify parts of speech visually•great for ELL students learning sentence structure.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Representation**: Provides customization of perception (Guideline 1), letting learners access content at their zone of proximal development with personalized supports."}},{"k":"wordsounds_title","v":{"s":"Word Sounds"}},{"k":"wordsounds_text","v":{"s":"Build foundational literacy skills with the Word Sounds Studio•a comprehensive phonemic awareness and phonics practice environment.\n### Panel Options\n• **Grade Level**: Adjust word difficulty (K-2, 3-5, Custom).\n• **Activity Mode**: Select 'Phonics' (Letters+Sounds) or 'Sound Only' (Auditory Focus).\n• **Source**: Use Glossary terms or generate new words by phoneme pattern.\n### 8 Activity Types\n• **Count Sounds**: How many phonemes in the word?\n• **Find Sounds (Isolation)**: Identify first/middle/last sounds.\n• **Blend Sounds**: Listen to phonemes, blend into a word.\n• **Break Apart (Segmentation)**: Separate words into sounds using Elkonin boxes.\n• **Rhyme Time**: Find rhyming words from options.\n• **Sound Mapping**: Connect phonemes to graphemes (letters).\n• **Sight & Spell**: Orthography and spelling practice.\n• **Word Families**: Match words with the same start or end sound (-at, -ing, etc.).\n### Gamification Features\n• **6 Achievement Badges**: First Sound, On Fire, Perfect 10, Rhyme Master, Blend Wizard, Daily Star.\n• **Streak System**: Build consecutive correct answers for bonus XP.\n• **Adaptive Difficulty**: Auto-adjusts based on accuracy (Easy/Medium/Hard/Auto).\n• **Session Goals**: Set daily word count targets.\n• **Phoneme Mastery Tracking**: Identifies struggling sounds for targeted practice.\n• **Confusion Pattern Detection**: AI detects and addresses common mistakes (b/d, short vowels).\n### Audio & Visual Modes\n• **TTS Speed Control**: Slow down or speed up pronunciation.\n• **Phonics Toggle**: Switch between letters+sounds or sounds-only mode.\n• **Auto-Generated Images**: Visual cues accompanying each word.\n• **Phoneme Bank Picker**: Browse and preview all phoneme sounds.\n### Teacher Features\n• **Pre-Activity Review Panel**: Audit and correct AI-generated phonetic data before students play.\n• **Word Regeneration**: Replace problematic words with teacher-curated alternatives.\n• **Progress Reports**: Track individual phoneme accuracy across sessions.\n### Pro Tip\nUse the Phoneme Bank Picker to select specific sounds for targeted intervention•great for RTI groups!\n### UDL Connection\n• **Representation**: Provides multiple means of perception (Guideline 1) through auditory-only, visual, and combined phonics modes."}},{"k":"outline_title","v":{"s":"Visual Organizer"}},{"k":"outline_text","v":{"s":"Create visual representations of your content's structure. Transform text into 6 different graphic organizer formats, each tailored to specific thinking and reasoning patterns.\n### Panel Options\n• **Structure Type**: Choose your organizer format from the 6 available types.\n• **Custom Instructions**: Add specific guidance for tailored organization (e.g., \"focus on cause chains\" or \"use these specific terms\").\n### Organizer Types\n• **Venn Diagram**: Compare and contrast two or more concepts with draggable sections.\n• **Structured Outline**: Hierarchical list showing main ideas and supporting details.\n• **Key Concept Map**: Spider-web visualization connecting central ideas to related concepts.\n• **Flow Chart**: Visualize sequential processes, timelines, or decision trees.\n• **Cause and Effect**: Fishbone/Ishikawa diagrams showing relationships between factors and outcomes.\n• **Problem Solution**: Identify problems, analyze contributing factors, and propose solutions.\n### Interactive Features\n• **Drag-and-Drop Sorting**: Students move items between Venn sections or reorder outline points.\n• **Game Mode**: Convert static organizers into competitive sorting activities.\n• **Edit Mode**: Rename headings, add sub-points, or restructure content manually.\n• **Bilingual Mode**: View organizers with translated labels for multilingual learners.\n### Pro Tip\nUse Cause & Effect organizers for science experiments and Problem Solution for persuasive writing assignments.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Representation**: Guides processing and visualization (Guideline 3.3) by transforming linear text into spatial relationships."}},{"k":"visual_title","v":{"s":"AI Visuals"}},{"k":"visual_text","v":{"s":"Enhance comprehension with AI-generated imagery. Create visual representations of key concepts using diverse art styles and intelligent layout modes to support Dual Coding strategies.\n### Panel Options\n• **Worksheet Mode**: Creates fill-in-the-blank style visuals for student activities.\n• **Enhanced Visuals**: Uses creative logic for more artistic, less literal interpretations.\n• **Text Reduced**: Generates pure visuals without labels or captions to reduce cognitive load.\n• **Layout Mode**: Direct the AI Art Director to generate Single Images, Before/After Comparisons, Step-by-Step Sequences, or Labeled Diagrams.\n• **Art Style**: Choose from Default, Isometric, Pixel Art, Watercolor, Blueprint, Comic, Line Art, or 3D Render.\n• **Custom Instructions**: Describe specific visual requirements or constraints.\n### Interactive Features\n• **Regenerate**: Request a new variation with one click.\n• **Download**: Save high-quality images for slides or handouts.\n• **Delete**: Remove and start fresh if needed.\n### Pro Tip\nUse the \"Sequence\" layout mode with the \"Line Art\" style to instantly generate printable multi-step instructional guides!\n### UDL Connection\n• **Representation**: Clarify syntax and structure (Guideline 2) by providing visual alternatives to text."}},{"k":"faq_title","v":{"s":"Predictive FAQ"}},{"k":"faq_text","v":{"s":"Anticipate student confusion before it happens. Automatically generates a predictive FAQ based on the text's complexity, proactively addressing common misconceptions.\n### Panel Options\n• **Question Count**: Choose 3, 5, 8, or 10 Q&A pairs to generate.\n• **Custom Instructions**: Guide generation with specific focus areas (e.g., \"focus on vocabulary\" or \"target common errors\").\n### Key Features\n• **Auto-Generation**: Instantly creates Questions & Answers based on text analysis.\n• **Audio Support**: Text-to-Speech for both questions and answers; click any Q or A to hear it aloud.\n• **Bilingual Support**: View and hear translations if a target language is selected.\n• **Click-to-Hear Mode**: Interactive listening station for independent study.\n### Pro Tip\nUse the audio feature to create a listening station activity where students check understanding—great for centers!\n### UDL Connection\n• **Representation**: Highlights patterns and critical features (Guideline 3) by explicitly addressing common misconceptions."}},{"k":"scaffolds_title","v":{"s":"Writing Scaffolds"}},{"k":"scaffolds_text","v":{"s":"Comprehensive writing support system with AI-powered grading and customizable sentence structures. Perfect for differentiated writing instruction.\n### Scaffold Types\n• **Sentence Starters**: List-based prompts to help students begin their thoughts.\n• **Paragraph Frames**: Cloze-style fill-in-the-blank paragraphs for structured argumentation.\n• **Discussion Prompts**: Conversation starters for collaborative discussions.\n• **Custom Instructions**: Tailor frames to specific rhetorical functions (e.g., 'agreeing/disagreeing', 'cause and effect').\n### Rubric & Assessment System\n• **Auto-Generated Rubrics**: AI creates criteria-based rubrics aligned to your content.\n• **Self-Assessment Checklists**: Student-facing success criteria for self-monitoring.\n• **Mastery Assessment**: Evaluate student understanding with structured rubric grading.\n• **Rubric Zoom**: Enlarge rubric view for detailed criteria review.\n### AI Auto-Grader\n• **Instant Feedback**: Submit student drafts for immediate AI-powered evaluation.\n• **Criteria-Based Scoring**: Grades each response against rubric criteria points.\n• **Glow & Grow**: Provides specific praise (\"glow\") and improvement suggestions (\"grow\").\n• **TTS Feedback**: Allobot reads grading results aloud for accessibility.\n• **XP Rewards**: Students earn Mastery XP (100 points) for completed drafts.\n### Input Options\n• **Voice Dictation**: Students can dictate responses using the FAB microphone button.\n• **Edit Mode**: Teachers can customize sentence starters and prompts.\n• **Reset & Retry**: Clear student work for fresh attempts.\n### Pro Tip\nUse the 'Start Check' button to initiate the AI grading loop•students can revise based on feedback and resubmit!\n### UDL Connection\n• **Action & Expression**: Optimized for construction and composition (Guideline 5), providing graduated levels of support for practice and performance."}},{"k":"quiz_title","v":{"s":"Gamified Quiz"}},{"k":"quiz_text","v":{"s":"Create an assessment, present it for discussion, or choose Games to practice with the same resource.\n### Game Modes\n• **Live Quiz**: Real-time synchronized sessions with score trackings and session codes for students to join.\n• **Team Showdown**: Team-based competition with color-coded groups and collaborative scoring.\n• **Boss Battle**: Class vs AI boss•answer correctly to deal damage and defeat the boss together!\n• **Puzzle Challenge**: Solve question-based puzzles, including matching, sequencing, and ciphers, with hints and a final challenge.\n• **Escape Room**: Explore connected objects, collect evidence and tools, and combine discoveries to open the exit. Play solo or together.\n• **Board Game**: Explore lesson locations and solve activities, solo or together.\n• **Review Game**: Choose questions from a category board and award team points.\n• **Review Mode**: Self-paced practice with immediate feedback.\n### Question Types\n• **Multiple Choice**: Standard MCQ with configurable question count.\n• **Reflection Questions**: Open-ended responses for deeper thinking.\n• **Fill-in-the-Blank**: Complete sentences with missing key terms.\n• **Matching**: Connect related concepts.\n• **Cipher Puzzles**: Decode encrypted messages in Puzzle Challenge.\n### Gamification Features\n• **Leaderboards**: Real-time ranking during live sessions.\n• **Team Colors**: Auto-assigned team identities for group competitions.\n• **Hints System**: Spend hint tokens for clues in Puzzle Challenge (limited supply!).\n• **Completion Tracking**: Track Puzzle Challenge completions and quiz scores across sessions.\n### AI Auto-Grader\n• **Reflection Grading**: AI evaluates open-ended answers with rubric-based feedback.\n• **Instant Scores**: Automatic scoring with personalized feedback for each response.\n### Live Differentiated Delivery\n• **Group Overrides**: Assign different resources or language versions to specific student groups mid-session.\n• **Targeted Push**: Send a scaffolded quiz to Tier 3 students while the rest work on standard material.\n• **Real-Time Switching**: No need to end the session•differentiate on the fly from the teacher dashboard.\n### Teacher Features\n• **Presentation Mode**: Project a large question board for whole-class discussion. Select an answer to check it or reveal the answer guide; presentation responses do not submit learner assessments.\n• **Session Codes**: Generate join codes for students to connect from any device.\n• **Show/Hide Answers**: Toggle answer key visibility during review.\n• **DOK Levels**: Align questions to Depth of Knowledge standards.\n### Pro Tip\nChoose Puzzle Challenge for question practice or Escape Room for an investigation that connects clues from the lesson.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Engagement**: Optimize challenge (Guideline 8.2) through incremental difficulty and gamified feedback loops."}},{"k":"brainstorm_title","v":{"s":"Activity Designer"}},{"k":"brainstorm_text","v":{"s":"Four activity modes in one tool: quick Idea Starters, runnable Discussion Kits, Jigsaw cooperative activities, and interactive Canvas Simulations. Pick a mode at the top of the panel.\n### Discussion Kit Mode\n• **Protocols**: Think-Pair-Share, Socratic Seminar, Fishbowl, or Gallery Walk.\n• **Ramped Questions**: Literal, inferential, and evaluative question sets drawn from your source.\n• **Talk Stems**: Student sentence starters for agreeing, disagreeing, clarifying, and building on ideas.\n• **Teacher Notes**: Facilitation timing, pitfalls, and participation look-fors (teacher view only).\n### Jigsaw Mode\n• **Expert Packets**: The source is split into interdependent chunks, one per expert group.\n• **Teach-Back Cards**: Key points and check questions each expert uses to teach their home group.\n• **Accountability Check**: Short free-response questions spanning every chunk, with a teacher-only answer key.\n### Idea Starters Mode\n• **Custom Instructions**: Add specific focus areas or context for ideas.\n• **Real-World Connections**: Activities linking content to careers and daily life.\n• **Discussion Hooks**: Provocative questions to spark class conversations.\n• **Project-Based Ideas**: Long-term project concepts with driving questions.\n### Gemini Canvas (Simulation Generator)\nGenerate interactive Canvas simulations with iterative AI refinement:\n• **Simulation Types**: React components, Python visualizations, Physics simulations, Custom chatbots.\n• **Step Count Slider** (1-10): More steps = more refined prompts for deeper exploration.\n• **Canvas Prompt Button**: Auto-launches Gemini Canvas with your simulation code.\n### Generated Idea Cards\nEach idea includes:\n• **Title & Description**: Core activity overview.\n• **Connection Field**: How it links to your content.\n• **Teacher Guide**: Generate step-by-step implementation instructions per idea.\n• **Edit Mode**: Modify any field after generation.\n### Pro Tip\nUse Python simulation mode to create auto-graded math practice tools•students input values and get instant feedback!\n### UDL Connection\n• **Engagement**: Optimize relevance, value, and authenticity (Guideline 7) by connecting learning to real-world problems and interactive experiences."}},{"k":"persona_title","v":{"s":"Persona Chat"}},{"k":"persona_text","v":{"s":"Persona Interview Mode brings content to life through immersive character conversations. Interview historical figures, fictional characters, or AI-generated experts in a gamified experience that builds empathy and deepens understanding.\n### Interview Modes\n• **1-on-1 Interview**: Deep conversation with a single character for focused exploration.\n• **Panel Discussion**: Select multiple personas for group debates and diverse perspectives.\n• **Free Response vs Multiple Choice**: Toggle between open-ended typing or guided question options.\n### Gamification Features\n• **XP System**: Earn Interview XP for quality questions and thoughtful engagement.\n• **Badges**: Unlock achievements like *Harmonizer*, *First Insight*, *Rapport Builder*, and *Master Interviewer*.\n• **Reflection Grading**: Submit a final reflection to earn bonus XP with AI-powered feedback.\n• **Hard Mode**: Disable hints for extra challenge and higher XP rewards.\n### Voice & Accessibility\n• **Auto-Read**: Personas speak their responses aloud using Text-to-Speech.\n• **Auto-Send**: Hands-free mode automatically sends your message after a pause.\n• **Custom Instructions**: Shape the persona's background, era, or expertise level.\n### Pro Tip\n• Project the Persona Chat on the board and have the whole class vote on what question to ask next.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Engagement**: Foster collaboration and community (Guideline 8) through simulated social learning interactions."}},{"k":"timeline_title","v":{"s":"Sequence Builder"}},{"k":"timeline_text","v":{"s":"Sequence Builder (Timeline) transforms events into an interactive drag-and-drop ordering activity. Perfect for chronological events, process steps, or cause-and-effect sequences.\n### Content Generation\n• **Auto-Extraction**: AI identifies dates, events, and milestones from your text.\n• **Event Count**: Customize 5-15 events for your timeline.\n• **Custom Topic**: Override with a specific sequence topic.\n• **Process Steps**: Visualize scientific procedures, recipes, or math steps.\n### Sequence Game Mode\nLaunch an interactive ordering challenge where students arrange events chronologically:\n**Gameplay Features**:\n• **Drag & Drop**: Intuitive event reordering with glowing drop zones.\n• **Move Up/Down Buttons**: Alternative navigation for accessibility or motor challenges.\n• **Check Button**: Submit answer•correct events lock with ?, incorrect ones shake for repositioning.\n• **Reset Button**: Scramble events for a fresh attempt.\n• **Completion Tracking**: Visual feedback when all events are correctly ordered.\n**Accessibility**:\n• **ARIA Labels**: Full screen reader support with position announcements.\n• **Keyboard Navigation**: Full keyboard control for drag operations.\n• **Visual States**: Lifted, dropped, and locked states clearly indicated.\n### Teacher Features\n• **Edit Mode**: Modify event text, dates, or descriptions before sharing.\n• **Preview Game**: Test the sequencing activity before students play.\n### Pro Tip\nUse Process Steps mode to break down complex lab instructions•students practice sequencing while learning the procedure!\n### UDL Connection\n• **Representation**: Illustrate through multiple media (Guideline 2.5) by converting text sequences into spatial/visual timelines.\n• **Action & Expression**: Physical manipulation of knowledge (Guideline 5) through drag-and-drop interaction."}},{"k":"concept_sort_title","v":{"s":"Concept Sort"}},{"k":"concept_sort_text","v":{"s":"Reinforce categorization skills and conceptual relationships. Students drag-and-drop terms into defined categories, actively processing connections between ideas.\n### Panel Options\n• **Category Setup**: Define category bins (e.g., \"Mammals vs Reptiles\", \"Renewable vs Non-Renewable\").\n• **Item Count**: Set how many items to generate for sorting.\n• **Custom Items**: Add your own terms or edit AI-generated ones.\n### Gameplay Features\n• **Drag-and-Drop**: Interactive sorting with visual feedback on desktop.\n• **Keyboard Sorting**: Use arrow buttons for accessible keyboard navigation•no mouse required.\n• **Image Cards**: Items can include AI-generated visuals alongside text for dual coding.\n• **Instant Feedback**: Immediate validation of correct/incorrect sorts with color indicators.\n• **Check Answers**: Reveal all correct placements to validate learning.\n### Print & Export\n• **Printable Worksheet**: Generates a cut-and-paste activity layout for offline use.\n### Accessibility\n• **Screen Reader Support**: Full ARIA labels announce item status (sorted/unsorted) and available actions.\n• **Keyboard Focus**: Tab navigation and visual focus states for all interactive elements.\n### Pro Tip\nUse image-based cards when introducing visual vocabulary to younger learners or ELL students!\n### UDL Connection\n• **Action & Expression**: Facilitate managing information and resources (Guideline 6) by physically manipulating information."}},{"k":"math_title","v":{"s":"STEM Solver"}},{"k":"math_text","v":{"s":"A comprehensive STEM Problem Solver that goes beyond word problems. Covers 10 subject areas with 4 different solution modes, LaTeX equation support, and auto-generated visual aids.\n### Panel Options\n• **Subject Area**: Choose from 10 disciplines:\n  - General Math, Algebra, Geometry, Calculus\n  - Chemistry, Physics, Biology, Earth Science\n  - Computer Science, Economics\n• **Solution Mode**: Pick your instructional approach:\n  - **Problem Set Generator**: Create multiple practice problems with answers\n  - **Step-by-Step**: Detailed worked solutions with explanations\n  - **Conceptual**: Focus on understanding \"why\" before \"how\"\n  - **Real-World Application**: Authentic contexts and scenarios\n• **Problem Quantity**: Set how many problems to generate (for Problem Set mode)\n### Output Features\n• **Contextualized Problems**: Word problems use characters/themes from your source text\n• **Worked Solutions**: Complete step-by-step explanations with clear reasoning\n• **LaTeX Equations**: Beautiful mathematical notation rendered inline\n• **Visual Aids**: Auto-generated SVG graphs and diagrams for applicable problems\n### Pro Tip\nUse \"Real-World Application\" mode in Economics or Earth Science to create cross-curricular STEM challenges!\n### UDL Connection\n• **Expression**: Builds fluency with graduated levels of support (Guideline 5.3) by offering multiple solution modes from conceptual to procedural."}},{"k":"adventure_title","v":{"s":"Adventure Mode"}},{"k":"adventure_text","v":{"s":"Adventure Mode transforms content into immersive interactive experiences. Choose from multiple simulation modes with deep gamification for truly engaging learning.\n### Input Modes\n• **Multiple Choice**: Select from 4 AI-generated options per turn (beginner-friendly).\n• **Debate Mode**: Persuade characters with arguments•momentum shifts based on logic.\n• **System Simulation**: Manage factions, resources, and macro-level policy decisions.\n### Simulation Types\n• **Standard Adventure**: Classic choose-your-own-adventure branching narratives.\n• **Social Story (SEL)**: Scenarios with social-emotional challenges•friendship, teamwork, frustration management.\n• **Story Mode**: Narrative focus with descriptive passages and character development.\n### Gamification Features\n• **XP & Energy System**: Earn Adventure XP as you progress; energy depletes with risky choices.\n• **D20 Dice Chance Mode**: Risky actions trigger dice rolls•teaches probability and risk assessment.\n• **Difficulty Levels**: Story (narrative focus), Normal (balanced), Hardcore (strict penalties, resource depletion).\n• **Level Progression**: Advance through adventure levels with increasing complexity.\n### Faction & Resource System\n• **Resource Tracking**: Gold, Health, Morale, or custom variables with real consequences.\n• **AI or Manual Mode**: Let AI manage resources or define your own starting values.\n• **Consequences**: Actions drain or replenish resources•strategic thinking required!\n### Democracy Mode (Whole-Class)\n• **Class Voting**: Project the adventure on the board and let students vote on which path to take.\n• **Collective Agency**: The most popular choice advances the story•teaches democratic decision-making.\n• **Presentation Mode**: Perfect for whole-class instruction where everyone participates in a shared narrative.\n### Interactive Features\n• **Free Response**: Type any action freely•AI adapts dynamically to creative inputs.\n• **Immersive Mode**: Fullscreen cinematic experience for complete immersion.\n• **Auto-Read TTS**: Story narration read aloud automatically.\n• **Storybook Export**: Export illustrated adventures as HTML with AI-generated scene art.\n### Pro Tip\nUse System Simulation mode to teach economics, civics, or ecology through hands-on resource management decisions.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Engagement**: Foster collaboration and community (Guideline 8) through simulated social and strategic scenarios."}},{"k":"alignment_title","v":{"s":"Alignment Report"}},{"k":"alignment_text","v":{"s":"Ensure your lesson hits the mark. This report automatically cross-references your generated resources against Common Core Standards and UDL Guidelines, identifying strengths and gaps.\n### AI Standards Finder\n• **Smart Search**: Enter a topic or skill and AI suggests matching CCSS, NGSS, or TEKS standards.\n• **AI Consultation**: Get strategy advice on how your content addresses specific standards.\n• **Multi-Framework**: Supports Common Core ELA/Math, NGSS, and state-specific frameworks.\n### Alignment Checks\n• **CAST UDL Guidelines**: Checks for Engagement, Representation, and Action/Expression.\n• **Standards Verification**: Cross-reference with Common Core, NGSS, or State Standards.\n• **Gap Analysis**: Identifies missing elements or weak points in your lesson plan.\n• **Suggestions**: Actionable advice to improve alignment.\n### Pro Tip\n• Use the Gap Analysis to justify resource requests or co-planning time to administration.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Action & Expression**: Enhance capacity for monitoring progress (Guideline 6.4) by establishing clear goals and success criteria."}},{"k":"lesson_plan_title","v":{"s":"Lesson Plan"}},{"k":"lesson_plan_text","v":{"s":"Generate a complete, structured Lesson Plan that ties everything together. It provides a roadmap for instruction, including specific scripts for 'I Do, We Do, You Do' teaching phases.\n### Mode-Adaptive Naming\n• **Teacher Mode**: Full Lesson Plan with instructional scripts.\n• **Student Mode**: Becomes a structured Study Guide.\n• **Parent Mode**: Becomes a Family Guide for home support.\n### Panel Options\n• **Custom Additions**: Specify any special requests (e.g., \"include technology integration\" or \"focus on visual learners\").\n### Plan Components\n• **Learning Objectives**: SMART goals derived from the content.\n• **Materials List**: Comprehensive checklist of required resources.\n• **Direct Instruction**: Scripted 'I Do' section.\n• **Guided Practice**: Collaborative 'We Do' activities.\n• **Independent Practice**: 'You Do' assignments.\n• **Access Planning**: UDL supports and differentiation ideas for educator review.\n### Pro Tip\nTreat generated supports as planning suggestions. Verify any student-specific accommodation or modification against the documented plan, assessment conditions, and local procedures before use.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Engagement**: Heighten salience of goals and objectives (Guideline 8.1) by clearly structuring the learning path."}},{"k":"fullpack_title","v":{"s":"Full Pack"}},{"k":"fullpack_text","v":{"s":"Build a coordinated set of resources from one source while keeping the educator in control of the plan.\n### Plan Before Generating\n• **Auto-Configuration**: AI proposes resource types and instructions from the source, grade, and standards.\n• **Editable Review**: Add or remove resources, change resource types and instructions, and move rows before approval.\n• **Capacity Preview**: Review estimated AI and image calls before generation.\n### Text Access\n• The primary/source text remains the instructional anchor by default.\n• Adapted Text is optional and, when included, is labeled as a supplemental companion.\n• The system does not infer a primary-text replacement or an IEP modification.\n### Typical Resources\nPlans may include analysis, glossary, visuals, outlines, sentence frames, questions, activities, quizzes, and a lesson plan. Analyze Source generally works best first; Lesson Plan works best last so it can use earlier resources.\n### Pro Tip\nOpen each proposed row and make the plan match your instructional purpose before selecting Generate full pack.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Action & Expression**: Streamlines coordinated resource creation (Guideline 5) while preserving educator review and multiple access paths."}},{"k":"utils_title","v":{"s":"Accessibility Hub"}},{"k":"utils_text","v":{"s":"The Accessibility and Settings Hub. Customize the entire application for diverse learner needs.\n### Reading Accessibility\n• **Text Size**: Adjust font scale for visual comfort.\n• **Font Style**: Choose a font that you find comfortable.\n• **Line Height & Spacing**: Increase vertical spacing for easier reading.\n• **Bionic Reading**: Bold first portion of words to guide reading flow.\n• **Color Overlay**: Apply a visual tint over the page.\n### Theme & Display\n• **Dark Mode**: Low-light interface for reduced eye strain.\n• **High Contrast Mode**: Maximum contrast with bold outlines for low vision.\n• **Reduce Animations**: Toggle off motion effects for vestibular sensitivity.\n### Voice & Audio\n• **Voice Selection**: Choose from multiple TTS voices (male/female, accents).\n• **Speed Control**: Adjust speech rate from 0.5• to 2• speed.\n• **Volume Control**: Set TTS volume independently from system audio.\n### AlloBot Settings\n• **Show/Hide AlloBot**: Toggle the animated assistant character.\n• **Disable Tips**: Turn off proactive tips from AlloBot.\n### Profile & System\n• **Profile Context**: Add your teaching context (grade, subject) to improve AI output.\n• **Language Preferences**: Set default interface and target translation languages.\n• **Documentation**: Access user guides, tutorials, and pedagogical resources.\n### Pro Tip\nReading Accessibility preferences support display and access. They do not designate a primary-text replacement or change an IEP, 504 plan, or assessment condition.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Representation**: Offer alternatives for auditory and visual information (Guidelines 1.1-1.3)."}},{"k":"dashboard_title","v":{"s":"Dashboard / Tools"}},{"k":"dashboard_text","v":{"s":"The Tool Navigation Bar and Teacher Dashboard access point.\n### Tool Navigation Bar\n• **Tool Icons**: One-click jump to any generator (Quiz, Glossary, Adventure, etc.).\n• **Status Dots**: Green = active content, Orange = processing, Gray = empty.\n• **Logical Flow**: Tools ordered left-to-right from Input → Generate → Export.\n### Teacher Dashboard Button\nClick the Dashboard icon to open the **Teacher Grading Dashboard** - a dedicated panel for tracking student progress:\n• **Upload Student JSONs**: Students export their work as JSON files; upload them here for batch analysis.\n• **Student Roster**: View all uploaded students with nickname, date, quiz progress, and Adventure level.\n• **Individual Review**: Click any student to see their full history•quizzes, adventures, responses.\n• **Mark as Graded**: Checkbox to track which students you've reviewed.\n• **Class Insights Tab**: Analytics charts showing common misconceptions and class-wide performance.\n• **Export to CSV**: Download class data for gradebook import.\n### Related Header Actions\n• **Jump to Lesson**: Quick-return to your most recent lesson plan.\n• **View Toggle**: Switch between Teacher and Student views.\n### Pro Tip\nHave students export their JSON saves at the end of class, then batch-upload them here for efficient overnight grading!"}},{"k":"actions_title","v":{"s":"Action Bar"}},{"k":"actions_text","v":{"s":"Use the header controls to set the interface language, manage live sessions, translate resources, and open export tools.\n### Review before delivery\n• Check translated content for meaning and accuracy.\n• Open Document Builder to review the selected resources and available download formats. Preview the result before sharing it with learners.\n• Start a live session to obtain a join code, or create a supported homework share for independent work.\n### Continue exploring\nThe Educator and Learning tool menus open additional planning, assessment, creative, and interactive activities. Guided Mode helps you build a focused lesson before exploring those options."}},{"k":"history_title","v":{"s":"Session History"}},{"k":"history_text","v":{"s":"History holds the resources in your current workspace. Open a saved item to review it or return to an earlier result.\n### Keep a backup\n• Save a project backup to continue on another device or recover your work later. Guided Mode also shows whether progress was saved on this device.\n• A workspace may contain materials from several lessons. Check the selected resources before exporting or sharing.\n### Guided lesson packages\nOpen Document Builder from Guided Mode to work with that lesson’s selected resources. The general Builder can use the wider workspace, so review its contents before delivery."}},{"k":"spotlight_title","v":{"s":"Spotlight"}},{"k":"spotlight_message","v":{"s":"Say hello to {name}!"}},{"k":"dbq_title","v":{"s":"Document-Based Questions"}},{"k":"dbq_text","v":{"s":"Document-Based Questions: students analyze primary sources, build evidence-based arguments, and practice the central skill of social-studies + ELA assessments. Generates source documents, scaffolded questions, and answer keys aligned to your standards."}},{"k":"quiz_mode_title","v":{"s":"Pick the right quiz mode"}},{"k":"quiz_mode_text","v":{"s":"Choose what this quiz is for. Exit Ticket checks today’s learning. Pre-Check probes prior knowledge before teaching and surfaces gaps as concept cards with a one-click \"Explain to class\" AI broadcast. Formative Check is a quick mid-lesson pulse. Spaced Review tracks each student’s cross-session retention with a per-concept sparkline. Each mode tunes prompts, item-type mix, and the live dashboard layout."}},{"k":"anchor_chart_title","v":{"s":"Anchor Charts"}},{"k":"anchor_chart_text","v":{"s":"Generate classroom-ready Anchor Charts that make concepts, vocabulary, and procedures stick. A visual reference students can return to throughout a unit.\n### Panel Options\n- **Chart Type**: Use Auto or choose Reference, Process, Concept Map, Comparison, Strategy, Vocabulary, Routine, Worked Example, Success Criteria, Misconceptions, or Question Guide.\n### Chart Components\n- **Title Banner**: Eye-catching topic header.\n- **Visual Hierarchy**: Headings, bullets, and callouts organized for skim-reading.\n- **Iconography**: Auto-generated icons reinforcing each idea with dual-coded visual cues.\n### Teacher Controls\n- **Edit Mode**: Rewrite text, reorder sections, add or remove sections, and regenerate icons.\n- **Interactive Mode**: Optional student fill-in and feedback workflow when you want it.\n- **Print-Ready**: Download PNG or print as a poster or handout.\n### Pro Tip\n- Use Misconceptions before a review lesson and Success Criteria before a writing task.\n### UDL Connection\n- **Representation**: Activate or supply background knowledge (Guideline 3.1) with persistent visual anchors students can revisit independently."}},{"k":"note_taking_title","v":{"s":"Note-Taking Templates"}},{"k":"note_taking_text","v":{"s":"Scaffolded Note-Taking Templates that teach students *how* to take notes, not just *what* to write. Pick the structure that matches the cognitive task.\n### Template Types\n• **Cornell Notes**: Classic two-column layout with cues, notes, and bottom summary.\n• **Two-Column Notes**: Main idea / details organization for content-heavy reading.\n• **T-Chart**: Compare/contrast or pros/cons side-by-side.\n• **Sketchnotes**: Visual note-taking with prompts for icons, arrows, and color-coding.\n• **KWL Chart**: Know / Want to know / Learned — perfect for pre/post-reading.\n• **Outline Notes**: Hierarchical structure for lectures or textbook chapters.\n### Generation Features\n• **Pre-Filled Prompts**: Each template seeded with cues drawn from your source text.\n• **Question Stems**: Built-in metacognitive prompts (\"What surprised you?\", \"How does this connect to…?\").\n• **Vocabulary Slots**: Pre-populated key terms students should listen/read for.\n• **Custom Instructions**: Target a specific cognitive task (synthesis, summary, evaluation).\n### Print & Digital\n• **Printable PDF**: Clean handout layout with generous writing space.\n• **Digital Fillable**: Students type directly into the template for paperless workflows.\n• **Editable Headings**: Teachers tailor column labels and section titles before sharing.\n### Pro Tip\n• Pair *Cornell Notes* with the **Adapted Text**: students take notes at their reading level, then use the bottom-summary box as a formative-assessment check.\n### UDL Connection\n• **Action & Expression**: Support planning and strategy development (Guideline 6.2) by giving learners explicit structures for organizing information."}},{"k":"applied_challenge_text","v":{"s":"Create one sustained transfer challenge. Auto Match or choose Investigate, Design, Decide, Propose, or Explore, then decide how much AI framing to provide while students own the work."}},{"k":"applied_challenge_title","v":{"s":"Applied Challenge Studio"}},{"k":"memory_aid_text","v":{"s":"Create a purposeful mix of memory aids. You can model one, scaffold one, coach student authorship, and ask students to explain why their cue works."}},{"k":"memory_aid_title","v":{"s":"Memory Aid Studio"}}],"id":10}},{"k":"checkpoint","v":{"o":[{"k":"offer","v":{"s":"Talk about your work"}},{"k":"offer_sub","v":{"s":"A couple of questions about what you wrote. You can skip them."}},{"k":"working","v":{"s":"Getting a question ready..."}},{"k":"too_little","v":{"s":"Write a bit more first, then this can ask you about it."}},{"k":"answer","v":{"s":"Answer"}},{"k":"answer_label","v":{"s":"Your answer"}},{"k":"later","v":{"s":"I’ll come back to this"}},{"k":"listening","v":{"s":"🔴 Listening — say your answer"}},{"k":"misfit","v":{"s":"This question doesn’t fit my work"}},{"k":"mode_audio","v":{"s":"🎤 Speak"}},{"k":"mode_choice","v":{"s":"☑️ Choose"}},{"k":"mode_point","v":{"s":"👆 Point to it"}},{"k":"mode_text","v":{"s":"⌨️ Type"}},{"k":"no_grade","v":{"s":"This is not graded here, there is no timer, and your work stays open while you answer."}},{"k":"point_help","v":{"s":"Click the sentence in your work that this is about, then press Answer."}},{"k":"speak","v":{"s":"🎤 Speak your answer (it becomes text on this device)"}},{"k":"support_note","v":{"s":"Still available while you answer: "}},{"k":"support_note2","v":{"s":". Only the answer helper is paused."}},{"k":"title","v":{"s":"A quick check-in about your work"}}],"id":11}},{"k":"launch_pad","v":{"o":[{"k":"subtitle","v":{"s":"Choose your learning pathway"}},{"k":"full_title","v":{"s":"Full Platform"}},{"k":"full_desc","v":{"s":"Complete access to all AlloFlow features: lessons, STEAM Lab, and tools"}},{"k":"guided_title","v":{"s":"Guided Mode"}},{"k":"guided_desc","v":{"s":"Step-by-step guidance through lesson creation and student activities"}},{"k":"stem_title","v":{"s":"STEAM Lab"}},{"k":"stem_desc","v":{"s":"100+ interactive science, math, and engineering simulations"}},{"k":"educator_tools_title","v":{"s":"Educator Tools"}},{"k":"educator_tools_desc","v":{"s":"BehaviorLens, Report Writer, and professional clinical tools — password protected"}},{"k":"badge_recommended","v":{"s":"Recommended"}},{"k":"badge_3_tools","v":{"s":"8 Tools"}},{"k":"badge_new","v":{"s":"New"}},{"k":"badge_educator","v":{"s":"🔒 Educator"}},{"k":"badge_educator_open","v":{"s":"🛠️ Educator"}},{"k":"switch_hint","v":{"s":"You can switch modes anytime from the menu"}},{"k":"learning_tools_title","v":{"s":"Learning Tools"}},{"k":"learning_tools_desc","v":{"s":"STEAM Lab, StoryForge, SEL Hub, Research Hub & more: explore, create, investigate, and grow"}},{"k":"mic_title","v":{"s":"Microphone Setup"}},{"k":"mic_desc","v":{"s":"Some tools use your microphone for dictation, recording, and voice input."}},{"k":"mic_canvas_warning","v":{"s":"In this environment, enabling the microphone will briefly reload the app. It's best to do it now before you start working."}},{"k":"change_language","v":{"s":"Change language"}},{"k":"current_language","v":{"s":"Current"}},{"k":"available_languages","v":{"s":"Available languages"}}],"id":12}},{"k":"guided","v":{"o":[{"k":"resume_saved_step","v":{"s":"Your saved step: {step}"}},{"k":"customize_short","v":{"s":"Customize"}},{"k":"settings_checkpoint_label","v":{"s":"Class settings"}},{"k":"settings_adjust","v":{"s":"Adjust"}},{"k":"settings_adjust_aria","v":{"s":"Review and adjust universal settings before generating"}},{"k":"step_cost_differentiated","v":{"s":"Differentiation is on: this step will generate {n} grade-level versions."}},{"k":"summary_emoji","v":{"s":"emoji support"}},{"k":"lesson_brief_settings","v":{"s":"Settings"}},{"k":"indicator_title","v":{"s":"Guided Mode"}},{"k":"step_of","v":{"s":"Step {current} of {total}"}},{"k":"phase_context","v":{"s":"Guided phase"}},{"k":"phase_of","v":{"s":"Phase {current} of {total}"}},{"k":"phase_plan","v":{"s":"Plan"}},{"k":"phase_plan_description","v":{"s":"Choose the source and intended outcome."}},{"k":"phase_understand","v":{"s":"Understand"}},{"k":"phase_understand_description","v":{"s":"Find barriers, concepts, and instructional priorities."}},{"k":"phase_access","v":{"s":"Make accessible"}},{"k":"phase_access_description","v":{"s":"Build multiple ways to perceive and understand the content."}},{"k":"phase_participate","v":{"s":"Build participation"}},{"k":"phase_participate_description","v":{"s":"Add ways to practice, discuss, explore, and create."}},{"k":"phase_assess","v":{"s":"Check learning"}},{"k":"phase_assess_description","v":{"s":"Gather evidence and verify alignment."}},{"k":"phase_organize","v":{"s":"Organize"}},{"k":"phase_organize_description","v":{"s":"Connect resources into a teachable sequence."}},{"k":"phase_assign","v":{"s":"Assign"}},{"k":"phase_assign_description","v":{"s":"Write student-facing directions, goals, and success criteria."}},{"k":"phase_deliver","v":{"s":"Preview & deliver"}},{"k":"phase_deliver_description","v":{"s":"Choose the right export, sharing, or live-session route."}},{"k":"phase_finish","v":{"s":"Review & finish"}},{"k":"phase_finish_description","v":{"s":"Review the lesson and save the completion summary."}},{"k":"phase_checkpoint_title","v":{"s":"{phase} phase complete"}},{"k":"phase_checkpoint_summary","v":{"s":"{completed} completed · {skipped} skipped · {resources} resources created"}},{"k":"phase_checkpoint_review","v":{"s":"Review latest resource"}},{"k":"phase_checkpoint_adjust","v":{"s":"Adjust remaining path"}},{"k":"phase_checkpoint_continue","v":{"s":"Continue to {phase}"}},{"k":"phase_jump_summary_title","v":{"s":"Moved from {from} to {to}"}},{"k":"phase_jump_summary","v":{"s":"{skipped} unfinished steps were marked skipped across {phases} phase(s)."}},{"k":"back","v":{"s":"← Back"}},{"k":"skip","v":{"s":"Next Step →"}},{"k":"all_done","v":{"s":"🎉 All Done! View All Tools"}},{"k":"about","v":{"s":"About"}},{"k":"source_prompt","v":{"s":"Paste or enter source text to begin"}},{"k":"history_hint","v":{"s":"💡 Your generated resources are saved in the History tab — you can revisit and export them anytime!"}},{"k":"about_prefix","v":{"s":"📖"}},{"k":"exit","v":{"s":"Exit"}},{"k":"resume_later","v":{"s":"Resume later"}},{"k":"resume_later_hint","v":{"s":"Save your place and return from Setup"}},{"k":"progress_saved","v":{"s":"Guided progress saved. Resume anytime from Setup."}},{"k":"progress_saving","v":{"s":"Saving progress…"}},{"k":"progress_saving_short","v":{"s":"Saving"}},{"k":"progress_saved_at","v":{"s":"Saved on this device at {time}"}},{"k":"progress_saved_short","v":{"s":"Saved"}},{"k":"progress_not_saved","v":{"s":"Progress is not saved"}},{"k":"progress_not_saved_short","v":{"s":"Not saved"}},{"k":"progress_not_saved_title","v":{"s":"Progress could not be saved"}},{"k":"progress_not_saved_hint","v":{"s":"Device storage is unavailable. Retry the save, preserve the lesson as a project backup, or keep Guided Mode open."}},{"k":"retry_progress_save","v":{"s":"Retry save"}},{"k":"save_project_backup","v":{"s":"Save project backup"}},{"k":"progress_not_saved_exit","v":{"s":"Guided Mode closed, but this device could not save your progress."}},{"k":"resume_later_unsaved_hint","v":{"s":"Progress is not saved; review before exiting"}},{"k":"keep_guided_open","v":{"s":"Keep Guided Mode open"}},{"k":"exit_without_saving","v":{"s":"Exit without saving"}},{"k":"just_now","v":{"s":"just now"}},{"k":"choose_steps","v":{"s":"Choose which steps to include"}},{"k":"customize","v":{"s":"Choose which steps to include"}},{"k":"detail_tablist","v":{"s":"Section detail"}},{"k":"example_consistent","v":{"s":"The same lesson runs through every step."}},{"k":"example_heading","v":{"s":"Example output"}},{"k":"example_lesson","v":{"s":"Photosynthesis"}},{"k":"full_lesson_scroll","v":{"s":"Worked lesson steps"}},{"k":"full_lesson_sub","v":{"s":"One consistent example — a photosynthesis passage — carried through every Guided step, end to end."}},{"k":"full_lesson_title","v":{"s":"The full worked lesson"}},{"k":"io_how","v":{"s":"How it works"}},{"k":"io_inputs","v":{"s":"Inputs"}},{"k":"io_outputs","v":{"s":"Outputs"}},{"k":"io_verified","v":{"s":"Verified against the actual tool behavior in AlloFlow."}},{"k":"listen","v":{"s":"Read this aloud"}},{"k":"listen_short","v":{"s":"Listen"}},{"k":"next_step","v":{"s":"Next step →"}},{"k":"progress_label","v":{"s":"Guided tour progress"}},{"k":"recap_count","v":{"s":"You created {n} resources:"}},{"k":"recap_empty","v":{"s":"Generate resources from the tools, then download your full pack below."}},{"k":"recap_hub","v":{"s":"Looking for more? The Learning Hub has StoryForge, PoetTree, and LitLab."}},{"k":"recap_more","v":{"s":"more"}},{"k":"recap_title","v":{"s":"Your lesson is built"}},{"k":"summary_label","v":{"s":"Guided Mode completion summary"}},{"k":"summary_completed","v":{"s":"Completed"}},{"k":"summary_skipped","v":{"s":"Skipped"}},{"k":"summary_resources","v":{"s":"Resources"}},{"k":"required","v":{"s":"(required)"}},{"k":"resume_version_skip","v":{"s":"This saved tutorial progress is from a newer version and was not restored."}},{"k":"resumed","v":{"s":"Resumed your guided tutorial."}},{"k":"stop","v":{"s":"Stop"}},{"k":"stop_listening","v":{"s":"Stop reading aloud"}},{"k":"tab_example","v":{"s":"Worked example"}},{"k":"tab_how","v":{"s":"How it works"}},{"k":"try_example","v":{"s":"New here? Try it with an example passage"}},{"k":"view_full_lesson","v":{"s":"View the full worked lesson"}},{"k":"skip_step","v":{"s":"Skip this step"}},{"k":"started_from_header","v":{"s":"Guided Mode started."}},{"k":"expand","v":{"s":"Expand Guided Mode"}},{"k":"collapse","v":{"s":"Collapse Guided Mode"}},{"k":"complete","v":{"s":"Complete!"}},{"k":"estimate_label","v":{"s":"Step estimate"}},{"k":"estimated_remaining","v":{"s":"About {minutes} min remaining"}},{"k":"lesson_brief_title","v":{"s":"Lesson brief"}},{"k":"lesson_brief_active","v":{"s":"Active plan"}},{"k":"lesson_brief_goal","v":{"s":"Goal"}},{"k":"lesson_brief_why_step","v":{"s":"Why this step"}},{"k":"lesson_brief_why_path","v":{"s":"Why this path"}},{"k":"kind_manual","v":{"s":"Manual"}},{"k":"kind_interactive","v":{"s":"Interactive"}},{"k":"kind_image_ai","v":{"s":"Image AI"}},{"k":"kind_export","v":{"s":"Export"}},{"k":"kind_ai_generation","v":{"s":"AI generation"}},{"k":"jump_to_step","v":{"s":"Jump to step"}},{"k":"advanced_navigation","v":{"s":"Browse or jump to another step"}},{"k":"phase_progress","v":{"s":"Guided phase progress"}},{"k":"jump_confirm_title","v":{"s":"Jump forward?"}},{"k":"jump_confirm_text","v":{"s":"{count} unfinished steps will be marked skipped."}},{"k":"jump_and_skip","v":{"s":"Jump and mark skipped"}},{"k":"choose_goal_title","v":{"s":"What would you like to build?"}},{"k":"choose_goal_hint","v":{"s":"Choose a focused lesson path, or keep all available steps."}},{"k":"ai_plan_button","v":{"s":"Plan with AI"}},{"k":"ai_plan_button_hint","v":{"s":"Describe your lesson goals, timing, learners, and delivery needs. Review the proposed path before applying it."}},{"k":"ai_plan_or_presets","v":{"s":"Or choose a ready-made path"}},{"k":"ai_plan_title","v":{"s":"Plan your Guided experience with AI"}},{"k":"ai_plan_intro","v":{"s":"Tell AlloFlow what you are teaching, what students should accomplish, and any timing or delivery constraints."}},{"k":"ai_plan_studio_title","v":{"s":"Guided Planning Studio"}},{"k":"ai_plan_studio_intro","v":{"s":"Describe the lesson, customize the path, then review everything before applying it."}},{"k":"ai_plan_stage_navigation","v":{"s":"Planning stages"}},{"k":"ai_plan_stage_describe","v":{"s":"Describe"}},{"k":"ai_plan_stage_customize","v":{"s":"Customize"}},{"k":"ai_plan_stage_review","v":{"s":"Review & start"}},{"k":"ai_plan_describe_title","v":{"s":"What are you planning?"}},{"k":"ai_plan_describe_hint","v":{"s":"Include the goal, learners, available time, evidence of learning, and delivery needs you already know."}},{"k":"ai_plan_saved_toggle","v":{"s":"Saved plans ({count})"}},{"k":"ai_plan_continue_customize","v":{"s":"Continue to customize"}},{"k":"ai_plan_back_describe","v":{"s":"Back to description"}},{"k":"ai_plan_continue_review","v":{"s":"Review plan"}},{"k":"ai_plan_review_ready_title","v":{"s":"Review the complete path"}},{"k":"ai_plan_back_customize","v":{"s":"Back to customize"}},{"k":"ai_plan_draft_saving","v":{"s":"Saving private draft…"}},{"k":"ai_plan_draft_saved_at","v":{"s":"Draft saved at {time}"}},{"k":"ai_plan_just_now","v":{"s":"just now"}},{"k":"ai_plan_undo","v":{"s":"Undo last change"}},{"k":"ai_plan_restore_original","v":{"s":"Restore original"}},{"k":"ai_plan_edited_by_you","v":{"s":"Edited by you"}},{"k":"ai_plan_unsaved_title","v":{"s":"Keep this unfinished plan?"}},{"k":"ai_plan_unsaved_text","v":{"s":"Your work can be kept as a private draft on this device, or discarded without affecting saved plans."}},{"k":"ai_plan_keep_draft","v":{"s":"Keep draft and close"}},{"k":