ion"}},{"k":"recall_cue_described","v":{"s":"The picture shows: {desc}"}},{"k":"recall_cue_undescribed","v":{"s":"This concept is cued by a picture that has no text description."}},{"k":"recall_summary","v":{"s":"Named {first} of {total} first try."}},{"k":"recall_summary_detail","v":{"s":"{eventual} took another go · {revealed} shown · {points} points"}},{"k":"recall_framing","v":{"s":"Naming a concept from its picture is retrieval practice, which is what makes the images worth making. It is a study strategy, not a measure of ability."}},{"k":"recall_again","v":{"s":"Go again"}},{"k":"recall_exit","v":{"s":"Exit recall"}},{"k":"recall_unavailable","v":{"s":"The recall game could not load — try again."}},{"k":"furnish_framing","v":{"s":"Students can still make and refine art on any single concept by clicking it. Building the image yourself is where most of the memory benefit lives, so use this to seed a space rather than to replace their turn."}},{"k":"refine_placeholder","v":{"s":"Tell the AI what to change…"}},{"k":"refine_done","v":{"s":"✨ Refined!"}},{"k":"refine_failed","v":{"s":"Could not refine — try rephrasing."}},{"k":"arrange_tooltip","v":{"s":"Ask the AI to score every concept on the sequence, abstraction, and strand axes, then re-project the space"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"Reset arrangement"}},{"k":"reset_tooltip","v":{"s":"Discard the saved arrangement and return to the default layout"}},{"k":"fullscreen","v":{"s":"Fullscreen"}},{"k":"fullscreen_tooltip","v":{"s":"Open this concept space full screen"}},{"k":"empty_title","v":{"s":"Nothing to map yet"}},{"k":"empty_body","v":{"s":"Generate this organizer from a source text (or add sections in Edit text) and the concepts will appear here as an orbitable 3D space."}},{"k":"challenge_play","v":{"s":"Strand Challenge"}},{"k":"challenge_tooltip","v":{"s":"Practice: every concept falls off its strand — put each one back where it belongs"}},{"k":"challenge_hint","v":{"s":"🎯 Click a fallen concept, then give it 