ky. A Glossary would help support this text."}},{"k":"simplified_outline","v":{"s":"Visual learners might benefit from a Graphic Organizer of this content."}},{"k":"glossary_bingo","v":{"s":"You can turn these terms into word games like Bingo, Memory Match, Crosswords, or Word Search!"}},{"k":"glossary_memory","v":{"s":"Try the Memory Game to help students review."}},{"k":"glossary_visuals","v":{"s":"Visual icons help anchor these definitions. Try generating visuals."}},{"k":"quiz_presentation","v":{"s":"Use 'Presentation Mode' to project this quiz for the whole class."}},{"k":"quiz_autograder","v":{"s":"I can grade open-ended reflection answers with the Auto-Grader!"}},{"k":"quiz_rigor","v":{"s":"Want to ensure this quiz is rigorous? Run a Standard Audit."}},{"k":"adventure_sim","v":{"s":"Adventures allow students to apply what they've learned in a safe simulation."}},{"k":"adventure_inventory","v":{"s":"Check the 'Inventory' to see what items have been collected."}},{"k":"adventure_context","v":{"s":"Your adventure about {topic} gets richer with more resources — try adding a {suggestion}!"}},{"k":"adventure_context_fallback","v":{"s":"The more resources you generate, the richer the adventure context becomes."}},{"k":"timeline_drag","v":{"s":"Drag and drop events to reorder the sequence."}},{"k":"timeline_visualize","v":{"s":"This helps students visualize cause-and-effect relationships."}},{"k":"input_ready","v":{"s":"I'm ready! Paste a URL or topic to start building your lesson."}},{"k":"input_next","v":{"s":"You've built {count} resources on {topic}. How about a {suggestion} next?"}},{"k":"input_next_fallback","v":{"s":"What's next? Maybe a fun review game or a lesson plan?"}},{"k":"parent_bedtime","v":{"s":"Ask me to turn this text into a bedtime story!"}},{"k":"parent_adventure","v":{"s":"Try the Adventure Mode for a fun rainy-day activity."}},{"k":"parent_read_along","v":{"s":"Use 'Read Along' to practice reading together."}},{"k":"fallback_lesson_plan","v":{"s":"You have great resources. Synthesize them into a Lesson Plan?"}},{"k":"fallback_brainstorm","v":{"s":"Feeling stuck? Try chatting with me and toggle Auto-Complete to activate Blueprint Mode — I'll help you design your entire lesson!"}},{"k":"fallback_export","v":{"s":"You have {count} resources on {topic} — export them as a single PDF!"}},{"k":"fallback_export_fallback","v":{"s":"You can export all these resources as a single PDF packet."}},{"k":"fallback_guide","v":{"s":"Select 'Show Me' in the AI Guide if you get lost!"}},{"k":"student_simplified_definition","v":{"s":"Tap any unfamiliar word to see its meaning, then read the sentence again."}},{"k":"student_simplified_word","v":{"s":"Find '{word}' in the text. Read its sentence, check the meaning, and use the word in a new sentence of your own."}},{"k":"student_simplified_topic","v":{"s":"After each section about {topic}, pause and explain the most important idea without looking back."}},{"k":"student_simplified_summary","v":{"s":"After each section, pause and explain the main idea in your own words."}},{"k":"student_glossary_practice","v":{"s":"Pick one term, hide its meaning, and explain it in your own words before checking."}},{"k":"student_glossary_term","v":{"s":"Without looking at the definition, explain '{term}' in your own words and give an example."}},{"k":"student_glossary_pair","v":{"s":"Compare '{term1}' and '{term2}'. How are they connected, and how are they different?"}},{"k":"student_glossary_connection","v":{"s":"Choose two glossary terms and describe how they connect."}},{"k":"student_quiz_count","v":{"s":"This quiz has {count} questions. After every few questions, pause and check which idea needs another look."}},{"k":"student_quiz_reasoning","v":{"s":"Before you submit an answer, ask yourself: What evidence or steps support it?"}},{"k":"student_quiz_review","v":{"s":"If you miss a question, review the feedback and try explaining the answer a new way."}},{"k":"student_adventure_topic","v":{"s":"In this adventure about {topic}, use facts and clues from the learning material to guide your next move."}},{"k":"student_adventure_evidence","v":{"s":"Use clues from what you learned when you choose your next adventure action."}},{"k":"student_adventure_inventory","v":{"s":"Check your inventory before your next move; an item you collected may help."}},{"k":"student_timeline_count","v":{"s":"This timeline has {count} events. Look for the event that caused the biggest change and explain why."}},{"k":"student_timeline_sequence","v":{"s":"After ordering the events, explain why one event leads to the next."}},{"k":"student_math_count","v":{"s":"You have {count} math problems to practice. Show each step and check whether each answer is reasonable."}},{"k":"student_math_steps","v":{"s":"Show each step of your math thinking, then use estimation or the opposite operation to check your answer."}},{"k":"student_faq_count","v":{"s":"There are {count} questions here. Predict each answer before revealing it, then correct your explanation if needed."}},{"k":"student_faq_predict","v":{"s":"Try answering each question from memory before you reveal the answer."}},{"k":"student_outline_count","v":{"s":"This outline has {count} sections. Turn each section heading into a question and answer it from memory."}},{"k":"student_outline_checkpoint","v":{"s":"Use each outline heading as a checkpoint: pause and state the main idea before moving on."}},{"k":"student_concept_sort_counts","v":{"s":"Sort the {itemCount} items into {categoryCount} groups, and explain the rule you used for each placement."}},{"k":"student_concept_sort_reason","v":{"s":"As you sort each item, say why it belongs in that group and what would make another group incorrect."}},{"k":"student_scaffolds_count","v":{"s":"You have {count} writing supports. Pick the one that best matches your idea, then complete it with your own evidence."}},{"k":"student_scaffolds_own_idea","v":{"s":"Use a sentence starter to organize your thinking, but finish it with your own idea and evidence."}},{"k":"student_analysis_count","v":{"s":"The analysis identifies {count} key concepts. Choose one, explain it simply, and connect it to another concept."}},{"k":"student_analysis_question","v":{"s":"Choose one key idea from the analysis and turn it into a question you can answer from the source."}},{"k":"student_image_topic","v":{"s":"Study the visual about {topic}. Name one detail you notice and explain what that detail helps you understand."}},{"k":"student_image_notice","v":{"s":"Study the visual closely. Name one detail you notice, one idea it represents, and one question it raises."}},{"k":"student_recent_resource","v":{"s":"You have {count} learning activities. Reopen '{title}' and name one idea you remember before reviewing it."}},{"k":"student_input_choose","v":{"s":"Choose one saved activity to practice, and focus on one idea you want to understand better."}},{"k":"student_brainstorm_choose","v":{"s":"Choose one brainstorm idea that interests you, then explain how it connects to the topic and what you could do with it."}},{"k":"student_brainstorm_count","v":{"s":"Your brainstorm has {count} ideas. Compare two, then choose the one that best supports your learning goal."}},{"k":"student_persona_question","v":{"s":"Ask your interview partner one focused question, then record a detail from the answer that changes or strengthens your thinking."}},{"k":"student_persona_name","v":{"s":"Ask {name} a focused question, then use one specific detail from the answer in your notes."}},{"k":"student_dbq_evidence","v":{"s":"Choose a claim, find evidence in a document, and explain how that evidence supports your reasoning."}},{"k":"student_dbq_count","v":{"s":"You have {count} documents to investigate. Compare evidence from at least two before deciding which claim is strongest."}},{"k":"student_notes_recall","v":{"s":"After completing a notes section, cover it and write what you remember before checking for missing details."}},{"k":"student_notes_count","v":{"s":"Your note-taking resource has {count} sections. Pause after each one and write the main idea from memory."}},{"k":"student_anchor_chart_recall","v":{"s":"Use the anchor chart as a quick check: cover one part, explain it from memory, and then uncover it to verify."}},{"k":"student_anchor_chart_count","v":{"s":"This anchor chart has {count} sections. Explain how the sections connect instead of memorizing them separately."}},{"k":"student_study_guide_plan","v":{"s":"Turn each study-guide heading into a question, answer it from memory, and mark the sections that need another look."}},{"k":"student_study_guide_topic","v":{"s":"Use the study guide about {topic} to plan short practice rounds. Start with the section you can explain least confidently."}},{"k":"student_alignment_next_step","v":{"s":"Use the skill-check feedback to choose one specific next step, then practice that skill with evidence from your work."}},{"k":"student_alignment_topic","v":{"s":"Use the skill check for {topic} to choose one strength to keep and one skill to practice next."}},{"k":"student_word_sounds_practice","v":{"s":"Say the word slowly, listen for each sound, and then blend the sounds together before checking."}},{"k":"student_word_sounds_count","v":{"s":"You have {count} words to practice. Sort them by a sound or spelling pattern you notice."}},{"k":"student_directions_check","v":{"s":"Before starting, restate the directions in your own words and identify what a finished response must include."}},{"k":"student_directions_count","v":{"s":"These directions have {count} steps. Complete them in order and check off each step as you finish."}},{"k":"student_video_transcript","v":{"s":"Pause after a transcript section and summarize what was said before continuing."}},{"k":"student_video_notice","v":{"s":"Before replaying, predict what detail you should watch or listen for, then check your prediction."}},{"k":"student_reading_book","v":{"s":"After each page or section, pause to name the most important event, idea, or detail."}},{"k":"student_reading_book_count","v":{"s":"This reading has {count} sections or pages. Stop at each break and make a quick prediction or summary."}},{"k":"student_reading_set","v":{"s":"Compare two texts in the reading set: identify one idea they share and one way they differ."}},{"k":"student_reading_set_count","v":{"s":"This set has {count} readings. Track one idea across the set and notice how each text adds to it."}},{"k":"student_aac_board","v":{"s":"Explore where important words are on the AAC board, then practice building one complete message."}},{"k":"student_aac_count","v":{"s":"This AAC board has {count} choices. Find the words you need first, then build and review your message."}},{"k":"student_fluency_strategy","v":{"s":"Choose a math strategy before entering the fluency maze, and notice which facts still need a slower check."}},{"k":"student_manipulative_explain","v":{"s":"Move the model, then explain what each piece represents and how the model matches the math."}},{"k":"student_assessment_evidence","v":{"s":"For each assessment response, include the evidence, steps, or reasoning that shows how you know."}},{"k":"student_explore_reflect","v":{"s":"After the challenge, name the strategy that helped most and one change you would make on another try."}},{"k":"student_creative_assignment_plan","v":{"s":"Review the assignment goal, choose one idea to develop, and make a short plan before creating."}},{"k":"student_creative_submission_review","v":{"s":"Review your submission once for meaning and once for craft. Keep your own voice while improving one specific part."}},{"k":"student_lingua_practice","v":{"s":"Practice the target language in a complete phrase, then vary one word to create a new meaning."}},{"k":"student_lingua_reflect","v":{"s":"Review your language record and choose one word, sound, or sentence pattern to practice again."}},{"k":"student_guide_choice","v":{"s":"Choose the support that matches your current barrier, try it, and then decide whether it helped."}},{"k":"student_simulation_predict","v":{"s":"Before changing a simulation control, predict what will happen. Change one variable at a time and use the result to revise your thinking."}},{"k":"student_simulation_topic","v":{"s":"In the simulation about {topic}, change one variable at a time and explain whether the result matched your prediction."}},{"k":"student_fluency_probe_reflect","v":{"s":"Use the math-practice result to identify one fact pattern or strategy to strengthen before your next attempt."}},{"k":"student_fluency_record_reflect","v":{"s":"Use your reading-practice record to notice one strength and choose one word or reading pattern to practice again."}},{"k":"student_extra_goal","v":{"s":"Name your goal before you continue: what should you be able to explain, solve, or create when you finish?"}},{"k":"student_extra_reflect","v":{"s":"Pause and notice what changed in your thinking. What do you understand now that was less clear before?"}},{"k":"student_extra_retrieve","v":{"s":"Look away from the resource and recall the most important idea. Then check what you remembered and what you missed."}},{"k":"student_extra_question","v":{"s":"Write one how or why question about the current idea, then use the resource to build an answer."}},{"k":"student_extra_connect","v":{"s":"Connect this idea to something you already know, another subject, or an example from life."}},{"k":"student_extra_evidence","v":{"s":"Point to the exact detail, step, example, or source that supports your thinking."}},{"k":"student_extra_check","v":{"s":"Check your work a different way. If both methods agree, explain why that increases your confidence."}},{"k":"student_extra_transfer","v":{"s":"Imagine a new situation where this idea would matter. Explain what you would do and why."}},{"k":"student_extra_compare","v":{"s":"Choose two examples or ideas. Name one meaningful similarity and one meaningful difference."}},{"k":"student_extra_cause","v":{"s":"Trace one cause-and-effect chain. Explain what happened, why it happened, and what followed."}},{"k":"student_extra_explain","v":{"s":"Explain your thinking as if you were helping a classmate who is seeing the idea for the first time."}},{"k":"student_extra_sequence","v":{"s":"Put the key steps or ideas in order, then explain why that order makes sense."}},{"k":"student_extra_create","v":{"s":"Make a new example that follows the same idea, pattern, or rule, and explain how it fits."}},{"k":"student_extra_observe","v":{"s":"Notice three specific details before deciding what they mean. Separate what you see from what you infer."}},{"k":"student_extra_choice","v":{"s":"Choose the option that best matches your goal, and name the reason for your choice."}},{"k":"student_extra_organize","v":{"s":"Group your notes into what is important, what supports it, and what you still need to ask."}},{"k":"student_extra_feedback","v":{"s":"Turn the feedback into one small action you can try now, then check whether your work improves."}},{"k":"student_extra_predict","v":{"s":"Make a prediction before the next step. Use the result to confirm or revise your explanation."}},{"k":"student_extra_pattern","v":{"s":"Look for a repeated sound, structure, relationship, or rule. Test whether it works with another example."}},{"k":"student_extra_plan","v":{"s":"Break the task into a first step, a check-in point, and a final review before you begin."}},{"k":"student_extra_summarize","v":{"s":"Summarize this part in one sentence without copying. Add the detail that best supports your summary."}},{"k":"student_extra_rehearse","v":{"s":"Practice once slowly for accuracy, then again smoothly. Notice the one part that still needs attention."}},{"k":"student_extra_strategy","v":{"s":"Name the strategy you are using and why it fits this task. Switch strategies if the evidence shows it is not helping."}},{"k":"student_extra_revise","v":{"s":"Choose one part to improve. Make a purposeful change, then explain how it makes your work clearer or stronger."}},{"k":"educator_sequence_resources","v":{"s":"Sequence resources by purpose: activate prior knowledge, model the thinking, provide guided practice, and end with transfer."}},{"k":"educator_check_prior_knowledge","v":{"s":"Begin with a low-stakes prompt that reveals what learners already know and which assumptions need attention."}},{"k":"educator_monitor_access","v":{"s":"Check whether language, layout, audio, and navigation create barriers before interpreting a learner response as lack of understanding."}},{"k":"educator_plan_retrieval","v":{"s":"Add a brief retrieval pause before learners reopen the resource; recall first, then review and correct."}},{"k":"educator_surface_misconceptions","v":{"s":"Use one carefully chosen distractor or contrasting example to surface the misconception you most need to see."}},{"k":"educator_require_evidence","v":{"s":"Ask learners to attach evidence, steps, or a source detail to their response so the reasoning is visible."}},{"k":"educator_plan_transfer","v":{"s":"Plan a new context where learners must apply the same idea without copying the original example."}},{"k":"educator_student_voice","v":{"s":"Preserve learner ownership by offering meaningful choices while keeping the success criteria consistent."}},{"k":"educator_model_thinking","v":{"s":"Model one worked example aloud, including a decision point, a self-check, and how you recover from an error."}},{"k":"educator_plan_discussion","v":{"s":"Plan a prompt that invites more than one defensible response, followed by a request to compare reasoning."}},{"k":"educator_fade_scaffold","v":{"s":"Decide how the support will fade: model it, use it together, then invite learners to try without it."}},{"k":"educator_accessibility_check","v":{"s":"Check that the essential information is available without relying on color, sound, fine motor control, or a single reading format."}},{"k":"educator_offer_choice","v":{"s":"Offer two or three valid ways to engage or respond, and make the learning goal clear across every option."}},{"k":"educator_feedback_loop","v":{"s":"Keep feedback actionable: name the current strength, one next move, and a quick chance to apply it."}},{"k":"educator_compare_perspectives","v":{"s":"Invite learners to compare sources or perspectives, then identify what evidence would resolve a disagreement."}},{"k":"educator_quiz_count","v":{"s":"This quiz has {count} questions. Check the balance of recall, application, and explanation before assigning it."}},{"k":"educator_glossary_count","v":{"s":"This glossary has {count} terms. Identify the essential few, then plan repeated use in speaking, reading, and writing."}},{"k":"educator_document_count","v":{"s":"This inquiry includes {count} documents. Check source variety, readability, and whether the set supports more than one defensible claim."}},{"k":"educator_section_count","v":{"s":"{resource} has {count} sections. Mark where learners should pause, retrieve, discuss, or show understanding."}},{"k":"educator_sort_counts","v":{"s":"This sort has {itemCount} items and {categoryCount} categories. Include at least one productive boundary case that requires justification."}},{"k":"educator_reading_set_count","v":{"s":"This set has {count} readings. Give each text a purpose and plan how learners will synthesize across the set."}},{"k":"educator_directions_count","v":{"s":"These directions have {count} steps. Check that each step uses observable language and that success criteria are easy to find."}},{"k":"educator_fluency_accuracy","v":{"s":"This practice record shows {accuracy}% accuracy. Look at error patterns and strategy use before choosing the next practice target."}},{"k":"educator_recent_resource","v":{"s":"You have {count} resources; the latest is {title}. Decide what instructional purpose it serves and what should come immediately before and after it."}},{"k":"educator_topic_lens","v":{"s":"For {topic}, identify the one understanding learners should carry into the next task and the evidence that would demonstrate it."}},{"k":"educator_fallback_review","v":{"s":"Review the current resource through a learner lens: where might directions, vocabulary, or response demands create unnecessary friction?"}},{"k":"educator_fallback_sequence","v":{"s":"Choose the next resource because of the learning move it enables, not simply because it is another format."}},{"k":"student_fluency_accuracy","v":{"s":"This attempt shows {accuracy}% accuracy. Notice the pattern in what was difficult, choose one focused strategy, and try again when ready."}},{"k":"student_creative_vocab_count","v":{"s":"Your creative task includes {count} focus words. Choose the ones that fit your meaning naturally instead of forcing every word into your work."}},{"k":"student_lingua_language","v":{"s":"Your practice is in {language}. Build one useful message, then change a word or phrase to express a new meaning."}},{"k":"student_story_word_count","v":{"s":"Your draft has {count} words. Find one place where a precise detail, stronger transition, or clearer sentence would help the reader most."}},{"k":"student_submission_line_count","v":{"s":"Your submission has {count} lines. Rehearse or reread them once for meaning and once for sound, rhythm, or expression."}},{"k":"student_lingua_record_context","v":{"s":"Your {language} record includes {count} practice activities. Choose one pattern that improved and one that needs another short practice round."}},{"k":"student_lingua_record_language","v":{"s":"Review your {language} learning record. Choose one phrase you can use confidently and one pattern to practice next."}},{"k":"educator_aac_count","v":{"s":"This AAC board contains {count} choices. Check motor access, core-word availability, navigation depth, and whether learners can say more than the expected answer."}},{"k":"educator_creative_vocab_count","v":{"s":"This creative task includes {count} focus words. Decide which are essential, how they will be modeled, and how natural use will be recognized."}},{"k":"educator_lingua_language","v":{"s":"This activity targets {language}. Check the accuracy of the model, cultural context, meaningful repetition, and opportunities for original communication."}},{"k":"educator_story_word_count","v":{"s":"This submission contains {count} words. Respond to meaning and organization first, then select one high-leverage craft move for revision."}},{"k":"educator_submission_line_count","v":{"s":"This submission contains {count} lines. Review meaning, evidence, and performance choices before offering one focused next step."}},{"k":"educator_lingua_record_context","v":{"s":"Review this {language} record for patterns across attempts, then choose one achievable language target and a quick opportunity to reuse it."}},{"k":"student_fallback_explain","v":{"s":"Try explaining the current idea in your own words. If you get stuck, ask me for a hint."}},{"k":"student_fallback_progress","v":{"s":"Pause and name one thing you understand now and one question you still have."}},{"k":"intro_greeting","v":{"s":"Click me to adjust my voice settings."}},{"k":"student_profiles_tip","v":{"s":"Use the {icon} Student Profiles feature to save settings (Grade, Language, Interests) for different groups."}},{"k":"pro_tip_label","v":{"s":"Pro Tip:"}}],"id":328}},{"k":"bot_events","v":{"o":[{"k":"intro_greeting","v":{"s":"Click me to adjust my voice settings. I'll chime in with helpful tips as you go!"}},{"k":"text_generated","v":{"s":"Your adapted text on {topic} is ready! Try clicking a word to see its definition, or explore tools like Glossary or Quiz to deepen understanding."}},{"k":"flashcards_created","v":{"s":"Flashcards created! You can export them to Quizlet, print them, or try the Memory Game."}},{"k":"quiz_generated","v":{"s":"Quiz ready! Use Presentation Mode for the class, or try the Auto-Grader for open responses."}},{"k":"glossary_generated","v":{"s":"Glossary complete! Try the word games — Bingo, Memory Match, Crosswords, Word Search, and more!"}},{"k":"adventure_started","v":{"s":"Your adventure begins! Type your action below, or use the choice buttons to decide what happens next."}},{"k":"adventure_scene","v":{"s":"What will you do? Every choice shapes your story!"}},{"k":"analysis_complete","v":{"s":"Analysis complete! I found some vocabulary and key concepts worth exploring."}},{"k":"first_resource","v":{"s":"Great start! Your first resource is saved. Generate more to build a complete lesson."}},{"k":"lesson_plan_ready","v":{"s":"Lesson plan ready! Review the activities and adjust timing as needed."}},{"k":"student_quiz_ready","v":{"s":"Your quiz is ready. Answer each question before checking feedback, and explain how you know."}},{"k":"student_quiz_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your quiz is ready with {count} questions. Answer each one before checking feedback, and explain how you know."}},{"k":"student_glossary_ready","v":{"s":"Your glossary is ready. Pick one key term and explain it in your own words before checking the meaning."}},{"k":"student_glossary_ready_term","v":{"s":"Your glossary has {count} key terms. Start with '{term}': explain it in your own words before checking the definition."}},{"k":"student_simplified_ready","v":{"s":"Your easier-to-read version is ready. Tap an unfamiliar word for help, then summarize each section in your own words."}},{"k":"student_simplified_ready_level","v":{"s":"Your text is ready at the {level} level. Read one section at a time, then explain its main idea in your own words."}},{"k":"student_adventure_ready","v":{"s":"Your adventure is ready. Use what you learned and the clues in the story to choose your next move."}},{"k":"student_adventure_ready_topic","v":{"s":"Your adventure about {topic} is ready. Use what you learned and clues from the story to choose your next move."}},{"k":"student_analysis_ready","v":{"s":"Your content guide is ready. Start with the key concepts and mark one idea you want to understand better."}},{"k":"student_analysis_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your content guide identifies {count} key concepts. Choose one to explain simply, then connect it to another idea."}},{"k":"student_scaffolds_ready","v":{"s":"Your writing supports are ready. Choose a sentence starter that matches what you want to say, then finish it with your own idea."}},{"k":"student_scaffolds_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your {count} writing supports are ready. Choose the starter that matches your idea, then finish it with your own evidence."}},{"k":"student_faq_ready","v":{"s":"Your question set is ready. Try answering each question before you reveal the answer."}},{"k":"student_faq_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your {count} questions are ready. Predict each answer before revealing it, then revise your explanation if needed."}},{"k":"student_outline_ready","v":{"s":"Your outline is ready. Use each section as a checkpoint and say the main idea before moving on."}},{"k":"student_outline_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your outline has {count} sections. Turn each heading into a question and answer it from memory."}},{"k":"student_brainstorm_ready","v":{"s":"Your brainstorm is ready. Choose one idea that interests you and explain how it connects to the topic."}},{"k":"student_brainstorm_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your brainstorm has {count} ideas. Choose one that interests you and explain how it connects to the topic."}},{"k":"student_concept_sort_ready","v":{"s":"Your concept sort is ready. As you place each item, explain why it belongs in that group."}},{"k":"student_concept_sort_ready_counts","v":{"s":"Your concept sort has {itemCount} items and {categoryCount} groups. Explain the rule behind every placement."}},{"k":"student_math_ready","v":{"s":"Your math practice is ready. Show your steps, then check whether your answer makes sense."}},{"k":"student_math_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your {count} math problems are ready. Show your steps, then check whether each answer makes sense."}},{"k":"student_persona_ready","v":{"s":"Your interview partner is ready. Ask a question, then use details from the answer in your notes."}},{"k":"student_persona_ready_name","v":{"s":"{name} is ready for your interview. Ask a focused question, then use details from the answer in your notes."}},{"k":"student_alignment_ready","v":{"s":"Your skill check is ready. Start with one area and use the feedback to choose what to practice next."}},{"k":"student_timeline_ready","v":{"s":"Your timeline is ready. Put the events in order, then explain how one event leads to the next."}},{"k":"student_timeline_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your timeline has {count} events. Put them in order, then explain how one event leads to the next."}},{"k":"student_study_guide_ready","v":{"s":"Your study guide is ready. Start with one section, cover it, and explain the main idea from memory."}},{"k":"student_image_ready","v":{"s":"Your visual is ready. Study the details and name one thing the image helps you understand."}},{"k":"student_image_ready_topic","v":{"s":"Your visual about {topic} is ready. Study one detail and explain what it helps you understand."}},{"k":"student_resource_ready","v":{"s":"Your learning activity is ready. Try it, then pause to explain what you learned in your own words."}},{"k":"student_dbq_ready","v":{"s":"Your document investigation is ready. Compare evidence from more than one source before making a claim."}},{"k":"student_dbq_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your document investigation has {count} sources. Compare evidence from at least two before making a claim."}},{"k":"student_notes_ready","v":{"s":"Your guided notes are ready. Pause after each section and record the main idea in your own words."}},{"k":"student_notes_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your guided notes have {count} sections. Pause after each one and record the main idea from memory."}},{"k":"student_anchor_chart_ready","v":{"s":"Your anchor chart is ready. Study how its parts connect, then explain one section without looking."}},{"k":"student_anchor_chart_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your anchor chart has {count} sections. Study how they connect, then explain one without looking."}},{"k":"student_word_sounds_ready","v":{"s":"Your word-sounds practice is ready. Say each word slowly, listen for its parts, and blend the sounds again."}},{"k":"student_word_sounds_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your word-sounds practice has {count} words. Look for a sound or spelling pattern they share."}},{"k":"student_directions_ready","v":{"s":"Your directions are ready. Restate the task in your own words before you begin."}},{"k":"student_directions_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your directions have {count} steps. Restate each step in your own words and check them off as you work."}},{"k":"student_video_ready","v":{"s":"Your video resource is ready. Choose one detail to watch or listen for, then summarize what you learned."}},{"k":"student_reading_ready","v":{"s":"Your reading is ready. Pause at natural breaks to predict, question, or summarize."}},{"k":"student_reading_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your reading has {count} sections or pages. Pause at each break to predict or summarize."}},{"k":"student_reading_set_ready","v":{"s":"Your reading set is ready. Compare the texts for one shared idea and one important difference."}},{"k":"student_reading_set_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your set has {count} readings. Track one idea across them and notice what each text adds."}},{"k":"student_aac_ready","v":{"s":"Your AAC board is ready. Find the words you need, build a complete message, and review it before sharing."}},{"k":"student_fluency_ready","v":{"s":"Your fluency challenge is ready. Choose a strategy, work accurately, and notice which facts need more practice."}},{"k":"student_manipulative_ready","v":{"s":"Your math model is ready. Use the pieces, then explain how the model represents the math."}},{"k":"student_assessment_ready","v":{"s":"Your assessment is ready. Show evidence, steps, or reasoning for each response."}},{"k":"student_explore_ready","v":{"s":"Your exploration challenge is ready. Try a strategy, observe what happens, and reflect before trying again."}},{"k":"student_creative_assignment_ready","v":{"s":"Your creative assignment is ready. Review the goal and make a short plan before you begin."}},{"k":"student_creative_submission_ready","v":{"s":"Your creative submission is ready to review. Check meaning first, then improve one craft choice while keeping your voice."}},{"k":"student_lingua_ready","v":{"s":"Your language activity is ready. Practice complete phrases and change one part at a time to create new meanings."}},{"k":"student_lingua_record_ready","v":{"s":"Your language learning record is ready. Choose one word, sound, or sentence pattern to practice again."}},{"k":"student_simulation_ready","v":{"s":"Your interactive simulation is ready. Make a prediction, change one variable, and explain what the result shows."}},{"k":"student_fluency_probe_ready","v":{"s":"Your math-practice result is ready. Notice which fact pattern or strategy should be your next focus."}},{"k":"student_fluency_record_ready","v":{"s":"Your reading-practice record is ready. Notice one strength and choose one word or reading pattern to practice again."}},{"k":"student_fluency_record_ready_accuracy","v":{"s":"Your reading-practice record shows {accuracy}% word accuracy for this attempt. Choose one reading pattern to practice, then try again."}},{"k":"student_guide_ready","v":{"s":"Your learning-support guide is ready. Choose one suggestion that matches your current barrier, try it, and decide whether it helped."}},{"k":"educator_assessment_ready","v":{"s":"Your assessment resource is ready. Review cognitive demand, accessibility, and what evidence each response will reveal."}},{"k":"educator_vocabulary_ready","v":{"s":"Your vocabulary resource is ready. Prioritize essential terms and plan repeated use across multiple contexts."}},{"k":"educator_text_ready","v":{"s":"Your adapted text is ready. Compare it with the learning goal and confirm that access improved without removing essential meaning."}},{"k":"educator_transfer_ready","v":{"s":"Your application activity is ready. Confirm that learners must use the target idea in a new context and can explain their choices."}},{"k":"educator_analysis_ready","v":{"s":"Your content analysis is ready. Use it to anticipate vocabulary barriers, prerequisite knowledge, and likely misconceptions."}},{"k":"educator_scaffold_ready","v":{"s":"Your writing supports are ready. Match each scaffold to a barrier and decide how learners can move toward independent expression."}},{"k":"educator_questions_ready","v":{"s":"Your question resource is ready. Use it for prediction, retrieval, or discussion rather than revealing every answer immediately."}},{"k":"educator_organizer_ready","v":{"s":"Your organizer is ready. Add purposeful checkpoints where learners retrieve, connect, or explain ideas."}},{"k":"educator_choice_ready","v":{"s":"Your choice resource is ready. Check that options differ in pathway, not in the rigor of the learning goal."}},{"k":"educator_sort_ready","v":{"s":"Your concept sort is ready. Include a boundary case and ask learners to justify the rule behind each placement."}},{"k":"educator_math_ready","v":{"s":"Your math resource is ready. Make strategy use visible and include a reasonableness check, not only final answers."}},{"k":"educator_perspective_ready","v":{"s":"Your perspective activity is ready. Prepare follow-up questions that require evidence and comparison across viewpoints."}},{"k":"educator_alignment_ready","v":{"s":"Your alignment review is ready. Convert one finding into a specific revision to task demand, evidence, or support."}},{"k":"educator_sequence_ready","v":{"s":"Your sequence resource is ready. Ask learners to explain causality and significance, not only chronological order."}},{"k":"educator_plan_ready","v":{"s":"Your instructional plan is ready. Check pacing, transitions, learner choices, and where you will gather evidence of understanding."}},{"k":"educator_media_ready","v":{"s":"Your media resource is ready. Add an observation purpose, accessible alternatives, and a prompt that requires interpretation."}},{"k":"educator_inquiry_ready","v":{"s":"Your source inquiry is ready. Check source variety and ask learners to connect claims, evidence, and reasoning."}},{"k":"educator_notes_ready","v":{"s":"Your guided notes are ready. Decide which information learners should record and which thinking they should generate themselves."}},{"k":"educator_anchor_ready","v":{"s":"Your anchor chart is ready. Plan when learners will help complete, reference, and eventually recreate it from memory."}},{"k":"educator_simulation_ready","v":{"s":"Your simulation is ready. Ask for a prediction, vary one factor at a time, and use the result to revise a model."}},{"k":"educator_language_ready","v":{"s":"Your language-practice resource is ready. Plan accurate modeling, meaningful repetition, and a chance to use the pattern in a new message."}},{"k":"educator_directions_ready","v":{"s":"Your directions are ready. Read them as a learner and check sequence, observable verbs, choice points, and success criteria."}},{"k":"educator_reading_ready","v":{"s":"Your reading resource is ready. Add a purpose for reading and brief pauses for prediction, retrieval, and synthesis."}},{"k":"educator_reading_set_ready","v":{"s":"Your reading set is ready. Give each text a role and plan how learners will compare and synthesize evidence."}},{"k":"educator_aac_ready","v":{"s":"Your AAC board is ready. Confirm that core language, needed topic words, navigation, and genuine communication choices are available."}},{"k":"educator_fluency_ready","v":{"s":"Your fluency resource is ready. Emphasize accuracy and strategy patterns before speed, then choose a focused next practice target."}},{"k":"educator_fluency_record_ready","v":{"s":"Your fluency record is ready. Review error patterns and self-corrections before selecting the next instructional move."}},{"k":"educator_model_ready","v":{"s":"Your interactive model is ready. Ask learners to connect each representation to the underlying concept and explain what changes."}},{"k":"educator_creative_ready","v":{"s":"Your creative assignment is ready. Check that learner choice, criteria, exemplars, and authentic purpose are all visible."}},{"k":"educator_submission_ready","v":{"s":"A learner submission is ready. Respond first to meaning and evidence, then offer one focused revision move that preserves the learner voice."}},{"k":"educator_support_ready","v":{"s":"Your learner-support guidance is ready. Match each suggestion to an observed barrier and plan how you will know whether it helped."}},{"k":"educator_resource_ready","v":{"s":"Your resource is ready. Clarify its instructional purpose, check accessibility, and decide what evidence of learning you will collect."}},{"k":"educator_quiz_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your {count}-question quiz is ready. Check the balance of recall, application, explanation, and accessible response options."}},{"k":"educator_quiz_ready_context","v":{"s":"Your quiz has {count} questions; {higherOrderCount} explicitly prompt analysis, evaluation, comparison, prediction, inference, or justification. Review the balance against your goal."}},{"k":"educator_glossary_ready_context","v":{"s":"Your glossary has {count} terms, including {complexCount} longer or multiword terms that may need extra modeling, examples, or repeated exposure."}},{"k":"educator_glossary_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your glossary contains {count} terms. Prioritize the essential few and plan repeated use across contexts."}},{"k":"educator_analysis_ready_counts","v":{"s":"The analysis identifies {conceptCount} concepts and {vocabularyCount} vocabulary terms. Use those findings to plan prerequisites and access supports."}},{"k":"educator_dbq_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your inquiry contains {count} sources. Check perspective, readability, and whether learners can build more than one defensible claim."}},{"k":"educator_sections_ready_count","v":{"s":"{resource} is ready with {count} sections. Add checkpoints for retrieval, discussion, and evidence of understanding."}},{"k":"educator_sort_ready_counts","v":{"s":"Your sort has {itemCount} items and {categoryCount} categories. Add a boundary case that makes learners justify the sorting rule."}},{"k":"educator_directions_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your directions contain {count} steps. Check observable verbs, sequence, choice points, and visible success criteria."}},{"k":"educator_reading_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your reading resource contains {count} sections or texts. Give each one a purpose and plan how learners will synthesize across them."}},{"k":"educator_fluency_ready_accuracy","v":{"s":"This practice record shows {accuracy}% accuracy. Review error patterns and strategy use before choosing the next target."}},{"k":"educator_resource_ready_topic","v":{"s":"{resource} for {topic} is ready. Clarify its purpose, check access, and decide what learner evidence you will collect."}},{"k":"student_aac_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your AAC board is ready with {count} choices. Find the words for the message you want to share, build it, and check that it says what you mean."}},{"k":"student_creative_assignment_ready_vocab","v":{"s":"Your creative assignment includes {count} focus words. Plan where a few can strengthen your meaning naturally."}},{"k":"student_story_ready_words","v":{"s":"Your story draft has {count} words. Review one section for meaning, then improve the detail or transition that will help your reader most."}},{"k":"student_creative_submission_ready_lines","v":{"s":"Your creative submission has {count} lines. Review once for meaning and once for sound, rhythm, or expression."}},{"k":"student_lingua_ready_language","v":{"s":"Your {language} activity is ready. Practice one complete, useful message and then vary it to express a new meaning."}},{"k":"student_lingua_record_ready_context","v":{"s":"Your {language} learning record includes {count} practice activities. Choose one pattern to strengthen in your next short practice round."}},{"k":"student_lingua_record_ready_language","v":{"s":"Your {language} learning record is ready. Choose one phrase you can use confidently and one pattern to practice next."}},{"k":"educator_scaffold_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your resource includes {count} writing supports. Match each one to a specific barrier and identify when learners can try without it."}},{"k":"educator_brainstorm_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your brainstorm includes {count} activity ideas. Compare them for learning value, access, time, and authentic learner choice before selecting one."}},{"k":"educator_math_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your math resource includes {count} problems. Check strategy variety, representation, cognitive demand, and where learners must explain reasoning."}},{"k":"educator_timeline_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your timeline includes {count} events. Add prompts about causality, significance, and perspective so the task goes beyond ordering."}},{"k":"educator_aac_ready_count","v":{"s":"Your AAC board contains {count} choices. Check motor access, core language, navigation, and whether it supports genuine messages beyond the task."}},{"k":"educator_creative_ready_vocab","v":{"s":"Your creative assignment includes {count} focus words. Prioritize natural, meaningful use and make the success criteria visible without narrowing learner voice."}},{"k":"educator_story_submission_ready_words","v":{"s":"This story submission contains {count} words. Respond to meaning and organization first, then offer one high-leverage revision move."}},{"k":"educator_submission_ready_lines","v":{"s":"This creative submission contains {count} lines. Review meaning, evidence, and expressive choices before choosing one focused feedback move."}},{"k":"educator_lingua_ready_language","v":{"s":"Your {language} resource is ready. Check model accuracy, cultural context, meaningful repetition, and opportunities for original communication."}},{"k":"student_lingua_ready_context","v":{"s":"Your {language} activity includes {count} focus words. Practice them in complete messages, then change the messages to express your own meaning."}},{"k":"educator_lingua_ready_context","v":{"s":"Your {language} resource includes {count} focus words. Check model accuracy and plan repeated, meaningful use in original communication."}},{"k":"image_generated","v":{"s":"Image generated! You can refine it or download it for your materials."}},{"k":"idle_fallback","v":{"s":"Need ideas? I'm happy to suggest what to do next!"}},{"k":"rigor_feedback_aligned","v":{"s":"Great job! This text is fully aligned with the grade level standards."}},{"k":"rigor_feedback_partial","v":{"s":"This is close, but some elements are missing or slightly off-target."}},{"k":"rigor_feedback_misaligned","v":{"s":"Heads up! This text doesn't quite meet the rigor requirements for this grade level."}},{"k":"feedback_lesson_generic","v":{"s":"Crafting a UDL-optimized lesson for {grade}."}},{"k":"feedback_audit_start","v":{"s":"Analyzing this text against {standard}..."}},{"k":"feedback_complexity_match","v":{"s":"The reading level fits your {grade} grade target perfectly."}},{"k":"feedback_complexity_mismatch","v":{"s":"This text might be a bit complex for {grade} grade students."}},{"k":"feedback_safety_clean","v":{"s":"Safety scan complete. No PII or sensitive content detected."}},{"k":"feedback_safety_flagged","v":{"s":"I've flagged some potential safety issues. Please review the highlighted sections."}},{"k":"feedback_analysis_result","v":{"s":"Analysis complete. I've detected a reading level around {level}."}},{"k":"feedback_export_complete","v":{"s":"Export complete! Your files are ready for the classroom."}},{"k":"feedback_persona_start","v":{"s":"Connecting you with {name} now! This character will respond in-character based on your source material. Have a great conversation!"}},{"k":"feedback_adventure_start","v":{"s":"Your personalized adventure story is loading! Get ready for an interactive narrative where your choices shape the outcome."}},{"k":"feedback_error_apology","v":{"s":"I hit a snag trying to generate that. Could you try asking again? I'm ready now."}},{"k":"brainstorming_start","v":{"s":"Let's brainstorm some ideas!"}}],"id":329}},{"k":"help_mode","v":{"o":[{"k":"header_rerun_wizard_title","v":{"s":"Start & setup"}},{"k":"header_quickstart_setup_title","v":{"s":"Setup Wizard"}},{"k":"header_guided_mode_start_title","v":{"s":"Start or resume Guided Mode"}},{"k":"tool_directions_title","v":{"s":"Assignment Directions"}},{"k":"header_export_title","v":{"s":"Export and Document Builder"}},{"k":"export_pdf_title","v":{"s":"PDF preview"}},{"k":"export_worksheet_title","v":{"s":"Printable worksheet"}},{"k":"export_html_title","v":{"s":"HTML lesson"}},{"k":"export_slides_title","v":{"s":"Presentation slides"}},{"k":"export_qti_title","v":{"s":"Assessment export for an LMS"}},{"k":"export_ims_title","v":{"s":"Lesson package for an LMS"}},{"k":"tool_universal_settings_title","v":{"s":"Shared generation settings"}},{"k":"guided_workflow_title","v":{"s":"Guided lesson workflow"}},{"k":"guided_path_choice_title","v":{"s":"Choose a Guided path"}},{"k":"guided_ai_plan_title","v":{"s":"Plan with AI"}},{"k":"guided_customize_title","v":{"s":"Customize included steps"}},{"k":"guided_next_step_title","v":{"s":"Continue to the next step"}},{"k":"guided_back_step_title","v":{"s":"Return to the previous step"}},{"k":"guided_skip_step_title","v":{"s":"Skip an unfinished step"}},{"k":"guided_step_help_title","v":{"s":"About this step"}},{"k":"guided_resume_later_title","v":{"s":"Resume later"}},{"k":"guided_resume_card_title","v":{"s":"Return to your lesson"}},{"k":"guided_collapse_title","v":{"s":"Collapse or expand Guided Mode"}},{"k":"guided_example_source_title","v":{"s":"Try a sample passage"}},{"k":"guided_progress_storage_title","v":{"s":"Progress saved on this device"}},{"k":"guided_resources_title","v":{"s":"Resources from this lesson"}},{"k":"guided_plan_navigation_title","v":{"s":"Plan and navigation"}},{"k":"guided_phase_review_title","v":{"s":"Review this phase"}},{"k":"guided_document_builder_title","v":{"s":"Package this Guided lesson"}},{"k":"guided_homework_share_title","v":{"s":"Create a homework share"}},{"k":"guided_live_session_title","v":{"s":"Set up a live session"}},{"k":"guided_learner_preview_title","v":{"s":"Preview the learner link"}},{"k":"guided_readiness_title","v":{"s":"Review classroom readiness"}},{"k":"guided_finish_title","v":{"s":"Finish Guided Mode"}},{"k":"directions_composer_title","v":{"s":"Prepare student directions"}},{"k":"directions_title_title","v":{"s":"Directions title"}},{"k":"directions_body_title","v":{"s":"Steps for learners"}},{"k":"directions_due_title","v":{"s":"Due label"}},{"k":"directions_draft_title","v":{"s":"Draft directions from the lesson"}},{"k":"directions_add_pack_title","v":{"s":"Add reviewed directions to the pack"}},{"k":"doc_builder_document_title","v":{"s":"Review the document"}},{"k":"doc_builder_format_title","v":{"s":"Choose an output format"}},{"k":"doc_builder_export_action_title","v":{"s":"Create the selected output"}},{"k":"activate","v":{"s":"Turn on Help Mode to learn about any UI element. Click on buttons, panels, or tools to see detailed explanations."}},{"k":"deactivate","v":{"s":"Turn off Help Mode and return to normal interaction. All tooltips and spotlights will be dismissed."}},{"k":"wizard_tone_select","v":{"s":"Choose how the generated content is written • informative, narrative, persuasive, humorous, or procedural. This adjusts vocabulary, sentence structure, and engagement style to match your instructional goals."}},{"k":"wizard_tone_select_title","v":{"s":"Writing Tone"}},{"k":"wizard_length_select","v":{"s":"Set the approximate word count for generated content. Choose from short (200 words) for quick reads to deep (2000 words) for comprehensive coverage. Longer texts allow more examples and detail."}},{"k":"wizard_length_select_title","v":{"s":"Content Length"}},{"k":"wizard_level_select","v":{"s":"Override the grade level for this specific generation. Content complexity, vocabulary, and sentence length are automatically calibrated to your selection."}},{"k":"wizard_level_select_title","v":{"s":"Reading Level"}},{"k":"wizard_dok_select","v":{"s":"Set Webb's Depth of Knowledge level. Level 1 (recall) uses simple fact-based content. Level 4 (extended thinking) creates complex texts requiring synthesis and analysis."}},{"k":"wizard_dok_select_title","v":{"s":"Depth of Knowledge"}},{"k":"wizard_format_select","v":{"s":"Choose the output format for generated content • standard text, dialogue script, news report, podcast script, social media thread, poetry, or narrative story. Each format has a unique structure."}},{"k":"wizard_format_select_title","v":{"s":"Output Format"}},{"k":"wizard_lang_common_select","v":{"s":"Quickly add a common language for multilingual output. Generated content will include translated versions in all selected languages."}},{"k":"wizard_lang_common_select_title","v":{"s":"Quick Language Add"}},{"k":"wizard_lang_input","v":{"s":"Type a language name and press Enter or click + to add it for multilingual generation. Up to 4 languages can be added."}},{"k":"wizard_lang_input_title","v":{"s":"Language Input"}},{"k":"wizard_interest_input","v":{"s":"Add student interests (e.g., soccer, dinosaurs, space) to personalize generated content. The AI weaves these into examples and analogies for higher engagement."}},{"k":"wizard_interest_input_title","v":{"s":"Student Interests"}},{"k":"wizard_topic_input","v":{"s":"Enter the subject or topic for AI-generated source material. Be specific for better results (e.g., \"Photosynthesis in desert plants\" rather than just \"Plants\")."}},{"k":"wizard_topic_input_title","v":{"s":"Topic Input"}},{"k":"wizard_url_input","v":{"s":"Paste a URL to import web content as source material. The system fetches, cleans, and extracts the main article text."}},{"k":"wizard_url_input_title","v":{"s":"URL Input"}},{"k":"wizard_search_input","v":{"s":"Describe what you need and let the AI find relevant educational resources. Results include titles, descriptions, and direct links."}},{"k":"wizard_search_input_title","v":{"s":"Search Query"}},{"k":"onboarding_hint","v":{"s":"💡 Click <strong>?</strong> anytime for help!"}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_web_url_input","v":{"s":"Paste the address of the web page you want checked (for example https://yourdistrict.org/handbook), then click Fetch to pull its HTML so you can audit and remediate it."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_web_fetch_btn","v":{"s":"Downloads the page at the URL above and drops its HTML into the box below. If the site blocks fetching, paste the page source into the HTML box yourself."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_web_html_textarea","v":{"s":"The actual HTML being audited — either dropped in by Fetch or pasted by you. You can edit it here before running an audit (for example, remove a navigation bar you don't own)."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_web_audit_btn","v":{"s":"Scores the page for WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility using both an AI auditor and the axe-core engine (the same engine professional auditors use). Nothing is changed — use this when you just want to know how the page stands today."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_web_remediate_btn","v":{"s":"Scores the page, then rewrites the HTML to fix what it can (contrast, language tag, skip-link, landmarks) and gives you a downloadable accessible copy. Always re-check the output yourself before publishing."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_dropzone","v":{"s":"Drag PDF files from your desktop or downloads folder right onto this box to add them to the batch queue. Non-PDF files are ignored."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_browse_btn","v":{"s":"Opens your file picker to choose one or more PDFs. Use this if dragging files isn't easy (touch device, screen reader, low vision, or a Chromebook)."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_resume_btn","v":{"s":"Picks up your last batch where it left off — already-finished PDFs are kept and only the ones that didn't finish get re-run. Use this when a batch was cut short (closed tab, refresh, crash)."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_discard_btn","v":{"s":"Throws away the saved progress from your last interrupted batch — the banner goes away and cached results are deleted from your browser."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_clear_all_btn","v":{"s":"Removes every PDF from the queue so you can start over. Only available before you press Start Batch."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_row_retry_btn","v":{"s":"Re-runs just this one failed file without touching the rest of the batch. Hover the red X first to read why it failed — if it's structural (corrupted PDF, image-only scan), retrying won't help."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_row_remove_btn","v":{"s":"Removes this one PDF from the queue so the batch will skip it. Only available before the batch is running."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_stop_btn","v":{"s":"Asks the batch to stop after the file it's working on right now finishes. Already-completed PDFs stay done — you won't lose finished work, and you can resume the rest later."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_retry_all_failed_btn","v":{"s":"Re-queues every PDF that failed and re-runs them. Already-succeeded files are not touched. Worth one try if failures look like flaky network errors; don't keep retrying truly broken PDFs."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_start_btn","v":{"s":"Starts auditing and fixing every PDF in the queue. A confirmation appears first with an estimate of AI calls (and cost, on the self-hosted plan) so you can decide before kicking it off."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_download_zip_btn","v":{"s":"Downloads every successfully remediated PDF as a single ZIP file. Handy for handing a whole folder back to a teacher or district contact in one go."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_new_batch_btn","v":{"s":"Clears the finished batch so you can drop in a new set of PDFs. Any ZIP you already downloaded stays on your computer — this just resets the screen."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_batch_dashboard_btn","v":{"s":"Opens a printable compliance dashboard in a new tab — average score, how many PDFs hit 90+, the most common WCAG issues. Useful for sharing with an administrator or attaching to a Title II / 504 record."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_settings_panel","v":{"s":"Tuning knobs for the audit and remediation pipeline. Defaults are sensible — only change these if the standard run isn't giving you what you need (more thoroughness, lower cost, different stopping point)."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_audit_passes_slider","v":{"s":"How many independent AI auditors look at the PDF — they agree on real problems and disagree on noise, so more auditors mean fewer false alarms. 5 is the sweet spot; raise for high-stakes compliance docs, lower for quick checks."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_target_score_slider","v":{"s":"The score you want the remediated PDF to reach — this is an internal improvement target, not a WCAG pass threshold or conformance percentage. Pair with Auto-continue to let the pipeline keep working until the score is hit."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_max_fix_passes_slider","v":{"s":"How many automated fix-rounds the pipeline is allowed to run before stopping. 8 is the default; lower this to cap cost on a self-hosted plan, or set to 0 to skip auto-fix entirely (audit-only)."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_auto_continue_toggle","v":{"s":"When on, the pipeline keeps doing extra fix rounds (up to 3 more) until the Target Score is hit, then stops on its own. Turn off if you want exactly one pass and a single result to inspect."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_polish_passes_slider","v":{"s":"Extra cleanup rounds after the real accessibility fixes — tightens spacing, headings, visual polish. 0 skips, 2 is standard, 3 is for documents going to print or external audiences."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_branding_panel","v":{"s":"Optional — controls how the remediated PDF looks: brand colors and overall design style. Skip for the default accessible look, or expand if the document needs to match a school or district brand."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_brand_mode_auto_btn","v":{"s":"Pulls brand colors out of the PDF you uploaded so the remediated version looks like the original. Best default — keeps the document recognizable to staff and families."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_brand_mode_upload_input","v":{"s":"Upload a separate brand sheet, logo, or style guide (image or PDF) and the pipeline pulls colors and fonts from it. Useful when the original PDF is plain-looking but needs to match district branding."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_brand_mode_none_btn","v":{"s":"Skip brand colors entirely and use the built-in accessible palette. Pick this for generic worksheets, or when the original colors fail contrast and you don't need to preserve the look."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_results_tab_remediation_btn","v":{"s":"Show the audit results after AlloFlow remediated the PDF. Use this tab to see the improved score and which issues are now fixed."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_results_tab_original_btn","v":{"s":"Switch back to the audit of the original PDF before AlloFlow fixed anything. Useful for comparing before-vs-after scores side by side."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_results_score_badge","v":{"s":"Your PDF's overall accessibility score from 0 to 100. Green (80+) is close to WCAG AA, amber (50-79) needs work, red (<50) has major barriers for students using screen readers or assistive tech."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_results_reliability_details","v":{"s":"Expand to see how confident the AI auditors were in this score. Multiple AI passes run in parallel — tight agreement means the score is trustworthy, wide spread means review the individual issues yourself."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_results_score_breakdown_details","v":{"s":"Expand to see exactly how the score was calculated — how many checks ran, what was deducted per issue, and how the AI rubric and axe-core scores were averaged together. This is the transparency layer behind the headline number."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_results_score_how_ai_details","v":{"s":"Expand to see how harshly the AI grades each problem: bigger deductions for critical issues that block screen-reader users, smaller deductions for minor ones, and points recovered for checks that pass."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_results_score_how_axe_details","v":{"s":"Expand to see how the axe-core checker (the same engine professional accessibility auditors use) scored your PDF, with the exact WCAG rule IDs that failed."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_results_issue_explain","v":{"s":"Click to read what this issue actually blocks for students and how the WCAG rule applies. Includes a link to the official WCAG explanation if you want to go deeper."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_results_image_failures_details","v":{"s":"Expand to see any images that were dropped during remediation. Each row offers a one-click Regenerate button so no figure is silently lost."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_results_image_regenerate_btn","v":{"s":"Recreates this missing image using AI based on its stored description. The new image lands directly back in the document — no manual upload needed."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_report_menu_btn","v":{"s":"Open the report menu to download an accessibility report in different formats — Adobe-style for compliance officers, formatted PDF for general sharing, JSON for research, or a signed trail for audit records."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_adobe_report_btn","v":{"s":"Download a report formatted like Adobe's Accessibility Checker, scored against PDF/UA-1 (the federal accessibility standard for PDFs). Best for sharing with compliance officers or attaching to a Title II / 504 filing."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_tierb_diff_view_btn","v":{"s":"Review the words that went missing during the last save before deciding whether to run a restoration pass. Read-only — nothing is changed until you choose to restore."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_tierb_rerun_restore_btn","v":{"s":"Splice the missing source words back into the document and rebuild the tagged PDF. Words that can't be safely placed end up in a Content Recovery section so nothing is lost — the residual count before and after is always shown so you can see if it helped."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_formatted_report_btn","v":{"s":"Open a printable before/after accessibility report in a new tab — click Save as PDF in the banner to keep a copy for your records or a parent meeting."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_html_report_btn","v":{"s":"Download the before/after report as an HTML file you can host on a website or edit. Content matches the printable PDF version."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_json_data_btn","v":{"s":"Export the raw audit numbers and rule-by-rule data as JSON. Use this when you want to analyze accessibility results in a spreadsheet, research notebook, or another tool."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_audit_trail_signed_btn","v":{"s":"Generate a self-verifying audit trail (an HTML file with a built-in Verify Integrity button that detects tampering). Good for compliance evidence — note it's a browser-side signature, not a legally-binding one."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_save_project_btn","v":{"s":"Saves your remediation work — accessible HTML, scores, settings, page-by-page progress — to a portable file. Re-open with Load Project to keep editing without re-running the AI."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_load_project_btn","v":{"s":"Re-open a project file you saved earlier. Brings back the remediated HTML, scores, and any page ranges already completed — picks up exactly where you left off."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_view_save_template_btn","v":{"s":"Save the document's accessible structure (heading outline, tables, lists, landmarks) as a reusable template. Use it in Document Builder to start new documents — IEPs, syllabi — already pre-structured for accessibility."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_alt_formats_summary","v":{"s":"Expand for alternative formats — ePub, electronic Braille, plain text, Markdown — for students who need a different file type than PDF or HTML."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_alt_formats_epub_btn","v":{"s":"Save the remediated document as an ePub file with table of contents and accessibility metadata. Works on Kindle, Apple Books, and most mobile readers — students can change font size, color, and reading speed."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_alt_formats_braille_btn","v":{"s":"Save a Grade-1 (uncontracted) Braille file that can be embossed on a Braille printer or sent to a refreshable Braille display. For Grade-2 contractions, hand the file to a TVI (teacher of students with visual impairments) for finishing."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_alt_formats_text_btn","v":{"s":"Save a plain .txt file with all formatting stripped out — easiest format for screen readers, large-print conversion, or pasting into another tool."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_alt_formats_markdown_btn","v":{"s":"Save the document as Markdown — drops cleanly into Canvas, Schoology, or D2L pages, Google Docs (via paste), wikis, and GitHub-style notes without losing headings or links."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_alt_formats_daisy_btn","v":{"s":"Save a DAISY 3 full-text talking-book package. DAISY readers (common in special education) add their own speech, braille, or large print with full navigation. Text-only here — for synced read-aloud, use Read-along ebook."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_alt_formats_readalong_btn","v":{"s":"Build a read-along ebook (EPUB3 Media Overlays): each paragraph is narrated with text-to-speech and synced to the text so words highlight as they're spoken. One voice call per section, so it can take a few minutes."}},{"k":"pdf_audit_alt_formats_odt_btn","v":{"s":"Save an OpenDocument Text (.odt) file — native to LibreOffice and Google Docs (Word opens it too). Use it when your school isn't all-Microsoft but you still want an editable document with structure intact."}},{"k":"tool_anchor_chart","v":{"s":"Anchor Chart"}},{"k":"tool_note_taking","v":{"s":"Note-Taking Templates"}},{"k":"tool_memory_aid","v":{"s":"Memory Aid Studio"}},{"k":"tool_applied_challenge","v":{"s":"Applied Challenge Studio"}}],"id":330}},{"k":"groups","v":{"o":[{"k":"title","v":{"s":"Differentiation Groups"}},{"k":"modal_title","v":{"s":"Manage Groups & Resources"}},{"k":"modal_subtitle","v":{"s":"Create groups, assign differentiated resources, and manage your roster."}},{"k":"manage_button","v":{"s":"Manage Groups & Resources"}},{"k":"manage_button_desc","v":{"s":"Create groups and assign differentiated content."}},{"k":"create_group","v":{"s":"Create a New Group"}},{"k":"new_group_placeholder","v":{"s":"New Group Name"}},{"k":"add_button","v":{"s":"Add"}},{"k":"remove_button","v":{"s":"REMOVE"}},{"k":"resource_label","v":{"s":"Resource: The currently loaded or generated learning resource that tools will analyze and adapt."}},{"k":"assign_resource_label","v":{"s":"Assigned Resource: The specific content or activity assigned to a student or group for completion."}},{"k":"assign_resource_placeholder","v":{"s":"Select or search for a resource to assign to this group. Resources include lessons, quizzes, and activities."}},{"k":"default_resource","v":{"s":"Default (Same as Class)"}},{"k":"no_groups","v":{"s":"No groups created yet."}},{"k":"roster_title","v":{"s":"Student Roster & Assignment"}},{"k":"roster_assignment","v":{"s":"Assign Students to Groups"}},{"k":"active_groups","v":{"s":"Active Groups"}},{"k":"main_class","v":{"s":"Main Class"}},{"k":"return_main","v":{"s":"Return to Main Class"}},{"k":"move_to","v":{"s":"Move to..."}},{"k":"unassigned","v":{"s":"Unassigned"}},{"k":"waiting_for_students","v":{"s":"Waiting for students to join..."}},{"k":"resource_library","v":{"s":"Resource Library: Browse and manage all your saved lessons, materials, and generated content in one organized location."}},{"k":"resource_library_hint","v":{"s":"Use the group dropdowns below to assign resources to groups."}},{"k":"done_button","v":{"s":"Done"}},{"k":"created","v":{"s":"Group created successfully!"}},{"k":"deleted","v":{"s":"Group deleted."}},{"k":"drag_to_reorder","v":{"s":"Drag to reorder"}},{"k":"language_default","v":{"s":"English (Default)"}},{"k":"language_label","v":{"s":"Language"}},{"k":"language_tooltip","v":{"s":"Students see quizzes in this language"}},{"k":"wizard_step_codename","v":{"s":"Pick Your Codename!"}},{"k":"wizard_step_preferences","v":{"s":"How Do You Learn Best?"}},{"k":"wizard_preferences_sub","v":{"s":"These help your teacher personalize your experience. All optional!"}},{"k":"wizard_home_language","v":{"s":"What language do you speak at home?"}},{"k":"wizard_reading_comfort","v":{"s":"How do you like to read?"}},{"k":"wizard_tts_preference","v":{"s":"How do you like to hear text?"}},{"k":"wizard_visual_support","v":{"s":"Do pictures help you learn?"}},{"k":"wizard_next","v":{"s":"Next"}},{"k":"wizard_back","v":{"s":"Back"}},{"k":"reading_level_label","v":{"s":"Reading Level"}},{"k":"reading_level_tooltip","v":{"s":"Set the target reading level for adapted text in this group"}},{"k":"visual_density_label","v":{"s":"Visuals"}},{"k":"visual_density_tooltip","v":{"s":"How much visual support students in this group receive"}},{"k":"visuals_minimal","v":{"s":"Minimal"}},{"k":"visuals_normal","v":{"s":"Normal"}},{"k":"visuals_high","v":{"s":"High (More images)"}},{"k":"tts_speed_label","v":{"s":"TTS Speed"}},{"k":"tts_speed_tooltip","v":{"s":"Text-to-speech playback speed for students in this group"}},{"k":"karaoke_label","v":{"s":"Karaoke Mode"}},{"k":"karaoke_tooltip","v":{"s":"Auto-enable word highlighting during read-aloud for this group"}},{"k":"class_default","v":{"s":"Class Default"}},{"k":"communication_mode_label","v":{"s":"Communication"}},{"k":"communication_mode_tooltip","v":{"s":"Communication modality for students in this group"}},{"k":"comm_verbal","v":{"s":"Verbal"}},{"k":"comm_limited","v":{"s":"Limited Verbal"}},{"k":"comm_aac","v":{"s":"AAC/Visual"}},{"k":"no_resources","v":{"s":"No resources in this session"}},{"k":"resources_reordered","v":{"s":"Resources reordered"}},{"k":"waiting_students","v":{"s":"Waiting for students to join..."}},{"k":"pushed","v":{"s":"Pushed"}},{"k":"pushing","v":{"s":"Pushing…"}},{"k":"resource_count","v":{"s":"({count} items)"}},{"k":"move_earlier","v":{"s":"Earlier"}},{"k":"move_later","v":{"s":"Later"}},{"k":"reorder_aria","v":{"s":"Reorder {title}"}},{"k":"move_earlier_aria","v":{"s":"Move {title} earlier"}},{"k":"move_later_aria","v":{"s":"Move {title} later"}},{"k":"untitled_resource","v":{"s":"resource"}}],"id":331}},{"k":"roster","v":{"o":[{"k":"title","v":{"s":"Class Roster Key"}},{"k":"subtitle","v":{"s":"Organize student groups with differentiated profiles for instruction"}},{"k":"import","v":{"s":"Import JSON"}},{"k":"export","v":{"s":"Export JSON"}},{"k":"sync_session","v":{"s":"Sync to Live Session"}},{"k":"class_name","v":{"s":"Class Name"}},{"k":"new_group_placeholder","v":{"s":"New group name..."}},{"k":"add_group","v":{"s":"Add"}},{"k":"delete_group","v":{"s":"Delete Group"}},{"k":"manage_students","v":{"s":"Manage Students"}},{"k":"student_codename","v":{"s":"Student codename..."}},{"k":"add_student","v":{"s":"Add"}},{"k":"unassigned","v":{"s":"Unassigned"}},{"k":"unassigned_students","v":{"s":"Unassigned Students"}},{"k":"no_students","v":{"s":"No students assigned"}},{"k":"students_in_group","v":{"s":"Students"}},{"k":"apply_to_generator","v":{"s":"Apply to Generator"}},{"k":"applied","v":{"s":"Applied settings to generator"}},{"k":"synced","v":{"s":"Groups synced to live session"}},{"k":"sync_error","v":{"s":"Could not sync roster to session"}},{"k":"auto_assigned","v":{"s":"Auto-assigned student(s) to groups"}},{"k":"grade","v":{"s":"Grade"}},{"k":"language","v":{"s":"Language"}},{"k":"reading","v":{"s":"Reading Lvl"}},{"k":"interests","v":{"s":"Interests"}},{"k":"dok","v":{"s":"DOK Level"}},{"k":"tts_speed","v":{"s":"TTS Speed"}},{"k":"karaoke","v":{"s":"Karaoke"}},{"k":"simplify","v":{"s":"Simplify"}},{"k":"custom","v":{"s":"Custom Instr."}},{"k":"batch_generate","v":{"s":"Generate for All Groups"}},{"k":"generating_for_group","v":{"s":"Generating for group..."}},{"k":"batch_complete","v":{"s":"Generated differentiated versions for all groups!"}},{"k":"batch_failed","v":{"s":"Batch generation failed"}},{"k":"batch_config_title","v":{"s":"Differentiate by Group"}},{"k":"batch_config_subtitle","v":{"s":"Choose which resources to generate for each group"}},{"k":"resource_types","v":{"s":"Resource Types"}},{"k":"type_adapted_text","v":{"s":"Adapted Text"}},{"k":"type_adapted_desc","v":{"s":"Reading adapted to each group's grade & language"}},{"k":"type_glossary","v":{"s":"Glossary"}},{"k":"type_glossary_desc","v":{"s":"Key terms with definitions"}},{"k":"type_quiz","v":{"s":"Quiz"}},{"k":"type_quiz_desc","v":{"s":"Comprehension check questions"}},{"k":"type_frames","v":{"s":"Sentence Frames"}},{"k":"type_frames_desc","v":{"s":"Writing scaffolds matched to proficiency level"}},{"k":"type_brainstorm","v":{"s":"Brainstorm"}},{"k":"type_brainstorm_desc","v":{"s":"Discussion prompts tuned to group interests"}},{"k":"type_faq","v":{"s":"FAQ"}},{"k":"type_faq_desc","v":{"s":"Anticipated questions at each reading level"}},{"k":"type_outline","v":{"s":"Outline"}},{"k":"type_outline_desc","v":{"s":"Content structure adapted to grade level"}},{"k":"type_adventure","v":{"s":"Adventure"}},{"k":"type_adventure_desc","v":{"s":"Choose-your-own-adventure opening scene at group level"}},{"k":"type_concept_sort","v":{"s":"Concept Sort"}},{"k":"type_concept_sort_desc","v":{"s":"Categorization activity scaled to grade complexity"}},{"k":"type_image","v":{"s":"Visual"}},{"k":"type_image_desc","v":{"s":"AI-generated visual incorporating group interests & language"}},{"k":"type_timeline","v":{"s":"Sequence Builder"}},{"k":"type_timeline_desc","v":{"s":"Sequencing activity adapted to grade level"}},{"k":"full_pack","v":{"s":"Full Resource Pack • Select All"}},{"k":"deselect_all","v":{"s":"↩ Deselect All"}},{"k":"estimate","v":{"s":"Estimate"}},{"k":"api_calls","v":{"s":"API calls"}},{"k":"start_batch","v":{"s":"Generate"}},{"k":"no_groups_to_generate","v":{"s":"Add groups to your roster key first"}},{"k":"bridge_title","v":{"s":"Message from your teacher"}},{"k":"bridge_play_en","v":{"s":"Play English"}},{"k":"bridge_play_translated","v":{"s":"Play Translation"}},{"k":"bridge_save_terms","v":{"s":"Save Terms"}},{"k":"bridge_read_again","v":{"s":"Read Again"}},{"k":"bridge_close","v":{"s":"Close"}},{"k":"bridge_english","v":{"s":"English"}},{"k":"bridge_karaoke_on","v":{"s":"Karaoke highlighting active"}},{"k":"bridge_test","v":{"s":"Test Bridge"}},{"k":"bridge_send_title","v":{"s":"Bridge • Send to Students"}},{"k":"bridge_send_placeholder","v":{"s":"Type a concept, sentence, or instructions..."}},{"k":"bridge_send_mode_explain","v":{"s":"Explain"}},{"k":"bridge_send_mode_translate","v":{"s":"Translate"}},{"k":"bridge_send_mode_visual","v":{"s":"Visual + Explain"}},{"k":"bridge_send_btn","v":{"s":"Send to Class"}},{"k":"bridge_send_sending","v":{"s":"Generating..."}},{"k":"bridge_send_target_all","v":{"s":"All Groups"}},{"k":"bridge_send_success","v":{"s":"Bridge message sent!"}},{"k":"bridge_send_no_session","v":{"s":"Start a session to send to students"}},{"k":"bridge_receiving","v":{"s":"Receiving message from teacher..."}},{"k":"bridge_from_teacher","v":{"s":"From your teacher"}},{"k":"bridge_generating","v":{"s":"Creating your personalized version..."}},{"k":"bridge_projection","v":{"s":"Projection Mode"}},{"k":"bridge_exit_projection","v":{"s":"Exit Projection"}},{"k":"bridge_offline_info","v":{"s":"No live session — preview on this device only"}},{"k":"bridge_term_saved","v":{"s":"Saved \"{term}\" to glossary"}},{"k":"bridge_term_save_failed","v":{"s":"Failed to save term"}},{"k":"bridge_save_term","v":{"s":"Save to glossary"}},{"k":"bridge_saving_terms","v":{"s":"Saving {count} terms to glossary..."}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_title","v":{"s":"Face-to-Face Translation"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_ferpa","v":{"s":"Private: never saved or synced. Translation is processed by a secure AI service."}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_both_speak","v":{"s":"Both sides speak or type in their own language"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_ready","v":{"s":"Ready for conversation"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_ready_desc","v":{"s":"Press the microphone or type to begin"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_end","v":{"s":"End"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_translating","v":{"s":"Translating..."}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_translate_failed","v":{"s":"Translation failed"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_type_or_speak","v":{"s":"Type or speak..."}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_type_in","v":{"s":"Type in {lang}..."}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_local_only","v":{"s":"Not saved"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_messages","v":{"s":"messages"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_tts_auto","v":{"s":"TTS auto-plays"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_mic_speak","v":{"s":"Hold mic to speak"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_enter_send","v":{"s":"Enter to send"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_person_a","v":{"s":"Person A"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_person_b","v":{"s":"Person B"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_no_speech","v":{"s":"Speech recognition not supported"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_custom_lang","v":{"s":"Custom language..."}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_custom_placeholder","v":{"s":"e.g. Yoruba, Tigrinya, Dari..."}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_thread_label","v":{"s":"Conversation"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_pick_lang","v":{"s":"Type the custom language name first"}},{"k":"bridge_phrases_title","v":{"s":"Quick phrases"}},{"k":"bridge_phrases_hint","v":{"s":"(tap to edit, then Enter to send)"}},{"k":"bridge_ai_placeholder","v":{"s":"Ask the AI: how do I say..., words for..., explain simply..."}},{"k":"bridge_ai_btn","v":{"s":"Ask AI"}},{"k":"bridge_ai_helper","v":{"s":"AI helper"}},{"k":"bridge_ai_thinking","v":{"s":"Thinking..."}},{"k":"bridge_ai_unavailable","v":{"s":"AI unavailable right now"}},{"k":"bridge_export","v":{"s":"Export the conversation"}},{"k":"bridge_export_short","v":{"s":"Export"}},{"k":"bridge_exported","v":{"s":"Conversation copied to clipboard"}},{"k":"bridge_downloaded","v":{"s":"Conversation downloaded"}},{"k":"bridge_no_convo","v":{"s":"Nothing to export yet"}},{"k":"bridge_all_saved","v":{"s":"All terms saved to glossary!"}},{"k":"bridge_terms_saved","v":{"s":"✅ All Saved"}},{"k":"fullpack_group_target","v":{"s":"Target Group"}},{"k":"fullpack_group_current","v":{"s":"Current Settings"}},{"k":"fullpack_group_all","v":{"s":"All Groups"}},{"k":"fullpack_group_tooltip","v":{"s":"Generate for a specific group or all groups"}},{"k":"strip_title","v":{"s":"Class Groups"}},{"k":"strip_empty","v":{"s":"No class roster yet"}},{"k":"strip_create","v":{"s":"Create one"}},{"k":"emojis_label","v":{"s":"Use Emojis"}},{"k":"format_standard","v":{"s":"Standard Text"}},{"k":"format_bullets","v":{"s":"Bullet Points"}},{"k":"format_outline","v":{"s":"Outline"}},{"k":"bridge_mode_btn","v":{"s":"Bridge Mode"}},{"k":"display_name_placeholder","v":{"s":"Enter display name..."}},{"k":"assign_group","v":{"s":"Assign group"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_custom_lang_a","v":{"s":"Custom language for Person A"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_custom_lang_b","v":{"s":"Custom language for Person B"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_person_a_input","v":{"s":"Person A: type or speak…"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_person_a_language","v":{"s":"Person A language"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_person_b_input","v":{"s":"Person B: type or speak…"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_person_b_language","v":{"s":"Person B language"}},{"k":"group_name","v":{"s":"Group name"}},{"k":"submissions_active","v":{"s":"Submissions On"}},{"k":"setup_submissions","v":{"s":"Set up offline submissions"}},{"k":"import_submissions","v":{"s":"Import submissions"}},{"k":"set_group_color","v":{"s":"Set group color"}},{"k":"new_group_color","v":{"s":"New group color"}},{"k":"bridge_exit_fullscreen","v":{"s":"Exit full screen"}},{"k":"bridge_f2f_ferpa_ondevice","v":{"s":"Private: translated on this device — nothing is sent out."}},{"k":"bridge_fullscreen","v":{"s":"Full screen"}},{"k":"bridge_gen_btn","v":{"s":"Generate"}},{"k":"bridge_gen_label","v":{"s":"Generate custom phrases"}},{"k":"bridge_gen_loading","v":{"s":"Generating…"}},{"k":"bridge_gen_placeholder","v":{"s":"e.g. reassure a parent their child had a hard morning"}},{"k":"bridge_gen_results","v":{"s":"Generated — tap to edit and send"}},{"k":"bridge_ondevice_enable","v":{"s":"Translate on this device (private)"}},{"k":"bridge_ondevice_failed","v":{"s":"Could not load on-device translation; using the secure service."}},{"k":"bridge_ondevice_hint","v":{"s":"Download a small model so this language pair translates on your device, with nothing sent out"}},{"k":"bridge_ondevice_loading","v":{"s":"Loading on-device translation…"}},{"k":"bridge_ondevice_pair_na","v":{"s":"On-device translation isn't available for this language pair yet; using the secure service."}},{"k":"bridge_ondevice_ready","v":{"s":"On-device translation on — this language pair now stays on your device."}},{"k":"bridge_phrase_edit_hint","v":{"s":"Tap to edit, then press Enter to send"}},{"k":"seating_chart","v":{"s":"Seating Chart"}}],"id":332}},{"k":"adventure","v":{"o":[{"k":"title","v":{"s":"Adventure Mode"}},{"k":"resume","v":{"s":"Resume Previous Adventure"}},{"k":"new_game","v":{"s":"New Game"}},{"k":"start","v":{"s":"Start Adventure"}},{"k":"view_standard","v":{"s":"Standard View"}},{"k":"view_immersive","v":{"s":"Reading view"}},{"k":"locked_status","v":{"s":"Locked"}},{"k":"earn","v":{"s":"Earn"}},{"k":"to_unlock","v":{"s":"to unlock."}},{"k":"enter_immersive","v":{"s":"Open reading view"}},{"k":"exit_immersive","v":{"s":"Return to standard view"}},{"k":"show_ui","v":{"s":"Show UI"}},{"k":"hide_ui","v":{"s":"Hide UI"}},{"k":"sequel_prompt","v":{"s":"Adventure Complete! Continue above or..."}},{"k":"start_sequel","v":{"s":"Continue the story"}},{"k":"inventory_fallback_desc","v":{"s":"A useful item found during your adventure. Use it wisely!"}},{"k":"toasts","v":{"o":[{"k":"state_restored","v":{"s":"Adventure state restored."}},{"k":"teacher_sync_warning","v":{"s":"Teacher View Only (Students not synced)"}},{"k":"options_broadcast","v":{"s":"Options updated and broadcast to class."}},{"k":"key_item_usage","v":{"s":"{item} is a Key Item used via story choices."}},{"k":"rewind_limit","v":{"s":"Cannot rewind further back!"}},{"k":"rewind_success","v":{"s":"Time rewinds... You have a second chance."}},{"k":"item_used","v":{"s":"Used {item}"}},{"k":"broadcast_error","v":{"s":"Failed to broadcast adventure update."}},{"k":"options_broadcast_success","v":{"s":"Options broadcast to students!"}}],"id":334}},{"k":"defaults","v":{"o":[{"k":"key_item_desc","v":{"s":"A key item used in story choices."}},{"k":"energy_desc","v":{"s":"Restores energy."}}],"id":335}},{"k":"shop","v":{"s":"Adventure Shop"}},{"k":"shop_desc","v":{"s":"Spend your hard-earned gold!"}},{"k":"global_xp","v":{"s":"Global XP"}},{"k":"xp_earn_tip","v":{"s":"Gold is automatically granted based on your Global XP."}},{"k":"buy_now","v":{"s":"Buy Now"}},{"k":"no_gold","v":{"s":"Not Enough Gold"}},{"k":"inventory","v":{"s":"Inventory"}},{"k":"log","v":{"s":"Log"}},{"k":"level","v":{"s":"Lvl"}},{"k":"xp","v":{"s":"XP"}},{"k":"energy","v":{"s":"Energy"}},{"k":"gold","v":{"s":"Gold"}},{"k":"locked","v":{"s":"Locked"}},{"k":"unlocked","v":{"s":"Unlocked"}},{"k":"unlock_at","v":{"s":"Earn {xp} more XP to unlock."}},{"k":"game_over","v":{"s":"Adventure Complete!"}},{"k":"storybook","v":{"s":"Export Storybook PDF"}},{"k":"storybook_writing","v":{"s":"Writing Storybook..."}},{"k":"storybook_locked","v":{"s":"Earn {needed} more XP to unlock Storybook."}},{"k":"export_options","v":{"s":"Export Options: Choose how to download or share your work. Options include PDF, HTML, Slides, QTI packages, and more."}},{"k":"storybook_export_description","v":{"s":"Would you like to include the scene illustrations in your storybook? Including images creates a richer experience but increases file size."}},{"k":"source_input","v":{"s":"Paste or type your source text here. This is the foundation for all generated content - lesson plans, quizzes, glossaries, and more. Longer, well-organized text produces better results."}},{"k":"source_generate_btn","v":{"s":"Generate adapted content from your source material. The AI will analyze your text and create educational resources based on your settings."}},{"k":"source_generate_button","v":{"s":"Generate adapted content from your source material. The AI will analyze your text and create educational resources based on your settings."}},{"k":"source_link_btn","v":{"s":"Import content from a web URL. The system will fetch and extract text from the linked page for use as source material."}},{"k":"source_upload_btn","v":{"s":"Upload a file (PDF, DOCX, or TXT) to use as source material. The text will be extracted and ready for content generation."}},{"k":"source_settings_length","v":{"s":"Set your preferred output length. Shorter outputs are more concise; longer outputs include more detail and examples."}},{"k":"source_settings_instructions","v":{"s":"Add custom instructions to guide the AI. For example: 'Focus on vocabulary for English learners' or 'Include real-world examples.'"}},{"k":"source_verify_checkbox","v":{"s":"Enable fact-checking to verify claims in the source material. The AI will flag potentially inaccurate or outdated information."}},{"k":"wizard_topic_input","v":{"s":"Enter the topic or subject area for your lesson. Be specific for best results (e.g., 'Photosynthesis in plants' vs just 'Science')."}},{"k":"wizard_grade_option","v":{"s":"Select the target grade level for your content. This affects vocabulary complexity, reading level, and conceptual depth."}},{"k":"wizard_next_grade_btn","v":{"s":"Proceed to the next step in the wizard. You can always go back to previous steps to modify your choices."}},{"k":"wizard_prev_btn","v":{"s":"Go back to the previous wizard step to change your selections. Your progress is saved automatically."}},{"k":"wizard_skip_btn","v":{"s":"Skip this optional step and proceed with default settings. You can always customize these settings later."}},{"k":"wizard_complete_btn","v":{"s":"Complete the wizard and generate your content with the selected settings. This may take a few moments."}},{"k":"wizard_close_btn","v":{"s":"Close the wizard. If you've made progress, you'll be asked if you want to save your selections."}},{"k":"wizard_standard_select","v":{"s":"Select education standards to align your content with (Common Core, NGSS, state standards, etc.)."}},{"k":"wizard_search_input","v":{"s":"Search for specific standards by keyword or code (e.g., 'CCSS.ELA-LITERACY.RI.5.1' or 'main idea')."}},{"k":"wizard_search_btn","v":{"s":"Search the standards database for matching entries. Results can be added to your lesson alignment."}},{"k":"wizard_level_select","v":{"s":"Choose the complexity level for generated content (Basic, Intermediate, Advanced, or Mixed levels)."}},{"k":"wizard_format_select","v":{"s":"Select the output format for your content (Paragraph, Bullet Points, Numbered List, etc.)."}},{"k":"wizard_length_select","v":{"s":"Choose the approximate length of generated content (Brief, Standard, Detailed, or Comprehensive)."}},{"k":"wizard_dok_select","v":{"s":"Select the Depth of Knowledge level (DOK 1-4) to target appropriate cognitive complexity."}},{"k":"wizard_tone_select","v":{"s":"Choose the writing tone (Friendly, Academic, Conversational, or Formal) for generated content."}},{"k":"wizard_instructions_input","v":{"s":"Add custom instructions for the AI to follow. Be specific about what you want included or emphasized."}},{"k":"wizard_url_input","v":{"s":"Enter a webpage URL to import content from. The text will be extracted for use in the wizard."}},{"k":"wizard_url_fetch_btn","v":{"s":"Fetch and extract text content from the entered URL to use as source material."}},{"k":"wizard_verify_checkbox","v":{"s":"Enable fact-checking to verify accuracy of generated content against reliable sources."}},{"k":"quiz_generate_button","v":{"s":"Generate quiz questions based on your source material and settings. Customize question count and types first."}},{"k":"quiz_question_count","v":{"s":"Set how many questions to generate. More questions provide broader coverage but take longer to create."}},{"k":"quiz_mode_select","v":{"s":"Choose quiz mode: Multiple Choice, Fill-in-blank, Short Answer, or Mixed. Different modes assess different skills."}},{"k":"quiz_dok","v":{"s":"Select Depth of Knowledge level (1-4) to control cognitive complexity of questions."}},{"k":"quiz_custom_instructions","v":{"s":"Add specific requirements for quiz questions (e.g., 'Include questions about vocabulary' or 'Focus on cause and effect')."}},{"k":"quiz_start_question_btn","v":{"s":"Start the quiz presentation. Questions will display one at a time for whole-class or individual use."}},{"k":"quiz_next_question_btn","v":{"s":"Move to the next question in the quiz sequence. Students' previous answers are saved."}},{"k":"quiz_prev_question_btn","v":{"s":"Return to the previous question to review or change the answer."}},{"k":"quiz_reveal_btn","v":{"s":"Reveal the correct answer for the current question. Use for class discussion or answer review."}},{"k":"quiz_student_mode_header","v":{"s":"Student Quiz Mode is active. Students see questions one at a time and submit responses directly."}},{"k":"quiz_student_question","v":{"s":"Read the question carefully and select or type your answer. Click submit when ready."}},{"k":"quiz_student_answer_option","v":{"s":"Click to select this answer choice. You can change your selection before submitting."}},{"k":"quiz_student_overlay","v":{"s":"The quiz interface is ready for student responses. Share the class code for students to join."}},{"k":"adventure_difficulty","v":{"s":"Set adventure difficulty. Easier modes provide more hints; harder modes have greater challenges."}},{"k":"adventure_language","v":{"s":"Choose the language for your adventure story narration and interface."}},{"k":"adventure_input_mode","v":{"s":"Select how you respond: Choose from options or type free responses (depending on settings)."}},{"k":"adventure_free_response","v":{"s":"Free response mode is enabled. Type what you want your character to do or say."}},{"k":"tool_concept_sort","v":{"s":"Concept Sort: Create category sorting activities to help students organize and classify concepts."}},{"k":"tool_lesson_plan","v":{"s":"Lesson Planner: Generate comprehensive lesson plans with objectives, activities, and assessments."}},{"k":"tool_udl","v":{"s":"UDL Analysis: Analyze content for Universal Design for Learning principles and accessibility."}},{"k":"tool_wordsounds","v":{"s":"Word Sounds Studio: Phonics instruction with letter sounds, blending, and tracing activities."}},{"k":"chat_close","v":{"s":"Close the chat panel. Your conversation history is preserved for when you return."}},{"k":"chat_expand","v":{"s":"Expand the chat panel for more space to view conversation history and type longer messages."}},{"k":"chat_voice_mode","v":{"s":"Toggle voice input mode. When enabled, you can speak instead of typing your messages."}},{"k":"chat_auto_send","v":{"s":"Auto-send mode: Messages are sent automatically after you finish speaking or typing."}},{"k":"chat_show_me","v":{"s":"Show Me mode: Ask AlloBot to demonstrate features by highlighting elements on screen."}},{"k":"chat_save_advice_btn","v":{"s":"Save AlloBot's advice and suggestions to your hints collection for later reference."}},{"k":"glossary_search","v":{"s":"Search for specific terms in your glossary. Type a word to filter the list."}},{"k":"glossary_add_term","v":{"s":"Add a custom term to the glossary. Include the word and optionally a definition."}},{"k":"glossary_edit","v":{"s":"Edit this glossary term including definition, tier, images, and translations."}},{"k":"glossary_speak_term","v":{"s":"Hear this word pronounced aloud. Helpful for learning correct pronunciation."}},{"k":"glossary_standard_flashcards","v":{"s":"Generate traditional flashcards with term on front and definition on back."}},{"k":"glossary_language_flashcards","v":{"s":"Generate bilingual flashcards with translations in the selected language."}},{"k":"glossary_export_standard","v":{"s":"Export glossary as printable flashcard PDF or image files."}},{"k":"glossary_export_language","v":{"s":"Export bilingual glossary with translations for language learners."}},{"k":"glossary_memory_game","v":{"s":"Play a memory matching game to practice vocabulary. Match terms with definitions."}},{"k":"glossary_crossword","v":{"s":"Create a crossword puzzle from your glossary. Definitions as clues, terms as answers."}},{"k":"glossary_matching","v":{"s":"Generate a matching activity. Draw lines to connect terms with their definitions."}},{"k":"glossary_word_search","v":{"s":"Create a word search puzzle featuring your glossary terms. Fun vocabulary practice!"}},{"k":"glossary_scramble","v":{"s":"Generate a word scramble activity. Unscramble letters to spell vocabulary terms."}},{"k":"simplified_grade_level","v":{"s":"Adjust the reading level of the text. Lower grades = more supported vocabulary and shorter sentences."}},{"k":"simplified_language","v":{"s":"Translate the adapted text into another language for multilingual classrooms."}},{"k":"simplified_read_mode","v":{"s":"Activate Read Mode: Listen to the text read aloud with word-by-word highlighting."}},{"k":"simplified_define_mode","v":{"s":"Activate Define Mode: Click any word to see its definition and hear pronunciation."}},{"k":"simplified_phonics_mode","v":{"s":"Activate Phonics Mode: Click words to see letter-sound breakdowns and hear phonemes."}},{"k":"simplified_explain_mode","v":{"s":"Activate Explain Mode: Click sentences to get simpler explanations of complex ideas."}},{"k":"simplified_immersive_reader","v":{"s":"Open in Immersive Reader: A focused reading experience with customizable text settings."}},{"k":"simplified_copy_text","v":{"s":"Copy the adapted text to your clipboard for use in other applications."}},{"k":"simplified_edit","v":{"s":"Edit the adapted passage directly. Make manual adjustments to the generated text."}},{"k":"global_mute_toggle","v":{"s":"Mute all sounds and speech throughout the application. Overrides individual settings."}},{"k":"bingo_card_count_input","v":{"s":"Set how many unique Bingo cards to generate. Each card has a randomized layout."}},{"k":"bingo_images_chk","v":{"s":"Include images on Bingo cards. Terms will show both the word and a visual illustration."}},{"k":"bingo_print_btn","v":{"s":"Print Bingo cards for classroom distribution. Generates a PDF with all cards."}},{"k":"bingo_regenerate_btn","v":{"s":"Generate new random Bingo card arrangements. Keeps the same vocabulary terms."}},{"k":"bingo_launch_caller_btn","v":{"s":"Start the Bingo caller for whole-class play. Terms are called one at a time."}},{"k":"bingo_exit_caller_btn","v":{"s":"Exit the Bingo caller and return to card view."}},{"k":"bingo_next_clue","v":{"s":"Call the next term. The definition or clue is shown for students to mark their cards."}},{"k":"bingo_prev_clue","v":{"s":"Go back to the previous term to repeat or review the clue."}},{"k":"bingo_speed_slider","v":{"s":"Adjust how quickly terms are called in auto-play mode."}},{"k":"bingo_toggle_autoplay","v":{"s":"Toggle automatic calling. When enabled, terms are called at regular intervals."}},{"k":"bingo_toggle_history","v":{"s":"Show or hide the history of called terms for reference during the game."}},{"k":"bingo_close_btn","v":{"s":"Close the Bingo game and return to the glossary."}},{"k":"glossary_play_bingo","v":{"s":"Launch the Bingo game using your glossary terms! Great for whole-class vocabulary review."}},{"k":"crossword_game_container","v":{"s":"Interactive crossword puzzle generated from your glossary. Click a cell to start typing."}},{"k":"crossword_grid","v":{"s":"The crossword grid. Click any cell to select a word, then type your answer."}},{"k":"crossword_clues_list","v":{"s":"Across and Down clues for the puzzle. Click a clue to highlight its cells in the grid."}},{"k":"crossword_controls","v":{"s":"Puzzle controls: Check answers, reveal letters, or restart the puzzle."}},{"k":"escape_room_progress","v":{"s":"Your Puzzle Challenge progress. Complete each puzzle and the final challenge."}},{"k":"escape_room_timer","v":{"s":"Time remaining in Puzzle Challenge. The timer pauses when the game is paused."}},{"k":"escape_room_lives","v":{"s":"Remaining attempts. Incorrect answers cost lives. Run out and you must restart."}},{"k":"escape_room_streak","v":{"s":"Current correct answer streak. Build streaks for bonus points!"}},{"k":"escape_room_hint_button","v":{"s":"Get a hint for the current puzzle. Hints reduce your final score but help you progress."}},{"k":"escape_room_object","v":{"s":"Click to interact with this room object. It may contain a puzzle or clue."}},{"k":"escape_room_mcq_option","v":{"s":"Select this answer option for the current puzzle question."}},{"k":"escape_room_fillin_input","v":{"s":"Type your answer to the fill-in-the-blank puzzle."}},{"k":"escape_room_fillin_submit","v":{"s":"Submit your fill-in-the-blank answer to check if it's correct."}},{"k":"escape_room_scramble_input","v":{"s":"Unscramble the letters to form the correct word."}},{"k":"escape_room_scramble_submit","v":{"s":"Submit your unscrambled word answer."}},{"k":"escape_room_cipher_input","v":{"s":"Enter the decoded message from the cipher puzzle."}},{"k":"escape_room_cipher_submit","v":{"s":"Submit your cipher solution."}},{"k":"escape_room_matching_container","v":{"s":"Drag items to match related pairs in this puzzle."}},{"k":"escape_room_sequence_container","v":{"s":"Arrange items in the correct order or sequence."}},{"k":"escape_room_leaderboard","v":{"s":"View high scores and completion times from other players."}},{"k":"escape_room_team","v":{"s":"Team mode: Collaborate with classmates to solve puzzles together."}},{"k":"escape_room_close_btn","v":{"s":"Close this Puzzle Challenge activity and return to the room."}},{"k":"venn_game_container","v":{"s":"Interactive Venn diagram for compare-and-contrast activities."}},{"k":"venn_header","v":{"s":"The concepts being compared. Facts can belong to one or both categories."}},{"k":"venn_item_bank","v":{"s":"Drag items from this bank into the appropriate Venn diagram regions."}},{"k":"venn_drop_zone_a","v":{"s":"Drop zone for left category. Items here belong ONLY to this category."}},{"k":"venn_drop_zone_b","v":{"s":"Drop zone for right category. Items here belong ONLY to this category."}},{"k":"venn_drop_zone_shared","v":{"s":"Overlapping drop zone. Items here belong to BOTH categories."}},{"k":"concept_sort_panel","v":{"s":"Concept Sort activity: Categorize items into the correct groups."}},{"k":"concept_sort_header","v":{"s":"Activity instructions and category names for sorting."}},{"k":"concept_sort_categories","v":{"s":"The category buckets where you'll sort items."}},{"k":"concept_sort_category","v":{"s":"A category bucket. Drag items here that belong to this group."}},{"k":"concept_sort_bucket","v":{"s":"Drop sorted items in this bucket. Items should match this category."}},{"k":"concept_sort_deck","v":{"s":"Unsorted items waiting to be categorized. Drag items to the correct bucket."}},{"k":"concept_sort_item","v":{"s":"An unsorted item. Read carefully and drag to the matching category."}},{"k":"concept_sort_items","v":{"s":"The collection of items to be sorted into categories."}},{"k":"concept_sort_game","v":{"s":"The active concept sort game interface for categorization practice. Drag items into the correct category buckets to demonstrate understanding of classification concepts. Immediate feedback shows correct and incorrect placements. Supports 2-4 categories and any number of sortable items. Great for vocabulary tiers, science classifications, or grammar sorting."}},{"k":"concept_sort_check_answers","v":{"s":"Check if all items are sorted correctly. Incorrect placements are highlighted."}},{"k":"concept_sort_reset","v":{"s":"Reset the activity. All items return to the deck for re-sorting."}},{"k":"concept_sort_generate_button","v":{"s":"Generate a new concept sort activity based on your source content."}},{"k":"concept_sort_start_button","v":{"s":"Start the sorting activity. Items will shuffle and the timer begins."}},{"k":"concept_sort_add_item","v":{"s":"Add your own custom item to sort. Specify which category it belongs to."}},{"k":"word_sounds_mic","v":{"s":"Use your microphone to record yourself pronouncing sounds or words."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_back","v":{"s":"Return to the main Word Sounds activity from review mode."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_start","v":{"s":"Begin reviewing words and phonemes. Practice each sound carefully."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_play_word","v":{"s":"Hear the complete word pronounced. Listen for each sound."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_play_phonemes","v":{"s":"Hear the word broken into individual phonemes (sounds)."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_play_distractor","v":{"s":"Hear the distractor word for comparison in rhyme activities."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_regen_word","v":{"s":"Generate a different word if this one doesn't fit your needs."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_delete_word","v":{"s":"Remove this word from the current activity word list."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_move_word","v":{"s":"Reorder this word in the list by moving it up or down."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_image_gen","v":{"s":"Generate an illustration for this word to add visual support."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_distractor_input","v":{"s":"Enter a custom distractor word for rhyming activities."}},{"k":"word_sounds_review_phoneme_bank","v":{"s":"Phoneme tiles for the current word. Click to hear each sound."}},{"k":"word_sounds_loading_minimized","v":{"s":"Word Sounds is processing in the background. Click to expand."}},{"k":"wordsounds_open_btn","v":{"s":"Open the Word Sounds Studio for phonics instruction and activities."}},{"k":"wordsounds_pool_item","v":{"s":"A word in your activity pool. Click to edit or preview."}},{"k":"wordsounds_test_sequence","v":{"s":"Test the phoneme sequence for accurate sound-by-sound playback."}},{"k":"ws_gen_close","v":{"s":"Close the word generator panel."}},{"k":"ws_gen_expand","v":{"s":"Expand the generator for more options and settings."}},{"k":"ws_gen_minimize","v":{"s":"Minimize the generator to continue other work."}},{"k":"ws_gen_review_btn","v":{"s":"Review and finalize the generated word list before starting."}},{"k":"scaffolds_type","v":{"s":"Select scaffold type: Sentence Starters, Paragraph Frames, or both."}},{"k":"scaffolds_custom_instructions","v":{"s":"Add specific requirements for the writing scaffolds (e.g., 'Include transition words')."}},{"k":"math_panel","v":{"s":"The Math Helper panel for generating and solving problems."}},{"k":"math_input","v":{"s":"Enter a math problem or equation to solve step-by-step."}},{"k":"math_generate_button","v":{"s":"Generate practice problems based on the topic and difficulty."}},{"k":"math_generate_similar","v":{"s":"Generate more problems similar to the current one."}},{"k":"math_student_work","v":{"s":"Space for students to show their work and solution process."}},{"k":"math_toggle_answers","v":{"s":"Show or hide answers for all problems (teacher control)."}},{"k":"math_graph","v":{"s":"Visual graph representation of the equation or function."}},{"k":"math_mode","v":{"s":"Select problem type: Arithmetic, Algebra, Geometry, or Word Problems."}},{"k":"math_subject","v":{"s":"Choose the math topic (fractions, decimals, equations, etc.)."}},{"k":"math_context","v":{"s":"Add real-world context for word problems (e.g., 'shopping scenario')."}},{"k":"math_quantity","v":{"s":"Set how many problems to generate."}},{"k":"brainstorm_panel","v":{"s":"The Brainstorm panel for generating creative ideas and discussions."}},{"k":"brainstorm_generate_button","v":{"s":"Generate brainstorming ideas based on your source content."}},{"k":"brainstorm_card","v":{"s":"A brainstorm idea card. Click to expand for details and follow-ups."}},{"k":"brainstorm_guide","v":{"s":"Tips and strategies for effective brainstorming sessions."}},{"k":"brainstorm_simulation_type","v":{"s":"Choose brainstorm format: Mind Map, Discussion Questions, or What-If scenarios."}},{"k":"brainstorm_step_count","v":{"s":"Number of brainstorming prompts or steps to generate."}},{"k":"brainstorm_custom_instructions","v":{"s":"Add specific focus areas or requirements for the brainstorm."}},{"k":"persona_panel","v":{"s":"The AI Persona chat panel - engage in authentic conversations with historical figures, scientists, literary characters, or custom personas. Uses advanced AI to simulate period-accurate speech patterns, knowledge, and perspectives. Perfect for primary source analysis, perspective-taking, and empathy-building exercises. Supports multiple response modes: In-Character (fully immersive), Educational (with learning scaffolds), or Mixed (balanced approach)."}},{"k":"persona_card","v":{"s":"An AI persona ready for conversation. Each card shows the character's name, time period, and expertise area. Click to start an interview - the AI will respond authentically based on their historical context, beliefs, and knowledge. Use personas for primary source analysis, perspective-taking exercises, or creative writing inspiration."}},{"k":"persona_generate_button","v":{"s":"Generate AI personas automatically from your source content. The system analyzes your text to identify key figures, historical periods, or character archetypes and creates authentic conversational partners. Generated personas include accurate biographical details, period-appropriate vocabulary, and contextual knowledge limitations (they won't know about events after their time)."}},{"k":"persona_select_button","v":{"s":"Select this persona to begin your interview or conversation. Once selected, you'll enter an immersive chat interface where you can ask questions, explore their perspective, and earn XP for meaningful exchanges. The AI responds based on the character's historical knowledge, personality, and cultural context."}},{"k":"persona_back_btn","v":{"s":"Return to the persona selection screen to choose a different character. Your current conversation progress is automatically saved, and you can return to continue it later. This allows exploring multiple perspectives on the same historical topic."}},{"k":"persona_custom_instructions","v":{"s":"Add specific requirements for how the persona should behave during conversations. Examples: focus on a specific time period, emphasize certain beliefs or values, maintain particular speech patterns, or limit responses to historically accurate knowledge. Teachers can use this to align personas with specific learning objectives."}},{"k":"persona_response_mode","v":{"s":"Choose how the persona responds to create different learning experiences. IN CHARACTER: Fully immersive historical voice with no modern explanations. EDUCATIONAL: Character speaks but includes learning scaffolds, vocabulary support, and context. MIXED: Balanced approach with authentic voice plus occasional clarifications. Choose based on student readiness and learning goals."}},{"k":"persona_free_response","v":{"s":"Type your own open-ended response instead of selecting from pre-written options. Free response mode promotes creative expression, critical thinking, and authentic dialogue skills. Responses are analyzed for historical accuracy, empathy, and depth of inquiry. Higher-quality questions earn more XP."}},{"k":"persona_hints_toggle","v":{"s":"Show or hide response suggestions and conversation hints. When enabled, the system provides scaffolded question starters, historical context prompts, and engagement suggestions. Helpful for students new to historical inquiry or those needing support with open-ended questioning. Teachers can disable hints for more advanced assessment scenarios."}},{"k":"persona_show_hints","v":{"s":"Display helpful hints for engaging with the persona. Hints include historically relevant questions to ask, topics the character would find interesting, and prompts that lead to deeper understanding. Great for students who need scaffolding or aren't sure how to begin a historical interview."}},{"k":"persona_submit_btn","v":{"s":"Send your message to the persona character. Your question or response is analyzed for relevance and depth. The AI persona will respond authentically based on their historical context, knowledge, and personality. Well-crafted questions that show historical understanding earn bonus XP."}},{"k":"persona_close","v":{"s":"Close the persona conversation panel. Your chat history and earned XP are automatically saved. You can resume this conversation later from the History tab."}},{"k":"persona_close_title","v":{"s":"Close Persona Chat"}},{"k":"persona_reflection_input","v":{"s":"Write your reflection on the conversation for assessment. Reflect on what you learned about the historical figure, how their perspective differs from modern viewpoints, and how this conversation changed your understanding. Reflections are evaluated using a rubric aligned to historical thinking skills and can earn significant XP."}},{"k":"persona_conclude","v":{"s":"End the conversation and generate a comprehensive summary of your discussion. The summary includes: key topics covered, historical insights gained, quality of your questions, empathy demonstrated, and XP earned. This summary can be exported for assessment, added to student portfolios, or used as a writing prompt for reflection activities."}},{"k":"persona_save_chat","v":{"s":"Save this conversation to review or share later. Saved chats preserve the complete dialogue, XP earned, timestamps, and any reflections. Use saved chats for student portfolios, assessment evidence, class discussions, or exemplar models. Saved conversations can be exported as PDF or shared with other students."}},{"k":"persona_topic_spark","v":{"s":"Get a conversation starter or topic suggestion when you're not sure what to ask. The system generates historically relevant questions based on the persona's background, expertise, and time period. Great for overcoming writer's block or discovering new angles to explore in your historical inquiry."}},{"k":"persona_auto_send","v":{"s":"Automatically send your message when you stop typing for a few seconds. Creates a more natural conversational flow, especially when using voice dictation. Disable this if you prefer to review and edit messages before sending, or if you need more time to compose thoughtful responses."}},{"k":"analysis_generate_button","v":{"s":"Analyze your source text for reading level, complexity, and features."}},{"k":"analysis_check_accuracy","v":{"s":"Fact-check the source content against reliable references."}},{"k":"outline_generate_button","v":{"s":"Generate a visual organizer from your source content."}},{"k":"timeline_generate_button","v":{"s":"Generate a timeline of events from your source content."}},{"k":"timeline_topic","v":{"s":"The main topic or theme of the timeline being generated. The AI creates historically accurate events based on this topic and your source content. Example topics: American Revolution, Life Cycle of Stars, Shakespeare's Career. Events are automatically ordered chronologically for sequencing practice."}},{"k":"timeline_count","v":{"s":"Number of events to include in the timeline. More events create longer, more detailed timelines but increase difficulty. Recommended: 4-6 events for beginners, 8-10 for intermediate, 12+ for advanced learners. Events are draggable for sequencing practice after generation."}},{"k":"faq_custom_instructions","v":{"s":"Add specific requirements for the FAQ questions (e.g., 'Focus on misconceptions')."}},{"k":"faq_count","v":{"s":"Number of FAQ question-answer pairs to generate."}},{"k":"lesson_plan_custom_additions","v":{"s":"Add specific activities, standards, or content to include in the lesson plan."}},{"k":"group_modal_container","v":{"s":"Class group manager for organizing students and resources."}},{"k":"group_create_input","v":{"s":"Enter a name for the new student group."}},{"k":"group_create_button","v":{"s":"Create a new student group with the entered name."}},{"k":"group_roster_list","v":{"s":"List of students in the selected group."}},{"k":"roster_panel_header","v":{"s":"The Class Roster Key is your differentiation command center. Create student groups with unique learning profiles (grade level, language, reading level, interests, DOK), then apply those profiles to any generator. Roster data is stored in your browser's local storage and never leaves your device unless you explicitly export or sync to a live session. Use 'Apply to Generator' to instantly configure settings for a group, or 'Differentiate by Group' to batch-generate resources for all groups at once."}},{"k":"roster_import_export","v":{"s":"Import a previously exported roster JSON file, or export your current roster for backup or sharing between devices. Exported files contain group names, colors, student assignments, and all profile settings."}},{"k":"roster_sync_session","v":{"s":"Push your roster group metadata to the active Firebase session so students are automatically assigned to their designated group when they join. Group-specific settings (TTS speed, karaoke mode) take effect on student devices."}},{"k":"roster_batch_generate","v":{"s":"Generate differentiated resources for every group simultaneously. Select which resource types to create (adapted text, glossary, quiz, etc.) and the system will iterate through each group, applying their profile settings before generating. Resources are tagged with group identifiers for easy filtering."}},{"k":"bridge_send_button","v":{"s":"Open Bridge Mode to send bilingual messages to students during live instruction. Type a concept, sentence, or instructions, choose a mode (Explain, Translate, or Visual+Explain), and select a target group. The message is generated using AI with the group's language and reading level settings, then displayed as a large, readable bilingual panel on student devices with TTS and karaoke highlighting."}},{"k":"group_active_list","v":{"s":"Currently active student groups with assigned resources."}},{"k":"group_resource_library","v":{"s":"Browse resources available to assign to groups."}},{"k":"resource_delete_button","v":{"s":"Delete this resource from the library (cannot be undone)."}},{"k":"standards_query_input","v":{"s":"Search for education standards by keyword or code."}},{"k":"standards_search_btn","v":{"s":"Search the standards database."}},{"k":"standards_region_input","v":{"s":"Enter your state/region for localized standards."}},{"k":"include_images","v":{"s":"Include Images"}},{"k":"text_only","v":{"s":"Text Only"}},{"k":"storybook_image_warning","v":{"s":"Note: Including images may increase file size significantly."}},{"k":"interaction_mode","v":{"s":"Interaction Mode"}},{"k":"mode_choice","v":{"s":"Standard Adventure Mode"}},{"k":"mode_debate","v":{"s":"Debate Mode (Structured Argument)"}},{"k":"mode_system","v":{"s":"Systems / Collective (Sim Mode)"}},{"k":"mode_choice_desc","v":{"s":"Students choose from AI-generated options."}},{"k":"mode_debate_desc","v":{"s":"Students defend a perspective against an AI opponent."}},{"k":"mode_system_desc","v":{"s":"Students control a society or system (Macro-scale)."}},{"k":"language_label","v":{"s":"Adventure Language"}},{"k":"language_help","v":{"s":"Choose the language for story text and choices. Add languages in the Glossary tool first."}},{"k":"lang_options","v":{"o":[{"k":"english_only","v":{"s":"English Only"}},{"k":"only_suffix","v":{"s":"{lang} Only"}},{"k":"plus_english","v":{"s":"{lang} + English"}},{"k":"all_plus_english","v":{"s":"All ({langs}) + English"}}],"id":336}},{"k":"settings","v":{"o":[{"k":"core","v":{"s":"Core Settings"}},{"k":"modifiers","v":{"s":"Game Modifiers"}},{"k":"customization","v":{"s":"Customization"}}],"id":337}},{"k":"free_response_label","v":{"s":"Enable Free Response"}},{"k":"free_response_desc","v":{"s":"(Type your own actions)"}},{"k":"chance_mode_label","v":{"s":"Enable Chance Mode"}},{"k":"chance_mode_desc","v":{"s":"(d20 Rolls influence outcome)"}},{"k":"system_state_label","v":{"s":"Enable Resource Management"}},{"k":"system_state_desc","v":{"s":"(Track thematic variables like Stability, Tension, Progress)"}},{"k":"system_state_mode_label","v":{"s":"State Mode"}},{"k":"system_state_ai_decides","v":{"s":"AI Decides"}},{"k":"system_state_manual_entry","v":{"s":"Manual Entry"}},{"k":"system_state_ai_desc","v":{"s":"AI will create thematically appropriate state variables for your scenario."}},{"k":"system_state_manual_desc","v":{"s":"Define your own custom state variables below."}},{"k":"add_state_variable","v":{"s":"Add State Variable"}},{"k":"story_mode_label","v":{"s":"Peaceful Mode"}},{"k":"story_mode_desc","v":{"s":"Reduces combat/danger. Focuses on exploration and puzzles."}},{"k":"social_story_mode_label","v":{"s":"Social Scenario Mode (SEL role-play)"}},{"k":"social_story_mode_desc","v":{"s":"Focus on social-emotional skills and conflict resolution."}},{"k":"social_story_focus_label","v":{"s":"Target Social Skill / Focus:"}},{"k":"social_story_focus_placeholder","v":{"s":"e.g., Sharing toys, managing frustration, turn-taking..."}},{"k":"low_quality_label","v":{"s":"Faster, simpler visuals"}},{"k":"low_quality_desc","v":{"s":"(Faster generation, saves data)"}},{"k":"cloud_storage_label","v":{"s":"Save Images to Cloud"}},{"k":"cloud_storage_desc","v":{"s":"(For Storybook export only)"}},{"k":"lock_settings_label","v":{"s":"Lock Settings"}},{"k":"lock_settings_desc","v":{"s":"(Prevents students from changing settings)"}},{"k":"allow_cloud_storage_label","v":{"s":"Allow Student Cloud Storage"}},{"k":"allow_cloud_storage_desc","v":{"s":"When enabled, students can toggle cloud image saving."}},{"k":"ferpa_warning","v":{"s":"Disable for FERPA compliance if required by your institution."}},{"k":"pii_warning_title","v":{"s":"Privacy Reminder:"}},{"k":"pii_warning_desc","v":{"s":"Cloud saving is enabled with free response mode. Remind students not to include personal information (names, schools, addresses) in their responses."}},{"k":"difficulty_label","v":{"s":"Difficulty Level"}},{"k":"diff_story_option","v":{"s":"Easy"}},{"k":"diff_normal_option","v":{"s":"Normal"}},{"k":"diff_hard_option","v":{"s":"Hard"}},{"k":"diff_hardcore_option","v":{"s":"Hardcore"}},{"k":"diff_story_desc","v":{"s":"Focuses on narrative and exploration. Reduced penalties."}},{"k":"diff_normal_desc","v":{"s":"Standard risk and reward balance."}},{"k":"diff_hard_desc","v":{"s":"Higher energy costs and stricter success thresholds."}},{"k":"diff_hardcore_desc","v":{"s":"Unforgiving. Massive risks, massive rewards."}},{"k":"explore_hint","v":{"s":"Read the scene, then choose or write what happens next."}},{"k":"start_prompt","v":{"s":"Start the adventure to begin simulation."}},{"k":"tooltips","v":{"o":[{"k":"energy","v":{"s":"Energy: {value}%"}},{"k":"xp","v":{"s":"XP: {current} / {next}"}},{"k":"gold","v":{"s":"Current Gold: {value}"}},{"k":"dictation_start","v":{"s":"Use Voice Input"}},{"k":"dictation_stop","v":{"s":"Stop Dictation"}},{"k":"snapshot","v":{"s":"Take Snapshot"}},{"k":"exit_immersive","v":{"s":"Exit Immersive Mode"}},{"k":"democracy_toggle","v":{"s":"Toggle Class Voting Mode"}},{"k":"remove_option","v":{"s":"Remove Option"}},{"k":"stability","v":{"s":"Stability: {value}%"}}],"id":338}},{"k":"option_placeholder","v":{"s":"Option {n}"}},{"k":"inventory_action","v":{"o":[{"k":"obtained","v":{"s":"Obtained: {item}"}},{"k":"lost","v":{"s":"Lost: {item}"}},{"k":"used","v":{"s":"Used {item}"}}],"id":339}},{"k":"use_item","v":{"s":"Use Item"}},{"k":"key_item_btn","v":{"s":"Story Item"}},{"k":"current_scene","v":{"s":"Current Scene"}},{"k":"generating_scene","v":{"s":"Generating scene..."}},{"k":"no_image","v":{"s":"No Scene Image"}},{"k":"alt_scene","v":{"s":"Scene"}},{"k":"read_aloud_title","v":{"s":"Click to read aloud"}},{"k":"feedback","v":{"o":[{"k":"level_up","v":{"s":"LEVEL UP! {level}"}},{"k":"xp_gain","v":{"s":"+{amount} XP"}},{"k":"energy_gain","v":{"s":"+{amount} Energy"}},{"k":"double_xp","v":{"s":"Double XP!"}},{"k":"detector_found","v":{"s":"(Detector Found!)"}},{"k":"gold_gain","v":{"s":"{amount} Gold"}},{"k":"energy_restored","v":{"s":"+{amount} Energy Restored!"}},{"k":"time_rewind","v":{"s":"Time rewinds... You have a second chance."}}],"id":340}},{"k":"error","v":{"o":[{"k":"title","v":{"s":"Simulation Glitch Detected"}},{"k":"fallback","v":{"s":"The storyteller encountered an invalid data structure (WSOD). Don't worry—we can rewind time to the moment before this error occurred."}},{"k":"retry","v":{"s":"Rewind & Restore"}}],"id":341}},{"k":"locked_title","v":{"s":"Adventure Locked"}},{"k":"locked_desc_prefix","v":{"s":"You need"}},{"k":"locked_desc_suffix","v":{"s":"to unlock this mode."}},{"k":"locked_tip","v":{"s":"Tip: Complete quizzes, word searches, or matching games to earn XP!"}},{"k":"loading_save","v":{"s":"Loading Save..."}},{"k":"overwrite_title","v":{"s":"Start New Adventure?"}},{"k":"overwrite_warning","v":{"s":"This will overwrite your current progress (Level {level}). This action cannot be undone."}},{"k":"confirm_new","v":{"s":"Yes, Start New Game"}},{"k":"confirm_export_images","v":{"s":"Would you like to include scene images in the storybook PDF?\n(Note: This may increase file size)"}},{"k":"placeholder_debate","v":{"s":"Type your argument here..."}},{"k":"placeholder_action","v":{"s":"Describe your action in detail... (The AI will evaluate your solution)"}},{"k":"action_placeholder_short","v":{"s":"Describe your action..."}},{"k":"placeholder_locked","v":{"s":"Locked by Teacher"}},{"k":"placeholder_custom","v":{"s":"e.g. Focus on historical accuracy, include a specific character..."}},{"k":"aria_debate","v":{"s":"Debate Argument Input"}},{"k":"aria_action","v":{"s":"Adventure Action Input"}},{"k":"effects","v":{"o":[{"k":"energy","v":{"s":"Energy"}},{"k":"hint","v":{"s":"Hint"}},{"k":"modifier","v":{"s":"Buff"}},{"k":"xp_boost","v":{"s":"XP Boost: You're earning bonus experience points! Complete activities to level up faster during this boost period."}},{"k":"xp_boost_label","v":{"s":"XP Boost"}},{"k":"gold_boost","v":{"s":"Gold Find"}},{"k":"story_assist","v":{"s":"Story Assist"}},{"k":"story_assist_label","v":{"s":"Story Assist"}},{"k":"key_item","v":{"s":"Key Item"}}],"id":342}},{"k":"shop_items","v":{"o":[{"k":"ration_name","v":{"s":"Emergency Ration"}},{"k":"ration_desc","v":{"s":"Restores 20 Energy immediately."}},{"k":"feast_name","v":{"s":"Field Feast"}},{"k":"feast_desc","v":{"s":"Completely restores your energy to maximum."}},{"k":"hint_name","v":{"s":"Oracle Whisper"}},{"k":"hint_desc","v":{"s":"Rewinds the previous turn so you can choose again."}},{"k":"stability","v":{"s":"Stability"}},{"k":"charm_name","v":{"s":"Luck Charm"}},{"k":"charm_desc","v":{"s":"+5 Modifier to your next roll."}},{"k":"journal_name","v":{"s":"Scholar's Journal"}},{"k":"journal_desc","v":{"s":"Document your findings. Double XP for the next turn."}},{"k":"detector_name","v":{"s":"Metal Detector"}},{"k":"detector_desc","v":{"s":"Boosts Gold finds for the next 3 scenes."}},{"k":"guiding_hand_name","v":{"s":"Guiding Hand"}},{"k":"guiding_hand_desc","v":{"s":"A timely intervention resolves the current obstacle and teaches useful knowledge for later scenes. Assisted turns award no XP or Gold."}}],"id":343}},{"k":"status","v":{"o":[{"k":"reset_prompt","v":{"s":"Reset to start a new journey."}},{"k":"waiting","v":{"s":"Waiting for story..."}},{"k":"loading_story","v":{"s":"The story continues..."}}],"id":344}},{"k":"nano_badge","v":{"s":"Nano-Banana Engine"}},{"k":"status_messages","v":{"o":[{"k":"initiating_debate","v":{"s":"Initiating debate..."}},{"k":"starting","v":{"s":"Starting your adventure..."}},{"k":"not_enough_gold","v":{"s":"Not enough Gold!"}},{"k":"bought","v":{"s":"Bought {item}!"}},{"k":"log_updated","v":{"s":"Adventure Log Updated"}},{"k":"continue","v":{"s":"The adventure continues."}},{"k":"teacher_control","v":{"s":"Teacher controls the adventure in live sessions."}},{"k":"turn_complete","v":{"s":"Turn complete."}}],"id":345}},{"k":"guiding_hand_unavailable","v":{"s":"Guiding Hand needs an active scene."}},{"k":"guiding_hand_climax","v":{"s":"Guiding Hand cannot resolve the final challenge."}},{"k":"guiding_hand_started","v":{"s":"A guiding hand is stepping into the story..."}},{"k":"guiding_hand_complete","v":{"s":"Guiding Hand moved the story forward. No XP or Gold was awarded."}},{"k":"guiding_hand_failed","v":{"s":"The intervention could not be generated. Guiding Hand was not consumed."}},{"k":"guiding_hand_knowledge_label","v":{"s":"Knowledge gained"}},{"k":"hint_card_title","v":{"s":"Strategy Hint"}},{"k":"hint_loading","v":{"s":"Building a strategy hint..."}},{"k":"hint_notice_label","v":{"s":"Notice"}},{"k":"hint_connect_label","v":{"s":"Connect"}},{"k":"hint_try_label","v":{"s":"Try"}},{"k":"hint_use_starter","v":{"s":"Use this sentence starter"}},{"k":"hint_button_title","v":{"s":"Get one grounded clue and a response strategy"}},{"k":"hint_button","v":{"s":"Give me a clue"}},{"k":"hint_button_helper","v":{"s":"One clue per scene. You still decide what happens."}},{"k":"hint_used","v":{"s":"Clue used this scene"}},{"k":"hint_started","v":{"s":"Building a strategy hint..."}},{"k":"hint_ready","v":{"s":"Strategy hint ready."}},{"k":"hint_failed","v":{"s":"Couldn't build a useful strategy hint. Please try again."}},{"k":"hint_footer","v":{"s":"The next move is still yours."}},{"k":"ledger_empty","v":{"s":"No long-term memory generated yet. Play a few turns to generate a summary!"}},{"k":"storybook_toast_writing","v":{"s":"Writing storybook summary..."}},{"k":"storybook_toast_popup","v":{"s":"Please allow popups to view t