cience Quiz"}},{"k":"marine_science_quiz_2","v":{"s":"🧠 Marine Science Quiz"}},{"k":"next_question","v":{"s":"Next Question"}},{"k":"next_question_2","v":{"s":"Next Question →"}},{"k":"aquarium_curriculum_library","v":{"s":"Aquarium Curriculum Library"}},{"k":"long_form_articles_on_the_science_and_","v":{"s":"Long-form articles on the science and craft of keeping aquariums. Each piece reads in under 12 minutes. Use the category filter to narrow the list, then click any article to open the full text on the right."}},{"k":"key_idea","v":{"s":"Key idea: "}},{"k":"further_reading","v":{"s":"Further reading"}},{"k":"aquarium_quiz_lab","v":{"s":"Aquarium Quiz Lab"}},{"k":"test_yourself_on_aquarium_science_chem","v":{"s":"Test yourself on aquarium science: chemistry, cycling, stocking, plants, equipment, health, saltwater, marine biology, and conservation. Filter by category or difficulty, work through at your pace, and review explanations after each answer."}},{"k":"answered","v":{"s":"Answered"}},{"k":"correct","v":{"s":"Correct"}},{"k":"accuracy","v":{"s":"Accuracy"}},{"k":"streak","v":{"s":"Streak"}},{"k":"category","v":{"s":"Category"}},{"k":"difficulty","v":{"s":"Difficulty"}},{"k":"explanation","v":{"s":"— Explanation"}},{"k":"previous","v":{"s":"← Previous"}},{"k":"next_question_3","v":{"s":"Next Question →"}},{"k":"reset_all_answers","v":{"s":"↻ Reset All Answers"}},{"k":"jump_to_next_unanswered","v":{"s":"⤤ Jump to next unanswered"}},{"k":"ammonia_is_toxic_0_25_ppm_damages_gill","v":{"s":"Ammonia is toxic. >0.25 ppm damages gills. Immediate water change required."}},{"k":"trace_ammonia_re_check_cycle_reduce_fe","v":{"s":"Trace ammonia — re-check cycle, reduce feeding, partial water change."}},{"k":"nitrite_oxidizes_hemoglobin_brown_bloo","v":{"s":"Nitrite oxidizes hemoglobin (brown blood). Add aquarium salt; do a 30-50% water change."}},{"k":"nitrite_trace_cycle_is_incomplete_or_b","v":{"s":"Nitrite trace — cycle is incomplete or bacteria stressed."}},{"k":"nitrate_is_elevated_schedule_larger_wa","v":{"s":"Nitrate is elevated. Schedule larger water changes; consider live plants for absorption."}},{"k":"nitrate_above_40_ppm_comfortable_upper","v":{"s":"Nitrate above 40 ppm — comfortable upper limit. Water change recommended this week."}},{"k":"ph_below_6_may_stall_nitrifying_bacter","v":{"s":"pH below 6 may stall nitrifying bacteria. Raise KH with crushed coral."}},{"k":"ph_above_8_5_is_too_alkaline_for_most_","v":{"s":"pH above 8.5 is too alkaline for most tropicals. Use peat or RO blend."}},{"k":"low_kh_low_ph_unstable_ph_can_crash_ov","v":{"s":"Low KH + low pH = unstable. pH can crash overnight. Add crushed coral or alkalinity buffer."}},{"k":"temperature_okay_for_coldwater_species","v":{"s":"Temperature okay for coldwater species (goldfish, white clouds). Wrong for tropicals."}},{"k":"high_temperature_stresses_fish_and_low","v":{"s":"High temperature stresses fish and lowers dissolved oxygen. Add fans, lower heater."}},{"k":"dissolved_oxygen_is_dangerously_low_in","v":{"s":"Dissolved oxygen is dangerously low. Increase surface agitation and air stones."}},{"k":"co_above_35_ppm_risks_gassing_fish_red","v":{"s":"CO₂ above 35 ppm risks gassing fish. Reduce injection rate; verify drop checker."}},{"k":"all_parameters_within_healthy_ranges_m","v":{"s":"All parameters within healthy ranges. Maintain current schedule."}},{"k":"water_chemistry_simulator_2","v":{"s":"Water Chemistry Simulator"}},{"k":"drag_the_sliders_to_see_how_water_chem","v":{"s":"Drag the sliders to see how water chemistry parameters interact. The diagnosis panel updates in real time with warnings, recommended actions, and color-coded ideal ranges. Load a scenario from the right column to compare healthy vs. stressed tanks."}},{"k":"parameters","v":{"s":"— Parameters"}},{"k":"new_water_no_ammonia_source_yet_cyclin","v":{"s":"New water, no ammonia source yet — cycling has not begun."}},{"k":"ammonia_is_rising_toxic_nitrosomonas_b","v":{"s":"Ammonia is rising (