lator"}},{"k":"toad","v":{"s":"Toad"}},{"k":"period_2_6_cells_that_shift_back_and_f","v":{"s":"Period 2 — 6 cells that shift back and forth"}},{"k":"beacon","v":{"s":"Beacon"}},{"k":"period_2_two_blocks_that_blink","v":{"s":"Period 2 — two blocks that blink"}},{"k":"pulsar","v":{"s":"Pulsar"}},{"k":"period_3_beautiful_rotational_symmetry","v":{"s":"Period 3 — beautiful rotational symmetry"}},{"k":"glider","v":{"s":"Glider"}},{"k":"moves_diagonally_discovered_1970","v":{"s":"Moves diagonally — discovered 1970"}},{"k":"lightweight_spaceship_moves_horizontal","v":{"s":"Lightweight spaceship — moves horizontally"}},{"k":"middleweight_spaceship_9_cells","v":{"s":"Middleweight spaceship — 9 cells"}},{"k":"heavyweight_spaceship_largest_basic_sh","v":{"s":"Heavyweight spaceship — largest basic ship"}},{"k":"5_cells_1103_generations_to_stabilize","v":{"s":"5 cells → 1103 generations to stabilize!"}},{"k":"acorn","v":{"s":"Acorn"}},{"k":"7_cells_takes_5206_generations","v":{"s":"7 cells → takes 5206 generations!"}},{"k":"diehard","v":{"s":"Diehard"}},{"k":"7_cells_dies_completely_at_gen_130","v":{"s":"7 cells → dies completely at gen 130"}},{"k":"7_cells_stabilizes_at_gen_173","v":{"s":"7 cells → stabilizes at gen 173"}},{"k":"gosper_gun","v":{"s":"Gosper Gun"}},{"k":"first_gun_found_shoots_gliders_endless","v":{"s":"First gun found — shoots gliders endlessly"}},{"k":"rule_editor_b_s_notation","v":{"s":"🧬 Rule Editor (B/S Notation)"}},{"k":"change_the_rules_b_counts_that_birth_a","v":{"s":"Change the rules! B = counts that birth a cell. S = counts that keep it alive."}},{"k":"birth_b","v":{"s":"Birth (B)"}},{"k":"birth_rule","v":{"s":"Birth rule"}},{"k":"survival_s","v":{"s":"Survival (S)"}},{"k":"survival_rule","v":{"s":"Survival rule"}},{"k":"conway_b3_s23","v":{"s":"Conway B3/S23"}},{"k":"the_classic_balanced_growth","v":{"s":"The classic — balanced growth"}},{"k":"seeds_b2_s","v":{"s":"Seeds B2/S"}},{"k":"explosive_every_cell_dies_immediately","v":{"s":"Explosive! Every cell dies immediately"}},{"k":"highlife_b36_s23","v":{"s":"Highlife B36/S23"}},{"k":"like_conway_but_has_a_replicator","v":{"s":"Like Conway but has a replicator!"}},{"k":"day_night_b3678_s34678","v":{"s":"Day&Night B3678/S34678"}},{"k":"symmetric_dead_alive_are_interchangeab","v":{"s":"Symmetric — dead/alive are interchangeable"}},{"k":"diamoeba_b35678_s5678","v":{"s":"Diamoeba B35678/S5678"}},{"k":"creates_diamond_shaped_amoebas","v":{"s":"Creates diamond-shaped amoebas"}},{"k":"pattern_challenges_10_xp_each","v":{"s":"🎯 Pattern Challenges (+10 XP each)"}},{"k":"still_life","v":{"s":"🧱 Still Life"}},{"k":"draw_a_pattern_that_stays_perfectly_un","v":{"s":"Draw a pattern that stays perfectly unchanged after 1 step"}},{"k":"oscillator","v":{"s":"🔄 Oscillator"}},{"k":"draw_a_pattern_that_repeats_itself_com","v":{"s":"Draw a pattern that repeats itself (comes back to initial state)"}},{"k":"extinction","v":{"s":"💀 Extinction"}},{"k":"draw_a_pattern_that_completely_dies_ou","v":{"s":"Draw a pattern that completely dies out"}},{"k":"methuselah","v":{"s":"🌋 Methuselah"}},{"k":"use_5_cells_to_create_a_pattern_that_s","v":{"s":"Use ≤5 cells to create a pattern that survives 50+ generations"}},{"k":"pop_boom","v":{"s":"📈 Pop Boom"}},{"k":"use_exactly_5_cells_maximize_populatio","v":{"s":"Use exactly 5 cells — maximize population within 50 generations!"}},{"k":"draw_your_pattern_then_press_run_to_te","v":{"s":"Draw your pattern, then press ▶ Run to test!"}},{"k":"the_science_of_cellular_automata","v":{"s":"🧠 The Science of Cellular Automata"}},{"k":"conway_s_game_of_life_2","v":{"s":"Conway's Game of Life"}},{"k":"was_invented_by_mathematician_john_hor","v":{"s":" was invented by mathematician John Horton Conway in 1970. Despite having only 4 simple rules, it can produce extraordinary complexity — it's actually "}},{"k":"turing_complete","v":{"s":"Turing complete"}},{"k":"meaning_it_can_compute_anything_a_real","v":{"s":", meaning it can compute anything a real computer can."}},{"k":"the_rules","v":{"s":"📏 The Rules:"}},{"k":"a_live_cell_with_2_3_neighbors_stays_a","v":{"s":" A live cell with 2–3 neighbors stays alive"}},{"k":"a_dead_cell_with_exactly_3_neighbors_b","v":{"s":" A dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors becomes alive"}},{"k":"all_other_live_cells_die_loneliness_or","v":{"s":" All other live cells die (loneliness or overcrowding)"}},{"k":"use_x_ray_mode_to_see_neighbor_counts_","v":{"s":"Use 🔬 X-Ray mode to see neighbor counts and understand why each cell lives or dies!"}},{"k":"pattern_types","v":{"s":"📚 Pattern Types:"}},{"k":"still_lifes","v":{"s":"Still Lifes"}},{"k":"patterns_that_never_change_every_cell_","v":{"s":" — patterns that never change (every cell has 2–3 neighbors)"}},{"k":"oscillators","v":{"s":"Oscillators"}},{"k":"patterns_that_cycle_through_states_and","v":{"s":" — patterns that cycle through states and repeat"}},{"k":"spaceships","v":{"s":"Spaceships"}},{"k":"patterns_that_move_across_the_grid","v":{"s":" — patterns that move across the grid"}},{"k":"methuselahs","v":{"s":"Methuselahs"}},{"k":"small_patterns_that_take_very_long_to_","v":{"s":" — small patterns that take very long to stabilize"}},{"k":"guns","v":{"s":"Guns"}},{"k":"patterns_that_emit_spaceships_forever","v":{"s":" — patterns that emit spaceships forever"}},{"k":"gliders","v":{"s":"Gliders"}},{"k":"are_patterns_that_move_across_the_grid","v":{"s":" are patterns that move across the grid. The "}},{"k":"gosper_glider_gun","v":{"s":"Gosper Glider Gun"}},{"k":"1970_was_the_first_pattern_proven_to_g","v":{"s":" (1970) was the first pattern proven to grow without bound."}},{"k":"the_game_of_life_demonstrates_how_comp","v":{"s":" The Game of Life demonstrates how complex, seemingly “intelligent” behavior can arise from very simple rules with no central controller. This same principle appears in ant colonies, flocking birds, brain neurons, and even market economies."}},{"k":"in_2010_andrew_wade_built_a_pattern_ca","v":{"s":" In 2010, Andrew Wade built a pattern called “Gemini” that creates a complete copy of itself and then destroys the original — true self-replication from simple rules."}},{"k":"click_drag_to_draw_run_to_simulate_x_r","v":{"s":"👆 Click/drag to draw • ▶ Run to simulate • 🔬 X-Ray to learn"}},{"k":"game_of_life_simulation_canvas","v":{"s":"Game of Life simulation canvas"}},{"k":"population_over_time","v":{"s":"📈 Population over time"}},{"k":"snapshot","v":{"s":"Snapshot"}},{"k":"art_studio","v":{"s":"Art Studio"}},{"k":"snapshot_2","v":{"s":"📸 Snapshot"}},{"k":"harmony_desc","v":{"s":"Explore musical consonance, intervals, and visual sound relationships"}},{"k":"sculpt_3d","v":{"s":"Sculpt 3D"}},{"k":"harmony_lab_title","v":{"s":"Harmony - sound, ratio, and color"}},{"k":"harmony_lab_hint","v":{"s":"Compare consonant and dissonant intervals, connect frequency ratios to pattern, and translate musical relationships into visual harmony."}},{"k":"hue","v":{"s":"Hue"}},{"k":"contrast_result","v":{"s":"WCAG 2.2 contrast result"}},{"k":"wcag_22_contrast_guidance","v":{"s":"WCAG 2.2 AA requires 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text. AAA requires 7:1 for normal text."}},{"k":"sculpt_loading","v":{"s":"Loading the sculpting engine…"}},{"k":"sculpt_failed","v":{"s":"Sculpting failed — try a simpler description."}},{"k":"pause","v":{"s":"Pause"}},{"k":"resume","v":{"s":"Resume"}},{"k":"sculpt_export","v":{"s":"Save picture"}},{"k":"sculpt_clear","v":{"s":"Clear"}},{"k":"sculpt_title","v":{"s":"Sculpt with primitive shapes"}},{"k":"sculpt_presets","v":{"s":"Start from a preset"}},{"k":"sculpt_add_part","v":{"s":"Add a part"}},{"k":"sculpt_parts","v":{"s":"Parts"}},{"k":"sculpt_move","v":{"s":"Move the selected part"}},{"k":"sculpt_tools","v":{"s":"Shape tools"}},{"k":"sculpt_refine_ph","v":{"s":"Describe a change (\"longer tail\")…"}},{"k":"sculpt_create_ph","v":{"s":"Or describe something to sculpt…"}},{"k":"sculpt_ai_label","v":{"s":"Describe a sculpture or a change"}},{"k":"sculpt_gallery","v":{"s":"My gallery"}},{"k":"sculpt_save_ph","v":{"s":"Name it…"}},{"k":"sculpt_gallery_empty","v":{"s":"Saved sculptures appear here."}},{"k":"redraw_spirograph","v":{"s":"↻ Redraw"}},{"k":"export_spirograph_png","v":{"s":"Export spirograph as PNG"}},{"k":"redraw_string_art","v":{"s":"↻ Redraw"}},{"k":"export_string_art_png","v":{"s":"Export string art as PNG"}},{"k":"export_op_art_png","v":{"s":"Export Op Art as PNG"}},{"k":"horizontal_pan","v":{"s":"Horizontal pan"}},{"k":"vertical_pan","v":{"s":"Vertical pan"}},{"k":"fractal_keyboard_instructions","v":{"s":"Keyboard: use the Zoom, Horizontal pan, and Vertical pan sliders to explore every view. Pointer users can also double-click a location or use the mouse wheel."}},{"k":"export_gradient_png","v":{"s":"Export gradient as PNG"}},{"k":"copy_gradient_css","v":{"s":"Copy gradient CSS to clipboard"}},{"k":"absorption","v":{"s":"Absorption"}},{"k":"advanced_watercolor_controls","v":{"s":"Advanced pigment, paper, flow, and climate controls"}},{"k":"artist_explorer_hint","v":{"s":"Explore 28 practices across seven regions. Learn from artistic decisions and cultural context, then carry the question—not a copied signature style—into an interactive Studio lab."}},{"k":"artist_explorer_title","v":{"s":"Artists & Traditions — decisions, context, and making"}},{"k":"artists_traditions","v":{"s":"Artists & Traditions"}},{"k":"artists_traditions_desc","v":{"s":"Explore 28 globally representative creative practices"}},{"k":"balanced_studio","v":{"s":"Balanced"}},{"k":"bleed","v":{"s":"Bleed"}},{"k":"bloom_sensitivity","v":{"s":"Bloom sensitivity"}},{"k":"chromatic_separation","v":{"s":"Chromatic separation"}},{"k":"clear_water_brush","v":{"s":"Clear water"}},{"k":"clear_watercolor","v":{"s":"Clear"}},{"k":"climate_presets","v":{"s":"Studio climate:"}},{"k":"cold_press","v":{"s":"Cold press"}},{"k":"diagnostics_export_note","v":{"s":"Screen-only overlays; autosaves and exports remain clean."}},{"k":"dry_brush","v":{"s":"Dry"}},{"k":"dry_studio","v":{"s":"Dry studio"}},{"k":"dry_watercolor","v":{"s":"Dry paint"}},{"k":"drying_rate","v":{"s":"Drying rate"}},{"k":"export_watercolor_png","v":{"s":"Export PNG"}},{"k":"flat_brush","v":{"s":"Flat"}},{"k":"flow_guides","v":{"s":"Flow guides"}},{"k":"granulation","v":{"s":"Granulation"}},{"k":"hot_press","v":{"s":"Hot press"}},{"k":"humid_studio","v":{"s":"Humid studio"}},{"k":"lift_brush","v":{"s":"Lift"}},{"k":"load_mixed_pigment","v":{"s":"Load mixed pigment"}},{"k":"masking_fluid_brush","v":{"s":"Masking fluid"}},{"k":"mix_pigment_a","v":{"s":"Pigment A"}},{"k":"mix_pigment_b","v":{"s":"Pigment B"}},{"k":"mop_brush","v":{"s":"Mop"}},{"k":"no_flow","v":{"s":"Still"}},{"k":"paper_chemistry_tip","v":{"s":"Paper chemistry: "}},{"k":"paper_chemistry_tip_desc","v":{"s":"Higher sizing keeps water and pigment near the surface, extending flow and making dry color easier to lift. Lower sizing pulls washes into the fibers sooner. Bloom sensitivity controls how strongly wetness boundaries create backruns and cauliflower edges."}},{"k":"paper_presets","v":{"s":"Paper preset:"}},{"k":"paper_sizing","v":{"s":"Paper sizing"}},{"k":"paper_texture","v":{"s":"Paper texture"}},{"k":"pause_watercolor_drying","v":{"s":"Pause drying"}},{"k":"peel_mask_brush","v":{"s":"Peel mask"}},{"k":"pigment_amount","v":{"s":"Pigment"}},{"k":"pigment_character","v":{"s":"Pigment character: "}},{"k":"pigment_mobility","v":{"s":"Pigment mobility"}},{"k":"pigment_opacity","v":{"s":"Pigment opacity"}},{"k":"redo_watercolor","v":{"s":"Redo"}},{"k":"reload_watercolor_brush","v":{"s":"Reload brush"}},{"k":"remove_all_masking_fluid","v":{"s":"Remove all mask"}},{"k":"resume_watercolor_drying","v":{"s":"Resume drying"}},{"k":"rewetting_sensitivity","v":{"s":"Rewetting sensitivity"}},{"k":"rewetting_tip","v":{"s":"Rewetting and glazing: "}},{"k":"rewetting_tip_desc","v":{"s":"Clear water and wet glazes reactivate low-staining color more readily. Highly staining and strongly granulating layers stay anchored in the paper."}},{"k":"rigger_brush","v":{"s":"Rigger"}},{"k":"rough_paper","v":{"s":"Rough"}},{"k":"round_brush","v":{"s":"Round"}},{"k":"salt_texture_brush","v":{"s":"Salt texture"}},{"k":"separation_tip","v":{"s":"Chromatic separation: "}},{"k":"separation_tip_desc","v":{"s":"When pigments with different mobility meet on wet paper, higher settings let faster color channels travel ahead of heavier ones. Premixed pigments remain more uniform."}},{"k":"simulate_watercolor_diffusion_and_paper","v":{"s":"Simulate pigment, water, and paper texture"}},{"k":"splatter_brush","v":{"s":"Splatter"}},{"k":"staining_strength","v":{"s":"Staining strength"}},{"k":"studio_airflow","v":{"s":"Studio airflow"}},{"k":"studio_humidity","v":{"s":"Studio humidity"}},{"k":"tilt_strength","v":{"s":"Tilt strength"}},{"k":"undo_watercolor","v":{"s":"Undo"}},{"k":"wash_brush","v":{"s":"Wash"}},{"k":"water_amount","v":{"s":"Water"}},{"k":"watercolor","v":{"s":"Watercolor"}},{"k":"watercolor_2","v":{"s":"Watercolor"}},{"k":"watercolor_brush","v":{"s":"Brush:"}},{"k":"watercolor_color","v":{"s":"Pigment color"}},{"k":"watercolor_diagnostics","v":{"s":"View diagnostics:"}},{"k":"watercolor_flow","v":{"s":"Flow:"}},{"k":"watercolor_keyboard_help","v":{"s":"Draw with a pointer or stylus; pressure, tilt, and stroke speed shape the mark. Focus the canvas and use Arrow keys to move; press Enter or Space to dab, P to pause drying, and Ctrl/Command+Z to undo."}},{"k":"watercolor_mixing_help","v":{"s":"Blend two material profiles using optical absorbance."}},{"k":"watercolor_mixing_tray","v":{"s":"Pigment mixing tray"}},{"k":"watercolor_science","v":{"s":"Why it looks wet: "}},{"k":"watercolor_science_desc","v":{"s":"Water diffuses pigment into nearby paper fibers. Every deposited wash carries its own granulation, staining, opacity, and mobility through mixtures. Each color channel retains mobility-weighted transport, so faster pigments can separate at wet edges while heavier colors lag and settle. Granulating particles collect in texture, staining colors resist lifting, and opaque particles scatter more light. Paper sizing controls how long water and pigment remain mobile on the surface before absorption; highly sized sheets lift and rewet more readily, while lightly sized sheets anchor washes sooner. Bloom sensitivity controls the strength of backruns at uneven wetness boundaries. Dry layers can be selectively remobilized by clear water or wet glazes; low-staining color releases more readily while staining and granulation anchor pigment in the fibers. Studio humidity slows evaporation and preserves blooms, while airflow accelerates surface drying. Round, flat, mop, rigger, wash, and dry brushes vary footprint, softness, water load, spacing, and reservoir drain. Slow, pressured strokes deposit more paint, stylus tilt spreads the footprint, and optical absorption deepens mixtures. Masking fluid, evaporation, gravity, clear water, salt, blooms, and tide marks remain physically layered. Wetness maps and flow guides visualize the simulation without changing saved artwork."}},{"k":"watercolor_simulation","v":{"s":"Watercolor — pigment, water, and paper"}},{"k":"watercolor_simulation_hint","v":{"s":"Water carries pigment across paper; as the brush unloads and water evaporates, clustered pigment creates granulation and darker drying edges. Try a wash, then a dry brush."}},{"k":"watercolor_surface","v":{"s":"Paper:"}},{"k":"wet_on_dry","v":{"s":"Wet-on-dry"}},{"k":"wet_on_wet","v":{"s":"Wet-on-wet"}},{"k":"wetness_map","v":{"s":"Wetness map"}},{"k":"learning_artists_traditions_9c00979","v":{"s":"Artists & Traditions"}},{"k":"learning_color_wheel_f3ff339","v":{"s":"Color Wheel"}},{"k":"learning_color_mixer_2448ebb","v":{"s":"Color Mixer"}},{"k":"learning_watercolor_150fcde","v":{"s":"Watercolor"}},{"k":"learning_pixel_art_1110e84","v":{"s":"Pixel Art"}},{"k":"learning_symmetry_cc14de6","v":{"s":"Symmetry"}},{"k":"learning_spirograph_fd81fd4","v":{"s":"Spirograph"}},{"k":"learning_generative_art_f6c5978","v":{"s":"Generative Art"}},{"k":"learning_spin_art_aff2d28","v":{"s":"Spin Art"}},{"k":"learning_string_art_56c43ff","v":{"s":"String Art"}},{"k":"learning_op_art_4f90eb0","v":{"s":"Op Art"}},{"k":"learning_tessellation_6e05511","v":{"s":"Tessellation"}},{"k":"learning_fractal_f014553","v":{"s":"Fractal"}},{"k":"learning_gradient_2523561","v":{"s":"Gradient"}},{"k":"learning_stereogram_b92dd79","v":{"s":"Stereogram"}},{"k":"learning_3d_sculpture_6d697c8","v":{"s":"3D Sculpture"}},{"k":"learning_contrast_08795ba","v":{"s":"Contrast"}},{"k":"learning_harmony_ccfe55d","v":{"s":"Harmony"}},{"k":"learning_explore_3b73900","v":{"s":"Explore"}},{"k":"learning_paint_color_0cfeba8","v":{"s":"Paint & color"}},{"k":"learning_pattern_mathematics_b2fb534","v":{"s":"Pattern & mathematics"}},{"k":"learning_digital_generative_102373f","v":{"s":"Digital & generative"}},{"k":"learning_space_sculpture_8be160a","v":{"s":"Space & sculpture"}},{"k":"learning_perception_access_5e1f966","v":{"s":"Perception & access"}},{"k":"learning_paint_50d0cce","v":{"s":"Paint"}},{"k":"learning_paint_something_df20e35","v":{"s":"Paint something"}},{"k":"learning_start_with_a_responsive_watercolor_canvas_then_e_f3e07d5","v":{"s":"Start with a responsive watercolor canvas, then explore pigment and paper when you are ready."}},{"k":"learning_digital_42be1f5","v":{"s":"Digital"}},{"k":"learning_make_pixel_art_e52999f","v":{"s":"Make pixel art"}},{"k":"learning_build_a_sprite_or_icon_one_deliberate_cell_at_a__4a186e3","v":{"s":"Build a sprite or icon one deliberate cell at a time."}},{"k":"learning_pattern_4288ade","v":{"s":"Pattern"}},{"k":"learning_create_a_pattern_24735f3","v":{"s":"Create a pattern"}},{"k":"learning_draw_once_and_let_reflection_rotation_and_repeti_fd16a42","v":{"s":"Draw once and let reflection, rotation, and repetition transform the mark."}},{"k":"learning_space_20eac5a","v":{"s":"Space"}},{"k":"learning_build_in_3d_8c535dc","v":{"s":"Build in 3D"}},{"k":"learning_combine_simple_forms_into_a_sculpture_you_can_or_5283a61","v":{"s":"Combine simple forms into a sculpture you can orbit and photograph."}},{"k":"learning_learn_ce78afd","v":{"s":"Learn"}},{"k":"learning_explore_an_artist_b7fa9a5","v":{"s":"Explore an artist"}},{"k":"learning_study_a_creative_decision_and_carry_the_question_c5cf038","v":{"s":"Study a creative decision and carry the question, not a copied style, into your own work."}},{"k":"learning_inspect_e0723a8","v":{"s":"Inspect"}},{"k":"learning_design_accessible_color_e403379","v":{"s":"Design accessible color"}},{"k":"learning_test_color_choices_and_understand_how_contrast_c_efa861e","v":{"s":"Test color choices and understand how contrast changes who can use a design."}},{"k":"learning_tiny_night_world_47920ff","v":{"s":"Tiny night world"}},{"k":"learning_shape_a_small_evening_scene_that_remains_readabl_01319b1","v":{"s":"Shape a small evening scene that remains readable at a glance."}},{"k":"learning_use_three_related_hues_and_one_bright_focal_poin_790bca0","v":{"s":"Use three related hues and one bright focal point."}},{"k":"learning_choose_the_atmosphere_41085f4","v":{"s":"Choose the atmosphere"}},{"k":"learning_build_a_three_hue_night_palette_with_one_deliber_40634f5","v":{"s":"Build a three-hue night palette with one deliberately brighter accent."}},{"k":"learning_reduce_it_to_a_silhouette_2a2cf73","v":{"s":"Reduce it to a silhouette"}},{"k":"learning_make_a_tiny_scene_whose_largest_shapes_still_rea_a71086b","v":{"s":"Make a tiny scene whose largest shapes still read when you squint."}},{"k":"learning_check_the_focal_point_4aec05e","v":{"s":"Check the focal point"}},{"k":"learning_test_whether_the_accent_and_essential_details_re_44aa700","v":{"s":"Test whether the accent and essential details remain distinguishable."}},{"k":"learning_pattern_with_a_pulse_de9d99b","v":{"s":"Pattern with a pulse"}},{"k":"learning_turn_one_mark_into_rhythm_then_decide_where_the__aaf64d5","v":{"s":"Turn one mark into rhythm, then decide where the rhythm should break."}},{"k":"learning_repeat_one_unit_and_change_only_one_interval_ad64261","v":{"s":"Repeat one unit and change only one interval."}},{"k":"learning_invent_the_unit_8b7cea0","v":{"s":"Invent the unit"}},{"k":"learning_draw_one_off_center_mark_and_choose_how_reflecti_073e644","v":{"s":"Draw one off-center mark and choose how reflection or rotation transforms it."}},{"k":"learning_build_the_rhythm_2f1e148","v":{"s":"Build the rhythm"}},{"k":"learning_repeat_the_unit_until_the_negative_space_becomes_ab37abc","v":{"s":"Repeat the unit until the negative space becomes part of the pattern."}},{"k":"learning_introduce_tension_b80668e","v":{"s":"Introduce tension"}},{"k":"learning_change_one_interval_and_notice_where_still_patte_bc706ae","v":{"s":"Change one interval and notice where still pattern begins to feel active."}},{"k":"learning_rule_to_wonder_f6656e3","v":{"s":"Rule to wonder"}},{"k":"learning_begin_with_a_creative_question_and_let_a_repeata_01db883","v":{"s":"Begin with a creative question and let a repeatable rule surprise you."}},{"k":"learning_change_one_variable_at_a_time_and_keep_the_most__158bbc3","v":{"s":"Change one variable at a time and keep the most interesting result."}},{"k":"learning_find_a_question_aa45746","v":{"s":"Find a question"}},{"k":"learning_choose_an_artist_and_name_the_decision_beneath_t_78f08c0","v":{"s":"Choose an artist and name the decision beneath the surface, not a signature style."}},{"k":"learning_write_the_visual_rule_0aced0a","v":{"s":"Write the visual rule"}},{"k":"learning_translate_that_question_into_one_repeatable_rule_816344d","v":{"s":"Translate that question into one repeatable rule, then run a variation."}},{"k":"learning_look_across_scales_9cc7d8a","v":{"s":"Look across scales"}},{"k":"learning_inspect_what_the_rule_preserves_and_what_changes_56e65b1","v":{"s":"Inspect what the rule preserves and what changes as scale or iteration shifts."}},{"k":"learning_choose_one_profile_and_name_a_decision_the_artis_0a01894","v":{"s":"Choose one profile and name a decision the artist keeps making."}},{"k":"learning_look_for_how_material_place_history_and_audience_0843962","v":{"s":"Look for how material, place, history, and audience change the meaning of that decision."}},{"k":"learning_carry_the_underlying_question_into_a_lab_without_69e9e7f","v":{"s":"Carry the underlying question into a lab without copying a signature style."}},{"k":"learning_choose_one_hue_then_make_a_three_color_family_by_9188f27","v":{"s":"Choose one hue, then make a three-color family by changing saturation and lightness."}},{"k":"learning_the_same_hue_can_feel_vivid_muted_near_or_distan_a0b29f5","v":{"s":"The same hue can feel vivid, muted, near, or distant as those two values move."}},{"k":"learning_reserve_one_contrasting_color_for_the_part_that__4f6e91b","v":{"s":"Reserve one contrasting color for the part that must be noticed first."}},{"k":"learning_mix_the_same_two_colors_as_pigment_and_as_light_2da9c52","v":{"s":"Mix the same two colors as pigment and as light."}},{"k":"learning_subtractive_mixtures_absorb_wavelengths_while_ad_8e316b5","v":{"s":"Subtractive mixtures absorb wavelengths while additive mixtures combine emitted light."}},{"k":"learning_predict_the_result_before_moving_the_ratio_then__ef40c59","v":{"s":"Predict the result before moving the ratio, then explain any surprise."}},{"k":"learning_place_one_wet_wash_beside_one_dry_brush_mark_usi_dc6d780","v":{"s":"Place one wet wash beside one dry-brush mark using the same pigment."}},{"k":"learning_water_movement_paper_texture_and_drying_edges_re_9bbc08d","v":{"s":"Water movement, paper texture, and drying edges redistribute pigment after the brush leaves."}},{"k":"learning_make_depth_using_only_one_pigment_and_three_wate_e070101","v":{"s":"Make depth using only one pigment and three water levels."}},{"k":"learning_begin_at_16_by_16_and_block_only_the_silhouette__2aabb56","v":{"s":"Begin at 16 by 16 and block only the silhouette before adding details."}},{"k":"learning_every_pixel_changes_an_edge_so_clusters_usually__53c745d","v":{"s":"Every pixel changes an edge, so clusters usually read more clearly than isolated dots."}},{"k":"learning_use_four_colors_and_make_the_image_readable_at_b_190fdb1","v":{"s":"Use four colors and make the image readable at both canvas size and thumbnail size."}},{"k":"learning_draw_one_off_center_mark_and_compare_reflection__c334db0","v":{"s":"Draw one off-center mark and compare reflection with rotation."}},{"k":"learning_the_same_source_mark_creates_different_visual_we_86eb3ae","v":{"s":"The same source mark creates different visual weight depending on the transformation."}},{"k":"learning_break_the_symmetry_once_exactly_where_attention__4141f5f","v":{"s":"Break the symmetry once, exactly where attention should land."}},{"k":"learning_change_one_radius_ratio_while_keeping_the_pen_of_338a03e","v":{"s":"Change one radius ratio while keeping the pen offset fixed."}},{"k":"learning_small_ratio_changes_can_alter_petal_count_closur_de638e2","v":{"s":"Small ratio changes can alter petal count, closure, and the density of crossings."}},{"k":"learning_find_two_different_settings_that_create_related__e73c03c","v":{"s":"Find two different settings that create related silhouettes."}},{"k":"learning_choose_one_rule_run_it_twice_and_compare_what_st_3ec4c4e","v":{"s":"Choose one rule, run it twice, and compare what stays stable."}},{"k":"learning_the_artist_designs_the_system_controlled_randomn_c1f2fe2","v":{"s":"The artist designs the system; controlled randomness designs each result."}},{"k":"learning_change_only_one_variable_and_decide_which_versio_ed7e1f5","v":{"s":"Change only one variable and decide which version better serves your intention."}},{"k":"learning_place_paint_near_the_center_then_repeat_near_the_a8bc6a1","v":{"s":"Place paint near the center, then repeat near the edge at the same speed."}},{"k":"learning_distance_from_the_center_changes_how_strongly_th_46b508a","v":{"s":"Distance from the center changes how strongly the spinning motion spreads a mark."}},{"k":"learning_build_a_calm_area_and_an_energetic_area_without__f481f5e","v":{"s":"Build a calm area and an energetic area without changing the palette."}},{"k":"learning_connect_every_third_peg_then_compare_every_fifth_bfb8c9e","v":{"s":"Connect every third peg, then compare every fifth peg."}},{"k":"learning_straight_segments_create_the_envelope_of_a_curve_bf94302","v":{"s":"Straight segments create the envelope of a curve through accumulation."}},{"k":"learning_use_two_step_sizes_to_make_one_curve_interrupt_a_50c8355","v":{"s":"Use two step sizes to make one curve interrupt another."}},{"k":"learning_repeat_one_interval_then_gradually_compress_it_a_cdb9ece","v":{"s":"Repeat one interval, then gradually compress it across the field."}},{"k":"learning_your_visual_system_reads_contrast_and_spacing_as_d70dc1f","v":{"s":"Your visual system reads contrast and spacing as motion even when nothing moves."}},{"k":"learning_create_strong_energy_without_relying_on_maximum__8a3167c","v":{"s":"Create strong energy without relying on maximum black-and-white contrast."}},{"k":"learning_repeat_one_tile_until_both_the_shape_and_the_gap_eaa8f35","v":{"s":"Repeat one tile until both the shape and the gap around it become visible."}},{"k":"learning_a_successful_tiling_organizes_negative_space_as__bcd7471","v":{"s":"A successful tiling organizes negative space as carefully as positive form."}},{"k":"learning_introduce_a_color_rhythm_that_crosses_the_tile_b_105a6ac","v":{"s":"Introduce a color rhythm that crosses the tile boundaries."}},{"k":"learning_change_one_parameter_slightly_then_zoom_into_the_b94cf98","v":{"s":"Change one parameter slightly, then zoom into the boundary rather than the center."}},{"k":"learning_self_similarity_preserves_relationships_while_pr_25f795f","v":{"s":"Self-similarity preserves relationships while producing new detail at different scales."}},{"k":"learning_save_two_views_that_feel_related_but_not_identic_d06caea","v":{"s":"Save two views that feel related but not identical."}},{"k":"learning_use_three_stops_and_move_the_middle_stop_away_fr_462b3e0","v":{"s":"Use three stops and move the middle stop away from the exact center."}},{"k":"learning_stop_position_changes_perceived_emphasis_as_much_9d63d4e","v":{"s":"Stop position changes perceived emphasis as much as the colors themselves."}},{"k":"learning_make_a_transition_that_communicates_depth_withou_4cec66d","v":{"s":"Make a transition that communicates depth without adding an object."}},{"k":"learning_start_with_a_simple_depth_shape_and_a_pattern_wi_1a98fa7","v":{"s":"Start with a simple depth shape and a pattern with clear small-scale texture."}},{"k":"learning_depth_appears_when_each_eye_matches_repeated_inf_d9bb94c","v":{"s":"Depth appears when each eye matches repeated information at a slightly different position."}},{"k":"learning_reduce_depth_until_the_hidden_form_is_discoverab_e700f4a","v":{"s":"Reduce depth until the hidden form is discoverable but not immediately obvious."}},{"k":"learning_combine_three_forms_and_orbit_before_adding_a_fo_7e94b4d","v":{"s":"Combine three forms and orbit before adding a fourth."}},{"k":"learning_silhouette_balance_and_negative_space_change_wit_cd72e27","v":{"s":"Silhouette, balance, and negative space change with every viewpoint."}},{"k":"learning_make_the_sculpture_feel_stable_from_one_view_and_8e2fff9","v":{"s":"Make the sculpture feel stable from one view and precarious from another."}},{"k":"learning_test_one_color_pair_then_change_only_the_foregro_f990a46","v":{"s":"Test one color pair, then change only the foreground lightness."}},{"k":"learning_readable_contrast_depends_on_relative_luminance__64b8ca8","v":{"s":"Readable contrast depends on relative luminance, text size, and visual context."}},{"k":"learning_keep_the_relationship_expressive_while_meeting_t_c663445","v":{"s":"Keep the relationship expressive while meeting the intended accessibility target."}},{"k":"learning_compare_a_simple_frequency_ratio_with_a_more_com_0ca2eeb","v":{"s":"Compare a simple frequency ratio with a more complex one."}},{"k":"learning_small_whole_number_relationships_often_feel_more_e776ebe","v":{"s":"Small whole-number relationships often feel more stable in sound and pattern."}},{"k":"learning_translate_one_interval_into_spacing_scale_or_col_5576f8a","v":{"s":"Translate one interval into spacing, scale, or color rather than illustrating a note."}},{"k":"study_intention_label","v":{"s":"Intention"}},{"k":"compare_different_labs","v":{"s":"These studies use different labs. Compare their intention and visual decisions."}},{"k":"compare_seed_match","v":{"s":"Same seed and step. Check the other settings and any added bursts to identify what changed."}},{"k":"compare_seed_mismatch","v":{"s":"The seed or step differs. For a controlled experiment, use the same seed and compare at the same step."}},{"k":"learning_creative_thread_41cdd22","v":{"s":"Creative Thread"}},{"k":"learning_constraint_value1_f523f52","v":{"s":"Constraint: {value1}"}},{"k":"learning_step_value1_of_value2_196d3db","v":{"s":"Step {value1} of {value2}"}},{"k":"learning_value1_steps_11a083b","v":{"s":"{value1} steps"}},{"k":"learning_go_to_step_value1_value2_value3_f760000","v":{"s":"Go to step {value1}: {value2}{value3}"}},{"k":"learning_study_saved_cf7a246","v":{"s":"📸 Study saved"}},{"k":"learning_step_value1_e3415b9","v":{"s":"✓ Step {value1}"}},{"k":"learning_step_value1_cd4a348","v":{"s":"Step {value1}"}},{"k":"learning_your_move_981ab1b","v":{"s":"Your move: "}},{"k":"learning_you_are_exploring_value1_your_thread_is_waiting__f7f1a61","v":{"s":"You are exploring {value1}. Your thread is waiting at {value2}."}},{"k":"learning_optional_reflection_f371c5f","v":{"s":"Optional reflection"}},{"k":"learning_keep_183f00f","v":{"s":"Keep"}},{"k":"learning_change_c0bf75b","v":{"s":"Change"}},{"k":"learning_wonder_f3cb6ed","v":{"s":"Wonder"}},{"k":"learning_short_note_optional_095d2cf","v":{"s":"Short note (optional)"}},{"k":"learning_what_should_carry_forward_d6820ac","v":{"s":"What should carry forward?"}},{"k":"learning_what_will_you_revise_3896390","v":{"s":"What will you revise?"}},{"k":"learning_what_question_appeared_53d10f7","v":{"s":"What question appeared?"}},{"k":"learning_fork_ready_saving_creates_a_new_branch_and_prese_16292e1","v":{"s":"Fork ready: saving creates a new branch and preserves the original study."}},{"k":"learning_this_step_already_has_a_study_saving_again_updat_7abf721","v":{"s":"This step already has a study. Saving again updates that checkpoint."}},{"k":"learning_back_aceb696","v":{"s":"← Back"}},{"k":"learning_return_to_current_step_29e3562","v":{"s":"Return to current step"}},{"k":"learning_updates_the_existing_study_for_this_step_4ddc7ff","v":{"s":"Updates the existing study for this step"}},{"k":"learning_save_branch_next_75e1f34","v":{"s":"Save branch & next →"}},{"k":"learning_save_study_next_0e4c9f1","v":{"s":"Save study & next →"}},{"k":"learning_next_without_saving_993a688","v":{"s":"Next without saving"}},{"k":"learning_save_branch_review_0f86e2e","v":{"s":"Save branch & review"}},{"k":"learning_save_study_review_aa40018","v":{"s":"Save study & review"}},{"k":"learning_review_without_saving_aef3123","v":{"s":"Review without saving"}},{"k":"learning_leave_brief_36fe1e0","v":{"s":"Leave brief"}},{"k":"learning_carry_ideas_between_labs_9e835f3","v":{"s":"Carry ideas between labs"}},{"k":"learning_thread_kit_f20ce46","v":{"s":"Thread Kit"}},{"k":"learning_this_palette_stays_with_the_project_until_you_ex_e0789b1","v":{"s":"This palette stays with the project until you explicitly apply it."}},{"k":"learning_collect_a_palette_in_color_wheel_then_carry_it_i_de84c90","v":{"s":"Collect a palette in Color Wheel, then carry it into Pixel Art and Contrast."}},{"k":"learning_thread_kit_palette_colors_6c952d1","v":{"s":"Thread Kit palette colors"}},{"k":"learning_nothing_is_applied_automatically_your_current_ar_ca4f6a0","v":{"s":"Nothing is applied automatically. Your current artwork always stays unchanged until you choose a transfer."}},{"k":"study_notes_optional","v":{"s":"Study notes (optional)"}},{"k":"study_notes_help","v":{"s":"Capture your intention and discoveries. These notes travel with your next saved study."}},{"k":"study_title","v":{"s":"Title"}},{"k":"study_intention_prompt","v":{"s":"What are you trying to make or find out?"}},{"k":"study_reflection","v":{"s":"Reflection"}},{"k":"reflection_keep","v":{"s":"Keep"}},{"k":"reflection_change","v":{"s":"Change"}},{"k":"reflection_wonder","v":{"s":"Wonder"}},{"k":"study_observation","v":{"s":"What did you notice, or what will you change?"}},{"k":"study_description","v":{"s":"Describe the artwork for someone who cannot see it"}},{"k":"save_study_with_notes","v":{"s":"Save study with notes"}},{"k":"studio_inspector_dialog","v":{"s":"Studio inspector"}},{"k":"back_to_artwork","v":{"s":"Back to artwork"}},{"k":"pixel_palette_options","v":{"s":"Palettes and colors"}},{"k":"sculpt_draw_lathe","v":{"s":"Draw your own shape - it spins around the axis"}},{"k":"sculpt_draw_extrude","v":{"s":"Draw your own outline - it is pushed out into a solid"}},{"k":"sculpt_draw_lathe_help","v":{"s":"Click on the pad to add a point, drag a point to move it. Points run from the bottom to the top; the dashed line is the spin axis."}},{"k":"sculpt_draw_extrude_help","v":{"s":"Click on the pad to add a point after the nearest one, drag a point to move it. The outline closes itself."}},{"k":"spin_palette_options","v":{"s":"Palettes and paint color"}},{"k":"julia_parameter_connection_explained","v":{"s":" use the same formula but fix c and vary the starting z. For z squared plus c, parameters in the Mandelbrot set give connected Julia sets; parameters outside it give disconnected, dust-like Cantor Julia sets. The Fatou set is the complement of the Julia set."}},{"k":"gradient_interpolation_explained","v":{"s":" follows a path around the hue circle. RGB interpolation blends channel values: halfway between pure red and pure blue is purple, not gray. Neither HSL nor RGB is perceptually uniform; spaces such as OKLab are designed for more even perceived changes. A hue path and a pigment mixture describe different processes."}},{"k":"learning_artist_el_anatsui_life","v":{"s":"born 1944"}},{"k":"learning_artist_el_anatsui_places","v":{"s":"Ghana and Nigeria"}},{"k":"learning_artist_el_anatsui_overview","v":{"s":"Transforms discarded bottle caps and metal into vast, flexible fields that change with every installation."}},{"k":"learning_artist_el_anatsui_lookFor","v":{"s":"Repetition, material history, changing surfaces, and the tension between precious appearance and discarded matter."}},{"k":"learning_artist_el_anatsui_context","v":{"s":"His works connect trade, consumption, colonial histories, labor, and the ability of a material to carry memory."}},{"k":"learning_artist_el_anatsui_tryThis","v":{"s":"Build a repeated unit from safe reused material, then test three arrangements instead of treating the first layout as final."}},{"k":"learning_artist_el_anatsui_respect","v":{"s":"Study transformation and systems; do not reduce West African histories to a decorative metallic effect."}},{"k":"learning_artist_ibrahim_el_salahi_life","v":{"s":"born 1930"}},{"k":"learning_artist_ibrahim_el_salahi_places","v":{"s":"Sudan and the United Kingdom"}},{"k":"learning_artist_ibrahim_el_salahi_overview","v":{"s":"A foundational figure in African modernism whose drawings and paintings join calligraphic energy, memory, landscape, and abstraction."}},{"k":"learning_artist_ibrahim_el_salahi_lookFor","v":{"s":"Branching lines, compressed figures, black-and-white rhythm, and forms that hover between writing and image."}},{"k":"learning_artist_ibrahim_el_salahi_context","v":{"s":"His work emerged through Sudanese, African, Arab, Islamic, and international modernist conversations rather than a single inherited category."}},{"k":"learning_artist_ibrahim_el_salahi_tryThis","v":{"s":"Let one continuous line grow into an image, then identify where it reads as symbol, body, landscape, or writing."}},{"k":"learning_artist_ibrahim_el_salahi_respect","v":{"s":"Explore the relationship between mark and meaning without copying sacred or unfamiliar scripts as decoration."}},{"k":"learning_artist_esther_mahlangu_life","v":{"s":"born 1935"}},{"k":"learning_artist_esther_mahlangu_places","v":{"s":"South Africa; Ndebele"}},{"k":"learning_artist_esther_mahlangu_overview","v":{"s":"Extends Ndebele mural painting through architecture, canvas, vehicles, and public commissions while asserting the knowledge of women artists."}},{"k":"learning_artist_esther_mahlangu_lookFor","v":{"s":"Bold boundaries, geometric sequencing, high-contrast color, scale, and the adaptation of a living mural practice."}},{"k":"learning_artist_esther_mahlangu_context","v":{"s":"Ndebele house painting is a living cultural practice tied to community, identity, and women’s knowledge—not a generic pattern library."}},{"k":"learning_artist_esther_mahlangu_tryThis","v":{"s":"Create a geometric rhythm from shapes drawn from your own environment and explain what your repeated choices mean."}},{"k":"learning_artist_esther_mahlangu_respect","v":{"s":"Credit Ndebele artists and context. Do not claim Ndebele identity or reproduce culturally meaningful motifs as anonymous décor."}},{"k":"learning_artist_skunder_boghossian_life","v":{"s":"1937–2003"}},{"k":"learning_artist_skunder_boghossian_places","v":{"s":"Ethiopia, France, and the United States"}},{"k":"learning_artist_skunder_boghossian_overview","v":{"s":"Built dense, layered paintings from Ethiopian visual histories, personal symbols, jazz-like rhythm, and international modernism."}},{"k":"learning_artist_skunder_boghossian_lookFor","v":{"s":"Layering, icon-like forms, luminous color, improvisation, and figures emerging from complex grounds."}},{"k":"learning_artist_skunder_boghossian_context","v":{"s":"His work challenges accounts of modernism that place innovation only in Europe and North America."}},{"k":"learning_artist_skunder_boghossian_tryThis","v":{"s":"Layer three translucent systems—marks, shapes, and a limited palette—then decide which layer should lead."}},{"k":"learning_artist_skunder_boghossian_respect","v":{"s":"Study how multiple histories coexist in a work rather than extracting Ethiopian symbols from their meanings."}},{"k":"learning_artist_hokusai_life","v":{"s":"1760–1849"}},{"k":"learning_artist_hokusai_places","v":{"s":"Japan"}},{"k":"learning_artist_hokusai_overview","v":{"s":"Used woodblock design, dramatic cropping, repeated series, and close observation to make everyday labor and landscape feel monumental."}},{"k":"learning_artist_hokusai_lookFor","v":{"s":"Strong silhouettes, compressed depth, directional movement, foreground cropping, and recurring viewpoints."}},{"k":"learning_artist_hokusai_context","v":{"s":"Ukiyo-e prints were collaborative works involving designer, carver, printer, and publisher—not the product of one isolated hand."}},{"k":"learning_artist_hokusai_tryThis","v":{"s":"Compose the same place from three viewpoints using only flat shapes and a four-color palette."}},{"k":"learning_artist_hokusai_respect","v":{"s":"Name the collaborative print process and avoid treating Japanese design as a timeless exotic aesthetic."}},{"k":"learning_artist_amrita_sher_gil_life","v":{"s":"1913–1941"}},{"k":"learning_artist_amrita_sher_gil_places","v":{"s":"India and Hungary"}},{"k":"learning_artist_amrita_sher_gil_overview","v":{"s":"Joined European painting study with sustained attention to people, color, and social life in India, refusing an easy division between East and West."}},{"k":"learning_artist_amrita_sher_gil_lookFor","v":{"s":"Weighted figures, quiet group psychology, earthy color, simplified volume, and carefully held space."}},{"k":"learning_artist_amrita_sher_gil_context","v":{"s":"Her work belongs to histories of Indian modernism, migration, gender, and the unequal conditions through which art histories are written."}},{"k":"learning_artist_amrita_sher_gil_tryThis","v":{"s":"Arrange three simplified figures so posture and spacing communicate a relationship without facial detail."}},{"k":"learning_artist_amrita_sher_gil_respect","v":{"s":"Study composition and social attention rather than using clothing or identity as costume."}},{"k":"learning_artist_pacita_abad_life","v":{"s":"1946–2004"}},{"k":"learning_artist_pacita_abad_places","v":{"s":"The Philippines and a global studio practice"}},{"k":"learning_artist_pacita_abad_overview","v":{"s":"Created exuberant trapunto paintings by stitching, stuffing, painting, and attaching materials to build color into physical relief."}},{"k":"learning_artist_pacita_abad_lookFor","v":{"s":"Quilted depth, accumulated surfaces, portable materials, intense color, and the movement between abstraction and social witness."}},{"k":"learning_artist_pacita_abad_context","v":{"s":"Her global practice grew through travel and relationships; it should not be flattened into a collection of interchangeable cultural motifs."}},{"k":"learning_artist_pacita_abad_tryThis","v":{"s":"Design a relief surface in three layers: base shape, stitched or repeated boundary, and attached texture."}},{"k":"learning_artist_pacita_abad_respect","v":{"s":"Credit specific material traditions when using them and avoid presenting cultural borrowing as placeless “world pattern.”"}},{"k":"learning_artist_yayoi_kusama_life","v":{"s":"1929–2026"}},{"k":"learning_artist_yayoi_kusama_places","v":{"s":"Japan and the United States"}},{"k":"learning_artist_yayoi_kusama_overview","v":{"s":"Uses repetition, mirrored space, accumulation, performance, painting, and sculpture to alter how a viewer experiences body and environment."}},{"k":"learning_artist_yayoi_kusama_lookFor","v":{"s":"Accumulation, serial marks, scale shifts, reflection, immersion, and the point where repetition changes perception."}},{"k":"learning_artist_yayoi_kusama_context","v":{"s":"Her long practice cannot be reduced to polka dots; it includes painting, political performance, publishing, fashion, sculpture, and installation."}},{"k":"learning_artist_yayoi_kusama_tryThis","v":{"s":"Choose one simple mark and vary density and scale until the surrounding space—not the mark itself—becomes the subject."}},{"k":"learning_artist_yayoi_kusama_respect","v":{"s":"Study repetition and perception in Kusama’s work; develop your own visual decisions instead of copying a signature composition."}},{"k":"learning_artist_artemisia_gentileschi_life","v":{"s":"1593–c.1654"}},{"k":"learning_artist_artemisia_gentileschi_places","v":{"s":"Italy"}},{"k":"learning_artist_artemisia_gentileschi_overview","v":{"s":"Built large narrative paintings through forceful gesture, directional light, compressed action, and protagonists with physical presence."}},{"k":"learning_artist_artemisia_gentileschi_lookFor","v":{"s":"Chiaroscuro, diagonals, weight, hands at work, and the moment in a story selected for maximum consequence."}},{"k":"learning_artist_artemisia_gentileschi_context","v":{"s":"Her biography matters, but reducing every painting to personal trauma can erase her professional ambition, learning, patrons, and invention."}},{"k":"learning_artist_artemisia_gentileschi_tryThis","v":{"s":"Stage a three-shape scene where light and diagonal movement identify the decisive moment without adding text."}},{"k":"learning_artist_artemisia_gentileschi_respect","v":{"s":"Do not treat an artist’s suffering as the only explanation for artistic intelligence."}},{"k":"learning_artist_kathe_kollwitz_life","v":{"s":"1867–1945"}},{"k":"learning_artist_kathe_kollwitz_places","v":{"s":"Germany"}},{"k":"learning_artist_kathe_kollwitz_overview","v":{"s":"Used drawing, etching, lithography, woodcut, and sculpture to address grief, labor, poverty, war, care, and resistance."}},{"k":"learning_artist_kathe_kollwitz_lookFor","v":{"s":"Compressed value, expressive hands, repeated figures, carved silhouettes, and empathy without sentimentality."}},{"k":"learning_artist_kathe_kollwitz_context","v":{"s":"Printmaking allowed images to circulate beyond a single painting, joining formal decisions to public witness."}},{"k":"learning_artist_kathe_kollwitz_tryThis","v":{"s":"Tell a social story using only black, paper color, and three values; remove every mark that does not carry meaning."}},{"k":"learning_artist_kathe_kollwitz_respect","v":{"s":"Approach represented suffering with specificity and dignity, not as visual drama detached from people’s lives."}},{"k":"learning_artist_hilma_af_klint_life","v":{"s":"1862–1944"}},{"k":"learning_artist_hilma_af_klint_places","v":{"s":"Sweden"}},{"k":"learning_artist_hilma_af_klint_overview","v":{"s":"Developed large abstract systems of color, geometry, notation, and organic form years before abstraction entered the standard modernist story."}},{"k":"learning_artist_hilma_af_klint_lookFor","v":{"s":"Paired forms, spirals, diagrams, botanical growth, letter-like signs, scale, and sequences across groups of works."}},{"k":"learning_artist_hilma_af_klint_context","v":{"s":"Her practice joined artistic experiment, spiritual inquiry, scientific curiosity, collaboration, and careful systems of documentation."}},{"k":"learning_artist_hilma_af_klint_tryThis","v":{"s":"Invent five nonverbal forms for growth, tension, balance, change, and return; arrange them as a visual argument."}},{"k":"learning_artist_hilma_af_klint_respect","v":{"s":"Distinguish studying symbolic systems from claiming that unfamiliar spiritual signs have meanings you invented."}},{"k":"learning_artist_bridget_riley_life","v":{"s":"born 1931"}},{"k":"learning_artist_bridget_riley_places","v":{"s":"United Kingdom"}},{"k":"learning_artist_bridget_riley_overview","v":{"s":"Builds precise arrangements of line, interval, contrast, and color that make perception feel unstable and active."}},{"k":"learning_artist_bridget_riley_lookFor","v":{"s":"Rhythm, optical vibration, repeated intervals, figure-ground reversal, and movement produced without animation."}},{"k":"learning_artist_bridget_riley_context","v":{"s":"Op art is not merely an illusion trick; it asks how seeing unfolds over time in an embodied viewer."}},{"k":"learning_artist_bridget_riley_tryThis","v":{"s":"Change one interval across a repeated grid and record where still pattern begins to appear mobile."}},{"k":"learning_artist_bridget_riley_respect","v":{"s":"Riley is a living artist. Investigate perceptual variables rather than copying a recognizable composition."}},{"k":"learning_artist_tarsila_do_amaral_life","v":{"s":"1886–1973"}},{"k":"learning_artist_tarsila_do_amaral_places","v":{"s":"Brazil"}},{"k":"learning_artist_tarsila_do_amaral_overview","v":{"s":"Combined vivid color, transformed bodies and landscapes, industrial change, and Brazilian modernist debates into an unmistakable visual language."}},{"k":"learning_artist_tarsila_do_amaral_lookFor","v":{"s":"Elastic scale, simplified volume, saturated local color, landscape-body relationships, and tension between city and countryside."}},{"k":"learning_artist_tarsila_do_amaral_context","v":{"s":"Brazilian modernism wrestled with colonial inheritance and national identity; cultural cannibalism was a critical strategy, not a decorative theme."}},{"k":"learning_artist_tarsila_do_amaral_tryThis","v":{"s":"Exaggerate the scale of one ordinary form to show how power or attention operates in a place you know."}},{"k":"learning_artist_tarsila_do_amaral_respect","v":{"s":"Study transformation and national self-definition without turning Brazilian identity into tropical shorthand."}},{"k":"learning_artist_wifredo_lam_life","v":{"s":"1902–1982"}},{"k":"learning_artist_wifredo_lam_places","v":{"s":"Cuba, Spain, and France"}},{"k":"learning_artist_wifredo_lam_overview","v":{"s":"Created hybrid, compressed figures amid cane-like vegetation while confronting colonialism and the European appetite for primitivism."}},{"k":"learning_artist_wifredo_lam_lookFor","v":{"s":"Mask-like heads, blade forms, unstable bodies, dense vertical space, and figures that resist easy reading."}},{"k":"learning_artist_wifredo_lam_context","v":{"s":"Lam engaged Afro-Cuban histories and modernism while rejecting the treatment of African and Caribbean culture as raw material for Europe."}},{"k":"learning_artist_wifredo_lam_tryThis","v":{"s":"Construct a figure from plant, tool, and body shapes so no single category fully explains it."}},{"k":"learning_artist_wifredo_lam_respect","v":{"s":"Do not call unfamiliar sacred or cultural forms “primitive,” and do not detach Afro-Cuban references from colonial history."}},{"k":"learning_artist_frida_kahlo_life","v":{"s":"1907–1954"}},{"k":"learning_artist_frida_kahlo_places","v":{"s":"Mexico"}},{"k":"learning_artist_frida_kahlo_overview","v":{"s":"Made tightly constructed paintings in which body, disability, clothing, plants, politics, place, and self-representation carry layered meanings."}},{"k":"learning_artist_frida_kahlo_lookFor","v":{"s":"Direct gaze, compressed symbols, doubled selves, bodily specificity, staged space, and objects functioning as evidence."}},{"k":"learning_artist_frida_kahlo_context","v":{"s":"Her work exceeds the simplified label “pain transformed into art”; it also involves humor, politics, national identity, intimacy, and deliberate self-fashioning."}},{"k":"learning_artist_frida_kahlo_tryThis","v":{"s":"Create a symbolic self-portrait without drawing a face: choose five objects and explain what relationship each one carries."}},{"k":"learning_artist_frida_kahlo_respect","v":{"s":"Do not romanticize disability or reduce a complex artist to trauma and inspirational perseverance."}},{"k":"learning_artist_joaquin_torres_garcia_life","v":{"s":"1874–1949"}},{"k":"learning_artist_joaquin_torres_garcia_places","v":{"s":"Uruguay, Spain, and France"}},{"k":"learning_artist_joaquin_torres_garcia_overview","v":{"s":"Organized grids, pictographic signs, proportion, and a School of the South that reoriented modern art away from Europe as the automatic center."}},{"k":"learning_artist_joaquin_torres_garcia_lookFor","v":{"s":"Modular grids, unequal rectangles, compact signs, primary colors, and relationships between universal systems and local place."}},{"k":"learning_artist_joaquin_torres_garcia_context","v":{"s":"His inverted map of South America made orientation itself an argument: north need not determine cultural authority."}},{"k":"learning_artist_joaquin_torres_garcia_tryThis","v":{"s":"Design a grid-map of your community using only ten personal symbols, then rotate it and ask what the new orientation changes."}},{"k":"learning_artist_joaquin_torres_garcia_respect","v":{"s":"Invent symbols from your own life instead of borrowing Indigenous signs as supposedly universal marks."}},{"k":"learning_artist_etel_adnan_life","v":{"s":"1925–2021"}},{"k":"learning_artist_etel_adnan_places","v":{"s":"Lebanon, France, and the United States"}},{"k":"learning_artist_etel_adnan_overview","v":{"s":"Moved among poetry, painting, tapestry, leporello books, journalism, and philosophy, often returning to compact landscapes and the changing presence of a mountain."}},{"k":"learning_artist_etel_adnan_lookFor","v":{"s":"Small fields of strong color, horizon, sun, folded sequence, repeated place, and the exchange between writing and image."}},{"k":"learning_artist_etel_adnan_context","v":{"s":"Her multilingual, diasporic practice resists being assigned to one nation, language, medium, or identity."}},{"k":"learning_artist_etel_adnan_tryThis","v":{"s":"Observe the same view at three times and reduce each version to five color shapes; bind them into a sequence."}},{"k":"learning_artist_etel_adnan_respect","v":{"s":"Treat migration and multilingual identity as lived complexity, not as an exotic source of visual hybridity."}},{"k":"learning_artist_shirin_neshat_life","v":{"s":"born 1957"}},{"k":"learning_artist_shirin_neshat_places","v":{"s":"Iran and the United States"}},{"k":"learning_artist_shirin_neshat_overview","v":{"s":"Uses photography, film, sound, performance, and divided installations to examine power, gender, exile, collective voice, and representation."}},{"k":"learning_artist_shirin_neshat_lookFor","v":{"s":"Black-white contrast, opposing screens, gaze, calligraphic overlay, sound across space, and individuals positioned within groups."}},{"k":"learning_artist_shirin_neshat_context","v":{"s":"Her work addresses Iranian and diasporic histories while also questioning Western expectations about Muslim women."}},{"k":"learning_artist_shirin_neshat_tryThis","v":{"s":"Storyboard two simultaneous viewpoints on the same event and decide what each frame allows or withholds."}},{"k":"learning_artist_shirin_neshat_respect","v":{"s":"Neshat is a living artist. Do not imitate her signature imagery or use pseudo-calligraphy; study viewpoint, opposition, and spectatorship."}},{"k":"learning_artist_monir_farmanfarmaian_life","v":{"s":"1922–2019"}},{"k":"learning_artist_monir_farmanfarmaian_places","v":{"s":"Iran and the United States"}},{"k":"learning_artist_monir_farmanfarmaian_overview","v":{"s":"Joined mirror mosaic, reverse-glass painting, geometry, craft collaboration, and modern abstraction in radiant constructed works."}},{"k":"learning_artist_monir_farmanfarmaian_lookFor","v":{"s":"Reflection, polygon systems, cut modules, changing light, symmetry, and the viewer becoming part of the surface."}},{"k":"learning_artist_monir_farmanfarmaian_context","v":{"s":"Her work grew through Iranian architectural and craft traditions as well as international abstraction; neither side is a decorative footnote."}},{"k":"learning_artist_monir_farmanfarmaian_tryThis","v":{"s":"Build a symmetric polygon system whose appearance changes when a light source or viewer position moves."}},{"k":"learning_artist_monir_farmanfarmaian_respect","v":{"s":"Credit mirror-work traditions and workshop collaboration rather than describing the work as geometry discovered by modernism alone."}},{"k":"learning_artist_laila_shawa_life","v":{"s":"1940–2022"}},{"k":"learning_artist_laila_shawa_places","v":{"s":"Palestine and the United Kingdom"}},{"k":"learning_artist_laila_shawa_overview","v":{"s":"Combined screenprint, photography, painting, text, pattern, and pop color to confront occupation, gender, violence, propaganda, and mass media."}},{"k":"learning_artist_laila_shawa_lookFor","v":{"s":"Repetition, photographic fragments, bright color against difficult content, fences or grids, and images transformed through printing."}},{"k":"learning_artist_laila_shawa_context","v":{"s":"Surface attraction and political critique operate together; brightness does not make the subject uncomplicated."}},{"k":"learning_artist_laila_shawa_tryThis","v":{"s":"Repeat one news-derived shape, changing scale and color to reveal how repetition can normalize or challenge a message."}},{"k":"learning_artist_laila_shawa_respect","v":{"s":"Keep political images connected to real histories and people; do not aestheticize violence into an empty pattern."}},{"k":"learning_artist_alma_thomas_life","v":{"s":"1891–1978"}},{"k":"learning_artist_alma_thomas_places","v":{"s":"United States"}},{"k":"learning_artist_alma_thomas_overview","v":{"s":"Developed luminous abstractions from gardens, music, light, and space exploration after a long career as a public-school art teacher."}},{"k":"learning_artist_alma_thomas_lookFor","v":{"s":"Broken color marks, white intervals, vertical and circular rhythm, optical mixing, and movement built from small variation."}},{"k":"learning_artist_alma_thomas_context","v":{"s":"Thomas became Howard University’s first fine-arts graduate and produced her best-known work after retiring from thirty-five years of teaching."}},{"k":"learning_artist_alma_thomas_tryThis","v":{"s":"Build a rhythm from separated color marks, leaving the ground active; vary one interval so the pattern breathes rather than becoming mechanical."}},{"k":"learning_artist_alma_thomas_respect","v":{"s":"Study rhythm, nature, and late-life experimentation rather than copying a signature mosaic surface."}},{"k":"learning_artist_ruth_asawa_life","v":{"s":"1926–2013"}},{"k":"learning_artist_ruth_asawa_places","v":{"s":"United States; Japanese American"}},{"k":"learning_artist_ruth_asawa_overview","v":{"s":"Created suspended looped-wire forms whose interior and exterior remain visible, while also building arts education and public-making programs."}},{"k":"learning_artist_ruth_asawa_lookFor","v":{"s":"Continuous line in space, nested volume, transparency, shadow, hand process, and structures that hold air rather than conceal it."}},{"k":"learning_artist_ruth_asawa_context","v":{"s":"Her work connects craft knowledge, experimental education, unjust wartime incarceration, family, public art, and sustained community organizing."}},{"k":"learning_artist_ruth_asawa_tryThis","v":{"s":"Model a volume using only a continuous line or mesh; make its shadow a second composition."}},{"k":"learning_artist_ruth_asawa_respect","v":{"s":"Do not use incarceration as an inspirational prelude; recognize it as state violence within a larger life and practice."}},{"k":"learning_artist_jacob_lawrence_life","v":{"s":"1917–2000"}},{"k":"learning_artist_jacob_lawrence_places","v":{"s":"United States"}},{"k":"learning_artist_jacob_lawrence_overview","v":{"s":"Built narrative series from repeated colors, angular figures, research, text, and scenes of migration, labor, resistance, and everyday life."}},{"k":"learning_artist_jacob_lawrence_lookFor","v":{"s":"Series structure, recurring palette, diagonals, compressed rooms, repeated figures, and the relation between caption and image."}},{"k":"learning_artist_jacob_lawrence_context","v":{"s":"The Migration Series treats history through many connected panels, making movement and collective experience structural rather than incidental."}},{"k":"learning_artist_jacob_lawrence_tryThis","v":{"s":"Tell one community change in four panels using a fixed six-color palette and one recurring shape."}},{"k":"learning_artist_jacob_lawrence_respect","v":{"s":"Research the people and history represented; do not turn collective struggle into a generic heroic storyline."}},{"k":"learning_artist_maria_martinez_life","v":{"s":"c.1887–1980"}},{"k":"learning_artist_maria_martinez_places","v":{"s":"San Ildefonso Pueblo, United States"}},{"k":"learning_artist_maria_martinez_overview","v":{"s":"Worked with family and community collaborators to refine celebrated black-on-black pottery grounded in Pueblo knowledge and material practice."}},{"k":"learning_artist_maria_martinez_lookFor","v":{"s":"Form, burnished and matte contrast, firing knowledge, surface-light relationships, and the precision of a vessel as a whole."}},{"k":"learning_artist_maria_martinez_context","v":{"s":"Maria Martinez’s pottery is inseparable from San Ildefonso Pueblo, family collaboration, clay knowledge, firing, and the pressures of an outside art market."}},{"k":"learning_artist_maria_martinez_tryThis","v":{"s":"Design a vessel through silhouette and two surface finishes; explain how light—not borrowed motif—creates contrast."}},{"k":"learning_artist_maria_martinez_respect","v":{"s":"Pueblo designs are not a pattern pack. Credit Maria, Julian Martinez, family collaborators, San Ildefonso Pueblo, and living pottery traditions."}},{"k":"learning_artist_emily_kame_kngwarreye_life","v":{"s":"c.1910–1996"}},{"k":"learning_artist_emily_kame_kngwarreye_places","v":{"s":"Anmatyerr Country, Australia"}},{"k":"learning_artist_emily_kame_kngwarreye_overview","v":{"s":"Began painting on canvas late in life after decades of cultural and artistic work, creating varied paintings grounded in Alhalker Country and Anmatyerr knowledge."}},{"k":"learning_artist_emily_kame_kngwarreye_lookFor","v":{"s":"Gesture, seasonal change, layered mark, scale, Country, and dramatic shifts between dense fields and spare lines."}},{"k":"learning_artist_emily_kame_kngwarreye_context","v":{"s":"The work is not generic abstraction: it arises from Country, kinship, plants, ceremony, and knowledge that viewers do not automatically possess."}},{"k":"learning_artist_emily_kame_kngwarreye_tryThis","v":{"s":"Map change in a place you personally know through gesture, density, and season rather than copying dots or cultural symbols."}},{"k":"learning_artist_emily_kame_kngwarreye_respect","v":{"s":"Do not copy Anmatyerr marks or claim their meanings. Learn from sustained attention to your own relationship with place."}},{"k":"learning_artist_lisa_reihana_life","v":{"s":"born 1964"}},{"k":"learning_artist_lisa_reihana_places","v":{"s":"Aotearoa New Zealand; Māori"}},{"k":"learning_artist_lisa_reihana_overview","v":{"s":"Uses photography, moving image, sound, performance, costume, and digital compositing to question colonial representation and reactivate histories."}},{"k":"learning_artist_lisa_reihana_lookFor","v":{"s":"Panoramic sequence, staged encounter, gaze, costume, sound, quotation, and the difference between being pictured and representing oneself."}},{"k":"learning_artist_lisa_reihana_context","v":{"s":"Her work often speaks back to European images of the Pacific rather than simply illustrating the historical record they created."}},{"k":"learning_artist_lisa_reihana_tryThis","v":{"s":"Take one historical image and storyboard what occurs immediately outside its frame from another participant’s viewpoint."}},{"k":"learning_artist_lisa_reihana_respect","v":{"s":"Reihana is a living Māori artist. Study counter-narrative and framing; do not imitate culturally specific imagery or performance."}},{"k":"learning_artist_yuki_kihara_life","v":{"s":"born 1975"}},{"k":"learning_artist_yuki_kihara_places","v":{"s":"Sāmoa and Aotearoa New Zealand"}},{"k":"learning_artist_yuki_kihara_overview","v":{"s":"Works across photography, performance, video, dance, and curating to examine colonial imagery, climate, gender, labor, and Sāmoan histories."}},{"k":"learning_artist_yuki_kihara_lookFor","v":{"s":"Re-enactment, serial photographs, pose, archival quotation, costume, absence, and who controls the camera."}},{"k":"learning_artist_yuki_kihara_context","v":{"s":"Kihara’s perspective as a faʻafafine artist is specific; it should not be translated into a generic Western category or spectacle."}},{"k":"learning_artist_yuki_kihara_tryThis","v":{"s":"Restage the composition—not the identity or costume—of an archival image and change who has agency in the frame."}},{"k":"learning_artist_yuki_kihara_respect","v":{"s":"Kihara is a living artist. Use the work to study power in representation, not to imitate Sāmoan or faʻafafine identity."}},{"k":"learning_artist_fiona_foley_life","v":{"s":"born 1964"}},{"k":"learning_artist_fiona_foley_places","v":{"s":"Badtjala Country, Australia"}},{"k":"learning_artist_fiona_foley_overview","v":{"s":"Uses sculpture, photography, public art, text, and research to expose colonial violence, contested language, memory, and Badtjala histories."}},{"k":"learning_artist_fiona_foley_lookFor","v":{"s":"Encoded text, archival evidence, public placement, material symbolism, withheld information, and work that changes as history is uncovered."}},{"k":"learning_artist_fiona_foley_context","v":{"s":"Her projects demonstrate that public monuments and official archives are active political forms, not neutral containers of facts."}},{"k":"learning_artist_fiona_foley_tryThis","v":{"s":"Identify a phrase or omission in a local public record and design a nonliteral memorial that asks viewers to investigate it."}},{"k":"learning_artist_fiona_foley_respect","v":{"s":"Foley is a living Badtjala artist. Research local Indigenous authority and history rather than borrowing her symbols or speaking for her community."}},{"k":"learning_category_all_regions","v":{"s":"All regions"}},{"k":"learning_category_africa","v":{"s":"Africa"}},{"k":"learning_category_asia","v":{"s":"Asia"}},{"k":"learning_category_europe","v":{"s":"Europe"}},{"k":"learning_category_latin_america_caribbean","v":{"s":"Latin America & Caribbean"}},{"k":"learning_category_middle_east_north_africa","v":{"s":"Middle East & North Africa"}},{"k":"learning_category_north_america","v":{"s":"North America"}},{"k":"learning_category_oceania","v":{"s":"Oceania"}},{"k":"learning_category_all_eras","v":{"s":"All eras"}},{"k":"learning_category_early_modern","v":{"s":"Early modern"}},{"k":"learning_category_modern","v":{"s":"Modern"}},{"k":"learning_category_contemporary","v":{"s":"Contemporary"}},{"k":"learning_category_all_media","v":{"s":"All media"}},{"k":"learning_category_painting_drawing","v":{"s":"Painting & drawing"}},{"k":"learning_category_printmaking","v":{"s":"Printmaking"}},{"k":"learning_category_sculpture","v":{"s":"Sculpture"}},{"k":"learning_category_ceramics","v":{"s":"Ceramics"}},{"k":"learning_category_textiles_pattern_design","v":{"s":"Textiles, pattern & design"}},{"k":"learning_category_photography_video","v":{"s":"Photography & video"}},{"k":"learning_category_installation_mixed_media","v":{"s":"Installation & mixed media"}},{"k":"learning_artist_comparison_prompt_0","v":{"s":"What appears similar at first, and what different histories or purposes change its meaning?"}},{"k":"learning_artist_comparison_prompt_1","v":{"s":"How does each material or process shape what the artist can ask a viewer to notice?"}},{"k":"learning_artist_comparison_prompt_2","v":{"s":"Which underlying decision could you translate into your own context without copying identity, symbols, or a signature style?"}},{"k":"learning_update_palette_in_thread_kit_22e10e4","v":{"s":"Update palette in Thread Kit"}},{"k":"learning_add_palette_to_thread_kit_298303d","v":{"s":"Add palette to Thread Kit"}},{"k":"learning_use_palette_in_pixel_art_503ec14"