tuning — chassis adjustments"}},{"k":"8_levers_a_setup_engineer_pulls_to_bal","v":{"s":"8 levers a setup engineer pulls to balance the car. Some are pre-race only; some are mid-race adjustments at every pit stop."}},{"k":"what_it_is_3","v":{"s":"🎯 What it is: "}},{"k":"when_to_use","v":{"s":"🧪 When to use: "}},{"k":"adjustment_cycle","v":{"s":"🔄 Adjustment cycle: "}},{"k":"driver_radio_crew_chief_diagnosis","v":{"s":"📻 Driver radio → crew chief diagnosis"}},{"k":"pick_a_driver_radio_quote_see_what_it_","v":{"s":"Pick a driver-radio quote. See what it means + likely cause + which adjustment lever to pull. This is the diagnostic vocabulary of every crew chief."}},{"k":"meaning","v":{"s":"🔍 Meaning: "}},{"k":"likely_causes","v":{"s":"🎯 Likely causes: "}},{"k":"adjust","v":{"s":"🔧 Adjust: "}},{"k":"maine_northeast_racing","v":{"s":"🌲 Maine + Northeast racing"}},{"k":"active_short_tracks","v":{"s":"🏁 Active short tracks"}},{"k":"major_series","v":{"s":"🏆 Major series"}},{"k":"how_to_start_volunteering","v":{"s":"🚪 How to start volunteering"}},{"k":"race_mechanic_sections","v":{"s":"Race mechanic sections"}},{"k":"6_phases_triage_to_daily_driver","v":{"s":"🚗 6 phases — triage to daily-driver"}},{"k":"tap_a_phase_to_see_the_tasks_check_off","v":{"s":"Tap a phase to see the tasks. Check off as you complete each. Total tasks: "}},{"k":"completed","v":{"s":" · Completed: "}},{"k":"goal","v":{"s":"🎯 Goal: "}},{"k":"triage_scoring_rubric","v":{"s":"🎯 Triage scoring rubric"}},{"k":"score_the_candidate_before_you_commit_","v":{"s":"Score the candidate before you commit. Two MUST-PASS items are deal-breakers regardless of score. Otherwise: total ≥80 = buy. 60-79 = negotiate hard. <60 = walk."}},{"k":"good","v":{"s":"✅ Good = "}},{"k":"project_car_sections","v":{"s":"Project car sections"}},{"k":"diesel_heavy_equipment_maine_s_working","v":{"s":"🚜 Diesel + heavy equipment — Maine's working economy"}},{"k":"entry","v":{"s":"🔰 Entry"}},{"k":"mid","v":{"s":"⚙️ Mid"}},{"k":"senior","v":{"s":"🏆 Senior"}},{"k":"specialist","v":{"s":"🎯 Specialist"}},{"k":"ase_certifications","v":{"s":"🎓 ASE certifications"}},{"k":"maine_schools","v":{"s":"🏫 Maine schools"}},{"k":"where_the_work_is","v":{"s":"🌲 Where the work is"}},{"k":"what_s_different_from_gasoline","v":{"s":"🔄 What's different from gasoline"}},{"k":"8_key_differences_a_tech_transitioning","v":{"s":"8 key differences a tech transitioning to diesel needs to know."}},{"k":"what_it_is_4","v":{"s":"🔍 What it is: "}},{"k":"implication","v":{"s":"🎯 Implication: "}},{"k":"diesel_specific_obd_codes","v":{"s":"🔌 Diesel-specific OBD codes"}},{"k":"codes_you_ll_see_on_diesel_pickups_hea","v":{"s":"Codes you'll see on diesel pickups + heavy trucks. Most are emissions-related (DPF / DEF / SCR)."}},{"k":"fix","v":{"s":"🔧 Fix: "}},{"k":"maine_heavy_equipment_specialties","v":{"s":"🚛 Maine heavy-equipment specialties"}},{"k":"5_distinct_maine_career_paths_each_pay","v":{"s":"5 distinct Maine career paths. Each pays well + has more demand than supply of trained techs."}},{"k":"what_it_is_5","v":{"s":"What it is"}},{"k":"typical_equipment","v":{"s":"Typical equipment"}},{"k":"maintenance_focus","v":{"s":"Maintenance focus"}},{"k":"maine_pay","v":{"s":"🌲 Maine pay"}},{"k":"schooling_2","v":{"s":"🎓 Schooling"}},{"k":"diesel_sections","v":{"s":"Diesel sections"}},{"k":"small_engine_powersports_maine_s_recre","v":{"s":"🛷 Small engine + powersports — Maine's recreation economy"}},{"k":"the_seasonal_stack","v":{"s":"📅 The seasonal stack"}},{"k":"entry_2","v":{"s":"🔰 Entry"}},{"k":"mid_2","v":{"s":"⚙️ Mid"}},{"k":"senior_2","v":{"s":"🏆 Senior"}},{"k":"schooling_3","v":{"s":"🎓 Schooling: "}},{"k":"6_powersport_platforms","v":{"s":"🏷️ 6 powersport platforms"}},{"k":"each_engine_type_key_annual_service_ma","v":{"s":"Each: engine type, key annual service, Maine peak season, common failures, career path."}},{"k":"engine","v":{"s":"⚙️ Engine"}},{"k":"key_annual_service","v":{"s":"🔧 Key annual service"}},{"k":"maine_peak_season","v":{"s":"📅 Maine peak season"}},{"k":"most_common_failures","v":{"s":"🚩 Most common failures"}},{"k":"career_path_2","v":{"s":"🎓 Career path"}},{"k":"2_stroke_vs_4_stroke_what_changes","v":{"s":"⚙️ 2-stroke vs 4-stroke — what changes"}},{"k":"two_engine_architectures_with_very_dif","v":{"s":"Two engine architectures with very different service realities. 2-strokes are simpler but less forgiving (no oil = seized engine in 30 sec)."}},{"k":"2_stroke","v":{"s":"🔄 2-stroke"}},{"k":"4_stroke","v":{"s":"🔁 4-stroke"}},{"k":"carburetor_basics","v":{"s":"🔧 Carburetor basics"}},{"k":"most_modern_cars_are_fuel_injected_but","v":{"s":"Most modern cars are fuel-injected, but small engines are often still carbureted. Knowing carbs is core to small-engine + older-vehicle work. The #1 spring-failure cause: old fuel sitting in carb all winter."}},{"k":"tip","v":{"s":"💡 Tip: "}},{"k":"powersports_sections","v":{"s":"Powersports sections"}},{"k":"a_4_week_curated_walkthrough","v":{"s":"🛤️ A 4-week curated walkthrough"}},{"k":"new_here_this_is_the_most_valuable_4_w","v":{"s":"New here? This is the most valuable 4 weeks you can spend in this tool. "}},{"k":"each_week","v":{"s":"Each week: "}},{"k":"theme_3_6_target_modules_measurable_ou","v":{"s":"theme + 3-6 target modules + measurable outcome. "}},{"k":"decode_any_tire_size","v":{"s":"📏 Decode any tire size"}},{"k":"every_tire_has_a_label_like","v":{"s":"Every tire has a label like "}},{"k":"on_the_sidewall_each_piece_tells_you_s","v":{"s":" on the sidewall. Each piece tells you something specific."}},{"k":"5_tire_types","v":{"s":"☀️❄️ 5 tire types"}},{"k":"different_rubber_compounds_tread_desig","v":{"s":"Different rubber compounds + tread designs for different conditions. Each one has Maine-specific tradeoffs."}},{"k":"best_for","v":{"s":"🎯 Best for: "}},{"k":"maine_pros","v":{"s":"✅ Maine pros: "}},{"k":"maine_cons","v":{"s":"❌ Maine cons: "}},{"k":"treadwear","v":{"s":"📊 Treadwear: "}},{"k":"verdict_2","v":{"s":"🌲 Verdict: "}},{"k":"rotation_patterns_by_drive_type","v":{"s":"🔄 Rotation patterns by drive type"}},{"k":"different_drive_systems_wear_tires_dif","v":{"s":"Different drive systems wear tires differently. The pattern matters — wrong rotation = uneven wear + (on AWD) drivetrain damage."}},{"k":"pattern","v":{"s":"↔️ Pattern: "}},{"k":"detail_2","v":{"s":"🔍 Detail: "}},{"k":"interval","v":{"s":"📅 Interval: "}},{"k":"when_to_replace","v":{"s":"🚩 When to replace"}},{"k":"7_conditions_that_mean_replacement_any","v":{"s":"7 conditions that mean replacement. Any one of these = new tire. Multiple = often a full set."}},{"k":"tire_sections","v":{"s":"Tire sections"}},{"k":"60_second_daily_check","v":{"s":"🚶 60-second daily check"}},{"k":"pro_drivers_truckers_walk_around_their","v":{"s":"Pro drivers + truckers walk around their vehicles before EVERY drive. 60 seconds catches 90% of \"I would have wished I noticed before driving\" surprises. Especially valuable in Maine winter when problems hide."}},{"k":"build_the_habit","v":{"s":"Build the habit: "}},{"k":"use_this_once_today_as_a_checklist_aft","v":{"s":"use this once today as a checklist; after a week you'll do it from memory in under a minute. "}},{"k":"reset_walk_around","v":{"s":"Reset walk-around"}},{"k":"reset_2","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"check_2","v":{"s":"👀 Check: "}},{"k":"flag","v":{"s":"🚩 Flag: "}},{"k":"first_log_entry","v":{"s":"First Log Entry"}},{"k":"log_keeper","v":{"s":"Log Keeper"}},{"k":"inspection_self_walk","v":{"s":"Inspection Self-Walk"}},{"k":"maine_winter_prepped","v":{"s":"Maine Winter Prepped"}},{"k":"trunk_kit_packed","v":{"s":"Trunk Kit Packed"}},{"k":"30_day_plan_complete","v":{"s":"30-Day Plan Complete"}},{"k":"walk_around_pro","v":{"s":"Walk-Around Pro"}},{"k":"tire_pro","v":{"s":"Tire Pro"}},{"k":"obd_explorer","v":{"s":"OBD Explorer"}},{"k":"listener","v":{"s":"Listener"}},{"k":"fluid_reader","v":{"s":"Fluid Reader"}},{"k":"visual_inspector","v":{"s":"Visual Inspector"}},{"k":"decision_tree_explorer","v":{"s":"Decision Tree Explorer"}},{"k":"lab_master","v":{"s":"Lab Master"}},{"k":"damage_id_ace","v":{"s":"Damage ID Ace"}},{"k":"safety_jack_stands","v":{"s":"Safety: Jack stands"}},{"k":"safety_electrical","v":{"s":"Safety: Electrical"}},{"k":"safety_refrigerant","v":{"s":"Safety: Refrigerant"}},{"k":"safety_hot_exhaust","v":{"s":"Safety: Hot exhaust"}},{"k":"safety_spring_tension","v":{"s":"Safety: Spring tension"}},{"k":"safety_fluid_disposal","v":{"s":"Safety: Fluid disposal"}},{"k":"used_car_buyer","v":{"s":"Used Car Buyer"}},{"k":"estimate_decoder_2","v":{"s":"Estimate Decoder"}},{"k":"scam_aware","v":{"s":"Scam Aware"}},{"k":"ev_safety_aware","v":{"s":"EV Safety Aware"}},{"k":"race_crew_explorer","v":{"s":"Race Crew Explorer"}},{"k":"race_radio_decoded","v":{"s":"Race Radio Decoded"}},{"k":"pit_stop_master","v":{"s":"Pit Stop Master"}},{"k":"project_car_master","v":{"s":"Project Car Master"}},{"k":"diesel_aware","v":{"s":"Diesel Aware"}},{"k":"quiz_passed","v":{"s":"Quiz Passed"}},{"k":"curriculum_path_graduate","v":{"s":"Curriculum Path Graduate"}},{"k":"curriculum_mastery","v":{"s":"Curriculum mastery"}},{"k":"pre_ignition_knock","v":{"s":"💥 Pre-ignition / knock"}},{"k":"too_much_advance_high_compression_spon","v":{"s":"Too much advance + high compression → spontaneous detonation. Engine damage."}},{"k":"misfire","v":{"s":"⚠️ Misfire"}},{"k":"insufficient_timing_or_excessive_overl","v":{"s":"Insufficient timing or excessive overlap → unstable combustion."}},{"k":"smooth_idle","v":{"s":"🟢 Smooth idle"}},{"k":"engine_runs_smoothly_but_not_at_peak_o","v":{"s":"Engine runs smoothly but not at peak output."}},{"k":"peak_performance","v":{"s":"🚀 Peak performance"}},{"k":"sweet_spot_maximum_power_without_deton","v":{"s":"Sweet spot. Maximum power without detonation."}},{"k":"hypothesis_what_combination_triggers_k","v":{"s":"Hypothesis: What combination triggers knock?"}},{"k":"explain_why_timing_must_match_compress","v":{"s":"Explain why timing must match compression and fuel."}},{"k":"battery-test_detail","v":{"s":"Cold weather doubles cranking load while cutting battery output. A weak battery in November is a dead battery in February. Free at NAPA / O'Reilly / AutoZone."}},{"k":"tires-check_detail","v":{"s":"Below 4/32\" tread = unsafe in slush. Below 2/32\" = illegal. Cold drops tire pressure ~1 psi per 10°F drop — a 70°F to 0°F swing drops pressure 7 psi."}},{"k":"antifreeze_detail","v":{"s":"A coolant tester (hydrometer or refractometer, $5–15) tells you the freeze point. Should protect to at least -34°F. Old / contaminated coolant freezes higher."}},{"k":"wiper-fluid_detail","v":{"s":"Standard summer washer fluid freezes around 32°F. In Maine, that fluid sits in the reservoir frozen for 4 months — and shatters the reservoir if it expands."}},{"k":"wipers_detail","v":{"s":"Summer-worn blades chatter on first slush storm. Full-frame \"winter blades\" handle ice better than sleek beam blades."}},{"k":"block-heater_detail","v":{"s":"Block heater = a small heating element in the engine block, plugged in overnight. Warms oil + coolant for easier cold start. Many Maine homes have an outlet near the driveway for exactly this."}},{"k":"oil-grade_detail","v":{"s":"Below 0°F, conventional oil thickens and starves the engine on cold start. Most modern cars spec 0W-20 or 5W-30 full-synthetic — verify yours and switch to synthetic if you're not already."}},{"k":"belts-hoses_detail","v":{"s":"Cold makes rubber stiffer. A cracked serpentine belt that's been \"fine\" all summer can snap on the first -10°F morning. Hoses can burst."}},{"k":"emergency-kit_detail","v":{"s":"Maine rural drivers can be stranded in below-zero temps for hours waiting on AAA or a tow. The trunk kit is genuine survival equipment."}},{"k":"door-locks_detail","v":{"s":"Frozen door locks at 6am on a Tuesday is the most Maine-of-Maine moments. Graphite lock lubricant (NOT oil — oil collects ice)."}},{"k":"windshield-wash_detail","v":{"s":"A small chip in November becomes a coast-to-coast crack on the first -20°F morning when you turn the defroster on. Thermal shock is real."}},{"k":"undercarriage-rinse_detail","v":{"s":"After winter, undercarriage is caked with salt brine. Rinse off ASAP and inspect for new rust scaling on brake/fuel lines, frame, exhaust."}},{"k":"lab-misfire_intro","v":{"s":"Customer drives in a 2014 Toyota Camry. \"Check-engine light is FLASHING and the car shakes hard at stoplights. Started this morning.\""}},{"k":"lab-no-start_intro","v":{"s":"Customer text: \"Won't start. Just clicks. -5°F here in Caribou.\""}},{"k":"lab-brakes_intro","v":{"s":"Customer: \"Pedal shakes hard when I brake from highway speed. Started after winter — fine in spring.\""}},{"k":"lab-overheat_intro","v":{"s":"Customer: \"Temp gauge climbs to red when stopped at lights, drops when I start moving. Highway is fine.\""}},{"k":"lab-noise_intro","v":{"s":"Customer: \"Humming sound that gets louder above 40 mph. Worse turning right than left.\""}},{"k":"lab-leak_intro","v":{"s":"Customer: \"Sweet smell inside the car when the heat is on. Coolant level keeps dropping. No puddle in driveway.\""}},{"k":"no-start_intro","v":{"s":"Pick the symptom that matches what your car is doing right now."}},{"k":"misfire_intro","v":{"s":"Engine is running rough, hesitating, or shaking. Walk through what you're feeling."}},{"k":"brakes_intro","v":{"s":"Something off with the brakes. Pick what you're feeling or hearing."}},{"k":"overheating_intro","v":{"s":"Temp gauge is climbing or the engine is steaming. Pick the situation."}},{"k":"charging_intro","v":{"s":"Dim lights, dashboard battery icon, repeated dead-battery mornings — narrow it down."}},{"k":"steering_intro","v":{"s":"Something's off in how the car steers, tracks, or sounds at the wheels."}},{"k":"module_categories","v":{"s":"Auto Repair module categories"}},{"k":"under_hood_tour_menu","v":{"s":"Under-hood tour (3D)"}},{"k":"spin_the_engine_bay_find_all_12_parts","v":{"s":"Spin the engine bay. Find all 12 parts and learn what each one looks like."}},{"k":"change_a_tyre_menu","v":{"s":"Change a tyre (3D)"}},{"k":"13_steps_in_order_get_the_order_wrong","v":{"s":"13 steps, in order. Get the order wrong and the wheel just spins — or worse."}},{"k":"repair_bay_menu","v":{"s":"Repair Bay (3D)"}},{"k":"7_cases_inspect_test_commit_graded_on_","v":{"s":"7 cases. Inspect the 3D bay, run tests, commit one repair. Graded on evidence and safety."}},{"k":"questions_across_the_full_curriculum","v":{"s":" questions across the full curriculum."}},{"k":"under_hood_navigator","v":{"s":"Under-Hood Navigator"}},{"k":"uh_3d_unavailable","v":{"s":"3D view unavailable on this device or network — every part is still listed below with its location, check, and failure signs."}},{"k":"uh_3d_loading","v":{"s":"Loading the 3D engine bay…"}},{"k":"under_hood_tour","v":{"s":"Under-hood tour"}},{"k":"under_hood_tour_title","v":{"s":"🔎 Under-hood tour"}},{"k":"uh_back_to_case","v":{"s":"← Back to the case you were working"}},{"k":"uh_intro","v":{"s":"Pop the hood and nothing is labelled. This is the map. Drag to spin the bay, tap a part to learn what it is, how to check it, and what it looks like when it goes wrong."}},{"k":"uh_caveat_lead","v":{"s":"Read this first: "}},{"k":"uh_caveat","v":{"s":"this is a generic transverse four-cylinder, left-hand drive. Exact positions vary by make, model, and year — always confirm against your own car and its manual. What transfers is what each part LOOKS like and the one rule you can rely on: the brake fluid reservoir sits on the firewall on the driver's side, because it bolts to the back of the brake pedal's booster."}},{"k":"uh_viewer_label","v":{"s":"Engine bay, 3D"}},{"k":"uh_label_all","v":{"s":"🏷 Label all"}},{"k":"uh_clear","v":{"s":"✕ Clear"}},{"k":"uh_hint","v":{"s":"Drag or arrow keys to spin · scroll or + / − to zoom · 0 resets · tap a part to select it. Everything the 3D view shows is also in the parts list."}},{"k":"uh_parts_heading","v":{"s":"Parts in the bay"}},{"k":"uh_explored","v":{"s":" explored"}},{"k":"uh_where","v":{"s":"Where to look"}},{"k":"uh_what","v":{"s":"What it does"}},{"k":"uh_check","v":{"s":"How to check it"}},{"k":"uh_fail","v":{"s":"What failure looks like"}},{"k":"uh_safety","v":{"s":"Safety"}},{"k":"uh_maine","v":{"s":"Maine reality"}},{"k":"uh_empty","v":{"s":"Pick a part from the list or tap one in the 3D bay to see where it is, how to check it, and what it looks like when it fails."}},{"k":"uh_done_lead","v":{"s":"✓ Every part explored. "}},{"k":"uh_done","v":{"s":"Now do it for real: open your own hood with the engine cold and find all twelve. The ones that are somewhere different on your car are the ones you will actually remember."}},{"k":"repair_bay","v":{"s":"Repair Bay"}},{"k":"repair_bay_title","v":{"s":"🔧 Repair Bay — diagnose & fix"}},{"k":"rb_intro","v":{"s":"A car comes in with a complaint. Inspect it, run the tests that actually separate the possibilities, then commit to one repair. You are graded on your evidence and your safety, not just on getting the right answer."}},{"k":"rb_rule_lead","v":{"s":"The rule this bay teaches: "}},{"k":"rb_rule","v":{"s":"diagnose before you replace. Every case has a wrong answer that looks obvious and costs the customer real money. Guessing right still scores badly here — because on a real car, a guess that happens to work teaches you nothing and the next one strands somebody."}},{"k":"rb_solved","v":{"s":" cases correctly diagnosed"}},{"k":"repair_bay_ace","v":{"s":"Repair Bay Ace"}},{"k":"rb_cases","v":{"s":"← Cases"}},{"k":"rb_complaint","v":{"s":"Customer says"}},{"k":"rb_dash","v":{"s":"On the dash: "}},{"k":"rb_engine","v":{"s":"Engine: "}},{"k":"rb_running","v":{"s":"RUNNING"}},{"k":"rb_off","v":{"s":"OFF"}},{"k":"rb_shutoff","v":{"s":"Shut it off"}},{"k":"rb_start","v":{"s":"Start it"}},{"k":"rb_running_hint","v":{"s":"Some evidence only exists now — charging voltage, whether the fan kicks in. Some inspection is unsafe now."}},{"k":"rb_off_hint","v":{"s":"Safe to inspect belts and open the cooling system. Some tests need it running."}},{"k":"rb_viewer_label","v":{"s":"Engine bay for this case, 3D"}},{"k":"rb_3d_failed","v":{"s":"3D bay unavailable — inspect using the buttons below. Nothing in this case needs the 3D view."}},{"k":"rb_3d_loading","v":{"s":"Loading the bay…"}},{"k":"rb_3d_hint","v":{"s":"Click a part in the bay to inspect it, or use the buttons — they do the same thing. Green = already inspected."}},{"k":"rb_you_see","v":{"s":"You see — "}},{"k":"rb_key_evidence","v":{"s":"✓ Counts as key evidence"}},{"k":"rb_lookup","v":{"s":"📖 What is this part?"}},{"k":"rb_inspect","v":{"s":"Inspect"}},{"k":"rb_tests","v":{"s":"Tests"}},{"k":"rb_needs_engine","v":{"s":"Needs the engine "}},{"k":"rb_evidence","v":{"s":"Key evidence: "}},{"k":"rb_violations","v":{"s":"Safety violations: "}},{"k":"rb_notes_label","v":{"s":"Working notes — what do you think is wrong, and what makes you think it?"}},{"k":"rb_notes_ph","v":{"s":"Optional. Writing the reasoning down before you commit is what turns a guess into a diagnosis."}},{"k":"rb_call_it","v":{"s":"Call it"}},{"k":"rb_call_hint","v":{"s":"Pick one action. You cannot take it back, same as telling a customer."}},{"k":"rb_your_call","v":{"s":"YOUR CALL"}},{"k":"rb_trap","v":{"s":"Trap answer. "}},{"k":"rb_grade","v":{"s":"Grade: "}},{"k":"rb_evidence_gathered","v":{"s":"Evidence gathered before you called it: "}},{"k":"rb_safety","v":{"s":"Safety violations: "}},{"k":"rb_bill","v":{"s":"What the customer pays"}},{"k":"rb_bill_wasted","v":{"s":"Your repair: "}},{"k":"rb_bill_nofix","v":{"s":" — and it did not fix the car."}},{"k":"rb_bill_still","v":{"s":"The repair it still needs: "}},{"k":"rb_bill_total","v":{"s":"Total: "}},{"k":"rb_bill_extra","v":{"s":" of that was avoidable."}},{"k":"rb_bill_only","v":{"s":" — the repair it actually needed, and nothing else."}},{"k":"rb_bill_disclaimer","v":{"s":"Rough teaching figures only, not quotes. Real prices vary a lot by vehicle, region and shop rate."}},{"k":"rb_bill_hg","v":{"s":" The head-gasket job itself typically runs well into four figures at a shop — which is exactly why recognising it and handing it over is the valuable call."}},{"k":"rb_your_notes","v":{"s":"What you wrote before you committed"}},{"k":"rb_right_thin","v":{"s":"Right answer, thin evidence"}},{"k":"rb_right_thin_body","v":{"s":"You landed on the correct repair without collecting everything that proves it. On a real car that is a guess that happened to pay off — and the habit it builds is the one that eventually sells somebody a part they did not need. Reopen the case and find the tests you skipped."}},{"k":"rb_safety_first","v":{"s":"Safety comes before the diagnosis"}},{"k":"rb_safety_body","v":{"s":"A correct diagnosis does not undo an injury. Every violation above describes something that hurts people in real bays, and the habit of checking engine state first is what prevents all of them."}},{"k":"rb_takeaway","v":{"s":"What this case teaches"}},{"k":"rb_retry","v":{"s":"↺ Run it again"}},{"k":"rb_next_case","v":{"s":"Next case →"}},{"k":"roadside_ready","v":{"s":"Roadside Ready"}},{"k":"tc_unsafe","v":{"s":"☠️ Unsafe — this is never the answer"}},{"k":"tc_not_yet","v":{"s":"⏳ Right action, wrong moment"}},{"k":"tc_good","v":{"s":"✓ "}},{"k":"tc_title_aria","v":{"s":"Roadside tyre change"}},{"k":"tc_title","v":{"s":"🛞 Change a tyre"}},{"k":"tc_intro","v":{"s":"Every one of these actions is something you genuinely have to do. The skill is doing them in the right order — get that wrong and at best the wheel spins uselessly, at worst the car comes off the jack."}},{"k":"tc_rule_lead","v":{"s":"The rule that matters most: "}},{"k":"tc_rule","v":{"s":"a jack lifts a car, it does not hold one. Nothing of you goes under a car supported only by a jack — not an arm, not your head, ever. A roadside wheel change never needs you under there."}},{"k":"tc_viewer_label","v":{"s":"Car corner and wheel, 3D"}},{"k":"tc_3d_failed","v":{"s":"3D view unavailable — the full procedure is in the buttons below and nothing here needs the picture."}},{"k":"tc_3d_loading","v":{"s":"Loading the car…"}},{"k":"tc_3d_hint","v":{"s":"The car changes as you work: the chock appears, the jack goes under, the corner lifts, the wheel comes off. Click any part to read what it is. Every action is also a button below."}},{"k":"tc_progress","v":{"s":"Done so far"}},{"k":"tc_misorders","v":{"s":" out-of-order attempts"}},{"k":"tc_unsafe_count","v":{"s":" unsafe"}},{"k":"tc_nothing_yet","v":{"s":"Nothing yet. Pick the action you would take first."}},{"k":"tc_whats_next","v":{"s":"What do you do next?"}},{"k":"tc_already_flagged","v":{"s":"You already tried this — it is still unsafe"}},{"k":"tc_grade","v":{"s":"Wheel changed. Grade: "}},{"k":"tc_summary_wrong","v":{"s":" out-of-order attempts · "}},{"k":"tc_summary_unsafe","v":{"s":" unsafe actions"}},{"k":"tc_unsafe_recap","v":{"s":"The unsafe ones matter more than the grade"}},{"k":"tc_now_real","v":{"s":"Now do it for real, before you need to. "}},{"k":"tc_now_real_body","v":{"s":"Find your jack, your wrench and your spare, and check the spare actually holds air. Read your manual for where the jack points are on your car. A driveway on a dry afternoon is a much better place to learn this than a dark verge in February."}},{"k":"tc_again","v":{"s":"↺ Run it again"}},{"k":"tc_menu","v":{"s":"Back to menu"}},{"k":"hypothesis_input","v":{"s":"Engine timing hypothesis"}},{"k":"explanation_input","v":{"s":"Engine timing explanation"}},{"k":"badges_earned_lower","v":{"s":"badges earned"}},{"k":"build_a_safe_30_day_ownership_routine","v":{"s":"Build a safe 30-day ownership routine."}},{"k":"check_me","v":{"s":"Check me"}},{"k":"choose_the_safe_first_move","v":{"s":"Choose the safe first move."}},{"k":"complete","v":{"s":"Complete"}},{"k":"complete_lower","v":{"s":"complete"}},{"k":"confirmed","v":{"s":"Confirmed"}},{"k":"continue_learning","v":{"s":"Continue learning"}},{"k":"explore_the_full_shop","v":{"s":"Explore the full shop"}},{"k":"garage_learning_dashboard","v":{"s":"Garage learning dashboard"}},{"k":"guided_repair","v":{"s":"Guided repair"}},{"k":"hands_on_modules_active","v":{"s":"hands-on modules active"}},{"k":"i_just_got_a_car","v":{"s":"I just got a car"}},{"k":"i_understand","v":{"s":"I understand: "}},{"k":"im_stuck_roadside","v":{"s":"I’m stuck roadside"}},{"k":"in_progress","v":{"s":"In progress"}},{"k":"incident_decision_drill","v":{"s":"Incident decision drill"}},{"k":"learning_status","v":{"s":"Learning status"}},{"k":"modules_lower","v":{"s":"modules"}},{"k":"modules_to_explore","v":{"s":"modules to explore"}},{"k":"new_driver","v":{"s":"New driver"}},{"k":"open_a_category_then_choose_your_next_skill","v":{"s":"Open a category, then choose your next skill."}},{"k":"ordered_repair_steps","v":{"s":"Ordered repair steps"}},{"k":"pick_your_situation_for_a_fast_start","v":{"s":"Pick your situation for a fast start, or browse every module below."}},{"k":"read_the_clues_before_replacing_parts","v":{"s":"Read the clues before replacing parts."}},{"k":"repair_step_help","v":{"s":"Read the entire procedure before touching a vehicle. In this learning walkthrough, mark each step reviewed in order after clearing the safety check."}},{"k":"repair_workflow_progress","v":{"s":"Repair workflow progress"}},{"k":"reset_safety_check","v":{"s":"Reset safety check"}},{"k":"safety_check","v":{"s":"🛡️ Safety check — clear before step review"}},{"k":"safety_check_intro","v":{"s":"Actively acknowledge each condition. This learning check cannot verify a real vehicle or replace its service manual."}},{"k":"safety_check_locked","v":{"s":" understood — step review locked."}},{"k":"safety_check_progress","v":{"s":"Safety check: "}},{"k":"safety_check_ready","v":{"s":" understood — step review unlocked."}},{"k":"safety_setup","v":{"s":"Safety setup"}},{"k":"something_seems_wrong","v":{"s":"Something seems wrong"}},{"k":"start_the_4_week_learning_path","v":{"s":"Start the 4-week learning path"}},{"k":"symptom_first","v":{"s":"Symptom first"}},{"k":"tc_lug_group","v":{"s":"Five lug nuts arranged around a wheel"}},{"k":"tc_lug_instructions","v":{"s":"Any lug can be first on a real wheel. For this numbered practice, start at lug 1 (12 o’clock), then choose the farthest untightened lug each time. Do not move to the adjacent lug."}},{"k":"tc_lug_progress","v":{"s":"Pattern progress: "}},{"k":"tc_lug_real_note","v":{"s":"On a real wheel, use several gradual passes in this same cross pattern and finish at the vehicle manufacturer’s torque specification. Never guess the torque."}},{"k":"tc_lug_restart","v":{"s":"↺ Restart this pattern"}},{"k":"tc_lug_start","v":{"s":"Start with lug 1"}},{"k":"tc_lug_title","v":{"s":"⭐ Five-lug star-pattern practice"}},{"k":"urgent_safety","v":{"s":"Urgent safety"}},{"k":"view_badge_gallery","v":{"s":"View badge gallery"}},{"k":"walkthrough_complete","v":{"s":"Walkthrough complete"}},{"k":"what_brings_you_into_the_garage","v":{"s":"What brings you into the garage?"}}],"id":487}},{"k":"back","v":{"s":"Back to tools"}},{"k":"bakingscience","v":{"o":[{"k":"sr_stable_emulsion_great_mix","v":{"s":"Stable emulsion. Great mix."}},{"k":"sr_emulsion_broke_adjust_your_ratios","v":{"s":"Emulsion broke. Adjust your ratios."}},{"k":"sr_scenarios_reshuffled","v":{"s":"Scenarios reshuffled."}},{"k":"sr_returned_to_menu","v":{"s":"Returned to menu."}},{"k":"sr_explanation_ready","v":{"s":"Explanation ready."}},{"k":"baking_soda_is_sodium_bicarbonate_nahc","v":{"s":"Baking soda is sodium bicarbonate (NaHCO₃). When it meets an acid, two things happen:"}},{"k":"the_acid_donates_a_proton_h_to_the_bic","v":{"s":"The acid donates a proton (H⁺) to the bicarbonate."}},{"k":"this_makes_carbonic_acid_h_co_which_in","v":{"s":"This makes carbonic acid (H₂CO₃), which instantly falls apart into water and CO₂ gas."}},{"k":"baking_powder","v":{"s":"Baking powder"}},{"k":"already_contains_an_acid_usually_cream","v":{"s":" already contains an acid (usually cream of tartar or sodium aluminum sulfate), so it works without added acid. Many powders are \"double-acting\" — one burst of CO₂ when wet, another when heated."}},{"k":"yeast","v":{"s":"Yeast"}},{"k":"is_a_living_fungus_it_eats_sugars_and_","v":{"s":" is a living fungus. It eats sugars and releases CO₂ and alcohol. Slower than chemical leaveners, but it also develops flavor — that’s why sourdough tastes so different from quick bread."}},{"k":"oil_is_hydrophobic_water_fearing_and_w","v":{"s":"Oil is hydrophobic (\"water-fearing\") and water is hydrophilic. On their own, they separate because oil molecules are nonpolar and water molecules are polar."}},{"k":"emulsifiers","v":{"s":"Emulsifiers"}},{"k":"are_molecules_with_one_water_loving_en","v":{"s":" are molecules with one water-loving end and one oil-loving end — like soap, but edible. Egg yolks are full of one called "}},{"k":"lecithin_coats_tiny_droplets_of_oil_an","v":{"s":". Lecithin coats tiny droplets of oil and keeps them suspended in water."}},{"k":"that_s_why_mayonnaise_hollandaise_and_","v":{"s":"That’s why mayonnaise, hollandaise, and even cake batter hold together: a web of emulsifier-coated droplets."}},{"k":"baker_s_percentages","v":{"s":"Baker’s percentages"}},{"k":"measure_every_ingredient_relative_to_t","v":{"s":" measure every ingredient relative to the flour. If flour is 100%, water at 65% means 650g water per 1000g flour. Bakers use this so they can scale recipes up or down without recalculating ratios."}},{"k":"why_weight_beats_volume","v":{"s":"Why weight beats volume"}},{"k":"a_cup_of_flour_can_weigh_anywhere_from","v":{"s":": a cup of flour can weigh anywhere from 100g to 150g depending on how you scoop it. Grams don’t lie. Professional bakeries always use scales."}},{"k":"doubling_a_recipe_doesn_t_always_doubl","v":{"s":"Doubling a recipe doesn’t always double the bake time. Larger loaves have more insulation — the outside browns while the center catches up. Expect 10-30% longer for a 2× batch."}},{"k":"temperature_unit","v":{"s":"Temperature unit"}},{"k":"cold","v":{"s":"Cold"}},{"k":"warm","v":{"s":"Warm"}},{"k":"baking","v":{"s":"Baking"}},{"k":"crust","v":{"s":"Crust"}},{"k":"burn","v":{"s":"Burn"}},{"k":"steam","v":{"s":"Steam"}},{"k":"maillard","v":{"s":"Maillard"}},{"k":"caramel","v":{"s":"Caramel"}},{"k":"burn_2","v":{"s":"Burn"}},{"k":"maillard_vs_caramelization","v":{"s":"Maillard vs. caramelization"}},{"k":"maillard_reactions_need_protein_amino_","v":{"s":": Maillard reactions need protein (amino acids) + sugar + heat — that’s why bread crust, seared meat, and toasted marshmallows all develop similar brown, complex flavors. Caramelization only needs sugar + heat, and happens a bit hotter."}},{"k":"oven_spring","v":{"s":"Oven spring"}},{"k":"in_the_first_few_minutes_steam_from_th","v":{"s":": in the first few minutes, steam from the dough’s water expands violently. This is why sourdough scoring matters — it gives the steam somewhere to go."}},{"k":"convection_vs_conduction","v":{"s":"Convection vs. conduction"}},{"k":"conventional_ovens_bake_mostly_by_radi","v":{"s":": conventional ovens bake mostly by radiating heat from the walls. Convection ovens move hot air with a fan — about 25°F more effective, so recipes say \"reduce temp by 25°F\" for convection."}},{"k":"leavening","v":{"s":"Leavening"}},{"k":"emulsion","v":{"s":"Emulsion"}},{"k":"ratios","v":{"s":"Ratios"}},{"k":"oven_science","v":{"s":"Oven science"}},{"k":"baking_2","v":{"s":"Baking"}},{"k":"wheat_flour_has_two_proteins","v":{"s":": wheat flour has two proteins — "}},{"k":"when_you_add_water_they_link_up_into_l","v":{"s":". When you add water, they link up into long, elastic strands called "}},{"k":"more_protein_in_the_flour_more_gluten_","v":{"s":". More protein in the flour = more gluten potential."}},{"k":"without_enough_water_the_proteins_can_","v":{"s":": without enough water the proteins can’t unfold and meet each other; too much water and they’re diluted into a soup. The sweet spot for most breads is 60–75% hydration."}},{"k":"each_fold_and_stretch_aligns_the_prote","v":{"s":": each fold and stretch aligns the proteins into parallel sheets. Early kneading builds rapidly; past about 10–15 minutes the network plateaus and eventually tears itself apart (over-kneading)."}},{"k":"cakes_cookies_and_pie_crusts_use_low_p","v":{"s":": cakes, cookies, and pie crusts use low-protein flour and minimal mixing. Fat also "}},{"k":"gluten_strands_that_s_why_butter_makes","v":{"s":" gluten strands — that’s why butter makes pastry flaky."}},{"k":"285_m","v":{"s":"285 M"}},{"k":"320_c","v":{"s":"320 C"}},{"k":"400_burn","v":{"s":"400+ burn"}},{"k":"named_for_louis_camille_maillard_1912_","v":{"s":": named for Louis-Camille Maillard (1912). Amino acids from proteins react with "}},{"k":"reducing_sugars","v":{"s":"reducing sugars"}},{"k":"at_285_f_to_create_hundreds_of_new_fla","v":{"s":" at ~285°F+ to create hundreds of new flavor and aroma compounds. Seared steak, toasted bread, roasted coffee, and browned butter all owe their flavor to Maillard."}},{"k":"pure_sugars_melting_and_breaking_apart","v":{"s":": pure sugars melting and breaking apart around 320°F+. No protein needed. Gives the pure sweet-amber character of caramel sauce, crème brûlée tops, and roasted vegetables with high natural sugar."}},{"k":"neither_reaction_happens_below_212_f_b","v":{"s":": neither reaction happens below 212°F because water caps the surface temperature. This is why patting chicken skin dry before searing is the difference between rubbery and crispy."}},{"k":"above_400_f_carbon_carbon_bonds_break_","v":{"s":": above ~400°F, carbon-carbon bonds break into bitter, acrid pyrolysis products. You can smell it before you see it — burnt toast, scorched garlic, blackened coffee."}},{"k":"plain","v":{"s":"Plain"}},{"k":"using_simple_everyday_words_and_short_","v":{"s":"using simple everyday words and short sentences"}},{"k":"grade_5","v":{"s":"Grade 5"}},{"k":"for_a_5th_grade_student_brief_and_frie","v":{"s":"for a 5th grade student, brief and friendly"}},{"k":"high_school","v":{"s":"High School"}},{"k":"for_a_high_school_chemistry_student_ac","v":{"s":"for a high school chemistry student, accurate but accessible"}},{"k":"ai_baking_tutor","v":{"s":"AI baking tutor"}},{"k":"explain_at_my_level","v":{"s":"✨ Explain at my level"}},{"k":"reading_level","v":{"s":"Reading level"}},{"k":"click_explain_for_an_ai_breakdown_of_t","v":{"s":"Click “Explain” for an AI breakdown of the current activity at your chosen reading level."}},{"k":"raw_sugar","v":{"s":"⚪ Raw sugar"}},{"k":"below_caramelization_threshold_or_not_","v":{"s":"Below caramelization threshold or not heated long enough."}},{"k":"light_amber","v":{"s":"🟡 Light amber"}},{"k":"beginning_caramelization_color_and_fla","v":{"s":"Beginning caramelization. Color and flavor still subtle."}},{"k":"perfect_caramel","v":{"s":"🟠 Perfect caramel"}},{"k":"rich_amber_mahogany_full_caramel_flavo","v":{"s":"Rich amber-mahogany, full caramel flavor compounds present."}},{"k":"burnt_sugar","v":{"s":"⚫ Burnt sugar"}},{"k":"pyrolysis_dominates_bitter_acrid_sugar","v":{"s":"Pyrolysis dominates — bitter, acrid; sugar molecules broken to char."}},{"k":"caramel_discovery","v":{"s":"🍯 Caramel discovery"}},{"k":"temperature","v":{"s":"Temperature"}},{"k":"time","v":{"s":"Time"}},{"k":"log_observation","v":{"s":"📋 Log observation"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"your_hypothesis_free_text_no_right_ans","v":{"s":"Your hypothesis (free text — no right answer):"}},{"k":"which_slider_matters_most_for_hitting_","v":{"s":"Which slider matters most for hitting perfect caramel? Does moisture have a big effect or a small one?"}},{"k":"i_m_stuck_show_me_questions_to_think_a","v":{"s":"🤔 I'm stuck — show me questions to think about (no answers)"}},{"k":"open_prompts_investigate_by_manipulati","v":{"s":"Open prompts — investigate by manipulating:"}},{"k":"hold_two_sliders_steady_move_the_third","v":{"s":"Hold two sliders steady. Move the third. Watch what happens."}},{"k":"log_observations_from_each_of_the_four","v":{"s":"Log observations from each of the four stages. What patterns appear in the table?"}},{"k":"find_two_different_settings_that_both_","v":{"s":"Find two different settings that both produce the same stage. What do they share?"}},{"k":"notice_where_a_small_change_flips_the_","v":{"s":"Notice where a small change flips the stage versus where larger changes do nothing."}},{"k":"real_caramel_chefs_talk_about_controll","v":{"s":"Real caramel chefs talk about \"controlling the rate of Maillard.\" Investigate why moisture matters."}},{"k":"no_answers_no_specific_values_investig","v":{"s":"No answers, no specific values. Investigate."}},{"k":"i_think_i_understand_the_trade_offs_le","v":{"s":"I think I understand the trade-offs — let me explain them in my own words"}},{"k":"explain_in_your_own_words_how_do_tempe","v":{"s":"Explain in your own words: how do temperature, time, and moisture interact? What makes perfect caramel hard?"}},{"k":"saved_notice_nobody_checked_your_answe","v":{"s":"✓ Saved. Notice — nobody checked your answer. That is what learner-driven inquiry looks like."}},{"k":"design_note_no_caramel_quality_score_n","v":{"s":"Design note: no caramel-quality score, no reveal button. Stage is shown as a discrete 4-band marker, not a continuous gradient — by design, to discourage optimization-gaming behavior."}},{"k":"pie_note","v":{"s":"Barely touched. Cold fat = flakes."}},{"k":"pancake_note","v":{"s":"Lumpy is fine. Don’t develop gluten."}},{"k":"cake_note","v":{"s":"Tender crumb — low protein, gentle mix."}},{"k":"bread_note","v":{"s":"Strong network for oven-spring and chew."}},{"k":"pizza_note","v":{"s":"Elastic enough to stretch without tearing."}},{"k":"noodle_note","v":{"s":"Long knead + high protein = pull-without-break."}},{"k":"oven_temperature","v":{"s":"Oven 