ction + lessons."}},{"k":"confusing_id_pairs","v":{"s":"Confusing ID Pairs"}},{"k":"10_commonly_mistaken_pairs","v":{"s":"10 commonly mistaken pairs"}},{"k":"downy_vs_hairy_woodpecker_cooper_s_vs_","v":{"s":"Downy vs Hairy Woodpecker, Cooper's vs Sharp-shinned Hawk, Greater vs Lesser Yellowlegs, White-throated vs White-crowned Sparrow, Magnolia vs Yellow Warbler, Hermit vs Swainson's Thrush, Red-shouldered vs Red-tailed Hawk + more."}},{"k":"bird_families_overview","v":{"s":"Bird Families Overview"}},{"k":"12_major_orders","v":{"s":"12 major orders"}},{"k":"anseriformes_waterfowl_galliformes_gam","v":{"s":"Anseriformes (waterfowl), Galliformes (game birds), Procellariiformes (tube-noses), Pelecaniformes (pelicans + herons), Accipitriformes (hawks + eagles), Falconiformes (falcons), Charadriiformes (shorebirds + gulls), Strigiformes (owls), Apodiformes (hummingbirds + swifts), Coraciiformes (kingfishers), Piciformes (woodpeckers), Passeriformes (songbirds)."}},{"k":"birding_with_kids","v":{"s":"Birding with Kids"}},{"k":"age_appropriate_guide","v":{"s":"Age-appropriate guide"}},{"k":"toddler_preschooler_early_school_tween","v":{"s":"Toddler, preschooler, early school, tween, teen — what to do at each age. Attention spans, activities to try, things to avoid. Maine Audubon kids programs."}},{"k":"accessible_birding","v":{"s":"Accessible Birding"}},{"k":"birding_for_everyone","v":{"s":"Birding for everyone"}},{"k":"autistic_birders_mobility_limitations_","v":{"s":"Autistic birders, mobility limitations, vision + hearing differences, cost-accessibility, ADHD-friendly approaches. Birding can be entirely free + welcoming. Maine sites + tools."}},{"k":"teaching_birding","v":{"s":"Teaching Birding"}},{"k":"teacher_parent_resources","v":{"s":"Teacher + parent resources"}},{"k":"setting_up_school_birding_program_fiel","v":{"s":"Setting up school birding program, field trips, garden for birds, inquiry-based learning, citizen science participation, cross-curricular connections (