ive template for your daily birding log: date + time, location, weather, habitat, hours of effort, species, notable observations, photos, personal notes. Builds toward an eBird submission + a meaningful personal record."}},{"k":"bird_intelligence_cognition","v":{"s":"Bird Intelligence + Cognition"}},{"k":"8_cognition_topics","v":{"s":"8 cognition topics"}},{"k":"crows_tool_use_parrot_language_magpie_","v":{"s":"Crows + tool use, parrot language, magpie self-recognition, caching memory, long-term memory of human faces, theory of mind, chickadee predator-threat communication, migration memory. Birds are far smarter than once thought."}},{"k":"birds_ecosystem_services","v":{"s":"Birds + Ecosystem Services"}},{"k":"8_critical_services","v":{"s":"8 critical services"}},{"k":"pollination_hummingbirds_seed_dispersa","v":{"s":"Pollination (hummingbirds), seed dispersal (waxwings, robins), insect pest control (warblers), carrion removal (vultures), aquatic engineering (loons), nutrient cycling (seabird guano), cultural/recreational (107 billion/yr in US), education + research."}},{"k":"conservation_recovery_stories","v":{"s":"Conservation Recovery Stories"}},{"k":"8_species_recoveries","v":{"s":"8 species + recoveries"}},{"k":"bald_eagle_60_to_700_maine_pairs_pereg","v":{"s":"Bald Eagle (60 to 700 Maine pairs), Peregrine Falcon (0 to 30+ Maine pairs), Atlantic Puffin (Project Puffin), Brown Pelican, Whooping Crane, California Condor (22 to 500), Wild Turkey (0 to 50,000 in Maine), Eastern Bluebird. Conservation works."}},{"k":"wind_energy_birds","v":{"s":"Wind Energy + Birds"}},{"k":"4_dimensions_of_trade_off","v":{"s":"4 dimensions of trade-off"}},{"k":"wind_turbines_kill_birds_climate_chang","v":{"s":"Wind turbines kill birds; climate change kills far more. Mitigation strategies (siting, curtailment, painted blades). Maine + offshore wind decisions. The complex trade-off renewable energy + bird conservation must navigate."}},{"k":"bird_research_technology","v":{"s":"Bird Research Technology"}},{"k":"10_research_methods","v":{"s":"10 research methods"}},{"k":"bird_banding_geolocators_gps_tags_acou","v":{"s":"Bird banding, geolocators, GPS tags, acoustic monitoring, radar tracking, stable isotope analysis, eDNA, camera traps, citizen science apps, conservation genetics. How ornithologists study birds today."}},{"k":"maine_birding_events_festivals","v":{"s":"Maine Birding Events + Festivals"}},{"k":"10_maine_events","v":{"s":"10 Maine events"}},{"k":"acadia_birding_festival_june_project_p","v":{"s":"Acadia Birding Festival (June), Project Puffin Tours, Bradbury Mountain Hawkwatch, Great Backyard Bird Count, Maine CBCs, Maine Audubon walks, Bird-A-Thon, local birding clubs, World Migratory Bird Day. Year-round events."}},{"k":"30_maine_backyard_birds","v":{"s":"30 Maine Backyard Birds"}},{"k":"common_species_at_feeders","v":{"s":"Common species at feeders"}},{"k":"quick_reference_table_of_maine_s_30_mo","v":{"s":"Quick reference table of Maine's 30 most-commonly-seen backyard + feeder birds. Season, visit frequency, recommended feeder + food for each."}},{"k":"monthly_maine_bird_calendar","v":{"s":"Monthly Maine Bird Calendar"}},{"k":"12_months_of_expected_birds","v":{"s":"12 months of expected birds"}},{"k":"what_to_expect_each_month_of_the_year_","v":{"s":"What to expect each month of the year in Maine. January Bald Eagles to June dawn chorus to September hawkwatch peaks to December CBC. Species, activities, tips."}},{"k":"bird_naming_taxonomy","v":{"s":"Bird Naming + Taxonomy"}},{"k":"8_topics_2","v":{"s":"8 topics"}},{"k":"why_latin_common_vs_scientific_names_f","v":{"s":"Why Latin? Common vs scientific names. Family + order naming. Splits + lumps. Subspecies. Maine bird name origin stories."}},{"k":"bird_drawing_journaling","v":{"s":"Bird Drawing + Journaling"}},{"k":"8_sketching_tips","v":{"s":"8 sketching tips"}},{"k":"why_field_journal_equipment_quick_sket","v":{"s":"Why field journal? Equipment. Quick sketches. Adding details. N