":"Birding hotspot (numbered)"}},{"k":"maine_landmass","v":{"s":"Maine landmass"}},{"k":"major_rivers","v":{"s":"Major rivers"}},{"k":"plan_a_trip","v":{"s":"🔗 Plan a trip: "}},{"k":"visit","v":{"s":"Visit "}},{"k":"for_the_official_maine_birding_trail_w","v":{"s":" for the official Maine Birding Trail with directions, accessibility info, parking, and seasonal notes. Most hotspots have free Maine Audubon-led walks during peak migration."}},{"k":"migration_patterns_2","v":{"s":"Migration Patterns"}},{"k":"why_birds_move","v":{"s":"Why birds move"}},{"k":"migration_is_one_of_the_most_dramatic_","v":{"s":"Migration is one of the most dramatic phenomena in biology. Some birds fly continents twice a year, navigating by stars, magnetic fields, smell, and learned landmarks. Most don't. The patterns matter for both science and conservation: a species that breeds in Maine and winters in Costa Rica needs BOTH habitats intact."}},{"k":"this_module_covers_the_four_north_amer","v":{"s":"This module covers the four North American flyways, Maine's seasonal calendar, and 8 featured migrator strategies. For the physics of HOW birds fly (V-formation aerodynamics, energy efficiency), see the dedicated "}},{"k":"migration_wind_patterns_lab","v":{"s":"Migration & Wind Patterns Lab"}},{"k":"cross_link_below","v":{"s":" (cross-link below)."}},{"k":"migration_sections","v":{"s":"Migration sections"}},{"k":"flyways","v":{"s":"🗺️ Flyways"}},{"k":"maine_calendar","v":{"s":"📅 Maine Calendar"}},{"k":"8_featured_migrators","v":{"s":"🐦 8 Featured Migrators"}},{"k":"north_america_has_four_major_migration","v":{"s":"North America has four major migration flyways — geographic corridors that funnel migrating birds. Maine sits squarely on the "}},{"k":"atlantic_flyway","v":{"s":"Atlantic Flyway"}},{"k":"pacific","v":{"s":"Pacific"}},{"k":"central","v":{"s":"Central"}},{"k":"mississippi","v":{"s":"Mississippi"}},{"k":"atlantic","v":{"s":"Atlantic"}},{"k":"maine_2","v":{"s":"Maine"}},{"k":"4_flyways","v":{"s":"🦅 4 Flyways"}},{"k":"pick_a_flyway","v":{"s":"Pick a flyway"}},{"k":"maine_s_role","v":{"s":"🌲 Maine's role"}},{"k":"spring_fall_arrivals_departures_are_th","v":{"s":"Spring + fall arrivals/departures are the rhythm of Maine birding. Specific dates shift week-by-week with weather but the broad pattern holds year to year."}},{"k":"migration_intensity_through_the_year","v":{"s":"📅 Migration intensity through the year"}},{"k":"year_long_maine_migration_intensity_pe","v":{"s":"Year-long Maine migration intensity. Peaks in May (warbler arrivals) and October (raptor migration). Quiet in summer and winter."}},{"k":"peak_migration","v":{"s":"Peak migration"}},{"k":"migration_intensity_curve","v":{"s":"Migration intensity curve"}},{"k":"today","v":{"s":"Today"}},{"k":"activity","v":{"s":"Activity"}},{"k":"arrivals","v":{"s":"⬇️ Arrivals: "}},{"k":"departures","v":{"s":"⬆️ Departures: "}},{"k":"real_time_tracking","v":{"s":"🔗 Real-time tracking: "}},{"k":"birdcast_info_uses_weather_radar_to_fo","v":{"s":" (birdcast.info) uses weather radar to forecast nightly migration intensity. Check it on a clear May night to see if migrants are pouring in."}},{"k":"sedentary","v":{"s":"Sedentary"}},{"k":"irruptive","v":{"s":"Irruptive"}},{"k":"migrator","v":{"s":"Migrator"}},{"k":"8_species_the_migration_strategy_each_","v":{"s":"8 species + the migration strategy each one uses. Distance bars are scaled to the longest migrator (~6,000 miles, blackpoll warbler trans-Atlantic)."}},{"k":"distance_scale_one_way_miles","v":{"s":"📏 Distance scale (one-way miles)"}},{"k":"500_mi","v":{"s":"500 mi"}},{"k":"route_distance","v":{"s":"Route distance"}},{"k":"maine_3","v":{"s":"Maine"}},{"k":"stays_in_maine","v":{"s":"STAYS IN MAINE"}},{"k":"maine_note","v":{"s":"🌲 Maine note: "}},{"k":"cross_lab_link_2","v":{"s":"🔗 Cross-lab link"}},{"k":"migration_wind_patterns_lab_2","v":{"s":"Migration & Wind Patterns Lab"}},{"k":"for_how_birds_fly_open_the_migration_w","v":{"s":"For HOW birds fly: open t