iven — pay is modest until senior levels — but the work is meaningful and the community is unusually supportive."}},{"k":"honest_reality","v":{"s":"Honest reality: "}},{"k":"most_ornithologists_didn_t_start_with_","v":{"s":"Most ornithologists didn't start with a plan. They volunteered → got hooked → followed where the work led. The seasonal field-tech path (taking 3-month summer jobs in different states) is how many people start."}},{"k":"career_pathway","v":{"s":"🛤 Career pathway"}},{"k":"degree_credential","v":{"s":"🎓 Degree / credential"}},{"k":"who_hires","v":{"s":"🏢 Who hires"}},{"k":"maine_programs","v":{"s":"🌲 Maine programs"}},{"k":"honest_reality_2","v":{"s":"⚠️ Honest reality"}},{"k":"merlin_bird_id_4","v":{"s":"Merlin Bird ID"}},{"k":"project_feederwatch","v":{"s":"Project FeederWatch"}},{"k":"christmas_bird_count_cbc","v":{"s":"Christmas Bird Count (CBC)"}},{"k":"great_backyard_bird_count","v":{"s":"Great Backyard Bird Count"}},{"k":"maine_audubon_volunteer_programs","v":{"s":"Maine Audubon volunteer programs"}},{"k":"almost_none_but_i_m_curious","v":{"s":"Almost none — but I'm curious"}},{"k":"15_minutes_here_and_there","v":{"s":"15 minutes here and there"}},{"k":"a_few_hours_a_week_regularly","v":{"s":"A few hours a week, regularly"}},{"k":"i_d_join_a_real_project_take_training","v":{"s":"I'd join a real project + take training"}},{"k":"at_home_near_windows_a_possible_feeder","v":{"s":"At home, near windows + a possible feeder"}},{"k":"walking_outside_parks_trails_neighborh","v":{"s":"Walking outside (parks, trails, neighborhood)"}},{"k":"school_structured_activities","v":{"s":"School + structured activities"}},{"k":"specifically_in_maine_willing_to_drive","v":{"s":"Specifically in Maine, willing to drive to surveys"}},{"k":"i_can_t_name_5_birds_yet","v":{"s":"I can't name 5 birds yet"}},{"k":"i_know_the_obvious_ones_cardinal_robin","v":{"s":"I know the obvious ones (cardinal, robin, eagle)"}},{"k":"i_can_id_most_of_my_backyard_park_bird","v":{"s":"I can ID most of my backyard + park birds"}},{"k":"i_want_challenges_real_research_data","v":{"s":"I want challenges + real research data"}},{"k":"winter_more_time_indoors_near_windows","v":{"s":"Winter (more time indoors near windows)"}},{"k":"spring_summer_warm_outside","v":{"s":"Spring + summer (warm + outside)"}},{"k":"fall_migration_is_exciting","v":{"s":"Fall (migration is exciting)"}},{"k":"anytime_flexible","v":{"s":"Anytime — flexible"}},{"k":"maps_charts_contributing_to_research","v":{"s":"Maps, charts, contributing to research"}},{"k":"joining_a_community_of_people_who_care","v":{"s":"Joining a community of people who care"}},{"k":"solving_the_what_is_that_mystery","v":{"s":"Solving the \"what is that?\" mystery"}},{"k":"big_group_events_with_energy","v":{"s":"Big group events with energy"}},{"k":"citizen_science_bridge_2","v":{"s":"Citizen Science Bridge"}},{"k":"real_research_runs_on_volunteers","v":{"s":"🌍 Real research runs on volunteers"}},{"k":"bird_science_at_scale_population_trend","v":{"s":"Bird science at scale — population trends, range shifts, climate-impact tracking, conservation prioritization — runs on the data that ordinary people contribute. Every checklist on eBird, every CBC tally, every nest you monitor becomes a data point in published research."}},{"k":"these_projects_are_the_most_direct_con","v":{"s":"These projects are the most direct conservation action a student can take that doesn't require expert credentials. Pick one that fits your time + interest. "}},{"k":"take_the_match_quiz","v":{"s":"Take the match quiz"}},{"k":"below_for_a_personalized_recommendatio","v":{"s":" (below) for a personalized recommendation, or browse all 8."}},{"k":"citizen_science_view","v":{"s":"Citizen science view"}},{"k":"browse_all_8_projects","v":{"s":"📋 Browse all 8 projects"}},{"k":"match_quiz_which_project_fits_you","v":{"s":"🎯 Match quiz: which project fits you?"}},{"k":"best_for_you_if","v":{"s":"🎯 Best for you if..."}},{"k":"visit_project","v":{"s":"Visit project"}},{"k":"open","v":{"s":"Open ↗"}},{"k":"your_top_matches","v":{"s":"🎯 Your top matches"}},{"k":"based_on_your_answers_these_two_projec","v":{"s":"Based on your answers, these two projects fit you best. Start with the first one — it's the strongest match. The second is a good \"after that\" or alternative."}},{"k":"take_the_quiz_again","v":{"s":"🔁 Take the quiz again"}},{"k":"browse_all_8_projects_2","v":{"s":"📋 Browse all 8 projects"}},{"k":"back_to_previous_question","v":{"s":"← Back to previous question"}},{"k":"why_this_matters","v":{"s":"📚 Why this matters"}},{"k":"ebird_alone_has_been_used_in_700_peer_","v":{"s":"eBird alone has been used in 700+ peer-reviewed papers since 2010, including the Rosenberg et al. 2019 "}},{"k":"science","v":{"s":"Science"}},{"k":"study_that_documented_a_loss_of_3_bill","v":{"s":" study that documented a loss of ~3 billion North American birds since 1970. CBC data drove the federal Bald Eagle recovery decision. Citizen scientists are not \"amateur\" — your data is in the same datasets professional ornithologists use. The barrier to entry is paying attention."}},{"k":"bird","v":{"s":"Bird"}},{"k":"clear_2","v":{"s":"☀️ Clear"}},{"k":"partly_cloudy","v":{"s":"⛅ Partly cloudy"}},{"k":"cloudy","v":{"s":"☁️ Cloudy"}},{"k":"rain","v":{"s":"🌧 Rain"}},{"k":"snow","v":{"s":"🌨 Snow"}},{"k":"windy","v":{"s":"💨 Windy"}},{"k":"fog","v":{"s":"🌫 Fog"}},{"k":"field_observation_challenge_2","v":{"s":"Field Observation Challenge"}},{"k":"real_birding_is_three_skills_in_order","v":{"s":"🔭 Real birding is three skills, in order"}},{"k":"anyone_can_spot_a_bird_the_harder_skil","v":{"s":"Anyone can spot a bird. The harder skills are: "}},{"k":"holding_focus","v":{"s":"holding focus"}},{"k":"on_a_moving_target_long_enough_to_see_","v":{"s":" on a moving target long enough to see field marks, "}},{"k":"recording_disciplined_notes","v":{"s":"recording disciplined notes"}},{"k":"before_details_fade_and","v":{"s":" before details fade, and "}},{"k":"on_what_you_saw_so_it_sticks_this_acti","v":{"s":" on what you saw so it sticks. This activity practices all three."}},{"k":"your_saved_entries_become_a_personal_f","v":{"s":"Your saved entries become a personal field notebook (stored on this device only)."}},{"k":"how_it_works","v":{"s":"How it works"}},{"k":"move_your_binocular_reticle_to_keep_a_","v":{"s":"Move your binocular reticle to keep a moving bird in view. Reach 5 cumulative seconds on target within 30 seconds total."}},{"k":"fill_a_real_field_log_entry_date_locat","v":{"s":"Fill a real field-log entry — date, location, count, behavior, weather, notes. The same fields used by eBird and citizen-science apps."}},{"k":"write_2_3_sentences_on_what_stood_out_","v":{"s":"Write 2–3 sentences on what stood out. Reflection is what turns observation into learning."}},{"k":"begin_observation","v":{"s":"🔭 Begin observation"}},{"k":"tracking_keep_eyes_on_the_bird","v":{"s":"Tracking — keep eyes on the bird"}},{"k":"on_target_time","v":{"s":"🎯 On-target time"}},{"k":"time_remaining","v":{"s":"⏱ Time remaining"}},{"k":"bird_tracking_field_move_your_pointer_","v":{"s":"Bird tracking field. Move your pointer or finger to aim the binocular reticle. Stay on target for 5 cumulative seconds."}},{"k":"move_pointer_or_finger_to_aim_birds_da","v":{"s":"Move pointer or finger to aim. Birds dart unpredictably — anticipate movement instead of chasing it."}},{"k":"tracking_bird_flew_off","v":{"s":"Tracking — bird flew off"}},{"k":"bird_flying_away_into_the_distance","v":{"s":"Bird flying away into the distance"}},{"k":"on_target","v":{"s":"On target"}},{"k":"goal","v":{"s":"Goal"}},{"k":"of_goal","v":{"s":"Of goal"}},{"k":"birding_tip","v":{"s":"💡 Birding tip"}},{"k":"anticipate_movement_instead_of_chasing","v":{"s":"Anticipate movement instead of chasing it. Birds often dart in 2–3 second cycles — predict where they're headed, not where they are. Real binoculars use the same trick: lead the bird like a quarterback leading 