 gets 55% of electricity from wind already."}},{"k":"current_pace","v":{"s":"Current Pace"}},{"k":"the_world_adds_renewables_faster_than_","v":{"s":"The world adds renewables faster than ever."}},{"k":"pacific_island_nations","v":{"s":"Pacific Island Nations"}},{"k":"anote_tong","v":{"s":"Anote Tong"}},{"k":"arctic_communities","v":{"s":"Arctic Communities"}},{"k":"sheila_watt_cloutier","v":{"s":"Sheila Watt-Cloutier"}},{"k":"sahel_region_africa","v":{"s":"Sahel Region (Africa)"}},{"k":"hindou_oumarou_ibrahim","v":{"s":"Hindou Oumarou Ibrahim"}},{"k":"bangladesh_south_asia","v":{"s":"Bangladesh & South Asia"}},{"k":"saleemul_huq_1952_2023","v":{"s":"Saleemul Huq (1952–2023)"}},{"k":"caribbean_islands","v":{"s":"Caribbean Islands"}},{"k":"mia_mottley","v":{"s":"Mia Mottley"}},{"k":"us_environmental_justice","v":{"s":"US Environmental Justice"}},{"k":"catherine_coleman_flowers","v":{"s":"Catherine Coleman Flowers"}},{"k":"southeast_asia_coastal","v":{"s":"Southeast Asia Coastal"}},{"k":"yeb_sa_o","v":{"s":"Yeb Saño"}},{"k":"andean_communities","v":{"s":"Andean Communities"}},{"k":"tarcila_rivera_zea","v":{"s":"Tarcila Rivera Zea"}},{"k":"wabanaki_nations_maine","v":{"s":"Wabanaki Nations (Maine)"}},{"k":"sherri_mitchell_weh_na_ha_mu_kwasset","v":{"s":"Sherri Mitchell (Weh’na Ha’mu Kwasset)"}},{"k":"1_4_billion_people","v":{"s":"1.4 billion people."}},{"k":"greta_thunberg","v":{"s":"Greta Thunberg"}},{"k":"vanessa_nakate","v":{"s":"Vanessa Nakate"}},{"k":"autumn_peltier","v":{"s":"Autumn Peltier"}},{"k":"mari_copeny_little_miss_flint","v":{"s":"Mari Copeny (\"Little Miss Flint\")"}},{"k":"xiye_bastida","v":{"s":"Xiye Bastida"}},{"k":"disha_ravi","v":{"s":"Disha Ravi"}},{"k":"solar_power_revolution","v":{"s":"Solar Power Revolution"}},{"k":"wind_energy","v":{"s":"Wind Energy"}},{"k":"electric_vehicles","v":{"s":"Electric Vehicles"}},{"k":"forest_restoration","v":{"s":"Forest Restoration"}},{"k":"carbon_capture","v":{"s":"Carbon Capture"}},{"k":"ocean_kelp_farms","v":{"s":"Ocean Kelp Farms"}},{"k":"green_cities","v":{"s":"Green Cities"}},{"k":"youth_climate_movement","v":{"s":"Youth Climate Movement"}},{"k":"pre_industrial_1750","v":{"s":"Pre-industrial (1750)"}},{"k":"stable_for_10_000_years_holocene_clima","v":{"s":"Stable for 10,000 years. Holocene climate that all human civilization grew up in."}},{"k":"keeling_starts_measuring_1958","v":{"s":"Keeling starts measuring (1958)"}},{"k":"charles_david_keeling_begins_continuou","v":{"s":"Charles David Keeling begins continuous CO₂ monitoring at Mauna Loa. His curve proved human-caused warming was real."}},{"k":"350_ppm_1988","v":{"s":"350 ppm (1988)"}},{"k":"climate_scientist_james_hansen_tells_u","v":{"s":"Climate scientist James Hansen tells US Congress warming has begun. 350 ppm is considered the \"safe\" ceiling by 350.org."}},{"k":"400_ppm_2013","v":{"s":"400 ppm (2013)"}},{"k":"first_time_atmospheric_co_crossed_400_","v":{"s":"First time atmospheric CO₂ crossed 400 ppm in 3+ million years. Earth's last 400 ppm era: tropical forests at the poles."}},{"k":"420_ppm_2023","v":{"s":"420 ppm (2023)"}},{"k":"current_level_highest_in_at_least_800_","v":{"s":"Current level. Highest in at least 800,000 years (from ice cores). Equivalent to ~1.2°C warming."}},{"k":"450_ppm_projected_2035","v":{"s":"450 ppm (projected ~2035)"}},{"k":"threshold_associated_with_2_c_warming_","v":{"s":"Threshold associated with 2°C warming if sustained. Paris Agreement target: keep below 1.5°C."}},{"k":"tropical_coral_reef_die_off","v":{"s":"Tropical Coral Reef Die-off"}},{"k":"mass_coral_bleaching_events_hit_the_gr","v":{"s":"Mass coral bleaching events hit the Great Barrier Reef in 2016, 2017, 2020, 2022, and 2024. At 1.5°C warming, 70–90% of tropical coral reefs die. At 2°C, 99% die."}},{"k":"greenland_ice_sheet_collapse","v":{"s":"Greenland Ice Sheet Collapse"}},{"k":"the_greenland_ice_sheet_holds_enough_w","v":{"s":"The Greenland ice sheet holds enough water to raise sea levels 7 meters (23 ft). At ~1.5°C sustained, melt becomes irreversible over centuries to millennia."}},{"k":"amoc_collapse_gulf_stream","v":{"s":"AMOC Collapse (Gulf Stream)"}},{"k":"the_atlantic_meridional_overturning_ci","v":{"s":"The Atlantic Meridional Overturning Circulation moves heat from the tropics to Europe. It has weakened 15% since 1950. A full shutdown would cool northern Europe dramatically while disrupting monsoons in Africa and Asia."}},{"k":"amazon_rainforest_dieback","v":{"s":"Amazon Rainforest Dieback"}},{"k":"the_amazon_generates_half_its_own_rain","v":{"s":"The Amazon generates half its own rainfall. With 20–25% deforestation + rising temperatures, it risks flipping from rainforest to savanna. Some studies suggest the threshold is closer to 2°C with current deforestation rates."}},{"k":"permafrost_methane_release","v":{"s":"Permafrost Methane Release"}},{"k":"arctic_permafrost_holds_twice_the_carb","v":{"s":"Arctic permafrost holds twice the carbon currently in the atmosphere. Warming 3–4× faster than global average, it is already thawing and releasing CO₂ and methane (28× more potent than CO₂ over 100 years)."}},{"k":"west_antarctic_ice_sheet","v":{"s":"West Antarctic Ice Sheet"}},{"k":"marine_based_ice_sheets_anchored_below","v":{"s":"Marine-based ice sheets anchored below sea level. Warm ocean water is eroding them from beneath. Thwaites Glacier (\"Doomsday Glacier\") is the main risk. Collapse would raise sea levels 3.3 meters (11 ft)."}},{"k":"boreal_forest_die_off","v":{"s":"Boreal Forest Die-off"}},{"k":"northern_coniferous_forests_russia_can","v":{"s":"Northern coniferous forests (Russia, Canada, Scandinavia) are stressed by warming, bark beetles, and wildfires. A full transition to grassland could release vast amounts of stored carbon."}},{"k":"gulf_of_maine_rapid_warming","v":{"s":"Gulf of Maine Rapid Warming"}},{"k":"the_gulf_of_maine_has_warmed_faster_th","v":{"s":"The Gulf of Maine has warmed faster than 99% of the world’s oceans since 1980 — about 0.5°F per decade, roughly 3× the global ocean average. The cold-water Labrador current has weakened while warm Gulf Stream water reaches further north, fundamentally restructuring the food web in real time. Penobscot, Passamaquoddy, Maliseet, and Mi’kmaq coastal communities have documented these shifts in oral record decades before the satellites confirmed them."}},{"k":"onshore_wind_turbines","v":{"s":"Onshore Wind Turbines"}},{"k":"cheapest_electricity_worldwide_in_2024","v":{"s":"Cheapest electricity worldwide in 2024. Doubling capacity annually in several regions."}},{"k":"utility_scale_solar_farms","v":{"s":"Utility-Scale Solar Farms"}},{"k":"cheapest_electricity_in_history_grid_i","v":{"s":"Cheapest electricity in history. Grid integration is the main challenge now."}},{"k":"rooftop_solar","v":{"s":"Rooftop Solar"}},{"k":"distributed_resilient_typical_5kw_syst","v":{"s":"Distributed + resilient. Typical 5kW system payback: 6–10 years."}},{"k":"reduced_food_waste","v":{"s":"Reduced Food Waste"}},{"k":"1_3_of_food_is_wasted_preventing_waste","v":{"s":"1/3 of food is wasted. Preventing waste avoids methane from landfills AND the emissions to grow the food."}},{"k":"plant_rich_diets","v":{"s":"Plant-Rich Diets"}},{"k":"not_100_vegan_even_cutting_beef_3_a_we","v":{"s":"Not 100% vegan — even cutting beef 3× a week has huge impact. Frees land for reforestation."}},{"k":"tropical_forest_restoration","v":{"s":"Tropical Forest Restoration"}},{"k":"restore_125m_hectares_protects_biodive","v":{"s":"Restore 125M hectares. Protects biodiversity + draws down CO₂ via photosynthesis."}},{"k":"temperate_forest_restoration","v":{"s":"Temperate Forest Restoration"}},{"k":"plant_where_natural_conditions_support","v":{"s":"Plant where natural conditions support growth. Co-benefits: cooling, watershed protection."}},{"k":"silvopasture","v":{"s":"Silvopasture"}},{"k":"integrating_trees_into_grazing_land_li","v":{"s":"Integrating trees into grazing land. Livestock get shade; soil stores 4× more carbon than bare pasture."}},{"k":"regenerative_agriculture","v":{"s":"Regenerative Agriculture"}},{"k":"no_till_cover_crops_diverse_rotations_","v":{"s":"No-till + cover crops + diverse rotations. Builds soil carbon while maintaining yields."}},{"k":"peatlands_protection","v":{"s":"Peatlands Protection"}},{"k":"peatlands_store_3_more_carbon_than_for","v":{"s":"Peatlands store 3× more carbon than forests globally. Drained peat = major emitter."}},{"k":"refrigerant_management","v":{"s":"Refrigerant Management"}},{"k":"hfcs_are_1_000_9_000_more_potent_than_","v":{"s":"HFCs are 1,000–9,000× more potent than CO₂. Kigali Amendment (2016) is phasing them out."}},{"k":"electric_vehicles_personal","v":{"s":"Electric Vehicles (personal)"}},{"k":"evs_produce_50_70_less_lifetime_emissi","v":{"s":"EVs produce 50–70% less lifetime emissions than gas — improves as grid cleans up."}},{"k":"public_transit_rail","v":{"s":"Public Transit + Rail"}},{"k":"electric_trains_move_a_passenger_km_at","v":{"s":"Electric trains move a passenger-km at 1/10 the emissions of a car."}},{"k":"bike_infrastructure","v":{"s":"Bike Infrastructure"}},{"k":"dutch_cycling_cities_have_1_3_the_tran","v":{"s":"Dutch cycling cities have 1/3 the transport emissions. Infrastructure creates the behavior."}},{"k":"building_retrofits","v":{"s":"Building Retrofits"}},{"k":"insulation_heat_pumps_led_lighting_us_","v":{"s":"Insulation + heat pumps + LED lighting. US buildings use 40% of primary energy."}},{"k":"heat_pumps","v":{"s":"Heat Pumps"}},{"k":"3_4_more_efficient_than_gas_furnaces_w","v":{"s":"3–4× more efficient than gas furnaces. Work to −15°C in modern cold-climate models."}},{"k":"girls_education_family_planning","v":{"s":"Girls' Education & Family Planning"}},{"k":"consistently_top_ranked_educated_women","v":{"s":"Consistently top-ranked. Educated women have fewer children AND higher-impact lives. Compounds across generations."}},{"k":"clean_cookstoves","v":{"s":"Clean Cookstoves"}},{"k":"replaces_wood_charcoal_fires_benefits_","v":{"s":"Replaces wood/charcoal fires. Benefits: climate + indoor air pollution (kills 4M/yr) + deforestation."}},{"k":"kelp_reforestation_ocean","v":{"s":"Kelp Reforestation (ocean)"}},{"k":"grows_60_faster_than_land_trees_seques","v":{"s":"Grows 60× faster than land trees. Sequesters CO₂ + restores fisheries + fertilizer."}},{"k":"electricity_heat","v":{"s":"Electricity & Heat"}},{"k":"agriculture_land_use","v":{"s":"Agriculture + Land Use"}},{"k":"industry","v":{"s":"Industry"}},{"k":"transport","v":{"s":"Transport"}},{"k":"buildings","v":{"s":"Buildings"}},{"k":"other_waste_fugitive_aviation_bunkers","v":{"s":"Other (waste, fugitive, aviation bunkers)"}},{"k":"very_low_emissions_paris_aligned","v":{"s":"Very Low Emissions — Paris-Aligned"}},{"k":"low_emissions_strong_action","v":{"s":"Low Emissions — Strong Action"}},{"k":"middle_of_the_road_current_pledges","v":{"s":"Middle of the Road — Current Pledges"}},{"k":"high_emissions_regional_rivalry","v":{"s":"High Emissions — Regional Rivalry"}},{"k":"very_high_fossil_fueled_growth","v":{"s":"Very High — Fossil-Fueled Growth"}},{"k":"walk_bike_or_bus_to_school","v":{"s":"Walk, bike, or bus to school"}},{"k":"try_one_meatless_meal_per_week","v":{"s":"Try one meatless meal per week"}},{"k":"turn_off_lights_unplug_chargers","v":{"s":"Turn off lights & unplug chargers"}},{"k":"talk_to_your_family_about_energy_choic","v":{"s":"Talk to your family about energy choices"}},{"k":"plant_a_tree_or_start_a_school_garden","v":{"s":"Plant a tree or start a school garden"}},{"k":"write_a_letter_to_your_representative","v":{"s":"Write a letter to your representative"}},{"k":"start_a_recycling_program_at_school","v":{"s":"Start a recycling program at school"}},{"k":"organize_a_climate_awareness_event","v":{"s":"Organize a climate awareness event"}},{"k":"transport_2","v":{"s":"Transport"}},{"k":"food","v":{"s":"Food"}},{"k":"energy","v":{"s":"Energy"}},{"k":"waste","v":{"s":"Waste"}},{"k":"climate_explorer_keyboard_shortcuts_1_","v":{"s":"Climate Explorer. Keyboard shortcuts: 1 through 6 switch tabs, Q toggles quiz."}},{"k":"back_to_stem_lab","v":{"s":"Back to STEAM Lab"}},{"k":"export_your_climate_report_to_clipboar","v":{"s":"Export your climate report to clipboard"}},{"k":"climate_explorer_sections","v":{"s":"Climate Explorer sections"}},{"k":"carbon_calculator","v":{"s":"Carbon Calculator"}},{"k":"renewables","v":{"s":"Renewables"}},{"k":"keeling_curve","v":{"s":"Keeling Curve"}},{"k":"tipping_points","v":{"s":"Tipping Points"}},{"k":"climate_justice","v":{"s":"Climate Justice"}},{"k":"solutions","v":{"s":"Solutions"}},{"k":"policy_pathways","v":{"s":"Policy Pathways"}},{"k":"radiative_forcing","v":{"s":"Radiative Forcing"}},{"k":"carbon_calculator_2","v":{"s":"Carbon Calculator"}},{"k":"average_us_household_emits_16_tons_co_","v":{"s":"Average US household emits ~16 tons CO₂/yr. The biggest levers are home heating, transport, and diet — not plastic straws."}},{"k":"renewable_energy","v":{"s":"Renewable energy"}},{"k":"solar_wind_are_now_cheaper_than_new_fo","v":{"s":"Solar + wind are now cheaper than new fossil plants in most markets. The hard part is grid integration, not generation cost."}},{"k":"the_keeling_curve","v":{"s":"The Keeling Curve"}},{"k":"continuous_co_measurement_at_mauna_loa","v":{"s":"Continuous CO₂ measurement at Mauna Loa since 1958 — the longest-running atmospheric record. Sawtooth pattern from N. Hemisphere photosynthesis."}},{"k":"climate_tipping_points","v":{"s":"Climate tipping points"}},{"k":"thresholds_where_the_system_shifts_sta","v":{"s":"Thresholds where the system shifts state and stays there — Greenland melt, Amazon dieback, AMOC slowdown. Recent work suggests several may be closer than thought."}},{"k":"climate_justice_2","v":{"s":"Climate justice"}},{"k":"the_countries_that_emitted_the_least_f","v":{"s":"The countries that emitted the least face the worst impacts. Climate is an equity issue first — vulnerability tracks income, geography, and historical responsibility."}},{"k":"solutions_toolkit","v":{"s":"Solutions toolkit"}},{"k":"drawdown_ranks_100_solutions_by_gigato","v":{"s":"Drawdown ranks 100 solutions by gigatons of CO₂ avoided. Refrigerants, food waste, and educating girls top the list — not what most people guess."}},{"k":"climate_policy_pathways_40_year_maine_","v":{"s":"Climate Policy Pathways: 40-year Maine campaign"}},{"k":"interactive_climate_explorer_carbon_fo","v":{"s":"Interactive climate explorer carbon footprint donut chart visualization"}},{"k":"transport_3","v":{"s":"Transport"}},{"k":"food_2","v":{"s":"Food"}},{"k":"energy_2","v":{"s":"Energy"}},{"k":"waste_2","v":{"s":"Waste"}},{"k":"interactive_climate_explorer_emissions","v":{"s":"Interactive climate explorer emissions timeline visualization"}},{"k":"annual_global_co2_emission_rate","v":{"s":"Annual global CO2 emission rate"}},{"k":"baseline_today_s_coastlines","v":{"s":"Baseline — today's coastlines."}},{"k":"locked_in_at_1_5_c_sustained_warming_m","v":{"s":"Locked in at ~1.5°C sustained warming. Most coastal adaptation still possible with seawalls, managed retreat."}},{"k":"associated_with_2_5_c_warming_displace","v":{"s":"Associated with ~2.5°C warming. Displaces more people than any war in history. Hurricane surge becomes catastrophic for inland areas."}},{"k":"likely_by_2300_at_3_c_entire_nations_l","v":{"s":"Likely by 2300 at 3°C. Entire nations lose viable territory. New Orleans, Venice, much of Vietnam."}},{"k":"multi_century_commitment_at_4_c_warmin","v":{"s":"Multi-century commitment at 4°C warming. Requires Greenland + West Antarctic collapse. Human civilization's coastal geography permanently rewritten."}},{"k":"locked_in_with_greenland_most_of_west_","v":{"s":"Locked-in with Greenland + most of West Antarctic gone. A hotter Pliocene-era coastline. Several centuries to millennia to fully realize."}},{"k":"sea_level_rise_in_meters","v":{"s":"Sea level rise in meters"}},{"k":"risks","v":{"s":"⚠️ Risks"}},{"k":"emissions","v":{"s":"🏭 Emissions"}},{"k":"resilience","v":{"s":"💪 Resilience"}},{"k":"cop28_host_pledge_dec_2023","v":{"s":"COP28 host pledge, Dec 2023"}},{"k":"100m_cop28","v":{"s":"€100M, COP28"}},{"k":"100m_cop28_2","v":{"s":"€100M, COP28"}},{"k":"100m_cop28_3","v":{"s":"€100M, COP28"}},{"k":"40m_cop28","v":{"s":"£40M, COP28"}},{"k":"25m_cop28","v":{"s":"€25M, COP28"}},{"k":"cop28_note_25_of_all_historical_co","v":{"s":"COP28 — note: ~25% of all historical CO₂"}},{"k":"record_year_pakistan_floods_alone_disp","v":{"s":"Record year — Pakistan floods alone displaced ~8.2M"}},{"k":"know_your_household_number","v":{"s":"Know your household number"}},{"k":"welcome_the_people_the_climate_is_alre","v":{"s":"Welcome the people the climate is already moving"}},{"k":"pressure_the_loss_damage_fund_pledge_u","v":{"s":"Pressure the Loss & Damage Fund pledge upward"}},{"k":"read_the_people_you_just_heard_from","v":{"s":"Read the people you just heard from"}},{"k":"show_up_where_the_decisions_actually_g","v":{"s":"Show up where the decisions actually get made"}},{"k":"ipcc_first_assessment_report","v":{"s":"IPCC First Assessment Report"}},{"k":"un_framework_convention_on_climate_cha","v":{"s":"UN Framework Convention on Climate Change"}},{"k":"aosis_proposes_loss_damage_at_cop1_ber","v":{"s":"AOSIS proposes Loss & Damage at COP1 Berlin"}},{"k":"idmc_begins_tracking_weather_displacem","v":{"s":"IDMC begins tracking weather displacement"}},{"k":"cop15_copenhagen_100b_yr_finance_pledg","v":{"s":"COP15 Copenhagen — $100B/yr finance pledge"}},{"k":"paris_agreement_article_8_mentions_l_d","v":{"s":"Paris Agreement — Article 8 mentions L&D"}},{"k":"un_hrc_teitiota_v_new_zealand_ruling","v":{"s":"UN HRC Teitiota v. New Zealand ruling"}},{"k":"world_bank_groundswell_part_ii_report","v":{"s":"World Bank Groundswell Part II report"}},{"k":"cop27_sharm_el_sheikh_l_d_fund_created","v":{"s":"COP27 Sharm el-Sheikh — L&D Fund created"}},{"k":"cop28_dubai_l_d_fund_capitalized","v":{"s":"COP28 Dubai — L&D Fund capitalized"}},{"k":"first_l_d_fund_disbursements","v":{"s":"First L&D Fund disbursements"}},{"k":"ipcc_1_5_c_deadline_target_year","v":{"s":"IPCC 1.5°C deadline (target year)"}},{"k":"start_drawdown_sleuth","v":{"s":"Start Drawdown Sleuth"}},{"k":"pick_the_biggest_impact_solution","v":{"s":"Pick the biggest-impact solution"}},{"k":"energy_3","v":{"s":"⚡ Energy"}},{"k":"transport_4","v":{"s":"🚌 Transport"}},{"k":"nature","v":{"s":"🌳 Nature"}},{"k":"capture","v":{"s":"🏭 Capture"}},{"k":"a_quiet_period","v":{"s":"A Quiet Period"}},{"k":"no_major_political_or_climate_event_ro","v":{"s":"No major political or climate event. Routine policy work continued."}},{"k":"net_zero_plus_equity","v":{"s":"Net-zero Plus Equity"}},{"k":"you_hit_deep_decarbonization_across_se","v":{"s":"You hit deep decarbonization across sectors, built resilience, and held equity at the center. This is what a successful climate transition looks like when the social contract holds."}},{"k":"decarbonized_but_uneven","v":{"s":"Decarbonized but Uneven"}},{"k":"significant_decarbonization_across_the","v":{"s":"Significant decarbonization across the energy and transport sectors, but adaptation and justice lagged. The carbon curves are right; the political coalition is fragile."}},{"k":"partial_progress","v":{"s":"Partial Progress"}},{"k":"some_sectors_moved_others_stalled_publ","v":{"s":"Some sectors moved. Others stalled. Public support eroded over time. This is the trajectory most real-world climate policies have run."}},{"k":"climate_policy_failure","v":{"s":"Climate Policy Failure"}},{"k":"decarbonization_stalled_adaptation_gap","v":{"s":"Decarbonization stalled. Adaptation gaps widened. Public support collapsed. This is the trajectory we work to avoid: climate impacts compounding without the social or technical infrastructure to respond."}},{"k":"initial_conditions_are_workable_spread","v":{"s":"Initial conditions are workable. Spread investment across 2-3 sectors in the first period to find which feedback rules fire first. Public education + citizen assemblies pays off slowly but durably."}},{"k":"ai_climate_policy_reading","v":{"s":"AI Climate Policy Reading"}},{"k":"dismiss_tip","v":{"s":"Dismiss tip"}},{"k":"strong_warming","v":{"s":"🔥 Strong warming"}},{"k":"positive_feedback_dominates_earth_warm","v":{"s":"Positive feedback dominates; Earth warms toward a hotter equilibrium. (A true \"runaway\" greenhouse — oceans boiling away — is a Venus scenario, not Earth at these forcings.)"}},{"k":"rapid_cooling","v":{"s":"🧊 Rapid cooling"}},{"k":"high_albedo_negative_feedback_ice_age_","v":{"s":"High albedo + negative feedback. Ice-age trajectory."}},{"k":"stable_climate","v":{"s":"🟢 Stable climate"}},{"k":"net_forcing_0_w_m_earth_equilibrium","v":{"s":"Net forcing ≈ 0 W/m². Earth equilibrium."}},{"k":"albedo_paradox","v":{"s":"⚖️ Albedo paradox"}},{"k":"forcings_partially_offset_climate_slow","v":{"s":"Forcings partially offset. Climate slowly drifts."}},{"k":"energy_balance_diagram_shortwave_sunli","v":{"s":"Energy-balance diagram: shortwave sunlight passes through the greenhouse-gas layer and warms the surface; the surface radiates infrared, some of which the gas layer absorbs and re-emits back downward, trapping heat."}},{"k":"hypothesis_when_does_albedo_overcome_g","v":{"s":"Hypothesis: When does albedo overcome GHG forcing?"}},{"k":"explain_how_albedo_cloud_feedback_and_","v":{"s":"Explain how albedo, cloud feedback, and GHGs jointly drive climate state."}},{"k":"energyGrid_desc","v":{"s":"Maine's electricity supply. Currently about 30% hydro, 20% wind, 6% solar, the rest natural gas + biomass + imported nuclear. Renewable share has to rise sharply for transportation and building electrification to be worth doing."}},{"k":"transportation_desc","v":{"s":"Maine's largest direct emissions source (about 50% of state CO₂ output). Long rural commutes, limited transit, near-zero passenger rail. EV adoption is climbing but still under 5% of registrations. The bigger lever may be reducing vehicle-miles-traveled through housing density and remote work."}},{"k":"buildings_desc","v":{"s":"Buildings account for about 30% of Maine emissions (heating dominant; Maine has the highest oil-heat share in the US). Heat pumps work in Maine winter and have been the state's defining decarbonization win. Retrofits of older housing stock are the hard, expensive work."}},{"k":"workingLands_desc","v":{"s":"Maine is 89% forested, the most forested state by percentage. Working forests sequester roughly 6 million tons CO₂ annually. Agricultural soils, salt marshes, and seagrass beds are smaller but additive carbon sinks. This is one of Maine's climate advantages most states lack."}},{"k":"adaptation_desc","v":{"s":"Maine is already experiencing climate impacts: sea level rising about 4 mm/year along the coast, more intense rainstorms, warming Gulf of Maine waters that affected lobster, increased winter ticks driving moose decline. Adaptation is not optional; the question is who pays and who gets protected."}},{"k":"climateJustice_desc","v":{"s":"Who bears the costs of climate change, who pays for solutions, and who is at the decision-making table. Frontline communities (low-income, BIPOC, Wabanaki, coastal, rural elderly) face the highest impacts and often the lowest capacity to respond. Without equity investment, climate support across all other sectors degrades over time."}},{"k":"optimist_desc","v":{"s":"24 hrs / period, gentler events. Good for first runs."}},{"k":"realist_desc","v":{"s":"18 hrs / period, standard events. Default."}},{"k":"constrained_desc","v":{"s":"14 hrs / period, harsher events. Real political reality."}},{"k":"route_carbon_hint","v":{"s":"Estimate footprint drivers."}},{"k":"route_keeling_hint","v":{"s":"Read the CO2 record."}},{"k":"route_justice_hint","v":{"s":"Compare risk and responsibility."}},{"k":"route_solutions_hint","v":{"s":"Choose practical levers."}},{"k":"hero_mix","v":{"s":"Your energy mix:"}},{"k":"hero_fossil","v":{"s":"fossil — watch the sky"}},{"k":"hero_footprint","v":{"s":"Your footprint:"}},{"k":"hero_paris","v":{"s":"Paris target: 2,300"}},{"k":"hero_ppm","v":{"s":"CO₂ today: ~424 ppm — the highest in over 3 million years"}},{"k":"climate_mission","v":{"s":"Climate mission"}},{"k":"climate_explorer","v":{"s":"Climate Explorer"}},{"k":"mission_panel_copy","v":{"s":"Move from personal data to global evidence, justice, and solutions. Advanced policy and forcing labs stay available when you expand them."}},{"k":"status_hope","v":{"s":"Hope"}},{"k":"status_badges","v":{"s":"Badges"}},{"k":"status_xp","v":{"s":"XP"}},{"k":"status_advanced","v":{"s":"Advanced"}},{"k":"visible","v":{"s":"Visible"}},{"k":"hidden","v":{"s":"Hidden"}},{"k":"hide_advanced_labs","v":{"s":"Hide advanced labs"}},{"k":"show_advanced_labs","v":{"s":"Show advanced labs"}},{"k":"climate_explorer_keyboard_shortcuts_alt","v":{"s":"Climate Explorer. Keyboard shortcuts: Alt plus 1 through 6 switches tabs; Alt plus Q toggles the quiz."}},{"k":"resume_atmospheric_animation","v":{"s":"Resume atmospheric animation"}},{"k":"pause_atmospheric_animation","v":{"s":"Pause atmospheric animation"}},{"k":"resume_animation","v":{"s":"Resume animation"}},{"k":"pause_animation","v":{"s":"Pause animation"}}],"id":501}},{"k":"coding","v":{"o":[{"k":"turtle","v":{"s":"Turtle"}},{"k":"rocket","v":{"s":"Rocket"}},{"k":"butterfly","v":{"s":"Butterfly"}},{"k":"pumpkin","v":{"s":"Pumpkin"}},{"k":"star","v":{"s":"Star"}},{"k":"first_program","v":{"s":"First Program"}},{"k":"run_your_first_program","v":{"s":"Run your first program"}},{"k":"loop_master","v":{"s":"Loop Master"}},{"k":"use_a_repeat_block","v":{"s":"Use a Repeat block"}},{"k":"color_artist","v":{"s":"Color Artist"}},{"k":"use_3_different_colors","v":{"s":"Use 3+ different colors"}},{"k":"century_club","v":{"s":"Century Club"}},{"k":"draw_100_line_segments","v":{"s":"Draw 100+ line segments"}},{"k":"robot_commander","v":{"s":"Robot Commander"}},{"