}},{"k":"classroom","v":{"s":"Classroom"}},{"k":"dino_lab_sections","v":{"s":"Dino Lab sections"}},{"k":"search_by_name_meaning_clade_or_place","v":{"s":"Search by name, meaning, clade, or place..."}},{"k":"search_dinosaurs","v":{"s":"Search dinosaurs"}},{"k":"seen","v":{"s":"Seen"}},{"k":"earth_forms","v":{"s":"Earth forms"}},{"k":"first_life_simple_microbes","v":{"s":"First life — simple microbes"}},{"k":"microbes_fill_the_air_with_oxygen","v":{"s":"Microbes fill the air with oxygen"}},{"k":"first_complex_eukaryotic_cells","v":{"s":"First complex (eukaryotic) cells"}},{"k":"first_animals","v":{"s":"First animals"}},{"k":"cambrian_explosion_animals_diversify","v":{"s":"Cambrian explosion — animals diversify"}},{"k":"plants_spread_onto_land","v":{"s":"Plants spread onto land"}},{"k":"first_four_legged_animals_walk_on_land","v":{"s":"First four-legged animals walk on land"}},{"k":"first_reptiles","v":{"s":"First reptiles"}},{"k":"the_great_dying_end_permian_extinction","v":{"s":"The Great Dying (end-Permian extinction)"}},{"k":"first_dinosaurs_appear","v":{"s":"First dinosaurs appear"}},{"k":"first_mammals","v":{"s":"First mammals"}},{"k":"first_birds_archaeopteryx","v":{"s":"First birds (Archaeopteryx)"}},{"k":"asteroid_non_bird_dinosaurs_end","v":{"s":"Asteroid — non-bird dinosaurs end"}},{"k":"first_human_ancestors_hominins","v":{"s":"First human ancestors (hominins)"}},{"k":"first_homo_sapiens_us","v":{"s":"First Homo sapiens (us)"}},{"k":"right_now","v":{"s":"Right now"}},{"k":"map_of_where_dinosaur_fossils_are_foun","v":{"s":"Map of where dinosaur fossils are found today, by continent"}},{"k":"theropod_mostly_meat_eaters_two_legs","v":{"s":"Theropod (mostly meat-eaters, two legs)"}},{"k":"sauropodomorph_long_necked_plant_eater","v":{"s":"Sauropodomorph (long-necked plant-eaters)"}},{"k":"ornithischian_bird_hipped_plant_eaters","v":{"s":"Ornithischian (bird-hipped plant-eaters)"}},{"k":"search_terms","v":{"s":"Search terms..."}},{"k":"search_glossary","v":{"s":"Search glossary"}},{"k":"feathers","v":{"s":"Feathers"}},{"k":"dozens_of_dinosaurs_are_preserved_with","v":{"s":"Dozens of dinosaurs are preserved with feathers, from simple fuzz to true flight feathers. Many were feathered long before any of them could fly."}},{"k":"the_wishbone","v":{"s":"The wishbone"}},{"k":"birds_have_a_furcula_or_wishbone_so_di","v":{"s":"Birds have a furcula, or wishbone. So did theropod dinosaurs like T. rex and Velociraptor. It is the very same bone."}},{"k":"hollow_air_filled_bones","v":{"s":"Hollow, air-filled bones"}},{"k":"bird_bones_are_light_and_filled_with_a","v":{"s":"Bird bones are light and filled with air sacs. The same air-filled bones appear in many dinosaurs, part of a bird-like breathing system."}},{"k":"three_toed_feet","v":{"s":"Three-toed feet"}},{"k":"the_classic_bird_footprint_three_toes_","v":{"s":"The classic bird footprint, three toes forward, matches theropod feet. Fossil dinosaur tracks look like giant bird tracks."}},{"k":"eggs_and_brooding","v":{"s":"Eggs and brooding"}},{"k":"dinosaurs_laid_eggs_in_nests_and_some_","v":{"s":"Dinosaurs laid eggs in nests, and some, like Citipati and Oviraptor, sat on them to brood their young, exactly as birds do."}},{"k":"a_wrist_that_folds","v":{"s":"A wrist that folds"}},{"k":"birds_fold_their_wings_using_a_special","v":{"s":"Birds fold their wings using a special half-moon wrist bone. The same bone let some dinosaurs tuck their arms against the body."}},{"k":"fast_growth_warm_bodies","v":{"s":"Fast growth, warm bodies"}},{"k":"growth_rings_in_dinosaur_bones_show_ma","v":{"s":"Growth rings in dinosaur bones show many grew quickly and ran warm, more like birds and mammals than like modern reptiles."}},{"k":"ext_ordovician_note","v":{"s":"The second-largest extinction, long before any land vertebrates walked."}},{"k":"ext_devonian_note","v":{"s":"A drawn-out crisis rather than a single sudden blow."}},{"k":"ext_permian_note","v":{"s":"About 19 of every 20 marine species disappeared. Recovery took millions of years."}},{"k":"ext_triassic_note","v":{"s":"A case where extinction helped, not hurt, the dinosaurs."}},{"k":"ext_kpg_note","v":{"s":"The only mass extinction firmly tied to an asteroid impact. Birds carry the dinosaur line forward."}},{"k":"hellcreek_note","v":{"s":"A window onto the very last days of the non-bird dinosaurs, right up to the K-Pg layer."}},{"k":"morrison_note","v":{"s":"The classic American \"dinosaur graveyard\" of the Jurassic giants."}},{"k":"dinopark_note","v":{"s":"One of the richest dinosaur fossil areas in the world."}},{"k":"yixian_note","v":{"s":"Fine volcanic ash preserved feathers and even color. It transformed how we see dinosaurs."}},{"k":"nemegt_note","v":{"s":"A river-and-floodplain world that preserved many strange Asian dinosaurs."}},{"k":"djadochta_note","v":{"s":"An ancient desert that froze behavior in time, including the Fighting Dinosaurs."}},{"k":"solnhofen_note","v":{"s":"A still lagoon whose fine limestone preserved feathers in stunning detail."}},{"k":"kemkem_note","v":{"s":"A river system that somehow supported several giant predators at once."}},{"k":"ischigualasto_note","v":{"s":"The \"Valley of the Moon\", recording the dawn of the dinosaurs."}},{"k":"tendaguru_note","v":{"s":"An African match to the Morrison, excavated in huge early expeditions."}},{"k":"twomedicine_note","v":{"s":"Egg Mountain here proved dinosaurs nested in colonies and cared for young."}},{"k":"kaiparowits_note","v":{"s":"A remote site revealing the lost southern world of the continent Laramidia."}},{"k":"longest_pred_detail","v":{"s":"About 15 meters long, the longest known meat-eating dinosaur."}},{"k":"heaviest_detail","v":{"s":"A titanosaur estimated near 70 tonnes or more, among the largest land animals ever."}},{"k":"longest_detail","v":{"s":"A diplodocid that may have stretched past 30 meters from nose to tail."}},{"k":"longest_neck_detail","v":{"s":"Some neck estimates reach about 15 meters, the longest of any animal."}},{"k":"biggest_claw_detail","v":{"s":"Hand claws up to about a meter long, the longest of any known animal."}},{"k":"smallest_detail","v":{"s":"Crow-sized four-winged gliders, among the smallest non-bird dinosaurs."}},{"k":"biggest_bite_detail","v":{"s":"A bite force estimated near 35,000 newtons, the strongest of any known land animal."}},{"k":"biggest_brain_detail","v":{"s":"Some of the highest brain-to-body ratios among dinosaurs."}},{"k":"first_named_detail","v":{"s":"Named in 1824, before the word \"dinosaur\" was coined in 1842."}},{"k":"first_color_detail","v":{"s":"The first dinosaur whose color, a ginger-and-white tail, was worked out from fossils."}},{"k":"best_preserved_detail","v":{"s":"A baby with preserved internal organs, down to the intestines."}},{"k":"biggest_hadrosaur_detail","v":{"s":"A crestless hadrosaur up to about 15 meters long."}},{"k":"field_station_3d","v":{"s":"Field Station"}}],"id":513}},{"k":"dissection","v":{"o":[{"k":"sr_saved_progress_is_still_unavailable_temporary_ses","v":{"s":"Saved progress is still unavailable. Temporary-session changes remain and saving stays paused."}},{"k":"sr_no_stored_record_was_found_temporary_session_work","v":{"s":"No stored record was found. Temporary-session work was kept, and saving resumed from it."}},{"k":"sr_protected_saved_progress_reloaded_safely_saving_h","v":{"s":"Protected saved progress reloaded safely. Saving has resumed from that saved version."}},{"k":"sr_evidence_notebook_full_no_frame_was_replaced_down","v":{"s":"Evidence notebook full. No frame was replaced. Download or remove a frame before capturing another."}},{"k":"sr_checking_protected_saved_progress_temporary_sessi","v":{"s":"Checking protected saved progress. Temporary-session changes will remain unless the saved version can be read safely."}},{"k":"sr_practice_assessment_started_choose_multiple_choic","v":{"s":"Practice assessment started. Choose multiple choice or answer directly on the specimen."}},{"k":"a11y_curre