 phase."}},{"k":"first_part_of_the_cold_season_phase_pr","v":{"s":"First part of the Cold Season phase. Primary cultural-burn window."}},{"k":"second_part_of_the_cold_season_phase_p","v":{"s":"Second part of the Cold Season phase. Pile-burn and coppice window."}},{"k":"fire_dependent_rhizomatous_shrub_burne","v":{"s":"Fire-dependent rhizomatous shrub. Burned every 2 to 3 years."}},{"k":"less_tannic_than_red_oak_preferred_aco","v":{"s":"Less tannic than red oak; preferred acorn source."}},{"k":"maine_state_tree_pitch_and_canoe_wood","v":{"s":"Maine state tree. Pitch and canoe wood."}},{"k":"red_spruce_dominates_higher_elevations","v":{"s":"Red spruce dominates higher elevations."}},{"k":"white_pine_and_birchbark_canoe_traditi","v":{"s":"White pine and birchbark canoe traditions are central to Wabanaki travel."}},{"k":"smudge_for_ceremony_binding_band_on_ba","v":{"s":"Smudge for ceremony; binding band on baskets."}},{"k":"engineer_of_the_riparian_zone_raises_w","v":{"s":"Engineer of the riparian zone; raises water tables and creates firebreaks."}},{"k":"the_basketry_tree_annual_growth_rings_","v":{"s":"The basketry tree. Annual growth rings split into splints when the trunk is pounded."}},{"k":"spring_sap_run_for_syrup","v":{"s":"Spring sap run for syrup."}},{"k":"alluvial_river_floodplain_land_warm_lo","v":{"s":"Alluvial river-floodplain land. Warm, loose, fertile."}},{"k":"white_flint_corn_was_the_wabanaki_stap","v":{"s":"White flint corn was the Wabanaki staple; dried and ground."}},{"k":"one_of_the_three_sisters_with_corn_and","v":{"s":"One of the Three Sisters with corn and beans."}},{"k":"wabanaki_vocabulary_glossary","v":{"s":"Wabanaki vocabulary glossary"}},{"k":"vocabulary","v":{"s":"Vocabulary"}},{"k":"wabanaki_vocabulary_in_this_sim","v":{"s":"Wabanaki vocabulary in this sim"}},{"k":"close_glossary","v":{"s":"Close glossary"}},{"k":"close","v":{"s":"✕ Close"}},{"k":"the_bilingual_terms_across_this_sim_th","v":{"s":"The bilingual terms across this sim. The Wabanaki Confederacy is five distinct nations (Penobscot, Passamaquoddy, Maliseet, Mi'kmaq, Abenaki), each with its own language. Spellings vary by orthography and dialect; the forms here are representative, not authoritative. For language teaching consult the language program of each nation, the University of Maine Wabanaki Center, or community resources directly."}},{"k":"cultural_deep_dive","v":{"s":"Cultural deep-dive"}},{"k":"close_deep_dive","v":{"s":"Close deep-dive"}},{"k":"close_2","v":{"s":"✕ Close"}},{"k":"ecological_knowledge","v":{"s":"🌿 Ecological knowledge"}},{"k":"traditional_use_and_preparation","v":{"s":"🧺 Traditional use and preparation"}},{"k":"modern_context","v":{"s":"🌍 Modern context"}},{"k":"a_wabanaki_teaching","v":{"s":"✨ A Wabanaki teaching"}},{"k":"paraphrased_from_documented_wabanaki_s","v":{"s":"Paraphrased from documented Wabanaki stewardship practice. The Wabanaki Confederacy includes Penobscot, Passamaquoddy, Maliseet, Mi'kmaq, and Abenaki nations, each with its own distinct language; the bilingual term above is one representative form."}},{"k":"a_quiet_year","v":{"s":"A Quiet Year"}},{"k":"no_major_event_the_seasons_turned_as_e","v":{"s":"No major event. The seasons turned as expected and the community kept its rhythm."}},{"k":"wabanaki_stewardship_mastery","v":{"s":"Wabanaki Stewardship Mastery"}},{"k":"the_mosaic_thrives_berry_harvests_are_","v":{"s":"The mosaic thrives. Berry harvests are abundant, intervale corn fills the longhouse, ash splints supply every basketmaker, canoes leave the pine grove finished and tight, sweetgrass braids fill every ceremony. The land remembers good fire."}},{"k":"skilled_mosaic_steward","v":{"s":"Skilled Mosaic Steward"}},{"k":"you_held_the_mosaic_together_some_zone","v":{"s":"You held the mosaic together. Some zones thrived, others held steady. The community has what it needs."}},{"k":"mosaic_apprentice","v":{"s":"Mosaic Apprentice"}},{"k":"you_kept_the_land_alive_but_it_is_fray","v":{"s":"You kept the land alive but it is fraying. Some zones missed their fire-return windows; harvests were thin in places."}},{"k":"ecology_slipping","v":{"s":"Ecology Slipping"}},{"k":"the_mosaic_is_unraveling_without_consi","v":{"s":"The mosaic is unraveling. Without consistent stewardship the habitats are blending together and the cultural species are losing ground."}},{"k":"wabanaki_cultural_mosaic","v":{"s":"Wabanaki Cultural Mosaic"}},{"k":"steward_a_real_maine_territory_across_","v":{"s":"Steward a real Maine territory across 8 years."}},{"k":"your_land_is_divided_into_5_zones_each","v":{"s":"Your land is divided into 7 zones, each with its own habitat, its own cultural use, and its own fire-return interval. "}},{"k":"a_blueberry_barren_needs_fire_every_2_","v":{"s":"A blueberry barren needs fire every 2 years; a riparian corridor needs fire almost never."}},{"k":"real_indigenous_stewardship_is_patchwo","v":{"s":" Real Indigenous stewardship is patchwork, not uniform."}},{"k":"this_sim_is_built_on_documented_wabana","v":{"s":"This sim is built on documented Wabanaki practice (Penobscot, Passamaquoddy, Maliseet, Mi'kmaq, Abenaki). Where details are simplified for an 8-year window, the underlying logic is faithful."}},{"k":"open_wabanaki_vocabulary_glossary","v":{"s":"Open Wabanaki vocabulary glossary"}},{"k":"wabanaki_vocabulary","v":{"s":"📖 Wabanaki vocabulary"}},{"k":"your_territory","v":{"s":"Your Territory"}},{"k":"starting_state_of_your_land","v":{"s":"Starting state of your land"}},{"k":"cultural_deep_dive_2","v":{"s":"📚 Cultural deep-dive →"}},{"k":"difficulty","v":{"s":"Difficulty"}},{"k":"how_a_year_works","v":{"s":"How a year works: "}},{"k":"each_year_splits_into_a","v":{"s":"each year splits into a "}},{"k":"warm_season_sigwan_nipon","v":{"s":"☼ Warm Season (Sigwan-Nipon)"}},{"k":"and_a","v":{"s":" and a "}},{"k":"cold_season_toqaq_pun","v":{"s":"❄ Cold Season (Toqaq-Pun)"}},{"k":"begin_wabanaki_mosaic","v":{"s":"Begin Wabanaki Mosaic"}},{"k":"begin_8_year_stewardship","v":{"s":"🧩 Begin 8-year Stewardship"}},{"k":"notes_for_educators","v":{"s":"📝 Notes for educators"}},{"k":"this_sim_is_a_teaching_tool_wabanaki_f","v":{"s":"This sim is a teaching tool. Wabanaki fire stewardship is a living practice held by living people, not a historical artifact. The simulation is intentionally a simplification across an 8-year window; real stewardship operates on multi-generational time horizons, ties into ceremony, language, and treaty relationships, and is led by Wabanaki nations themselves."}},{"k":"for_pairing_with_classroom_work_consid","v":{"s":"For pairing with classroom work, consider these resources:"}},{"k":"wabanaki_public_health_and_wellness_wa","v":{"s":"Wabanaki Public Health and Wellness (wabanakipublichealth.org) for community-led programming."}},{"k":"maine_indian_basketmakers_alliance_mai","v":{"s":"Maine Indian Basketmakers Alliance (maineindianbaskets.org) for brown-ash crisis and craft revitalization."}},{"k":"university_of_maine_wabanaki_center_um","v":{"s":"University of Maine Wabanaki Center (umaine.edu/nativeamericanprograms) for academic resources."}},{"k":"each_nation_s_cultural_offices_penobsc","v":{"s":"Each nation's cultural offices: Penobscot Cultural and Historic Preservation Department; Passamaquoddy Cultural Heritage Museum; Maliseet, Mi'kmaq, and Abenaki community resources."}},{"k":"discussion_prompts_after_the_campaign","v":{"s":"Discussion prompts after the campaign:"}},{"k":"where_in_your_local_landscape_do_you_s","v":{"s":"Where in your local landscape do you see evidence of past or ongoing Indigenous fire stewardship?"}},{"k":"how_did_the_seasonal_split_sigwan_nipo","v":{"s":"How did the seasonal split (Sigwan-Nipon and Toqaq-Pun) change which moves felt high-leverage?"}},{"k":"which_zone_did_you_find_hardest_to_kee","v":{"s":"Which zone did you find hardest to keep healthy, and what does that suggest about the cultural infrastructure (food, basketry, canoe-building, ceremony) it supports?"}},{"k":"how_is_the_loss_of_brown_ash_to_emeral","v":{"s":"How is the loss of brown ash to emerald ash borer a parallel to other ongoing cultural-ecological emergencies you know about?"}},{"k":"final_state_of_your_mosaic","v":{"s":"Final state of your mosaic"}},{"k":"avg_ecological_health","v":{"s":"Avg ecological health"}},{"k":"total_cultural_yield","v":{"s":"Total cultural yield"}},{"k":"continuity_wins","v":{"s":"Continuity wins"}},{"k":"what_if_you_had_done_nothing","v":{"s":"↔ What if you had done nothing?"}},{"k":"your_mosaic","v":{"s":"Your mosaic"}},{"k":"neglected_mosaic","v":{"s":"Neglected mosaic"}},{"k":"eight_year_cultural_harvest","v":{"s":"🌾 Eight-year cultural harvest"}},{"k":"final_state_by_zone","v":{"s":"Final state by zone"}},{"k":"start_a_new_mosaic_with_fresh_random_c","v":{"s":"Start a new mosaic with fresh random conditions"}},{"k":"new_mosaic_new_conditions","v":{"s":"↻ New mosaic, new conditions"}},{"k":"replay_the_same_starting_conditions_an","v":{"s":"Replay the same starting conditions and event sequence with a different strategy"}},{"k":"same_seed_same_starting_state_same_yea","v":{"s":"Same seed = same starting state + same yearly events. Try a different stewardship plan."}},{"k":"replay_same_conditions","v":{"s":"🔁 Replay same conditions"}},{"k":"campaign_seed","v":{"s":"Campaign seed: "}},{"k":"a_teacher_or_classmate_using_the_same_","v":{"s":"A teacher or classmate using the same seed on the same difficulty gets the same starting state and the same sequence of yearly events."}},{"k":"avg_health","v":{"s":"Avg health"}},{"k":"total_yield","v":{"s":"Total yield"}},{"k":"continuity_this_year","v":{"s":"Continuity this year"}},{"k":"hit_the_fire_return_window","v":{"s":"🎯 Hit the fire-return window: "}},{"k":"no_zone_hit_its_fire_return_window_thi","v":{"s":"No zone hit its fire-return window this year. The mosaic drifts when no habitat gets the right treatment on time."}},{"k":"what_changed_this_year","v":{"s":"What changed this year"}},{"k":"this_year_the_community_gathered","v":{"s":"🌾 This year the community gathered"}},{"k":"elder_guidance","v":{"s":"✨ Elder Guidance"}},{"k":"first_year_tip","v":{"s":"First-year tip: "}},{"k":"dismiss_tip","v":{"s":"Dismiss tip"}},{"k":"year_3","v":{"s":"Year"}},{"k":"season","v":{"s":"Season"}},{"k":"hours_this_phase","v":{"s":"Hours this phase"}},{"k":"continuity_wins_2","v":{"s":"Continuity wins"}},{"k":"ask_ai_fire_ecologist_to_read_your_lan","v":{"s":"Ask AI fire ecologist to read your land state"}},{"k":"ai_fire_ecology_educator_reads_your_cu","v":{"s":"AI fire ecology educator reads your current land state"}},{"k":"cultural_deep_dive_3","v":{"s":"Cultural deep-dive"}},{"k":"no_actions_yet_this_year_pick_a_zone_p","v":{"s":"No actions yet this year. Pick a zone, pick a technique."}},{"k":"how_beaver_dams_create_fire_refugia","v":{"s":"🌊 How Beaver Dams Create Fire Refugia"}},{"k":"cross_section_beaver_pond_creates_a_gr","v":{"s":"Cross-section: Beaver pond creates a green, fire-resistant corridor even when surrounding forest burns"}},{"k":"the_integrated_vision_fire_beavers_ind","v":{"s":"⭐ The Integrated Vision: Fire + Beavers + Indigenous Knowledge"}},{"k":"the_most_fire_resilient_landscapes_on_","v":{"s":"The most fire-resilient landscapes on Earth share three features: "}},{"k":"regular_low_intensity_fire","v":{"s":"regular low-intensity fire"}},{"k":"managed_by_knowledgeable_practitioners","v":{"s":" managed by knowledgeable practitioners, "}},{"k":"intact_beaver_populations","v":{"s":"intact beaver populations"}},{"k":"maintaining_wetland_corridors_and","v":{"s":" maintaining wetland corridors, and "}},{"k":"indigenous_stewardship","v":{"s":"Indigenous stewardship"}},{"k":"that_understands_fire_water_and_wildli","v":{"s":" that understands fire, water, and wildlife as interconnected systems. Restoring all three together — not just one in isolation — is the most effective strategy for building landscape resilience in an era of increasing wildfire risk."}},{"k":"the_firekeeper_challenge","v":{"s":"The Firekeeper Challenge"}},{"k":"select_difficulty","v":{"s":"Select Difficulty:"}},{"k":"start_game","v":{"s":"Start Game"}},{"k":"begin_the_challenge","v":{"s":"Begin the Challenge"}},{"k":"begin_the_challenge_2","v":{"s":"🔥 Begin the Challenge"}},{"k":"decision_event","v":{"s":"DECISION EVENT"}},{"k":"resolve_decision","v":{"s":"Resolve Decision"}},{"k":"moderate_2","v":{"s":"Moderate"}},{"k":"high_2","v":{"s":"High"}},{"k":"rank_progression","v":{"s":"Rank progression"}},{"k":"apprentice","v":{"s":"Apprentice"}},{"k":"journeyman","v":{"s":"Journeyman"}},{"k":"skilled","v":{"s":"Skilled"}},{"k":"master","v":{"s":"Master"}},{"k":"legendary","v":{"s":"Legendary"}},{"k":"report_card","v":{"s":"📋 Report Card"}},{"k":"years_survived","v":{"s":"Years Survived"}},{"k":"cultural_burns","v":{"s":"Cultural Burns"}},{"k":"wildfires","v":{"s":"Wildfires"}},{"k":"beaver_dams","v":{"s":"Beaver Dams"}},{"k":"decisions_won","v":{"s":"Decisions Won"}},{"k":"final_biodiversity","v":{"s":"Final Biodiversity"}},{"k":"final_soil_health","v":{"s":"Final Soil Health"}},{"k":"village_health","v":{"s":"Village Health"}},{"k":"species_returned","v":{"s":"Species Returned"}},{"k":"best_decade","v":{"s":"Best Decade"}},{"k":"species_that_returned_to_your_forest","v":{"s":"🦋 Species That Returned to Your Forest"}},{"k":"achievements_earned","v":{"s":"🏅 Achievements Earned"}},{"k":"play_again","v":{"s":"Play Again"}},{"k":"play_again_2","v":{"s":"🔄 Play Again"}},{"k":"year_4","v":{"s":"Year"}},{"k":"score_2","v":{"s":"Score"}},{"k":"fire_risk","v":{"s":"Fire Risk"}},{"k":"wildfires_2","v":{"s":"Wildfires"}},{"k":"village","v":{"s":"Village"}},{"k":"species_returned_2","v":{"s":"Species returned:"}},{"k":"choose_your_action","v":{"s":"🎮 Choose Your Action:"}},{"k":"cultural_burn_3","v":{"s":"🔥 Cultural Burn"}},{"k":"prescribed_burn_2","v":{"s":"📋 Prescribed Burn"}},{"k":"good_fuel_reduction","v":{"s":"Broad planned burn"}},{"k":"mech_thin","v":{"s":"🪓 Mech. Thin"}},{"k":"remove_heavy_fuel","v":{"s":"Machines cut and haul fuel"}},{"k":"plant_natives","v":{"s":"🌱 Plant Natives"}},{"k":"biodiversity_soil","v":{"s":"Sow native seed"}},{"k":"beaver_dams_2","v":{"s":"🦫 Beaver Dams"}},{"k":"water_fire_breaks","v":{"s":"Wetlands along the stream"}},{"k":"firebreaks","v":{"s":"🛡️ Firebreaks"}},{"k":"protect_village","v":{"s":"Clear a strip near the village"}},{"k":"educate","v":{"s":"🏫 Educate"}},{"k":"village_support","v":{"s":"Community fire workshops"}},{"k":"do_nothing","v":{"s":"⏸️ Do Nothing"}},{"k":"fuel_accumulates","v":{"s":"Let the decade pass"}},{"k":"timeline","v":{"s":"📊 Timeline"}},{"k":"biodiversity_2","v":{"s":"■ Biodiversity"}},{"k":"fuel_load_2","v":{"s":"■ Fuel Load"}},{"k":"log","v":{"s":"📜 Log"}},{"k":"did_you_know","v":{"s":"Did You Know? "}},{"k":"next_fact","v":{"s":"Next fact"}},{"k":"next_fact_2","v":{"s":"Next fact →"}},{"k":"back_to_stem_lab","v":{"s":"Back to STEAM Lab"}},{"k":"fire_ecology_indigenous_stewardship","v":{"s":"Fire Ecology & Indigenous Stewardship"}},{"k":"this_tool_honors_the_fire_stewardship_","v":{"s":"This tool honors the fire stewardship knowledge of Indigenous peoples worldwide, developed over tens of thousands of years. We recognize that this knowledge belongs to these nations and is shared here with the intent of education and respect, not appropriation. We encourage learners to seek out and support Indigenous-led fire management organizations and to listen to Indigenous fire keepers as the primary authorities on these practices."}},{"k":"healthy_ecosystem","v":{"s":"🌲 Lower modeled concern"}},{"k":"fuel_fire_balance_maintained_cultural_","v":{"s":"Lower concern in this classroom index; this is not an ecosystem-health determination."}},{"k":"dangerous_fuel_buildup","v":{"s":"⚠️ Dangerous fuel buildup"}},{"k":"decades_of_fire_suppression_next_ignit","v":{"s":"Elevated classroom index. Actual fire behavior also depends on fuels, weather, topography, and ignition."}},{"k":"megafire_risk","v":{"s":"🔥 Megafire risk"}},{"k":"high_fuel_drought_suppression_catastro","v":{"s":"High classroom index, not a forecast of ignition, spread, severity, or impacts."}},{"k":"type_conversion_forest_grassland","v":{"s":"🌾 Very short interval flag"}},{"k":"frequent_low_fuel_burns_convert_forest","v":{"s":"A very short interval may alter some communities, but outcomes depend on ecosystem, season, severity, and stewardship goals."}},{"k":"fire_regime_discovery","v":{"s":"🔥 Fire regime discovery"}},{"k":"sliders_for_fuel_accumulation_fire_ret","v":{"s":"Form a hypothesis, then test how fuel accumulation, return interval, and drought interact."}},{"k":"log_2","v":{"s":"📋 Log"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"hypothesis_how_does_drought_magnify_fu","v":{"s":"Hypothesis: How does drought magnify fuel-load risk?"}},{"k":"stuck_show_open_prompts","v":{"s":"🤔 Stuck — show open prompts"}},{"k":"cultural_burns_used_5_10_yr_intervals_","v":{"s":"Compare intervals only after naming the ecosystem, season, and stewardship objective."}},{"k":"why_does_80_year_fire_suppression_crea","v":{"s":"How can long fire exclusion alter fuels in some fire-adapted ecosystems?"}},{"k":"i_understand_explain_in_own_words","v":{"s":"I understand — explain in own words"}},{"k":"explain_how_fuel_load_fire_interval_an","v":{"s":"Explain how fuel load, fire interval, and drought jointly determine fire regime."}},{"k":"design_note_discrete_4_state_fire_regi","v":{"s":"Model limit: arbitrary index = fuel accumulation x drought severity / return interval. It omits fuel type and arrangement, wind, slope, ignition, season, prior treatments, and local ecology; labels are inquiry prompts, not predictions."}},{"k":"blueberryBarren_desc","v":{"s":"Open scrubland on glacial outwash. Frequent fire keeps heath low and clears competing shrubs. Wabanaki burned for thousands of years to maintain the blueberry crop."}},{"k":"oakSavanna_desc","v":{"s":"Open oak grassland. Ground fire every few years kills competing maple and birch saplings while mature oaks survive on their thick fire-resistant bark."}},{"k":"mixedConifer_desc","v":{"s":"Higher-elevation pine and spruce. Burns rarely; mostly self-maintaining. Hand thinning is the main intervention. A small understory burn maybe once a generation."}},{"k":"riparian_desc","v":{"s":"Stream banks and beaver wetlands. Almost never burned, moisture keeps fire out, and stream health depends on shaded canopy. Beavers do the work here."}},{"k":"whitePineGrove_desc","v":{"s":"A grove of eastern white pine on sandy soil. Tolerates surface fire once mature. Gentle burns every 20 to 30 years keep the understory open and the crowns healthy. Center of canoe-making and pitch economy."}},{"k":"intervaleMeadow_desc","v":{"s":"Rich river-floodplain land along the Penobscot, Kennebec, and Saco intervales. Wabanaki villages grew corn, beans, and squash here using fire to clear and frost-protect the fields. The most productive land in the territory."}},{"k":"hardwoodStand_desc","v":{"s":"Mature beech, birch, brown ash, sugar maple. Burns once a generation, very low intensity. Most stewardship is coppicing brown ash for the splints that define Wabanaki basketry."}},{"k":"apprentice_desc","v":{"s":"40 hours / year, kinder events. Good for a first run."}},{"k":"steward_desc","v":{"s":"32 hours / year, standard events. Default."}},{"k":"keeper_desc","v":{"s":"24 hours / year, harsher events. Tight constraint."}},{"k":"easy_description","v":{"s":"Fewer events. Wildfires only at extreme fuel levels."}},{"k":"medium_description","v":{"s":"Regular events + decision moments. Standard fire risk."}},{"k":"hard_description","v":{"s":"Frequent events. Climate change escalation. 150-year survival."}},{"k":"learn_route","v":{"s":"Learn"}},{"k":"investigate_route","v":{"s":"Investigate"}},{"k":"apply_route","v":{"s":"Apply"}},{"k":"choose_learning_route","v":{"s":"Choose a learning route"}},{"k":"route_help","v":{"s":"Move from knowledge to investigation, then apply what you discover."}},{"k":"activity_progress","v":{"s":"Activity"}},{"k":"ai_question_input","v":{"s":"Ask the AI fire ecology tutor"}},{"k":"land_stewardship_lab","v":{"s":"Land stewardship lab"}},{"k":"learning_status","v":{"s":"Learning status"}},{"k":"active_activity","v":{"s":"Active activity"}},{"k":"field_notes","v":{"s":"Field notes"}},{"k":"badges","v":{"s":"Badges"}},{"k":"learning_band","v":{"s":"Learning band"}},{"k":"about_this_learning_context","v":{"s":"About this learning context"}},{"k":"knowledge_acknowledgment","v":{"s":"Knowledge acknowledgment"}},{"k":"acknowledgment_label","v":{"s":"Acknowledgment: "}},{"k":"hypothesis_input","v":{"s":"Fire regime hypothesis"}},{"k":"explanation_input","v":{"s":"Fire regime explanation"}},{"k":"before_outcome_comparison","v":{"s":"Before and outcome model comparison"}},{"k":"before_treatment","v":{"s":"Before treatment"}},{"k":"burn_visualization_playback","v":{"s":"Burn visualization playback"}},{"k":"canopy_cover","v":{"s":"Canopy cover"}},{"k":"compare_same_start","v":{"s":"Both modeled forests begin with the same conditions. Advance them to see how the classroom scenarios diverge."}},{"k":"comparison_landscapes","v":{"s":"Modeled comparison landscapes"}},{"k":"cross_section_2d","v":{"s":"2D cross-section"}},{"k":"cultural_stewardship_scenario","v":{"s":"Cultural stewardship"}},{"k":"current_forest","v":{"s":"Current forest"}},{"k":"during_treatment","v":{"s":"During treatment"}},{"k":"flame_encoding","v":{"s":"Lower, patchier flames illustrate a surface-fire treatment; flames entering tree crowns appear only in the wildfire example."}},{"k":"forest_a_cultural","v":{"s":"Forest A: cultural stewardship"}},{"k":"forest_b_suppression","v":{"s":"Forest B: suppression"}},{"k":"ground_fuel","v":{"s":"Ground fuel"}},{"k":"landscape_3d","v":{"s":"3D landscape"}},{"k":"landscape_legend","v":{"s":"Landscape legend"}},{"k":"landscape_view","v":{"s":"Landscape view"}},{"k":"living_landscape_view","v":{"s":"Living landscape view"}},{"k":"loading_local_3d","v":{"s":"Loading the local 3D landscape..."}},{"k":"outcome","v":{"s":"Outcome"}},{"k":"pause","v":{"s":"Pause"}},{"k":"phase_before","v":{"s":"Before treatment"}},{"k":"phase_during","v":{"s":"During treatment"}},{"k":"phase_outcome","v":{"s":"Outcome"}},{"k":"prescribed_fire_scenario","v":{"s":"Prescribed fire"}},{"k":"replay_last_change","v":{"s":"Replay last change"}},{"k":"reset_view","v":{"s":"Reset view"}},{"k":"resume","v":{"s":"Resume"}},{"k":"rotate_left","v":{"s":"Rotate left"}},{"k":"rotate_right","v":{"s":"Rotate right"}},{"k":"scenario_separator_one","v":{"s":", "}},{"k":"scenario_separator_two","v":{"s":", or "}},{"k":"sim_goal_v2","v":{"s":"keep biodiversity above 70 and fuel load below 30 across 50+ modeled years without triggering a catastrophic wildfire. Return intervals in this activity are scenario-specific learning choices—not recommendations. Real stewardship decisions depend on place, governance, season, objectives, weather, and practitioner knowledge."}},{"k":"sim_strategy_context_v2","v":{"s":". These are not Indigenous-versus-Western categories: prescribed fire can be Indigenous-led or collaborative, while cultural burning is a broader place-based practice that this numerical model cannot reproduce."}},{"k":"sim_strategy_intro_v2","v":{"s":"Explore three simplified classroom scenarios over modeled decades: "}},{"k":"simulation_safety_note_v2","v":{"s":"Illustrative, time-compressed classroom visualization—not a fire-behavior forecast, burn plan, or authorization to use fire. Wind, slope, direction, ignition pattern, and containment are not modeled. Cultural burning is place-based, practitioner-led knowledge that includes relationships, governance, timing, and responsibilities beyond flame behavior; this scene does not reproduce a real cultural practice."}},{"k":"skip_to_outcome","v":{"s":"Skip to outcome"}},{"k":"smoke","v":{"s":"Smoke"}},{"k":"surface_fire","v":{"s":"Surface fire"}},{"k":"three_d_camera_controls","v":{"s":"3D camera controls"}},{"k":"three_d_fallback","v":{"s":"3D was unavailable, so the accessible 2D view is active. All simulation results are preserved."}},{"k":"tilt_down","v":{"s":"Tilt down"}},{"k":"tilt_up","v":{"s":"Tilt up"}},{"k":"total_suppression_scenario","v":{"s":"total fire suppression"}},{"k":"unburned_refuge","v":{"s":"Unburned refuge"}},{"k":"understory_density","v":{"s":"Understory"}},{"k":"visualization_phases","v":{"s":"Visualization phases"}},{"k":"visualizing","v":{"s":"Visualizing: "}},{"k":"what_changed","v":{"s":"What changed: "}},{"k":"zoom_in","v":{"s":"Zoom in"}},{"k":"zoom_out","v":{"s":"Zoom out"}}],"id":522}},{"k":"firstresponse","v":{"o":[{"k":"sr_consent_accepted_welcome_to_first_response_lab","v":{"s":"Consent accepted. Welcome to First Response Lab."}},{"k":"sr_back_to_menu","v":{"s":"Back to menu"}},{"k":"sr_quiz_started_question_1_of_5","v":{"s":"Quiz started. Question 1 of 5."}},{"k":"sr_quiz_restarted_question_1_of_5","v":{"s":"Quiz restarted. Question 1 of 5."}},{"k":"sr_back_to_recognize_cards","v":{"s":"Back to recognize cards"}},{"k":"sr_practice_mode","v":{"s":"Practice mode"}},{"k":"sr_aed_walkthrough","v":{"s":"AED walkthrough"}},{"k":"sr_begin_chest_compressions_now_30_second_timer_star","v":{"s":"Begin chest compressions now. 30 second timer started."}},{"k":"sr_aed_walkthrough_complete","v":{"s":"AED walkthrough complete."}},{"k":"sr_reset_to_step_1","v":{"s":"Reset to step 1."}},{"k":"sr_shock_advised_branch","v":{"s":"Shock advised branch."}},{"k":"sr_no_shock_advised_branch","v":{"s":"No shock advised branch."}},{"k":"sr_detailed_protocol","v":{"s":"Detailed protocol"}},{"k":"sr_tourniquet_placement","v":{"s":"Tourniquet placement"}},{"k":"sr_check_scene_safety_use_gloves_if_available_call_9","v":{"s":"Check scene safety, use gloves if available, call 911, and begin care."}},{"k":"sr_apply_steady_firm_direct_pressure_now","v":{"s":"Apply steady, firm direct pressure now."}},{"k":"sr_pressure_started_keep_holding_steadily","v":{"s":"Pressure started. Keep holding steadily."}},{"k":"sr_scenario_complete_keep_monitoring_breathing_respo","v":{"s":"Scenario complete. Keep monitoring breathing, responsiveness, warmth, and signs of shock until EMS arrives."}},{"k":"sr_pressure_hold_practiced_choose_the_next_action_fo","v":{"s":"Pressure hold practiced. Choose the next action for this wound location."}},{"k":"sr_correct_choose_a_safe_tourniquet_position","v":{"s":"Correct. Choose a safe tourniquet position."}},{"k":"sr_correct_pack_the_deep_wound_if_trained_then_keep","v":{"s":"Correct. Pack the deep wound if trained, then keep firm pressure."}},{"k":"sr_placement_correct_tighten_until_the_bleeding_stop","v":{"s":"Placement correct. Tighten until the bleeding stops."}},{"k":"sr_bleeding_stopped_secure_the_windlass_note_the_tim","v":{"s":"Bleeding stopped. Secure the windlass, note the time, and do not loosen the tourniquet."}},{"k":"sr_still_bleeding_keep_tightening","v":{"s":"Still bleeding. Keep tightening."}},{"k":"sr_wound_packed_apply_steady_firm_pressure_on_top_an","v":{"s":"Wound packed. Apply steady, firm pressure on top and keep holding."}},{"k":"sr_decide_whether_this_is_a_mild_or_severe_airway_ob","v":{"s":"Decide whether this is a mild or severe airway obstruction."}},{"k":"sr_severe_obstruction_activate_911_while_beginning_c","v":{"s":"Severe obstruction. Activate 911 while beginning care."}},{"k":"sr_give_5_separate_back_blows","v":{"s":"Give 5 separate back blows."}},{"k":"sr_choose_the_correct_thrust_placement","v":{"s":"Choose the correct thrust placement."}},{"k":"sr_they_become_unresponsive_choose_the_next_action","v":{"s":"They become unresponsive. Choose the next action."}},{"k":"sr_before_breaths_open_the_mouth_and_look_for_a_visi","v":{"s":"Before breaths, open the mouth and look for a visible object."}},{"k":"sr_scenario_complete_continue_cpr_and_follow_dispatc","v":{"s":"Scenario complete. Continue CPR and follow dispatcher or AED prompts until help arrives."}},{"k":"sr_pick_someone_else","v":{"s":"Pick someone else"}},{"k":"sr_back_to_scenario_list","v":{"s":"Back to scenario list"}},{"k":"sr_content_warning_shown","v":{"s":"Content warning shown."}},{"k":"sr_new_scene_loaded","v":{"s":"New scene loaded."}},{"k":"sr_generating_scene","v":{"s":"Generating scene..."}},{"k":"sr_scene_loaded","v":{"s":"Scene loaded."}},{"k":"sr_ai_unavailable_using_a_built_in_scene","v":{"s":"AI unavailable. Using a built-in scene."}},{"k":"sr_local_critique_ready","v":{"s":"Local critique ready."}},{"k":"sr_getting_critique","v":{"s":"Getting critique..."}},{"k":"sr_critique_ready","v":{"s":"Critique ready."}},{"k":"sr_no_normal_response_or_breathing_call_911_on_speak","v":{"s":"No normal response or breathing. Call 911 on speaker."}},{"k":"sr_begin_30_compressions_now_aim_for_100_to_120_per","v":{"s":"Begin 30 compressions now. Aim for 100 to 120 per minute."}},{"k":"sr_aed_step_complete_resume_compressions_now","v":{"s":"AED step complete. Resume compressions now."}},{"k":"sr_30_give_two_breaths_about_one_second_each","v":{"s":"30. Give two breaths, about one second each."}},{"k":"sr_second_breath_let_the_chest_fall_then_resume_comp","v":{"s":"Second breath. Let the chest fall, then resume compressions."}},{"k":"sr_aed_arrives_apply_the_aed_and_follow_its_prompts","v":{"s":"AED arrives. Apply the AED and follow its prompts."}},{"k":"sr_resume_compressions_now","v":{"s":"Resume compressions now."}},{"k":"sr_first_breath_let_the_chest_fall_then_give_the_sec","v":{"s":"First breath. Let the chest fall, then give the second breath."}},{"k":"a11y_tourniquet_tightening_practice","v":{"s":"Tourniquet tightening practice"}},{"k":"a11y_body_position_practice_sections","v":{"s":"Body position practice sections"}},{"k":"a11y_compressions_in_this_cycle","v":{"s":"Compressions in this cycle"}},{"k":"call_911","v":{"s":"Call 911"}},{"k":"start_cpr","v":{"s":"Start CPR"}},{"k":"apply_aed","v":{"s":"Apply AED"