k approach for math instruction in special education. "}},{"k":"move_through_three_stages_with_the_sam","v":{"s":"Move through three stages with the same fraction to build conceptual understanding before procedural fluency."}},{"k":"cra_stage","v":{"s":"CRA stage"}},{"k":"numerator_2","v":{"s":"Numerator"}},{"k":"denominator_2","v":{"s":"Denominator"}},{"k":"previous_stage","v":{"s":"← Previous stage"}},{"k":"next_stage","v":{"s":"Next stage →"}},{"k":"real_world_word_problems","v":{"s":"📖 Real-world word problems"}},{"k":"fractions_make_sense_when_they_connect","v":{"s":"Fractions make sense when they connect to the world. Pick a context and a grade level to find problems that match your interests."}},{"k":"context_filter","v":{"s":"Context filter"}},{"k":"all_contexts","v":{"s":"All contexts"}},{"k":"difficulty_filter","v":{"s":"Difficulty filter"}},{"k":"all_grades","v":{"s":"All grades"}},{"k":"easy_3_4","v":{"s":"Easy (3-4)"}},{"k":"medium_4_5","v":{"s":"Medium (4-5)"}},{"k":"hard_5_6","v":{"s":"Hard (5-6)"}},{"k":"word_problem_answer","v":{"s":"Word problem answer"}},{"k":"check","v":{"s":"Check"}},{"k":"show_solution","v":{"s":"📚 Show solution"}},{"k":"previous_problem","v":{"s":"Previous problem"}},{"k":"prev","v":{"s":"← Prev"}},{"k":"next_problem","v":{"s":"Next problem"}},{"k":"next","v":{"s":"Next →"}},{"k":"common_core_standards_k_8_fraction_tra","v":{"s":"📋 Common Core Standards — K-8 fraction trajectory"}},{"k":"each_tool_in_fraction_lab_is_mapped_to","v":{"s":"Each tool in Fraction Lab is mapped to one or more CCSS standards. Use this view to plan instruction, find tools for a specific standard, or build evidence for IEP goal alignment."}},{"k":"common_fraction_misconceptions","v":{"s":"⚠️ Common fraction misconceptions"}},{"k":"a_reference_library_of_the_12_most_doc","v":{"s":"A reference library of the 12 most-documented fraction misconceptions, each with research-grounded remediation strategies. "}},{"k":"click_any_misconception_to_expand_its_","v":{"s":"Click any misconception to expand its full description, why it happens, and what to do about it."}},{"k":"why_it_happens","v":{"s":"🤔 Why it happens"}},{"k":"remediation_strategies","v":{"s":"🛠️ Remediation strategies"}},{"k":"pizza_shop","v":{"s":"Pizza Shop"}},{"k":"customers_will_order_fractional_pizzas","v":{"s":"Customers will order fractional pizzas. Slice the pizza into the right number of pieces and serve the right amount. "}},{"k":"earn_tips_serve_10_customers_to_win","v":{"s":"Earn tips. Serve 10 customers to win!"}},{"k":"start_serving","v":{"s":"🍕 Start serving"}},{"k":"restart","v":{"s":"↺ Restart"}},{"k":"i_d_like","v":{"s":"\"I'd like "}},{"k":"of_a_pizza_please","v":{"s":" of a pizza, please!\""}},{"k":"pizza_size_total_slices","v":{"s":"Pizza size (total slices):"}},{"k":"slices_to_serve","v":{"s":"Slices to serve:"}},{"k":"fraction_race","v":{"s":"Fraction Race"}},{"k":"see_a_visual_fraction_type_it_as_fast_","v":{"s":"See a visual fraction. Type it as fast as you can. Score as many as possible in 30 seconds!"}},{"k":"start_race","v":{"s":"🏁 Start race"}},{"k":"restart_2","v":{"s":"↺ Restart"}},{"k":"what_fraction_is_this","v":{"s":"What fraction is this?"}},{"k":"e_g_3_4","v":{"s":"e.g., 3/4"}},{"k":"race_answer","v":{"s":"Race answer"}},{"k":"submit","v":{"s":"Submit"}},{"k":"equivalent_match","v":{"s":"Equivalent Match"}},{"k":"find_pairs_of_equivalent_fractions_6_p","v":{"s":"Find pairs of equivalent fractions. 6 pairs total. Try to do it in as few moves as possible."}},{"k":"start_matching","v":{"s":"🃏 Start matching"}},{"k":"restart_3","v":{"s":"↺ Restart"}},{"k":"fraction_fish","v":{"s":"Fraction Fish"}},{"k":"each_round_shows_a_target_fraction_and","v":{"s":"Each round shows a target fraction and 4 fish. Catch the one that matches. "}},{"k":"you_have_3_lives_wrong_catches_lose_a_","v":{"s":"You have 3 lives. Wrong catches lose a life."}},{"k":"cast_a_line","v":{"s":"🎣 Cast a line"}},{"k":"game_over","v":{"s":"Game over!"}},{"k":"final_score","v":{"s":"Final score: "}},{"k":"cast_again","v":{"s":"🎣 Cast again"}},{"k":"restart_4","v":{"s":"↺ Restart"}},{"k":"catch_the_fish_that_equals","v":{"s":"Catch the fish that equals:"}},{"k":"build_the_whole","v":{"s":"🧱 Build the Whole"}},{"k":"combine_fraction_strips_to_make_exactl","v":{"s":"Combine fraction strips to make exactly 1. Choose pieces that add to the whole."}},{"k":"current_sum","v":{"s":"Current sum: "}},{"k":"clear","v":{"s":"↺ Clear"}},{"k":"no_pieces_yet_add_from_below","v":{"s":"No pieces yet. Add from below."}},{"k":"pick_a_piece_to_add","v":{"s":"Pick a piece to add:"}},{"k":"build_again","v":{"s":"🧱 Build again"}},{"k":"pattern_builder","v":{"s":"Pattern Builder"}},{"k":"see_a_sequence_of_fractions_what_comes","v":{"s":"See a sequence of fractions. What comes next?"}},{"k":"start","v":{"s":"🔢 Start"}},{"k":"restart_5","v":{"s":"↺ Restart"}},{"k":"what_comes_next","v":{"s":"What comes next?"}},{"k":"e_g_3_4_2","v":{"s":"e.g., 3/4"}},{"k":"guess","v":{"s":"Guess"}},{"k":"fraction_bingo","v":{"s":"Fraction Bingo"}},{"k":"5_5_bingo_card_with_fractions_call_a_f","v":{"s":"5×5 bingo card with fractions. Call a fraction, then mark any cell with an equivalent fraction. Get 5 in a row to win!"}},{"k":"new_card","v":{"s":"🎱 New card"}},{"k":"new_card_2","v":{"s":"↺ New card"}},{"k":"now_calling","v":{"s":"Now calling:"}},{"k":"or_any_equivalent","v":{"s":"(or any equivalent)"}},{"k":"call_a_number","v":{"s":"🎲 Call a number"}},{"k":"tug_of_war","v":{"s":"Tug of War"}},{"k":"two_fractions_face_off_pick_which_is_l","v":{"s":"Two fractions face off. Pick which is larger to pull the rope. 5 correct pulls = win the tug!"}},{"k":"start_tugging","v":{"s":"🪢 Start tugging"}},{"k":"restart_6","v":{"s":"↺ Restart"}},{"k":"tap_the_bigger_fraction_to_pull","v":{"s":"Tap the bigger fraction to pull!"}},{"k":"hide_and_seek","v":{"s":"Hide and Seek"}},{"k":"a_fraction_is_hiding_use_the_clues_to_","v":{"s":"A fraction is hiding. Use the clues to guess what it is. Fewer hints = more points."}},{"k":"start_hunt","v":{"s":"🔍 Start hunt"}},{"k":"new_hunt","v":{"s":"↺ New hunt"}},{"k":"what_fraction_is_hiding","v":{"s":"🔮 What fraction is hiding?"}},{"k":"guess_e_g_3_4","v":{"s":"Guess (e.g., 3/4)"}},{"k":"guess_2","v":{"s":"Guess"}},{"k":"belt_speed","v":{"s":"Belt speed"}},{"k":"belt_speed_2","v":{"s":"Belt speed"}},{"k":"plate_rush_the_even_steven_diner","v":{"s":"Plate Rush: The Even-Steven Diner"}},{"k":"house_rule_every_guest_at_a_table_gets","v":{"s":"House rule: every guest at a table gets an EXACTLY equal plate. Divide each dish into the table's number of equal shares, then read off the fraction each guest gets."}},{"k":"cook_zen_no_timer","v":{"s":"▶ Cook (Zen - no timer)"}},{"k":"timed_service","v":{"s":"⏱ Timed Service"}},{"k":"level","v":{"s":"Level"}},{"k":"show_read_it_pick_choose_the_fraction_","v":{"s":"Show = read it; Pick = choose the fraction; Type = type it (hardest). Auto-set by level; change anytime."}},{"k":"accessibility_comfort","v":{"s":"♿ Accessibility & Comfort"}},{"k":"quiet_kid","v":{"s":"Quiet Kid"}},{"k":"motor","v":{"s":"Motor"}},{"k":"visual_3","v":{"s":"Visual"}},{"k":"audio_only","v":{"s":"Audio only"}},{"k":"zen_mode_has_no_timer_and_no_game_over","v":{"s":"Zen mode has no timer and no game-over. A missed plate in Timed mode just loops back around."}},{"k":"service_complete_even_steven_approves","v":{"s":"Service complete - Even Steven approves!"}},{"k":"practice_this_sitting","v":{"s":"📋 Practice this sitting"}},{"k":"no_stumbles_every_serve_was_fair","v":{"s":"No stumbles - every serve was fair."}},{"k":"a_record_of_what_was_practiced_not_a_m","v":{"s":"A record of what was practiced, not a measure of ability."}},{"k":"same_level_again","v":{"s":"Same level again"}},{"k":"change_mode","v":{"s":"Change mode"}},{"k":"each_guest","v":{"s":"each guest:"}},{"k":"each_guest_gets","v":{"s":"Each guest gets "}},{"k":"each_guest_gets_2","v":{"s":"Each guest gets "}},{"k":"each_guest_gets_3","v":{"s":"Each guest gets "}},{"k":"of_the_tray","v":{"s":" of the tray"}},{"k":"those_groups_are_not_equal_every_guest","v":{"s":"Those groups are not equal - every guest must get the same."}},{"k":"how_much_does_each_guest_get","v":{"s":"How much does each guest get?"}},{"k":"type_how_much_each_guest_gets","v":{"s":"Type how much each guest gets:"}},{"k":"each_guest_gets_4","v":{"s":"Each guest gets"}},{"k":"any_equal_form_counts_2_8_is_the_same_","v":{"s":"Any equal form counts - 2/8 is the same as 1/4."}},{"k":"to_zen","v":{"s":"To Zen"}},{"k":"menu","v":{"s":"↺ Menu"}},{"k":"split_equally_for_this_table","v":{"s":"Split equally for this table:"}},{"k":"equal_shares","v":{"s":"Equal shares:"}},{"k":"fewer_shares","v":{"s":"Fewer shares"}},{"k":"more_shares","v":{"s":"More shares"}},{"k":"show_me","v":{"s":"Show me"}},{"k":"serve","v":{"s":"SERVE 🍽️"}},{"k":"back_to_games","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"back_to_games_2","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"back_to_games_3","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"back_to_games_4","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"back_to_games_5","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"back_to_games_6","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"back_to_games_7","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"back_to_games_8","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"back_to_games_9","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"back_to_games_10","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"back_to_games_11","v":{"s":"← Back to games"}},{"k":"plate_rush","v":{"s":"Plate Rush"}},{"k":"share_dishes_into_equal_plates_for_tab","v":{"s":"Share dishes into equal plates for tables of guests. Zen (no-timer) default."}},{"k":"pizza_shop_2","v":{"s":"Pizza Shop"}},{"k":"serve_customers_fractional_pizzas_earn","v":{"s":"Serve customers fractional pizzas. Earn tips. 10 customers to win."}},{"k":"fraction_race_2","v":{"s":"Fraction Race"}},{"k":"type_the_fraction_you_see_beat_the_30_","v":{"s":"Type the fraction you see. Beat the 30-second clock."}},{"k":"equivalent_match_2","v":{"s":"Equivalent Match"}},{"k":"memory_pairing_find_6_pairs_of_equival","v":{"s":"Memory pairing — find 6 pairs of equivalent fractions."}},{"k":"fraction_fish_2","v":{"s":"Fraction Fish"}},{"k":"catch_the_fish_whose_fraction_matches_","v":{"s":"Catch the fish whose fraction matches the target. 3 lives."}},{"k":"fraction_bingo_2","v":{"s":"Fraction Bingo"}},{"k":"5_5_card_mark_equivalent_fractions_to_","v":{"s":"5×5 card. Mark equivalent fractions to get 5-in-a-row."}},{"k":"tug_of_war_2","v":{"s":"Tug of War"}},{"k":"pick_the_larger_fraction_to_pull_the_r","v":{"s":"Pick the larger fraction to pull the rope. First to 5 wins."}},{"k":"hide_seek","v":{"s":"Hide & Seek"}},{"k":"guess_the_hidden_fraction_using_progre","v":{"s":"Guess the hidden fraction using progressive clues."}},{"k":"build_the_whole_2","v":{"s":"Build the Whole"}},{"k":"combine_fraction_strips_to_make_exactl_2","v":{"s":"Combine fraction strips to make exactly 1."}},{"k":"pattern_builder_2","v":{"s":"Pattern Builder"}},{"k":"identify_the_next_fraction_in_a_sequen","v":{"s":"Identify the next fraction in a sequence."}},{"k":"place_fraction_discs_in_a_7_6_grid_two","v":{"s":"Place fraction discs in a 7×6 grid. Two players."}},{"k":"fraction_games","v":{"s":"🎮 Fraction games"}},{"k":"four_games_practice_different_fraction","v":{"s":"Four games practice different fraction skills. Pizza Shop drills part-of-whole intuition. Race drills speed. Match drills equivalence. Fish drills magnitude comparison."}},{"k":"identify_fractions","v":{"s":"Identify fractions"}},{"k":"simplify","v":{"s":"Simplify"}},{"k":"equivalent_fractions","v":{"s":"Equivalent fractions"}},{"k":"compare","v":{"s":"Compare"}},{"k":"add_unlike_denominators","v":{"s":"Add (unlike denominators)"}},{"k":"subtract_unlike_denominators","v":{"s":"Subtract (unlike denominators)"}},{"k":"multiply","v":{"s":"Multiply"}},{"k":"divide","v":{"s":"Divide"}},{"k":"worksheet_generator_teacher_tool","v":{"s":"📝 Worksheet generator (teacher tool)"}},{"k":"generate_printable_practice_worksheets","v":{"s":"Generate printable practice worksheets with answer keys. Pick a topic, number of problems, and print."}},{"k":"topic","v":{"s":"Topic"}},{"k":"worksheet_topic","v":{"s":"Worksheet topic"}},{"k":"number_of_problems","v":{"s":"Number of problems"}},{"k":"problem_count","v":{"s":"Problem count"}},{"k":"include_answer_key","v":{"s":"Include answer key"}},{"k":"include_answer_key_on_a_separate_page","v":{"s":"Include answer key on a separate page"}},{"k":"print_worksheet","v":{"s":"🖨 Print worksheet"}},{"k":"progress_report_teacher_tool","v":{"s":"📊 Progress report (teacher tool)"}},{"k":"snapshot_of_student_practice_in_this_s","v":{"s":"Snapshot of student practice in this session. Useful as supplementary evidence for IEP/RTI documentation. "}},{"k":"not_a_standardized_assessment","v":{"s":"Not a standardized assessment."}},{"k":"attempted","v":{"s":"Attempted"}},{"k":"accuracy","v":{"s":"Accuracy"}},{"k":"best_streak","v":{"s":"Best streak"}},{"k":"skill_breakdown","v":{"s":"Skill breakdown"}},{"k":"equivalent_fractions_2","v":{"s":"Equivalent fractions"}},{"k":"simplifications","v":{"s":"Simplifications"}},{"k":"operations","v":{"s":"Operations"}},{"k":"conversions","v":{"s":"Conversions"}},{"k":"challenge_types_attempted","v":{"s":"Challenge types attempted"}},{"k":"badges_earned","v":{"s":"Badges earned"}},{"k":"copy_to_clipboard","v":{"s":"📋 Copy to clipboard"}},{"k":"download_txt","v":{"s":"💾 Download .txt"}},{"k":"preview_report","v":{"s":"👀 Preview report"}},{"k":"fraction_vocabulary","v":{"s":"📖 Fraction vocabulary"}},{"k":"definitions_of_every_fraction_term_use","v":{"s":"Definitions of every fraction term used in K-8 math instruction, with examples. Searchable."}},{"k":"search_vocabulary","v":{"s":"Search vocabulary..."}},{"k":"search_vocabulary_2","v":{"s":"Search vocabulary"}},{"k":"no_matches","v":{"s":"No matches."}},{"k":"iep_goal_bank_fraction_specific","v":{"s":"🎯 IEP Goal Bank — fraction-specific"}},{"k":"pre_formatted_smart_goals_for_iep_team","v":{"s":"Pre-formatted SMART goals for IEP teams. Each goal links to a CCSS standard, suggests progress-monitoring data sources within AlloFlow, and lists common accommodations. Copy and adapt for your student."}},{"k":"show_accommodations_and_progress_monit","v":{"s":"Show accommodations and progress monitoring"}},{"k":"progress_monitoring","v":{"s":"Progress monitoring: "}},{"k":"copy_goal_to_clipboard","v":{"s":"📋 Copy goal to clipboard"}},{"k":"all_lesson_plans","v":{"s":"← All lesson plans"}},{"k":"learning_objectives","v":{"s":"🎯 Learning objectives"}},{"k":"lesson_plan_templates","v":{"s":"📚 Lesson plan templates"}},{"k":"ready_to_use_micro_units_3_5_days_each","v":{"s":"Ready-to-use micro-units (3-5 days each) for common fraction topics. Each plan ties activities to specific Fraction Lab tabs so you can demo or assign directly."}},{"k":"where_do_fractions_come_from","v":{"s":"Where do fractions come from?"}},{"k":"the_earliest_fraction_notation_dates_t","v":{"s":"The earliest fraction notation dates to ancient Egypt around 1800 BCE. The Egyptians used \"unit fractions\" — only fractions with numerator 1 (like 1/2, 1/3, 1/4). They wrote any other fraction as a sum of unit fractions: 2/5 = 1/3 + 1/15. The modern bar notation (numerator over denominator) comes from medieval Arabic mathematicians around the 1200s CE."}},{"k":"where_do_the_fraction_words_come_from","v":{"s":"Where do the fraction words come from?"}},{"k":"numerator_comes_from_the_latin_numerar","v":{"s":"\"Numerator\" comes from the Latin \"numerare\" (to count) — it counts how many parts. \"Denominator\" comes from \"denominare\" (to name) — it names the size of the parts. Together: the denominator names what kind of pieces; the numerator counts how many of those pieces you have."}},{"k":"the_decimal_point","v":{"s":"The decimal point"}},{"k":"decimals_as_we_know_them_were_populari","v":{"s":"Decimals as we know them were popularized by Simon Stevin in 1585 in his book \"De Thiende\" (The Tenth). Before that, fractions were the only way to express non-whole numbers. The decimal point became universally adopted only in the 1700s."}},{"k":"what_does_percent_mean","v":{"s":"What does percent mean?"}},{"k":"percent_comes_from_the_latin_per_centu","v":{"s":"\"Percent\" comes from the Latin \"per centum\" — \"per hundred.\" So 25% literally means 25 per 100, or 25/100. The % symbol evolved from the abbreviation \"per c.\" in 15th-century Italian commercial writing."}},{"k":"what_is_a_reciprocal","v":{"s":"What is a reciprocal?"}},{"k":"the_reciprocal_of_a_b_is_b_a_flip_it_u","v":{"s":"The reciprocal of a/b is b/a — flip it upside down. Every nonzero fraction has a reciprocal. The product of a fraction and its reciprocal is always 1: (3/4) × (4/3) = 12/12 = 1. This is why dividing by a fraction is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal."}},{"k":"why_is_1_2_the_most_used_fraction","v":{"s":"Why is 1/2 the most-used fraction?"}},{"k":"1_2_is_the_most_common_fraction_in_eve","v":{"s":"1/2 is the most common fraction in everyday speech because it sits exactly in the middle of 0 and 1. It is also the only fraction we routinely express in words: \"half\" instead of \"one over two.\" Other languages have unique words for 1/3 and 1/4 too (third, quarter)."}},{"k":"pizza_is_mathematical","v":{"s":"Pizza is mathematical"}},{"k":"a_pizza_is_a_perfect_fraction_model_be","v":{"s":"A pizza is a perfect fraction model because it is a circle (so all slices radiate from the center), the slices are easy to count, and the model maps onto the formal mathematical definition: a fraction n/d is n equal parts out of d total equal parts."}},{"k":"when_fractions_are_not_enough","v":{"s":"When fractions are not enough"}},{"k":"some_numbers_like_and_2_cannot_be_writ","v":{"s":"Some numbers, like π and √2, cannot be written as a fraction of two whole numbers. These are called irrational numbers. The Pythagoreans (around 500 BCE) reportedly killed the mathematician Hippasus when he proved that √2 could not be written as a fraction."}},{"k":"continued_fractions","v":{"s":"Continued fractions"}},{"k":"any_real_number_can_be_written_as_a_co","v":{"s":"Any real number can be written as a \"continued fraction\" — a nested fraction like 1 + 1/(2 + 1/(2 + 1/(2 + ...))). This gives the best fraction approximations. π ≈ 22/7 from the first few terms; even better is 355/113."}},{"k":"fractions_in_music","v":{"s":"Fractions in music"}},{"k":"musical_pitch_ratios_are_fractions_the","v":{"s":"Musical pitch ratios are fractions. The octave is a 2:1 ratio (frequency doubles). The perfect fifth is 3:2. The major third is 5:4. Pythagoras discovered that simple integer ratios produce harmonious sounds."}},{"k":"why_the_common_denominator","v":{"s":"Why the common denominator?"}},{"k":"two_pizzas_can_only_be_combined_if_the","v":{"s":"Two pizzas can only be combined if they are cut into the same-size slices. Different denominators = different-size slices = can't directly combine. The common denominator literally means \"same-size pieces.\""}},{"k":"baseball_stats_are_fractions","v":{"s":"Baseball stats are fractions"}},{"k":"a_batting_average_like_333_means_1_3_o","v":{"s":"A batting average like .333 means 1/3 of at-bats result in a hit. A pitcher's ERA, on-base percentage, slugging percentage — all of them are fractions. Baseball was the first sport to popularize this kind of statistical thinking, starting in the 1850s."}},{"k":"cuisenaire_rods","v":{"s":"Cuisenaire rods"}},{"k":"georges_cuisenaire_was_a_belgian_prima","v":{"s":"Georges Cuisenaire was a Belgian primary teacher in the 1950s who invented colored rods of length 1 to 10 to help children grasp number relationships including fractions. The \"fraction wall\" you see in many classrooms is the digital descendant of his physical rods."}},{"k":"fractions_in_ancient_china","v":{"s":"Fractions in ancient China"}},{"k":"the_chinese_mathematical_text_nine_cha","v":{"s":"The Chinese mathematical text \"Nine Chapters on the Mathematical Art\" (around 100 BCE) included fraction arithmetic, including a procedure for finding common denominators that is mathematically equivalent to what we teach today."}},{"k":"computers_and_fractions","v":{"s":"Computers and fractions"}},{"k":"computers_store_decimal_fractions_in_b","v":{"s":"Computers store decimal fractions in binary. The decimal 0.1 cannot be represented exactly in binary — it becomes a repeating fraction in base 2. This is why 0.1 + 0.2 sometimes gives 0.30000000000000004 in programming languages."}},{"k":"fraction_adjacent_sayings","v":{"s":"🗣 Fraction-adjacent sayings"}},{"k":"dogs_spend_about_1_2_their_lives_sleep","v":{"s":"Dogs spend about 1/2 their lives sleeping. A 12-year-old dog has slept about 6 years."}},{"k":"cats_sleep_about_2_3_of_every_day_that","v":{"s":"Cats sleep about 2/3 of every day. That's 16 hours daily."}},{"k":"elephants_drink_about_1_8_of_their_bod","v":{"s":"Elephants drink about 1/8 of their body weight in water per day. A 12,000-pound elephant drinks 1,500 lbs of water!"}},{"k":"a_blue_whale_s_tongue_weighs_about_1_2","v":{"s":"A blue whale's tongue weighs about 1/2 of a small car (~6,000 lbs)."}},{"k":"a_bee_visits_about_1_500_flowers_to_ma","v":{"s":"A bee visits about 1,500 flowers to make 1/12 teaspoon of honey."}},{"k":"a_giraffe_s_neck_is_about_1_3_of_its_t","v":{"s":"A giraffe's neck is about 1/3 of its total height."}},{"k":"a_snail_moves_at_about_1_40_of_a_mile_","v":{"s":"A snail moves at about 1/40 of a mile per hour. It would take 40 hours to crawl 1 mile."}},{"k":"a_kangaroo_can_leap_a_distance_about_3","v":{"s":"A kangaroo can leap a distance about 3/2 of its body length in one hop."}},{"k":"a_dolphin_sleeps_with_half_its_brain_a","v":{"s":"A dolphin sleeps with half its brain at a time — only 1/2 of the brain rests while the other half stays alert."}},{"k":"a_giant_tortoise_can_live_to_150_years","v":{"s":"A giant tortoise can live to 150+ years. A 100-year-old tortoise has lived 2/3 of its potential lifespan."}},{"k":"animal_fractions","v":{"s":"🐾 Animal fractions"}},{"k":"real_world_fraction_facts_from_the_ani","v":{"s":"Real-world fraction facts from the animal kingdom. Use as journal prompts, attention-grabbers, or cross-curricular tie-ins to science."}},{"k":"acknowledgments","v":{"s":"🙏 Acknowledgments"}},{"k":"alloflow_fraction_lab_stands_on_the_sh","v":{"s":"AlloFlow Fraction Lab stands on the shoulders of decades of mathematics education research and practice."}},{"k":"pedagogical_foundations","v":{"s":"Pedagogical foundations: "}},{"k":"robert_siegler_and_colleagues_for_the_","v":{"s":"Robert Siegler and colleagues for the IES Practice Guide that shaped this tool's emphasis on magnitude reasoning and the number-line model. "}},{"k":"cra_framework","v":{"s":"CRA framework: "}},{"k":"jerome_bruner_1966_for_the_original_en","v":{"s":"Jerome Bruner (1966) for the original enactive-iconic-symbolic progression. Sealander et al. for evidence in special education contexts. "}},{"k":"manipulatives_heritage","v":{"s":"Manipulatives heritage: "}},{"k":"georges_cuisenaire_1952_for_the_rod_sy","v":{"s":"Georges Cuisenaire (1952) for the rod system that became the fraction wall and fraction strip models. "}},{"k":"misconception_research","v":{"s":"Misconception research: "}},{"k":"vamvakoussi_vosniadou_stafylidou_lorti","v":{"s":"Vamvakoussi, Vosniadou, Stafylidou, Lortie-Forgues, and many others whose careful documentation of student thinking made the Misconceptions tab possible. "}},{"k":"number_talks","v":{"s":"Number Talks: "}},{"k":"sherry_parrish_for_the_routine_that_in","v":{"s":"Sherry Parrish for the routine that informed the Math Talks tab. "}},{"k":"universal_design_for_learning","v":{"s":"Universal Design for Learning: "}},{"k":"cast_for_the_udl_guidelines_that_shape","v":{"s":"CAST for the UDL guidelines that shape every feature decision. "}},{"k":"alloflow_developer","v":{"s":"AlloFlow developer: "}},{"k":"open_source_spirit","v":{"s":"Open-source spirit: "}},{"k":"mathematics_is_the_music_of_reason_jam","v":{"s":"\"Mathematics is the music of reason.\" — James Joseph Sylvester"}},{"k":"changelog","v":{"s":"📜 Changelog"}},{"k":"version_history_of_alloflow_fraction_l","v":{"s":"Version history of AlloFlow Fraction Lab. The v3.0 expansion brought it to its current size."}},{"k":"connect_four_fractions","v":{"s":"Connect-Four Fractions"}},{"k":"2_player_game_place_discs_that_show_ra","v":{"s":"2-player game. Place discs that show random fractions in the 7×6 grid. Have fun naming the fractions."}},{"k":"start_game","v":{"s":"⚪ Start game"}},{"k":"restart_7","v":{"s":"↺ Restart"}},{"k":"grades_k_3_morning_warm_up_10_min","v":{"s":"Grades K-3 morning warm-up (10 min)"}},{"k":"pick_one_number_talk_string_students_e","v":{"s":"Pick one Number Talk string. Students explain reasoning out loud."}},{"k":"show_3_4_fractions_in_the_pie_model_st","v":{"s":"Show 3-4 fractions in the pie model. Students identify or describe."}},{"k":"5_quick_benchmark_questions","v":{"s":"5 quick benchmark questions."}},{"k":"grades_4_5_fraction_block_30_min","v":{"s":"Grades 4-5 fraction block (30 min)"}},{"k":"number_talk_string","v":{"s":"Number Talk string."}},{"k":"walk_through_1_worked_example","v":{"s":"Walk through 1 Worked Example."}},{"k":"practice_with_the_operation_taught","v":{"s":"Practice with the operation taught."}},{"k":"quick_3_question_check","v":{"s":"Quick 3-question check."}},{"k":"rti_tier_2_small_group_20_min","v":{"s":"RTI Tier 2 small-group (20 min)"}},{"k":"quick_fluency_check_charted_weekly","v":{"s":"Quick fluency check (charted weekly)."}},{"k":"walk_through_concrete_representational","v":{"s":"Walk through Concrete → Representational → Abstract for current topic."}},{"k":"curated_practice_items_at_student_s_le","v":{"s":"Curated practice items at student's level."}},{"k":"look_at_mastery_dashboard_together","v":{"s":"Look at mastery dashboard together."}},{"k":"enrichment_30_min","v":{"s":"Enrichment (30 min)"}},{"k":"pick_a_hard_puzzle_discuss_strategies","v":{"s":"Pick a hard puzzle. Discuss strategies."}},{"k":"race_or_hide_seek","v":{"s":"Race or Hide & Seek."}},{"k":"read_a_real_world_tool_example_aloud_d","v":{"s":"Read a real-world tool example aloud. Discuss."}},{"k":"review_day_45_min","v":{"s":"Review day (45 min)"}},{"k":"estimation_trainer","v":{"s":"Estimation Trainer."}},{"k":"mixed_worksheet","v":{"s":"Mixed worksheet."}},{"k":"3_problems_with_hints_if_needed","v":{"s":"3 problems with hints if needed."}},{"k":"student_picks_a_game","v":{"s":"Student picks a game."}},{"k":"quick_assessment","v":{"s":"Quick assessment."}},{"k":"daily_routine_templates","v":{"s":"⏱ Daily routine templates"}},{"k":"pre_built_sequences_of_activities_that","v":{"s":"Pre-built sequences of activities that fit common time blocks (10 min, 30 min, 45 min). Pick one and follow it."}},{"k":"identify_fractions_2","v":{"s":"Identify fractions"}},{"k":"equivalent_fractions_3","v":{"s":"Equivalent fractions"}},{"k":"compare_fractions","v":{"s":"Compare fractions"}},{"k":"add_fractions","v":{"s":"Add fractions"}},{"k":"multiply_fractions","v":{"s":"Multiply fractions"}},{"k":"exit_ticket_generator","v":{"s":"🎫 Exit ticket generator"}},{"k":"generate_a_3_question_exit_ticket_on_t","v":{"s":"Generate a 3-question exit ticket on the topic just taught. Print and hand out at the end of the lesson."}},{"k":"topic_2","v":{"s":"Topic"}},{"k":"generate_and_print_exit_ticket","v":{"s":"🖨 Generate and print exit ticket"}},{"k":"grade_3_fraction_assessment_checklist","v":{"s":"Grade 3 Fraction Assessment Checklist"}},{"k":"grade_4_fraction_assessment_checklist","v":{"s":"Grade 4 Fraction Assessment Checklist"}},{"k":"grade_5_fraction_assessment_checklist","v":{"s":"Grade 5 Fraction Assessment Checklist"}},{"k":"assessment_checklist","v":{"s":"☑ Assessment checklist"}},{"k":"per_grade_skills_checklists_use_during","v":{"s":"Per-grade skills checklists. Use during one-on-one assessment or to plan instruction."}},{"k":"my_child_says_i_hate_fractions","v":{"s":"My child says \"I hate fractions\""}},{"k":"very_common_fractions_break_the_rules_","v":{"s":"Very common. Fractions break the rules students learn for whole numbers — bigger numbers don't always mean bigger values. The frustration is real and normal. Help by: (1) using visual models like pizzas or fraction strips, (2) connecting to real life (cooking, time, money), (3) practicing little and often (5 min a day) rather than long sessions, (4) celebrating effort, not just correct answers."}},{"k":"my_child_doesn_t_understand_why_proced","v":{"s":"My child doesn't understand WHY procedures work"}},{"k":"they_are_not_alone_most_students_learn","v":{"s":"They are not alone — most students learn the procedure first and the why later. Help by always showing what the procedure looks like with a picture. \"Multiply 3/4 by 1/2\" can be drawn as a rectangle. The Op Proofs tab does this for you. Ask \"why?\" gently and frequently."}},{"k":"how_can_i_help_with_homework_without_d","v":{"s":"How can I help with homework without doing it for them?"}},{"k":"use_the_worked_examples_tab_they_show_","v":{"s":"Use the Worked Examples tab — they show step-by-step procedures with reasoning. Walk through similar problems together, not the exact same one. If they say \"I don't know how to start,\" ask \"What does the problem ask you to find? What do we already know?\" The hint system in Word Problems gives layered hints — try the first one before the answer."}},{"k":"what_should_i_drill","v":{"s":"What should I drill?"}},{"k":"ies_practice_guide_recommends_1_magnit","v":{"s":"IES Practice Guide recommends: (1) magnitude reasoning (number line work), (2) connections between visual and symbolic, (3) word problems in context. AVOID: drill on procedures without understanding. Spend 5 minutes on Benchmark Trainer, 5 on Word Problems, and 5 on a game — that's a great 15-minute session."}},{"k":"my_child_gets_the_procedure_right_but_","v":{"s":"My child gets the procedure right but the answer wrong"}},{"k":"usually_means_a_small_arithmetic_error","v":{"s":"Usually means a small arithmetic error (e.g., multiplied wrong) or didn't simplify. Show them the Cheat Sheet — they can check their work step by step. Encourage them to verify with a different method (estimate first, or use a different model)."}},{"k":"what_if_i_don_t_remember_fractions_wel","v":{"s":"What if I don't remember fractions well myself?"}},{"k":"you_don_t_have_to_be_the_expert_use_th","v":{"s":"You don't have to be the expert! Use the Tab Guide and Worked Examples — they explain procedures clearly. Better: model \"let's figure this out together.\" You can learn alongside your child. The Vocabulary tab is helpful even for adults."}},{"k":"how_do_i_know_if_my_child_is_on_track","v":{"s":"How do I know if my child is on track?"}},{"k":"look_at_the_standards_tab_to_see_which","v":{"s":"Look at the Standards tab to see which CCSS standards they should know for their grade. The Mastery tab shows progress. For a quick check: can they (a) draw a model for 3/4, (b) say a fraction equivalent to 1/2, (c) compare 2/3 and 3/4 and explain? Those three tests cover most K-5 fraction expectations."}},{"k":"parent_guide","v":{"s":"👨‍👩‍👧 Parent guide"}},{"k":"guidance_for_parents_helping_kids_with","v":{"s":"Guidance for parents helping kids with fractions at home. Common challenges, practical tips, and what to ask."}},{"k":"the_why_of_learning_recruiting_interes","v":{"s":"The \"WHY\" of learning — recruiting interest, sustaining effort, self-regulation"}},{"k":"the_what_of_learning_perception_langua","v":{"s":"The \"WHAT\" of learning — perception, language, comprehension"}},{"k":"the_how_of_learning_physical_action_ex","v":{"s":"The \"HOW\" of learning — physical action, expression, executive function"}},{"k":"udl_alignment_cast_guidelines","v":{"s":"🎨 UDL alignment — CAST guidelines"}},{"k":"every_fraction_lab_feature_mapped_to_a","v":{"s":"Every Fraction Lab feature mapped to a Universal Design for Learning (UDL) guideline from CAST. "}},{"k":"use_this_to_articulate_to_administrato","v":{"s":"Use this to articulate to administrators or grant reviewers how AlloFlow operationalizes UDL."}},{"k":"feature","v":{"s":"Feature"}},{"k":"udl_principle","v":{"s":"UDL principle"}},{"k":"the_foundational_ies_practice_guide_5_","v":{"s":"The foundational IES Practice Guide. 5 recommendations including the central use of the number-line model."}},{"k":"origin_of_the_enactive_concrete_iconic","v":{"s":"Origin of the enactive (concrete) → iconic (representational) → symbolic (abstract) progression that becomes CRA."}},{"k":"cra_in_special_education_context_evide","v":{"s":"CRA in special education context. Evidence for sequencing."}},{"k":"origin_of_the_translation_model_moving","v":{"s":"Origin of the translation model — moving between symbolic, visual, verbal, manipulatives, and real-world contexts."}},{"k":"documents_the_whole_number_bias_miscon","v":{"s":"Documents the \"whole-number bias\" misconception."}},{"k":"maps_how_students_construct_fraction_m","v":{"s":"Maps how students construct fraction magnitude over time."}},{"k":"synthesizes_the_cognitive_challenges_o","v":{"s":"Synthesizes the cognitive challenges of fraction arithmetic."}},{"k":"foundational_text_for_the_number_talk_","v":{"s":"Foundational text for the Number Talk routine."}},{"k":"growth_mindset_applied_to_mathematics_","v":{"s":"Growth mindset applied to mathematics education."}},{"k":"original_cuisenaire_rod_system_that_be","v":{"s":"Original Cuisenaire rod system that became the prototype for fraction strips."}},{"k":"meta_analysis_showing_positive_effects","v":{"s":"Meta-analysis showing positive effects of manipulatives on math achievement."}},{"k":"effects_of_ed_tech_integration_on_math","v":{"s":"Effects of ed-tech integration on math learning."}},{"k":"worked_example_effect_why_showing_solu","v":{"s":"Worked-example effect — why showing solutions can be more effective than practice alone for novices."}},{"k":"research_citations","v":{"s":"📚 Research citations"}},{"k":"the_research_base_for_alloflow_fractio","v":{"s":"The research base for AlloFlow Fraction Lab. Use these citations when justifying tool use to administrators, in IEP documentation, or in grant applications."}},{"k":"practice","v":{"s":"Practice"}},{"k":"use_the_slider_to_change_numerator_and","v":{"s":"Use the slider to change numerator and denominator. The pie/bar updates live."}},{"k":"models","v":{"s":"Models"}},{"k":"toggle_between_pie_and_number_line_to_","v":{"s":"Toggle between pie and number-line to build flexibility."}},{"k":"number_line_4","v":{"s":"Number Line"}},{"k":"plot_multiple_fractions_to_see_their_r","v":{"s":"Plot multiple fractions to see their relative size."}},{"k":"cra_progression","v":{"s":"CRA Progression"}},{"k":"don_t_skip_stages_linger_on_concrete_u","v":{"s":"Don't skip stages. Linger on Concrete until confident."}},{"k":"fraction_wall","v":{"s":"Fraction Wall"}},{"k":"click_two_rows_to_compare_their_height","v":{"s":"Click two rows to compare their heights directly."}},{"k":"vocabulary","v":{"s":"Vocabulary"}},{"k":"use_the_search_to_find_a_specific_term","v":{"s":"Use the search to find a specific term."}},{"k":"worked_examples","v":{"s":"Worked Examples"}},{"k":"don_t_skip_the_explanation_steps_read_","v":{"s":"Don't skip the explanation steps — read each one."}},{"k":"read_aloud_as_class_discussion_prompts","v":{"s":"Read aloud as class discussion prompts."}},{"k":"compare_strategies","v":{"s":"Compare Strategies"}},{"k":"make_this_a_poster","v":{"s":"Make this a poster."}},{"k":"cheat_sheet","v":{"s":"Cheat Sheet"}},{"k":"print_and_laminate","v":{"s":"Print and laminate."}},{"k":"conversion_tables","v":{"s":"Conversion Tables"}},{"k":"notice_the_patterns_5_8_0_625_62_5","v":{"s":"Notice the patterns: 5/8 = 0.625 = 62.5%."}},{"k":"glossary","v":{"s":"Glossary"}},{"k":"di