Amazon River"}},{"k":"second_longest_river_largest_by_water_","v":{"s":"Second longest river, largest by water flow"}},{"k":"novice","v":{"s":"Novice"}},{"k":"explorer","v":{"s":"Explorer"}},{"k":"navigator","v":{"s":"Navigator"}},{"k":"geographer","v":{"s":"Geographer"}},{"k":"globetrotter","v":{"s":"Globetrotter"}},{"k":"master_cartographer","v":{"s":"Master Cartographer"}},{"k":"explorer_2","v":{"s":"Explorer"}},{"k":"answer_10_questions","v":{"s":"Answer 10 questions"}},{"k":"on_fire","v":{"s":"On Fire"}},{"k":"5x_streak","v":{"s":"5x streak"}},{"k":"century","v":{"s":"Century"}},{"k":"reach_100_points","v":{"s":"Reach 100 points"}},{"k":"distance_pro","v":{"s":"Distance Pro"}},{"k":"nail_5_distance_challenges","v":{"s":"Nail 5 distance challenges"}},{"k":"globetrotter_2","v":{"s":"Globetrotter"}},{"k":"answer_25_questions","v":{"s":"Answer 25 questions"}},{"k":"lightning","v":{"s":"Lightning"}},{"k":"10x_streak","v":{"s":"10x streak"}},{"k":"find_country","v":{"s":"Find Country"}},{"k":"capitals","v":{"s":"Capitals"}},{"k":"continents","v":{"s":"Continents"}},{"k":"landmarks","v":{"s":"Landmarks"}},{"k":"size_compare","v":{"s":"Size Compare"}},{"k":"globe_view","v":{"s":"Globe View"}},{"k":"quiz_builder","v":{"s":"Quiz Builder"}},{"k":"distance","v":{"s":"Distance"}},{"k":"distance_slider","v":{"s":"Distance Slider"}},{"k":"geography_quiz","v":{"s":"Geography Quiz"}},{"k":"smaller_regions_easier_quiz_start_smal","v":{"s":"Smaller regions = easier quiz. Start small, expand as you improve."}},{"k":"easy","v":{"s":"Easy"}},{"k":"medium","v":{"s":"Medium"}},{"k":"hard","v":{"s":"Hard"}},{"k":"find_country_the_visual_atlas","v":{"s":"Find Country — the visual atlas"}},{"k":"195_sovereign_nations_recognized_by_th","v":{"s":"195 sovereign nations recognized by the UN. Mercator projection distorts size near the poles — Greenland looks the size of Africa but is 14× smaller. Equal-area projections (Goode, Robinson) trade angle accuracy for honest area."}},{"k":"capitals_govt_seats_cultural_anchors","v":{"s":"Capitals — govt seats + cultural anchors"}},{"k":"most_capitals_also_house_head_of_state","v":{"s":"Most capitals also house head-of-state, supreme court, parliament. South Africa has 3 (Pretoria executive, Cape Town legislative, Bloemfontein judicial). Bolivia, Tanzania, Switzerland, Honduras, Eswatini also split."}},{"k":"continents_7_or_5_depending_who_you_as","v":{"s":"Continents — 7 (or 5, depending who you ask)"}},{"k":"7_continent_model_us_uk_africa_antarct","v":{"s":"7-continent model (US/UK): Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Australia, Europe, N. America, S. America. Many countries teach 6 (combining N+S America) or 5 (combining Europe+Asia into Eurasia). Russia + Turkey straddle two."}},{"k":"landmarks_the_visual_mnemonics","v":{"s":"Landmarks — the visual mnemonics"}},{"k":"eiffel_paris_christ_the_redeemer_rio_s","v":{"s":"Eiffel (Paris), Christ the Redeemer (Rio), Sydney Opera House, Petra (Jordan), Burj Khalifa (Dubai). Cultural anchoring: when students learn the building, the country sticks 10× better."}},{"k":"size_compare_fight_mercator_distortion","v":{"s":"Size Compare — fight Mercator distortion"}},{"k":"russia_is_17m_km_largest_usa_china_ind","v":{"s":"Russia is 17M km² (largest). USA + China + India fit inside Russia with room to spare. Africa is 30M km² — fits USA + China + India + Mexico + Western Europe combined. Maps lie about scale."}},{"k":"globe_view_honest_spherical_geometry","v":{"s":"Globe View — honest spherical geometry"}},{"k":"earth_is_an_oblate_spheroid_21_km_wide","v":{"s":"Earth is an oblate spheroid — 21 km wider at the equator than pole-to-pole. The shortest path between two cities is a great-circle arc, not a straight line on a flat map. Why flights bend over the Arctic."}},{"k":"quiz_builder_graded_geography_practice","v":{"s":"Quiz Builder — graded geography practice"}},{"k":"mix_country_capital_continent_landmark","v":{"s":"Mix country / capital / continent / landmark items at chosen difficulty. Spaced retrieval beats cramming for long-term recall (Karpicke 2008). NCSS curriculum standards aligned through grade 8."}},{"k":"distance_great_circle_math","v":{"s":"Distance — great-circle math"}},{"k":"haversine_formula_gives_the_great_circ","v":{"s":"Haversine formula gives the great-circle distance between two lat/lng pairs. NYC to Tokyo ≈ 10,840 km going north over the pole — shorter than the flat-map straight line. Pilot routes prove it daily."}},{"k":"click_on_the_map_to_find","v":{"s":"Click on the map to find:"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"♻ Reset"}},{"k":"what_is_the_capital_of","v":{"s":"What is the capital of:"}},{"k":"type_the_capital_city","v":{"s":"Type the capital city..."}},{"k":"capital_city_answer","v":{"s":"Capital city answer"}},{"k":"check","v":{"s":"Check"}},{"k":"sort_countries_by_continent","v":{"s":"🌍 Sort Countries by Continent"}},{"k":"which_continent_is","v":{"s":"Which continent is"}},{"k":"famous_landmarks","v":{"s":"🏔️ Famous Landmarks"}},{"k":"which_country_is_this_in","v":{"s":"Which country is this in?"}},{"k":"previous","v":{"s":"◀ Previous"}},{"k":"next","v":{"s":"Next ▶"}},{"k":"which_country_is_bigger","v":{"s":"📏 Which Country is Bigger?"}},{"k":"click_if_bigger","v":{"s":"Click if bigger"}},{"k":"mercator_maps_distort_sizes_countries_","v":{"s":"💡 Mercator maps distort sizes — countries near the equator look smaller than they really are!"}},{"k":"drag_to_rotate_scroll_to_zoom_click_co","v":{"s":"🌐 Drag to rotate • Scroll to zoom • Click countries for info"}},{"k":"loading_3d_globe","v":{"s":"Loading 3D Globe..."}},{"k":"not_in_the_117_country_dataset_basic_i","v":{"s":"Not in the 117-country dataset — basic info only."}},{"k":"close_country_info","v":{"s":"Close country info"}},{"k":"click_any_country_on_the_globe_to_see_","v":{"s":"Click any country on the globe to see its info here."}},{"k":"ai_quiz_builder","v":{"s":"🏆 AI Quiz Builder"}},{"k":"describe_the_quiz_you_want_and_ai_will","v":{"s":"Describe the quiz you want 