","v":{"s":"of the max"}},{"k":"puzzle_win","v":{"s":"🏆 Optimal! A cube is the fattest solid for a given surface area."}},{"k":"puzzle_hint","v":{"s":"Try a cube: surface 6s² ≤ 54 means s ≤ 3, so a 3×3×3 cube (volume 27) is unbeatable."}},{"k":"net_unfold","v":{"s":"📦 Unfold net"}},{"k":"hide","v":{"s":"Hide"}},{"k":"show","v":{"s":"Show"}},{"k":"net_oblique","v":{"s":"Turn off Oblique to unfold this prism — a slanted prism has non-rectangular flaps."}},{"k":"printable_prism_net","v":{"s":"Printable prism net"}},{"k":"net_faces","v":{"s":"6 faces · edges {a}×{b}×{c}"}},{"k":"net_popup","v":{"s":"Allow pop-ups to print the net."}},{"k":"net_title","v":{"s":"Prism net"}},{"k":"net_print","v":{"s":"Print / cut-out net"}},{"k":"scale_explorer","v":{"s":"🔎 Scale explorer — square–cube law"}},{"k":"scale_factor","v":{"s":"Scale factor k"}},{"k":"square_cube_note","v":{"s":"Double the sides and the volume grows 8×, not 2× — why big animals need thick legs and small ones do not."}},{"k":"place_scaled_copy","v":{"s":"Place a scaled copy beside the original"}},{"k":"place_scaled","v":{"s":"Place ×{k} copy"}},{"k":"cross_section","v":{"s":"🍰 Cross-section slicer"}},{"k":"slicing_on","v":{"s":"Slicing ✓"}},{"k":"slice_show","v":{"s":"Show slice"}},{"k":"slice_height","v":{"s":"Slice height"}},{"k":"cross_area","v":{"s":"Cross-section area"}},{"k":"cross_constant","v":{"s":"Same at every height — that is why volume = area × height (Cavalieri)."}},{"k":"stack_slices","v":{"s":"Stack of {n} slices"}},{"k":"slice_count","v":{"s":"Number of slices in the stack"}},{"k":"stack_note","v":{"s":"More slices → the stack of areas adds up to the true volume."}},{"k":"analyzer_plot_aria","v":{"s":"Top-down plot of construction objects around their centroid"}},{"k":"view_angle_aria","v":{"s":"Analyzer view angle"}},{"k":"detail_decimals_aria","v":{"s":"Decimal places shown in the analyzer metrics"}},{"k":"your_hypothesis","v":{"s":"Your geometry scaling hypothesis"}},{"k":"scaling_explanation","v":{"s":"Explain geometry scaling in your own words"}},{"k":"torus_radius_constraint","v":{"s":"Tube radius stays smaller than the major radius so the torus does not self-intersect."}},{"k":"choose_shape_color","v":{"s":"Choose shape color"}},{"k":"scene_labels","v":{"s":"Scene labels"}},{"k":"construction_name","v":{"s":"Construction name"}},{"k":"save_named_construction","v":{"s":"Save construction"}},{"k":"delete_saved_construction","v":{"s":"Delete saved construction"}},{"k":"confirm_delete","v":{"s":"Confirm deletion"}},{"k":"delete_saved_prompt","v":{"s":"Delete this saved construction?"}},{"k":"hide_math","v":{"s":"🧮 Hide the math"}},{"k":"show_math","v":{"s":"🧮 Show the math"}},{"k":"xs_intro","v":{"s":"Slide the cut up and down. A solid is a stack of these slices — that is why volume = cross-section area × height."}},{"k":"cut_height","v":{"s":"Cut height"}},{"k":"cut_height_aria","v":{"s":"Cross-section cut height"}},{"k":"xs_area","v":{"s":"area"}},{"k":"conic_sections","v":{"s":"🍦 Conic sections (tilt the cut)"}},{"k":"tilt","v":{"s":"Tilt"}},{"k":"conic_tilt_aria","v":{"s":"Conic section cutting-plane tilt"}},{"k":"unfold_net_single","v":{"s":"📦 Unfold net"}},{"k":"shape_net_details","v":{"s":"Shape net details"}},{"k":"faces_sum","v":{"s":"Σ pieces"}},{"k":"real_world_size","v":{"s":"Real-world size"}},{"k":"if_one_unit","v":{"s":"1 unit = 10 cm"}},{"k":"cups","v":{"s":"cups"}},{"k":"toggle_fullscreen","v":{"s":"Toggle fullscreen"}},{"k":"fullscreen","v":{"s":"Fullscreen"}},{"k":"touch_controls_hint","v":{"s":"Drag: rotate • Pinch: zoom • Two fingers: pan"}},{"k":"shortcut_focus_note","v":{"s":"(these act while the sandbox has focus)"}},{"k":"challenge_result","v":{"s":"Challenge result"}},{"k":"open_immersive_fallback","v":{"s":"Pop-ups are blocked, so the Immersive Geometry Lab is opening in this tab. Use Back to return."}},{"k":"workbench_whole","v":{"s":"Whole sculpture"}},{"k":"workbench_redo","v":{"s":"Redo"}},{"k":"workbench_title","v":{"s":"