ble region — the foundation of linear programming."}},{"k":"aria_expression_input","v":{"s":"Inequality expression input"}},{"k":"aria_number_line_graph","v":{"s":"Number line inequality graph"}},{"k":"legend_closed","v":{"s":"Closed (≤ ≥) includes the value"}},{"k":"legend_open","v":{"s":"Open (< >) excludes the value"}},{"k":"shift_range_left","v":{"s":"Shift range left"}},{"k":"zoom_out","v":{"s":"Zoom out"}},{"k":"zoom","v":{"s":"Zoom"}},{"k":"zoom_in","v":{"s":"Zoom in"}},{"k":"shift_range_right","v":{"s":"Shift range right"}},{"k":"reset_range","v":{"s":"Reset range"}},{"k":"test_included","v":{"s":"x INCLUDED in solution (coef·x < bound)"}},{"k":"test_excluded","v":{"s":"x EXCLUDED (coef·x > bound)"}},{"k":"test_boundary","v":{"s":"AT boundary (coef·x ≈ bound)"}},{"k":"test_discovery_title","v":{"s":"Inequality test discovery"}},{"k":"test_discovery_desc","v":{"s":"Sliders for x, coefficient, bound. Test whether coef·x < bound. 3 discrete states. No score, no reveal."}},{"k":"log","v":{"s":"Log"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"Reset"}},{"k":"hypothesis_placeholder","v":{"s":"Hypothesis: When does a negative coefficient flip the inequality?"}},{"k":"hypothesis","v":{"s":"Inequality relationship hypothesis"}},{"k":"stuck_show_prompts","v":{"s":"Stuck — show open prompts"}},{"k":"prompt_test_x5","v":{"s":"Test x = 5 with coef = -2 and bound = 5. What happens?"}},{"k":"prompt_why_flip","v":{"s":"Why does multiplying by negative flip < to >?"}},{"k":"understand_explain","v":{"s":"I understand — explain in own words"}},{"k":"explain_placeholder","v":{"s":"Explain inequality test logic."}},{"k":"explanation","v":{"s":"Explain inequality test logic"}},{"k":"design_note_test","v":{"s":"Design note: discrete 3-state test marker; no answer reveal — by design."}},{"k":"interval_notation","v":{"s":"Interval Notation"}},{"k":"set_builder_notation","v":{"s":"Set-Builder Notation"}},{"k":"test_a_value","v":{"s":"Test a Value"}},{"k":"enter_a_number","v":{"s":"Enter a number…"}},{"k