","v":{"s":"At the boundary: excluded because the inequality is strict (<)."}},{"k":"test_discovery_reasoning","v":{"s":"Change x, the coefficient, or the bound. Substitute the value, then decide whether the strict inequality is true."}},{"k":"strict_boundary_note","v":{"s":"Equality does not satisfy <. A boundary point belongs only when the inequality includes equality."}}],"id":539}},{"k":"kitchenlab","v":{"o":[{"k":"sr_handwash_complete_20_seconds_reached","v":{"s":"Handwash complete — 20 seconds reached."}},{"k":"sr_handwash_timer_reset","v":{"s":"Handwash timer reset."}},{"k":"sr_pasta_pot_turned_on_water_will_boil_in_about_3_mi","v":{"s":"Pasta pot turned on. A big pot takes about six minutes to boil."}},{"k":"sr_pasta_dropped_into_boiling_water_about_9_minutes","v":{"s":"Pasta dropped into boiling water. About 9 minutes to al dente."}},{"k":"sr_cooking_paused_recipe_and_competition_timers_are","v":{"s":"Cooking paused. Recipe and competition timers are stopped."}},{"k":"sr_cooking_resumed","v":{"s":"Cooking resumed."}},{"k":"sr_recipe_abandoned","v":{"s":"Recipe abandoned."}},{"k":"sr_tournament_started_3_rounds_escalating_difficulty","v":{"s":"Tournament started. 3 rounds, escalating difficulty."}},{"k":"sr_pan_in_range_step_complete","v":{"s":"Pan in range — step complete."}},{"k":"sr_heat_removed_carryover_cooking_begins","v":{"s":"Heat removed — carryover cooking begins."}},{"k":"sr_step_complete","v":{"s":"Step complete."}},{"k":"a11y_handwash_timer_progress","v":{"s":"Handwash timer progress"}},{"k":"a11y_maillard_reaction_hypothesis","v":{"s":"Maillard reaction hypothesis"}},{"k":"a11y_explain_the_chemistry_of_maillard_browning","v":{"s":"Explain the chemistry of Maillard browning"}},{"k":"safety","v":{"s":"Safety"}},{"k":"knife_lab","v":{"s":"Knife Lab"}},{"k":"heat_technique","v":{"s":"Heat & Technique"}},{"k":"maillard","v":{"s":"Maillard"}},{"k":"recipe_sim","v":{"s":"Recipe Sim"}},{"k":"resources","v":{"s":"Resources"}},{"k":"kitchen_lab","v":{"s":"Kitchen Lab"}},{"k":"cooking_life_skills_culinary_science_f","v":{"s":"Cooking life skills + culinary science. Food safety, knife technique, heat methods, Maillard chemistry, recipes, glossary. Built for life skills classrooms + family + consumer science."}},{"k":"safety_2","v":{"s":"Safety"}},{"k":"knife_lab_2","v":{"s":"Knife Lab"}},{"k":"heat_technique_2","v":{"s":"Heat & Technique"}},{"k":"maillard_2","v":{"s":"Maillard"}},{"k":"recipe_sim_2","v":{"s":"Recipe Sim"}},{"k":"resources_2","v":{"s":"Resources"}},{"k":"browning_lab","v":{"s":"Browning Lab"}},{"k":"kitchen_lab_sections","v":{"s":"Kitchen Lab sections"}},{"k":"the_danger_zone_fda_food_code","v":{"s":"🌡️ The Danger Zone (FDA Food Code)"}},{"k":"bacteria_grow_fastest_between_40_f_and","v":{"s":"Bacteria grow fastest between 40°F and 140°F (4°C–60°C). This is \"the danger zone.\" Food shouldn't sit here for more than 2 hours total (1 hour if it's over 90°F outside). Drag the slider to see what happens at different temps."}},{"k":"food_temperature","v":{"s":"Food temperature"}},{"k":"food_temperature_in_fahrenheit","v":{"s":"Food temperature in Fahrenheit"}},{"k":"after_2_hours_at_this_temp","v":{"s":"After 2 hours at this temp"}},{"k":"starting_bacterial_population","v":{"s":"starting bacterial population"}},{"k":"usda_safe_cooking_temperatures","v":{"s":"🔥 USDA Safe Cooking Temperatures"}},{"k":"these_are_the_minimum_internal_tempera","v":{"s":"These are the minimum internal temperatures. A meat thermometer is the only way to know for sure. Color is unreliable — pink chicken at 165°F is safe; brown chicken at 140°F is not."}},{"k":"pitfall","v":{"s":"⚠️ Pitfall: "}},{"k":"cross_contamination_rules","v":{"s":"🚫 Cross-Contamination Rules"}},{"k":"pathogens_move_from_raw_meat_hands_cut","v":{"s":"Pathogens move from raw meat → hands → cutting board → ready-to-eat food. The fixes are simple but easy to forget mid-cook."}},{"k":"red_board_for_raw_meat_green_for_produ","v":{"s":"Red board for raw meat, green for produce. Many home kitchens skip this — it's the #1 home-kitchen cross-contamination source."}},{"k":"20_seconds_with_soap_hot_water_the_20_","v":{"s":"20 seconds with soap + hot water. The 20 seconds is what dislodges the bacteria — soap alone doesn't."}},{"k":"surface_thaws_fast_bacteria_multiply_o","v":{"s":"Surface thaws fast → bacteria multiply on the outside while inside is still frozen. Fridge keeps the whole thing under 40°F."}},{"k":"marinade_that_touched_raw_meat_contain","v":{"s":"Marinade that touched raw meat contains those pathogens. Boil it 1 min before using as a finishing sauce, or make extra separately."}},{"k":"damp_kitchen_sponges_harbor_more_bacte","v":{"s":"Damp kitchen sponges harbor more bacteria per square cm than the toilet seat. Microwaving wet for 90 seconds sanitizes most of it."}},{"k":"cooked_food_in_danger_zone_40_140_f_in","v":{"s":"Cooked food in danger zone (40-140°F) → into fridge within 2 hours (1 hour if room is 90°F+)."}},{"k":"the_top_9_allergens_fda_faster_act","v":{"s":"⚠️ The Top 9 Allergens (FDA + FASTER Act)"}},{"k":"these_9_cause_90_of_all_severe_food_al","v":{"s":"These 9 cause ~90% of all severe food allergic reactions in the US. Sesame was added in 2023. By law, packaged food must declare these. The \"hidden in\" column matters most — that's where surprises happen."}},{"k":"hidden_in","v":{"s":"🕵️ Hidden in: "}},{"k":"20_second_handwash_cdc_who","v":{"s":"🧼 20-Second Handwash (CDC + WHO)"}},{"k":"soap_20_seconds_friction_the_minimum_f","v":{"s":"Soap + 20 seconds + friction = the minimum for hand sanitation in a kitchen. The mechanical action (friction) is what dislodges bacteria — soap loosens them, water rinses them away."}},{"k":"pick_a_cut_to_learn","v":{"s":"Pick a cut to learn"}},{"k":"why_uniformity_matters","v":{"s":"🎯 Why Uniformity Matters"}},{"k":"when_pieces_are_different_sizes_they_f","v":{"s":"When pieces are different sizes, they finish cooking at different times. Small pieces burn while large pieces are still raw. Uniform cuts = uniform cook = no kitchen guessing."}},{"k":"uneven_cuts","v":{"s":"❌ Uneven cuts"}},{"k":"small_pieces_blacken_at_6_min_while_la","v":{"s":"Small pieces blacken at 6 min while large pieces are still raw inside at 12 min. You either eat charcoal + crunchy, or you cook so long the small pieces are inedible."}},{"k":"uniform_cuts","v":{"s":"✅ Uniform cuts"}},{"k":"every_piece_reaches_doneness_at_the_sa","v":{"s":"Every piece reaches doneness at the same moment. You can leave the pan and trust the clock. This is why professional kitchens drill knife skills before anything else."}},{"k":"the_claw_grip_finger_safety","v":{"s":"✋ The Claw Grip (Finger Safety)"}},{"k":"curl_your_guiding_fingers_inward_so_yo","v":{"s":"Curl your guiding fingers INWARD so your knuckles face the blade, not your fingertips. The flat of the blade slides along your knuckles as a guide. If the knife slips, it slides up your knuckle wall — not into your fingertip."}},{"k":"pan_is_at_the_right_temp_for_this_tech","v":{"s":"Pan is at the right temp for this technique. Food browns + cooks evenly."}},{"k":"too_cold","v":{"s":"🥶 Too cold"}},{"k":"below_threshold_food_will_steam_in_its","v":{"s":"Below threshold — food will steam in its own juices instead of browning. No Maillard. Gray + soggy."}},{"k":"hot_but_tolerable","v":{"s":"🔥 Hot but tolerable"}},{"k":"workable_for_fast_cooks_but_easy_to_bu","v":{"s":"Workable for fast cooks but easy to burn. Watch carefully."}},{"k":"smoking_risky","v":{"s":"☠️ Smoking + risky"}},{"k":"past_the_smoke_point_of_most_cooking_o","v":{"s":"Past the smoke point of most cooking oils. Acrolein-forming, bitter flavors, fire risk. Reduce heat or change oil to one with higher smoke point (avocado, refined peanut, ghee)."}},{"k":"pick_a_technique","v":{"s":"Pick a technique"}},{"k":"your_pan_temperature","v":{"s":"Your pan temperature"}},{"k":"pan_temperature_in_fahrenheit","v":{"s":"Pan temperature in Fahrenheit"}},{"k":"coming_in_the_next_ship","v":{"s":"🚧 Coming in the next ship"}},{"k":"this_section_is_being_built_below_is_w","v":{"s":"This section is being built. Below is what's planned. The architecture pieces are in place — content depth is what's in flight."}},{"k":"what_s_actually_happening","v":{"s":"🔬 What's actually happening"}},{"k":"maillard_is_a_cascade_of_chemical_reac","v":{"s":"Maillard is a cascade of chemical reactions between "}},{"k":"amino_acids","v":{"s":"amino acids"}},{"k":"the_building_blocks_of_protein_and","v":{"s":" (the building blocks of protein) and "}},{"k":"reducing_sugars","v":{"s":"reducing sugars"}},{"k":"glucose_fructose_lactose_sugars_that_c","v":{"s":" (glucose, fructose, lactose — sugars that can give up an electron). It needs heat to start (~280°F / 140°C surface temp), and once running it produces:"}},{"k":"melanoidins","v":{"s":"Melanoidins"}},{"k":"the_brown_pigments_why_crust_is_brown","v":{"s":" — the brown pigments. Why crust is brown."}},{"k":"1000_volatile_aroma_compounds","v":{"s":"1000+ volatile aroma compounds"}},{"k":"pyrazines_nutty_roasty_furans_sweet_ca","v":{"s":" — pyrazines (nutty/roasty), furans (sweet/caramel), thiophenes (meaty/sulfury). These don't exist in raw food at all."}},{"k":"complex_flavor","v":{"s":"Complex flavor"}},{"k":"maillard_is_why_seared_beef_tastes_lik","v":{"s":" — Maillard is why seared beef tastes like more than the sum of \"raw beef + salt.\" You're eating compounds that didn't exist 30 seconds earlier."}},{"k":"temperature_explorer","v":{"s":"🌡️ Temperature Explorer"}},{"k":"drag_the_slider_to_see_what_s_happenin","v":{"s":"Drag the slider to see what's happening at different surface temperatures. Note: "}},{"k":"surface_temp_internal_temp","v":{"s":"surface temp ≠ internal temp"}},{"k":"pan_temp_surface_temp_can_be_much_high","v":{"s":" ≠ pan temp. Surface temp can be much higher than internal because the surface is touching the hot pan or air."}},{"k":"food_surface_temperature","v":{"s":"Food surface temperature"}},{"k":"food_surface_temperature_in_fahrenheit","v":{"s":"Food surface temperature in Fahrenheit"}},{"k":"visual_color","v":{"s":"visual color"}},{"k":"science","v":{"s":"⚗️ Science"}},{"k":"all_six_zones_at_a_glance","v":{"s":"📊 All six zones at a glance"}},{"k":"caramelization_vs_maillard","v":{"s":"🆚 Caramelization vs Maillard"}},{"k":"often_confused_they_re_different_react","v":{"s":"Often confused — they're different reactions. Caramelization is sugar alone breaking down. Maillard needs amino acids + reducing sugars together. Most \"browning\" you see is Maillard, even when called \"caramelizing.\""}},{"k":"aspect","v":{"s":"Aspect"}},{"k":"caramelization","v":{"s":"Caramelization"}},{"k":"maillard_3","v":{"s":"Maillard"}},{"k":"browning_in_the_wild","v":{"s":"🍽️ Browning in the wild"}},{"k":"same_chemistry_different_foods_each_ca","v":{"s":"Same chemistry, different foods. Each carries its own characteristic flavor profile because amino acid + reducing sugar mixes differ."}},{"k":"ph_effects_on_maillard","v":{"s":"⚗️ pH effects on Maillard"}},{"k":"the_acidity_of_your_food_dramatically_","v":{"s":"The acidity of your food dramatically changes how fast Maillard runs. This is one of the most underused kitchen \"cheat codes.\""}},{"k":"use","v":{"s":"💡 Use: "}},{"k":"the_dark_side_acrylamide","v":{"s":"☠️ The dark side: acrylamide"}},{"k":"above_250_f_120_c_starchy_foods_the_am","v":{"s":"Above ~250°F (120°C), starchy foods + the amino acid "}},{"k":"react_to_form","v":{"s":" react to form "}},{"k":"classified_by_iarc_as_a","v":{"s":" — classified by IARC as a "}},{"k":"probable_human_carcinogen","v":{"s":"probable human carcinogen"}},{"k":"group_2a_it_s_the_same_compound_used_i","v":{"s":" (Group 2A). It's the same compound used in some industrial polymer manufacturing."}},{"k":"foods_most_affected_french_fries_potat","v":{"s":"Foods most affected: french fries, potato chips, breakfast cereal, toast (especially dark), coffee, baked goods. The darker the brown, the more acrylamide. The FDA campaign tagline:"}},{"k":"go_for_gold_not_brown","v":{"s":"\"Go for gold, not brown.\""}},{"k":"practical_advice_aim_for_golden_yellow","v":{"s":"Practical advice: aim for golden-yellow on starchy foods, not deep brown. Don't store potatoes in the fridge (cold storage raises their reducing-sugar content → more acrylamide when cooked)."}},{"k":"gold","v":{"s":"Gold"}},{"k":"master_chef_tier_extraordinary_command","v":{"s":"Master chef tier — extraordinary command of heat, timing, and constraint."}},{"k":"silver","v":{"s":"Silver"}},{"k":"real_cook_confident_across_heat_ranges","v":{"s":"Real cook. Confident across heat ranges + constraints."}},{"k":"bronze","v":{"s":"Bronze"}},{"k":"solid_home_cook_some_constraints_still","v":{"s":"Solid home cook. Some constraints still tripping you up."}},{"k":"honorable_mention","v":{"s":"Honorable Mention"}},{"k":"you_made_it_through_tournament_punishe","v":{"s":"You made it through. Tournament punishes mistakes — that's the point."}},{"k":"new_personal_best","v":{"s":"🌟 New personal best!"}},{"k":"round_by_round","v":{"s":"📋 Round-by-round"}},{"k":"new_tournament","v":{"s":"🏅 New tournament"}},{"k":"back_to_recipe_list","v":{"s":"🍽️ Back to recipe list"}},{"k":"what_should_i_cook_tonight","v":{"s":"What should I cook tonight?"}},{"k":"tell_the_ai_what_you_have_how_much_tim","v":{"s":"Tell the AI what you have, how much time, or who you're feeding — it picks the right recipe from your unlocked list + explains why."}},{"k":"ask_the_ai_chef","v":{"s":"💡 Ask the AI chef"}},{"k":"competition_mode","v":{"s":"Competition Mode"}},{"k":"chopped_style_challenge_random_recipe_","v":{"s":"Chopped-style challenge. Random recipe + 2 mystery constraints (time pressure, heat caps, ingredient discipline, restaurant-grade standard, and more). Combine recipe skill + constraint mastery for a score up to 150. Beat your personal best."}},{"k":"start_a_random_challenge","v":{"s":"🎲 Start a random challenge"}},{"k":"tournament_mode_3_rounds","v":{"s":"Tournament Mode (3 rounds)"}},{"k":"round_1_1_constraint_full_time_round_2","v":{"s":"Round 1: 1 constraint, full time. Round 2: 2 constraints, 80% time. Round 3: 3 constraints (Restaurant Standard + Speed Demon forced), 60% time. Compete for cumulative score across 450 points."}},{"k":"start_tournament","v":{"s":"🏅 Start tournament"}},{"k":"your_personal_bests","v":{"s":"🥇 Your personal bests"}},{"k":"achievements","v":{"s":"🏆 Achievements"}},{"k":"tutorial_mode_recipes_mastered","v":{"s":"📖 Tutorial mode — recipes mastered"}},{"k":"recipes_mastered","v":{"s":"recipes mastered"}},{"k":"tutorial_mode_is_the_unhurried_run_no_","v":{"s":"Tutorial mode is the unhurried run — no time pressure, no constraints. Use it to learn each recipe before taking it into competition. v0.5 adds Competition Mode + personal bests. v0.6 will unlock multi-pot recipes (Pasta + Pan Sauce, Sheet-Pan, Roast Chicken)."}},{"k":"mastered","v":{"s":"✓ Mastered"}},{"k":"locked","v":{"s":"🔒 Locked"}},{"k":"unlocks_in_a_future_ship","v":{"s":"Unlocks in a future ship"}},{"k":"competition","v":{"s":"🏆 Competition"}},{"k":"time_left","v":{"s":"time left"}},{"k":"what_s_happening","v":{"s":"🧠 What's happening: "}},{"k":"pan_temperature","v":{"s":"Pan temperature"}},{"k":"food_in_pan","v":{"s":"Food in pan"}},{"k":"0_off","v":{"s":"0 OFF"}},{"k":"10_max","v":{"s":"10 MAX"}},{"k":"ingredients_tray","v":{"s":"🧺 Ingredients tray"}},{"k":"all_ingredients_are_in_the_pan","v":{"s":"All ingredients are in the pan."}},{"k":"continue_to_next_step","v":{"s":"✓ Continue to next step"}},{"k":"abandon","v":{"s":"✕ Abandon"}},{"k":"ai_recipe_suggester","v":{"s":"AI recipe suggester"}},{"k":"what_should_i_cook","v":{"s":"What should I cook?"}},{"k":"powered_by_ai_picks_from_your_unlocked","v":{"s":"Powered by AI · picks from your unlocked recipes"}},{"k":"close_suggester","v":{"s":"Close suggester"}},{"k":"chef_s_pick","v":{"s":"💡 Chef's pick"}},{"k":"cook_this","v":{"s":"🍳 Cook this"}},{