Voice / music AI"}},{"k":"can_clone_voices_from_a_few_seconds_of","v":{"s":"Can clone voices from a few seconds of recording. Consent and deepfake risks apply."}},{"k":"video_generators","v":{"s":"🎬 Video generators"}},{"k":"newer_and_even_more_convincing_than_de","v":{"s":"Newer and even more convincing than deepfakes used to be. Assume any short clip could be synthetic."}},{"k":"the_core_literacy_skills_check_sources","v":{"s":"The core literacy skills — check sources, notice when tone doesn't match certainty, treat output as draft not truth — transfer across all of these."}},{"k":"about_this_lab","v":{"s":"About this lab: "}},{"k":"written_by_a_clinician_psyd_with_stude","v":{"s":"Written by a clinician (PsyD) with students who have executive-function, attention, and learning differences in mind. The rubric in Section 5 is the part most AI-literacy curricula miss — it is also the most important."}},{"k":"you_write_text","v":{"s":"You write text"}},{"k":"your_prompt_or_the_model_s_own_previou","v":{"s":"Your prompt or the model's own previous output."}},{"k":"tokenize","v":{"s":"Tokenize"}},{"k":"split_text_into_small_pieces_tokens_wo","v":{"s":"Split text into small pieces (tokens). Words, sub-words, punctuation."}},{"k":"score_every_next_token","v":{"s":"Score every next token"}},{"k":"assign_a_probability_to_every_possible","v":{"s":"Assign a probability to every possible next token."}},{"k":"sample_one","v":{"s":"Sample one"}},{"k":"temperature_picks_how_random_the_choic","v":{"s":"Temperature picks how random the choice is (see the playground below)."}},{"k":"append_repeat","v":{"s":"Append, repeat"}},{"k":"add_the_new_token_feed_it_back_in_do_t","v":{"s":"Add the new token. Feed it back in. Do this hundreds of times."}},{"k":"the_generation_loop","v":{"s":"🔁 The generation loop"}},{"k":"everything_an_llm_does_is_a_loop_of_th","v":{"s":"Everything an LLM does is a loop of these 5 steps. Not \"thinking\" — pattern matching on tokens, over and over."}},{"k":"loops_back","v":{"s":"Loops back: "}},{"k":"the_newly_sampled_token_becomes_part_o","v":{"s":"The newly sampled token becomes part of the input for the next step. One sentence of AI output is hundreds of these loops."}},{"k":"generation_loop","v":{"s":"Generation loop"}},{"k":"tokenization","v":{"s":"Tokenization"}},{"k":"temperature","v":{"s":"Temperature"}},{"k":"playground","v":{"s":"Playground"}},{"k":"tokens","v":{"s":"Tokens"}},{"k":"text_sub_word_ids","v":{"s":"Text → sub-word IDs"}},{"k":"embeddings","v":{"s":"Embeddings"}},{"k":"ids_high_d_vectors","v":{"s":"IDs → high-D vectors"}},{"k":"context_window","v":{"s":"Context window"}},{"k":"n_tokens_visible_at_once","v":{"s":"N tokens visible at once"}},{"k":"probabilities_over_vocab","v":{"s":"Probabilities over vocab"}},{"k":"temperature_2","v":{"s":"Temperature"}},{"k":"how_far_from_the_top_pick","v":{"s":"How far from the top pick"}},{"k":"sample_repeat","v":{"s":"Sample + repeat"}},{"k":"append_loop_until_stop","v":{"s":"Append → loop until stop"}},{"k":"the_full_pipeline_at_a_glance","v":{"s":"🛤 The full pipeline at a glance"}},{"k":"each_block_below_explores_one_of_these","v":{"s":"Each block below explores one of these stages. Click any chip to jump straight to it."}},{"k":"an_llm_never_sees_words_it_sees","v":{"s":"An LLM never sees \"words\" — it sees "}},{"k":"which_are_pieces_of_words_type_a_sente","v":{"s":", which are pieces of words. Type a sentence and watch it split."}},{"k":"text_to_tokenize","v":{"s":"Text to tokenize"}},{"k":"english","v":{"s":"English"}},{"k":"the_dog_was_running_quickly_because_it","v":{"s":"The dog was running quickly because it was unhappy."}},{"k":"code","v":{"s":"Code"}},{"k":"function_hello_name_return_hi_name","v":{"s":"function hello(name) {\n  return \"Hi, \" + name + \"!\";\n}"}},{"k":"emoji","v":{"s":"Emoji"}},{"k":"i_had_pizza_and_ice_cream_at_the_park_","v":{"s":"I had pizza 🍕 and ice cream 🍨 at the park 🏞️ today!"}},{"k":"unusual_words","v":{"s":"Unusual words"}},{"k":"the_paleontologist_misidentified_the_p","v":{"s":"The paleontologist misidentified the pseudoscorpion as an arthropod."}},{"k":"type_something_above","v":{"s":"(type something above)"}},{"k":"word","v":{"s":"🟦 word"}},{"k":"subword","v":{"s":"🟪 subword"}},{"k":"punctuation","v":{"s":"🟨 punctuation"}},{"k":"space","v":{"s":"⬜ space"}},{"k":"why_this_matters","v":{"s":"Why this matters: "}},{"k":"the_model_predicts_the_next_token_not_","v":{"s":"The model predicts the next TOKEN, not the next word. Short common words become one token; longer words often split (e.g. \"unhappy\" → \"un\" + \"happy\"). This is also how billing works — API costs are per token, not per word."}},{"k":"all_the_llm_is_really_doing_guessing_w","v":{"s":"All the LLM is really doing: guessing what token comes next. Given the same context, it has a PROBABILITY for every possible next token."}},{"k":"controls_how_random_the_next_token_cho","v":{"s":" controls how RANDOM the next-token choice is. Low (0.2) = pick the highest-probability token almost always. High (1.2) = sample from the long tail, including unlikely tokens. Same prompt, three temperatures:"}},{"k":"temp_0_2_conservative","v":{"s":"Temp 0.2 — conservative"}},{"k":"temp_0_7_balanced","v":{"s":"Temp 0.7 — balanced"}},{"k":"temp_1_2_wild","v":{"s":"Temp 1.2 — wild"}},{"k":"show_the_recorded_example_outputs_agai","v":{"s":"Show the recorded example outputs again"}},{"k":"show_recorded","v":{"s":"↺ Show recorded"}},{"k":"live_results_shown_above","v":{"s":"✅ Live results shown above"}},{"k":"showing_recorded_examples","v":{"s":"Showing recorded examples"}},{"k":"static_mode_recorded_examples_only","v":{"s":"Static mode — recorded examples only"}},{"k":"low_temperature_is_right_for_facts_wha","v":{"s":"Low temperature is right for facts (\"what is the capital of France?\"). High temperature is right for creative work. Most AI chat tools default somewhere in the middle — which is why a factual question sometimes drifts."}},{"k":"temperature_playground","v":{"s":"Temperature playground"}},{"k":"pick_any_temperature_and_any_prompt_ru","v":{"s":"Pick any temperature and any prompt. Run it live. Then run the same prompt at a different temperature and compare. The last 5 runs stay visible so you can watch the output shift with the dial."}},{"k":"your_prompt","v":{"s":"Your prompt"}},{"k":"playground_prompt","v":{"s":"Playground prompt"}},{"k":"temperature_3","v":{"s":"Temperature"}},{"k":"temperature_slider","v":{"s":"Temperature slider"}},{"k":"0_0_deterministic","v":{"s":"0.0 ❄️ deterministic"}},{"k":"1_0_balanced","v":{"s":"1.0 ⚜️ balanced"}},{"k":"2_0_chaotic","v":{"s":"2.0 🔥 chaotic"}},{"k":"clear_runs","v":{"s":"🗑️ Clear runs"}},{"k":"live_ai_required_for_the_playground_th","v":{"s":"Live AI required for the playground — the 3-preset compare above uses recorded examples."}},{"k":"coach_paused_before_ai","v":{"s":"🪶 Coach (paused before AI)"}},{"k":"llms_don_t_know_what_they_don_t_know_t","v":{"s":"LLMs don't know what they don't know. They generate the most plausible-sounding next token even when the plausible answer is wrong — this is called "}},{"k":"or_sometimes","v":{"s":" (or sometimes "}},{"k":"here_are_seven_failure_modes_every_stu","v":{"s":"). Here are seven failure modes every student should recognize."}},{"k":"cutoff","v":{"s":"Cutoff"}},{"k":"why_it_happens","v":{"s":"Why it happens"}},{"k":"model_comparison","v":{"s":"Model comparison"}},{"k":"failure_gallery","v":{"s":"Failure gallery"}},{"k":"confidence_chart","v":{"s":"Confidence chart"}},{"k":"analyze_ai_text","v":{"s":"Analyze AI text"}},{"k":"where_the_ai_s_knowledge_ends","v":{"s":"Where the AI’s knowledge ends"}},{"k":"every_model_has_a","v":{"s":"Every model has a "}},{"k":"the_date_its_training_data_ends_anythi","v":{"s":" — the date its training data ends. Anything after that is unknown, though the model may still sound confident. Ask it: "}},{"k":"what_is_your_knowledge_cutoff_date","v":{"s":"\"What is your knowledge cutoff date?\""}},{"k":"known_training_data","v":{"s":"✓ KNOWN — training data"}},{"k":"unknown_after_cutoff","v":{"s":"UNKNOWN — after cutoff"}},{"k":"cutoff_2","v":{"s":"Cutoff"}},{"k":"model_s_last_now","v":{"s":"model's last \"now\""}},{"k":"today","v":{"s":"Today"}},{"k":"what_to_do","v":{"s":"What to do: "}},{"k":"if_the_question_is_about_something_tha","v":{"s":"If the question is about something that could have changed or happened recently, do not trust the AI's answer without a live web source. You can also ask the model directly what its cutoff is — it usually knows."}},{"k":"why_hallucination_even_happens","v":{"s":"Why hallucination even happens"}},{"k":"the_llm_doesn_t_have_a_truth_step_it_h","v":{"s":"The LLM doesn't have a \"truth\" step. It has a \"plausible\" step. The exact same pipeline produces both right and wrong answers — with the same confident tone."}},{"k":"your_question","v":{"s":"Your question"}},{"k":"could_be_about_anything","v":{"s":"Could be about anything."}},{"k":"plausible_text_generator","v":{"s":"Plausible-text generator"}},{"k":"picks_likely_next_tokens_has_no_fact_c","v":{"s":"Picks likely next tokens. Has no fact check."}},{"k":"sometimes_right","v":{"s":"Sometimes RIGHT"}},{"k":"the_pattern_was_common_in_training_dat","v":{"s":"The pattern was common in training data, so the model matched it (not a lookup — still prediction)."}},{"k":"sometimes_wrong","v":{"s":"Sometimes WRONG"}},{"k":"fact_wasn_t_present_or_the_pattern_loo","v":{"s":"Fact wasn't present, or the pattern looks right but isn't."}},{"k":"the_hard_part","v":{"s":"The hard part: "}},{"k":"both_paths_come_out_the_same_way_same_","v":{"s":"both paths come out the same way — same confident tone, same fluent sentences. The only way to tell them apart is to check against something outside the AI."}},{"k":"the_ai_is_not_one_thing","v":{"s":"\"The AI\" is not one thing"}},{"k":"same_prompt_three_different_models_rea","v":{"s":"Same prompt, three different models. Read carefully — the science is the same, but the voice, length, and hedging differ. If your class tested with one model and your friend tested with another, you’d get different answers and both would be \"right.\""}},{"k":"what_to_notice","v":{"s":"What to notice"}},{"k":"length_varies_by_10_words_one_model_le","v":{"s":"Length varies by 10+ words. One model leads with the explanation, another with the visible effect. One uses \"wavelengths\" explicitly, another says \"colors.\" None is more correct — but if you needed a specific phrasing for an assignment, the model you picked would matter."}},{"k":"recorded_examples_for_teaching_not_liv","v":{"s":"Recorded examples for teaching, not live calls. Live calls here use Gemini only."}},{"k":"you_asked","v":{"s":"You asked: "}},{"k":"ai_says","v":{"s":"AI SAYS"}},{"k":"send_this_exact_question_to_gemini_rig","v":{"s":"Send this exact question to Gemini right now and see what comes back"}},{"k":"compare_the_live_answer_to_the_canned_","v":{"s":"Compare the live answer to the canned one above."}},{"k":"live_gemini_response","v":{"s":"🤖 Live Gemini response"}},{"k":"reveal_what_went_wrong","v":{"s":"Reveal: what went wrong"}},{"k":"why_it_fails","v":{"s":"⚠️ Why it fails"}},{"k":"what_you_can_do","v":{"s":"✓ What you can do"}},{"k":"previous","v":{"s":"← Previous"}},{"k":"next","v":{"s":"Next →"}},{"k":"fake_citation","v":{"s":"fake citation"}},{"k":"math_error","v":{"s":"math error"}},{"k":"fake_event","v":{"s":"fake event"}},{"k":"stale_fact","v":{"s":"stale fact"}},{"k":"biased_framing","v":{"s":"biased framing"}},{"k":"correct_fact","v":{"s":"correct fact"}},{"k":"correct_def","v":{"s":"correct def."}},{"k":"right_answer","v":{"s":"right answer"}},{"k":"confidence_is_not_calibration","v":{"s":"Confidence is NOT calibration"}},{"k":"if_ai_confidence_tracked_correctness_t","v":{"s":"If AI-confidence tracked correctness, the dots below would form a diagonal. Instead, almost every AI answer reads as high-confidence — whether it's right or not. The tone is the same."}},{"k":"scatter_plot_ai_confidence_on_the_x_ax","v":{"s":"Scatter plot: AI confidence on the x axis vs. accuracy on the y axis. Most answers cluster at high confidence regardless of accuracy."}},{"k":"ai_confidence","v":{"s":"AI confidence →"}},{"k":"actually_correct","v":{"s":"Actually correct →"}},{"k":"confident_but_wrong","v":{"s":"CONFIDENT BUT WRONG"}},{"k":"what_you_re_seeing","v":{"s":"What you're seeing"}},{"k":"if_ai_confidence_tracked_truth_dots_wo","v":{"s":"If AI confidence tracked truth, dots would line up on the dashed diagonal."}},{"k":"red_dots","v":{"s":"Red dots"}},{"k":"in_the_bottom_right_are_the_danger_zon","v":{"s":" in the bottom-right are the danger zone: sounds sure, actually wrong."}},{"k":"green_dots","v":{"s":"Green dots"}},{"k":"look_identical_to_red_in_tone_that_s_t","v":{"s":" look identical to red in tone. That's the teaching point."}},{"k":"you_can_t_tell_which_is_which_from_ins","v":{"s":"You can't tell which is which from inside the AI. Only external checking works."}},{"k":"analyze_any_ai_output","v":{"s":"Analyze any AI output"}},{"k":"paste_any_ai_generated_text_from_here_","v":{"s":"Paste any AI-generated text (from here, another chatbot, an article that claims to be AI-written, etc.). The tool highlights "}},{"k":"kinds_of_red_flags_so_you_can_see_wher","v":{"s":" kinds of red flags so you can see where to verify. No AI call required — this runs locally."}},{"k":"paste_an_ai_response_here_to_see_which","v":{"s":"Paste an AI response here to see which phrases deserve a second look..."}},{"k":"paste_ai_output_for_red_flag_analysis","v":{"s":"Paste AI output for red-flag analysis"}},{"k":"nothing_to_analyze_yet_paste_some_ai_g","v":{"s":"Nothing to analyze yet. Paste some AI-generated text above to see which phrases might need verification."}},{"k":"clear_your_entire_prompt_journal","v":{"s":"Clear your entire prompt journal?"}},{"k":"this_removes_all_saved_prompts_from_th","v":{"s":"This removes all saved prompts from this section. You can't undo it."}},{"k":"role","v":{"s":"Role"}},{"k":"context","v":{"s":"Context"}},{"k":"try_adding_i_am_a_9th_grader_studying_","v":{"s":"Try adding: \"I am a 9th grader studying for...\" — tells the AI about YOU."}},{"k":"constraints","v":{"s":"Constraints"}},{"k":"try_adding_a_don_t_don_t_write_the_who","v":{"s":"Try adding a DON'T: \"Don't write the whole essay for me.\" Constraints prevent unhelpful outputs."}},{"k":"format","v":{"s":"Format"}},{"k":"try_adding_a_format_give_me_a_3_step_l","v":{"s":"Try adding a format: \"Give me a 3-step list\" or \"One sentence only\" — controls how easy the answer is to USE."}},{"k":"examples","v":{"s":"Examples"}},{"k":"try_adding_a_sample_here_s_one_i_did_e","v":{"s":"Try adding a sample: \"Here's one I did: [example]. Do the next one in the same style.\""}},{"k":"a_weak_prompt_gives_you_a_shallow_answ","v":{"s":"A weak prompt gives you a shallow answer, fast. A strong prompt gives you a useful answer, still fast. The difference is craft — and it is very learnable."}},{"k":"five_patterns","v":{"s":"Five patterns"}},{"k":"anatomy","v":{"s":"Anatomy"}},{"k":"cookbook","v":{"s":"Cookbook"}},{"k":"template_builder","v":{"s":"Template builder"}},{"k":"weak_vs_strong","v":{"s":"Weak vs strong"}},{"k":"workshop","v":{"s":"Workshop"}},{"k":"the_five_patterns","v":{"s":"The five patterns"}},{"k":"role_2","v":{"s":"Role"}},{"k":"context_2","v":{"s":"Context"}},{"k":"constraint","v":{"s":"Constraint"}},{"k":"format_2","v":{"s":"Format"}},{"k":"examples_2","v":{"s":"Examples"}},{"k":"prompt_anatomy","v":{"s":"Prompt anatomy"}},{"k":"here_is_one_strong_prompt_with_every_p","v":{"s":"Here is one strong prompt with every pattern color-coded. Hover any phrase to see which pattern it is."}},{"k":"prompt_cookbook","v":{"s":"Prompt cookbook"}},{"k":"why_this_works","v":{"s":"Why this works: "}},{"k":"copy_to_use_in_your_own_ai_tool","v":{"s":"Copy to use in your own AI tool"}},{"k":"copy","v":{