plain why the ocean is salty to a curious 7th grader who already knows what an atom is. Use no more than 4 sentences.\""}},{"k":"your_prompt_2","v":{"s":"Your prompt"}},{"k":"check_which_of_the_five_patterns_your_","v":{"s":"Check which of the five patterns your prompt uses (no AI call needed)"}},{"k":"critique_my_prompt","v":{"s":"🔍 Critique my prompt"}},{"k":"copy_your_prompt_to_use_elsewhere","v":{"s":"Copy your prompt to use elsewhere"}},{"k":"copy_4","v":{"s":"📋 Copy"}},{"k":"save_this_prompt_to_your_journal_for_l","v":{"s":"Save this prompt to your journal for later"}},{"k":"save_2","v":{"s":"⭐ Save"}},{"k":"live_ai_unavailable_the_critique_still","v":{"s":"Live AI unavailable — the critique still works."}},{"k":"critique","v":{"s":"🔍 CRITIQUE"}},{"k":"this_critique_uses_keyword_heuristics_","v":{"s":"This critique uses keyword heuristics, not AI. It can miss creative phrasings. Use it as a checklist prompt, not a grade."}},{"k":"output","v":{"s":"🤖 OUTPUT"}},{"k":"copy_5","v":{"s":"📋 Copy"}},{"k":"my_prompt_journal","v":{"s":"📔 My prompt journal"}},{"k":"nothing_saved_yet_every_successful_liv","v":{"s":"Nothing saved yet. Every successful live run auto-saves here. You can also ⭐ Save a prompt without running it."}},{"k":"load_into_workshop_3","v":{"s":"Load into workshop"}},{"k":"load","v":{"s":"↑ Load"}},{"k":"copy_6","v":{"s":"Copy"}},{"k":"delete_this_entry","v":{"s":"Delete this entry"}},{"k":"delete_saved_prompt","v":{"s":"Delete saved prompt"}},{"k":"save_your_journal_as_a_markdown_file","v":{"s":"Save your journal as a Markdown file"}},{"k":"export_as_markdown","v":{"s":"⬇️ Export as Markdown"}},{"k":"clear_all","v":{"s":"🗑️ Clear all"}},{"k":"role_persona","v":{"s":"Role / Persona"}},{"k":"task","v":{"s":"Task"}},{"k":"context_3","v":{"s":"Context"}},{"k":"output_format","v":{"s":"Output format"}},{"k":"example_few_shot","v":{"s":"Example / few-shot"}},{"k":"constraint_2","v":{"s":"Constraint"}},{"k":"summarize_the_following_article","v":{"s":"Summarize the following article."}},{"k":"the_audience_is_parents_who_don_t_have","v":{"s":"The audience is parents who don't have a science background."}},{"k":"output_as_3_bullet_points_max_20_words","v":{"s":"Output as 3 bullet points, max 20 words each."}},{"k":"for_instance_photosynthesis_is_how_pla","v":{"s":"For instance: \"Photosynthesis is how plants eat sunlight.\""}},{"k":"do_not_use_the_words_simply_or_just","v":{"s":"Do not use the words \"simply\" or \"just.\""}},{"k":"pretend_you_are_an_admissions_officer_","v":{"s":"Pretend you are an admissions officer at a small liberal-arts college."}},{"k":"use_a_warm_but_professional_tone","v":{"s":"Use a warm but professional tone."}},{"k":"the_parent_emailed_yesterday_asking_wh","v":{"s":"The parent emailed yesterday asking why their child is on a behavior watchlist."}},{"k":"format_subject_line_2_paragraph_body_s","v":{"s":"Format: subject line, 2-paragraph body, sign-off."}},{"k":"example_output_your_essay_shows_strong","v":{"s":"Example output: \"Your essay shows strong voice but lacks structure. Try…\""}},{"k":"write_a_follow_up_email_to_the_parent","v":{"s":"Write a follow-up email to the parent."}},{"k":"prompt_anatomy_2","v":{"s":"🧩 Prompt Anatomy"}},{"k":"you_will_see_12_phrases_pulled_from_re","v":{"s":"You will see 12 phrases pulled from realistic prompts. For each, pick which of six anatomical roles the phrase plays — persona, task, context, format, example, or constraint. Tests whether you can *parse* a prompt as an artifact, not just write or read one."}},{"k":"the_six_anatomical_roles","v":{"s":"The six anatomical roles"}},{"k":"start_phrase_1_of_12","v":{"s":"🧩 Start — phrase 1 of 12"}},{"k":"prompt_anatomy_3","v":{"s":"🧩 Prompt Anatomy"}},{"k":"phrase","v":{"s":"Phrase "}},{"k":"score","v":{"s":"Score "}},{"k":"accuracy","v":{"s":"Accuracy "}},{"k":"streak","v":{"s":"Streak "}},{"k":"best","v":{"s":"Best "}},{"k":"pick_the_anatomical_role","v":{"s":"Pick the anatomical role"}},{"k":"all_12_phrases_complete","v":{"s":"🏆 All 12 phrases complete!"}},{"k":"restart","v":{"s":"🔄 Restart"}},{"k":"next_phrase","v":{"s":"➡️ Next phrase"}},{"k":"check_my_answers","v":{"s":"Check my answers"}},{"k":"reveal_one_error_using_any_hints_forfe","v":{"s":"Reveal one error. Using any hints forfeits the perfect-score bonus — but helps if you're stuck."}},{"k":"try_again","v":{"s":"Try again"}},{"k":"hints_used_perfect_bonus_forfeited_on_","v":{"s":"Hints used — perfect bonus forfeited on this attempt. Reset and retry without hints to earn it."}},{"k":"error_you_didn_t_flag","v":{"s":" error you didn't flag"}},{"k":"flagged_but_fine","v":{"s":"flagged but fine"}},{"k":"false_alarm","v":{"s":" false alarm"}},{"k":"why_each_error_was_plausible","v":{"s":"WHY EACH ERROR WAS PLAUSIBLE"}},{"k":"write_your_own_trap_passage","v":{"s":"Write your own trap passage"}},{"k":"pick_a_topic_you_know_well_write_a_sho","v":{"s":"Pick a topic you know well. Write a short AI-style paragraph on it, but wrap 2–3 wrong phrases in double brackets like "}},{"k":"trade_passages_with_someone_else_whoev","v":{"s":". Trade passages with someone else — whoever catches all the bracketed errors wins."}},{"k":"your_draft_use_brackets_to_mark_errors","v":{"s":"Your draft (use [[brackets]] to mark errors)"}},{"k":"e_g_mitosis_has_four_main_phases_proph","v":{"s":"e.g. \"Mitosis has four main phases: prophase, metaphase, [[telophase]], and anaphase. During metaphase, chromosomes line up [[along the nuclear membrane]] before separating.\""}},{"k":"write_your_trap_passage","v":{"s":"Write your trap passage"}},{"k":"preview","v":{"s":"👀 Preview"}},{"k":"copy_to_share","v":{"s":"📋 Copy to share"}},{"k":"clear","v":{"s":"↺ Clear"}},{"k":"good_trap_passages_have_2_3_seeded_err","v":{"s":"Good trap passages have 2–3 seeded errors. More than that feels unfair; fewer is too easy. Aim for errors that sound plausible at first read."}},{"k":"the_barrier_you_described_sounds_mecha","v":{"s":"The barrier you described sounds mechanical (slow typing, memory retrieval, formatting, organization). Using AI to remove that barrier is not the same as having AI do the skill itself. Go ahead — but keep the core thinking on you."}},{"k":"the_barrier_is_cognitive_and_the_skill","v":{"s":"The barrier is cognitive, and the skill you named is exactly the kind of skill school is trying to build (thinking, composing, reasoning). Letting AI do this means you skip the practice. Consider: can AI COACH you through the skill instead of performing it for you? That flips it back to scaffold."}},{"k":"the_barrier_is_cognitive_but_the_skill","v":{"s":"The barrier is cognitive, but the skill you described may not be the one being practiced here. Re-read the assignment: what specific skill is it really testing? Use AI to reduce barriers to that specific skill, not to replace it."}},{"k":"the_question_is_not_is_ai_good_or_bad_","v":{"s":"The question is not \"is AI good or bad\" — it's \"does AI REMOVE a barrier to the skill I'm practicing, or does it REPLACE the skill itself?\" "}},{"k":"the_first","v":{"s":" = the first. "}},{"k":"the_second","v":{"s":" = the second."}},{"k":"decision_chart","v":{"s":"Decision chart"}},{"k":"scenarios","v":{"s":"Scenarios"}},{"k":"your_situation","v":{"s":"Your situation"}},{"k":"the_decision_visualized","v":{"s":"The decision, visualized"}},{"k":"before_you_use_ai_for_something_run_it","v":{"s":"Before you use AI for something, run it through these two questions. The answers route to one of three outcomes."}},{"k":"question_1","v":{"s":"Question 1"}},{"k":"what_specific_skill_is_this_task_meant","v":{"s":"What specific skill is this task meant to build?"}},{"k":"question_2","v":{"s":"Question 2"}},{"k":"is_ai_removing_a_barrier_to_that_skill","v":{"s":"Is AI removing a BARRIER to that skill, or doing the SKILL itself?"}},{"k":"scaffold","v":{"s":"Scaffold"}},{"k":"removes_barrier_go_ahead_keep_the_core","v":{"s":"Removes barrier. Go ahead — keep the core thinking on you."}},{"k":"it_depends","v":{"s":"It depends"}},{"k":"can_ai_coach_you_through_the_skill_ins","v":{"s":"Can AI coach you through the skill instead of doing it? If yes — reframe as scaffold."}},{"k":"substitute","v":{"s":"Substitute"}},{"k":"doing_the_skill_itself_skipping_ai_her","v":{"s":"Doing the skill itself. Skipping AI here preserves the practice you need."}},{"k":"scaffold_2","v":{"s":"Scaffold"}},{"k":"remove_a_barrier","v":{"s":"Remove a barrier"}},{"k":"use_ai_in_a_way_that_helps_you_do_the_","v":{"s":"Use AI in a way that helps you DO the work yourself."}},{"k":"substitute_2","v":{"s":"Substitute"}},{"k":"replace_the_skill","v":{"s":"Replace the skill"}},{"k":"use_ai_to_do_the_work_for_you","v":{"s":"Use AI to do the work FOR you."}},{"k":"your_instinct","v":{"s":"Your instinct: "}},{"k":"now_compare_both_worked_versions_there","v":{"s":". Now compare both worked versions — there's no \"wrong\" pick, only clearer thinking about what the skill actually is."}},{"k":"scaffold_version","v":{"s":"🪡 SCAFFOLD VERSION"}},{"k":"substitute_version","v":{"s":"🧱 SUBSTITUTE VERSION"}},{"k":"why_this_one_matters","v":{"s":"🔬 WHY THIS ONE MATTERS"}},{"k":"previous_2","v":{"s":"← Previous"}},{"k":"next_2","v":{"s":"Next →"}},{"k":"bring_your_own_situation","v":{"s":"Bring your own situation"}},{"k":"the_five_scenarios_above_are_common_bu","v":{"s":"The five scenarios above are common, but the real question is ALWAYS about your specific moment. Describe yours, name the skill, and name the barrier. You'll get a direction — not an answer."}},{"k":"1_your_situation","v":{"s":"1. Your situation"}},{"k":"e_g_i_have_a_biology_lab_report_due_fr","v":{"s":"e.g. \"I have a biology lab report due Friday and I can’t focus long enough to write the intro.\""}},{"k":"describe_your_situation","v":{"s":"Describe your situation"}},{"k":"2_the_skill_the_assignment_is_practici","v":{"s":"2. The skill the assignment is practicing"}},{"k":"e_g_writing_a_scientific_intro_that_st","v":{"s":"e.g. \"writing a scientific intro that states the hypothesis\""}},{"k":"name_the_skill_this_assignment_is_prac","v":{"s":"Name the skill this assignment is practicing"}},{"k":"3_what_kind_of_barrier_is_in_the_way","v":{"s":"3. What kind of barrier is in the way?"}},{"k":"mechanical","v":{"s":"Mechanical"}},{"k":"cognitive","v":{"s":"Cognitive"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"heuristic_direction_no_ai_call","v":{"s":"Heuristic direction (no AI call)"}},{"k":"ai_coaching_live","v":{"s":"🧑‍🏫 AI coaching (live)"}},{"k":"live_ai_unavailable_here_the_heuristic","v":{"s":"Live AI unavailable here — the heuristic direction above uses only your answers, no AI call needed."}},{"k":"prompt_craft","v":{"s":"Prompt Craft"}},{"k":"prompt_craft_2","v":{"s":"Prompt Craft"}},{"k":"go_2","v":{"s":"Go →"}},{"k":"a_one_page_summary","v":{"s":"A one-page summary"}},{"k":"printable_use","v":{"s":" — printable. Use "}},{"k":"to_print_other_ui_hides_automatically","v":{"s":" to print; other UI hides automatically."}},{"k":"download_a_markdown_report_of_your_pro","v":{"s":"Download a Markdown report of your progress, checks passed, and saved prompts. Hand to a teacher."}},{"k":"export_session_report","v":{"s":"📝 Export session report"}},{"k":"print","v":{"s":"🖨️ Print"}},{"k":"ai_literacy_lab_quick_reference","v":{"s":"AI Literacy Lab — Quick Reference"}},{"k":"alloflow_for_students_grades_6_12_clin","v":{"s":"AlloFlow · for students grades 6–12 · clinician-authored"}},{"k":"breaks_your_text_into","v":{"s":"Breaks your text into "}},{"k":"predicts_the_next_token_by_probability","v":{"s":"Predicts the next token by probability"}},{"k":"controls_how_random_the_pick_is","v":{"s":" controls how random the pick is"}},{"k":"it_has_no_idea_what_s_true_only_what_s","v":{"s":"It has no idea what's \"true\" — only what's plausible"}},{"k":"fake_citations_verify_with_google_scho","v":{"s":"Fake citations (verify with Google Scholar)"}},{"k":"math_errors_use_a_calculator","v":{"s":"Math errors — use a calculator"}},{"k":"past_the","v":{"s":"Past the "}},{"k":"may_invent","v":{"s":" = may invent"}},{"k":"fills_gaps_with_plausible_stories","v":{"s":": fills gaps with plausible stories"}},{"k":"it_sounds_confident_exactly_the_same_w","v":{"s":"It sounds confident exactly the same whether right or wrong"}},{"k":"does_the_answer_cite_anything_verify_e","v":{"s":"Does the answer cite anything? Verify each citation."}},{"k":"is_it_past_the_model_s_cutoff_use_web_","v":{"s":"Is it past the model's cutoff? Use web search if so."}},{"k":"any_math_redo_it_with_a_calculator","v":{"s":"Any math? Redo it with a calculator."}},{"k":"sound_too_confident_ask_are_you_sure_w","v":{"s":"Sound too confident? Ask \"are you sure?\" — watch if the answer changes."}},{"k":"scaffold_3","v":{"s":"🪡 Scaffold: "}},{"k":"ai_removes_a_barrier_so_you_can_do_the","v":{"s":"AI removes a barrier so YOU can do the skill. (Quiz me. Organize my ideas. Ask me questions.)"}},{"k":"substitute_3","v":{"s":"🧱 Substitute: "}},{"k":"ai_does_the_skill_for_you_write_my_ess","v":{"s":"AI does the skill for you. (Write my essay. Solve my problem. Summarize instead of read.)"}},{"k":"ask_what_skill_is_this_assignment_real","v":{"s":"Ask: \"What skill is this assignment really testing?\" Then keep that on you."}},{"k":"i_am_a_grade_student_don_t_solve_this_","v":{"s":"\"I am a [grade] student. Don't solve this for me — ask me questions that help me find the answer.\""}},{"k":"quiz_me_on_topic_one_question_at_a_tim","v":{"s":"\"Quiz me on [topic] one question at a time. Wait for my answer before the next.\""}},{"k":"are_you_certain_this_event_actually_ha","v":{"s":"\"Are you certain this event actually happened? Cite a source.\""}},{"k":"explain_concept_using_only_middle_scho","v":{"s":"\"Explain [concept] using only middle-school vocabulary. No jargon.\""}},{"k":"alloflow_ai_literacy_lab_built_for_stu","v":{"s":"AlloFlow · AI Literacy Lab · built for students who need AI as a scaffold, not a substitute."}},{"k":"back_to_ai_literacy_lab_home","v":{"s":"Back to AI Literacy Lab home"}},{"k":"back","v":{"s":"← Back"}},{"k":"1_how_llms_work_2","v":{"s":"1. How LLMs Work"}},{"k":"2_why_llms_get_things_wrong_2","v":{"s":"2. Why LLMs Get Things Wrong"}},{"k":"3_prompt_craft_2","v":{"s":"3. Prompt Craft"}},{"k":"4_prompt_anatomy_2","v":{"s":"4. Prompt Anatomy"}},{"k":"5_hallucination_spotter_2","v":{"s":"5. Hallucination Spotter"}},{"k":"6_when_to_use_ai_2","v":{"s":"6. When to Use AI"}},{"k":"7_quick_reference_2","v":{"s":"7. Quick Reference"}},{"k":"8_inquiry_trust_calibration","v":{"s":"8. Inquiry: Trust Calibration"}},{"k":"pick_another_answer_to_try_again","v":{"s":"Pick another answer to try again."}},{"k":"on_this_page","v":{"s":"On this page"}},{"k":"all_sections","v":{"s":"🏠 All sections"}},{"k":"you_ve_worked_through_every_section_2","v":{"s":"🏁 You've worked through every section."}},{"k":"safe_to_use","v":{"s":"Safe to use"}},{"k":"low_stakes_high_familiarity_high_sourc","v":{"s":"Low stakes, high familiarity, high source quality. Spot-check still good practice, but you can trust the output."}},{"k":"verify_one_source","v":{"s":"Verify one source"}},{"k":"trust_most_of_it_but_check_one_or_two_","v":{"s":"Trust most of it, but check one or two key claims against an authoritative source before acting."}},{"k":"verify_multiple","v":{"s":"Verify multiple"}},{"k":"treat_as_draft_every_concrete_claim_nu","v":{"s":"Treat as draft. Every concrete claim (number, name, quote) needs independent verification."}},{"k":"risky","v":{"s":"Risky"}},{"k":"high_stakes_or_low_source_quality_use_","v":{"s":"High stakes or low source quality. Use only for brainstorming; do not present any AI output as a final answer."}},{"k":"don_t_use_for_this","v":{"s":"Don't use for this"}},{"k":"medical_diagnosis_legal_advice_citing_","v":{"s":"Medical diagnosis, legal advice, citing primary sources you cannot verify — wrong tool for the job. Use a human expert or authoritative source."}},{"k":"trust_calibration_how_much_should_i_tr","v":{"s":"🔬 Trust Calibration — How Much Should I Trust This Output?"}},{"k":"set_task_familiarity_stakes_source_qua","v":{"s":"Set task familiarity, stakes, source quality, and stated model confidence. Predict where the trust threshold lands. No score, no reveal."}},{"k":"green_red_safer_to_use","v":{"s":"green > red = safer to use"}},{"k":"your_familiarity_1_10","v":{"s":"Your familiarity (1-10)"}},{"k":"stakes_1_10","v":{"s":"Stakes (1-10)"}},{"k":"source_quality_1_10","v":{"s":"Source quality (1-10)"}},{"k":"model_confidence","v":{"s":"Model confidence (%)"}},{"k":"log_this_calibration","v":{"s":"📋 Log this calibration"}},{"k":"reset_2","v":{"s":"Reset"}},{"k":"your_hypothesis_which_slider_should_we","v":{"s":"Your hypothesis (which slider should weigh MOST in the threshold? Does stated confidence even belong here?)"}},{"k":"e_g_stakes_should_dominate_everything_","v":{"s":"e.g., stakes should dominate everything else — confidently wrong on low stakes < uncertainly right on high stakes..."}},{"k":"i_m_stuck_show_open_questions","v":{"s":"🤔 I'm stuck — show open questions"}},{"k":"open_questions_no_answer_key","v":{"s":"Open questions (no answer key)"}},{"k":"why_does_your_familiarity_matter_what_","v":{"s":"Why does YOUR familiarity matter? What does the model not know that you might?"}},{"k":"when_llms_report_95_confidence_what_do","v":{"s":"When LLMs report 95% confidence, what does that actually mean? Are they calibrated?"}},{"k":"when_should_you_never_use_an_llm_regar","v":{"s":"When should you NEVER use an LLM, regardless of source quality?"}},{"k":"how_would_your_trust_threshold_differ_","v":{"s":"How would your trust threshold differ for a math proof vs a creative essay vs a citation?"}},{"k":"i_can_explain_why_this_combination_yie","v":{"s":"I can explain why this combination yields this trust state."}},{"k":"explain_in_your_own_words","v":{"s":"Explain in your own words..."}},{"k":"inquiry_widget_no_score_no_reveal_no_a","v":{"s":"Inquiry widget — no score, no reveal, no answer dump. Trust formula is a heuristic, not a published framework. LLMs are NOT well-calibrated — stated confidence often diverges from accuracy. Always verify high-stakes outputs against authoritative sources."}},{"k":"skip_to_main_content","v":{"s":"Skip to main content"}},{"k":"ai_literacy_lab_main_content","v":{"s":"AI Literacy Lab main content"}},{"k":"something_went_wrong_rendering_this_se","v":{"s":"Something went wrong rendering this section. Check the console for details."}},{"k":"back_to_home_2","v":{"s":"← Back to home"}},{"k":"tokens_goal","v":{"s":"Make the model’s machinery visible so “AI magic” stops being a category students use."}},{"k":"fails_goal","v":{"s":"Build a working taxonomy of AI failure modes so “don’t trust AI” becomes “check for THESE specific things.”"}},{"k":"prompt_goal","v":{"s":"Treat prompting as a learnable craft with five concrete patterns, not as a mystical skill."}},{"k":"spotter_goal","v":{"s":"Convert hallucination-detection from a passive warning into an active skill students practice."}},{"k":"udl_goal","v":{"s":"Give students a rubric for deciding when AI is a legitimate accommodation vs. a shortcut that undermines the learning target."}},{"k":"ref_goal","v":{"s":"A printable takeaway students (or teachers) can keep nearby while actually using AI."}},{"k":"hypothesis_input","v":{"s":"LLM trust hypothesis"}},{"k":"explanation_input","v":{"s":"LLM trust explanation"}},{"k":"detector_heading","v":{"s":"🚩 If you are accused and you did not do it"}},{"k":"detector_not_a_loophole","v":{"s":"Read this the right way round: detectors being unreliable is not a reason to think you can get away with it. It is a reason to keep your drafts, and a reason to speak up if a number is used against you or someone in your class."}},{"k":"detector_protect_heading","v":{"s":"What protects you — and costs you nothing if you are honest"}},{"k":"detector_sub","v":{"s":"Schools run AI detectors. You should know what they are actually worth before one is pointed at your work."}},{"k":"tokenizer_approximation_note","v":{"s":"It shows the shape of subword splitting, not real token counts. A real tokenizer splits a string according to how often it saw that string while training, which spelling alone cannot tell you — so do not read anything into how your own name comes out here."}},{"k":"tokenizer_is_an_approximation","v":{"s":"This is an approximation. "}}],"id":543}},{"k":"logiclab","v":{"o":[{"k":"implication","v":{"s":"Implication"}},{"k":"de_morgan_s_1","v":{"s":"De Morgan's 1"}},{"k":"de_morgan_s_2","v":{"s":"De Morgan's 2"}},{"k":"contrapositive","v":{"s":"Contrapositive"}},{"k":"tautology","v":{"s":"Tautology"}},{"k":"contradiction","v":{"s":"Contradiction"}},{"k":"biconditional","v":{"s":"Biconditional"}},{"k":"distributive","v":{"s":"Distributive"}},{"k":"modus_ponens_form","v":{"s":"Modus Ponens form"}},{"k":"modus_ponens","v":{"s":"Modus Ponens"}},{"k":"modus_tollens","v":{"s":"Modus Tollens"}},{"k":"hypothetical_syllogism","v":{"s":"Hypothetical Syllogism"}},{"k":"disjunctive_syllogism","v":{"s":"Disjunctive Syllogism"}},{"k":"conjunction","v":{"s":"Conjunction"}},{"k":"simplification","v":{"s":"Simplification"}},{"k":"addition","v":{"s":"Addition"}},{"k":"double_negation","v":{"s":"Double Negation"}},{"k":"contrapositive_2","v":{"s":"Contrapositive"}},{"k":"de_morgan_s","v":{"s":"De Morgan's"}},{"k":"simple_deduction","v":{"s":"Simple Deduction"}},{"k":"use_modus_ponens_p_q_and_p_gives_q","v":{"s":"Use Modus Ponens: P→Q and P gives Q"}},{"k":"denial","v":{"s":"Denial"}},{"k":"use_modus_tollens_p_q_and_q_gives_p","v":{"s":"Use Modus Tollens: P→Q and ¬Q gives ¬P"}},{"k":"chain_reaction","v":{"s":"Chain Reaction"}},{"k":"hs_chains_p_q_and_q_r_then_mp_with_p","v":{"s":"HS chains P→Q and Q→R, then MP with P"}},{"k":"elimination","v":{"s":"Elimination"}},{"k":"disjunctive_syllogism_p_q_and_p_gives_","v":{"s":"Disjunctive Syllogism: P∨Q and ¬P gives Q"}},{"k":"combine_conclude","v":{"s":"Combine & Conclude"}},{"k":"conjunction_gives_p_q_then_modus_ponen","v":{"s":"Conjunction gives P∧Q, then Modus Ponens gives R"}},{"k":"long_chain","v":{"s":"Long Chain"}},{"k":"chain_p_q_and_q_r_with_hs_then_again_w","v":{"s":"Chain P→Q and Q→R with HS, then again with R→S, then MP"}},{"k":"double_deny","v":{"s":"Double Deny"}},{"k":"mt_on_p_q_gives_p_then_ds_on_p_r_gives","v":{"s":"MT on P→Q gives ¬P, then DS on P∨R gives R"}},{"k":"master_proof","v":{"s":"Master Proof"}},{"k":"hs_gives_p_r_then_mt_with_r_gives_p","v":{"s":"HS gives P→R, then MT with ¬R gives ¬P"}},{"k":"affirming_the_consequent","v":{"s":"Affirming the Consequent"}},{"k":"denying_the_antecedent","v":{"s":"Denying the Antecedent"}},{"k":"valid_syllogism","v":{"s":"Valid Syllogism"}},{"k":"affirming_the_consequent_2","v":{"s":"Affirming the Consequent"}},{"k":"disjunctive_syllogism_2","v":{"s":"Disjunctive Syllogism"}},{"k":"modus_tollens_2","v":{"s":"Modus Tollens"}},{"k":"affirming_the_consequent_3","v":{"s":"Affirming the Consequent"}},{"k":"affirming_the_consequent_4","v":{"s":"Affirming the Consequent"}},{"k":"denying_the_antecedent_2","v":{"s":"Denying the Antecedent"}},{"k":"modus_ponens_2","v":{"s":"Modus Ponens"}},{"k":"false_exclusive_disjunction","v":{"s":"False Exclusive Disjunction"}},{"k":"denying_the_antecedent_3","v":{"s":"Denying the Antecedent"}},{"k":"and_gate","v":{"s":"AND gate"}},{"k":"or_gate","v":{"s":"OR gate"}},{"k":"implication_2","v":{"s":"Implication"}},{"k":"negation","v":{"s":"Negation"}},{"k":"exclusive_or","v":{"s":"Exclusive OR"}},{"k":"biconditional_equivalence","v":{"s":"Biconditional equivalence"}},{"k":"nand_gate","v":{"s":"NAND gate"}},{"k":"nor_gate","v":{"s":"NOR gate"}},{"k":"contradiction_2","v":{"s":"Contradiction"}},{"k":"tautology_2","v":{"s":"Tautology"}},{"k":"logic_lab","v":{"s":"Logic Lab"}},{"k":"propositional_logic_reasoning","v":{"s":"Propositional Logic & Reasoning"}},{"k":"truth_tables_every_input_combination_e","v":{"s":"Truth Tables — every input combination, every output"}},{"k":"for_n_variables_the_table_has_2_rows_a","v":{"s":"For n variables, the table has 2ⁿ rows. AND, OR, NOT, XOR, IFF — each gate is just a column. Boolean algebra (Boole 1854) underlies every digital circuit, every search query, every conditional in code."}},{"k":"proof_builder_derive_conclusions_step_","v":{"s":"Proof Builder — derive conclusions step by step"}},{"k":"modus_ponens_modus_tollens_hypothetica","v":{"s":"Modus ponens, modus tollens, hypothetical syllogism, disjunctive syllogism — the eight inference rules cover most introductory propositional logic. Each step justifies itself by NAME, not vibe."}},{"k":"challenges_graded_tautology_contradict","v":{"s":"Challenges — graded tautology + contradiction puzzles"}},{"k":"tautology_always_true_contradiction_al","v":{"s":"Tautology = always true; contradiction = always false; contingency = sometimes both. Aristotle’s law of non-contradiction (350 BCE) is the oldest published rule. AP CS Principles practice + intro discrete math."}},{"k":"logic_gates_transistors_all_the_way_do","v":{"s":"Logic Gates — transistors all the way down"}},{"k":"nand_is_functionally_complete_you_can_","v":{"s":"NAND is functionally complete — you can build every other gate from NAND alone. A modern CPU contains ~10 billion transistors implementing the same boolean math you’re building here."}},{"k":"probability_logic_inference_under_unce","v":{"s":"Probability Logic — inference under uncertainty"}},{"k":"p_and_q_each_carry_a_probability_inste","v":{"s":"P and Q each carry a probability instead of a hard true/false. For independent events, P(P∧Q) = P(P) × P(Q). Watch how a confidence threshold turns soft probabilities into discrete inferences."}},{"k":"drag_and_drop_expression_builder","v":{"s":"Drag-and-Drop Expression Builder"}},{"k":"drag_tiles_or_click_to_add","v":{"s":"Drag tiles or click to add"}},{"k":"variables","v":{"s":"Variables"}},{"k":"connectives","v":{"s":"Co