_ec","v":{"s":"Imported values land as L0 (verbatim echoes). Rows missing or non-numeric in the mapped x/y are reported on bind, never silently dropped. No AI call fires during ingest."}},{"k":"16_sourced_benchmark_workspace","v":{"s":"§16 SOURCED — benchmark workspace"}},{"k":"benchmark_workspace_16_sourced","v":{"s":"▣ Benchmark workspace — §16 SOURCED"}},{"k":"drop_a_benchmark_document_text_extract","v":{"s":"Drop a benchmark document. Text extracts deterministically (no AI). You byte-check each cell against the source and sign it off; verified cells fold into the NORM_SPINE JSON for paste-back. "}},{"k":"ai_search_is_intentionally_deferred_16","v":{"s":"AI-search is intentionally deferred (§16.4 Phase 2B)."}},{"k":"import_benchmark_document","v":{"s":"⇪ Import benchmark document…"}},{"k":"grades_e_g_1_6","v":{"s":"Grades (e.g. 1-6)"}},{"k":"seasons","v":{"s":"Seasons"}},{"k":"percentiles_e_g_25_50_75","v":{"s":"Percentiles (e.g. 25,50,75)"}},{"k":"extracted_text_deterministic_no_ai_par","v":{"s":"Extracted text (deterministic; no AI parse) — read here, type values on the right"}},{"k":"scaffold_cells_fill_the_value_paste_th","v":{"s":"Scaffold cells — fill the value, paste the source excerpt, tick to verify"}},{"k":"pick_a_grade_range_season_percentile_a","v":{"s":"Pick a grade range / season / percentile above, then Rebuild scaffold."}},{"k":"source_excerpt_optional_traceability","v":{"s":"Source excerpt (optional, traceability)"}},{"k":"unverify_edit","v":{"s":"Unverify (edit)"}},{"k":"verify_this_cell","v":{"s":"✓ Verify this cell"}},{"k":"verify_at_least_one_cell_to_see_the_pa","v":{"s":"Verify at least one cell to see the paste-back JSON."}},{"k":"spine_cells_json_paste_into_stem_tool_","v":{"s":"Spine cells JSON (paste into stem_tool_lumen.js → NORM_SPINE.cells)"}},{"k":"after_pasting_setting_reviewedon_in_so","v":{"s":"After pasting + setting reviewedOn in source, the spine's `validateNormSpine` returns \"ready\" and assertExportClean lets curated benchmark refs draw at a formal export. The signoff hash spans every truth-bearing field, so a stale (edited-after) cell re-blocks."}},{"k":"bars_are_per_cell_means_descriptive_sm","v":{"s":"Bars are per-cell means (descriptive); small cells (n<3) are faded. Every point is in the data table."}},{"k":"synthetic_practice_data_this_finding_i","v":{"s":"◇ Synthetic practice data — this finding includes fabricated points; not a defensible measurement."}},{"k":"practice_data","v":{"s":"PRACTICE DATA"}},{"k":"signed_off_kept_as_an_ai_reading_not_a","v":{"s":"✓ Signed off — kept as an AI reading, not a measured finding."}},{"k":"sign_off_before_a_formal_export","v":{"s":"⚠ Sign off before a formal export:"}},{"k":"own_it","v":{"s":"Own it"}},{"k":"demote_remove","v":{"s":"Demote (remove)"}},{"k":"add_orf_benchmark","v":{"s":"Add ORF benchmark:"}},{"k":"grade","v":{"s":"Grade"}},{"k":"season","v":{"s":"Season"}},{"k":"present_export_this_view","v":{"s":"Present / export this view:"}},{"k":"present","v":{"s":"▶ Present"}},{"k":"brief_html","v":{"s":"Brief (HTML)"}},{"k":"data_csv","v":{"s":"Data (CSV)"}},{"k":"include_identifiable_data_ferpa","v":{"s":"Include identifiable data (FERPA)"}},{"k":"insufficient_evidence","v":{"s":"Insufficient evidence"}},{"k":"slope_to_noise_ratio_too_low_anything_","v":{"s":"Slope-to-noise ratio too low. Anything you claim will be defensible only as a hypothesis to test next."}},{"k":"suggestive","v":{"s":"Suggestive"}},{"k":"pattern_hints_at_change_but_could_be_n","v":{"s":"Pattern hints at change but could be noise. Useful for generating hypotheses, weak for action."}},{"k":"supported","v":{"s":"Supported"}},{"k":"clear_trend_with_adequate_sample_reaso","v":{"s":"Clear trend with adequate sample. Reasonable basis for action with continued monitoring."}},{"k":"robust","v":{"s":"Robust"}},{"k":"strong_slope_and_large_sample_could_pr","v":{"s":"Strong slope and large sample. Could probably re-derive same conclusion from another subset."}},{"k":"ai_dial_cranked_too_high_relative_to_e","v":{"s":"AI dial cranked too high relative to evidence. The narrative confidence outruns the data — exactly what Lumen's ladder is designed to prevent."}},{"k":"evidence_inquiry_a_what_if_sandbox_not","v":{"s":"🔬 Evidence Inquiry — a what-if sandbox (not your data)"}},{"k":"a_learning_sandbox_drag_these_hypothet","v":{"s":"A learning sandbox: drag these HYPOTHETICAL dials — trend strength, sample size, baseline, and a what-if AI level — to feel where evidence sits between insufficient and over-interpreted. It does not read your data and does not change your live AI ceiling. No score, no reveal."}},{"k":"trend_strength","v":{"s":"Trend strength"}},{"k":"observations","v":{"s":"Observations"}},{"k":"baseline_value","v":{"s":"Baseline value"}},{"k":"what_if_ai_level_not_your_live_dial","v":{"s":"What-if AI level (not your live dial)"}},{"k":"log_this_evidence_call","v":{"s":"📋 Log this evidence call"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"Reset"}},{"k":"your_hypothesis_when_does_dialing_ai_u","v":{"s":"Your hypothesis (when does dialing AI up start to mislead, and what guard would you add?)"}},{"k":"e_g_past_l2_you_need_to_surface_the_sl","v":{"s":"e.g., past L2 you need to surface the slope/noise ratio so the AI cannot manufacture certainty..."}},{"k":"i_m_stuck_show_open_questions","v":{"s":"🤔 I'm stuck — show open questions"}},{"k":"open_questions_no_answer_key","v":{"s":"Open questions (no answer key)"}},{"k":"why_does_lumen_default_to_l1_math_only","v":{"s":"Why does Lumen DEFAULT to L1 (math only) and force you to opt up?"}},{"k":"a_flat_baseline_with_n_40_vs_noisy_slo","v":{"s":"A flat baseline with n=40 vs noisy slope with n=8 — which would you act on?"}},{"k":"how_would_you_communicate_suggestive_v","v":{"s":"How would you communicate \"suggestive\" vs \"supported\" to a parent at an IEP meeting?"}},{"k":"when_is_regression_to_the_mean_the_rea","v":{"s":"When is regression to the mean the real explanation for an apparent trend?"}},{"k":"i_can_explain_why_this_evidence_config","v":{"s":"I can explain why this evidence configuration yields this evidentiary state."}},{"k":"explain_in_your_own_words","v":{"s":"Explain in your own words..."}},{"k":"inquiry_widget_no_score_no_reveal_no_a","v":{"s":"Inquiry widget — no score, no reveal, no answer dump. Slope-to-noise is a heuristic; Lumen argues from the data you bring, it does not set goals. For formal IEP goal decisions (aimlines, decision rules, RTI tiers) use the Teacher Dashboard or BehaviorLens."}},{"k":"phase_1_l1_default_fires_zero_ai_dial_","v":{"s":"Phase 1 — L1 default fires zero AI; dial up for gated, marked AI. Exports are FERPA-gated: both the brief and the CSV are finding-only unless you opt in to identifiable data, and formal exports require sign-off on any AI reading. docs/lumen_design.md."}},{"k":"lumen_present_mode","v":{"s":"Lumen present mode"}},{"k":"keyframes_lumenreveal_from_opacity_0_t","v":{"s":"@keyframes lumenReveal{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(10px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}.lumen-reveal{animation:lumenReveal .55s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1) both}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.lumen-reveal{animation:none}}"}},{"k":"lumen_2","v":{"s":"Lumen"}},{"k":"present_mode","v":{"s":"present mode"}},{"k":"synthetic_practice_data_not_a_real_stu_2","v":{"s":"⚗ Synthetic practice data — not a real student. For demonstration only; not a defensible record."}},{"k":"add_at_least_3_observations_to_show_a_","v":{"s":"Add at least 3 observations to show a chart."}},{"k":"ceiling_l1","v":{"s":"L1 · Data only"}},{"k":"ceiling_l2","v":{"s":"L2 · Assisted"}},{"k":"ceiling_l3","v":{"s":"L3 · Interpretive"}},{"k":"face_working","v":{"s":"Working"}},{"k":"face_formal","v":{"s":"Formal"}},{"k":"face_plain","v":{"s":"Plain language"}},{"k":"chart_trend","v":{"s":"Trend"}},{"k":"chart_bar","v":{"s":"Bar"}},{"k":"chart_dot","v":{"s":"Dot"}},{"k":"chart_box","v":{"s":"Box"}},{"k":"chart_histogram","v":{"s":"Histogram"}},{"k":"chart_scatter","v":{"s":"Scatter"}},{"k":"chart_slope","v":{"s":"Slope"}},{"k":"chart_multi_line","v":{"s":"Multi-line"}},{"k":"chart_grouped_bar","v":{"s":"Grouped bar"}},{"k":"view_options","v":{"s":"View options"}},{"k":"audience_label","v":{"s":"Audience:"}},{"k":"face_working_title","v":{"s":"For your own analysis — the full technical wording."}},{"k":"face_formal_title","v":{"s":"A defensible artifact for a formal decision — an IEP team, a review board, a grant reviewer. Sign-off + FERPA gates apply here."}},{"k":"face_plain_title","v":{"s":"For a lay audience — a parent, a student, the public. Keeps the uncertainty; never overstates."}},{"k":"chart_label","v":{"s":"Chart:"}},{"k":"ob_step1_bold","v":{"s":"Name your measure"}},{"k":"ob_step1_rest","v":{"s":" in the Setup row (anything — plant height / Day, survey score / Round, words-per-minute / Week)."}},{"k":"ob_step2_bold","v":{"s":"Add data"}},{"k":"ob_step2_rest","v":{"s":" — type points, paste a table, or import a CSV / Excel / JSON file."}},{"k":"ob_step3_bold","v":{"s":"Read the finding"}},{"k":"ob_step3_rest","v":{"s":" — a chart + plain-language finding appear at 3+ points; export an honest artifact to hand to a colleague, a parent, a team, or a reviewer."}},{"k":"phase_tooltip","v":{"s":"Optional condition tag (e.g. before / after). When the tag changes between points, a phase line is drawn there. Sticks until you change it."}},{"k":"phase_optional","v":{"s":"Phase (optional)"}},{"k":"undo_last_tooltip","v":{"s":"Remove the most recently added data point."}},{"k":"undo_last","v":{"s":"↩ Undo last"}},{"k":"clear_all_tooltip","v":{"s":"Remove every data point and start fresh."}},{"k":"clear_all","v":{"s":"🗑 Clear all"}},{"k":"hide_practice_data","v":{"s":"⚗ Hide practice data"}},{"k":"show_practice_data","v":{"s":"⚗ Practice data…"}},{"k":"hide_paste_box","v":{"s":"⎘ Hide paste box"}},{"k":"show_paste_box","v":{"s":"⎘ Paste data…"}},{"k":"scenario_improving","v":{"s":"Improving trend"}},{"k":"scenario_flat","v":{"s":"Flat / no change"}},{"k":"scenario_variable","v":{"s":"Highly variable"}},{"k":"scenario_declining","v":{"s":"Declining trend"}},{"k":"scenario_responsive","v":{"s":"Responds after a change"}},{"k":"practice_data_samples","v":{"s":"⚗ Practice data & samples"}},{"k":"everything_here_is_marked_synthetic","v":{"s":"Everything here loads clearly-marked synthetic practice data — great for exploring Lumen, watermarked on every chart and export, and never exportable as a defensible formal document."}},{"k":"scenario","v":{"s":"Scenario"}},{"k":"map_columns_from","v":{"s":"⇪ Map columns from"}},{"k":"imported_file","v":{"s":"imported file"}},{"k":"open_benchmark_workspace","v":{"s":"▣ Benchmark workspace (verify external norms)…"}},{"k":"showing","v":{"s":"Showing"}},{"k":"of","v":{"s":"of"}},{"k":"stats_use_only_focused","v":{"s":"stats and the chart use only the focused points"}},{"k":"show_all","v":{"s":"Show all"}},{"k":"series_same_measure","v":{"s":" series (same measure)"}},{"k":"mean_per_phase_series","v":{"s":" mean per phase × series"}},{"k":"copy_finding_tooltip","v":{"s":"Copy the finding sentence — the level word and interval travel with it."}},{"k":"copy_finding","v":{"s":"⧉ Copy finding"}},{"k":"hide_data_table","v":{"s":"Hide data table"}},{"k":"show_data_table","v":{"s":"Show data table (the chart as a table)"}},{"k":"data_table_caption","v":{"s":"the chart as an accessible table; each row is one charted point"}},{"k":"focus_col","v":{"s":"Focus"}},{"k":"remove_col","v":{"s":"Remove"}},{"k":"ai_off_while_focused","v":{"s":"AI is off while a focus is active — it reads the full dataset. Choose “Show all” to re-enable it."}},{"k":"thinking","v":{"s":"Thinking…"}},{"k":"generate_ai_reading","v":{"s":"Generate AI reading (hypotheses)"}},{"k":"generate_ai_reword","v":{"s":"Generate AI re-word"}},{"k":"add_external_benchmark","v":{"s":"Add external benchmark (reading-fluency norms):"}},{"k":"add_benchmark_btn","v":{"s":"Add"}},{"k":"benchmark_spine_empty_note","v":{"s":"The built-in norm table ships empty on purpose — a benchmark line renders only after each value is verified against its primary source (see the Benchmark workspace below). Until then, adding one politely refuses rather than showing an unverified number."}},{"k":"iq_hide","v":{"s":"🔬 Hide the “should I trust a trend?” sandbox"}},{"k":"iq_learn","v":{"s":"🔬 Learn: “should I trust a trend?” sandbox"}},{"k":"hypothesis_input","v":{"s":"Evidence trend hypothesis"}},{"k":"explanation_input","v":{"s":"Evidence trend explanation"}},{"k":"footer_privacy_honesty","v":{"s":"Privacy & honesty: the default (Data only) mode fires zero AI — raise the AI ceiling for gated, clearly-marked AI. Exports are FERPA-gated: the brief and the CSV are finding-only unless you opt in to identifiable data, and formal exports require sign-off on any AI reading."}},{"k":"export_presentation_html","v":{"s":"⤓ Export presentation (HTML)"}},{"k":"fullscreen","v":{"s":"⤢ Fullscreen"}},{"k":"exit","v":{"s":"✕ Exit"}}],"id":545}},{"k":"manipulatives","v":{"o":[{"k":"5","v":{"s":"+ 5"}},{"k":"sr_zero_pair_removed_by_drag","v":{"s":"Zero pair removed by drag."}},{"k":"sr_counters_cleared","v":{"s":"Counters cleared"}},{"k":"a11y_manipulative_reasoning_pathway","v":{"s":"Manipulative reasoning pathway"}},{"k":"a11y_done","v":{"s":"Done!"}},{"k":"a11y_whole_number","v":{"s":"Whole number"}},{"k":"a11y_first_part","v":{"s":"First part"}},{"k":"a11y_grade_level","v":{"s":"Grade level"}},{"k":"a11y_abstractness","v":{"s":"Abstractness"}},{"k":"a11y_scaffold_density","v":{"s":"Scaffold density"}},{"k":"a11y_error_tolerance","v":{"s":"Error tolerance"}},{"k":"back","v":{"s":"Back"}},{"k":"math_manipulatives","v":{"s":"🧮 Math Manipulatives"}},{"k":"badges","v":{"s":"Badges"}},{"k":"badges_2","v":{"s":"🏅 Badges"}},{"k":"ai_tutor","v":{"s":"🤖 AI Tutor: "}},{"k":"base_10_blocks","v":{"s":"Base-10 Blocks"}},{"k":"abacus","v":{"s":"Abacus"}},{"k":"slide_rule","v":{"s":"Slide Rule"}},{"k":"quiz","v":{"s":"Quiz"}},{"k":"ten_frames","v":{"s":"Ten Frames"}},{"k":"counters","v":{"s":"Counters"}},{"k":"place_value_disks","v":{"s":"Place-Value Disks"}},{"k":"hundreds_chart","v":{"s":"Hundreds Chart"}},{"k":"pattern_blocks","v":{"s":"Pattern Blocks"}},{"k":"geoboard","v":{"s":"Geoboard"}},{"k":"cuisenaire","v":{"s":"Cuisenaire"}},{"k":"number_bonds","v":{"s":"Number Bonds"}},{"k":"fraction_bars","v":{"s":"Fraction Bars"}},{"k":"algebra_tiles","v":{"s":"Algebra Tiles"}},{"k":"cra_progression","v":{"s":"CRA Progression"}},{"k":"challenge_hub","v":{"s":"Challenge Hub"}},{"k":"brain_teasers","v":{"s":"Brain Teasers"}},{"k":"history","v":{"s":"History"}},{"k":"curriculum_map","v":{"s":"Curriculum Map"}},{"k":"activity_cards","v":{"s":"Activity Cards"}},{"k":"help_faq","v":{"s":"Help & FAQ"}},{"k":"glossary","v":{"s":"Glossary"}},{"k":"standards","v":{"s":"Standards"}},{"k":"library","v":{"s":"Library"}},{"k":"teacher","v":{"s":"Teacher"}},{"k":"math_inquiry","v":{"s":"Math Inquiry"}},{"k":"base_10_blocks_ones_tens_hundreds_thou","v":{"s":"Base-10 Blocks — ones, tens, hundreds, thousands"}},{"k":"the_whole_point_of_place_value_made_ta","v":{"s":"The whole point of place value made TANGIBLE. 10 ones = 1 ten; 10 tens = 1 hundred; 10 hundreds = 1 thousand. Regrouping (carrying / borrowing) becomes obvious when you have to physically swap blocks."}},{"k":"abacus_4_500_years_of_mental_arithmeti","v":{"s":"Abacus — 4,500 years of mental arithmetic"}},{"k":"soroban_japanese_and_suanpan_chinese_a","v":{"s":"Soroban (Japanese) and Suanpan (Chinese) are still taught — advanced users beat calculators on speed for many problems. Each rod is a place value; bead-state IS the number. Concrete → mental in months."}},{"k":"slide_rule_logarithms_in_your_hand","v":{"s":"Slide Rule — logarithms in your hand"}},{"k":"how_engineers_multiplied_before_electr","v":{"s":"How engineers multiplied before electronic calculators: align logarithmic scales, read the answer. Apollo 11 (1969) did orbital math with slide rules. Replaced en masse only after the HP-35 dropped in 1972."}},{"k":"quiz_graded_place_value_arithmetic","v":{"s":"Quiz — graded place-value + arithmetic"}},{"k":"ccss_1_nbt_2_nbt_3_nbt_4_nbt_progressi","v":{"s":"CCSS 1.NBT, 2.NBT, 3.NBT, 4.NBT progression. Mixed concrete-pictorial-abstract sequencing (CPA, Bruner 1966) is the spine of every well-designed elementary math curriculum."}},{"k":"ten_frames_the_k_2_number_sense_workho","v":{"s":"Ten Frames — the K-2 number-sense workhorse"}},{"k":"a_5_by_2_grid_fill_cells_to_show_a_num","v":{"s":"A 5-by-2 grid. Fill cells to show a number. Subitizing (instant recognition without counting) develops here. CCSS K.OA.A.4: the \"what makes 10?\" question is the gateway to all later arithmetic fluency."}},{"k":"two_color_counters_integers_concrete","v":{"s":"Two-Color Counters — integers concrete"}},{"k":"yellow_1_red_1_a_yellow_red_pair_0_a_z","v":{"s":"Yellow = +1; red = -1. A yellow + red pair = 0 (a \"zero pair\"). The most concrete model for understanding negative numbers and integer arithmetic. CCSS 6.NS.C.5, 7.NS.A.1."}},{"k":"place_value_disks_bridge_to_algorithm","v":{"s":"Place-Value Disks — bridge to algorithm"}},{"k":"each_disk_labeled_with_its_value_1_10_","v":{"s":"Each disk labeled with its value (1, 10, 100, 1000). Move 10 disks of one kind to trade for 1 of the next. The conceptual bridge from physical blocks to the standard algorithm. CCSS 4.NBT.B.4."}},{"k":"hundreds_chart_count_pattern_and_skip","v":{"s":"Hundreds Chart — count, pattern, and skip"}},{"k":"a_10x10_grid_of_1_100_click_to_highlig","v":{"s":"A 10x10 grid of 1-100. Click to highlight cells. Skip-count overlays reveal multiplication patterns. CCSS 2.NBT.A.2: skip-counting by 5s, 10s, 100s."}},{"k":"pattern_blocks_fractions_symmetry","v":{"s":"Pattern Blocks — fractions + symmetry"}},{"k":"hexagon_trapezoid_rhombus_triangle_squ","v":{"s":"Hexagon, trapezoid, rhombus, triangle, square, narrow rhombus. 2 trapezoids = 1 hexagon (so 1 trapezoid = 1/2 hex). 3 rhombi = 1 hex (so 1 rhombus = 1/3). 6 triangles = 1 hex (so 1 triangle = 1/6)."}},{"k":"geoboard_polygons_on_a_peg_grid","v":{"s":"Geoboard — polygons on a peg grid"}},{"k":"connect_pegs_with_rubber_bands_to_make","v":{"s":"Connect pegs with \"rubber bands\" to make polygons. Measure perimeter and area. The classic concrete tool for plane geometry and Pick's theorem."}},{"k":"cuisenaire_rods_numbers_in_color","v":{"s":"Cuisenaire Rods — numbers in color"}},{"k":"belgian_teacher_georges_cuisenaire_195","v":{"s":"Belgian teacher Georges Cuisenaire (1952): 10 rods, lengths 1-10, each a different color. Add rods to make new numbers. White=1, red=2, light green=3, purple=4, yellow=5, dark green=6, black=7, brown=8, blue=9, orange=10."}},{"k":"number_bonds_part_part_whole","v":{"s":"Number Bonds — part-part-whole"}},{"k":"the_whole_splits_into_two_parts_singap","v":{"s":"The whole splits into two parts. Singapore Math made this central. CCSS K.OA.A.3: decompose 10 into pairs. This builds toward all addition and subtraction."}},{"k":"fraction_bars_compare_and_add_fraction","v":{"s":"Fraction Bars — compare and add fractions"}},{"k":"equal_length_bars_partitioned_into_hal","v":{"s":"Equal-length bars partitioned into halves, thirds, fourths, sixths, eighths, twelfths. Stack to compare. Find equivalents visually. The cleanest single tool for fraction equivalence (3.NF, 4.NF)."}},{"k":"algebra_tiles_model_expressions_and_eq","v":{"s":"Algebra Tiles — model expressions and equations"}},{"k":"a_tile_for_1_unit_x_variable_x_square_","v":{"s":"A tile for 1 (unit), x (variable), x² (square). Two-color: positive and negative. Model expressions like 2x + 3 or factor quadratics by arranging tiles into rectangles. CCSS 7.EE, 8.EE."}},{"k":"cra_progression_concrete_picture_equat","v":{"s":"CRA Progression — concrete → picture → equation"}},{"k":"bruner_1966_students_master_each_conce","v":{"s":"Bruner (1966): students master each concept by moving through three modes of representation. We step you through the SAME problem in all three ways so the abstract symbol is grounded in a thing you can SEE and TOUCH."}},{"k":"challenge_hub_quick_practice_across_ev","v":{"s":"Challenge Hub — quick practice across every manipulative"}},{"k":"random_problems_spanning_all_12_manipu","v":{"s":"Random problems spanning all 12 manipulatives. Designed for distributed practice (Cepeda et al. 2006): a quick five-minute set, mixing kinds, beats twenty minutes of one kind in a row."}},{"k":"glossary_math_vocabulary_with_examples","v":{"s":"Glossary — math vocabulary, with examples"}},{"k":"vocabulary_is_the_curriculum_a_student","v":{"s":"Vocabulary IS the curriculum. A student who hears \"regroup,\" \"compose,\" \"decompose,\" \"fluently,\" and \"place value\" enough times in context will internalize the system. Definitions are tied to the specific manipulative that demonstrates each."}},{"k":"brain_teasers_classic_math_puzzles","v":{"s":"Brain Teasers — classic math puzzles"}},{"k":"classic_problems_that_are_solvable_sat","v":{"s":"Classic problems that are solvable, satisfying, and often easier with a manipulative in hand. Useful as warm-ups, sponge activities, or anchor tasks for class discussion."}},{"k":"history_math_tools_through_time","v":{"s":"History — math tools through time"}},{"k":"counting_bones_lebombo_35_000_bce_sume","v":{"s":"Counting bones (Lebombo, ~35,000 BCE) → Sumerian tokens → Roman abacus → Cuisenaire rods (1952) → today. Every manipulative in this tool is part of a long lineage of teaching aids."}},{"k":"curriculum_map_which_tool_which_grade","v":{"s":"Curriculum Map — which tool, which grade"}},{"k":"a_k_5_progression_chart_showing_which_","v":{"s":"A K-5 progression chart showing which manipulatives are typically introduced at which grade and which standards they support. Click any cell to open that tool."}},{"k":"activity_cards_printable_lessons","v":{"s":"Activity Cards — printable lessons"}},{"k":"ready_to_print_activity_cards_for_smal","v":{"s":"Ready-to-print activity cards for small-group or whole-class use. Each card names a goal, materials, steps, and an extension question. Designed to be used WITHOUT this app — but you can also walk through them in-app."}},{"k":"help_faq_2","v":{"s":"Help & FAQ"}},{"k":"quick_reference_answers_to_common_stud","v":{"s":"Quick-reference answers to common student and teacher questions, plus keyboard shortcuts, accessibility info, and how to contact AlloFlow support."}},{"k":"ccss_standards_browser","v":{"s":"CCSS Standards Browser"}},{"k":"common_core_state_standards_for_mathem","v":{"s":"Common Core State Standards for Mathematics, K–5. Browse by grade, see which manipulative addresses each standard, and jump straight to it."}},{"k":"library_saved_constructions","v":{"s":"Library — saved constructions"}},{"k":"every_manipulative_s_current_state_can","v":{"s":"Every manipulative’s current state can be named, saved, and reopened later. Useful for setting up class examples in advance, or for students to return to in-progress work."}},{"k":"teacher_dashboard_progress_planning","v":{"s":"Teacher Dashboard — progress + planning"}},{"k":"per_student_progress_badges_earned_mod","v":{"s":"Per-student progress (badges earned, modes visited, streak best, problems solved). Quick lesson-plan templates aligned to CCSS. Export progress as CSV/JSON."}},{"k":"keyframes_b10regroup_0_transform_scale","v":{"s":"@keyframes b10regroup { 0% { transform: scale(1); box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(168,85,247,0.5); } 40% { transform: scale(1.15); box-shadow: 0 0 20px 8px rgba(168,85,247,0.4); } 100% { transform: scale(1); box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(168,85,247,0); } }"}},{"k":"no_blocks","v":{"s":"no blocks"}},{"k":"cube_1000","v":{"s":"■ Cube = 1000"}},{"k":"flat_100","v":{"s":"▬ Flat = 100"}},{"k":"rod_10","v":{"s":"┃ Rod = 10"}},{"k":"unit_1","v":{"s":"▪ Unit = 1"}},{"k":"regroup_ungroup","v":{"s":"⇄ Regroup / Ungroup"}},{"k":"10_of_one_place_value_always_equals_1_","v":{"s":"💡 1