 Ocean with 75% of Earth's volcanoes. The Himalayas grow ~1cm/year as India pushes into Eurasia. The Mid-Atlantic Ridge is pulling Europe and N. America apart at ~2.5cm/year."}},{"k":"plate_encyclopedia","v":{"s":"🌍 Plate Encyclopedia"}},{"k":"complete_catalog_of_earth_tectonic_pla","v":{"s":"Complete catalog of Earth tectonic plates: 7 majors, ~10 minors, and ~50 microplates. Filter by tier or motion. Each plate links to bordering boundaries and notable earthquake or volcanic features."}},{"k":"search_plates_by_name_or_region","v":{"s":"Search plates by name or region..."}},{"k":"major_faults_of_the_world","v":{"s":"Major Faults of the World"}},{"k":"faults_are_where_rocks_slide_past_over","v":{"s":"Faults are where rocks slide past, over, or away from each other. 50 of the most significant fault systems are catalogued here, with type, region, length, and significance."}},{"k":"tsunami_history","v":{"s":"Tsunami History"}},{"k":"tsunamis_are_ocean_waves_triggered_by_","v":{"s":"Tsunamis are ocean waves triggered by earthquakes, volcanoes, landslides, or impacts. 60 events from 365 CE to 2023 are catalogued here. Sort by deaths, magnitude, or year."}},{"k":"no_human_casualties_recorded","v":{"s":"No human casualties recorded"}},{"k":"mantle_plumes_and_hotspots","v":{"s":"Mantle Plumes and Hotspots"}},{"k":"hotspots_are_stationary_heat_sources_i","v":{"s":"Hotspots are stationary heat sources in the mantle. As plates drift over them, they leave volcanic chains: the Hawaiian-Emperor track, the Yellowstone track. 40 hotspots catalogued."}},{"k":"rock_catalog","v":{"s":"Rock Catalog"}},{"k":"rocks_tell_the_story_of_how_the_earth_","v":{"s":"Rocks tell the story of how the Earth assembles itself. 60 rocks span igneous (from magma), sedimentary (from sediments), and metamorphic (transformed by heat and pressure). Filter by group."}},{"k":"fossils_and_evolution_milestones","v":{"s":"Fossils and Evolution Milestones"}},{"k":"40_key_fossils_from_3_5_billion_year_o","v":{"s":"40 key fossils, from 3.5-billion-year-old stromatolites to mammoths in Pleistocene tar. Each marks a step in biological history. Sorted oldest first."}},{"k":"geoscience_careers","v":{"s":"Geoscience Careers"}},{"k":"30_paths_in_the_geosciences_with_educa","v":{"s":"30 paths in the geosciences, with education requirements and outlook. Geology jobs span academia, government (USGS, NPS, EPA, NOAA), industry (oil, mining, environmental consulting), and education."}},{"k":"maine_geology","v":{"s":"Maine Geology"}},{"k":"maine_s_landscape_was_shaped_by_400_mi","v":{"s":"Maine's landscape was shaped by 400 million years of mountain-building and 20,000 years of glacial scouring. 30 specific Maine sites with the rocks and processes that made them."}},{"k":"volcano_catalog","v":{"s":"Volcano Catalog"}},{"k":"over_1500_volcanoes_have_been_active_i","v":{"s":"Over 1500 volcanoes have been active in the last 10,000 years. 60 of the most significant and studied volcanoes are here: subduction-zone strato-volcanoes, hotspot shields, and continental calderas."}},{"k":"search_volcanoes","v":{"s":"Search volcanoes..."}},{"k":"mountain_ranges","v":{"s":"Mountain Ranges"}},{"k":"every_mountain_range_tells_a_tectonic_","v":{"s":"Every mountain range tells a tectonic story: collision (Himalaya, Alps), volcanism (Andes, Cascades), or ancient orogeny (Appalachians, Urals). 50 ranges with peaks and history."}},{"k":"history_of_geology","v":{"s":"History of Geology"}},{"k":"plate_tectonics_was_only_confirmed_in_","v":{"s":"Plate tectonics was only confirmed in the 1960s. Before that, continents were thought to be fixed. The intellectual journey from biblical flood geology to a unifying Earth-system theory took 350 years."}},{"k":"geologist_biographies","v":{"s":"Geologist Biographies"}},{"k":"30_scientists_who_shaped_our_understan","v":{"s":"{n} scientists who shaped our understanding of the Earth, from Steno (1669) to modern researchers. Their personal stories illuminate how the science advanced."}},{"k":"geology_glossary","v":{"s":"Geology Glossary"}},{"k":"quick_reference_for_plate_tectonic_sei","v":{"s":"Quick reference for plate tectonic, seismic, volcanic, and structural terms."}},{"k":"search_glossary","v":{"s":"Search glossary..."}},{"k":"classroom_activities","v":{"s":"Classroom Activities"}},{"k":"30_hands_on_activities_for_teaching_pl","v":{"s":"30 hands-on activities for teaching plate tectonics, designed for K-12 with materials commonly available. Each lists grade level, time, prep, and learning objective."}},{"k":"earthquake_case_studies","v":{"s":"Earthquake Case Studies"}},{"k":"ten_major_historical_earthquakes_in_de","v":{"s":"Ten major historical earthquakes in depth: what happened, what evidence remains, and what we learned. From the 1700 Cascadia event recorded in Japanese orphan tsunami records to modern instrumented megathrusts."}},{"k":"1700_cascadia_m9","v":{"s":"1700 Cascadia M9"}},{"k":"1755_lisbon_m8_7","v":{"s":"1755 Lisbon M8.7"}},{"k":"1811_12_new_madrid","v":{"s":"1811-12 New Madrid"}},{"k":"1857_fort_tejon_m7_9","v":{"s":"1857 Fort Tejon M7.9"}},{"k":"1886_charleston_m7_3","v":{"s":"1886 Charleston M7.3"}},{"k":"1906_san_francisco_m7_9","v":{"s":"1906 San Francisco M7.9"}},{"k":"1923_great_kanto_m7_9","v":{"s":"1923 Great Kanto M7.9"}},{"k":"1933_long_beach_m6_4","v":{"s":"1933 Long Beach M6.4"}},{"k":"1960_valdivia_m9_5","v":{"s":"1960 Valdivia M9.5"}},{"k":"1964_alaska_good_friday_m9_2","v":{"s":"1964 Alaska Good Friday M9.2"}},{"k":"boundary_type","v":{"s":"Boundary type: "}},{"k":"volcano_eruption_case_studies","v":{"s":"Volcano Eruption Case Studies"}},{"k":"ten_devastating_eruptions_from_vesuviu","v":{"s":"Ten devastating eruptions from Vesuvius 79 CE to Hunga Tonga 2022, with phase-by-phase eruption narratives, eyewitness accounts, and modern context."}},{"k":"vesuvius_79_ce","v":{"s":"Vesuvius (79 CE)"}},{"k":"tambora_1815","v":{"s":"Tambora (1815)"}},{"k":"krakatoa_1883","v":{"s":"Krakatoa (1883)"}},{"k":"mt_pe