 with whip tail. Bone wars-era discovery by Marsh."}},{"k":"brontosaurus_genus_reinstated_2015_aft","v":{"s":"Brontosaurus genus reinstated 2015 after century-long synonymy with Apatosaurus."}},{"k":"brachiosaurus","v":{"s":"Brachiosaurus"}},{"k":"late_jurassic_154_153_ma","v":{"s":"Late Jurassic (154-153 Ma)"}},{"k":"western_us_morrison_2","v":{"s":"Western US (Morrison)"}},{"k":"26m_long_50_tonnes_herbivore_with_vert","v":{"s":"26m long, 50 tonnes, herbivore with vertical neck. Front legs longer than back."}},{"k":"first_found_colorado_1900_the_jurassic","v":{"s":"First found Colorado 1900. The 'Jurassic Park' giraffe-necked giant."}},{"k":"diplodocus","v":{"s":"Diplodocus"}},{"k":"late_jurassic_154_152_ma","v":{"s":"Late Jurassic (154-152 Ma)"}},{"k":"western_us_morrison_3","v":{"s":"Western US (Morrison)"}},{"k":"27m_long_12_tonnes_herbivore_with_whip","v":{"s":"27m long, 12 tonnes, herbivore with whip tail. Long but slender."}},{"k":"carnegie_museum_s_famous_dippy_replica","v":{"s":"Carnegie Museum's famous 'Dippy' replicas distributed to museums worldwide."}},{"k":"allosaurus_2","v":{"s":"Allosaurus"}},{"k":"late_jurassic_155_145_ma_2","v":{"s":"Late Jurassic (155-145 Ma)"}},{"k":"western_us_morrison_4","v":{"s":"Western US (Morrison)"}},{"k":"9m_long_1_5_tonnes_bipedal_predator_wi","v":{"s":"9m long, 1.5 tonnes, bipedal predator with serrated 8cm teeth."}},{"k":"cleveland_lloyd_quarry_ut_preserves_46","v":{"s":"Cleveland-Lloyd Quarry (UT) preserves 46 individuals - possible mass death from drought."}},{"k":"ankylosaurus","v":{"s":"Ankylosaurus"}},{"k":"late_cretaceous_68_66_ma_3","v":{"s":"Late Cretaceous (68-66 Ma)"}},{"k":"north_america_hell_creek_2","v":{"s":"North America (Hell Creek)"}},{"k":"8m_long_6_tonnes_herbivore_with_armore","v":{"s":"8m long, 6 tonnes, herbivore with armored back + tail club."}},{"k":"tail_club_may_have_shattered_t_rex_bon","v":{"s":"Tail club may have shattered T. rex bones. Armor included fused osteoderms."}},{"k":"spinosaurus"