vations."}},{"k":"geo_cont_determined_earth_s_age_precisely_lea","v":{"s":"Determined Earth's age precisely. Lead pollution research."}},{"k":"geo_cont_developed_richter_magnitude_scale_19","v":{"s":"Developed Richter magnitude scale (1935)."}},{"k":"geo_cont_developed_seafloor_spreading_theory","v":{"s":"Developed seafloor spreading theory (1962). Helped establish plate tectonics."}},{"k":"geo_cont_director_of_us_geological_survey_mar","v":{"s":"Director of US Geological Survey. Marine geophysics."}},{"k":"geo_cont_discovered_crust_mantle_boundary_moh","v":{"s":"Discovered crust-mantle boundary (Moho)."}},{"k":"geo_cont_discovered_earth_has_solid_inner_cor","v":{"s":"Discovered Earth has solid inner core (1936)."}},{"k":"geo_cont_earth_core_hypothesis_1897","v":{"s":"Earth core hypothesis (1897)."}},{"k":"geo_cont_elastic_rebound_theory_of_earthquake","v":{"s":"Elastic rebound theory of earthquakes."}},{"k":"geo_cont_estimated_earth_s_age_initially_inco","v":{"s":"Estimated Earth's age (initially incorrect - too short)."}},{"k":"geo_cont_father_of_modern_geology_deep_time_c","v":{"s":"Father of modern geology. Deep time concept. Uniformitarianism."}},{"k":"geo_cont_first_accurate_radiometric_dating_of","v":{"s":"First accurate radiometric dating of Earth (~4.5 billion years)."}},{"k":"geo_cont_first_geological_map_of_britain_prin","v":{"s":"First geological map of Britain. Principle of faunal succession."}},{"k":"geo_cont_global_carbon_cycle","v":{"s":"Global carbon cycle."}},{"k":"geo_cont_ice_age_theory_glacial_geology","v":{"s":"Ice age theory. Glacial geology."}},{"k":"geo_cont_independent_co_discovery_of_magnetic","v":{"s":"Independent co-discovery of magnetic stripes."}},{"k":"geo_cont_internal_earth_structure_co_develope","v":{"s":"Internal Earth structure. Co-developed Richter scale."}},{"k":"geo_cont_mapped_mid_atlantic_ridge_discovered","v":{"s":"Mapped Mid-Atlantic Ridge. Discovered rift valley confirming seafloor spreading."}},{"k":"geo_cont_mountain_bu