-Colombia"}},{"k":"quake_sumatra_andaman","v":{"s":"Sumatra-Andaman"}},{"k":"quake_turkey_syria","v":{"s":"Turkey-Syria"}},{"k":"nicolas_steno","v":{"s":"Nicolas Steno"}},{"k":"geo_cont_danish_anatomist_and_bishop_proposed","v":{"s":"Danish anatomist and bishop. Proposed law of superposition (1669). Later beatified by Catholic Church (2002)."}},{"k":"geo_cont_scottish_farmer_physician_geologist_f","v":{"s":"Scottish farmer-physician-geologist. Father of modern geology. Founded uniformitarianism. Siccar Point unconformity his outdoor classroom."}},{"k":"mary_anning","v":{"s":"Mary Anning"}},{"k":"geo_cont_british_fossil_hunter_lyme_regis_fou","v":{"s":"British fossil hunter, Lyme Regis. Found first ichthyosaur, plesiosaur, and pterosaur. Working class woman; excluded from learned societies despite immense contributions."}},{"k":"geo_cont_scottish_lawyer_turned_geologist_prin","v":{"s":"Scottish lawyer-turned-geologist. Principles of Geology was the standard text for decades. Mentor and friend to Darwin."}},{"k":"geo_cont_swiss_american_naturalist_proposed_ic","v":{"s":"Swiss-American naturalist. Proposed ice ages (1837). Founded Harvard Museum of Comparative Zoology. Later opposed Darwin evolution."}},{"k":"geo_cont_british_canal_surveyor_produced_first","v":{"s":"British canal surveyor. Produced first geological map of a nation. Realized fossils correlated strata. Imprisoned for debt despite his contributions."}},{"k":"geo_cont_german_meteorologist_and_polar_explore","v":{"s":"German meteorologist and polar explorer. Proposed continental drift (1912). Died on Greenland ice cap before vindication."}},{"k":"geo_cont_british_geologist_pioneered_radiometr","v":{"s":"British geologist. Pioneered radiometric dating and mantle convection. First accurate age of Earth (1913)."}},{"k":"geo_cont_american_oceanographer_with_bruce_hee","v":{"s":"American oceanographer. With Bruce Heezen, mapped the ocean floor and discovered mid-Atlantic rift. Long uncredited; recognized later in life."}},{"k":"geo_cont_princeton_geologist_and_navy_officer","v":{"s":"Princeton geologist and Navy officer. Proposed seafloor spreading (1962). Discovered Pacific guyots during WWII."}},{"k":"j_tuzo_wilson","v":{"s":"J. Tuzo Wilson"}},{"k":"geo_cont_canadian_geophysicist_defined_transfo","v":{"s":"Canadian geophysicist. Defined transform faults (1965), Wilson Cycle, mantle plumes. Triple international acclaim."}},{"k":"geo_cont_danish_seismologist_discovered_earth","v":{"s":"Danish seismologist. Discovered Earth inner core (1936) from seismic waves. Active in research until age 99."}},{"k":"geo_cont_german_american_seismologist_mantle_c","v":{"s":"German-American seismologist. Mantle-core boundary (Gutenberg discontinuity). Co-author of magnitude scale with Charles Richter."}},{"k":"geo_cont_american_seismologist_created_magnitu","v":{"s":"American seismologist. Created magnitude scale (1935). Caltech."}},{"k":"hiroo_kanamori","v":{"s":"Hiroo Kanamori"}},{"k":"geo_cont_japanese_american_seismologist_caltec","v":{"s":"Japanese-American seismologist (Caltech). Introduced moment magnitude scale that supplanted Richter for large quakes."}},{"k":"lucy_jones","v":{"s":"Lucy Jones"}},{"k":"geo_cont_american_seismologist_usgs_southern_c","v":{"s":"American seismologist. USGS Southern California science advisor. Public science communicator and advocate for disaster preparedness."}},{"k":"susan_hough","v":{"s":"Susan Hough"}},{"k":"geo_cont_usgs_pasadena_seismologist_books_on_t","v":{"s":"USGS Pasadena seismologist. Books on the history and sociology of earthquakes."}},{"k":"roger_bilham","v":{"s":"Roger Bilham"}},{"k":"geo_cont_university_of_colorado_himalayan_seis","v":{"s":"University of Colorado. Himalayan seismic hazard expert. Often comments on India earthquake risk."}},{"k":"brian_atwater","v":{"s":"Brian Atwater"}},{"k":"geo_cont_usgs_paleoseismologist_confirmed_1700","v":{"s":"USGS paleoseismologist. Confirmed 1700 Cascadia earthquake by combining ghost-forest dating and Japanese tsunami records."}},{"k":"kelin_wang","v":{"s":"Kelin Wang"}},{"k":"geo_cont_geological_survey_of_canada_cascadia","v":{"s":"Geological Survey of Canada. Cascadia and Japan subduction modeler. Slow-slip theorist."}},{"k":"robin_lacassin","v":{"s":"Robin Lacassin"}},{"k":"geo_cont_french_geologist_active_tectonics_of","v":{"s":"French geologist. Active tectonics of Asia and Mediterranean."}},{"k":"walter_alvarez","v":{"s":"Walter Alvarez"}},{"k":"geo_cont_uc_berkeley_geologist_with_father_lui","v":{"s":"UC Berkeley geologist. With father Luis, found iridium spike at K-Pg = asteroid evidence (1980)."}},{"k":"florence_bascom","v":{"s":"Florence Bascom"}},{"k":"geo_cont_first_woman_to_earn_phd_in_geology_in","v":{"s":"First woman to earn PhD in geology in US (Johns Hopkins, 1893). USGS geologist. Trained generation of women geologists at Bryn Mawr."}},{"k":"ann_whittall_boutwell","v":{"s":"Ann Whittall Boutwell"}},{"k":"geo_cont_usgs_field_geologist_surveyed_western","v":{"s":"USGS field geologist; surveyed Western US copper districts."}},{"k":"mary_lyell","v":{"s":"Mary Lyell"}},{"k":"geo_cont_british_geologist_wife_and_research_p","v":{"s":"British geologist. Wife and research partner of Charles Lyell. Field notebooks and conchology contributions; long unattributed."}},{"k":"sue_hendrickson","v":{"s":"Sue Hendrickson"}},{"k":"geo_cont_american_fossil_collector_discovered","v":{"s":"American fossil collector. Discovered T. rex Sue, the most complete T. rex ever found, now at Field Museum Chicago."}},{"k":"robert_hazen","v":{"s":"Robert Hazen"}},{"k":"geo_cont_carnegie_institution_mineral_evolutio","v":{"s":"Carnegie Institution. Mineral evolution and origin of life chemistry. Coined mineral evolution: most minerals younger than life."}},{"k":"marjorie_sweeting","v":{"s":"Marjorie Sweeting"}},{"k":"geo_cont_british_karst_geomorphologist_oxford","v":{"s":"British karst geomorphologist. Oxford geographer; queen of karst."}},{"k":"bertha_lewis","v":{"s":"Bertha Lewis"}},{"k":"geo_cont_african_american_geologist_early_howa","v":{"s":"African American geologist; early Howard University faculty; broke barriers in segregated era."}},{"k":"mei_po_kwan","v":{"s":"Mei-Po Kwan"}},{"k":"geo_cont_asian_american_geographer_and_geomorph","v":{"s":"Asian-American geographer and geomorphologist. GIS leadership; bridges geo and social science."}},{"k":"bd_proc_magma_rises_new_crust_forms","v":{"s":"Magma rises + new crust forms"}},{"k":"bd_feat_mid_ocean_ridges_mid_atlantic_ridge","v":{"s":"Mid-ocean ridges (Mid-Atlantic Ridge); East African Rift"}},{"k":"bd_haza_shallow_earthquakes_ridge_volcanism","v":{"s":"Shallow earthquakes; ridge volcanism; new oceanic crust; rift valleys"}},{"k":"bd_proc_denser_plate_subducts_under_younger","v":{"s":"Denser plate subducts under younger"}},{"k":"bd_feat_volcanic_island_arcs_ocean_trenches","v":{"s":"Volcanic island arcs + ocean trenches"}},{"k":"bd_haza_deep_earthquakes_wadati_benioff_zone","v":{"s":"Deep earthquakes (Wadati-Benioff zone); explosive volcanism; deep trenches"}},{"k":"bd_proc_oceanic_subducts_under_continental","v":{"s":"Oceanic subducts under continental"}},{"k":"bd_feat_coastal_mountain_ranges_volcanic_arc","v":{"s":"Coastal mountain ranges + volcanic arcs + trenches"}},{"k":"bd_haza_mountain_building_andesite_volcanoes","v":{"s":"Mountain building, andesite volcanoes, megathrust earthquakes"}},{"k":"bd_proc_neither_subducts_crumple_thicken","v":{"s":"Neither subducts - crumple + thicken"}},{"k":"bd_feat_mountain_belts_plateaus","v":{"s":"Mountain belts + plateaus"}},{"k":"bd_haza_thickened_crust_intermediate_depth_ea","v":{"s":"Thickened crust, intermediate-depth earthquakes, no volcanism (mostly)"}},{"k":"bd_proc_no_crust_created_or_destroyed","v":{"s":"No crust created or destroyed"}},{"k":"bd_feat_strike_slip_faults","v":{"s":"Strike-slip faults"}},{"k":"bd_haza_shallow_strike_slip_earthquakes_no_vo","v":{"s":"Shallow strike-slip earthquakes; no volcanism; lateral displacement"}},{"k":"boundary_types_in_detail","v":{"s":"Boundary Types in Detail"}},{"k":"the_table_above_names_the_motions_the","v":{"s":"The table above names the motions. These five say what each one builds, where you can go and see it, and what it hands the people who live there."}},{"k":"bd_l_how_it_works","v":{"s":"How it works"}},{"k":"bd_l_what_it_builds","v":{"s":"What it builds"}},{"k":"bd_l_where_to_see_it","v":{"s":"Where to see it"}},{"k":"bd_l_what_it_does_to_people","v":{"s":"What it does to people"}}],"id":563}},{"k":"playlab","v":{"o":[{"k":"sr_trading_card_export_cancelled","v":{"s":"Trading card export cancelled."}},{"k":"sr_enter_a_player_name_to_create_the_trading_card","v":{"s":"Enter a player name to create the trading card."}},{"k":"sr_player_positions_reset_to_preset","v":{"s":"Player positions reset to preset."}},{"k":"sr_please_give_the_play_a_name","v":{"s":"Please give the play a name."}},{"k":"sr_deleted_saved_play","v":{"s":"Deleted saved play."}},{"k":"sr_coach_is_offline","v":{"s":"Coach is offline."}},{"k":"sr_daily_challenge_already_complete_come_back_tomorr","v":{"s":"Daily Challenge already complete. Come back tomorrow."}},{"k":"sr_drill_stopped","v":{"s":"Drill stopped."}},{"k":"sr_saved_play_kept","v":{"s":"Saved play kept."}},{"k":"a11y_visible_overlays","v":{"s":"Visible overlays"}},{"k":"close_scenario_intro","v":{"s":"Close scenario intro"}},{"k":"the_story","v":{"s":"📜 The story"}},{"k":"try_these_before_you_run_it","v":{"s":"🤔 Try these before you run it"}},{"k":"run_it_now","v":{"s":"▶ Run it now"}},{"k":"explore_the_field_first","v":{"s":"🔧 Explore the field first"}},{"k":"play_added_to_your_catalog","v":{"s":"Play added to your catalog"}},{"k":"back_to_stem_lab","v":{"s":"Back to STEAM Lab"}},{"k":"back","v":{"s":"← Back"}},{"k":"every_play_is_a_coordinated_math_probl","v":{"s":"Every play is a coordinated math problem on a fixed grid."}},{"k":"play_catalog","v":{"s":"Play Catalog"}},{"k":"sport","v":{"s":"Sport"}},{"k":"a