","v":{"s":"Modern + NPR"}},{"k":"overview_71","v":{"s":"Overview"}},{"k":"seed_catalogs","v":{"s":"Seed catalogs"}},{"k":"gardening_books","v":{"s":"Gardening books"}},{"k":"gardening_magazines","v":{"s":"Gardening magazines"}},{"k":"overview_72","v":{"s":"Overview"}},{"k":"methods","v":{"s":"Methods"}},{"k":"famous_cases","v":{"s":"Famous cases"}},{"k":"modern_digital_11","v":{"s":"Modern + digital"}},{"k":"overview_73","v":{"s":"Overview"}},{"k":"library_binding_standards","v":{"s":"Library binding standards"}},{"k":"conservation","v":{"s":"Conservation"}},{"k":"modern_10","v":{"s":"Modern"}},{"k":"overview_74","v":{"s":"Overview"}},{"k":"founding_kelmscott","v":{"s":"Founding (Kelmscott)"}},{"k":"major_presses","v":{"s":"Major presses"}},{"k":"modern_fine_press","v":{"s":"Modern fine press"}},{"k":"overview_75","v":{"s":"Overview"}},{"k":"community_cookbooks","v":{"s":"Community cookbooks"}},{"k":"vegan_vegetarian","v":{"s":"Vegan + vegetarian"}},{"k":"bbq_grilling","v":{"s":"BBQ + grilling"}},{"k":"maine_cookbooks","v":{"s":"Maine cookbooks"}},{"k":"overview_76","v":{"s":"Overview"}},{"k":"audubon_19th_c","v":{"s":"Audubon + 19th c."}},{"k":"field_guides","v":{"s":"Field guides"}},{"k":"modern_digital_12","v":{"s":"Modern + digital"}},{"k":"built_for_aaron_pomeranz_s_may_12_2026","v":{"s":"Built for Aaron Pomeranz's May 12, 2026 demo at King Middle School (Portland, Maine). Focused on Gutenberg-era European print: press mechanism, type-setting, casting type, print run economics, before-and-after timeline, typography today, the people behind the press, broadside builder, the \"same fears\" parallel (1450 anti-print fears vs modern anti-internet fears), a day in the print shop, cumulative quiz, AI ask-the-printer, resources. ~9,200 lines."}},{"k":"after_the_king_middle_demo_the_tool_wa","v":{"s":"After the King Middle demo, the tool was substantially expanded to cover print culture globally + broadly. Twelve waves of module additions across about 80 new modules: non-Western printing (Korea + China + Japan + Islamic World + India + Africa + Pre-Columbian Americas), paper making, bookbinding, censorship, first newspapers, apprenticeships, type foundry workshop, Maine printers, music printing, maps + atlases, children's books, scientific publishing, letterpress today, press variants through time, the Reformation print war, color printing history, books that changed the world, print + revolution, the book as object, ink + press materials, translation + translators, print + propaganda, comics + graphic novels, the future of print, famous print shops tour, print + religion beyond Bibles, print + education, print + money (security printing), the library through history, the modern magazine, encyclopedias, dictionaries, cookbooks (mainstream + subcultures), self-help + how-to, paper sustainability, the newspaper comic strip, print + war, famous bookbinders, Maine authors, print + tourism, print + healthcare, font identification quiz, postage + direct mail, print + sports, print + architecture, print + law, romance novels, sci-fi + fantasy, mystery + crime fiction, manga deep dive, photography books, zines + fanzines, famous forgeries + fakes, manuscripts + calligraphy, bookplates + marginalia, the used book trade, the library card catalog, diaries + journals, tarot + oracle decks, pulp fiction era, pamphlets + tracts, greeting cards + ephemera, the memoir tradition, print + sound, the printed sermon, spelling + word puzzles, print + cinema, print + astronomy, beauty + fashion magazines, travel literature, print + mathematics, print advertising history, webcomics deep dive, the picture book craft, poetry magazines, pulp cover art, print + radio, print + gardening, forensic document examination, the library bindery, the fine press tradition, cookbook subcultures, print + natural history."}},{"k":"printingpress_is_part_of_alloflow_crea","v":{"s":"PrintingPress is part of AlloFlow, created by Dr. Aaron Pomeranz (school psychologist) for accessible + universal-design-for-learning-aligned educational tools. The tool serves K-12 + adult learners studying print history, typography, book arts, publishing, + adjacent cultural fields. The tool is open-source within the AlloFlow ecosystem + freely available to educators + students."}},{"k":"quick_reference_for_vocabulary_used_th","v":{"s":"Quick reference for vocabulary used throughout the tool. Filter by typing."}},{"k":"filter_terms_e_g_serif_binding_ink","v":{"s":"Filter terms (e.g., \"serif\", \"binding\", \"ink\")"}},{"k":"optimal_typography","v":{"s":"Optimal typography"}},{"k":"all_four_dimensions_in_the_historical_","v":{"s":"All four dimensions in the historical sweet spot. Reader can sustain long sessions without fatigue."}},{"k":"readable","v":{"s":"Readable"}},{"k":"generally_fine_one_parameter_is_subopt","v":{"s":"Generally fine. One parameter is suboptimal but compensated by the others."}},{"k":"uncomfortable","v":{"s":"Uncomfortable"}},{"k":"multiple_dimensions_are_off_reader_wil","v":{"s":"Multiple dimensions are off. Reader will tire quickly. Sales-killer for a book."}},{"k":"eye_strain","v":{"s":"Eye strain"}},{"k":"active_discomfort_causes_saccade_error","v":{"s":"Active discomfort. Causes saccade errors, mis-reading, headaches. Drops comprehension by 20-40%."}},{"k":"unreadable_in_practice","v":{"s":"Unreadable in practice"}},{"k":"reader_gives_up_the_text_physically_ex","v":{"s":"Reader gives up. The text physically exists but does not function."}},{"k":"typography_inquiry_predict_the_legibil","v":{"s":"🔬 Typography Inquiry — Predict the Legibility"}},{"k":"set_type_size_line_length_leading_pape","v":{"s":"Set type size, line length, leading, paper contrast. Predict where the layout lands on the legibility curve. No score, no reveal."}},{"k":"size","v":{"s":"Size"}},{"k":"length","v":{"s":"Length"}},{"k":"leading","v":{"s":"Leading"}},{"k":"contrast","v":{"s":"Contrast"}},{"k":"type_size_pt","v":{"s":"Type size (pt)"}},{"k":"line_length_chars","v":{"s":"Line length (chars)"}},{"k":"leading_multiplier","v":{"s":"Leading (multiplier)"}},{"k":"paper_contrast","v":{"s":"Paper contrast"}},{"k":"log_this_layout","v":{"s":"📋 Log this layout"}},{"k":"reset_2","v":{"s":"Reset"}},{"k":"menu_2","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"your_hypothesis_which_slider_drops_leg","v":{"s":"Your hypothesis (which slider drops legibility fastest? Why?)"}},{"k":"e_g_line_length_matters_most_because_s","v":{"s":"e.g., line length matters most because saccades break down past ~80 chars..."}},{"k":"i_m_stuck_show_open_questions","v":{"s":"🤔 I'm stuck — show open questions"}},{"k":"open_questions_no_answer_key","v":{"s":"Open questions (no answer key)"}},{"k":"why_is_the_optimal_line_length_65_char","v":{"s":"Why is the optimal line length ~65 characters (Tschichold, Bringhurst)?"}},{"k":"how_does_this_change_for_screen_vs_pri","v":{"s":"How does this change for screen vs print? For dyslexic readers?"}},{"k":"gutenberg_used_11_point_text_with_1_4_","v":{"s":"Gutenberg used 11-point text with 1.4 leading on cream paper. Why did that work for 30+ million Bibles printed by 1500?"}},{"k":"a_children_s_picture_book_uses_22pt_wi","v":{"s":"A children's picture book uses 22pt with 1.7 leading. Why so different from an adult novel?"}},{"k":"i_can_explain_why_this_typography_comb","v":{"s":"I can explain why this typography combination yields this legibility state."}},{"k":"explain_in_your_own_words","v":{"s":"Explain in your own words..."}},{"k":"inquiry_widget_no_score_no_reveal_no_a","v":{"s":"Inquiry widget — no score, no reveal, no answer dump. Legibility heuristics from Tschichold, Bringhurst, Tinker; real reading rates also depend on typeface design, reader age, content density, and lighting."}},{"k":"composed_and_pressed_by_hand_at_the_al","v":{"s":"Composed and pressed by hand at the AlloFlow PrintingPress · Mainz 1455 in spirit · MMXXVI"}},{"k":"printingpress_error","v":{"s":"PrintingPress error: "}},{"k":"mirror_word_answer_label","v":{"s":"Readable version of the mirror-reversed type"}},{"k":"restart_confirmation_title","v":{"s":"Restart this role-play?"}},{"k":"restart_confirmation_message","v":{"s":"Your current role-play progress and choices will be lost."}},{"k":"cancel","v":{"s":"Cancel"}},{"k":"role_play_restarted","v":{"s":"Role-play restarted"}},{"k":"clear_history_confirmation_title","v":{"s":"Clear saved AI answers?"}},{"k":"clear_history_confirmation_message","v":{"s":"This permanently removes every saved question and answer from this activity."}},{"k":"history_cleared","v":{"s":"History cleared"}},{"k":"dry_rag_weight_slider_label","v":{"s":"Dry rag weight in pounds"}},{"k":"paper_parchment_cost_table_caption","v":{"s":"Historical paper and parchment prices, 1300-1500"}},{"k":"fold_diagram_accessible_label","v":{"s":"Fold-to-size diagram for"}},{"k":"target_page_count_slider_label","v":{"s":"Target page count"}},{"k":"custom_letter_preview_accessible_label","v":{"s":"Custom letter M preview"}},{"k":"letter_anatomy_diagram_accessible_label","v":{"s":"Annotated word type showing the ascender on t, descenders on y and p, x-height on e, cap-height, baseline, and descender line."}},{"k":"x_height_slider_label","v":{"s":"typeface x-height"}},{"k":"weight_slider_label","v":{"s":"typeface weight"}},{"k":"contrast_slider_label","v":{"s":"typeface stroke contrast"}},{"k":"width_slider_label","v":{"s":"typeface width"}},{"k":"glossary_filter_label","v":{"s":"Filter print glossary terms"}},{"k":"explanation_label","v":{"s":"Explain why this typography combination produces the current legibility result"}},{"k":"1450_fear","v":{"s":"1450 fear"}},{"k":"a_1500_scholar_argues_that_printed_boo","v":{"s":"A 1500 scholar argues that printed books are inferior to manuscript copies because printers cut corners on accuracy. A 2026 scholar argues the same thing about AI-generated text. What do these two arguments share, and what makes them different?"}},{"k":"a_240_year_chain","v":{"s":". A 240-year chain."}},{"k":"a_competing_shop_in_strasbourg_offers_","v":{"s":"A competing shop in Strasbourg offers to merge with yours — combined capital, shared apprentices, larger market. You lose autonomy but gain scale."}},{"k":"a_composite_letter_drawn_from_survivin","v":{"s":"A composite letter drawn from surviving 1500s apprentice letters in family archives. The legal contract above is the official voice; this is the apprentice's own."}},{"k":"a_handful_of_facts_that_did_not_fit_th","v":{"s":"A handful of facts that did not fit the main stories above, but are too good not to know."}},{"k":"a_page_comes_out_smudged_the_composito","v":{"s":"A page comes out smudged. The compositor blames the tympan; the master suspects the spacing in the forme. You can feel by hand which is true. Naming the compositor as the cause damages a colleague."}},{"k":"a_quick_4_question_quiz_pick_the_answe","v":{"s":"A quick 4-question quiz. Pick the answer that feels truest to you, even if more than one fits. At the end you will see which 1450-1750 printer you most resemble — and what modern roles that maps to."}},{"k":"a_real_shop_kept_its_mark_for_generati","v":{"s":"A real shop kept its mark for generations. The Estiennes used the olive tree for over 100 years across three printer-generations. Your mark would have appeared on every book your shop made."}},{"k":"a_rival_shop_in_cologne_poaches_your_a","v":{"s":"A rival shop in Cologne poaches your apprentice mid-job with better pay. Your typesetting pace drops 30%. The Bible commission is due in two weeks."}},{"k":"a_student_asks_why_the_abbreviation_lb","v":{"s":"A student asks why the abbreviation \"lb\" is used for \"pound.\" What does typography history have to do with the answer?"}},{"k":"a_student_says_gutenberg_invented_the_","v":{"s":"A student says \"Gutenberg invented the printing press all by himself.\" What is a more historically accurate framing?"}},{"k":"a_typo_is_discovered_on_page_23_of_the","v":{"s":"A typo is discovered on page 23 of the Bible — already printed in 200 copies. Reprinting page 23 means re-setting and re-pressing 200 sheets. Errata slip (a printed correction tucked inside the book) is cheap but sloppy."}},{"k":"a_wealthy_patron_changes_the_order_the","v":{"s":"A wealthy patron changes the order: they want the dedication page set in italic instead of Roman. Your shop has no italic punches. Buying punches takes weeks; the patron expects delivery in three days."}},{"k":"a_wealthy_patron_offers_to_fund_a_cust","v":{"s":"A wealthy patron offers to fund a custom italic type set for your shop, in exchange for a 5-year exclusive on a single epic project — printing a complete Cicero in italic. It is a major investment of artistic capacity."}},{"k":"a_working_day_in_a_1455_print_shop_ran","v":{"s":"A working day in a 1455 print shop ran roughly dawn to dusk, with the highest-skill work in the bright morning hours when daylight made composing and casting easier. The diagram below tracks a representative day."}},{"k":"a_youth_of_twelve_years_to_be_his_appr","v":{"s":", a youth of twelve years, to be his apprentice in the art and "}},{"k":"accept_the_deal","v":{"s":"Accept the deal."}},{"k":"accept_the_recognition_you_earned_it","v":{"s":"Accept the recognition. You earned it."}},{"k":"ad_fontes_the_greek_before_the_latin_t","v":{"s":"“Ad fontes. The Greek before the Latin, the Latin before its copies — and let the press carry the original to every desk in Europe at once.”"}},{"k":"adrian_johns_the_nature_of_the_book_pr_2","v":{"s":"Adrian Johns, \"The Nature of the Book: Print and Knowledge in the Making\" (1998)"}},{"k":"ai_generated_round_2","v":{"s":"🤖 AI-generated round"}},{"k":"ai_generated_round_3","v":{"s":"🤖 AI-generated round"}},{"k":"aldine_books_were_bestsellers_across_e","v":{"s":"Aldine books were bestsellers across Europe in the 1500s. Lyonnaise and Venetian rivals copied the mark and sold lower-quality knockoffs. Aldus printed a small pamphlet describing the precise proportions of his mark so buyers could check for themselves. The first published anti-counterfeiting guide."}},{"k":"aldine_italic","v":{"s":"Aldine italic"}},{"k":"aldine_press_scholarship_yale_beinecke","v":{"s":"Aldine Press scholarship — Yale Beinecke Library"}},{"k":"aldus_had_a_dolphin_and_anchor_plantin","v":{"s":"Aldus had a dolphin and anchor. Plantin had a compass. Estienne had an olive tree. What would yours be? Pick a symbol that means something to you, choose a motto, and pick the finish. The result is YOUR mark, the way a 1500 printer would have signed every book they made."}},{"k":"aldus_manutius","v":{"s":"Aldus Manutius"}},{"k":"aldus_manutius_2","v":{"s":"Aldus Manutius"}},{"k":"anchor","v":{"s":"Anchor"}},{"k":"and_at_the_end_of_the_term_one_new_sui","v":{"s":", and at the end of the term one new suit of clothes "}},{"k":"and_entered_into_the_city_book_by_the_","v":{"s":", and entered into the city book by the clerk this day."}},{"k":"andrew_pettegree_the_invention_of_news","v":{"s":"Andrew Pettegree, \"The Invention of News\" (2014)"}},{"k":"ann_m_blair_too_much_to_know_managing_","v":{"s":"Ann M. Blair, \"Too Much to Know: Managing Scholarly Information Before the Modern Age\" (2010)"}},{"k":"apprentice_and_later_partner_in_mainz_","v":{"s":"Apprentice and later partner in Mainz. Skilled scribe before he ever set type."}},{"k":"apprentice_in_the_shop_of_master_heinr","v":{"s":"Apprentice in the shop of Master Heinrich the printer, Mainz"}},{"k":"apprentice_paths","v":{"s":"apprentice paths"}},{"k":"apprentice_year_1","v":{"s":"Apprentice (Year 1)"}},{"k":"apprenticeship_was_a_legal_contract_no","v":{"s":"Apprenticeship was a legal contract, not a handshake. The text below is a composite drawn from documented 1450-1500 European print-shop apprenticeship contracts (city archives in Frankfurt, Cologne, and Lyon). Names and a few terms are normalized for readability. Annotations on the right explain the period vocabulary."}},{"k":"approximate_top_down_floor_plan_of_a_1","v":{"s":"Approximate top-down floor plan of a 1455 Mainz workshop. A typical shop was about the size of a two-car garage. Light entered through tall windows; the press sat in the working bay; type cases lined the bright wall."}},{"k":"ask_the_master_to_inspect_it_together_","v":{"s":"Ask the master to inspect it together — let him diagnose."}},{"k":"benjamin_franklin","v":{"s":"Benjamin Franklin"}},{"k":"benjamin_franklin_2","v":{"s":"Benjamin Franklin"}},{"k":"benjamin_franklin_ran_away_from_his_ap","v":{"s":"Benjamin Franklin ran away from his apprenticeship at age 17."}},{"k":"better_paper_supply_chain_direct_relat","v":{"s":"Better paper supply chain — direct relationship with a mill."}},{"k":"blackletter_3","v":{"s":"Blackletter"}},{"k":"bodoni_4","v":{"s":"Bodoni"}},{"k":"british_library_bodleian_broadside_bal","v":{"s":"British Library — Bodleian Broadside Ballads"}},{"k":"british_library_early_printers_exhibit","v":{"s":"British Library — Early printers exhibition"}},{"k":"buy_more_type_open_a_second_press_line","v":{"s":"Buy more type — open a second press line."}},{"k":"by_master_heinrich_by_wilhelm_the_coop","v":{"s":" by Master Heinrich, by Wilhelm the cooper (the apprentice's father, acting for him), and by "}},{"k":"caslon_4","v":{"s":"Caslon"}},{"k":"charlotte_guillard","v":{"s":"Charlotte Guillard"}},{"k":"charlotte_guillard_biography_biblioth_","v":{"s":"Charlotte Guillard biography — Bibliothèque nationale de France"}},{"k":"charlotte_guillard_outlived_two_husban","v":{"s":"Charlotte Guillard outlived two husbands (both printers) and ran her shop for 40 years."}},{"k":"circular_diagram_of_a_1455_print_shop_","v":{"s":"Circular diagram of a 1455 print-shop working day"}},{"k":"classical_corner_fleurons","v":{"s":"Classical (corner fleurons)"}},{"k":"comic_sans_is_widely_mocked_online","v":{"s":"Comic Sans is widely mocked online."}},{"k":"common_sense_1776","v":{"s":"Common Sense (1776)"}},{"k":"common_sense_2","v":{"s":"Common Sense"}},{"k":"compass","v":{"s":"Compass"}},{"k":"composed_in_printingpress","v":{"s":"Composed in PrintingPress · "}},{"k":"compositor","v":{"s":"Compositor"}},{"k":"compositor_year_5","v":{"s":"Compositor (Year 5)"}},{"k":"consequence","v":{"s":"Consequence"}},{"k":"copper","v":{"s":"Copper"}},{"k":"counter_offer_3_year_exclusive_you_ret","v":{"s":"Counter-offer: 3-year exclusive, you retain rights to also print other italic works."}},{"k":"crew_manifesto","v":{"s":"Crew manifesto"}},{"k":"cumberland_gazette_1786_eastern_argus_","v":{"s":"Cumberland Gazette (1786), Eastern Argus (1803), and on to the modern "}},{"k":"daylight_was_the_constraint_that_shape","v":{"s":"Daylight was the constraint that shaped the day. Bright-hour activities (composing, casting) got the morning; lower-precision work (pressing, drying, hauling) got the afternoon. This pattern stayed roughly the same in print shops for 400 years, until gas lighting (1820s) and then electric (1880s) freed the workday from the sun."}},{"k":"decline_keep_your_shop_generalist","v":{"s":"Decline. Keep your shop generalist."}},{"k":"decline_stay_independent","v":{"s":"Decline. Stay independent."}},{"k":"desiderius_erasmus","v":{"s":"Desiderius Erasmus"}},{"k":"discussion_hint","v":{"s":"Discussion hint: "}},{"k":"discussion_modern_internships_and_trad","v":{"s":"Discussion: Modern internships and trade apprenticeships still inherit pieces of this structure — the term-of-service, the credential at the end, the implicit \"no moonlighting.\" What stays the same; what has changed; what should change?"}},{"k":"documents_the_information_overload_arg","v":{"s":"Documents the information-overload arguments from 1500-1700."}},{"k":"double_rule","v":{"s":"Double rule"}},{"k":"dove_branch","v":{"s":"Dove + branch"}},{"k":"drying_lines","v":{"s":"Drying lines"}},{"k":"dunlap_declaration_broadside","v":{"s":"Dunlap Declaration broadside"}},{"k":"emancipation_proclamation","v":{"s":"Emancipation Proclamation"}},{"k":"end_of_day","v":{"s":"End of day"}},{"k":"eric_foner_tom_paine_and_revolutionary","v":{"s":"Eric Foner, \"Tom Paine and Revolutionary America\" (1976)"}},{"k":"every_serious_shop_had_a_mark_called_a","v":{"s":"Every serious shop had a mark, called a \"device\" or colophon. It went on the title page and the last page. It signaled who printed the book, which mattered when (a) buyers wanted quality and (b) authorities wanted accountability. The dolphin-and-anchor was so successful Aldus Manutius spent half his career suing counterfeiters."}},{"k":"explicit_historical_parallels_between_","v":{"s":"Explicit historical parallels between print and modern social media."}},{"k":"falmouth_district_of_maine_january_1_1","v":{"s":"Falmouth, District of Maine · January 1, 1785"}},{"k":"falmouth_gazette_1785_reproduction","v":{"s":"Falmouth Gazette (1785) reproduction"}},{"k":"falmouth_gazette_and_weekly_advertiser_2","v":{"s":"Falmouth Gazette and Weekly Advertiser"}},{"k":"festina_lente_make_haste_but_slowly_a_","v":{"s":"“Festina lente — make haste, but slowly. A pocket book that pirates copy is still my book.”"}},{"k":"field_trip","v":{"s":"Field trip"}},{"k":"finish","v":{"s":"Finish"}},{"k":"fit_for_a_journeyman","v":{"s":"fit for a journeyman"}},{"k":"floral_vine","v":{"s":"Floral vine"}},{"k":"fore_street_falmouth_now_portland_bloc","v":{"s":"Fore Street, Falmouth (now Portland). Block walkable today from King Middle."}},{"k":"form_a_partnership_instead_of_merging_","v":{"s":"Form a partnership instead of merging — shared contracts, separate ownership."}},{"k":"foundational_scholarly_account_of_how_","v":{"s":"Foundational scholarly account of how printed accuracy and authority were socially constructed."}},{"k":"from_this_day","v":{"s":" from this day."}},{"k":"generate_a_new_ai_quote","v":{"s":"Generate a new AI quote"}},{"k":"generate_a_new_ai_typeface_round","v":{"s":"Generate a new AI typeface round"}},{"k":"generate_a_new_ai_typeface_round_2","v":{"s":"Generate a new AI typeface round"}},{"k":"gold","v":{"s":"Gold"}},{"k":"goldsmith_and_financier_sued_his_colla","v":{"s":"Goldsmith and financier. Sued his collaborator."}},{"k":"gutenberg_came_from_the_family_estate_","v":{"s":"\"Gutenberg\" came from the family estate \"zum Gutenberg\" in Mainz. Johannes Gensfleisch zur Laden zum Gutenberg is the full name. We remember the street he lived on, not his birth name."}},{"k":"gutenberg_s_actual_surname_was_gensfle","v":{"s":"Gutenberg's actual surname was Gensfleisch."}},{"k":"hammer_book","v":{"s":"Hammer + book"}},{"k":"help_sort_the_type_silently_do_not_say","v":{"s":"Help sort the type silently. Do not say who dropped it."}},{"k":"helvetica_4","v":{"s":"Helvetica"}},{"k":"hire_a_replacement_immediately_even_if","v":{"s":"Hire a replacement immediately, even if less skilled."}},{"k":"his_older_brother_james_was_a_boston_p","v":{"s":"His older brother James was a Boston printer who took Ben on as an apprentice at age 12. Five years in, Ben fled to Philadelphia rather than finish the term. The legal apprenticeship contract he broke is the same kind of contract you read above. He spent the rest of his life as a printer first and a politician second."}},{"k":"householder_of_this_city_has_taken_int","v":{"s":", householder of this city, has taken into his service "}},{"k":"i_write_to_you_in_my_own_hand_which_th","v":{"s":"I write to you in my own hand, which the Master says shows promise, though my fingers still ache from the cold of the morning. The shop is busy with the Bible. I have not seen any of the printed pages up close; the apprentices are not yet trusted to touch them. But I see them stacked under cloth in the back room. There must be thousands. The Master's shop has more books in it now than any cathedral library I have ever heard of."}},{"k":"if_the_apprentice_runs_away","v":{"s":"If the apprentice runs away"}},{"k":"in_your_school_context_which_signals_i","v":{"s":" in your school context? Which signals \"I am being playful?\" Where did you learn that?"}},{"k":"index_librorum_prohibitorum_catholic_c","v":{"s":"Index Librorum Prohibitorum (Catholic Church, 1559-1966)"}},{"k":"ink_supply_is_running_low_sending_the_","v":{"s":"Ink supply is running low. Sending the apprentice to the supplier is risky (he might get the wrong kind, as he did last month). Stopping the press is expensive. Going yourself means abandoning the platen for an hour."}},{"k":"ink_table","v":{"s":"Ink table"}},{"k":"insert_a_printed_errata_slip_in_the_fr","v":{"s":"Insert a printed errata slip in the front matter."}},{"k":"it_is_also_one_of_the_most_readable_fo","v":{"s":" It is also one of the most readable fonts for people with dyslexia. Does that change how you think about it?"}},{"k":"johann_fust","v":{"s":"Johann Fust"}},{"k":"johannes_gutenberg","v":{"s":"Johannes Gutenberg"}},{"k":"johannes_gutenberg_2","v":{"s":"Johannes Gutenberg"}},{"k":"jost_hochuli_detail_in_typography","v":{"s":"Jost Hochuli, \"Detail in Typography\""}},{"k":"junior_role_on_a_real_team_the_senior_","v":{"s":"Junior role on a real team. The senior staff are your masters; the work is real but supervised."}},{"k":"kitchen_prep_cook","v":{"s":"Kitchen prep cook"}},{"k":"konrad","v":{"s":"Konrad"}},{"k":"konrad_describes_a_small_burn_and_drop","v":{"s":"Konrad describes a \"small burn\" and dropping a tray. How does he treat these incidents? What does that say about workplace norms?"}},{"k":"konrad_describes_reading_a_full_line_o","v":{"s":"Konrad describes reading a full line of mirror-reversed type as a milestone. In a 2026 trade apprenticeship (electrical, plumbing, etc.), what would the equivalent \"I did the hard thing once\" milestone be?"}},{"k":"konrad_son_of_wilhelm_the_cooper","v":{"s":"Konrad, son of Wilhelm the cooper"}},{"k":"lab_or_shop_intern","v":{"s":"Lab or shop intern"}},{"k":"library_of_congress_american_broadside","v":{"s":"Library of Congress — American Broadsides Collection"}},{"k":"lighthouse","v":{"s":"Lighthouse"}},{"k":"maine_historical_society_and_the_wadsw","v":{"s":"Maine Historical Society and the Wadsworth-Longfellow House (Congress Street) hold early Falmouth Gazette issues."}},{"k":"mainz_the_feast_of_st_lawrence_1455","v":{"s":"Mainz, the Feast of St. Lawrence, 1455"}},{"k":"mainz_the_year_of_our_lord_1457","v":{"s":"Mainz · the year of Our Lord 1457"}},{"k":"map_the_1450_concern_to_its_2026_echo_","v":{"s":"Map the 1450 concern to its 2026 echo. The technology changed; the argument template did not. Read each row across, then ask yourself: same fear, or different?"}},{"k":"marshall_mcluhan_the_gutenberg_galaxy_","v":{"s":"Marshall McLuhan, \"The Gutenberg Galaxy\" (1962)"}},{"k":"master_heinrich_the_printer","v":{"s":"Master Heinrich the printer"}},{"k":"master_printer","v":{"s":"Master Printer"}},{"k":"master_s_desk","v":{"s":"Master’s desk"}},{"k":"master_with_a_tighter_alloy_and_a_slig","v":{"s":"“Master, with a tighter alloy and a slightly smaller body we could fit two more lines per page.”"}},{"k":"meat_and_drink_lodging_and_washing","v":{"s":"meat and drink, lodging and washing"}},{"k":"modern_reading_vs_attention_debates_wi","v":{"s":"Modern reading-vs-attention debates with historical context."}},{"k":"mother_when_the_work_is_done_at_night_","v":{"s":"Mother, when the work is done at night and the press is quiet, I sometimes go look at the locked-up forme on the imposing stone. The letters are backwards, of course, and at first they made my head ache. But last week I read a full line by myself, reversed and all, and I thought of you and of how I will some day set a page that you could read. I will be a journeyman in six years and a master in ten, the Lord willing. I will print a Bible of my own. You will be proud."}},{"k":"motto_latin","v":{"s":"Motto (Latin)"}},{"k":"multi_generational_scholar_printers_in","v":{"s":"Multi-generational scholar-printers. Introduced verse numbering still used today."}},{"k":"my_dearest_mother","v":{"s":"My dearest mother,"}},{"k":"my_duties_are_sweeping_the_shop_fetchi","v":{"s":"My duties are sweeping the shop, fetching ink from the cellar, carrying lead pigs to the casting room (they weigh as much as a small calf), and watching the journeymen at their work. The compositor, Master Konrad, has begun to let me sort distributed type back into the case. I am slow. He laughs but not unkindly. He says the slow apprentice becomes the careful master."}},{"k":"naomi_baron_words_onscreen_2015","v":{"s":"Naomi Baron, \"Words Onscreen\" (2015)"}},{"k":"next_quote","v":{"s":"Next quote →"}},{"k":"no_clean_answer_worth_noticing_the_int","v":{"s":"No clean answer. Worth noticing: the internet is ~30 years old, social media is ~20, generative AI is ~3. We are early in a 150-year settling."}},{"k":"none","v":{"s":"None"}},{"k":"northern_renaissance_humanist_pushed_p","v":{"s":"Northern Renaissance humanist. Pushed printers to publish ancient texts in their original languages."}},{"k":"note_on_the_silhouettes_many_of_these_","v":{"s":"Note on the silhouettes: many of these figures (especially the women) have no surviving portraits. The illustrations below are stylized period archetypes that signal era and role, not photographic likenesses. The point is that we know the work; we do not always know the face."}},{"k":"notice_period_announcement","v":{"s":"Notice / period announcement"}},{"k":"notice_the_shared_pattern_clear_single","v":{"s":"Notice the shared pattern: clear single message, plain language, specific audience, one sheet of paper that someone in 1450-1865 could hand to someone else and say \"read this.\" Aim for that when you compose yours below."}},{"k":"number_every_verse_a_reader_needs_to_f","v":{"s":"“Number every verse. A reader needs to find their place — and a scholar needs to argue from it.”"}},{"k":"of_printing_for_a_term_of","v":{"s":" of printing, for a term of "}},{"k":"olive_tree","v":{"s":"Olive tree"}},{"k":"on_the_moral_panic_surrounding_early_n","v":{"s":"On the moral panic surrounding early newsprint."}},{"k":"on_this_day_before_god_and_witnesses","v":{"s":"On this day before God and witnesses, "}},{"k":"open_question_worth_real_discussion_so","v":{"s":"Open question worth real discussion. Some candidates students might raise: leaded gasoline, asbestos, certain social-media features. The honest answer is that \"should have\" requires hindsight that critics did not have."}},{"k":"or_breaks_this_contract_he_shall_serve","v":{"s":" or breaks this contract, he shall serve double the time absent on his return, and forfeit the clothes promised at the end of the term. If he reveals the trade's secrets, he forfeits all and may be pursued at law."}},{"k":"ornamental_border","v":{"s":"Ornamental border:"}},{"k":"ornate_full_fleuron_chain","v":{"s":"Ornate (full fleuron chain)"}},{"k":"paper_finished_sheets","v":{"s":"Paper + finished sheets"}},{"k":"period_ballad_greensleeves","v":{"s":"Period ballad (Greensleeves)"}},{"k":"period_vocabulary","v":{"s":"Period vocabulary"}},{"k":"peter_sch_ffer","v":{"s":"Peter Schöffer"}},{"k":"peter_sch_ffer_printed_the_first_multi","v":{"s":"Peter Schöffer printed the first multicolor book using the press."}},{"k":"pioneer_of_portable_octavo_books_dolph","v":{"s":"Pioneer of portable octavo books. Dolphin-and-anchor mark."}},{"k":"plato_phaedrus_370_bce","v":{"s":"Plato, \"Phaedrus\" (~370 BCE)"}},{"k":"play_again_2","v":{"s":"↻ Play again"}},{"k":"poem","v":{"s":"Poem"}},{"k":"politely_decline_wait_until_you_are_a_","v":{"s":"Politely decline. Wait until you are a master."}},{"k":"portland_press_herald","v":{"s":"Portland Press Herald"}},{"k":"possible_angles_human_nature_does_not_","v":{"s":"Possible angles: human nature does not change; new tech always disrupts existing institutions; the arguments are templates we reach for whenever something powerful arrives."}},{"k":"pray_for_me_give_my_love_to_my_sisters","v":{"s":"Pray for me. Give my love to my sisters. Tell Father I am well, and I will write again at Christmas."}},{"k":"pressman_apprentice","v":{"s":"💪 pressman + apprentice"}},{"k":"pressman_year_6","v":{"s":"Pressman (Year 6)"}},{"k":"pretend_you_did_not_see_stay_out_of_it","v":{"s":"Pretend you did not see. Stay out of it."}},{"k":"primary_historical_artifact_of_institu","v":{"s":"Primary historical artifact of institutional content moderation."}},{"k":"print_exactly_as_the_manuscript_reads_","v":{"s":"Print exactly as the manuscript reads. Author intent rules."}},{"k":"print_the_error_and_add_an_editorial_n","v":{"s":"Print the error and add an editorial note: [recieve, sic]."}},{"k":"printed_sheets_hang_to_dry_hours_to_a_","v":{"s":"(printed sheets hang to dry, hours to a day)"}},{"k":"probably_right_some_workers_will_be_di","v":{"s":"Probably right: some workers WILL be displaced; some institutions WILL be disrupted. Probably wrong: humanity will not lose the ability to think. The hard work is sorting which is which."}},{"k":"pull_extra_hours_yourself_refuse_to_sl","v":{"s":"Pull extra hours yourself. Refuse to slow the deadline."}},{"k":"push_through_accept_5_lower_quality_th","v":{"s":"Push through. Accept 5% lower quality this morning."}},{"k":"ran_her_press_in_paris_for_nearly_four","v":{"s":"Ran her press in Paris for nearly four decades after her husband’s death."}},{"k":"re_level_it_lose_90_minutes","v":{"s":"Re-level it. Lose 90 minutes."}},{"k":"re_level_only_the_parts_that_affect_th","v":{"s":"Re-level only the parts that affect the title page; press through on body text."}},{"k":"reading_discussion","v":{"s":"Reading discussion"}},{"k":"real_concerns_usually_cite_specific_ha","v":{"s":"Real concerns usually: cite specific harms with evidence, propose specific interventions, distinguish populations affected. Moral panics usually: invoke vague civilizational decline, target whole technologies rather than uses, assume the worst about new generations."}},{"k":"reprint_page_23_in_full_insert_the_cor","v":{"s":"Reprint page 23 in full. Insert the corrected page."}},{"k":"reset_game","v":{"s":"↻ Reset game"}},{"k":"restart","v":{"s":"Restart"}},{"k":"robert_bringhurst_the_elements_of_typo_2","v":{"s":"Robert Bringhurst, \"The Elements of Typographic Style\" (4th ed., 2013)"}},{"k":"robert_estienne","v":{"s":"Robert Estienne"}},{"k":"run_to_the_supplier_on_your_own_show_i","v":{"s":"Run to the supplier on your own — show initiative."}},{"k":"same_model_low_pay_early_learn_by_watc","v":{"s":"Same model: low pay early, learn by watching, certify out in 4–6 years. Maine has thousands of openings and not enough hands."}},{"k":"save_against_the_next_bad_year","v":{"s":"Save against the next bad year."}},{"k":"say_it_is_the_tympan_volunteer_to_reti","v":{"s":"Say it is the tympan. Volunteer to retighten it."}},{"k":"say_nothing_hope_someone_else_notices","v":{"s":"Say nothing. Hope someone else notices."}},{"k":"school_announcement","v":{"s":"School announcement"}},{"k":"scribal_flourish","v":{"s":"Scribal flourish"}},{"k":"sealed_with_the_master_s_mark_witnesse","v":{"s":"— Sealed with the Master's mark · witnessed by the Guild of Printers, Mainz"}},{"k":"setting_type_for_the_manuscript_you_sp","v":{"s":"Setting type for the manuscript, you spot a clear misspelling — \"recieve\" instead of \"receive.\" The author is dead (a 14th-century theologian). Modern copies all preserve the error."}},{"k":"seven_full_years","v":{"s":"seven full years"}},{"k":"she_inherited_the_press_from_her_first","v":{"s":"She inherited the press from her first husband, kept it through her second marriage to another printer, and continued running it for decades after his death. Over her career the Guillard press produced more than 150 substantial scholarly books. Many bore her own preface or note. Standard 19th-century histories did not mention her."}},{"k":"ship_as_is_hope_buyers_do_not_notice","v":{"s":"Ship as-is. Hope buyers do not notice."}},{"k":"shop_day","v":{"s":"shop day"}},{"k":"show_the_apprentice_exactly_which_ink_","v":{"s":"Show the apprentice exactly which ink to ask for, give him a sample, send him with the master's seal."}},{"k":"shun_taverns_and_play","v":{"s":"shun taverns and play"}},{"k":"silently_correct_it_no_one_will_notice","v":{"s":"Silently correct it. No one will notice."}},{"k":"silver","v":{"s":"Silver"}},{"k":"skilled_trade_apprentice","v":{"s":"Skilled-trade apprentice"}},{"k":"slant_the_roman_type_slightly_using_sh","v":{"s":"Slant the Roman type slightly using shims. Hope the patron does not notice."}},{"k":"slip_the_smudged_page_under_a_clean_on","v":{"s":"Slip the smudged page under a clean one and hope."}},{"k":"start_at_prep_station_observe_sous_che","v":{"s":"Start at prep station, observe sous-chefs, advance through skill. Same apprenticeship structure with a faster ladder."}},{"k":"state_the_truth_it_is_the_compositor_s","v":{"s":"State the truth: it is the compositor's spacing. Volunteer to help him correct it."}},{"k":"stay_and_help_him_skip_dinner","v":{"s":"Stay and help him. Skip dinner."}},{"k":"stop_the_press_go_yourself","v":{"s":"Stop the press, go yourself."}},{"k":"str","v":{"s":"🧒 · · ·"}},{"k":"street_door","v":{"s":"street door"}},{"k":"stretch_what_you_have_with_a_thinner_b","v":{"s":"Stretch what you have with a thinner blend. Hope it holds."}},{"k":"studied_broadsides_that_shifted_public","v":{"s":"Studied broadsides that shifted public opinion or made law. Notice the design pattern: each one has a single clear message, plain language, and a specific audience."}},{"k":"subcontract_the_italic_dedication_page","v":{"s":"Subcontract the italic dedication page to the Aldine Press in Venice (overnight courier)."}},{"k":"successor_papers","v":{"s":"Successor papers"}},{"k":"suggest_the_colophon_list_both_your_na","v":{"s":"Suggest the colophon list both your names — master + journeyman."}},{"k":"suggest_you_both_ask_the_master_if_you","v":{"s":"Suggest you both ask the master if you can use the next slow hour during the day."}},{"k":"susan_broomhall_women_and_religion_in_","v":{"s":"Susan Broomhall, \"Women and Religion in Sixteenth-Century France\" (work on women printers)"}},{"k":"sworn","v":{"s":"Sworn"}},{"k":"symbol","v":{"s":"Symbol"}},{"k":"take_it_again","v":{"s":"↻ Take it again"}},{"k":"take_the_almanac","v":{"s":"Take the almanac."}},{"k":"take_the_bible","v":{"s":"Take the Bible."}},{"k":"take_the_heretical_pamphlet","v":{"s":"Take the heretical pamphlet."}},{"k":"tell_him_to_figure_it_out_himself_appr","v":{"s":"Tell him to figure it out himself. Apprentices need rest."}},{"k":"tell_the_master_immediately","v":{"s":"Tell the master immediately."}},{"k":"tell_the_master_immediately_accept_the","v":{"s":"Tell the master immediately, accept the blame."}},{"k":"tell_the_master_what_happened_so_he_kn","v":{"s":"Tell the master what happened so he knows."}},{"k":"tell_the_patron_honestly_you_cannot_do","v":{"s":"Tell the patron honestly you cannot do italic. Offer Roman instead."}},{"k":"tell_the_patron_the_deadline_must_slip","v":{"s":"Tell the patron the deadline must slip by a week. Explain why."}},{"k":"the_1457_mainz_psalter_fust_sch_ffer_u","v":{"s":"The 1457 Mainz Psalter (Fust & Schöffer) used a complicated two-color printing technique: the body type in black, the large initial capitals printed in red and blue on the same impression. This required printing each page through the press in multiple passes with the type inked in different colors. Most scholars consider it among the most beautifully printed books ever made."}},{"k":"the_95_theses_2","v":{"s":"The 95 Theses"}},{"k":"the_aldine_dolphin_and_anchor_was_so_h","v":{"s":"The Aldine dolphin-and-anchor was so heavily pirated that Aldus published a guide to spotting fakes."}},{"k":"the_apprentice_agrees","v":{"s":"The apprentice agrees:"}},{"k":"the_closing_two_paragraphs_shift_from_","v":{"s":"The closing two paragraphs shift from work to home. What does Konrad seem to want most from his mother's reply, and how is that different from what an apprentice in 2026 might want from a parent?"}},{"k":"the_compositor_a_journeyman_three_year","v":{"s":"The compositor — a journeyman three years your senior — drops a galley. The type \"falls in pi\" (becomes a jumbled pile). It will take an hour to sort. He glances at you. He saw you watching. He could blame you."}},{"k":"the_estienne_family","v":{"s":"The Estienne family"}},{"k":"the_first_newspaper_printed_in_what_wo","v":{"s":", the first newspaper printed in what would become Maine. They set up a press in Falmouth (now Portland) thirty-five years before Maine statehood, when Maine was still the District of Maine inside Massachusetts. Their press ran from a small shop on Fore Street."}},{"k":"the_food_is_plain_but_enough_the_maste","v":{"s":"The food is plain but enough. The Master's wife sees that I have bread and broth in the morning and meat at supper. I sleep on a straw mattress with the other apprentice in the loft above the press room. He is from Cologne and snores like a stuck pig."}},{"k":"the_interest_accrues_whether_you_finis","v":{"s":"“The interest accrues whether you finish the Bible or not. Pay, or the press is mine.”"}},{"k":"the_master_agrees","v":{"s":"The Master agrees:"}},{"k":"the_master_sends_you_to_fetch_oil_base","v":{"s":"The master sends you to fetch oil-based ink from the cellar. You realize the shop has only enough for half a day. Telling him will mean blame for not noticing earlier. Saying nothing means the press stops at midday."}},{"k":"the_original_writing_will_atrophy_memo","v":{"s":"The original \"writing will atrophy memory\" argument that print critics inherited."}},{"k":"the_platen_has_a_slight_warp_from_yest","v":{"s":"The platen has a slight warp from yesterday's heat. Re-leveling takes 90 minutes. Pressing through means slightly uneven impressions all morning."}},{"k":"the_press","v":{"s":"The press"}},{"k":"the_shop_carries_my_husband_s_name_the","v":{"s":"“The shop carries my husband’s name. The work carries mine.”"}},{"k":"the_shop_closes_at_sunset_another_appr","v":{"s":"The shop closes at sunset. Another apprentice asks if you would help him learn the letter positions in the type case (he is behind). Helping him means staying late. The master prefers apprentices rest so they work fresh tomorrow."}},{"k":"these_are_not_invented_or_exaggerated_","v":{"s":"These are not invented or exaggerated. Each was a genuine, documented concern voiced by someone in the 1450-1600 period. The voice attribution names the actual source where the concern was raised."}},{"k":"these_quotes_are_not_historical_transc","v":{"s":"These quotes are NOT historical transcripts — imagined paraphrases in the voice each figure is documented to have used. Pick the most likely speaker."}},{"k":"thomas_b_wait_benjamin_titcomb","v":{"s":"Thomas B. Wait & Benjamin Titcomb"}},{"k":"three_orders_arrive_this_morning_a_a_b","v":{"s":"Three orders arrive this morning. (A) A Bible commission — prestigious, low margin, 6 months of work. (B) An almanac — quick, mass-market, mid margin. (C) A heretical pamphlet — high margin, but printing it could mean Church penalties or worse."}},{"k":"title_size","v":{"s":"Title size: "}},{"k":"to_deal_with_the_apprentice_in_good_fa","v":{"s":". To deal with the apprentice in good faith and not to put him to work beneath the trade."}},{"k":"to_instruct_the_apprentice_in_casting_","v":{"s":" to instruct the apprentice in casting type, setting type, the working of the press, the mixing of ink, and the keeping of a shop. To furnish "}},{"k":"to_serve_faithfully_day_and_night_to_k","v":{"s":" to serve faithfully day and night, to keep the secrets of the trade and not reveal them to any rival shop, to "}},{"k":"to_take_no_wife_during_the_term_to_obe","v":{"s":", to take no wife during the term, to obey the Master and his household in all lawful things, and not to absent himself from service without leave."}},{"k":"today_i_dropped_a_tray_not_the_type_th","v":{"s":"Today I dropped a tray. Not the type, thank God, but the wooden tray underneath it. The journeyman pressman did not see, and Master Konrad pretended not to. I will be more careful. The trade is full of dangers I had not thought of when we spoke before I left home: the lead, the boiling oil for the ink, the heavy quoins that can crush a finger. Already I have a small burn on my left hand from the casting room. It is healing."}},{"k":"tom_standage_writing_on_the_wall_socia","v":{"s":"Tom Standage, \"Writing on the Wall: Social Media in the First 2,000 Years\" (2013)"}},{"k":"top_down_floor_plan_of_a_1455_mainz_pr","v":{"s":"Top-down floor plan of a 1455 Mainz print shop"}},{"k":"train_another_apprentice_long_term_cap","v":{"s":"Train another apprentice — long-term capacity."}},{"k":"try_to_clean_the_smudge_yourself_with_","v":{"s":"Try to clean the smudge yourself with a damp cloth."}},{"k":"two_witnesses_of_the_guild","v":{"s":"two witnesses of the guild"}},{"k":"type_cases","v":{"s":"Type cases"}},{"k":"type_cooper_typography_history_resourc","v":{"s":"Type@Cooper — Typography history resources"}},{"k":"upper_lower","v":{"s":"(upper / lower)"}},{"k":"wait_and_titcomb_founded_the","v":{"s":"Wait and Titcomb founded the "}},{"k":"what_does_konrad_reveal_about_apprenti","v":{"s":"What does Konrad reveal about apprenticeship that the contract did not? Where do the two documents agree; where do they differ in tone?"}},{"k":"when_you_design_your_own_broadside_bel","v":{"s":"When you design your own broadside below, the dolphin-and-anchor on the colophon (bottom of the page) is your tribute to Aldus. Your own version, with your own symbols, would have been someone’s job for life in 1500."}},{"k":"where_the_press_sat","v":{"s":"Where the press sat"}},{"k":"who_said_this_imagined_voices","v":{"s":"💬 Who said this? (imagined voices)"}},{"k":"why_it_worked","v":{"s":"Why it worked: "}},{"k":"why_this_matters_a_frontier_newspaper_","v":{"s":"Why this matters: a frontier newspaper in 1785 was a political act. The Falmouth Gazette covered the statehood debate, advertised land sales, reprinted Boston and London news arriving by ship, and gave coastal Maine its first sustained source of printed information. Without local presses, news traveled at the speed of a horse from Boston."}},{"k":"year_one_apprentice_work_observation_s","v":{"s":"Year-one apprentice work — observation, scut work, building trust through small reliable acts — is still how a lot of skilled-trade pathways begin."}},{"k":"you_accidentally_smudge_a_freshly_prin","v":{"s":"You accidentally smudge a freshly printed page. The master is on the other side of the shop. The smudge is small. The page will be inserted into a Bible that costs the buyer 3 years' wages."}},{"k":"you_care_about_accuracy_and_citation_y","v":{"s":"You care about accuracy and citation. You would have invented Bible verse numbers because you got tired of saying \"the bit near the end of Matthew.\" Your reference works become the standard everyone else cites. Your weakness: you can lose readers in the apparatus."}},{"k":"you_care_about_getting_things_exactly_","v":{"s":"You care about getting things exactly right. You would have been the person who tested 27 alloy ratios before committing to one. You measure twice and cut once. Your weakness: sometimes you forget that \"good enough and shipped\" beats \"perfect and abandoned.\""}},{"k":"you_care_about_impact_on_the_world_you","v":{"s":"You care about impact on the world. You would have run a newspaper, a postal service, and a revolution at the same time. You believe a well-aimed pamphlet beats a brilliant treatise. Your weakness: you sometimes choose persuasion over precision."}},{"k":"you_care_about_making_things_accessibl","v":{"s":"You care about making things accessible. You would have invented the paperback because you were sick of seeing classics locked up in expensive folios. You think reach matters at least as much as quality. Your weakness: sometimes you simplify what should stay complex."}},{"k":"you_chose","v":{"s":"You chose: "}},{"k":"you_close_the_books_for_the_year_the_s","v":{"s":"You close the books for the year. The shop made a small profit. Reinvest in: (A) more type, (B) better paper supply, (C) train another apprentice, (D) save for hard times?"}},{"k":"you_tied_between_multiple_archetypes_s","v":{"s":"(You tied between multiple archetypes; shown is one of them. You contain multitudes.)"}},{"k":"your_mark","v":{"s":"Your mark"}},{"k":"your_match","v":{"s":"Your match"}},{"k":"your_obedient_and_loving_son","v":{"s":"Your obedient and loving son,"}},{"k":"your_text_first_line_is_the_title_rest","v":{"s":"Your text (first line is the title, rest is body):"}}],"id":565}},{"k":"probability","v":{"o":[{"k":"a11y_d6_showing","v":{"s":"d6 showing {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_d_showing","v":{"s":"d{value1} showing {value2}"}},{"k":"a11y_select_mode","v":{"s":"Select mode: {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_d_p_equals_one_over","v":{"s":"d{value1}, P equals one over {value2}"}},{"k":"a11y_color_for_outcome","v":{"s":"Color for outcome {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_name_for_color","v":{"s":"Name for color {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_remove_marble_color","v":{"s":"Remove marble color {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_marble_bag_containing_marbles_across_colors","v":{"s":"Marble bag containing {value1} marbles across {value2} colors"}},{"k":"a11y_select_sport_scenario","v":{"s":"Select sport scenario: {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_select_input_mode","v":{"s":"Select {value1} input mode"}},{"k":"a11y_name_for_event","v":{"s":"Name for event {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_numerator_for_event","v":{"s":"Numerator for event {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_denominator_for_event","v":{"s":"Denominator for event {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_remove_event","v":{"s":"Remove event {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_name_for_marble_color","v":{"s":"Name for marble color {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_name_for_outcome","v":{"s":"Name for outcome {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_probability_for_outcome","v":{"s":"Probability for outcome {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_remove_outcome","v":{"s":"Remove outcome {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_simulate_rounds_of_each_strategy","v":{"s":"Simulate {value1} rounds of each strategy"}},{"k":"a11y_galton_board_with_peg_rows_and_histogram_bins_b","v":{"s":"Galton board with {value1} peg rows and {value2} histogram bins below"}},{"k":"a11y_set_group_size_to_people","v":{"s":"Set group size to {value1} people"}},{"k":"a11y_set_simulation_speed_to","v":{"s":"Set simulation speed to {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_run_trials","v":{"s":"Run {value1} trials"}},{"k":"a11y_convergence_chart_observed_percent_expected_per","v":{"s":"Convergence chart: observed {value1} percent, expected {value2} percent after {value3} trials"}},{"k":"a11y_monte_carlo_pi_scatter_plot_with_of_points_insi","v":{"s":"Monte Carlo pi scatter plot with {value1} of {value2} points inside the quarter circle; pi estimate {value3}"}},{"k":"sr_automatic_simulation_speed_set_to","v":{"s":"Automatic simulation speed set to {value1}."}},{"k":"sr_automatic_simulation_paused","v":{"s":"Automatic simulation paused."}},{"k":"sr_automatic_simulation_started","v":{"s":"Automatic simulation started."}},{"k":"a11y_probability_experiment_mode","v":{"s":"Probability experiment mode"}},{"k":"a11y_choose_a_probability_tree_model","v":{"s":"Choose a probability tree model"}},{"k":"a11y_scrollable_ordered_probability_path_table","v":{"s":"Scrollable ordered probability path table"}},{"k":"a11y_automatic_simulation_controls","v":{"s":"Automatic simulation controls"}},{"k":"a11y_automatic_simulation","v":{"s":"Automatic simulation"}},{"k":"a11y_automatic_simulation_speed","v":{"s":"Automatic simulation speed"}},{"k":"a11y_reset_current_run","v":{"s":"Reset current run"}},{"k":"a11y_slow_drop_100_points_one_at_a_time","v":{"s":"Slow-drop 100 points one at a time"}},{"k":"expected","v":{"s":"Expected: "}},{"k":"free_throws","v":{"s":"🏀 Free Throws"}},{"k":"nba_average_free_throw_percentage_is_7","v":{"s":"NBA average free throw percentage is ~77%"}},{"k":"3_pointers","v":{"s":"🏀 3-Pointers"}},{"k":"nba_average_3_point_percentage_is_36","v":{"s":"NBA average 3-point percentage is ~36%"}},{"k":"penalty_kicks","v":{"s":"⚽ Penalty Kicks"}},{"k":"soccer_penalty_kick_conversion_rate_is","v":{"s":"Soccer penalty kick conversion rate is ~76%"}},{"k":"batting_average","v":{"s":"⚾ Batting Average"}},{"k":"mlb_average_batting_average_is_250_hit","v":{"s":"MLB average batting average is ~.250 (hit 1 in 4)"}},{"k":"field_goals","v":{"s":"🏈 Field Goals"}},{"k":"nfl_field_goal_success_rate_is_84","v":{"s":"NFL field goal success rate is ~84%"}},{"k":"first_serves","v":{"s":"🎾 First Serves"}},{"k":"pro_tennis_first_serve_success_rate_is","v":{"s":"Pro tennis first serve success rate is ~62%"}},{"k":"shots_on_goal","v":{"s":"🏒 Shots on Goal"}},{"k":"nhl_average_shooting_percentage_is_10","v":{"s":"NHL average shooting percentage is ~10%"}},{"k":"blue","v":{"s":"Blue"}},{"k":"blue_2","v":{"s":"Blue"}},{"k":"keyframes_coinflip_0_transform_scalex_","v":{"s":"@keyframes coinFlip{0%{transform:scaleX(1)}25%{transform:scaleX(0.05) translateY(-10px)}60%{transform:scaleX(1.08) translateY(-4px)}100%{transform:scaleX(1) translateY(0)}} @keyframes diceRoll{0%{transform:rotate(0deg)scale(1)}25%{transform:rotate(-24deg)scale(1.12)}55%{transform:rotate(19deg)scale(1.08)}80%{transform:rotate(-8deg)scale(1.04)}100%{transform:rotate(0deg)scale(1)}} @keyframes resultPop{0%{transform:scale(0.78);opacity:0.35}55%{transform:scale(1.09);opacity:1}100%{transform:scale(1);opacity:1}} @keyframes sportBounce{0%{transform:translateY(0)scale(1)}40%{transform:translateY(-20px)scale(1.12)}70%{transform:translateY(-6px)scale(1.06)}100%{transform:translateY(0)scale(1)}}"}},{"k":"back_to_tools","v":{"s":"Back to tools"}},{"k":"probability_lab","v":{"s":"🎲 Probability Lab"}},{"k":"explore_probability_through_experiment","v":{"s":"Explore probability through experiments. Run trials and watch observed frequencies converge to expected values."}},{"k":"coin_the_simplest_50_50","v":{"s":"Coin — the simplest 50/50"}},{"k":"p_h_p_t_0_5_law_of_large_numbers_as_tr","v":{"s":"P(H) = P(T) = 0.5. Law of large numbers: as trials grow, the proportion of heads converges to 0.5. After 1,000 flips you’ll be within ~3% of 50%, but in any short streak anything is possible."}},{"k":"dice_uniform_1_n_each_d4_d6_d8_d10_d12","v":{"s":"Dice — uniform 1/N each (d4 / d6 / d8 / d10 / d12 / d20)"}},{"k":"pick_any_die_size_each_face_equally_li","v":{"s":"Pick any die size. Each face equally likely: P = 1/N. The math is identical across die types — what changes is the denominator. d4 is 1/4, d20 is 1/20."}},{"k":"two_dice_sum_the_triangular_distributi","v":{"s":"Two-Dice Sum — the triangular distribution"}},{"k":"roll_two_dice_of_the_chosen_type_and_a","v":{"s":"Roll TWO dice of the chosen type and add. The sum is no longer uniform: middle sums are MUCH more common. For 2d6, P(7)=6/36, P(2)=1/36. This is why orange properties in Monopoly get landed on the most — 6, 7, 8 are the most common sums after rolling from Jail."}},{"k":"spinner_4_color_uniform","v":{"s":"Spinner — 4-color uniform"}},{"k":"equal_area_sectors_equal_probability_u","v":{"s":"Equal-area sectors = equal probability. Unequal sectors → weighted draws. Spinners are the gentlest path into discrete distributions for elementary students."}},{"k":"sports_weighted_real_world_odds","v":{"s":"Sports — weighted real-world odds"}},{"k":"free_throw_75_nba_3_point_36_mlb_hit_2","v":{"s":"Free-throw 75%, NBA 3-point 36%, MLB hit ~25%. Probability isn’t always 50/50 — the math handles unequal weights the same way, just with different denominators."}},{"k":"marble_bag_with_vs_without_replacement","v":{"s":"Marble Bag — with vs without replacement"}},{"k":"with_replacement_independent_draws_wit","v":{"s":"With replacement: independent draws. Without: probabilities CHANGE each pull — conditional probability. The exact mechanism behind hypergeometric distribution and card-game odds."}},{"k":"custom_design_your_own_outcome_set","v":{"s":"Custom — design your own outcome set"}},{"k":"build_any_discrete_distribution_test_t","v":{"s":"Build any discrete distribution. Test the law of large numbers with skewed odds, demonstrate that simulations can answer ANY closed-form question if you have enough trials. Monte Carlo in miniature."}},{"k":"tree_multi_stage_probability","v":{"s":"Tree — multi-stage probability"}},{"k":"multiply_along_branches_add_across_lea","v":{"s":"Multiply along branches; add across leaves. Two coin flips: HH HT TH TT each 0.25. Tree diagrams scale up to medical-test base-rate problems and Bayes’ theorem."}},{"k":"pi_monte_carlo_estimation","v":{"s":"Pi — Monte Carlo π estimation"}},{"k":"throw_darts_at_a_unit_square_count_how","v":{"s":"Throw darts at a unit square; count how many land inside the inscribed quarter circle. π ≈ 4 × (inside / total). Convergence is O(1/√N) — each digit costs 100× more darts."}},{"k":"birthday_the_famous_paradox","v":{"s":"Birthday — the famous paradox"}},{"k":"in_a_room_of_23_the_probability_of_a_s","v":{"s":"In a room of 23, the probability of a shared birthday is > 50%. By 70 it’s > 99.9%. Counterintuitive because we count comparisons (23 choose 2 = 253), not people. The cleanest classroom counter to gut-feel probability."}},{"k":"marble_bag_setup","v":{"s":"🎱 Marble Bag Setup"}},{"k":"without_replacement_each_marble_drawn_","v":{"s":"💡 Without replacement: Each marble drawn is removed from the bag. Probabilities change after each draw! Bag refills when empty."}},{"k":"add_color","v":{"s":"+ Add Color"}},{"k":"add_color_2","v":{"s":"+ Add Color"}},{"k":"keyframes_mbshake_0_100_transform_rota","v":{"s":"@keyframes mbShake { 0%,100% { transform: rotate(0deg); } 15% { transform: rotate(-8deg); } 30% { transform: rotate(8deg); } 45% { transform: rotate(-5deg); } 60% { transform: rotate(5deg); } 75% { transform: rotate(-2deg); } }"}},{"k":"choose_a_sport","v":{"s":"🏆 Choose a Sport"}},{"k":"define_each_event_as_a_fraction_e_g_1_","v":{"s":"🎯 Define each event as a fraction — e.g., \"1 out of 20 times\""}},{"k":"out_of","v":{"s":"out of"}},{"k":"add_event","v":{"s":"+ Add Event"}},{"k":"add_event_2","v":{"s":"+ Add Event"}},{"k":"add_colored_marbles_to_a_bag_probabili","v":{"s":"🎱 Add colored marbles to a bag. Probability = your marble count ÷ total marbles."}},{"k":"add_color_3","v":{"s":"+ Add Color"}},{"k":"add_color_4","v":{"s":"+ Add Color"}},{"k":"drag_sliders_to_set_exact_probability_","v":{"s":"🎨 Drag sliders to set exact probability percentages for each outcome."}},{"k":"add_outcome","v":{"s":"+ Add Outcome"}},{"k":"add_outcome_2","v":{"s":"+ Add Outcome"}},{"k":"loading_monty_hall","v":{"s":"Loading Monty Hall…"}},{"k":"your_pick","v":{"s":"YOUR PICK"}},{"k":"the_monty_hall_problem","v":{"s":"🚪 The Monty Hall Problem"}},{"k":"behind_one_door_a_prize_behind_two_goa","v":{"s":"Behind one door: a prize. Behind two: goats. Pick a door, the host opens a goat-door, then you choose: stay or switch?"}},{"k":"stay","v":{"s":"🛡 Stay"}},{"k":"switch","v":{"s":"🔄 Switch"}},{"k":"play_another_round","v":{"s":"↻ Play another round"}},{"k":"strategy_win_rates","v":{"s":"📊 Strategy Win Rates"}},{"k":"stay_2","v":{"s":"🛡 Stay"}},{"k":"last_20_manual_stay_plays_green_wins_d","v":{"s":"Last 20 manual Stay plays — green wins, dark red losses"}},{"k":"switch_2","v":{"s":"🔄 Switch"}},{"k":"last_20_manual_switch_plays_green_wins","v":{"s":"Last 20 manual Switch plays — green wins, dark red losses"}},{"k":"outcome_strips_show_your_last_20_manua","v":{"s":"Outcome strips show your last 20 manual plays — green = win, red = loss. Visible streaks tell you what randomness actually feels like."}},{"k":"math_says_stay_wins_1_3_33_switch_wins","v":{"s":"Math says: Stay wins ≈ 1/3 (33%). Switch wins ≈ 2/3 (67%). With enough trials, the math wins out."}},{"k":"reset_stats","v":{"s":"↻ Reset stats"}},{"k":"the_galton_board","v":{"s":"⚙️ The Galton Board"}},{"k":"drop_balls_through_a_peg_grid_each_peg","v":{"s":"Drop balls through a peg grid. Each peg deflects 50/50 left or right. After enough balls, the histogram becomes a bell curve — the Central Limit Theorem in action."}},{"k":"empirical_your_drops","v":{"s":"Empirical (your drops)"}},{"k":"drop_balls_to_see","v":{"s":"Drop balls to see…"}},{"k":"theoretical_math","v":{"s":"Theoretical (math)"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"↻ Reset"}},{"k":"gold_dashed_line_theoretical_normal_cu","v":{"s":"⬆ Gold dashed line: theoretical normal curve. Your empirical bars should hug it more closely with more drops."}},{"k":"the_birthday_paradox","v":{"s":"🎂 The Birthday Paradox"}},{"k":"in_a_room_of_just_23_people_there_s_a_","v":{"s":"In a room of just 23 people, there’s a >50% chance two share a birthday. Drag the slider to explore!"}},{"k":"number_of_people_in_room","v":{"s":"Number of people in room"}},{"k":"50_threshold","v":{"s":"50% threshold"}},{"k":"probability_data_table","v":{"s":"probability data table"}},{"k":"people_n","v":{"s":"People (n)"}},{"k":"p_shared_birthday","v":{"s":"P(shared birthday)"}},{"k":"simulate_the_room","v":{"s":"🎂 Simulate the Room"}},{"k":"no_matches_this_time","v":{"s":"No matches this time"}},{"k":"re_randomize_all_birthdays","v":{"s":"Re-randomize all birthdays"}},{"k":"resample","v":{"s":"🎲 Resample"}},{"k":"run_100_simulations_of_this_room_size","v":{"s":"Run 100 simulations of this room size"}},{"k":"run_100_rooms","v":{"s":"⚡ Run 100 rooms"}},{"k":"reset_simulation_counts","v":{"s":"Reset simulation counts"}},{"k":"each_has_a_random_birthday_same_color_","v":{"s":"Each 🧑 has a random birthday. Same color + glow = matching pair. Resample to see how often matches appear."}},{"k":"two_event_compound_probability_tree","v":{"s":"🌳 Two-Event Compound Probability Tree"}},{"k":"multiply_the_two_probabilities_to_get_","v":{"s":"💡 Independent events: P(A then B) = P(A) × P(B). The second branch does not change after the first outcome."}},{"k":"streaks_are_normal_random_texture","v":{"s":"streaks are normal random texture"}},{"k":"toggle_auto_run_simulation","v":{"s":"Toggle auto-run simulation"}},{"k":"reset_all_trials","v":{"s":"Reset all trials"}},{"k":"reset_2","v":{"s":"🔄 Reset"}},{"k":"observed_vs_expected_frequencies","v":{"s":"📊 Observed vs Expected Frequencies"}},{"k":"statistical_analysis","v":{"s":"📊 Statistical Analysis"}},{"k":"total_trials","v":{"s":"Total Trials"}},{"k":"max_deviation","v":{"s":"Max Deviation"}},{"k":"statistic","v":{"s":"χ² Statistic"}},{"k":"fairness_0_05","v":{"s":"Fairness (α=0.05)"}},{"k":"did_you_know","v":{"s":"💡 Did You Know?"}},{"k":"theoretical_vs_observed_comparison","v":{"s":"📊 Theoretical vs Observed Comparison"}},{"k":"theoretical","v":{"s":"🎯 Theoretical"}},{"k":"as_you_run_more_trials_the_observed_ba","v":{"s":"💡 As you run more trials, the observed bars should get closer to the theoretical bars — that's the Law of Large Numbers in action!"}},{"k":"monte_carlo_scatter_plot","v":{"s":"🥧 Monte Carlo π Scatter Plot"}},{"k":"estimate","v":{"s":"π Estimate"}},{"k":"true_3_14159","v":{"s":"True π = 3.14159…"}},{"k":"inside","v":{"s":"🟢 Inside"}},{"k":"outside","v":{"s":"🔴 Outside"}},{"k":"error_from","v":{"s":"Error from π"}},{"k":"10k_points_needed_for_2_decimal_places","v":{"s":"~10k points needed for 2 decimal places of π"}},{"k":"draw_history_breakdown","v":{"s":"🎱 Draw History Breakdown"}},{"k":"last_30_results","v":{"s":"Last 30 Results"}},{"k":"streak_surge","v":{"s":"Streak Surge"}},{"k":"get_5_results_in_a_row_any_mode","v":{"s":"Get 5+ results in a row (any mode)"}},{"k":"balance_master","v":{"s":"Balance Master"}},{"k":"60_dice_rolls_all_within_10_of_expecte","v":{"s":"60+ dice rolls, all within 10% of expected"}},{"k":"law_witness","v":{"s":"Law Witness"}},{"k":"1000_coin_trials_with_max_deviation_3","v":{"s":"1000 coin trials with max deviation < 3%"}},{"k":"pi_hunter","v":{"s":"Pi Hunter"}},{"k":"1000_monte_carlo_pi_trials_error_0_05","v":{"s":"1000+ Monte Carlo Pi trials, error < 0.05"}},{"k":"birthday_breaker","v":{"s":"Birthday Breaker"}},{"k":"set_n_23_in_birthday_mode_to_see_the_p","v":{"s":"Set n=23 in Birthday mode to see the paradox"}},{"k":"challenges","v":{"s":"🏆 Challenges"}},{"k":"done","v":{"s":"✅ Done!"}},{"k":"claim","v":{"s":"Claim"}},{"k":"in_progress","v":{"s":"🔒 In progress"}},{"k":"snapshot","v":{"s":"Snapshot"}},{"k":"snapshot_2","v":{"s":"📸 Snapshot"}},{"k":"export_csv","v":{"s":"Export CSV"}},{"k":"export_csv_2","v":{"s":"📥 Export CSV"}},{"k":"explain_results_with_ai","v":{"s":"Explain results with AI"}},{"k":"narrate_results","v":{"s":"Narrate Results"}},{"k":"narrate_results_2","v":{"s":"🔊 Narrate Results"}},{"k":"uniform_flat","v":{"s":"⬛ Uniform (flat)"}},{"k":"all_outcomes_nearly_equal_in_probabili","v":{"s":"All outcomes nearly equal in probability."}},{"k":"peaked_center","v":{"s":"🔺 Peaked (center)"}},{"k":"middle_outcome_dominates_approaches_no","v":{"s":"Middle outcome dominates. Approaches normal-like shape with more buckets."}},{"k":"skewed","v":{"s":"↗️ Skewed"}},{"k":"one_tail_much_heavier_than_the_other_a","v":{"s":"One tail much heavier than the other. Asymmetric distribution."}},{"k":"mixed","v":{"s":"🔀 Mixed"}},{"k":"two_outcomes_share_roughly_equal_proba","v":{"s":"Two outcomes share roughly equal probability with the third much lower or higher."}},{"k":"distribution_shape_discovery","v":{"s":"❔ Distribution shape discovery"}},{"k":"three_sliders_set_the_relative_probabi","v":{"s":"Three sliders set the relative probabilities of low / mid / high outcomes. The distribution shape is classified into one of four discrete shapes. No score, no reveal — sweep and notice."}},{"k":"p_low_weight","v":{"s":"P(low) weight"}},{"k":"p_mid_weight","v":{"s":"P(mid) weight"}},{"k":"p_high_weight","v":{"s":"P(high) weight"}},{"k":"log","v":{"s":"📋 Log"}},{"k":"reset_3","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"hypothesis_free_text_what_combination_","v":{"s":"Hypothesis (free text): What combination produces uniform? What about peaked?"}},{"k":"stuck_show_open_prompts","v":{"s":"🤔 Stuck — show open prompts"}},{"k":"hold_two_sliders_steady_move_one_watch","v":{"s":"Hold two sliders steady. Move one. Watch the shape."}},{"k":"find_two_settings_that_produce_the_sam","v":{"s":"Find two settings that produce the same shape."}},{"k":"what_raw_weights_produce_a_peaked_shap","v":{"s":"What raw weights produce a peaked shape?"}},{"k":"i_understand_explain_in_my_own_words","v":{"s":"I understand — explain in my own words"}},{"k":"explain_how_relative_weights_produce_s","v":{"s":"Explain how relative weights produce shape."}},{"k":"design_note_discrete_4_shape_classific","v":{"s":"Design note: discrete 4-shape classification; no goodness-of-fit score; no reveal — by design."}},{"k":"dashboard_trials","v":{"s":"Trials"}},{"k":"dashboard_trials_hint","v":{"s":"current run"}},{"k":"dashboard_modes","v":{"s":"Modes tried"}},{"k":"dashboard_modes_hint","v":{"s":"quest progress"}},{"k":"dashboard_challenges","v":{"s":"Challenges"}},{"k":"dashboard_challenges_hint","v":{"s":"claimed"}},{"k":"dashboard_result","v":{"s":"Latest"}},{"k":"dashboard_result_hint","v":{"s":"last result"}},{"k":"route_foundations","v":{"s":"Foundations"}},{"k":"route_foundations_note","v":{"s":"Equally likely outcomes and sample spaces."}},{"k":"route_weighted","v":{"s":"Weighted Odds"}},{"k":"route_weighted_note","v":{"s":"Uneven chances, bags, and real-world rates."}},{"k":"route_surprises","v":{"s":"Probability Surprises"}},{"k":"route_surprises_note","v":{"s":"Simulations that challenge intuition."}},{"k":"route_monte_carlo","v":{"s":"Monte Carlo"}},{"k":"route_monte_carlo_note","v":{"s":"Random sampling, volumes, and compound events."}},{"k":"command_eyebrow","v":{"s":"Chance Lab"}},{"k":"command_title","v":{"s":"Run experiments, then compare the pattern"}},{"k":"command_copy","v":{"s":"Pick a probability model, run trials, and watch the observed results move toward the expected distribution."}},{"k":"run_10_trials","v":{"s":"Run 10 Trials"}},{"k":"start_with_coin","v":{"s":"Start With Coin"}},{"k":"try_a_paradox","v":{"s":"Try a Paradox"}},{"k":"command_visual_label","v":{"s":"Probability bars showing observed results settling toward expected values"}},{"k":"observed_vs_expected","v":{"s":"Observed vs. expected"}},{"k":"roll_two_dice_sum_monopoly_orange_39","v":{"s":"Roll TWO dice of the chosen type and add. The sum is no longer uniform: middle sums are MUCH more common. For 2d6, P(7)=6/36, P(2)=1/36. It is why Monopoly’s orange properties get landed on more than any other colour group: they sit 6, 8 and 9 steps past Jail, and those three sums come up 14 times in 36 — so a player leaving Jail hits orange nearly 39% of the time."}},{"k":"free_throw_77_nba_3_point_36_mlb_hit_2","v":{"s":"Free-throw 77%, NBA 3-point 36%, MLB hit ~25%. Probability isn’t always 50/50 — the math handles unequal weights the same way, just with different denominators."}},{"k":"volume3d_title","v":{"s":"🧊 3D Monte Carlo — measure a volume by throwing darts"}},{"k":"volume3d_intro","v":{"s":"The box is exactly 1×1×1, so its volume is 1. Throw darts at random spots inside it and the fraction that land in the solid IS the solid’s volume. No formula required — which is how you measure shapes that don’t have one."}},{"k":"volume3d_drag","v":{"s":"Drag to rotate · scroll to zoom · or focus the view and use arrow keys, + and −"}},{"k":"volume3d_loading","v":{"s":"⏳ Loading the 3D engine…"}},{"k":"volume3d_no_gl","v":{"s":"📊 The 3D view is unavailable — school networks often block the graphics library, and some devices have no WebGL. The experiment still works: every number below is real, and the dart-throwing is done in maths, not in the picture."}},{"k":"volume3d_idle","v":{"s":"Preparing the 3D view…"}},{"k":"volume3d_darts","v":{"s":"Darts thrown"}},{"k":"volume3d_hits","v":{"s":"Landed inside"}},{"k":"volume3d_estimate","v":{"s":"Estimated volume"}},{"k":"volume3d_exact","v":{"s":"Exact volume"}},{"k":"volume3d_no_formula","v":{"s":"* No volume formula"}},{"k":"volume3d_no_formula_body","v":{"s":"This lumpy solid isn’t in any textbook, so there is nothing to check the darts against. The estimate above is not an approximation of a known answer — it IS the answer, and the 95% range is how precisely you know it. Throw more darts to narrow it."}},{"k":"volume3d_darts_word","v":{"s":"darts"}},{"k":"volume3d_reset","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"volume3d_show_misses","v":{"s":"show misses"}},{"k":"volume3d_cloud_cap","v":{"s":"The picture shows the most recent 2,400 darts so it stays readable — every dart still counts toward the numbers."}},{"k":"volume3d_dim_head","v":{"s":"Why does the sphere catch so few? "}},{"k":"volume3d_dim_body","v":{"s":"A circle fills 78.5% of its square (π⁄4). A sphere fills only 52.4% of its cube (π⁄6). Same shape, same snug fit — but a cube has 8 corners to a square’s 4, and corners are where the round thing isn’t. Keep adding dimensions and the ball all but vanishes: in 10D it catches about 1 dart in 400."}},{"k":"pause_auto_run","v":{"s":"Pause automatic simulation"}},{"k":"start_auto_run","v":{"s":"Start automatic simulation"}},{"k":"chi_na","v":{"s":"N/A here"}},{"k":"not_yet","v":{"s":"Not yet"}},{"k":"chi_not_independent","v":{"s":"this test needs independent draws — switch replacement back on"}},{"k":"chi_needs_trials","v":{"s":"needs "}},{"k":"chi_needs_trials_suffix","v":{"s":" trials (5 expected per outcome)"}},{"k":"volume_surveyor","v":{"s":"Volume Surveyor"}},{"k":"5000_darts_in_3d_within_0_01_of_the_tr","v":{"s":"5,000+ darts in 3D, estimate within 0.01 of the true volume"}},{"k":"bucket_low","v":{"s":"low"}},{"k":"bucket_mid","v":{"s":"mid"}},{"k":"bucket_high","v":{"s":"high"}},{"k":"sample_of_draws","v":{"s":"Sample of "}},{"k":"sample_of_draws_suffix","v":{"s":" draws"}},{"k":"new_sample","v":{"s":"🎲 New sample"}},{"k":"expected_vs_observed_label","v":{"s":"Expected versus observed: "}},{"k":"dashed_expected_bar_observed","v":{"s":"Dashed rule = expected. Bar = what these draws actually gave. Each square is one draw. Move a slider and both change together."}},{"k":"hypothesis_label","v":{"s":"Probability distribution hypothesis"}},{"k":"explanation_label","v":{"s":"Explain how relative weights produce the distribution shape"}},{"k":"compatible_with_model","v":{"s":"Compatible with the model. "}},{"k":"expected_inside_interval","v":{"s":"The theoretical probability falls inside this run's 95% interval, so the difference is plausible sampling variation."}},{"k":"expected_outside_interval","v":{"s":"The theoretical probability falls outside this run's 95% interval. One unusual sample can happen; collect more trials and use the fairness test before concluding the model is biased."}},{"k":"face_one","v":{"s":"face 1"}},{"k":"from_the_model","v":{"s":"from the model"}},{"k":"from_this_run","v":{"s":"from this run"}},{"k":"heads","v":{"s":"Heads"}},{"k":"inside_quarter_circle","v":{"s":"inside the quarter circle"}},{"k":"interval_band","v":{"s":"95% interval band"}},{"k":"interval_interpretation","v":{"s":"Interpretation: across many repeated experiments, about 95% of Wilson intervals built this way would cover the true probability."}},{"k":"interval_paused","v":{"s":"Interval paused: "}},{"k":"interval_requires_independent_draws","v":{"s":"without-replacement pulls are dependent because every pull changes the next probability. Switch replacement on to use a binomial confidence interval; keep it off to study changing conditional odds."}},{"k":"observed_marker","v":{"s":"Observed marker"}},{"k":"observed_probability","v":{"s":"Observed"}},{"k":"plausible_range","v":{"s":"95% interval"}},{"k":"sampling_uncertainty","v":{"s":"🎯 Sampling Uncertainty"}},{"k":"sampling_uncertainty_copy","v":{"s":"How much of the observed difference could be ordinary random variation?"}},{"k":"sum_label","v":{"s":"sum"}},{"k":"theoretical_marker","v":{"s":"Theoretical marker"}},{"k":"theoretical_probability","v":{"s":"Theoretical"}},{"k":"tracked_outcome","v":{"s":"Tracked outcome"}},{"k":"unusual_for_model","v":{"s":"Unusual for this model. "}},{"k":"wilson_95_interval","v":{"s":"Wilson 95% interval"}},{"k":"wilson_method","v":{"s":"Wilson method"}}],"id":566}},{"k":"punnett","v":{"o":[{"k":"sr_opening_dna_lab","v":{"s":"Opening DNA Lab"}},{"k":"a11y_close_lab_guide","v":{"s":"Close lab guide"}},{"k":"a11y_back_to_stem_tools","v":{"s":"Back to STEM tools"}},{"k":"a11y_toggle_badges","v":{"s":"Toggle badges"}},{"k":"a11y_toggle_ai_genetics_tutor","v":{"s":"Toggle AI genetics tutor"}},{"k":"a11y_genetics_lab_activities","v":{"s":"Genetics lab activities"}},{"k":"a11y_quest_progress","v":{"s":"Quest progress"}},{"k":"a11y_ask_the_genetics_tutor","v":{"s":"Ask the genetics tutor"}},{"k":"a11y_punnett_square_results_scroll_horizontally_on_s","v":{"s":"Punnett square results; scroll horizontally on small screens"}},{"k":"a11y_four_by_four_dihybrid_punnett_square_scroll_hor","v":{"s":"Four by four dihybrid Punnett square; scroll horizontally on small screens"}},{"k":"a11y_toggle_pedigree_solve_mode","v":{"s":"Toggle pedigree solve mode"}},{"k":"a11y_random_genetic_drift_stronger_in_small_populati","v":{"s":"Random genetic drift (stronger in small populations)"}},{"k":"a11y_reset_population_simulation","v":{"s":"Reset population simulation"}},{"k":"a11y_filter_traits_by_inheritance_model","v":{"s":"Filter traits by inheritance model"}},{"k":"a11y_dna_template_strand_sequence","v":{"s":"DNA template strand sequence"}},{"k":"a11y_sample_1","v":{"s":"Sample 1"}},{"k":"a11y_sample_2","v":{"s":"Sample 2"}},{"k":"a11y_translate","v":{"s":"Translate"}},{"k":"a11y_point_mutation","v":{"s":"Point Mutation"}},{"k":"a11y_insertion","v":{"s":"Insertion"}},{"k":"a11y_deletion","v":{"s":"Deletion"}},{"k":"a11y_revert_to_original","v":{"s":"Revert to Original"}},{"k":"a11y_select_challenge_difficulty","v":{"s":"Select challenge difficulty"}},{"k":"a11y_retry","v":{"s":"Retry"}},{"k":"a11y_start_battle","v":{"s":"Start Battle"}},{"k":"a11y_battle_again","v":{"s":"Battle 