y"}},{"k":"by_category","v":{"s":"By Category"}},{"k":"pick_1_topic","v":{"s":"Pick 1 topic"}},{"k":"weak_areas","v":{"s":"Weak Areas"}},{"k":"wrong_answers_pause_3s_on_explanation_","v":{"s":"• Wrong answers pause 3s on explanation — read it"}},{"k":"per_category_mastery_is_saved_across_s","v":{"s":"• Per-category mastery is saved across sessions"}},{"k":"your_mastery_by_category","v":{"s":"Your Mastery by Category"}},{"k":"permit_start","v":{"s":"← Permit Start"}},{"k":"practice_by_category","v":{"s":"📚 Practice by Category"}},{"k":"each_category_is_padded_to_a_20_questi","v":{"s":"Each category is padded to a 20-question test if the topic alone has fewer than 20 Qs."}},{"k":"retake","v":{"s":"🔁 Retake"}},{"k":"print_practice_pass_certificate","v":{"s":"Print practice-pass certificate"}},{"k":"maine_permit_practice_certificate_of_m","v":{"s":"Maine Permit Practice — Certificate of Mastery"}},{"k":"about_this_certificate","v":{"s":"About this certificate"}},{"k":"categories_tested","v":{"s":"Categories tested"}},{"k":"important","v":{"s":"Important"}},{"k":"print_certificate","v":{"s":"🖨 Print certificate"}},{"k":"menu_6","v":{"s":"🏠 Menu"}},{"k":"your_answer","v":{"s":"✗ Your answer: "}},{"k":"correct_answer","v":{"s":"✓ Correct answer: "}},{"k":"question_locked_in","v":{"s":"Question locked in"}},{"k":"correct","v":{"s":"✓ Correct. "}},{"k":"incorrect_why_this_matters","v":{"s":"✗ INCORRECT — WHY THIS MATTERS"}},{"k":"drive_debrief","v":{"s":"Drive Debrief"}},{"k":"cinematic_replay","v":{"s":"🎬 Cinematic Replay"}},{"k":"start_end_events","v":{"s":"● START · ● END · 🏅 events"}},{"k":"your_drive_path","v":{"s":"🗺️ Your Drive Path"}},{"k":"coach_s_feedback","v":{"s":"💡 Coach's Feedback"}},{"k":"following_too_close_use_the_3_second_r","v":{"s":"👀 Following too close. Use the 3-second rule. Pick a fixed point ahead. Count after the car in front passes it."}},{"k":"zero_crashes_that_is_the_baseline_real","v":{"s":"✅ Zero crashes! That is the baseline real drivers are measured against."}},{"k":"beat_the_epa_sticker_average_hypermili","v":{"s":"🌿 Beat the EPA sticker average. Hypermiling working!"}},{"k":"ai_reflection","v":{"s":"🧑‍🏫 AI Reflection"}},{"k":"generate","v":{"s":"✨ Generate"}},{"k":"new","v":{"s":"↺ New"}},{"k":"your_coach_is_thinking","v":{"s":"✨ Your coach is thinking..."}},{"k":"tap_generate_for_a_personalized_coachi","v":{"s":"Tap Generate for a personalized coaching reflection based on this drive."}},{"k":"explore_again","v":{"s":"🌎 Explore Again"}},{"k":"drive_again","v":{"s":"🔁 Drive Again"}},{"k":"menu_7","v":{"s":"🏠 Menu"}},{"k":"crash_replay","v":{"s":"🔄 Crash Replay"}},{"k":"certificate","v":{"s":"📜 Certificate"}},{"k":"drive_debrief_2","v":{"s":"← Drive Debrief"}},{"k":"coaching_debrief","v":{"s":"Coaching Debrief"}},{"k":"clean_drive_no_coaching_moments","v":{"s":"Clean drive — no coaching moments."}},{"k":"no_hard_brakes_tailgates_speed_violati","v":{"s":"No hard brakes, tailgates, speed violations, or crashes were logged. Keep it up."}},{"k":"menu_8","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"maine_winter_driving_survival_guide","v":{"s":"Maine Winter Driving Survival Guide"}},{"k":"the_skills_that_keep_mainers_alive_fro","v":{"s":"The skills that keep Mainers alive from November to April."}},{"k":"before_you_drive","v":{"s":"🧊 Before You Drive"}},{"k":"moose","v":{"s":"Moose"}},{"k":"deer","v":{"s":"Deer"}},{"k":"coastal_fog","v":{"s":"Coastal Fog"}},{"k":"studded_snow_tires","v":{"s":"Studded/Snow Tires"}},{"k":"the_physics_of_winter","v":{"s":"🔬 The Physics of Winter"}},{"k":"dry_road_friction_0_72_snow_0_22_ice_0","v":{"s":"Dry road friction μ ≈ 0.72. Snow ≈ 0.22. Ice ≈ 0.10. "}},{"k":"that_means_your_braking_distance_on_ic","v":{"s":"That means your braking distance on ice is "}},{"k":"7_longer","v":{"s":"7× longer"}},{"k":"than_on_dry_pavement","v":{"s":" than on dry pavement. "}},{"k":"at_40_mph_on_ice_stopping_distance_600","v":{"s":"At 40 mph on ice: stopping distance ≈ 600+ feet (two football fields). "}},{"k":"at_40_mph_on_dry_100_feet","v":{"s":"At 40 mph on dry: ≈ 100 feet. "}},{"k":"this_is_not_opinion_it_is_v_2_g","v":{"s":"This is not opinion — it is v²/(2μg)."}},{"k":"sensory_load","v":{"s":"Sensory load"}},{"k":"executive_function_planning_the_drive","v":{"s":"Executive function — planning the drive"}},{"k":"adhd_attention_regulation_behind_the_w","v":{"s":"ADHD — attention regulation behind the wheel"}},{"k":"autism_predictability_and_novel_situat","v":{"s":"Autism — predictability and novel situations"}},{"k":"anxiety_regulation_while_driving","v":{"s":"Anxiety — regulation while driving"}},{"k":"menu_9","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"neurodivergent_driver_guide_2","v":{"s":"Neurodivergent Driver Guide"}},{"k":"for_adhd_autistic_anxious_sensory_diff","v":{"s":"For ADHD, autistic, anxious, sensory-different, and executive-function-different drivers. The disability-relevant angles other driver's-ed material skips. Identity-first; designed by school-psych guidance."}},{"k":"concrete_strategies","v":{"s":"Concrete strategies"}},{"k":"road_test_accommodations_you_can_reque","v":{"s":"Road test accommodations you can request"}},{"k":"you_do_not_have_to_go_into_the_bmv_roa","v":{"s":"You do not have to go into the BMV road test cold. Maine BMV examiners can grant accommodations on request when there is a documented disability — sometimes with paperwork, sometimes just with a reasonable conversation. Common ones, the same kind a 504 plan covers in school:"}},{"k":"call_ahead_ask_what_documentation_they","v":{"s":"Call ahead. Ask what documentation they need. Going in with a script and a request beats showing up unprepared."}},{"k":"disclosure_when_how_to_whom","v":{"s":"Disclosure — when, how, to whom"}},{"k":"driving_instructor","v":{"s":"Driving instructor: "}},{"k":"disclosure_helps_they_can_pace_differe","v":{"s":"Disclosure helps. They can pace differently, repeat instructions, route around your specific stressors. A simple sentence works: \"I have ADHD. I will stay on task better if you tell me each instruction one at a time instead of stacking them.\""}},{"k":"bmv_road_test_examiner","v":{"s":"BMV road-test examiner: "}},{"k":"disclose_if_you_are_requesting_an_acco","v":{"s":"Disclose if you are requesting an accommodation. Otherwise it is your choice. Some students disclose to manage their own pre-test anxiety; others find that examiners react better to a calm, plain-spoken driver of any neurotype."}},{"k":"police_at_a_stop","v":{"s":"Police at a stop: "}},{"k":"optional_many_autistic_and_adhd_driver","v":{"s":"Optional. Many autistic and ADHD drivers carry a printed glovebox card to disclose without speaking — useful if speech production drops under stress. Sample text: \"I am autistic. I may need a moment to process what you are asking. I am not being rude or evasive.\""}},{"k":"insurance_company","v":{"s":"Insurance company: "}},{"k":"generally_not_required_and_can_affect_","v":{"s":"Generally not required and can affect rates. Most disability advocates say disclose only if a specific incident, accommodation, or claim makes it relevant."}},{"k":"sources","v":{"s":"📚 Sources: "}},{"k":"drexel_autism_driving_project_peer_rev","v":{"s":"Drexel Autism Driving Project (peer-reviewed research on autistic driver outcomes); ADDitude Magazine + Russell Barkley's ADHD-and-driving research summaries; CHADD position statements on stimulant medication and driving safety; Autism Self Advocacy Network disclosure guidance; Maine BMV examiner-policy documentation. Identity-first language follows community-consensus norms (Kenny 2016, Bury 2020)."}},{"k":"menu_10","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"night_vision_training_2","v":{"s":"Night Vision Training"}},{"k":"a_focused_drill_headlights_sign_readin","v":{"s":"A focused drill. Headlights, sign reading, and scanning for what the dark hides."}},{"k":"what_you_ll_practice","v":{"s":"What you'll practice:"}},{"k":"reading_speed_limit_signs_at_low_light","v":{"s":"Reading speed limit signs at low light from your headlight cone."}},{"k":"spotting_pedestrians_and_cyclists_wear","v":{"s":"Spotting pedestrians and cyclists wearing dark clothing."}},{"k":"switching_low_high_beams_correctly_whe","v":{"s":"Switching low/high beams correctly when cars approach."}},{"k":"pacing_yourself_at_50_mph_at_night_you","v":{"s":"Pacing yourself — at 50+ mph at night you outdrive your headlights."}},{"k":"coach_prompts_during_the_drill","v":{"s":"🎙️ Coach prompts during the drill:"}},{"k":"every_25_40_seconds_your_coach_will_is","v":{"s":"Every 25–40 seconds your coach will issue a scanning prompt — what speed limit is up ahead, did you spot the pedestrian, etc. Answer aloud or just notice. The drill emphasizes habit, not grading."}},{"k":"start_night_drill","v":{"s":"🌃 Start Night Drill"}},{"k":"menu_11","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"parent_ride_check_2","v":{"s":"Parent Ride Check"}},{"k":"a_2_minute_structured_eval_you_ride_al","v":{"s":"A 2-minute structured eval. You ride along, tap to mark mistakes, get a clear coaching priority at the end."}},{"k":"how_it_works","v":{"s":"How it works:"}},{"k":"1_pick_a_scenario_your_learner_is_comf","v":{"s":"1. Pick a scenario your learner is comfortable with."}},{"k":"2_they_drive_you_watch","v":{"s":"2. They drive — you watch."}},{"k":"3_tap_one_of_the_colored_category_butt","v":{"s":"3. Tap one of the colored category buttons each time you see an issue (Speed, Signal, Following, Lane, Scan, Stop)."}},{"k":"4_after_2_minutes_you_get_a_one_page_c","v":{"s":"4. After 2 minutes, you get a one-page coaching summary you can save or print."}},{"k":"choose_scenario","v":{"s":"Choose scenario"}},{"k":"start_2_min_eval","v":{"s":"👨‍👧 Start 2-min Eval"}},{"k":"view_last_report","v":{"s":"📋 View Last Report"}},{"k":"menu_12","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"parent_ride_check_report","v":{"s":"Parent Ride Check Report"}},{"k":"errors_by_category","v":{"s":"Errors by Category"}},{"k":"coaching_priority","v":{"s":"🎯 COACHING PRIORITY"}},{"k":"no_errors_marked_great_drive_keep_prac","v":{"s":"🌟 No errors marked! Great drive — keep practicing similar scenarios."}},{"k":"export_report_markdown","v":{"s":"📋 Export Report (Markdown)"}},{"k":"menu_13","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"road_test_simulator_2","v":{"s":"Road Test Simulator"}},{"k":"a_4_minute_scored_exam_modeled_on_the_","v":{"s":"A 4-minute scored exam modeled on the Maine BMV road test. 100 pts — 90+ passes."}},{"k":"walk_around_vehicle_check_20_items_che","v":{"s":"Walk-around vehicle check. 20+ items checked required."}},{"k":"2_scored_driving_4_minutes","v":{"s":"2. Scored Driving (4 minutes)"}},{"k":"suburban_scenario_follow_speed_limits_","v":{"s":"Suburban scenario. Follow speed limits, signal all turns, full stops, keep lane."}},{"k":"start_drive","v":{"s":"Start Drive"}},{"k":"scoring_rubric_maine_bmv_style","v":{"s":"📋 Scoring Rubric (Maine BMV style)"}},{"k":"starts_at_100_90_pass","v":{"s":"• Starts at 100. 90+ = PASS."}},{"k":"speeding_5_15_over_1_per_second_max_10","v":{"s":"• Speeding 5-15 over: -1 per second (max -10)."}},{"k":"speeding_15_over_3_per_second_auto_fai","v":{"s":"• Speeding 15+ over: -3 per second (auto-fail at -18)."}},{"k":"unsignaled_lane_change_4_each","v":{"s":"• Unsignaled lane change: -4 each."}},{"k":"crash_any_speed_25_and_typically_auto_","v":{"s":"• Crash (any speed): -25 and typically auto-fail."}},{"k":"hard_brake_close_follow_skid_each_reco","v":{"s":"• Hard brake, close follow, skid: each recorded."}},{"k":"view_last_test_result","v":{"s":"📄 View Last Test Result"}},{"k":"menu_14","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"clean_drive_no_deductions_recorded","v":{"s":"🌟 Clean drive — no deductions recorded."}},{"k":"retry_test","v":{"s":"🪪 Retry Test"}},{"k":"menu_15","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"driving_logbook_2","v":{"s":"Driving Logbook"}},{"k":"print_logbook_for_parent_or_instructor","v":{"s":"Print logbook for parent or instructor"}},{"k":"roadready_practice_driving_log","v":{"s":"RoadReady — Practice Driving Log"}},{"k":"sessions_newest_first","v":{"s":"Sessions (newest first)"}},{"k":"parent_instructor_signature","v":{"s":"Parent / instructor signature"}},{"k":"note","v":{"s":"Note"}},{"k":"print_log_for_parent_instructor","v":{"s":"🖨 Print log for parent / instructor"}},{"k":"maine_70_hour_supervised_driving_progr","v":{"s":"Maine 70-hour supervised driving progress"}},{"k":"no_sessions_yet_complete_a_drive_to_st","v":{"s":"📝 No sessions yet. Complete a drive to start your logbook."}},{"k":"export_full_logbook_markdown","v":{"s":"📔 Export Full Logbook (Markdown)"}},{"k":"menu_16","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"scenarios_2","v":{"s":"Scenarios"}},{"k":"passed","v":{"s":"✓ PASSED"}},{"k":"retry_2","v":{"s":"✗ RETRY"}},{"k":"retry_3","v":{"s":"↺ Retry"}},{"k":"roundabout_drill","v":{"s":"Roundabout Drill"}},{"k":"maine_is_adding_these_fast","v":{"s":"Maine is adding these fast"}},{"k":"traffic_flows_counterclockwise","v":{"s":"Traffic flows counterclockwise"}},{"k":"in_the_u_s_all_roundabouts_circulate_c","v":{"s":"In the U.S., all roundabouts circulate counterclockwise. You enter to the right and exit to the right. Signal right as you approach your exit."}},{"k":"yield_don_t_stop","v":{"s":"Yield, don't stop"}},{"k":"at_entry_you_yield_to_traffic_already_","v":{"s":"At entry, you yield to traffic already IN the circle — but don't come to a hard stop if you can see a gap. Flow through. Inside the circle, never stop (except if forced by a crash ahead)."}},{"k":"pedestrians_at_every_exit","v":{"s":"Pedestrians at every exit"}},{"k":"marked_crosswalks_sit_just_outside_eac","v":{"s":"Marked crosswalks sit just outside each entry and exit. Yield to pedestrians ALWAYS — whether you're entering or leaving the circle."}},{"k":"trucks_may_use_both_lanes","v":{"s":"Trucks may use both lanes"}},{"k":"large_trucks_school_buses_and_emergenc","v":{"s":"Large trucks, school buses, and emergency vehicles often need to track both lanes of a multi-lane roundabout to clear the curb. Don't crowd them or try to pass inside."}},{"k":"entering_with_traffic_in_the_circle","v":{"s":"Entering with traffic in the circle"}},{"k":"ambulance_behind_while_you_re_circulat","v":{"s":"Ambulance behind while you're circulating"}},{"k":"truck_using_both_lanes","v":{"s":"Truck using both lanes"}},{"k":"which_lane_for_which_exit","v":{"s":"Which lane for which exit?"}},{"k":"pedestrian_at_your_exit","v":{"s":"Pedestrian at your exit"}},{"k":"how_do_you_signal","v":{"s":"How do you signal?"}},{"k":"oui_impaired_driving_drill","v":{"s":"OUI / Impaired-Driving Drill"}},{"k":"maine_limits_zero_tolerance_implied_co","v":{"s":"Maine limits, zero-tolerance, implied consent"}},{"k":"legal_limits","v":{"s":"Legal limits"}},{"k":"maine_0_08_bac_for_21_zero_tolerance_0","v":{"s":"Maine: 0.08 BAC for 21+. Zero tolerance — no alcohol level over 0.00 — for under-21/provisional drivers. For commercial drivers, 0.04. Any measurable alcohol under 21 can trigger suspension."}},{"k":"implied_consent","v":{"s":"Implied consent"}},{"k":"driving_on_a_maine_road_is_legal_conse","v":{"s":"Driving on a Maine road is legal consent to breath/blood testing when an officer has probable cause. First refusal triggers a 275-day license suspension; repeat refusals are longer and refusal can be used in court."}},{"k":"drugs_count_too","v":{"s":"Drugs count too"}},{"k":"prescription_medical_marijuana_otc_col","v":{"s":"Prescription, medical marijuana, OTC cold medicine, even \"legal\" recreational cannabis — if it impairs you, driving on it is OUI (Operating Under the Influence). \"The doctor prescribed it\" is not a defense."}},{"k":"one_drink_math","v":{"s":"One-drink math"}},{"k":"a_130_lb_teenager_drops_below_maine_s_","v":{"s":"One 12-oz beer can leave a teen above Maine's under-21 0.00 standard for hours. Food, fatigue, and body composition shift the curve — you can't reliably \"feel\" your BAC."}},{"k":"just_one_mile_pressure","v":{"s":"\"Just one mile\" pressure"}},{"k":"breath_test_refusal","v":{"s":"Breath test refusal"}},{"k":"prescribed_painkiller","v":{"s":"Prescribed painkiller"}},{"k":"zero_tolerance_at_20","v":{"s":"Zero tolerance at 20"}},{"k":"recreational_marijuana_driving","v":{"s":"Recreational marijuana + driving"}},{"k":"first_offense_consequences","v":{"s":"First-offense consequences"}},{"k":"runaway_red","v":{"s":"Runaway Red"}},{"k":"cyclist_swerve","v":{"s":"Cyclist Swerve"}},{"k":"rain_tailgater","v":{"s":"Rain Tailgater"}},{"k":"deer_at_dusk","v":{"s":"Deer at Dusk"}},{"k":"forced_merge","v":{"s":"Forced Merge"}},{"k":"ball_in_street","v":{"s":"Ball in Street"}},{"k":"hydroplane","v":{"s":"Hydroplane"}},{"k":"ambulance_behind","v":{"s":"Ambulance Behind"}},{"k":"menu_17","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"defensive_driving_drills","v":{"s":"Defensive Driving Drills"}},{"k":"passed_2","v":{"s":"✓ PASSED"}},{"k":"retry_4","v":{"s":"✗ RETRY"}},{"k":"retry_5","v":{"s":"↺ Retry"}},{"k":"by_the_numbers","v":{"s":"By the numbers"}},{"k":"maine_has_roughly_500_700_reported_moo","v":{"s":"Maine has roughly 500–700 reported moose–vehicle collisions per year. The state averages 3–5 fatal moose crashes annually."}},{"k":"worst_times","v":{"s":"Worst times"}},{"k":"dawn_and_dusk_low_light_plus_late_may_","v":{"s":"Dawn and dusk (low light) plus late May through June (calves) and September–November (the rut). Overnight hours are dangerous too — moose are dark and blend into the road."}},{"k":"why_swerving_fails","v":{"s":"Why swerving fails"}},{"k":"a_full_grown_moose_weighs_800_1_400_lb","v":{"s":"A full-grown moose weighs 800–1,400 lb. Its mass sits on long legs — your bumper takes the legs out and the body comes through the windshield. Roof-crush is the usual cause of death, not the impact itself."}},{"k":"maine_zones","v":{"s":"Maine zones"}},{"k":"route_201_route_2_route_6_route_11_nor","v":{"s":"Route 201, Route 2, Route 6, Route 11 north of Bangor, and the entire Moosehead Lake region are the highest-risk corridors. Yellow moose-warning signs mark known crossings — slow down and scan."}},{"k":"high_beams_2","v":{"s":"High beams"}},{"k":"in_moose_country_and_zero_oncoming_tra","v":{"s":"In moose country and zero oncoming traffic, use high beams. A moose's eyes don't always reflect like a deer's, but its body outline appears sooner. Dim for oncoming cars, then pop them back on."}},{"k":"if_impact_is_unavoidable","v":{"s":"If impact is unavoidable"}},{"k":"brake_hard_let_up_just_before_impact_h","v":{"s":"Brake hard, let up just before impact (helps the hood absorb force), duck your head low toward the wheel. This moves your skull below the predicted windshield-crush line."}},{"k":"moose_in_the_lane_at_dusk","v":{"s":"Moose in the lane at dusk"}},{"k":"cow_and_calf","v":{"s":"Cow and calf"}},{"k":"dark_shape_on_the_shoulder","v":{"s":"Dark shape on the shoulder"}},{"k":"moose_crossing_with_oncoming_traffic","v":{"s":"Moose crossing with oncoming traffic"}},{"k":"after_the_near_miss","v":{"s":"After the near-miss"}},{"k":"fog_in_a_moose_zone","v":{"s":"Fog in a moose zone"}},{"k":"menu_18","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"moose_encounter_drill","v":{"s":"Moose Encounter Drill"}},{"k":"before_the_drill_six_things_to_know","v":{"s":"Before the drill: six things to know"}},{"k":"scenarios_3","v":{"s":"Scenarios"}},{"k":"passed_3","v":{"s":"✓ PASSED"}},{"k":"retry_6","v":{"s":"✗ RETRY"}},{"k":"retry_7","v":{"s":"↺ Retry"}},{"k":"maine_law","v":{"s":"Maine law"}},{"k":"title_29_a_2054_when_an_emergency_vehi","v":{"s":"Title 29-A §2054: when an emergency vehicle with lights and siren approaches, pull as far right as practicable, clear of intersections, and stop until it passes. Failing to yield is a Class E crime with a minimum fine."}},{"k":"move_over_law","v":{"s":"Move Over law"}},{"k":"maine_2054_a_when_passing_a_stopped_em","v":{"s":"Maine §2070(8): when passing a stationary disabled or flashing-light vehicle, move to a non-adjacent lane if possible. If not, pass at a careful and prudent speed reasonable for safety."}},{"k":"why_it_matters","v":{"s":"Why it matters"}},{"k":"every_year_roadside_workers_and_respon","v":{"s":"Every year roadside workers and responders die on Maine shoulders because drivers don't move over. The law exists because \"rubbernecking at 65 mph\" kills people."}},{"k":"don_t_stop_mid_intersection","v":{"s":"Don't stop mid-intersection"}},{"k":"if_you_re_inside_an_intersection_when_","v":{"s":"If you're inside an intersection when you hear a siren, CLEAR the intersection first, then pull right. Stopping in the intersection blocks the emergency vehicle's path."}},{"k":"siren_behind_you_on_a_2_lane","v":{"s":"Siren behind you on a 2-lane"}},{"k":"siren_at_an_intersection","v":{"s":"Siren at an intersection"}},{"k":"oncoming_on_a_divided_highway","v":{"s":"Oncoming on a divided highway"}},{"k":"oncoming_on_an_undivided_road","v":{"s":"Oncoming on an undivided road"}},{"k":"stopped_cruiser_on_the_shoulder","v":{"s":"Stopped cruiser on the shoulder"}},{"k":"multiple_vehicles_in_response","v":{"s":"Multiple vehicles in response"}},{"k":"menu_19","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"emergency_vehicle_drill","v":{"s":"Emergency Vehicle Drill"}},{"k":"all_correct_you_know_the_rules","v":{"s":"✓ All correct — you know the rules."}},{"k":"key_rules","v":{"s":"Key rules"}},{"k":"scenarios_4","v":{"s":"Scenarios"}},{"k":"passed_4","v":{"s":"✓ PASSED"}},{"k":"retry_8","v":{"s":"✗ RETRY"}},{"k":"retry_9","v":{"s":"↺ Retry"}},{"k":"the_maine_rule","v":{"s":"The Maine rule"}},{"k":"title_29_a_2308_when_a_school_bus_is_s","v":{"s":"Title 29-A §2308: when a school bus is stopped with red lights flashing, traffic meeting or overtaking from either direction must stop. Opposite-direction traffic is excepted only when separated by curbing or another physical barrier, or under the limited-access/loading-zone exception."}},{"k":"yellow_vs_red","v":{"s":"Yellow vs red"}},{"k":"yellow_flashers_bus_is_about_to_stop_r","v":{"s":"Yellow flashers = bus is about to stop. Red flashers + stop arm = you must stop. The transition is your cue to slow down, not to speed past."}},{"k":"how_far_back","v":{"s":"How far back"}},{"k":"stop_far_enough_back_that_the_bus_driv","v":{"s":"Stop far enough back that the bus driver can see you (rule of thumb: at least 20 ft). Children cross from BOTH sides unpredictably — tight stopping is dangerous."}},{"k":"penalties","v":{"s":"Penalties"}},{"k":"passing_a_stopped_school_bus_in_maine_","v":{"s":"Passing a stopped school bus in Maine is a Class E crime. First offense: $250 minimum fine. A 2nd offense within 3 years carries a mandatory 30-day license suspension."}},{"k":"bus_stopped_ahead_in_your_direction","v":{"s":"Bus stopped ahead in your direction"}},{"k":"bus_stopped_in_opposite_lane_undivided","v":{"s":"Bus stopped in opposite lane (undivided road)"}},{"k":"bus_stopped_in_opposite_direction_on_a","v":{"s":"Bus stopped in opposite direction on a divided highway"}},{"k":"yellow_flashers_not_red_yet","v":{"s":"Yellow flashers, not red yet"}},{"k":"bus_stopped_on_a_neighborhood_street","v":{"s":"Bus stopped on a neighborhood street"}},{"k":"menu_20","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"school_bus_stop_drill","v":{"s":"School Bus Stop Drill"}},{"k":"all_correct_you_ll_stop_when_it_counts","v":{"s":"✓ All correct — you'll stop when it counts."}},{"k":"key_rules_2","v":{"s":"Key rules"}},{"k":"scenarios_5","v":{"s":"Scenarios"}},{"k":"passed_5","v":{"s":"✓ PASSED"}},{"k":"retry_10","v":{"s":"✗ RETRY"}},{"k":"retry_11","v":{"s":"↺ Retry"}},{"k":"the_law","v":{"s":"The law"}},{"k":"flashing_red_lights_at_a_crossing_mean","v":{"s":"Flashing red lights at a crossing mean STOP — treat them like a red traffic light. Never drive around lowered gates. If a gate appears stuck or a vehicle is trapped, call the posted crossing number or 911."}},{"k":"train_physics","v":{"s":"Train physics"}},{"k":"at_55_mph_a_freight_train_needs_over_1","v":{"s":"At 55 mph a freight train needs over 1 mile (≈ 6,000 ft) to stop. A 100-car train weighs roughly 18,000 tons — the equivalent of ~3,000 cars."}},{"k":"the_speed_illusion","v":{"s":"The speed illusion"}},{"k":"large_objects_appear_to_move_slower_th","v":{"s":"Large objects appear to move slower than they are. A train you judge \"distant and slow\" is usually moving 45–80 mph and covering 80+ feet per second."}},{"k":"if_you_stall_on_the_tracks","v":{"s":"If you stall on the tracks"}},{"k":"everyone_out_run_at_a_45_angle_toward_","v":{"s":"Everyone OUT. Run AT A 45° ANGLE TOWARD the oncoming train. Debris from an impact launches FORWARD in the train's direction of travel — running toward the train puts you behind the debris field."}},{"k":"flashing_red_lights_gates_down","v":{"s":"Flashing red lights, gates down"}},{"k":"i_can_beat_that_train","v":{"s":"\"I can beat that train\""}},{"k":"stalled_on_the_tracks","v":{"s":"Stalled on the tracks"}},{"k":"second_train_hidden","v":{"s":"Second train hidden"}},{"k":"rural_crossbuck_no_lights","v":{"s":"Rural crossbuck, no lights"}},{"k":"humped_low_clearance_crossing","v":{"s":"Humped / low-clearance crossing"}},{"k":"menu_21","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"railroad_crossing_drill","v":{"s":"Railroad Crossing Drill"}},{"k":"all_correct_you_know_the_rules_that_sa","v":{"s":"✓ All correct — you know the rules that save lives at crossings."}},{"k":"before_the_drill_four_things_to_know","v":{"s":"Before the drill: four things to know"}},{"k":"scenarios_6","v":{"s":"Scenarios"}},{"k":"passed_6","v":{"s":"✓ PASSED"}},{"k":"retry_12","v":{"s":"✗ RETRY"}},{"k":"retry_13","v":{"s":"↺ Retry"}},{"k":"black_ice_the_trap","v":{"s":"Black ice: the trap"}},{"k":"black_ice_forms_between_28_f_and_38_f_","v":{"s":"Black ice forms between 28°F and 38°F — it doesn't need to be below freezing. Highest risk: bridges and overpasses (cold air on both sides), shaded curves, and pre-dawn hours. The surface looks wet, not icy."}},{"k":"winter_tires_actually_matter","v":{"s":"Winter tires actually matter"}},{"k":"all_season_tires_lose_roughly_40_of_th","v":{"s":"All-season tires lose roughly 40% of their grip below 20°F because the rubber stiffens. Dedicated winter tires stay flexible and can halve your stopping distance on snow. Maine law allows studs Oct 1–May 1."}},{"k":"two_kinds_of_skid","v":{"s":"Two kinds of skid"}},{"k":"rear_wheel_skid_oversteer_tail_swings_","v":{"s":"Rear-wheel skid (oversteer): tail swings out — steer INTO the skid, toward where the front of the car is pointed. Front-wheel skid (understeer): car plows straight — ease off the throttle, don't add more steering."}},{"k":"4wd_doesn_t_help_you_stop","v":{"s":"4WD doesn't help you stop"}},{"k":"four_wheel_drive_and_awd_help_with_tra","v":{"s":"Four-wheel drive and AWD help with traction for ACCELERATION. Braking is identical to a 2WD car — same four brakes, same tires. A false sense of security in 4WD kills people every Maine winter."}},{"k":"snowplows","v":{"s":"Snowplows"}},{"k":"never_pass_a_plow_on_the_right_the_bla","v":{"s":"Never pass a plow on the right — the blade throws snow and debris that direction. Stay 4+ truck lengths back. Plows often travel 30–40 mph even on highways; that slow-moving orange light is your safest speed too."}},{"k":"windshield_roof","v":{"s":"Windshield + roof"}},{"k":"maine_2396_b_requires_a_clear_view_thr","v":{"s":"Maine §2093 requires reasonable measures to prevent snow or ice from falling off vehicles under 10,000 lb. Safest practice: clear the roof, windows, lights, and hood before driving."}},{"k":"hitting_black_ice","v":{"s":"Hitting black ice"}},{"k":"following_distance_on_snow","v":{"s":"Following distance on snow"}},{"k":"tail_swinging_out_oversteer","v":{"s":"Tail swinging out (oversteer)"}},{"k":"plowing_straight_understeer","v":{"s":"Plowing straight (understeer)"}},{"k":"passing_a_snowplow","v":{"s":"Passing a snowplow"}},{"k":"the_4wd_myth","v":{"s":"The 4WD myth"}},{"k":"menu_22","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"winter_driving_drill","v":{"s":"Winter Driving Drill"}},{"k":"all_correct_ready_for_your_first_maine","v":{"s":"✓ All correct — ready for your first Maine January."}},{"k":"before_the_drill_six_things_to_know_2","v":{"s":"Before the drill: six things to know"}},{"k":"scenarios_7","v":{"s":"Scenarios"}},{"k":"passed_7","v":{"s":"✓ PASSED"}},{"k":"retry_14","v":{"s":"✗ RETRY"}},{"k":"retry_15","v":{"s":"↺ Retry"}},{"k":"fines_are_doubled","v":{"s":"Construction speed fines"}},{"k":"maine_law_fines_are_doubled_in_posted_","v":{"s":"Maine law doubles fines for violations of restricted construction or maintenance speed limits posted with black-and-white speed-limit signs. Treat the restriction as active while those signs are displayed."}},{"k":"flaggers_are_the_law","v":{"s":"Flaggers are the law"}},{"k":"inside_a_work_zone_a_flagger_s_instruc","v":{"s":"Inside a work zone, a flagger's instructions override every other traffic control device — including traffic lights. Flagger STOP paddle means stop even if your light is green."}},{"k":"orange_temporary","v":{"s":"Orange = temporary"}},{"k":"orange_signs_and_barrels_always_mean_a","v":{"s":"Orange signs and barrels always mean a temporary traffic pattern. Pay extra attention: lanes shift, speed limits drop, and your GPS map may be wrong."}},{"k":"pilot_cars_one_way_zones","v":{"s":"Pilot cars & one-way zones"}},{"k":"a_follow_me_pilot_car_leads_traffic_th","v":{"s":"A \"FOLLOW ME\" pilot car leads traffic through a single-lane section where traffic alternates direction. Passing the pilot puts you head-on with opposing traffic waiting their turn."}},{"k":"flagger_with_stop_paddle","v":{"s":"Flagger with STOP paddle"}},{"k":"flagger_flips_to_slow","v":{"s":"Flagger flips to SLOW"}},{"k":"lane_closure_merge","v":{"s":"Lane closure merge"}},{"k":"worker_on_the_shoulder","v":{"s":"Worker on the shoulder"}},{"k":"gap_in_the_barrel_line","v":{"s":"Gap in the barrel line"}},{"k":"pilot_car_leading_traffic","v":{"s":"Pilot car leading traffic"}},{"k":"menu_23","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"construction_zone_drill","v":{"s":"Construction Zone Drill"}},{"k":"all_correct_safe_in_any_work_zone","v":{"s":"✓ All correct — safe in any work zone."}},{"k":"key_rules_3","v":{"s":"Key rules"}},{"k":"scenarios_8","v":{"s":"Scenarios"}},{"k":"passed_8","v":{"s":"✓ PASSED"}},{"k":"retry_16","v":{"s":"✗ RETRY"}},{"k":"retry_17","v":{"s":"↺ Retry"}},{"k":"three_phases","v":{"s":"Three phases"}},{"k":"maine_gdl_learner_s_permit_at_15_w_dri","v":{"s":"Maine GDL: Learner's Permit at 15 with driver's ed for applicants under 18. Intermediate License at 16 after holding the permit 6+ months and logging 70 supervised hours. Passenger, curfew, and device restrictions last 270 days and can extend if violated."}},{"k":"70_supervised_hours","v":{"s":"70 supervised hours"}},{"k":"before_the_road_test_maine_requires_70","v":{"s":"Before a license for an applicant under 21, Maine requires 70 hours of supervised driving, including 10 at night. These hours get certified on the driving log before the road test."}},{"k":"phones_zero_tolerance","v":{"s":"Phones — zero tolerance"}},{"k":"under_18_all_mobile_device_use_is_bann","v":{"s":"Under 18: all mobile-device interaction is banned while driving, including hands-free and GPS input. During the intermediate period, violations can bring a $250-$500 fine, a 60-day first-offense suspension, and another 270 days of restrictions."}},{"k":"the_clock_resets","v":{"s":"The clock resets"}},{"k":"a_moving_violation_conviction_during_i","v":{"s":"An intermediate-license restriction violation extends your passenger, curfew, and device restrictions by another 270 days. It can also mean a $250-$500 fine and license suspension."}},{"k":"friends_want_a_ride","v":{"s":"Friends want a ride"}},{"k":"the_2_am_diner_run","v":{"s":"The 2 AM diner run"}},{"k":"hands_free_call","v":{"s":"Hands-free call"}},{"k":"how_many_hours","v":{"s":"How many hours?"}},{"k":"ticket_consequence","v":{"s":"Ticket consequence"}},{"k":"sibling_to_practice","v":{"s":"Sibling to practice"}},{"k":"menu_24","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"teen_gdl_drill","v":{"s":