on your device only)"}},{"k":"birth_date","v":{"s":"Birth date"}},{"k":"permit_issued","v":{"s":"Permit issued"}},{"k":"intermediate_license_2","v":{"s":"Intermediate license"}},{"k":"current_stage","v":{"s":"Current stage"}},{"k":"your_current_restrictions","v":{"s":"⚠️ Your current restrictions"}},{"k":"no_active_restrictions_at_this_stage","v":{"s":"No active restrictions at this stage."}},{"k":"70_hour_supervised_driving_progress_fr","v":{"s":"📔 Simulator practice logged"}},{"k":"note_the_70_hour_maine_requirement_is_","v":{"s":"Maine separately requires 70 hours of real supervised driving, 10 of them at night, before the road test. Simulator hours do not count toward those 70 — that log is kept with a licensed adult in a real car."}},{"k":"10_permit_questions","v":{"s":"10 Permit Questions"}},{"k":"take_a_10_question_mini_permit_quiz_pa","v":{"s":"Take a 10-question mini permit quiz. Pass at 8/10."}},{"k":"get_8_or_more_correct","v":{"s":"Get 8 or more correct"}},{"k":"residential_run","v":{"s":"Residential Run"}},{"k":"complete_a_residential_scenario_drive_","v":{"s":"Complete a residential scenario drive with safety 85+."}},{"k":"safety_score_85_or_higher","v":{"s":"Safety score 85 or higher"}},{"k":"wet_pavement_master","v":{"s":"Wet Pavement Master"}},{"k":"complete_a_rain_scenario_with_zero_cra","v":{"s":"Complete a rain scenario with zero crashes and safety 75+."}},{"k":"safety_75_no_crashes","v":{"s":"Safety 75+, no crashes"}},{"k":"flashcard_sprint","v":{"s":"Flashcard Sprint"}},{"k":"review_15_permit_flashcards","v":{"s":"Review 15 permit flashcards."}},{"k":"15_flashcards_in_one_session","v":{"s":"15 flashcards in one session"}},{"k":"defensive_drill","v":{"s":"Defensive Drill"}},{"k":"complete_3_defensive_driving_scenarios","v":{"s":"Complete 3 defensive driving scenarios correctly."}},{"k":"3_defensive_scenarios_passed","v":{"s":"3 defensive scenarios passed"}},{"k":"diagnose_3_warnings","v":{"s":"Diagnose 3 Warnings"}},{"k":"correctly_identify_3_dashboard_warning","v":{"s":"Correctly identify 3 dashboard warning lights."}},{"k":"3_correct_in_maintenance_game","v":{"s":"3 correct in Maintenance Game"}},{"k":"right_of_way_review","v":{"s":"Right-of-Way Review"}},{"k":"nail_8_10_on_the_right_of_way_scenario","v":{"s":"Nail 8/10 on the Right-of-Way scenarios."}},{"k":"8_or_more_on_right_of_way","v":{"s":"8 or more on Right-of-Way"}},{"k":"night_driving_2","v":{"s":"Night Driving"}},{"k":"complete_a_night_drive_with_safety_75","v":{"s":"Complete a night drive with safety 75+."}},{"k":"safety_75","v":{"s":"Safety 75+"}},{"k":"parking_pro","v":{"s":"Parking Pro"}},{"k":"finish_the_parallel_parking_drill","v":{"s":"Finish the parallel parking drill."}},{"k":"complete_parallel_parking","v":{"s":"Complete parallel parking"}},{"k":"signs_quiz","v":{"s":"Signs Quiz"}},{"k":"score_8_10_on_the_road_signs_quiz","v":{"s":"Score 8/10 on the road signs quiz."}},{"k":"8_or_more_on_signs_quiz","v":{"s":"8 or more on signs quiz"}},{"k":"distracted_reality_check","v":{"s":"Distracted Reality Check"}},{"k":"visit_the_distracted_driving_lab_try_3","v":{"s":"Visit the Distracted Driving Lab. Try 3 different speed/glance combos."}},{"k":"read_the_lab_results","v":{"s":"Read the lab results"}},{"k":"reaction_baseline","v":{"s":"Reaction Baseline"}},{"k":"take_the_reaction_test_and_record_your","v":{"s":"Take the Reaction Test and record your baseline."}},{"k":"complete_one_reaction_test","v":{"s":"Complete one reaction test"}},{"k":"emergency_review","v":{"s":"Emergency Review"}},{"k":"read_2_emergency_scenarios_from_the_ha","v":{"s":"Read 2 emergency scenarios from the handbook."}},{"k":"read_2_emergency_procedures","v":{"s":"Read 2 emergency procedures"}},{"k":"menu_35","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"daily_challenge_2","v":{"s":"Daily Challenge"}},{"k":"goal","v":{"s":"🎯 Goal: "}},{"k":"start_challenge","v":{"s":"🚀 Start Challenge"}},{"k":"mark_done","v":{"s":"✓ Mark Done"}},{"k":"you_re_done_for_today_come_back_tomorr","v":{"s":"🎉 You're done for today! Come back tomorrow for a new challenge."}},{"k":"why_streaks_matter","v":{"s":"🔥 Why streaks matter"}},{"k":"daily_practice_beats_cramming_15_minut","v":{"s":"Daily practice beats cramming. 15 minutes a day for 30 days = 7.5 hours of spaced repetition — far more effective for passing the permit test than one 7-hour session."}},{"k":"the_streak_also_builds_the_habit_of","v":{"s":"The streak also builds the habit of "}},{"k":"thinking_about_driving_before_you_have","v":{"s":"thinking about driving before you have to do it for real"}},{"k":"which_is_exactly_what_good_drivers_do","v":{"s":" — which is exactly what good drivers do."}},{"k":"step_1_seat_distance","v":{"s":"Step 1: Seat Distance"}},{"k":"pedals_should_be_reachable_without_str","v":{"s":"Pedals should be reachable without stretching your leg fully."}},{"k":"press_the_brake_pedal_all_the_way_to_t","v":{"s":"Press the brake pedal ALL THE WAY to the floor. Your knee should still have a SLIGHT bend (about 20-30°). If your knee locks, you're too far back. If it's too bent, you're too close."}},{"k":"slight_bend","v":{"s":"✓ Slight bend"}},{"k":"step_2_seat_height_back_angle","v":{"s":"Step 2: Seat Height + Back Angle"}},{"k":"eyes_level_with_top_of_steering_wheel_","v":{"s":"Eyes level with top of steering wheel. Backrest nearly vertical (100-110°)."}},{"k":"raise_the_seat_until_your_eyes_are_lev","v":{"s":"Raise the seat until your EYES are level with the TOP of the steering wheel — you should see over it, not through it. Tilt the backrest slightly back (100-110° from vertical). Your back should touch the seat from tailbone to shoulders."}},{"k":"eye_level","v":{"s":"eye level"}},{"k":"step_3_headrest_height","v":{"s":"Step 3: Headrest Height"}},{"k":"top_of_headrest_even_with_the_top_of_y","v":{"s":"Top of headrest even with the TOP of your head — not your neck."}},{"k":"the_headrest_is_actually_a_head_restra","v":{"s":"The headrest is actually a HEAD restraint — it catches your HEAD in a rear-end collision. Raise it until its top is level with the crown of your head. The face should be no more than 4 inches from the back of your head."}},{"k":"level_w_head_top","v":{"s":"← level w/ head top"}},{"k":"step_4_steering_wheel_position","v":{"s":"Step 4: Steering Wheel Position"}},{"k":"wheel_10_12_inches_from_chest_hands_at","v":{"s":"Wheel 10-12 inches from chest. Hands at 9 and 3 o'clock."}},{"k":"with_a_straight_back_your_wrist_should","v":{"s":"With a straight back, your wrist should rest on the TOP of the wheel when your arm is fully extended. That gives you 10-12 inches clearance to your chest — enough for the airbag to deploy without slamming into you."}},{"k":"10_12_in","v":{"s":"10-12 in"}},{"k":"step_5_side_mirrors_bge_method","v":{"s":"Step 5: Side Mirrors (BGE method)"}},{"k":"you_should_not_see_your_own_car_body_i","v":{"s":"You should NOT see your own car body in the side mirrors."}},{"k":"most_drivers_set_side_mirrors_to_see_t","v":{"s":"Most drivers set side mirrors to see the back of their own car — that doubles the rearview mirror. Instead: LEAN LEFT until your head almost touches the window, then adjust the left mirror until you just see your car's side. Repeat on the right by leaning right. When sitting normally, you'll see the lanes beside you — ELIMINATING BLIND SPOTS."}},{"k":"bge_no_car_body_in_side_mirrors","v":{"s":"BGE: no car body in side mirrors"}},{"k":"step_6_rearview_mirror","v":{"s":"Step 6: Rearview Mirror"}},{"k":"frame_the_entire_rear_window","v":{"s":"Frame the ENTIRE rear window."}},{"k":"adjust_so_you_can_see_the_full_rear_wi","v":{"s":"Adjust so you can see the full rear window without moving your head. In glare or night: flip the day/night tab (classic mirrors) or wait for auto-dim (newer cars)."}},{"k":"rear_window_framed","v":{"s":"Rear window framed"}},{"k":"cars_directly_behind","v":{"s":"cars directly behind"}},{"k":"step_7_seatbelt","v":{"s":"Step 7: Seatbelt"}},{"k":"belt_low_across_hips_not_stomach_shoul","v":{"s":"Belt low across hips (NOT stomach), shoulder belt across chest."}},{"k":"lap_belt_should_ride_on_your_hip_bones","v":{"s":"Lap belt should ride on your HIP BONES, never on your soft stomach. Shoulder belt should cross your collarbone at the center of your shoulder — never under the arm or behind the back. Pull any slack out."}},{"k":"menu_36","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"seat_mirror_setup_2","v":{"s":"Seat & Mirror Setup"}},{"k":"goal_2","v":{"s":"🎯 Goal"}},{"k":"why_it_matters_2","v":{"s":"🔬 Why it matters: "}},{"k":"back_2","v":{"s":"← Back"}},{"k":"stop_breathe","v":{"s":"STOP & Breathe"}},{"k":"call_911_2","v":{"s":"Report / Call 911"}},{"k":"secure_the_scene","v":{"s":"Secure the Scene"}},{"k":"document_everything","v":{"s":"Document Everything"}},{"k":"exchange_info","v":{"s":"Exchange Info"}},{"k":"never_say_these_words","v":{"s":"Never Say These Words"}},{"k":"next_24_hours","v":{"s":"Next 24 Hours"}},{"k":"menu_37","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"post_crash_protocol_2","v":{"s":"Post-Crash Protocol"}},{"k":"the_first_10_15_minutes_after_a_crash_","v":{"s":"The first 10-15 minutes after a crash shape the next 6 months. Know this cold."}},{"k":"export_as_glove_box_reference_markdown","v":{"s":"📄 Export as Glove-Box Reference (Markdown)"}},{"k":"menu_38","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"cyclist_motorcyclist_awareness","v":{"s":"Cyclist & Motorcyclist Awareness"}},{"k":"they_re_legal_vehicles_they_re_small_t","v":{"s":"They're legal vehicles. They're small. They're vulnerable. You're responsible."}},{"k":"maine_law_29_a_m_r_s_2070","v":{"s":"⚖️ Maine Law: 29-A M.R.S. §2070"}},{"k":"3_foot_passing_law","v":{"s":"3-Foot Passing Law"}},{"k":"when_passing_a_bicyclist_maine_law_req","v":{"s":"When passing a bicyclist or roller skier, Maine law requires AT LEAST 3 FEET of clearance. "}},{"k":"you_may_cross_the_double_yellow_line","v":{"s":"No-passing-zone pass only when safe"}},{"k":"to_do_it_safely_as_long_as_the_oncomin","v":{"s":": clear view, no oncoming conflict, and enough room to complete the pass. Wait if not. "}},{"k":"violation_75_fine_plus_any_crash_liabi","v":{"s":"A collision with a bicycle or roller skier is prima facie evidence of a §2070 violation."}},{"k":"3_ft_min","v":{"s":"3 ft min"}},{"k":"cyclists_are_vehicles","v":{"s":"Cyclists are vehicles"}},{"k":"motorcyclists_swerve_for_reasons","v":{"s":"Motorcyclists swerve for reasons"}},{"k":"what_looks_like_reckless_lane_weaving_","v":{"s":"What looks like reckless lane weaving is usually: avoiding potholes, gravel, oil spots, grates, debris. A pothole that barely registers in your sedan can throw a motorcycle rider."}},{"k":"dooring_kills_cyclists","v":{"s":"Dooring kills cyclists"}},{"k":"before_opening_your_door_in_traffic_us","v":{"s":"Before opening your door in traffic, use your FAR hand — your right hand from the driver seat in the U.S. — so your body naturally turns to check behind. Dooring injuries are 50% of urban cyclist crashes."}},{"k":"shared_blind_spots","v":{"s":"Shared blind spots"}},{"k":"motorcycles_fit_entirely_in_your_a_pil","v":{"s":"Motorcycles fit ENTIRELY in your A-pillar blind spot (the pillar between windshield and door). Bikes + cyclists do the same. Always lean to see past pillars at intersections."}},{"k":"turning_across","v":{"s":"Turning across"}},{"k":"the_1_driver_vs_cyclist_crash_is_the_r","v":{"s":"The #1 driver-vs-cyclist crash is the RIGHT HOOK: driver turns right across a cyclist going straight in a bike lane. Before any right turn, shoulder-check for cyclists. Before left turns, scan for oncoming motorcycles."}},{"k":"wet_roads","v":{"s":"Wet roads"}},{"k":"painted_lines_are_slick_in_rain_motorc","v":{"s":"Painted lines are slick in rain. Motorcyclists and cyclists will AVOID them — giving them extra space in rain is crucial. Don't tailgate — they're reading the road surface."}},{"k":"kids_on_bikes","v":{"s":"Kids on bikes"}},{"k":"children_under_12_are_wobbly_unpredict","v":{"s":"Children under 12 are wobbly, unpredictable, and often don't know signals. Add extra clearance, slow to a crawl in residential zones. Scan for balls, toys — kid WILL follow."}},{"k":"most_crashes_are_i_didn_t_see_them","v":{"s":"Most crashes are \"I didn't see them\""}},{"k":"cyclists_motorcyclists_are_not_hidden_","v":{"s":"Cyclists + motorcyclists are not \"hidden\" — drivers aren't looking for them. Train yourself to scan for bikes specifically when approaching any intersection."}},{"k":"the_right_hook_practice_avoiding_this","v":{"s":"⚠️ The Right-Hook — practice avoiding this"}},{"k":"bike_lane","v":{"s":"BIKE LANE"}},{"k":"right_hook_crash_zone","v":{"s":"⚠️ Right-hook crash zone"}},{"k":"signal_100_ft_early_shoulder_check_for","v":{"s":"Signal 100 ft early. SHOULDER CHECK for cyclists before turning right. Yield to any bike that's going straight — they have the legal right-of-way."}},{"k":"accel","v":{"s":"Accel"}},{"k":"brake","v":{"s":"Brake"}},{"k":"steer","v":{"s":"Steer ←"}},{"k":"steer_2","v":{"s":"Steer →"}},{"k":"pause_2","v":{"s":"Pause"}},{"k":"drive_gear","v":{"s":"Drive gear"}},{"k":"reverse","v":{"s":"Reverse"}},{"k":"park","v":{"s":"Park"}},{"k":"left_signal_2","v":{"s":"Left signal"}},{"k":"right_signal_2","v":{"s":"Right signal"}},{"k":"cancel_signal","v":{"s":"Cancel signal"}},{"k":"cycle_camera","v":{"s":"Cycle camera"}},{"k":"high_low_beams","v":{"s":"High/low beams"}},{"k":"toggle_hud","v":{"s":"Toggle HUD"}},{"k":"photo_2","v":{"s":"📸 Photo"}},{"k":"horn","v":{"s":"Horn"}},{"k":"look_left_shoulder_check","v":{"s":"Look left (shoulder check)"}},{"k":"look_right_shoulder_check","v":{"s":"Look right (shoulder check)"}},{"k":"drive_brake","v":{"s":"Drive / brake"}},{"k":"gears","v":{"s":"Gears"}},{"k":"turn_signals","v":{"s":"Turn signals"}},{"k":"camera_hud","v":{"s":"Camera / HUD"}},{"k":"shoulder_check","v":{"s":"Shoulder check"}},{"k":"photo_horn","v":{"s":"Photo / horn"}},{"k":"meta_pause","v":{"s":"Meta (pause)"}},{"k":"menu_39","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"keyboard_shortcuts_2","v":{"s":"Keyboard Shortcuts"}},{"k":"every_drive_control_click_any_key_to_s","v":{"s":"Every drive control. Click any key to see what it does."}},{"k":"rr_kb_key_display_inline_flex_align_it","v":{"s":".rr-kb-key { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 48px; height: 48px; margin: 3px; border-radius: 6px; background: #334155; color: #e2e8f0; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 800; font-family: monospace; border: 2px solid #475569; box-shadow: 0 3px 0 #1e293b; cursor: default; transition: transform 0.12s; position: relative; } .rr-kb-key[data-active] { box-shadow: 0 0 12px currentColor, 0 3px 0 #1e293b; transform: translateY(-1px); cursor: help; } .rr-kb-key[data-active]:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); } .rr-kb-key[data-active]::after { content: attr(data-tooltip); position: absolute; bottom: -28px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); background: #020617; color: #e2e8f0; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; transition: opacity 0.2s; z-index: 10; border: 1px solid currentColor; } .rr-kb-key[data-active]:hover::after { opacity: 1; }"}},{"k":"gamepad_support","v":{"s":"💡 Gamepad support: "}},{"k":"roadready_auto_detects_a_connected_gam","v":{"s":"Default gamepad controls: left stick steers, right stick checks shoulders, RT accelerates, LT brakes, A sounds the horn, B changes cameras, D-pad up/down selects Drive/Reverse, D-pad left/right signals, Back/View selects Park, and Start pauses. Use Controls to view or change your bindings."}},{"k":"permit_test_20q_quiz","v":{"s":"Permit Test (20q quiz)"}},{"k":"permit_flashcards_3","v":{"s":"Permit Flashcards"}},{"k":"study_cheat_sheet_2","v":{"s":"Study Cheat Sheet"}},{"k":"printable_one_page_summary_of_all_key_","v":{"s":"Printable one-page summary of all key rules."}},{"k":"road_signs_reference_2","v":{"s":"Road Signs Reference"}},{"k":"19_common_signs_with_svg_illustrations","v":{"s":"19 common signs with SVG illustrations + quiz mode."}},{"k":"right_of_way_scenarios_2","v":{"s":"Right-of-Way Scenarios"}},{"k":"10_who_goes_first_intersection_puzzles","v":{"s":"20 right-of-way and intersection puzzles."}},{"k":"residential_highway_snow_fog_night_dow","v":{"s":"Residential, highway, snow, fog, night, downtown, and more."}},{"k":"free_explore_5","v":{"s":"Free Explore"}},{"k":"open_sandbox_with_landmarks_challenges","v":{"s":"Open sandbox with landmarks, challenges, road trips, dynamic weather."}},{"k":"lesson_path_3","v":{"s":"Lesson Path"}},{"k":"guided_10_lesson_progression_from_begi","v":{"s":"Guided 10-lesson progression from beginner to winter expert."}},{"k":"road_test_simulator_3","v":{"s":"Road Test Simulator"}},{"k":"full_maine_bmv_style_scored_exam_pre_t","v":{"s":"Full Maine BMV-style scored exam (pre-trip + 4min drive)."}},{"k":"parking_practice_7_scenarios","v":{"s":"Parking Practice (9 Scenarios)"}},{"k":"parallel_tight_parallel_3_point_backin","v":{"s":"Parallel, tight parallel, 3-point, backing, angle-back, obstacle, U-turn, hydrant, and hill parking. Personal-best scores save."}},{"k":"night_vision_training_3","v":{"s":"Night Vision Training"}},{"k":"focused_night_drive_drill_with_coach_p","v":{"s":"Focused night-drive drill with coach prompts."}},{"k":"parent_ride_check_3","v":{"s":"Parent Ride Check"}},{"k":"2_min_structured_eval_parent_taps_to_m","v":{"s":"2-min structured eval — parent taps to mark errors."}},{"k":"defensive_drills_2","v":{"s":"Defensive Drills"}},{"k":"8_hazard_response_scenarios_with_corre","v":{"s":"8 hazard-response scenarios with correct-answer reveals."}},{"k":"moose_encounter_drill_2","v":{"s":"Moose Encounter Drill"}},{"k":"maine_specific_what_to_do_when_a_moose","v":{"s":"Maine-specific: what to do when a moose is in the road."}},{"k":"emergency_vehicle_drill_2","v":{"s":"Emergency Vehicle Drill"}},{"k":"maine_move_over_law_pull_to_right_rule","v":{"s":"Maine Move Over law, pull-to-right rule, stationary vehicles."}},{"k"