ed while operating, including when temporarily stopped in traffic. Texting: "}},{"k":"250_fine","v":{"s":"$250 fine"}},{"k":"first_offense_primary_enforcement_unde","v":{"s":" minimum first offense under §2119. Hands-free is allowed only for drivers 18+ who are not on a learner's permit or intermediate license."}},{"k":"what_this_means","v":{"s":"🎯 What this means:"}},{"k":"the_habit_that_saves_lives","v":{"s":"💚 The habit that saves lives"}},{"k":"every_notification_silence_the_phone_o","v":{"s":"Every notification: silence the phone or put it in Do Not Disturb + Driving mode (automatic on most phones). The text can wait. The deer can't."}},{"k":"electric_cyan","v":{"s":"Electric Cyan"}},{"k":"fire_red","v":{"s":"Fire Red"}},{"k":"maine_gold","v":{"s":"Maine Gold"}},{"k":"forest_green","v":{"s":"Forest Green"}},{"k":"sunset_purple","v":{"s":"Sunset Purple"}},{"k":"hot_pink","v":{"s":"Hot Pink"}},{"k":"midnight_black","v":{"s":"Midnight Black"}},{"k":"arctic_white","v":{"s":"Arctic White"}},{"k":"blaze_orange","v":{"s":"Blaze Orange"}},{"k":"navy_blue","v":{"s":"Navy Blue"}},{"k":"deep_burgundy","v":{"s":"Deep Burgundy"}},{"k":"chestnut_brown","v":{"s":"Chestnut Brown"}},{"k":"menu_49","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"my_ride_3","v":{"s":"My Ride"}},{"k":"paint_color","v":{"s":"Paint Color"}},{"k":"driver_name_optional","v":{"s":"Driver Name (optional)"}},{"k":"driver_first_name_optional_stays_on_de","v":{"s":"Driver first name (optional, stays on device only)"}},{"k":"your_first_name","v":{"s":"Your first name"}},{"k":"shows_up_on_your_debrief_certificates_","v":{"s":"Shows up on your debrief certificates and journal exports. Stays on your device only — no cloud."}},{"k":"license_plate","v":{"s":"License Plate"}},{"k":"custom_license_plate_up_to_7_letters_o","v":{"s":"Custom license plate (up to 7 letters or numbers)"}},{"k":"e_g_maine07","v":{"s":"e.g. MAINE07"}},{"k":"7_characters_max_letters_numbers_only_","v":{"s":"7 characters max. Letters + numbers only. Pure personalization — no lookups or real data."}},{"k":"reset_to_default","v":{"s":"↺ Reset to Default"}},{"k":"menu_50","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"achievement_gallery_2","v":{"s":"Achievement Gallery"}},{"k":"approach_yield","v":{"s":"Approach & Yield"}},{"k":"slow_down_as_you_approach_look_left_fo","v":{"s":"Slow down as you approach. Look LEFT for traffic already in the roundabout. They have the right-of-way."}},{"k":"the_yield_sign_at_the_entry_means_give","v":{"s":"The yield sign at the entry means: give way. Stop only if needed."}},{"k":"find_your_gap","v":{"s":"Find Your Gap"}},{"k":"wait_for_a_gap_in_circulating_traffic_","v":{"s":"Wait for a gap in circulating traffic. Do not force your way in. Do not stop inside the roundabout."}},{"k":"count_3_seconds_if_no_car_is_arriving_","v":{"s":"Count 3 seconds — if no car is arriving in 3 seconds, you can enter."}},{"k":"enter_travel","v":{"s":"Enter & Travel"}},{"k":"enter_the_roundabout_going_countercloc","v":{"s":"Enter the roundabout going COUNTERCLOCKWISE (to the right). Stay in your lane. Travel at 15-25 mph."}},{"k":"in_a_multi_lane_roundabout_right_lane_","v":{"s":"In a multi-lane roundabout: right lane = first exit. Left lane = second or third exit."}},{"k":"signal_exit","v":{"s":"Signal & Exit"}},{"k":"signal_right_as_you_approach_your_desi","v":{"s":"Signal RIGHT as you approach your desired exit. Exit smoothly without stopping."}},{"k":"if_you_miss_your_exit_go_around_again_","v":{"s":"If you miss your exit, go around again. That is the beauty of a roundabout — no penalty for looping."}},{"k":"yield_to_peds","v":{"s":"Yield to Peds"}},{"k":"watch_for_pedestrians_in_the_crosswalk","v":{"s":"Watch for pedestrians in the crosswalk at each exit splitter island. They have the right-of-way."}},{"k":"the_splitter_island_gives_pedestrians_","v":{"s":"The splitter island gives pedestrians a safe refuge between the two traffic flows."}},{"k":"menu_51","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"roundabout_tutorial_3","v":{"s":"Roundabout Tutorial"}},{"k":"roundabouts_reduce_fatal_crashes_by_90","v":{"s":"Roundabouts reduce fatal crashes by 90% vs. signaled intersections. Here is how to use them."}},{"k":"practice_in_simulator","v":{"s":"🔄 Practice in Simulator"}},{"k":"count_arrivals_at_the_intersection_lik","v":{"s":"Count arrivals at the intersection like a queue. Most crashes happen because someone assumes they have the right-of-way."}},{"k":"a_stale_green_been_green_a_while_will_","v":{"s":"A stale green (been green a while) will turn yellow soon. Start covering the brake."}},{"k":"common_on_rural_roads_treat_them_like_","v":{"s":"Common on rural roads. Treat them like a hidden yield sign — slow, look, proceed only when safe."}},{"k":"roundabouts_reduce_fatal_crashes_by_90_2","v":{"s":"Roundabouts reduce fatal crashes by 90% vs. signals. Once you get used to them, they are faster and safer."}},{"k":"the_top_of_the_t_is_the_through_road_t","v":{"s":"The \"top of the T\" is the through road. The \"stem\" yields."}},{"k":"left_turns_are_the_1_most_dangerous_co","v":{"s":"Left turns are the #1 most dangerous common maneuver. 53% of intersection crashes involve left turns."}},{"k":"maine_is_strict_on_this_164_fine_for_f","v":{"s":"Maine §2056 is specific: marked crosswalks and visible intent matter; due care still applies everywhere."}},{"k":"menu_52","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"intersection_right_of_way_guide","v":{"s":"Intersection Right-of-Way Guide"}},{"k":"who_goes_first_the_answer_for_every_ty","v":{"s":"Who goes first? The answer for every type."}},{"k":"check_engine_mil","v":{"s":"Check Engine (MIL)"}},{"k":"steady_emissions_issue_safe_to_drive_t","v":{"s":"Steady = emissions issue, safe to drive to a shop. FLASHING = misfire, pull over immediately — catalytic converter damage."}},{"k":"oil_pressure","v":{"s":"Oil Pressure"}},{"k":"engine_oil_pressure_is_dangerously_low","v":{"s":"Engine oil pressure is dangerously low. Continuing will destroy the engine in minutes."}},{"k":"temperature_overheating","v":{"s":"Temperature / Overheating"}},{"k":"coolant_is_too_hot_driving_further_can","v":{"s":"Coolant is too hot. Driving further can crack the head gasket ($2,000+ repair)."}},{"k":"brake_system","v":{"s":"Brake System"}},{"k":"brake_failure_or_very_low_brake_fluid_","v":{"s":"Brake failure or very low brake fluid. Parking brake engaged also shows this light."}},{"k":"anti_lock_braking_system_fault_normal_","v":{"s":"Anti-lock braking system fault. Normal brakes still work, but ABS will not activate in hard stops."}},{"k":"tpms_tire_pressure","v":{"s":"TPMS (Tire Pressure)"}},{"k":"one_or_more_tires_is_significantly_und","v":{"s":"One or more tires is significantly under-inflated (usually 25%+ below spec)."}},{"k":"battery_charging","v":{"s":"Battery / Charging"}},{"k":"alternator_not_charging_the_battery_th","v":{"s":"Alternator not charging the battery. The car will run on battery power for 30-60 minutes, then die."}},{"k":"traction_control_tc_esc","v":{"s":"Traction Control (TC/ESC)"}},{"k":"blinking_system_is_actively_working_wh","v":{"s":"Blinking = system is actively working (wheels are slipping). Steady = system is OFF."}},{"k":"high_beam_indicator","v":{"s":"High Beam Indicator"}},{"k":"high_beams_are_on_remember_to_dim_for_","v":{"s":"High beams are on. Maine requires dimming for oncoming traffic and when following another vehicle."}},{"k":"airbag_srs","v":{"s":"Airbag (SRS)"}},{"k":"airbag_system_fault_airbags_may_not_de","v":{"s":"Airbag system fault. Airbags may not deploy in a crash."}},{"k":"menu_53","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"dashboard_warning_lights","v":{"s":"Dashboard Warning Lights"}},{"k":"what_each_light_means_how_serious_it_i","v":{"s":"What each light means, how serious it is, and exactly what to do."}},{"k":"pre_trip_vehicle_inspection","v":{"s":"Pre-Trip Vehicle Inspection"}},{"k":"tap_each_item_as_you_complete_the_walk","v":{"s":"Tap each item as you complete the walk-around. Pros do this every time."}},{"k":"reset_2","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"why_this_matters_2","v":{"s":"💡 Why this matters:"}},{"k":"maine_bmv_road_test_starts_with_a_brie","v":{"s":"Maine BMV road test starts with a brief vehicle inspection. Examiners will check that signals, brakes, horn, wipers, and seat belts work. Failing this means the test is over before you even drive. Build the habit now."}},{"k":"menu_54","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"vehicle_science_comparison","v":{"s":"Vehicle Science Comparison"}},{"k":"mass_drag_area_mpg_why_these_numbers_m","v":{"s":"Mass, drag, area, MPG — why these numbers matter"}},{"k":"key_insights","v":{"s":"🔑 Key Insights"}},{"k":"cd_a","v":{"s":"Cd × A"}},{"k":"is_the_single_number_that_determines_d","v":{"s":" is the single number that determines drag. Lower = less fuel wasted. The EV (0.53) beats the truck (1.34) by 2.5×."}},{"k":"mass","v":{"s":"Mass"}},{"k":"determines_braking_distance_heavier_sl","v":{"s":" determines braking distance (heavier = slower to stop) and rolling resistance. The school bus is 7.6× heavier than the sedan."}},{"k":"stopping_distance","v":{"s":"Stopping distance"}},{"k":"example_at_55_mph_sedan_200_ft_school_","v":{"s":" example at 55 mph: sedan ~200 ft, school bus ~480 ft (on dry). Physics is non-negotiable."}},{"k":"hybrid_city_highway_mpg_because_regene","v":{"s":"• Hybrid city > highway MPG because regenerative braking recovers energy in stop-and-go. Gas cars do the opposite."}},{"k":"menu_55","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"emergency_vehicle_response_drill","v":{"s":"Emergency Vehicle Response Drill"}},{"k":"sirens_will_sound_frequently_practice_","v":{"s":"Sirens will sound frequently. Practice the correct response every time."}},{"k":"the_protocol_all_50_states","v":{"s":"Emergency Vehicle Protocol"}},{"k":"check_mirrors_to_identify_the_emergenc","v":{"s":"Check mirrors to identify the emergency vehicle's position and direction."}},{"k":"signal_right_to_indicate_your_intent_t","v":{"s":"Signal RIGHT to indicate your intent to move over."}},{"k":"safely_move_to_the_right_shoulder_or_r","v":{"s":"Safely move to the RIGHT shoulder or right lane."}},{"k":"come_to_a_complete_stop_and_wait_until","v":{"s":"Come to a COMPLETE STOP and wait until the vehicle passes."}},{"k":"check_for_additional_emergency_vehicle","v":{"s":"Check for additional emergency vehicles before re-entering traffic."}},{"k":"signal_left_check_blind_spot_and_merge","v":{"s":"Signal left, check blind spot, and merge back carefully."}},{"k":"special_situations","v":{"s":"⚠️ Special situations"}},{"k":"at_an_intersection","v":{"s":"At an intersection:"}},{"k":"divided_highway","v":{"s":"Divided highway:"}},{"k":"if_the_emergency_vehicle_is_on_the_oth","v":{"s":" Maine §2054 does not list a median exception; move right when safe, stay clear of intersections, and stop until it passes."}},{"k":"cannot_move_right","v":{"s":"Cannot move right:"}},{"k":"if_right_shoulder_is_blocked_stop_wher","v":{"s":" If the right shoulder is blocked, signal and move as far right as practicable, stay clear of intersections, and stop where the lane stays clearest."}},{"k":"multiple_vehicles","v":{"s":"Multiple vehicles:"}},{"k":"stay_stopped_until_all_emergency_vehic","v":{"s":" Stay stopped until ALL emergency vehicles have passed. They often travel in convoys."}},{"k":"maine_move_over_law","v":{"s":"Maine Move Over law:"}},{"k":"also_applies_to_stopped_tow_trucks_uti","v":{"s":" Applies to stationary disabled vehicles and vehicles using flashing lights, including tow, utility, roadside assistance, and responders."}},{"k":"why_this_matters_3","v":{"s":"Why this matters"}},{"k":"every_second_counts_for_emergency_resp","v":{"s":"Every second counts for emergency responders. A 1-minute delay reaching a cardiac arrest patient reduces survival by 10%. In Maine, failure to yield to an emergency vehicle is a Class E crime with at least a $250 fine for a first offense; repeat offenses can trigger license suspension."}},{"k":"start_emergency_drill_sirens_will_be_f","v":{"s":"🚨 Start Emergency Drill — Sirens Will Be Frequent"}},{"k":"emergency_vehicles_will_spawn_every_20","v":{"s":"Emergency vehicles will spawn every 20-30 seconds. Practice until the response is automatic. Earns the \"First Responder\" achievement."}},{"k":"dry","v":{"s":"☀️ Dry"}},{"k":"rain","v":{"s":"🌧️ Rain"}},{"k":"snow","v":{"s":"❄️ Snow"}},{"k":"ice","v":{"s":"🧊 Ice"}},{"k":"menu_56","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"stopping_distance_lab_3","v":{"s":"Stopping Distance Lab"}},{"k":"play_with_speed_weather_and_reaction_t","v":{"s":"Play with speed, weather, and reaction time. Watch the physics."}},{"k":"speed_in_miles_per_hour","v":{"s":"Speed in miles per hour"}},{"k":"reaction_time","v":{"s":"REACTION TIME"}},{"k":"reaction_time_in_seconds","v":{"s":"Reaction time in seconds"}},{"k":"road_condition","v":{"s":"ROAD CONDITION"}},{"k":"reaction_distance","v":{"s":"Reaction Distance"}},{"k":"v_t_distance_covered_before_brakes_tou","v":{"s":"v × t = distance covered before brakes touch"}},{"k":"braking_distance","v":{"s":"Braking Distance"}},{"k":"v_2_g_grows_with_v_squared","v":{"s":"v² / (2·μ·g) — grows with v squared"}},{"k":"total_stopping_distance","v":{"s":"Total Stopping Distance"}},{"k":"live_physics","v":{"s":"🔬 Live Physics"}},{"k":"friction","v":{"s":"Friction μ: "}},{"k":"total_resist","v":{"s":"Total resist: "}},{"k":"safe_follow","v":{"s":"Safe follow: "}},{"k":"cruise_mpg","v":{"s":"Cruise MPG: "}},{"k":"visual_scale","v":{"s":"Visual Scale"}},{"k":"200_ft","v":{"s":"200 ft"}},{"k":"400_ft","v":{"s":"400 ft"}},{"k":"unsafe_stopping_distance_100m","v":{"s":"🚨 Unsafe stopping distance (>100m)"}},{"k":"cannot_stop_in_time_for_typical_road_h","v":{"s":"Cannot stop in time for typical road hazard."}},{"k":"aggressive_1g_deceleration","v":{"s":"⚠️ Aggressive (>1g deceleration)"}},{"k":"hard_braking_risk_of_skid_abs_engageme","v":{"s":"Hard braking. Risk of skid, ABS engagement."}},{"k":"long_stop_50_100m","v":{"s":"🟡 Long stop (50-100m)"}},{"k":"acceptable_but_marginal_longer_than_ty","v":{"s":"Acceptable but marginal. Longer than typical city block."}},{"k":"controlled_stop_50m","v":{"s":"🟢 Controlled stop (<50m)"}},{"k":"safe_deceleration_comfortable_for_pass","v":{"s":"Safe deceleration. Comfortable for passengers."}},{"k":"menu_57","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"braking_performance_discovery","v":{"s":"🚗 Braking performance discovery"}},{"k":"four_sliders_mass_speed_deceleration_c","v":{"s":"Four sliders: mass, speed, deceleration capability, road grade. Widget classifies braking outcome into 4 discrete states + renders SVG force diagram. No score, no reveal."}},{"k":"log","v":{"s":"📋 Log"}},{"k":"reset_3","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"hypothesis_free_text_why_does_kinetic_","v":{"s":"Hypothesis (free text): Why does kinetic energy grow with v² but only linearly with mass?"}},{"k":"stuck_show_open_prompts","v":{"s":"🤔 Stuck — show open prompts"}},{"k":"double_speed_does_stop_distance_double","v":{"s":"Double speed: does stop distance double or quadruple? Test."}},{"k":"a_1500kg_car_at_100_km_h_vs_5000kg_tru","v":{"s":"A 1500kg car at 100 km/h vs 5000kg truck at 50 km/h — which stops sooner?"}},{"k":"why_does_a_5_downhill_grade_dramatical","v":{"s":"Why does a 5° downhill grade dramatically extend stopping?"}},{"k":"abs_achieves_9_m_s_what_does_real_worl","v":{"s":"ABS achieves ~9 m/s². What does real-world friction coefficient imply about this?"}},{"k":"i_understand_explain_in_own_words","v":{"s":"I understand — explain in own words"}},{"k":"explain_why_does_v_dominate_stopping_d","v":{"s":"Explain: why does v² dominate stopping distance? What surprised you about grade?"}},{"k":"design_note_discrete_4_state_braking_m","v":{"s":"Design note: discrete 4-state braking marker; SVG force/energy diagram; no safety score — by design."}},{"k":"menu_58","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"parking_practice","v":{"s":"🅿️ Parking Practice"}},{"k":"9_scenarios_across_3_difficulty_tiers_","v":{"s":"9 hands-on drills in a top-down training car. Start with Standard Parallel; selected road vehicles do not change this trainer."}},{"k":"menu_59","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"fuel_cost_calculator_3","v":{"s":"Fuel Cost Calculator"}},{"k":"see_what_driving_really_costs_by_vehic","v":{"s":"See what driving really costs — by vehicle, habits, and fuel type."}},{"k":"annual_miles","v":{"s":"ANNUAL MILES"}},{"k":"annual_miles_driven","v":{"s":"Annual miles driven"}},{"k":"gas_gal","v":{"s":"GAS $/GAL"}},{"k":"gas_price_per_gallon_in_dollars","v":{"s":"Gas price per gallon in dollars"}},{"k":"electricity_kwh","v":{"s":"ELECTRICITY $/kWh"}},{"k":"electricity_price_per_kilowatt_hour_in","v":{"s":"Electricity price per kilowatt-hour in dollars"}},{"k":"insights","v":{"s":"💡 Insights"}},{"k":"the_average_american_drives_12_000_mi_","v":{"s":"• The average American drives ~12,000 mi/yr. At $3.50/gal in a 37-MPG sedan, that is ~$1,135/yr in fuel."}},{"k":"switching_from_a_pickup_21_mpg_avg_to_","v":{"s":"• Switching from a pickup (21 MPG avg) to a hybrid (53 MPG avg) saves ~$"}},{"k":"the_ev_at","v":{"s":"• The EV at $"}},{"k":"less_than_a_sedan","v":{"s":"% less than a sedan."}},{"k":"smooth_driving_no_jackrabbits_coast_to","v":{"s":"• Smooth driving (no jackrabbits, coast to stops) improves real-world MPG by 20-40% over the EPA sticker."}},{"k":"menu_60","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"hypermiling_lab_3","v":{"s":"Hypermiling Lab"}},{"k":"see_how_speed_kills_your_mpg_find_your","v":{"s":"See how speed kills your MPG. Find your sweet spot."}},{"k":"vehicle_3","v":{"s":"Vehicle"}},{"k":"conditions","v":{"s":"Conditions"}},{"k":"underinflated_tires_3_psi_low_across_a","v":{"s":"Underinflated tires (~3 PSI low across all 4 tires) raise rolling resistance ~25%, costing roughly 3% MPG."}},{"k":"air_conditioning_compressor_pulls_2_5_","v":{"s":"Air conditioning compressor pulls ~2.5 kW. Hits hardest in city driving (10–15% MPG); tiny on the highway (~3%)."}},{"k":"wind_mph_relative_to_your_direction","v":{"s":"💨 Wind (mph relative to your direction)"}},{"k":"wind_positive_is_headwind_slows_you_ne","v":{"s":"Wind: positive is headwind (slows you), negative is tailwind"}},{"k":"drag_scales_with_relative_airspeed_squ","v":{"s":"Drag scales with relative airspeed squared — a 20 mph headwind at 60 mph cruise is the same drag as an 80 mph car in still air."}},{"k":"mpg_vs_speed_steady_cruise","v":{"s":"MPG vs Speed (steady cruise)"}},{"k":"key_insights_2","v":{"s":"🔬 Key Insights"}},{"k":"at_65_mph","v":{"s":"• At 65 mph, "}},{"k":"of_your_fuel_goes_to_fighting_air_not_","v":{"s":" of your fuel goes to fighting AIR, not rolling friction. That share grows with v²."}},{"k":"going_75_mph_instead_of_65_mph_drag_is","v":{"s":"• Going 75 mph instead of 65 mph: drag is "}},{"k":"higher_most_cars_lose_15_20_mpg","v":{"s":" higher. Most cars lose 15-20% MPG."}},{"k":"ev_note_electric_cars_are_less_sensiti","v":{"s":"• EV note: electric cars are LESS sensitive to speed than gas — no idle waste, no wasted heat. They still lose to drag but win at all speeds."}},{"k":"tire_pressure_every_1_psi_low_0_3_mpg_","v":{"s":"• Tire pressure: every 1 PSI low ≈ 0.3% MPG loss. Free fuel from a $5 gauge."}},{"k":"debrief","v":{"s":"← Debrief"}},{"k":"crash_replay_black_box_data","v":{"s":"Crash Replay — Black Box Data"}},{"k":"speed_mph_over_time","v":{"s":"Speed (mph) over time"}},{"k":"what_the_black_box_shows","v":{"s":"🔍 What the black box shows:"}},{"k":"speed_at_impact","v":{"s":"• Speed at impact: "}},{"k":"speed_2_seconds_before","v":{"s":"• Speed 2 seconds before: "}},{"k":"steering_at_impact","v":{"s":"• Steering at impact: "}},{"k":"gear","v":{"s":"• Gear: "}},{"k":"back_3","v":{"s":"← Back"}},{"k":"media_print_body_visibility_hidden_roa","v":{"s":"@media print { body * { visibility: hidden; } #roadready-certificate, #roadready-certificate * { visibility: visible; } #roadready-certificate { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 100%; } }"}},{"k":"certificate_of_completion","v":{"s":"CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION"}},{"k":"driver_s_education_au