es."}},{"k":"wb_info_gain_end","v":{"s":" useful available tests."}},{"k":"wb_info_gain_mid","v":{"s":" candidates would remain after a typical result. Compared across "}},{"k":"wb_info_gain_start","v":{"s":"Best expected split: about "}},{"k":"wb_mohs_broad","v":{"s":"Broad bracket"}},{"k":"wb_mohs_narrow","v":{"s":"Narrow bracket"}},{"k":"wb_mohs_provisional","v":{"s":"Provisional band—confirm"}},{"k":"wb_mohs_unmeasured","v":{"s":"Not bracketed yet"}},{"k":"wb_mohs_useful","v":{"s":"Useful bracket"}},{"k":"wb_mohs_aria_candidates","v":{"s":"Remaining candidate positions: "}},{"k":"wb_mohs_aria_candidate_many","v":{"s":" candidates at Mohs "}},{"k":"wb_mohs_aria_candidate_one","v":{"s":" candidate at Mohs "}},{"k":"wb_mohs_aria_intro","v":{"s":"Mohs ordinal hardness ranking from 1 to 10. Modeled constraint: "}},{"k":"wb_mohs_aria_next","v":{"s":"Recommended next reference: "}},{"k":"wb_mohs_aria_none","v":{"s":"No candidates match the current scratch results"}},{"k":"wb_mohs_aria_start","v":{"s":"Mohs hardness scale from 1 to 10. The unknown is currently bracketed from "}},{"k":"wb_mohs_aria_to","v":{"s":"to"}},{"k":"wb_mohs_visual_title","v":{"s":"Mohs interval: "}},{"k":"wb_mohs_candidates_key","v":{"s":"Remaining candidate hardnesses"}},{"k":"wb_mohs_next_key","v":{"s":"Recommended next reference: "}},{"k":"wb_branch_if","v":{"s":"If "}},{"k":"wb_branch_keeps","v":{"s":"Would keep: "}},{"k":"wb_branch_many_remain","v":{"s":" candidates would remain: "}},{"k":"wb_branch_one_remains","v":{"s":" candidate would remain: "}},{"k":"wb_branch_then","v":{"s":" occurs, "}},{"k":"wb_branch_would_leave","v":{"s":"Would leave "}},{"k":"wb_predict_aria_mid","v":{"s":"This branch would leave "}},{"k":"wb_predict_aria_start","v":{"s":"Predict "}},{"k":"wb_working_hypothesis","v":{"s":"Working hypothesis"}},{"k":"tool_copper_reference","v":{"s":"Copper reference (modeled)"}},{"k":"tool_glass_reference","v":{"s":"Glass reference (modeled)"}},{"k":"tool_calibrated_point","v":{"s":"Calibrated point (modeled)"}},{"k":"reference_variability_note","v":{"s":"Reference values are modeled; real objects vary."}},{"k":"scratch_borderline","v":{"s":"Modeled near-match—retest to confirm"}},{"k":"scratch_borderline_detail","v":{"s":"The tool and mineral share the same modeled Mohs value, so the model narrows to approximate equality; real specimens vary, so confirm with another reference."}},{"k":"streak_plate_scratched_result","v":{"s":"Plate scratched — no reliable powder streak"}},{"k":"wb_ev_plate_scratched","v":{"s":"Streak plate: no powder; the plate groove gives H > about 6.5"}},{"k":"wb_forecast_plate_scratched","v":{"s":"No powder streak · plate groove gives H > 6.5"}},{"k":"wb_mohs_constraint_title","v":{"s":"Modeled hardness constraint: "}},{"k":"wb_mohs_rank_note","v":{"s":"Mohs is an ordinal ranking; equal spacing does not mean equal increases in hardness."}},{"k":"wb_mohs_conflict","v":{"s":"Conflicting scratch results — retest"}},{"k":"wb_cer_confidence_needed","v":{"s":"Record your confidence before submitting"}},{"k":"wb_stage_in_progress","v":{"s":"In progress"}},{"k":"wb_info_gain_assumption","v":{"s":"Estimate assumes each remaining candidate is equally likely."}},{"k":"tool_porcelain_reference","v":{"s":"Porcelain plate reference (modeled)"}},{"k":"wb_guided_toggle_aria","v":{"s":"Guided focus"}},{"k":"wb_plate_hardness_short","v":{"s":"PLATE GROOVE · H > 6.5"}},{"k":"wb_plate_mobile","v":{"s":"No powder streak; plate groove gives H > 6.5"}},{"k":"wb_plate_no_powder_short","v":{"s":"NO POWDER STREAK"}},{"k":"wb_result_near_short","v":{"s":"NEAR-MATCH · RETEST"}},{"k":"wb_result_nomark_short","v":{"s":"NO MARK"}},{"k":"wb_result_scratch_short","v":{"s":"SCRATCH"}},{"k":"wb_compatible_rejected_many","v":{"s":"rejected claims still match the measurements."}},{"k":"wb_compatible_rejected_one","v":{"s":"rejected claim still matches the measurements."}},{"k":"wb_confirmed_types_short","v":{"s":"confirmed"}},{"k":"wb_conflict_revision_end","v":{"s":" observation. Your notebook is preserved—review what changed, then choose a supported candidate."}},{"k":"wb_conflict_revision_mid","v":{"s":" no longer fits the "}},{"k":"wb_conflict_revision_title","v":{"s":"New evidence changed your working claim."}},{"k":"wb_conflict_reviewing_sr","v":{"s":"Reviewing the new evidence conflict for "}},{"k":"wb_measurement_matches","v":{"s":"measurement matches"}},{"k":"wb_new_evidence","v":{"s":"new evidence"}},{"k":"wb_provisional_confirm","v":{"s":"Provisional—confirm"}},{"k":"wb_provisional_not_claim","v":{"s":"Provisional model clue—confirm before using hardness in a claim"}},{"k":"wb_provisional_short","v":{"s":"provisional"}},{"k":"wb_rejection_not_evidence","v":{"s":"Rejection feedback is not physical evidence—run another diagnostic test."}},{"k":"wb_review_conflict_action","v":{"s":"Review conflict"}},{"k":"wb_support_provisional_detail","v":{"s":"A modeled near-match narrows the list, but confirm hardness before treating that narrowing as strong support."}},{"k":"wb_unknown_mobile","v":{"s":"Unknown specimen"}},{"k":"ls_process_igneous","v":{"s":"Magma rises, cools and hardens → igneous"}},{"k":"ls_process_sedimentary","v":{"s":"Sediment settles, compacts and cements → sedimentary"}},{"k":"ls_process_metamorphic","v":{"s":"Buried rock is squeezed and heated → metamorphic"}},{"k":"tour_cap_igneous","v":{"s":"Magma cools and hardens: igneous rock"}},{"k":"tour_cap_weather","v":{"s":"Weathering and erosion break it into sediment"}},{"k":"tour_cap_sedimentary","v":{"s":"Sediment settles, compacts and cements: sedimentary rock"}},{"k":"tour_cap_metamorphic","v":{"s":"Buried, squeezed and heated: metamorphic rock"}},{"k":"tour_cap_melt","v":{"s":"Deep enough, it melts back into magma"}},{"k":"tour_stopped","v":{"s":"Rock cycle tour stopped."}},{"k":"tour_stage","v":{"s":"Stage "}},{"k":"tour_of","v":{"s":" of "}},{"k":"ls_depth_top","v":{"s":"0 km · cool"}},{"k":"ls_depth_bottom","v":{"s":"~35 km · hot"}},{"k":"ls_younger","v":{"s":"younger"}},{"k":"ls_pressure","v":{"s":"pressure"}},{"k":"ls_uplift","v":{"s":"uplift"}},{"k":"ls_click_to_explore","v":{"s":"Click to explore →"}},{"k":"ls_weathering","v":{"s":"Weathering & erosion"}},{"k":"ls_melting","v":{"s":"Melting"}},{"k":"ls_deposition","v":{"s":"Deposition"}},{"k":"ls_cooling","v":{"s":"Cooling"}},{"k":"ls_cross_section","v":{"s":"Cross-Section View"}},{"k":"rock_cycle_landscape_aria2","v":{"s":"Rock cycle landscape. Press 1 for the volcano and igneous rocks, 2 for the river delta and sedimentary rocks, 3 for the mountain core and metamorphic rocks. The first press previews a zone; press it again, or Enter, to open it. Press T to follow one rock around the cycle, N and P to step through its stages."}},{"k":"landscape_preview_cleared","v":{"s":"Zone preview cleared."}},{"k":"landscape_preview_open_hint","v":{"s":"Press the same key again, Enter, or Space to open this zone; Escape to clear."}},{"k":"tour_controls_aria","v":{"s":"Rock cycle tour controls"}},{"k":"tour_stop","v":{"s":"Stop the tour"}},{"k":"tour_play","v":{"s":"Follow one rock around the cycle"}},{"k":"tour_prev","v":{"s":"Previous stage"}},{"k":"tour_next","v":{"s":"Next stage"}},{"k":"tour_hint_on","v":{"s":"Watch the tracer; each stage is announced. Reduced motion shows one still frame per stage."}},{"k":"tour_hint_off","v":{"s":"A guided trip through all five stages, one rock at a time. You can also click any process label on the picture to start there."}},{"k":"wb_ev_recorded_suffix","v":{"s":" (your classification)"}},{"k":"wb_ev_form","v":{"s":"Form: "}},{"k":"wb_ev_density_recheck","v":{"s":" (check your division: the readings do not land in this band)"}},{"k":"wb_coverage_form","v":{"s":"Form"}},{"k":"wb_forecast_form_title","v":{"s":"the fragment’s form"}},{"k":"wb_next_record","v":{"s":"Record what you observed"}},{"k":"wb_next_record_detail","v":{"s":"Look at the specimen station, then choose the description that matches what you actually see. The notebook only fills with observations you record yourself."}},{"k":"wb_kind_form","v":{"s":"form"}},{"k":"wb_match_form","v":{"s":"Form"}},{"k":"wb_faceoff_form","v":{"s":"Form"}},{"k":"wb_faceoff_form_prompt","v":{"s":"Look at how each fragment breaks: corners, sheets, columns or no faces at all."}},{"k":"wb_rail_form","v":{"s":"Form"}},{"k":"wb_go_observe","v":{"s":"Go to the observation card"}},{"k":"wb_guide_form_cue","v":{"s":"SHAPE"}},{"k":"wb_guide_form","v":{"s":"Form"}},{"k":"wb_guide_form_meaning","v":{"s":"The shape a mineral grows or breaks into: box-like corners, leaning rhombs, sheets, columns, pyramids, blades, or no faces at all."}},{"k":"wb_guide_form_use","v":{"s":"A free observation: describe the fragment on the bench (turn it in 3D) before running any instrument."}},{"k":"wb_guide_form_guard","v":{"s":"A broken fragment shows cleavage and fracture, not the perfect crystal in a textbook; judge the corners and faces you can see."}},{"k":"wb_specimen_aria","v":{"s":"Unknown hand specimen: an irregular broken fragment."}},{"k":"wb_lens_aria","v":{"s":"Magnified patch of the specimen surface under the lamp. "}},{"k":"wb_candidate_porthole_aria","v":{"s":" under the lens: "}},{"k":"wb_bench_aria_evidence","v":{"s":". Its outward colour is visible; every other property must be tested. Each test leaves visible evidence at the station, described in the observation card and the field notebook."}},{"k":"wb_record_prompt_short","v":{"s":"RECORD WHAT YOU SEE"}},{"k":"wb_plate_grooved_short","v":{"s":"PLATE GROOVED"}},{"k":"wb_look_closely_short","v":{"s":"LOOK CLOSELY"}},{"k":"wb_recorded_sr","v":{"s":"Recorded: "}},{"k":"wb_recorded_sr2","v":{"s":"The notebook and the candidate shortlist now use your observation."}},{"k":"wb_discarded_sr","v":{"s":"Trial discarded without recording. You can run it again."}},{"k":"wb_reexamine_sr","v":{"s":"Looking again. The station shows the evidence; choose what you see to replace the earlier record."}},{"k":"wb_luster_ref_aria","v":{"s":"Reference sheen on a neutral grey surface: "}},{"k":"wb_obs_scratched","v":{"s":"It cut a groove into the specimen"}},{"k":"wb_obs_scratched_hint","v":{"s":"A dark line with tiny chips thrown ahead of the tip: the reference is harder than the specimen."}},{"k":"wb_obs_no_mark","v":{"s":"No groove: only a smear rubbed off the reference"}},{"k":"wb_obs_no_mark_hint","v":{"s":"A pale mark that sits on top and wipes away; the reference is softer than the specimen."}},{"k":"wb_obs_borderline","v":{"s":"Hard to tell: a broken, uneven trace"}},{"k":"wb_obs_borderline_hint","v":{"s":"Record it as provisional and confirm with the next softer or harder reference."}},{"k":"wb_obs_fizz","v":{"s":"Bubbles rose from the drop"}},{"k":"wb_obs_fizz_hint","v":{"s":"Gas escaping means the acid is reacting with the mineral."}},{"k":"wb_obs_no_fizz","v":{"s":"The drop sat still: no bubbles"}},{"k":"wb_obs_no_fizz_hint","v":{"s":"No visible reaction in cold dilute acid."}},{"k":"wb_obs_pull","v":{"s":"The specimen moved toward the magnet"}},{"k":"wb_obs_pull_hint","v":{"s":"It slid across the bench: a strong attraction."}},{"k":"wb_obs_no_pull","v":{"s":"No movement at all"}},{"k":"wb_obs_no_pull_hint","v":{"s":"The magnet passed close by and nothing happened."}},{"k":"wb_t_form","v":{"s":"Describe its shape"}},{"k":"wb_trail_eyebrow","v":{"s":"Reasoning trail"}},{"k":"wb_trail_title","v":{"s":"How you got there"}},{"k":"wb_trail_revised_help","v":{"s":"Looking again and revising a reading is exactly what a careful observer does. Revised readings are kept here so you can see how your thinking changed."}},{"k":"wb_trail_help","v":{"s":"Every observation you recorded, in order, compared with the reference values for the mineral you identified."}},{"k":"wb_trail_match","v":{"s":"Matches reference"}},{"k":"wb_trail_revised","v":{"s":"Revised later"}},{"k":"wb_trail_mismatch","v":{"s":"Worth a second look: reference says "}},{"k":"wb_nb_title","v":{"s":"Mineral Workbench field notebook"}},{"k":"wb_nb_set","v":{"s":"Candidate set: "}},{"k":"wb_pool_challenge","v":{"s":"Challenge set"}},{"k":"wb_pool_standard","v":{"s":"Standard set"}},{"k":"wb_nb_observations","v":{"s":"Observations (in the order recorded):"}},{"k":"wb_nb_none","v":{"s":"none yet"}},{"k":"wb_nb_evidence","v":{"s":"Evidence in force:"}},{"k":"wb_nb_hardness","v":{"s":"Hardness constraint: "}},{"k":"wb_nb_shortlist","v":{"s":"Candidates still fitting: "}},{"k":"wb_nb_claim","v":{"s":"Claim: "}},{"k":"wb_nb_reasoning","v":{"s":"Reasoning: "}},{"k":"wb_nb_identified","v":{"s":"Identified: "}},{"k":"wb_nb_copied","v":{"s":"Notebook copied to the clipboard."}},{"k":"wb_nb_copy_failed","v":{"s":"Could not copy. Select the notebook text and copy it by hand."}},{"k":"wb_obs_title_lens","v":{"s":"What does the surface do with light?"}},{"k":"wb_obs_title_form","v":{"s":"What shape does the fragment break into?"}},{"k":"wb_obs_title_streak","v":{"s":"What is on the porcelain plate?"}},{"k":"wb_obs_title_scratch","v":{"s":"Did the reference leave a real scratch?"}},{"k":"wb_obs_title_acid","v":{"s":"What happened when the acid touched the specimen?"}},{"k":"wb_obs_title_magnet","v":{"s":"How did the specimen respond to the magnet?"}},{"k":"wb_obs_title_density","v":{"s":"Work out the density from the two readings"}},{"k":"wb_obs_help_form","v":{"s":"Look at the corners, faces and edges of the fragment on the bench; turn it in 3D if that helps. Form is about shape, not colour or shine. Compare with the reference crystals on the candidate cards."}},{"k":"wb_obs_help_lens","v":{"s":"Compare the porthole with the four reference sheens. They are all on the same grey surface, so the only difference between them is how they reflect the lamp. Colour is not luster."}},{"k":"wb_obs_help_streak","v":{"s":"Name the colour of the powder itself, not the specimen. If the plate is grooved with no powder, the mineral is harder than porcelain."}},{"k":"wb_obs_help_scratch","v":{"s":"A groove cuts INTO the surface and throws chips. A smear is the reference’s own material rubbed ON the surface with no depth."}},{"k":"wb_obs_help_acid","v":{"s":"Look at the drop on the specimen."}},{"k":"wb_obs_help_magnet","v":{"s":"Look at where the specimen is now compared with its outline on the bench."}},{"k":"wb_obs_help_density","v":{"s":"Density is mass divided by volume: ρ = m ÷ V. Divide the balance reading by the water the specimen displaced, then choose the band your answer falls in."}},{"k":"wb_obs_eyebrow","v":{"s":"Your observation"}},{"k":"wb_obs_tilt","v":{"s":"Tilt it: turn the specimen under the lamp and watch the highlight"}},{"k":"wb_obs_tilt_help","v":{"s":"A hard mirror flash that slides is metallic. One pin-sharp point with a lit interior is glassy. A wide soft glow along layers is pearly. No crisp highlight is dull or waxy."}},{"k":"wb_3d_closed_sr","v":{"s":"3D specimen closed."}},{"k":"wb_3d_opened_sr","v":{"s":"3D specimen opened below the bench. Drag or use the arrow buttons to turn it."}},{"k":"wb_3d_hide","v":{"s":"Hide 3D specimen"}},{"k":"wb_3d_show","v":{"s":"Turn it in 3D"}},{"k":"wb_form_large_aria","v":{"s":"The unknown fragment, enlarged. "}},{"k":"wb_obs_form_cue","v":{"s":"Look for corners, sheets, columns or points"}},{"k":"wb_obs_form_cue_help","v":{"s":"Right-angle steps mean box-like cleavage. Leaning faces mean rhombs. Layers that peel are sheets. A long six-sided column is a prism. Triangles meeting in points are pyramids. A thin slab is a blade. A rounded crystal of many small faces is a ball. Lumpy with no faces is massive."}},{"k":"wb_reading_mass","v":{"s":"Balance reading (mass)"}},{"k":"wb_reading_volume","v":{"s":"Water displaced (volume)"}},{"k":"wb_obs_choices_aria","v":{"s":"Choose the description that matches what you see"}},{"k":"wb_obs_honesty","v":{"s":"Record what you see, not what you expect. A misread will empty the shortlist, and you can look again."}},{"k":"wb_obs_discard","v":{"s":"Discard this trial"}},{"k":"wb_3d_unavailable","v":{"s":"The 3D specimen is unavailable on this host. The lens porthole above carries the same luster evidence."}},{"k":"wb_3d_title","v":{"s":"Hand specimen under the lamp"}},{"k":"wb_3d_controls_aria","v":{"s":"3D specimen view controls"}},{"k":"wb_3d_aria","v":{"s":"Rotating 3D model of the unknown hand specimen under a lamp. "}},{"k":"wb_3d_help","v":{"s":"Drag to turn it. Watch the highlight: does it slide like a mirror, stay as one sharp point, spread as a soft glow, or never appear?"}},{"k":"wb_running_form","v":{"s":"Looking at the fragment’s shape…"}},{"k":"wb_pool_aria","v":{"s":"Choose the candidate set"}},{"k":"wb_pool_challenge_help","v":{"s":"Adds diamond, garnet, olivine, sulfur, corundum, topaz, graphite and the two copper carbonates. Several are harder than the streak plate, and three of them fizz, so neither test finishes the job alone."}},{"k":"wb_pool_standard_help","v":{"s":"Twelve common minerals with clearly different signatures."}},{"k":"wb_meta_form","v":{"s":"Free look: corners, sheets, columns or no faces"}},{"k":"wb_t_form_aria","v":{"s":"Describe the form of the fragment on the bench"}},{"k":"wb_sr_record_prompt","v":{"s":"Choose the description that matches in the observation card."}},{"k":"wb_sr_lens_evidence","v":{"s":"Under the lens: "}},{"k":"wb_sr_streak_groove","v":{"s":"The specimen cut a groove into the porcelain and left no powder."}},{"k":"wb_sr_streak_powder","v":{"s":"A powder mark crosses the plate. Its colour is "}},{"k":"wb_sr_streak_powder2","v":{"s":", shown beside the specimen’s outward colour."}},{"k":"wb_sr_magnet_moved","v":{"s":"The specimen slid across the bench toward the magnet."}},{"k":"wb_sr_magnet_still","v":{"s":"The magnet passed close by and the specimen did not move."}},{"k":"wb_sr_acid_bubbles","v":{"s":"Bubbles rise steadily from the drop."}},{"k":"wb_sr_acid_still","v":{"s":"The drop sits still on the surface; nothing rises from it."}},{"k":"wb_sr_density_readings","v":{"s":"The balance reads "}},{"k":"wb_sr_density_readings2","v":{"s":" grams. The water level rose by "}},{"k":"wb_sr_density_readings3","v":{"s":" cubic centimetres. Divide mass by volume and choose the band your answer falls in."}},{"k":"wb_sr_scratch_groove","v":{"s":"The reference cut a dark groove with chips thrown ahead of the tip."}},{"k":"wb_sr_scratch_trace","v":{"s":"Only a broken, uneven trace: hard to tell whether it cut in."}},{"k":"wb_sr_scratch_smear","v":{"s":"Only a faint pale smear of the reference’s own material; the surface underneath is unmarked."}},{"k":"wb_of_seven_types","v":{"s":" of 7 confirmed property types"}},{"k":"wb_reexamine_aria","v":{"s":"Look again and re-record: "}},{"k":"wb_reexamine","v":{"s":"Look again"}},{"k":"wb_pool_next_challenge_sr","v":{"s":"Challenge set selected for the next unknown: "}},{"k":"wb_pool_next_standard_sr","v":{"s":"Standard set selected for the next unknown: "}},{"k":"wb_pool_on","v":{"s":"Challenge set on"}},{"k":"wb_pool_off","v":{"s":"Challenge set off"}},{"k":"wb_pool_next","v":{"s":"applies to the next unknown"}},{"k":"wb_nb_copy_aria","v":{"s":"Copy the field notebook as plain text for a lab report"}},{"k":"wb_nb_copy","v":{"s":"Copy notebook for my report"}},{"k":"wb_next_lookalike_aria","v":{"s":"Next: its closest look-alike, "}},{"k":"wb_next_lookalike","v":{"s":"Try its look-alike: "}},{"k":"wb_fact_form","v":{"s":"Form: "}},{"k":"wb_luster_metallic","v":{"s":"Metallic"}},{"k":"wb_luster_metallic_hint","v":{"s":"Shines like polished metal. Opaque: no light gets inside. A hard, mirror-like flash that slides as you tilt it."}},{"k":"wb_luster_glassy","v":{"s":"Glassy (vitreous)"}},{"k":"wb_luster_glassy_hint","v":{"s":"Shines like broken glass. A small, sharp highlight, and light passes a little way into the specimen."}},{"k":"wb_luster_pearly","v":{"s":"Pearly or silky"}},{"k":"wb_luster_pearly_hint","v":{"s":"A soft, layered sheen like the inside of a seashell. The highlight is broad and blurred, with faint rainbow tints."}},{"k":"wb_luster_dull","v":{"s":"Waxy, resinous or dull"}},{"k":"wb_luster_dull_hint","v":{"s":"A soft shine like candle wax or amber, or no shine at all like chalk. No crisp highlight anywhere."}},{"k":"wb_form_blocky_hint","v":{"s":"Breaks into box-like pieces; cleavage directions meet at about 90°."}},{"k":"wb_form_blocky_sr","v":{"s":"The fragment has box-like corners and stepped faces meeting near right angles."}},{"k":"wb_form_rhombs","v":{"s":"Leaning blocks (rhombs)"}},{"k":"wb_form_rhombs_hint","v":{"s":"Faces are parallelograms that lean, like a squashed box."}},{"k":"wb_form_rhombs_sr","v":{"s":"The fragment breaks into leaning, parallelogram-faced pieces."}},{"k":"wb_form_sheets","v":{"s":"Thin sheets or flakes"}},{"k":"wb_form_sheets_hint","v":{"s":"Peels into flexible layers like the pages of a book."}},{"k":"wb_form_sheets_sr","v":{"s":"The fragment is a stack of thin sheets that peel apart."}},{"k":"wb_form_prism","v":{"s":"Six-sided column"}},{"k":"wb_form_prism_hint","v":{"s":"A long prism with a pointed end and lines running along its length."}},{"k":"wb_form_prism_sr","v":{"s":"The fragment is a six-sided column with lengthwise lines."}},{"k":"wb_form_pyramids","v":{"s":"Pointed pyramids"}},{"k":"wb_form_pyramids_hint","v":{"s":"Triangular faces meeting in points, like two pyramids base to base."}},{"k":"wb_form_pyramids_sr","v":{"s":"The fragment shows triangular faces meeting in points."}},{"k":"wb_form_blades","v":{"s":"Flat blade or tablet"}},{"k":"wb_form_blades_hint","v":{"s":"A thin, flat slab much wider than it is thick."}},{"k":"wb_form_blades_sr","v":{"s":"The fragment is a thin, flat slab."}},{"k":"wb_form_ball","v":{"s":"Ball of many small faces"}},{"k":"wb_form_ball_hint","v":{"s":"A rounded crystal covered in small four-sided faces, like a soccer ball (a dodecahedron)."}},{"k":"wb_form_ball_sr","v":{"s":"The fragment is a rounded crystal covered in many small faces."}},{"k":"wb_form_massive","v":{"s":"No clear faces (massive)"}},{"k":"wb_form_massive_hint","v":{"s":"Lumpy or grainy with no flat faces or straight edges."}},{"k":"wb_form_massive_sr","v":{"s":"The fragment is a lumpy mass without flat faces."}},{"k":"wb_streak_choice_powder-white","v":{"s":"White"}},{"k":"wb_streak_choice_powder-greenish-black","v":{"s":"Greenish-black"}},{"k":"wb_streak_choice_powder-black","v":{"s":"Black"}},{"k":"wb_streak_choice_powder-red-brown","v":{"s":"Red-brown"}},{"k":"wb_streak_choice_powder-lead-gray","v":{"s":"Lead-gray"}},{"k":"wb_streak_choice_powder-yellow-brown","v":{"s":"Yellow-brown"}},{"k":"wb_streak_choice_powder-white-yellow","v":{"s":"Pale yellow"}},{"k":"wb_streak_choice_plate-scratched","v":{"s":"No powder — the plate itself was grooved"}},{"k":"ls_depth_mid1","v":{"s":"~5 km · burial"}},{"k":"ls_depth_mid2","v":{"s":"~15 km · heat + pressure"}},{"k":"wb_case_title","v":{"s":"Field case"}},{"k":"wb_case_complete","v":{"s":"Case complete"}},{"k":"wb_case_named","v":{"s":"named"}},{"k":"wb_case_aria","v":{"s":"Minerals named this session"}},{"k":"wb_case_remaining","v":{"s":"still unnamed"}}],"id":572}},{"k":"schoolbehaviortoolkit","v":{"o":[{"k":"a11y_acting_out_cycle_phases","v":{"s":"Acting-out cycle phases"}},{"k":"a11y_cycle_phase","v":{"s":"Cycle phase"}},{"k":"a11y_reset_to_phase_1_calm","v":{"s":"Reset to Phase 1 Calm"}},{"k":"a11y_scenario_picker","v":{"s":"Scenario picker"}},{"k":"a11y_completed","v":{"s":"completed"}},{"k":"a11y_pbis_three_tier_support_diagram_showing_univers","v":{"s":"PBIS three-tier support diagram showing universal, targeted, and intensive tiers"}},{"k":"a11y_behavior_tier","v":{"s":"Behavior tier"}},{"k":"a11y_intensity","v":{"s":"Intensity"}},{"k":"a11y_function_confidence","v":{"s":"Function confidence"}},{"k":"a11y_environment_stability","v":{"s":"Environment stability"}},{"k":"back_to_stem_lab","v":{"s":"Back to STEAM Lab"}},{"k":"school_behavior_toolkit","v":{"s":"School Behavior Toolkit"}},{"k":"12_sections_4_interactive","v":{"s":"12 sections · 4 interactive"}},{"k":"applied_k_12_practice_pbis_replacement","v":{"s":"Applied K-12 practice. PBIS · Replacement Behaviors (with function-spotter) · Setting Events · Acting-Out Cycle (with phase scrubber) · Restraint Ethics (with decision tree) · Equity & Disparities."}},{"k":"pbis_tiers","v":{"s":"PBIS Tiers"}},{"k":"fba_process","v":{"s":"FBA Process"}},{"k":"bip_template","v":{"s":"BIP Template"}},{"k":"replacement_behaviors","v":{"s":"Replacement Behaviors"}},{"k":"setting_events","v":{"s":"Setting Events"}},{"k":"acting_out_cycle","v":{"s":"Acting-Out Cycle"}},{"k":"restraint_seclusion","v":{"s":"Restraint & Seclusion"}},{"k":"cico_template","v":{"s":"CICO Template"}},{"k":"equity_disparities","v":{"s":"Equity & Disparities"}},{"k":"maine_resources","v":{"s":"Maine Resources"}},{"k":"connect","v":{"s":"Connect"}},{"k":"behavior_inquiry","v":{"s":"Behavior Inquiry"}},{"k":"school_behavior_toolkit_sections","v":{"s":"School Behavior Toolkit sections"}},{"k":"tier_3_5_intensive","v":{"s":"Tier 3 · ~5% · intensive"}},{"k":"tier_2_15_targeted","v":{"s":"Tier 2 · ~15% · targeted"}},{"k":"tier_1_80_universal_all_students","v":{"s":"Tier 1 · ~80% · universal (all students)"}},{"k":"pbis_pyramid_tier_1_universal_supports","v":{"s":"PBIS pyramid: Tier 1 universal supports for ~80% of students, Tier 2 targeted for ~15%, Tier 3 intensive for ~5%."}},{"k":"bands_are_area_proportional_to_the_80_","v":{"s":"bands are area-proportional to the ~80 / 15 / 5 split"}},{"k":"who_it_serves","v":{"s":"Who it serves: "}},{"k":"concrete_examples","v":{"s":"Concrete examples"}},{"k":"data_signal","v":{"s":"📊 Data signal"}},{"k":"when_to_escalate","v":{"s":"⏫ When to escalate"}},{"k":"problem_behavior_typically_looks_like","v":{"s":"⚠ Problem behavior typically looks like"}},{"k":"replacement_behavior","v":{"s":"↪ Replacement behavior"}},{"k":"how_to_teach_it","v":{"s":"🎓 How to teach it"}},{"k":"common_pitfall","v":{"s":"🪤 Common pitfall"}},{"k":"signs","v":{"s":"Signs"}},{"k":"do_this","v":{"s":"✓ Do this"}},{"k":"don_t_do","v":{"s":"✗ Don't do"}},{"k":"this_is_education_not_training","v":{"s":"⚠ This is education, not training."}},{"k":"reading_this_section_does_not_authoriz","v":{"s":"Reading this section does not authorize anyone to perform restraint or seclusion. State law requires specific certified training (CPI / NCI / Mandt or equivalent) and authorized-staff designation. This panel teaches the framework and ethics so school psychs and IEP-team members can recognize appropriate use, document properly, and revise BIPs in response to incidents."}},{"k":"counter_line","v":{"s":"↪ Counter-line:"}},{"k":"function_statement","v":{"s":"Function statement"}},{"k":"bip_8_parts","v":{"s":"BIP (8 parts)"}},{"k":"the_5_fba_steps_produce_one_function_s","v":{"s":"The 5 FBA steps produce one function statement — the spine every BIP strategy must trace back to."}},{"k":"what_to_do","v":{"s":"What to do"}},{"k":"key_idea","v":{"s":"🔑 Key idea"}},{"k":"common_pitfall_2","v":{"s":"🪤 Common pitfall:"}},{"k":"what_to_write","v":{"s":"What to write"}},{"k":"sample_entry","v":{"s":"📝 Sample entry"}},{"k":"common_pitfall_3","v":{"s":"🪤 Common pitfall:"}},{"k":"what_it_looks_like","v":{"s":"What it looks like"}},{"k":"sample_script","v":{"s":"🗣 Sample script"}},{"k":"common_pitfall_4","v":{"s":"🪤 Common pitfall:"}},{"k":"school_psych_equity_audit_five_questio","v":{"s":"School-psych equity audit — five questions"}},{"k":"practical_questions_to_bring_into_your","v":{"s":"Practical questions to bring into your next discipline-data review or PBIS team meeting. The federal numbers describe the pattern. These questions help your building see where your specific patterns sit and what to do about them."}},{"k":"stem_lab_behavioral_science","v":{"s":"STEAM Lab → Behavioral Science"}},{"k":"the_science_of_operant_conditioning_sk","v":{"s":"The science of operant conditioning — Skinner-box simulation, schedules of reinforcement, shaping, extinction, FBA practice. The mechanics behind what this Toolkit applies in K-12 settings."}},{"k":"9_progressive_levels_schedule_sleuth_f","v":{"s":"9 progressive levels · Schedule Sleuth · Function Sleuth · Glossary · Ethics"}},{"k":"disability_voices","v":{"s":"Disability Voices"}},{"k":"sel_hub_identity_care","v":{"s":"SEL Hub → Identity & Care"}},{"k":"real_autistic_and_disabled_advocates_w","v":{"s":"Real autistic and disabled advocates whose work shaped — and critiqued — disability practice. Centered as persons, not behavioral subjects. Read here for the human side of the work."}},{"k":"ari_ne_eman_temple_grandin_damian_milt","v":{"s":"Ari Ne'eman · Temple Grandin · Damian Milton · Henny Kupferstein · Kassiane Asasumasu · Mel Baggs · Ly Xīnzhèn M. Zhǎngsūn Brown · Patty Berne"}},{"k":"why_three_separate_spaces","v":{"s":"🧭 Why three separate spaces"}},{"k":"putting_skinner_box_imagery_applied_k_","v":{"s":"Putting Skinner-box imagery, applied K-12 practice, and named real autistic adults all in one tool would be exactly the dehumanizing arc the disability community has critiqued: animal-conditioning visuals → \"applied\" → and the people we apply it to. Splitting them into three connected but distinct spaces is a deliberate ethical choice. The science is the science (BehaviorLab). The K-12 practice is school-psych work (this Toolkit). The voices are the people (Disability Voices in SEL Hub). All three matter. None should crowd the others."}},{"k":"tier_mismatch","v":{"s":"Tier mismatch"}},{"k":"selected_tier_does_not_match_observed_","v":{"s":"Selected tier does not match observed intensity. Move up (under-supporting) or down (over-pathologizing) accordingly."}},{"k":"fba_needed_first","v":{"s":"FBA needed first"}},{"k":"tier_3_bip_requires_function_knowledge","v":{"s":"Tier 3 BIP requires function knowledge. Function confidence below 7 means you cannot ethically design a function-based plan yet."}},{"k":"environment_too_unstable","v":{"s":"Environment too unstable"}},{"k":"any_plan_will_look_like_it_failed_if_t","v":{"s":"Any plan will look like it failed if the setting events are constantly shifting. Stabilize the environment before measuring outcomes."}},{"k":"partially_ready","v":{"s":"Partially ready"}},{"k":"most_pieces_in_place_address_the_weake","v":{"s":"Most pieces in place. Address the weakest dimension before going live."}},{"k":"implementable_plan","v":{"s":"Implementable plan"}},{"k":"tier_matched_to_intensity_function_con","v":{"s":"Tier matched to intensity, function confidence adequate, environment stable enough. Pilot the plan with progress monitoring."}},{"k":"behavior_plan_inquiry_is_this_plan_rea","v":{"s":"🧪 Behavior Plan Inquiry — Is This Plan Ready to Pilot?"}},{"k":"set_tier_observed_intensity_function_c","v":{"s":"Set tier, observed intensity, function confidence, environment stability. Predict whether the plan is ready to implement. No score, no reveal."}},{"k":"pbis_multi_tiered_system_of_supports","v":{"s":"PBIS multi-tiered system of supports"}},{"k":"pbis_tier","v":{"s":"PBIS Tier"}},{"k":"behavior_intensity_1_10","v":{"s":"Behavior intensity (1-10)"}},{"k":"function_confidence_1_10","v":{"s":"Function confidence (1-10)"}},{"k":"environment_stability_1_10","v":{"s":"Environment stability (1-10)"}},{"k":"log_this_case","v":{"s":"📋 Log this case"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"Reset"}},{"k":"your_hypothesis_when_does_an_unstable_","v":{"s":"Your hypothesis (when does an unstable environment matter MORE than function knowledge?)"}},{"k":"e_g_if_setting_events_are_dominant_eve","v":{"s":"e.g., if setting events are dominant, even a perfect function-based plan fails because the antecedent context keeps changing..."}},{"k":"i_m_stuck_show_open_questions","v":{"s":"🤔 I'm stuck — show open questions"}},{"k":"open_questions_no_answer_key","v":{"s":"Open questions (no answer key)"}},{"k":"why_does_a_tier_3_plan_require_fba_lev","v":{"s":"Why does a Tier 3 plan require FBA-level function confidence before you can ethically design it?"}},{"k":"a_high_intensity_behavior_in_a_stable_","v":{"s":"A high-intensity behavior in a stable environment vs the same intensity in chaos — same plan?"}},{"k":"when_is_tier_mismatch_actually_a_sign_","v":{"s":"When is \"tier mismatch\" actually a sign that adult bias is driving over-pathologizing (especially across race/disability lines)?"}},{"k":"how_would_you_communicate_not_implemen","v":{"s":"How would you communicate \"not implementable yet\" to a frustrated team or parent without sounding dismissive?"}},{"k":"i_can_explain_why_this_tier_intensity_","v":{"s":"I can explain why this tier/intensity/function/environment combination yields this state."}},{"k":"explain_in_your_own_words","v":{"s":"Explain in your own words..."}},{"k":"inquiry_widget_no_score_no_reveal_no_a","v":{"s":"Inquiry widget — no score, no reveal, no answer dump. PBIS tier-matching heuristics from CASEL/PBIS Center; real plans should be team-developed and parent/family-centered. Equity audit (see Equity tab) is essential before assuming a tier-3 case is purely behavioral."}},{"k":"school_behavior_toolkit_2","v":{"s":"School Behavior Toolkit"}},{"k":"hypothesis_input","v":{"s":"Behavior plan readiness hypothesis"}},{"k":"explanation_input","v":{"s":"Explain behavior plan readiness"}},{"k":"14_sections_7_interactive","v":{"s":"14 sections · 7 interactive"}},{"k":"5_min_free_time","v":{"s":"5 min Free Time"}},{"k":"act_of_kindness","v":{"s":"Act of Kindness"}},{"k":"attention","v":{"s":"Attention"}},{"k":"behavior_maintained_by_access_to_a_pre","v":{"s":"Behavior maintained by access to a preferred item or activity. Example: A child screams in the store until the parent buys them candy. The screaming is reinforced by getting the candy."}},{"k":"behavior_maintained_by_removal_of_an_a","v":{"s":"Behavior maintained by removal of an aversive stimulus. Example: A student has a meltdown when given math work, and the teacher removes the assignment. The meltdown is negatively reinforced."}},{"k":"behavior_maintained_by_social_attentio","v":{"s":"Behavior maintained by social attention from others. Example: A student calls out in class to get the teacher to look at them. The attention (even if negative) reinforces the calling out."}},{"k":"behavior_maintained_by_the_sensory_sti","v":{"s":"Behavior maintained by the sensory stimulation it produces, independent of social consequences. The behavior itself feels good. Example: Hand-flapping may produce proprioceptive input that is reinforcing."}},{"k":"bip_back","v":{"s":"Back a step"}},{"k":"bip_back_label","v":{"s":"← Back"}},{"k":"bip_chain_h","v":{"s":"✅ Your reasoning chain — practice draft"}},{"k":"bip_chain_scope","v":{"s":"This is the reasoning, not the plan. A plan a team can run also needs the other components above — baseline data, response procedures, a crisis plan, fidelity and review — plus the student and family in the conversation and a supervising professional. Do not paste this into a real BIP."}},{"k":"bip_draft_h","v":{"s":"✏️ Draft the reasoning chain"}},{"k":"bip_draft_sub","v":{"s":"Five steps, in order. Each one has to follow from the one before it — if the replacement behaviour does not get the student the same thing the problem behaviour got, the plan will not hold, however well written the rest of it is."}},{"k":"bip_edit","v":{"s":"✏️ Edit"}},{"k":"bip_fill_first","v":{"s":"✏️ Fill in this step first."}},{"k":"bip_finish","v":{"s":"See the chain →"}},{"k":"bip_new","v":{"s":"↻ Start over"}},{"k":"bip_next","v":{"s":"Next step →"}},{"k":"bip_s1","v":{"s":"Step 1 — Target behaviour"}},{"k":"bip_s1_p","v":{"s":"Describe it so two observers would count the same thing. Not \"disruptive\" — what does it look like?"}},{"k":"bip_s2","v":{"s":"Step 2 — Antecedent"}},{"k":"bip_s2_p","v":{"s":"What reliably happens immediately before? Include the setting events that make it more likely."}},{"k":"bip_s3","v":{"s":"Step 3 — Hypothesised function"}},{"k":"bip_s3_p","v":{"s":"What does the behaviour reliably GET or AVOID? A hypothesis you would test with ABC data, not a label."}},{"k":"bip_s4","v":{"s":"Step 4 — Replacement behaviour"}},{"k":"bip_s4_p","v":{"s":"What should the student do INSTEAD that gets the same function, faster and more reliably than the problem behaviour did?"}},{"k":"bip_s5","v":{"s":"Step 5 — Teaching and reinforcement"}},{"k":"bip_s5_p","v":{"s":"How is the replacement taught, and how is it reinforced often enough at first to compete?"}},{"k":"clean_up_area","v":{"s":"Clean Up Area"}},{"k":"computer_time","v":{"s":"Computer Time"}},{"k":"fn_all_done","v":{"s":"🏆 Every vignette complete"}},{"k":"fn_correct","v":{"s":"✅ That is the function."}},{"k":"fn_final","v":{"s":"Final: "}},{"k":"fn_res_all","v":{"s":" — every function correctly identified. That is the concept; on a real case the function is a hypothesis you confirm with ABC data and supervision, not a label you read off a paragraph."}},{"k":"fn_res_more","v":{"s":" — these distinctions take many examples. Re-read the four reference cards above, then the reasoning on each miss, and run it again."}},{"k":"fn_res_ok","v":{"s":" — a solid baseline. Re-read the reasoning on the ones you missed, looking for what the behaviour consistently PRODUCES versus what it PREVENTS."}},{"k":"fn_res_strong","v":{"s":" — strong. The pair most often confused is attention versus escape, because adult attention and demand removal usually arrive together; the question is which one the behaviour is working for."}},{"k":"fn_wrong","v":{"s":"❌ Not this time — read the reasoning."}},{"k":"four_functions_h","v":{"s":"🔍 Four functions of behaviour"}},{"k":"four_functions_sub","v":{"s":"Every behaviour is maintained by what it PRODUCES or what it PREVENTS. Topography — what it looks like — does not tell you the function; two children can do the same thing for opposite reasons."}},{"k":"four_functions_tab","v":{"s":"Four Functions"}},{"k":"function_sleuth_h","v":{"s":"🕵️ Function Sleuth"}},{"k":"function_sleuth_sub","v":{"s":"Read the vignette and name what the behaviour is getting or avoiding. On a real case this is a hypothesis you then test with ABC data — here the answer is knowable from the paragraph, which is exactly what makes it practice rather than assessment."}},{"k":"functions_footer","v":{"s":"🎯 Function is a hypothesis, not a label. On a real case you confirm it with ABC data and, where the behaviour is dangerous or the hypothesis is contested, a functional analysis — under supervision. Matched intervention means the plan follows the function: escape-maintained behaviour is not fixed by taking away recess."}},{"k":"help_a_peer","v":{"s":"Help a Peer"}},{"k":"homework_complete","v":{"s":"Homework Complete"}},{"k":"homework_pass","v":{"s":"Homework Pass"}},{"k":"line_leader","v":{"s":"Line Leader"}},{"k":"looks_like","v":{"s":"Often looks like"}},{"k":"lunch_with_teacher","v":{"s":"Lunch with Teacher"}},{"k":"matched_intervention","v":{"s":"Matched intervention"}},{"k":"mystery_prize","v":{"s":"Mystery Prize"}},{"k":"next_vignette","v":{"s":"Next vignette →"}},{"k":"on_task_15_min","v":{"s":"On-task 15 min"}},{"k":"pick_the_function","v":{"s":"Pick the function"}},{"k":"quiet_transition","v":{"s":"Quiet Transition"}},{"k":"read_20_pages","v":{"s":"Read 20 Pages"}},{"k":"score_80","v":{"s":"Score 80%+"}},{"k":"snack_choice","v":{"s":"Snack Choice"}},{"k":"start_function_sleuth","v":{"s":"Start Function Sleuth"}},{"k":"start_over","v":{"s":"↻ Run it again"}},{"k":"start_the_drill","v":{"s":"▶ Start the drill"}},{"k":"sticker","v":{"s":"Sticker"}},{"k":"tangible","v":{"s":"Tangible"}},{"k":"tk_balance","v":{"s":"Token balance"}},{"k":"tk_build_h","v":{"s":"🛠️ Build one"}},{"k":"tk_build_sub","v":{"s":"Award tokens, then spend them. Watch the exchange ratio: a menu whose cheapest item takes a week to reach is a menu the student stops working for."}},{"k":"tk_earn","v":{"s":"Earn tokens"}},{"k":"tk_footer","v":{"s":"🪙 A token economy is a scaffold, not a destination. The plan should name from the start how the schedule thins, what natural reinforcer takes over, and how you would know it had."}},{"k":"tk_log","v":{"s":"Exchange record"}},{"k":"tk_part1","v":{"s":"1. What earns a token"}},{"k":"tk_part1_b","v":{"s":"Specific, observable, and already within reach. If the student cannot yet do it, a token system will not teach it — that is a job for instruction and shaping first."}},{"k":"tk_part2","v":{"s":"2. The token itself"}},{"k":"tk_part2_b","v":{"s":"Delivered immediately, visibly, and without negotiation. Its value is entirely borrowed from the exchange, which is why an exchange that keeps slipping kills the system."}},{"k":"tk_part3","v":{"s":"3. Backup reinforcers"}},{"k":"tk_part3_b","v":{"s":"Chosen by the student, not the adult. A reinforcer is defined by its effect on behaviour — if the behaviour does not increase, the thing on the menu is not a reinforcer, however much you would like it to be."}},{"k":"tk_pit1","v":{"s":"Paying for what the student already does reliably. That is not reinforcement, it is a wage — and it can reduce the behaviour once the wage stops."}},{"k":"tk_pit2","v":{"s":"An exchange ratio nobody can reach. If the cheapest item is days away, the token stops predicting anything and stops working."}},{"k":"tk_pit3","v":{"s":"Taking tokens away. Response cost is a punishment procedure with its own ethical and procedural requirements; bolting it onto an earn-only board is a change of intervention, not a tweak."}},{"k":"tk_pit4","v":{"s":"No plan to end. A board that never thins toward natural reinforcers is a board the student needs forever, which was never the goal."}},{"k":"tk_pit5","v":{"s":"A menu the adult picked. Preference is measured, not assumed — and it changes week to week."}},{"k":"tk_pitfalls_h","v":{"s":"⚠️ Where token boards go wrong"}},{"k":"tk_reset","v":{"s":"Reset the token board"}},{"k":"tk_reset_label","v":{"s":"↻ Reset board"}},{"k":"tk_spend","v":{"s":"Exchange"}},{"k":"token_economy_h","v":{"s":"🪙 Token economy"}},{"k":"token_economy_sub","v":{"s":"Tokens are conditioned reinforcers: worthless in themselves, valuable because of what they buy. Three parts have to be designed together — the behaviours that earn, the token, and the backup reinforcers it exchanges for."}},{"k":"token_economy_tab","v":{"s":"Token Economy"}},{"k":"vignette","v":{"s":"Vignette"}}],"id":573}},{"k":"semiconductor","v":{"o":[{"k":"silicon_si","v":{"s":"Silicon (Si)"}},{"k":"germanium_ge","v":{"s":"Germanium (Ge)"}},{"k":"diamond_c","v":{"s":"Diamond (C)"}},{"k":"copper_cu","v":{"s":"Copper (Cu)"}},{"k":"glass_sio","v":{"s":"Glass (SiO₂)"}},{"k":"intrinsic","v":{"s":"Intrinsic"}},{"k":"phosphorus_p","v":{"s":"Phosphorus (P)"}},{"k":"arsenic_as","v":{"s":"Arsenic (As)"}},{"k":"boron_b","v":{"s":"Boron (B)"}},{"k":"gallium_ga","v":{"s":"Gallium (Ga)"}},{"k":"antimony_sb","v":{"s":"Antimony (Sb)"}},{"k":"indium_in","v":{"s":"Indium (In)"}},{"k":"band_gap","v":{"s":"Band Gap"}},{"k":"doping","v":{"s":"Doping"}},{"k":"p_n_junction","v":{"s":"P-N Junction"}},{"k":"transistor","v":{"s":"Transistor"}},{"k":"logic_gates","v":{"s":"Logic Gates"}},{"k":"i_v_curves","v":{"s":"I-V Curves"}},{"k":"circuit_lab","v":{"s":"Circuit Lab"}},{"k":"wafer_fab","v":{"s":"Wafer Fab"}},{"k":"led_spectrum","v":{"s":"LED Spectrum"}},{"k":"solar_cell","v":{"s":"Solar Cell"}},{"k":"moore_s_law","v":{"s":"Moore's Law"}},{"k":"quantum_wells","v":{"s":"Quantum Wells"}},{"k":"memory_cells","v":{"s":"Memory Cells"}},{"k":"amplifier","v":{"s":"Amplifier"}},{"k":"doping_discovery","v":{"s":"Doping Discovery"}},{"k":"thinking","v":{"s":"✨ Thinking…"}},{"k":"read_aloud","v":{"s":"Read aloud"}},{"k":"photon_excitation","v":{"s":"Photon Excitation"}},{"k":"fermi_level","v":{"s":"Fermi Level"}},{"k":"carriers","v":{"s":"Carriers"}},{"k":"depletion","v":{"s":"Depletion"}},{"k":"i_v_curve","v":{"s":"I-V Curve"}},{"k":"led_mode","v":{"s":"LED Mode"}},{"k":"inverts_input_built_from_1_pmos_1_nmos","v":{"s":"Inverts input. Built from 1 PMOS + 1 NMOS (CMOS inverter)."}},{"k":"output_high_only_when_both_inputs_are_","v":{"s":"Output HIGH only when BOTH inputs are HIGH. NAND + NOT (6 transistors)."}},{"k":"output_high_when_any_input_is_high_nor","v":{"s":"Output HIGH when ANY input is HIGH. NOR + NOT (6 transistors)."}},{"k":"universal_gate_2_series_nmos_2_paralle","v":{"s":"Universal gate! 2 series NMOS + 2 parallel PMOS. All logic from NANDs."}},{"k":"universal_gate_2_parallel_nmos_2_serie","v":{"s":"Universal gate! 2 parallel NMOS + 2 series PMOS."}},{"k":"output_high_when_inputs_differ_key_for","v":{"s":"Output HIGH when inputs differ. Key for adders. Uses ~8 transistors."}},{"k":"output_high_when_inputs_match_used_in_","v":{"s":"Output HIGH when inputs match. Used in comparators."}},{"k":"data_table_a_b_q","v":{"s":"Data table: A, B, Q"}},{"k":"ohm_reference","v":{"s":"Ohm Reference"}},{"k":"resistor","v":{"s":"Resistor"}},{"k":"diode","v":{"s":"Diode"}},{"k":"capacitor","v":{"s":"Capacitor"}},{"k":"nmos_fet","v":{"s":"NMOS FET"}},{"k":"pmos_fet","v":{"s":"PMOS FET"}},{"k":"build_a_circuit_from_components_add_pa","v":{"s":"Build a circuit from components. Add parts, then simulate!"}},{"k":"click_components_above_to_add_them","v":{"s":"Click components above to add them"}},{"k":"simulation_results","v":{"s":"✓ Simulation Results"}},{"k":"crystal_growth","v":{"s":"Crystal Growth"}},{"k":"a_silicon_ingot_is_pulled_from_molten_","v":{"s":"A silicon ingot is pulled from molten silicon using the Czochralski method at ~1414°C."}},{"k":"wafer_slicing","v":{"s":"Wafer Slicing"}},{"k":"the_ingot_is_sliced_into_thin_wafers_7","v":{"s":"The ingot is sliced into thin wafers (~775μm thick) using diamond wire saws."}},{"k":"thermal_oxidation","v":{"s":"Thermal Oxidation"}},{"k":"a_thin_layer_of_sio_is_grown_on_the_wa","v":{"s":"A thin layer of SiO₂ is grown on the wafer surface at ~1000°C in an oxygen furnace."}},{"k":"photolithography","v":{"s":"Photolithography"}},{"k":"uv_light_transfers_circuit_patterns_fr","v":{"s":"UV light transfers circuit patterns from a mask onto photoresist-coated wafers."}},{"k":"etching","v":{"s":"Etching"}},{"k":"unwanted_material_is_removed_by_chemic","v":{"s":"Unwanted material is removed by chemical (wet) or plasma (dry) etching."}},{"k":"ion_implantation","v":{"s":"Ion Implantation"}},{"k":"dopant_atoms_are_shot_into_the_silicon","v":{"s":"Dopant atoms are shot into the silicon at high energy to change its electrical properties."}},{"k":"thin_film_deposition","v":{"s":"Thin Film Deposition"}},{"k":"metal_and_insulator_layers_are_deposit","v":{"s":"Metal and insulator layers are deposited by CVD, PVD, or ALD techniques."}},{"k":"metallization_cmp","v":{"s":"Metallization & CMP"}},{"k":"metal_interconnects_are_patterned_and_","v":{"s":"Metal interconnects are patterned and polished flat. Multiple layers build up the circuit wiring."}},{"k":"photoresist","v":{"s":"Photoresist"}},{"k":"doped_region","v":{"s":"Doped region"}},{"k":"poly_si_metal","v":{"s":"Poly-Si / Metal"}},{"k":"cu_interconnect","v":{"s":"Cu Interconnect"}},{"k":"gaas_infrared","v":{"s":"GaAs (Infrared)"}},{"k":"algaas_red","v":{"s":"AlGaAs (Red)"}},{"k":"gaasp_red","v":{"s":"GaAsP (Red)"}},{"k":"gaasp_orange","v":{"s":"GaAsP (Orange)"}},{"k":"gap_n_yellow","v":{"s":"GaP:N (Yellow)"}},{"k":"ingan_green","v":{"s":"InGaN (Green)"}},{"k":"ingan_blue","v":{"s":"InGaN (Blue)"}},{"k":"algan_uv","v":{"s":"AlGaN (UV)"}},{"k":"blue_ingan_phosphor","v":{"s":"Blue InGaN + Phosphor"}},{"k":"crystalline_si","v":{"s":"Crystalline Si"}},{"k":"cdte_thin_film","v":{"s":"CdTe Thin Film"}},{"k":"perovskite","v":{"s":"Perovskite"}},{"k":"gaas_iii_v","v":{"s":"GaAs (III-V)"}},{"k":"organic_pv","v":{"s":"Organic PV"}},{"k":"perovskite_si_tandem","v":{"s":"Perovskite/Si Tandem"}},{"k":"i_v_p_v_curve","v":{"s":"I-V / P-V Curve"}},{"k":"moore_s_paper_published","v":{"s":"Moore's paper published"}},{"k":"intel_4004","v":{"s":"Intel 4004"}},{"k":"intel_8086","v":{"s":"Intel 8086"}},{"k":"intel_386","v":{"s":"Intel 386"}},{"k":"pentium","v":{"s":"Pentium"}},{"k":"pentium_iii","v":{"s":"Pentium III"}},{"k":"prescott","v":{"s":"Prescott"}},{"k":"core_2_duo","v":{"s":"Core 2 Duo"}},{"k":"core_i7_westmere","v":{"s":"Core i7 (Westmere)"}},{"k":"core_i7_broadwell","v":{"s":"Core i7 (Broadwell)"}},{"k":"apple_a11","v":{"s":"Apple A11 Bionic"}},{"k":"apple_m1","v":{"s":"Apple M1"}},{"k":"apple_m1_ultra","v":{"s":"Apple M1 Ultra"}},{"k":"nvidia_b200","v":{"s":"NVIDIA B200"}},{"k":"moore_s_law_graph_showing_transistor_c","v":{"s":"Moore's Law graph showing transistor counts from 1965 to 2030"}},{"k":"moore_prediction","v":{"s":"Moore Prediction"}},{"k":"x_wavefunction","v":{"s":"ψ(x) Wavefunction"}},{"k":"probability","v":{"s":"|ψ|² Probability"}},{"k":"optical_transitions","v":{"s":"Optical Transitions"}},{"k":"sram_6t","v":{"s":"SRAM (6T)"}},{"k":"6_transistors_per_bit_2_cross_coupled_","v":{"s":"6 transistors per bit: 2 cross-coupled inverters + 2 access transistors. Used in CPU caches."}},{"k":"dram_1t1c","v":{"s":"DRAM (1T1C)"}},{"k":"1_transistor_1_capacitor_per_bit_must_","v":{"s":"1 transistor + 1 capacitor per bit. Must refresh every ~64ms. Used in main memory (RAM sticks)."}},{"k":"flash_nor","v":{"s":"Flash (NOR)"}},{"k":"floating_gate_transistor_traps_charge_","v":{"s":"Floating-gate transistor traps charge. NOR: random access, used in firmware/BIOS."}},{"k":"flash_nand","v":{"s":"Flash (NAND)"}},{"k":"series_connected_floating_gates_sequen","v":{"s":"Series-connected floating gates. Sequential access but extremely dense. SSDs, USB drives, SD cards."}},{"k":"ferroelectric_capacitor_stores_charge_","v":{"s":"Ferroelectric capacitor stores charge with remnant polarization. Non-volatile + fast write. Used in smart cards, automotive."}},{"k":"common_source_mosfet","v":{"s":"Common Source (MOSFET)"}},{"k":"voltage_amplifier_high_input_impedance","v":{"s":"Voltage amplifier. High input impedance (∞ for ideal). Gain = -gₘRₓ. Inverts signal. Most common MOSFET amp."}},{"k":"source_follower","v":{"s":"Source Follower"}},{"k":"voltage_buffer_gain_1_no_inversion_low","v":{"s":"Voltage buffer. Gain ≈ 1 (no inversion). Low output impedance → good for driving loads. Also called source follower."}},{"k":"common_gate_mosfet","v":{"s":"Common Gate (MOSFET)"}},{"k":"current_buffer_low_input_impedance_non","v":{"s":"Current buffer. Low input impedance. Non-inverting. Wide bandwidth → good for RF applications."}},{"k":"common_emitter_bjt","v":{"s":"Common Emitter (BJT)"}},{"k":"bjt_voltage_amplifier_gain_g_r_inverts","v":{"s":"BJT voltage amplifier. Gain = -gₘRᶜ. Inverts signal. Higher gain than MOSFET but lower input impedance."}},{"k":"differential_pair","v":{"s":"Differential Pair"}},{"k":"amplifies_difference_of_two_inputs_rej","v":{"s":"Amplifies difference of two inputs. Rejects common-mode noise. Foundation of op-amps. CMRR typically >60dB."}},{"k":"band_gaps_between_0_5_and_3_5_ev_are_s","v":{"s":"Band gaps between 0.5 and 3.5 eV are semiconductors."}},{"k":"extra_electrons_n_for_negative_charge_","v":{"s":"Extra electrons = N for Negative charge carriers."}},{"k":"think_of_it_as_multiplication_1_1_1_ev","v":{"s":"Think of it as multiplication: 1×1=1, everything else=0."}},{"k":"carriers_recombine_at_the_junction_lea","v":{"s":"Carriers recombine at the junction leaving fixed ions."}},{"k":"positive_gate_attracts_electrons_to_fo","v":{"s":"Positive gate attracts electrons to form a channel."}},{"k":"forward_pushing_carriers_toward_the_ju","v":{"s":"Forward = pushing carriers TOWARD the junction."}},{"k":"more_thermal_energy_more_electron_hole","v":{"s":"More thermal energy = more electron-hole pairs."}},{"k":"nand_can_implement_not_and_or_everythi","v":{"s":"NAND can implement NOT, AND, OR — everything!"}},{"k":"pmos_nmos_work_as_a_complementary_pair","v":{"s":"PMOS + NMOS work as a complementary pair."}},{"k":"speed_mobility_gaas_8500_vs_si_1400_cm","v":{"s":"Speed ∝ mobility. GaAs: 8500 vs Si: 1400 cm²/Vs."}},{"k":"zener_diodes_are_designed_to_conduct_i","v":{"s":"Zener diodes are designed to conduct in reverse!"}},{"k":"the_o_in_mos_stands_for_oxide_insulato","v":{"s":"The \"O\" in MOS stands for Oxide (insulator)."}},{"k":"boron_has_3_valence_electrons_1_fewer_","v":{"s":"Boron has 3 valence electrons (1 fewer than Si)."}},{"k":"v_kt_q_ln_n_n_n_for_typical_doping_lev","v":{"s":"Vₑᵢ = (kT/q)ln(NₐNₓ/nᵢ²) for typical doping levels."}},{"k":"carbon_forms_very_strong_bonds","v":{"s":"Carbon forms very strong bonds."}},{"k":"in_cmos_one_transistor_is_always_off_b","v":{"s":"In CMOS, one transistor is always OFF blocking current."}},{"k":"n_1_for_ideal_junction_n_2_for_recombi","v":{"s":"n=1 for ideal junction, n=2 for recombination in depletion region."}},{"k":"e_3_4_ev_allows_higher_voltage_operati","v":{"s":"E_g = 3.4 eV allows higher voltage operation."}},{"k":"sum_a_xor_b_carry_a_and_b","v":{"s":"Sum = A XOR B, Carry = A AND B."}},{"k":"higher_v_ce_widens_the_depletion_regio","v":{"s":"Higher V_CE widens the depletion region into the base."}},{"k":"e_1_l_smaller_box_higher_energy_steps","v":{"s":"E ∝ 1/L² — smaller box = higher energy steps."}},{"k":"telecom_lasers_use_ingaasp_quantum_wel","v":{"s":"Telecom lasers use InGaAsP quantum wells for precise wavelength control."}},{"k":"e_n_2m_l","v":{"s":"Eₙ = n²π²ħ²/(2m*L²)."}},{"k":"6t_sram_2_cross_coupled_inverters_4t_2","v":{"s":"6T SRAM: 2 cross-coupled inverters (4T) + 2 access transistors."}},{"k":"dram_stores_bits_as_charge_on_a_tiny_c","v":{"s":"DRAM stores bits as charge on a tiny capacitor — it leaks!"}},{"k":"the_floating_gate_is_electrically_isol","v":{"s":"The floating gate is electrically isolated by oxide layers."}},{"k":"l1_cache_needs_the_fastest_possible_ac","v":{"s":"L1 cache needs the fastest possible access time."}},{"k":"gain_is_negative_a_g_r","v":{"s":"Gain is negative: Aᵥ = -gₘRₓ."}},{"k":"it_s_a_buffer_unity_gain_impedance_tra","v":{"s":"It's a buffer: unity gain, impedance transformation."}},{"k":"higher_gain_lower_bandwidth_a_bw_gbw_c","v":{"s":"Higher gain = lower bandwidth. Aᵥ × BW = GBW = constant."}},{"k":"semiconductor_challenge","v":{"s":"Semiconductor Challenge"}},{"k":"progress_to_next_rank","v":{"s":"Progress to next rank"}},{"k":"a_swarm_of_logic_bugs_what_gate_output","v":{"s":"A swarm of logic bugs! What gate outputs 1 when A=0?"}},{"k":"a_voltage_spike_is_overloading_which_d","v":{"s":"A voltage spike is overloading! Which device regulates voltage?"}},{"k":"zener_diode","v":{"s":"Zener diode"}},{"k":"temperature_rising_in_a_semiconductor_","v":{"s":"Temperature rising! In a semiconductor, increasing temp does what to conductivity?"}},{"k":"increases_it","v":{"s":"Increases it"}},{"k":"an_enemy_flipped_all_bits_which_gate_c","v":{"s":"An enemy flipped all bits! Which gate can invert every signal?"}},{"k":"carriers_are_leaking_what_narrows_the_","v":{"s":"Carriers are leaking! What narrows the depletion region?"}},{"k":"forward_bias","v":{"s":"Forward bias"}},{"k":"electrostatic_discharge_what_protects_","v":{"s":"Electrostatic discharge! What protects ICs from ESD?"}},{"k":"diode_clamps","v":{"s":"Diode clamps"}},{"k":"clock_is_unstable_cmos_power_dissipati","v":{"s":"Clock is unstable! CMOS power dissipation is proportional to:"}},{"k":"frequency","v":{"s":"Frequency"}},{"k":"direct_short_what_is_the_threshold_vol","v":{"s":"Direct short! What is the threshold voltage of a typical Si MOSFET?"}},{"k":"electrons_are_tunneling_through_the_ox","v":{"s":"Electrons are tunneling through the oxide! In a quantum well, narrower well ="}},{"k":"wider_energy_spacing","v":{"s":"Wider energy spacing"}},{"k":"memory_bits_are_flipping_which_memory_","v":{"s":"Memory bits are flipping! Which memory type needs refreshing?"}},{"k":"signal_to_noise_ratio_dropping_what_do","v":{"s":"Signal-to-noise ratio dropping! What does a differential amplifier reject?"}},{"k":"common_mode_noise","v":{"s":"Common-mode noise"}},{"k":"final_boss_what_limits_transistor_scal",