tment: "}},{"k":"this_information_is_educational_only_i","v":{"s":"👨‍⚕️ This information is educational only. It is not medical advice. If you have concerns about your voice, see an otolaryngologist (ENT doctor) or speech-language pathologist."}},{"k":"vocal_warm_ups","v":{"s":"Vocal Warm-ups"}},{"k":"complete","v":{"s":"✅ Complete"}},{"k":"replay_tones","v":{"s":"🔁 Replay Tones"}},{"k":"cancel_warm_up_exercise","v":{"s":"Cancel warm-up exercise"}},{"k":"cancel_4","v":{"s":"Cancel"}},{"k":"vocal_health_tips","v":{"s":"Vocal Health Tips"}},{"k":"get_personalized_vocal_health_tips_app","v":{"s":"Get personalized vocal health tips appropriate for your grade level."}},{"k":"get_tips","v":{"s":"💡 Get Tips"}},{"k":"loading_tips","v":{"s":"Loading tips..."}},{"k":"refresh_tips","v":{"s":"🔁 Refresh Tips"}},{"k":"breathing_for_singing","v":{"s":"Breathing for Singing"}},{"k":"1_inhale","v":{"s":"1. Inhale"}},{"k":"breathe_deep_into_your_belly_diaphragm","v":{"s":"Breathe deep into your belly (diaphragm), not your chest."}},{"k":"2_support","v":{"s":"2. Support"}},{"k":"keep_your_core_engaged_to_control_airf","v":{"s":"Keep your core engaged to control airflow while singing."}},{"k":"3_release","v":{"s":"3. Release"}},{"k":"let_the_air_flow_smoothly_and_evenly_t","v":{"s":"Let the air flow smoothly and evenly through your vocal folds."}},{"k":"singing_posture","v":{"s":"Singing Posture"}},{"k":"feet_shoulder_width_apart_weight_balan","v":{"s":"Feet shoulder-width apart, weight balanced evenly"}},{"k":"shoulders_relaxed_and_rolled_back_not_","v":{"s":"Shoulders relaxed and rolled back (not hunched)"}},{"k":"chin_level_not_tilted_up_or_down","v":{"s":"Chin level — not tilted up or down"}},{"k":"jaw_relaxed_and_slightly_dropped_when_","v":{"s":"Jaw relaxed and slightly dropped when singing"}},{"k":"avoid_locking_knees_tensing_neck_or_cl","v":{"s":"Avoid: locking knees, tensing neck, or clenching jaw"}},{"k":"sight_reading_trainer","v":{"s":"Sight Reading Trainer"}},{"k":"read_the_notes_on_the_staff_and_sing_t","v":{"s":"Read the notes on the staff and sing them in order. Real-time pitch detection checks your accuracy."}},{"k":"random","v":{"s":"Random"}},{"k":"melodies","v":{"s":"Melodies"}},{"k":"ai_generate","v":{"s":"AI Generate"}},{"k":"choose_a_melody","v":{"s":"Choose a melody:"}},{"k":"staff","v":{"s":"Staff"}},{"k":"singing_visualization_7","v":{"s":"Singing visualization"}},{"k":"note","v":{"s":"Note "}},{"k":"preview","v":{"s":" Preview"}},{"k":"stop_preview","v":{"s":" Stop Preview"}},{"k":"stop","v":{"s":" Stop"}},{"k":"singing_slider","v":{"s":"Singing slider"}},{"k":"preview_tempo","v":{"s":"Preview tempo"}},{"k":"hear_target_note","v":{"s":"💡 Hear Target Note"}},{"k":"exercise_complete","v":{"s":"Exercise Complete!"}},{"k":"correct_1st_try","v":{"s":"Correct 1st Try"}},{"k":"avg_deviation","v":{"s":"Avg. Deviation"}},{"k":"time_2","v":{"s":"Time"}},{"k":"stars","v":{"s":"Stars"}},{"k":"note_by_note_results","v":{"s":"Note-by-Note Results"}},{"k":"best_scores","v":{"s":"Best Scores"}},{"k":"discover_your_vocal_range","v":{"s":"Discover your vocal range"}},{"k":"sing_5_intervals_correctly","v":{"s":"Sing 5 intervals correctly"}},{"k":"achieve_healthy_vibrato","v":{"s":"Achieve healthy vibrato"}},{"k":"quests","v":{"s":"Quests"}},{"k":"singing_and_vocal_lab","v":{"s":"Singing and Vocal Lab"}},{"k":"go_back_to_stem_lab_tool_list","v":{"s":"Go back to STEAM Lab tool list"}},{"k":"back","v":{"s":"Back"}},{"k":"singing_lab","v":{"s":"Singing Lab"}},{"k":"pitch_training_vocal_range_vibrato_int","v":{"s":"Pitch training, vocal range, vibrato & interval singing"}},{"k":"listening_2","v":{"s":"Listening"}},{"k":"singing_lab_sections","v":{"s":"Singing Lab sections"}},{"k":"pitch_detective_2","v":{"s":"Pitch Detective"}},{"k":"sing_into_the_mic_the_lab_tracks_frequ","v":{"s":"Sing into the mic; the lab tracks frequency in real time. Trained singers hold pitch within ±5 cents (1/20th of a semitone) — that is what perfect-pitch matching looks like."}},{"k":"vocal_range_your_tessitura","v":{"s":"Vocal Range — your tessitura"}},{"k":"most_untrained_voices_span_1_5_2_octav","v":{"s":"Most untrained voices span 1.5–2 octaves; trained classical singers reach 3+. Range expansion is mostly about REGISTER blending, not just stretching higher and lower."}},{"k":"vibrato_lab_2","v":{"s":"Vibrato Lab"}},{"k":"healthy_vibrato_5_7_hz_oscillation_60_","v":{"s":"Healthy vibrato: 5–7 Hz oscillation, ~60–100 cents wide. Slower = wobble; faster = tremor. Vibrato is a function of relaxed breath support, not a separate technique."}},{"k":"interval_singer_ear_training","v":{"s":"Interval Singer — ear training"}},{"k":"major_3rd_vs_minor_3rd_is_the_single_m","v":{"s":"Major 3rd vs minor 3rd is the single most-confused interval pair for beginners. Mnemonics: M3 = \"Oh when the saints,\" m3 = \"Greensleeves.\" Builds relative pitch."}},{"k":"lip_trills_sirens_before_any_sustained","v":{"s":"Lip trills + sirens before any sustained singing. 5–10 minutes of low-intensity warm-up halves the risk of vocal-fold strain. Skipping warm-ups is the #1 cause of preventable vocal injury."}},{"k":"sight_reading_2","v":{"s":"Sight reading"}},{"k":"solf_ge_do_re_mi_letter_names_for_sigh","v":{"s":"Solfège (do-re-mi) > letter names for sight-singing because the syllables encode interval relationships, not just pitch labels. Movable do beats fixed do for tonal music."}},{"k":"resonance_lab_discover_your_vocal_tone","v":{"s":"Resonance Lab — discover your vocal tone"}},{"k":"two_sliders_throat_openness_and_soft_p","v":{"s":"Two sliders — throat openness and soft palate lift — combine into four tone qualities (rich, bright, warm, nasal). No score, no reveal: experiment, log, and explain what you find."}},{"k":"rich_open_lifted","v":{"s":"🎶 Rich (open + lifted)"}},{"k":"operatic_professional_tone_full_resona","v":{"s":"Operatic / professional tone. Full resonance."}},{"k":"bright_open_lowered","v":{"s":"✨ Bright (open + lowered)"}},{"k":"forward_placement_pop_belt_style","v":{"s":"Forward placement. Pop / belt style."}},{"k":"warm_narrow_lifted","v":{"s":"🌅 Warm (narrow + lifted)"}},{"k":"mellow_tone_choral_acoustic","v":{"s":"Mellow tone. Choral / acoustic."}},{"k":"nasal_narrow_lowered","v":{"s":"🐝 Nasal (narrow + lowered)"}},{"k":"tight_resonance_often_unintended","v":{"s":"Tight resonance. Often unintended."}},{"k":"resonance_discovery","v":{"s":"🎙️ Resonance discovery"}},{"k":"sliders_for_throat_openness_soft_palat","v":{"s":"Sliders for throat openness, soft palate lift. Discrete 4-tone classification. No score, no reveal."}},{"k":"log","v":{"s":"📋 Log"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"hypothesis_what_anatomical_adjustments","v":{"s":"Hypothesis: What anatomical adjustments produce rich tone?"}},{"k":"stuck_show_open_prompts","v":{"s":"🤔 Stuck — show open prompts"}},{"k":"why_do_classical_singers_lift_the_pala","v":{"s":"Why do classical singers lift the palate?"}},{"k":"how_does_throat_openness_affect_overto","v":{"s":"How does throat openness affect overtone series?"}},{"k":"i_understand_explain_in_own_words","v":{"s":"I understand — explain in own words"}},{"k":"explain_how_resonance_cavity_shape_con","v":{"s":"Explain how resonance cavity shape controls vocal tone."}},{"k":"design_note_discrete_4_tone_marker_no_","v":{"s":"Design note: discrete 4-tone marker; no acoustic score; no reveal — by design."}},{"k":"lip_trills_desc","v":{"s":"Blow air through loosely closed lips while descending in pitch. This relaxes your vocal folds and warms up your airflow."}},{"k":"five_note_scale_desc","v":{"s":"Sing Do-Re-Mi-Fa-Sol ascending, then descending. Match the reference tones. This builds pitch accuracy."}},{"k":"octave_slides_desc","v":{"s":"Glide smoothly from C4 up to C5 and back down. Use an \"ooh\" or \"ahh\" vowel. This stretches your range gently."}},{"k":"staccato_ha_desc","v":{"s":"Sing short, detached \"Ha!\" on each note of an ascending scale. This strengthens your diaphragm support."}},{"k":"messa_di_voce_desc","v":{"s":"Start singing a note very quietly, gradually get louder, then gradually get quieter again. This builds dynamic control."}},{"k":"hypothesis_input","v":{"s":"Resonance discovery hypothesis"}},{"k":"explanation_input","v":{"s":"Resonance discovery explanation"}},{"k":"ai_exercise_generated","v":{"s":"AI exercise generated!"}},{"k":"ai_unavailable_using_random_exercise","v":{"s":"AI unavailable. Using random exercise."}},{"k":"canvas_anatomy_title","v":{"s":"Sagittal Cross-Section of the Vocal Tract"}},{"k":"canvas_flat","v":{"s":"Flat"}},{"k":"canvas_reference","v":{"s":"Reference"}},{"k":"canvas_sharp","v":{"s":"Sharp"}},{"k":"canvas_target","v":{"s":"Target"}},{"k":"canvas_vibrato_empty","v":{"s":"Sustain a note to see vibrato waveform"}},{"k":"canvas_you","v":{"s":"You"}},{"k":"could_not_parse_ai_response_using_rand","v":{"s":"Could not parse AI response. Using random exercise."}},{"k":"getting_there_aim_for_width","v":{"s":"Getting there! Aim for a 5-7 Hz rate and a 42-113 cent width."}},{"k":"healthy_vibrato_achieved","v":{"s":"Healthy vibrato achieved!"}},{"k":"ideal_width_range","v":{"s":"Ideal: 42-113¢ peak to peak"}},{"k":"mic_busy","v":{"s":"The microphone is in use by another app. Close it and try again."}},{"k":"mic_denied","v":{"s":"Microphone permission was blocked. Allow microphone access for this page, then try again."}},{"k":"mic_failed","v":{"s":"Could not access the microphone. Please allow microphone permissions and try again."}},{"k":"mic_missing","v":{"s":"No microphone was found. Plug one in or pick one in your system sound settings, then try again."}},{"k":"mic_unavailable","v":{"s":"Microphone capture is not available here. Open the web version over https to use the pitch tools."}},{"k":"quest_complete_5_intervals","v":{"s":"Quest complete: 5 intervals!"}},{"k":"roll_empty","v":{"s":"Start singing to see your pitch"}},{"k":"sight_reading_started_sing_each_note_s","v":{"s":"Sight reading started. Sing each note shown on the staff."}},{"k":"sr_mic_active","v":{"s":"Microphone active. Sing or hum to see your pitch visualized."}},{"k":"start_your_microphone_first","v":{"s":"Start your microphone first!"}},{"k":"start_your_microphone_first_2","v":{"s":"Start your microphone first!"}},{"k":"start_your_microphone_first_3","v":{"s":"Start your microphone first!"}},{"k":"start_your_microphone_first_4","v":{"s":"Start your microphone first!"}},{"k":"step_1_sing_your_lowest_comfortable_no","v":{"s":"Step 1: Sing your lowest comfortable note and hold it."}},{"k":"try_to_keep_vibrato_width","v":{"s":"Try to keep the vibrato width around 75 cents peak to peak. Not too wide, not too narrow."}},{"k":"vibrato_low_sample_rate","v":{"s":"This device is producing too few pitch readings per second to measure vibrato rate. Close other tabs or apps and try again."}},{"k":"vibrato_measuring","v":{"s":"Measuring…"}},{"k":"vibrato_width_too_wide","v":{"s":"Vibrato width exceeds 140 cents peak to peak. Try for a narrower oscillation."}},{"k":"warm_up_complete","v":{"s":"Warm-up complete!"}},{"k":"warm_ups","v":{"s":"Warm-ups"}},{"k":"width","v":{"s":"Width"}}],"id":575}},{"k":"skatelab","v":{"o":[{"k":"a11y_simulation_view","v":{"s":"Simulation view"}},{"k":"a11y_simulation_stage","v":{"s":"Simulation stage"}},{"k":"a11y_jump_to_a_motion_phase","v":{"s":"Jump to a motion phase"}},{"k":"a11y_physics_controls","v":{"s":"Physics controls"}},{"k":"a11y_experiment_type","v":{"s":"Experiment type"}},{"k":"a11y_live_model_outputs","v":{"s":"Live model outputs"}},{"k":"coach_is_offline_try_again_in_a_moment","v":{"s":"(Coach is offline. Try again in a moment.)"}},{"k":"maxed_out_on_pumps_but_still_bailing_t","v":{"s":"Maxed out on pumps but still bailing. Try a smaller trick to learn how much air this setup actually gives you."}},{"k":"at_max_speed_and_still_short_range_pea","v":{"s":"At max speed and still short. Range peaks at 45° on flat ground but ~30° works best when you need to land at the same height. Try 30°."}},{"k":"even_at_max_speed_and_ideal_angle_this","v":{"s":"Even at max speed and ideal angle, this gap is out of reach. Smaller gap to feel the calibration first."}},{"k":"flying_past_the_landing_too_much_speed","v":{"s":"Flying past the landing — too much speed. Trim it down and watch where the parabola peaks."}},{"k":"mastered","v":{"s":"Mastered"}},{"k":"solid","v":{"s":"Solid"}},{"k":"landed","v":{"s":"Landed"}},{"k":"tried","v":{"s":"Tried"}},{"k":"locked","v":{"s":"Locked"}},{"k":"going_off","v":{"s":"Going Off!!"}},{"k":"on_fire","v":{"s":"On Fire!"}},{"k":"hot_streak","v":{"s":"Hot Streak!"}},{"k":"ready","v":{"s":"Ready"}},{"k":"ready_2","v":{"s":"Ready"}},{"k":"close_scenario_intro","v":{"s":"Close scenario intro"}},{"k":"the_story","v":{"s":"📜 The story"}},{"k":"try_these_before_you_run_it","v":{"s":"🤔 Try these before you run it"}},{"k":"close_and_explore_controls_manually","v":{"s":"Close and explore controls manually"}},{"k":"explore_first","v":{"s":"🔧 Explore first"}},{"k":"run_this_scenario_now","v":{"s":"Run this scenario now"}},{"k":"run_it_now","v":{"s":"🛹 Run it now"}},{"k":"back_to_stem_lab","v":{"s":"Back to STEAM Lab"}},{"k":"skate_bmx_physics_same_math_that_lands","v":{"s":"Skate / BMX physics — same math that lands a 720."}},{"k":"today_s_daily_challenge","v":{"s":"Today's daily challenge"}},{"k":"try_it","v":{"s":"🛹 Try it"}},{"k":"famous_tricks","v":{"s":"🎬 Famous tricks"}},{"k":"save_current_settings_as_a_custom_scen","v":{"s":"Save current settings as a custom scenario"}},{"k":"capture_the_current_setup_as_a_reusabl","v":{"s":"Capture the current setup as a reusable preset"}},{"k":"save_current","v":{"s":"💾 Save current"}},{"k":"custom_scenarios","v":{"s":"Custom scenarios"}},{"k":"delete_this_custom_scenario","v":{"s":"Delete this custom scenario"}},{"k":"halfpipe_surface","v":{"s":"Halfpipe surface"}},{"k":"vehicle","v":{"s":"Vehicle"}},{"k":"skatelab_mode","v":{"s":"SkateLab mode"}},{"k":"halfpipe_energy_conservation_in_a_curv","v":{"s":"Halfpipe — energy conservation in a curved track"}},{"k":"drop_in_gravitational_pe_ke_at_the_bot","v":{"s":"Drop in: gravitational PE → KE at the bottom. Rise on the other side: KE → PE again. Friction + air drag bleed energy each cycle, so air height decreases unless the rider pumps. Pumping = doing work against gravity at the right phase."}},{"k":"gap_jump_projectile_motion_landing_phy","v":{"s":"Gap jump — projectile motion + landing physics"}},{"k":"once_airborne_x_and_y_are_independent_","v":{"s":"Once airborne, x and y are independent: x = v·cosθ·t, y = v·sinθ·t − ½gt². Landing speed depends on the height differential, not the horizontal distance. Steeper landing slope = lower impact force = safer."}},{"k":"print_this_scenario_as_a_student_activ","v":{"s":"Print this scenario as a student activity sheet"}},{"k":"print_classroom_friendly_activity_shee","v":{"s":"Print classroom-friendly activity sheet with the questions"}},{"k":"print","v":{"s":"🖨️ Print"}},{"k":"dismiss_lesson_card","v":{"s":"Dismiss lesson card"}},{"k":"dismiss","v":{"s":"✕ Dismiss"}},{"k":"questions","v":{"s":"📝 Questions"}},{"k":"welcome_to_skatelab","v":{"s":"Welcome to SkateLab"}},{"k":"this_is_a_physics_simulator_where_the_","v":{"s":"This is a physics simulator where the math is the same as real skating. Press 🛹 Drop In! to attempt a kickflip on Earth."}},{"k":"pumps_add_kinetic_energy","v":{"s":"Pumps add kinetic energy"}},{"k":"more_pumps_more_ke_more_air_more_rotat","v":{"s":"More pumps = more KE → more air → more rotation budget. Try 5 pumps and a 360 spin. Watch the Energy bar transform KE into PE as you climb."}},{"k":"famous_tricks_today_s_challenge","v":{"s":"Famous tricks + Today's Challenge"}},{"k":"the_scenarios_row_at_the_top_loads_rea","v":{"s":"The scenarios row at the top loads real moments from skate history — Tony Hawk's 900, Danny Way's Great Wall, Moonshot Kickflip. Today's Challenge is the same for every student in your class."}},{"k":"predict_before_you_run","v":{"s":"Predict before you run"}},{"k":"toggle_predict_mode_type_how_high_you_","v":{"s":"Toggle 🔮 Predict mode — type how high you think you'll go BEFORE pressing Drop In. Track how close you got. Your physics intuition will sharpen across attempts."}},{"k":"stay_safe_out_there","v":{"s":"Stay safe out there"}},{"k":"mastery_tree_trick_lab_gear_science_an","v":{"s":"Mastery Tree, Trick Lab, Gear Science, and the Park Session live in the panels below. Play, predict, invent — and wear a helmet in real life."}},{"k":"skip_tour","v":{"s":"Skip tour"}},{"k":"skip","v":{"s":"Skip"}},{"k":"back","v":{"s":"← Back"}},{"k":"start_a_park_session","v":{"s":"🎯 Start a park session"}},{"k":"run_a_fixed_number_of_attempts_and_get","v":{"s":"Run a fixed number of attempts and get aggregate stats at the end. See if your prediction accuracy improves across the session."}},{"k":"cancel","v":{"s":"Cancel"}},{"k":"session_complete","v":{"s":"🎯 Session complete"}},{"k":"lands","v":{"s":"Lands"}},{"k":"total_xp","v":{"s":"Total XP"}},{"k":"best_streak","v":{"s":"Best streak"}},{"k":"avg_prediction_error","v":{"s":"Avg prediction error"}},{"k":"first_attempt_to","v":{"s":" (first attempt) to "}},{"k":"attempts","v":{"s":"Attempts"}},{"k":"done","v":{"s":"✓ Done"}},{"k":"save_current_setup_as_a_scenario","v":{"s":"💾 Save current setup as a scenario"}},{"k":"custom_scenario_name_max_40_characters","v":{"s":"Custom scenario name (max 40 characters)"}},{"k":"e_g_ramp_out_back_or_wind_tunnel_test","v":{"s":"e.g., \"Ramp out back\" or \"Wind tunnel test\""}},{"k":"cancel_2","v":{"s":"Cancel"}},{"k":"save","v":{"s":"💾 Save"}},{"k":"reset_skatelab_stats","v":{"s":"🗑 Reset SkateLab stats?"}},{"k":"this_clears_your_landings_bails_person","v":{"s":"This clears your landings, bails, personal bests, and quest progress for SkateLab only. Your custom scenarios are kept. This cannot be undone."}},{"k":"cancel_3","v":{"s":"Cancel"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"🗑 Reset"}},{"k":"real_world_safety_reminder","v":{"s":"Real-world safety reminder"}},{"k":"open_the_skatelab_tour","v":{"s":"Open the SkateLab tour"}},{"k":"re_open_the_5_step_tour","v":{"s":"Re-open the 5-step tour"}},{"k":"tour","v":{"s":"💡 Tour"}},{"k":"mute_unmute_m_key","v":{"s":"Mute / unmute (M key)"}},{"k":"toggle_the_live_equation_that_updates_","v":{"s":"Toggle the live equation that updates as you change settings"}},{"k":"toggle_the_live_ke_pe_energy_bar_that_","v":{"s":"Toggle the live KE / PE energy bar that updates during the animation"}},{"k":"end_session_early","v":{"s":"End session early"}},{"k":"start_a_park_session_string_several_at","v":{"s":"Start a park session — string several attempts together"}},{"k":"run_a_park_session_aggregate_stats_acr","v":{"s":"Run a park session — aggregate stats across N attempts"}},{"k":"session","v":{"s":"🎯 Session"}},{"k":"real_world_safety_reminder_2","v":{"s":"Real-world safety reminder"}},{"k":"this_is_a_simulation_real_skating_isn_","v":{"s":"⚠️ This is a simulation. Real skating isn't."}},{"k":"skateboarding_is_the_leading_cause_of_","v":{"s":"Skateboarding is the leading cause of pediatric extremity fractures (CDC). The math here is the same in real life — the consequences aren't. Wear a "}},{"k":"helmet_wrist_guards_and_pads","v":{"s":"helmet, wrist guards, and pads"}},{"k":"skate_within_your_ability_and_learn_fa","v":{"s":", skate within your ability, and learn falls before tricks. Tap the ✓ chip when you've read this."}},{"k":"acknowledge_safety_message","v":{"s":"Acknowledge safety message"}},{"k":"got_it_wear_gear_in_real_life","v":{"s":"✓ Got it — wear gear in real life"}},{"k":"live_physics_equations","v":{"s":"Live physics equations"}},{"k":"each_pump_adds_kinetic_energy_ke_pe_at","v":{"s":"Each pump adds kinetic energy. KE → PE at the lip. More pumps = more air."}},{"k":"trick","v":{"s":"🛹 Trick"}},{"k":"air_time_each_trick_needs","v":{"s":"Air time each trick needs"}},{"k":"your_invented_tricks","v":{"s":"Your invented tricks"}},{"k":"delete_this_custom_trick","v":{"s":"Delete this custom trick"}},{"k":"trick_lore_origin_physics_pro_tip","v":{"s":"📖 Trick Lore — origin, physics, pro tip"}},{"k":"origin","v":{"s":"🛹 Origin: "}},{"k":"physics","v":{"s":"📐 Physics: "}},{"k":"pro_tip","v":{"s":"💡 Pro tip: "}},{"k":"trick_lab_invent_your_own_move","v":{"s":"🧪 Trick Lab — invent your own move"}},{"k":"real_world_safety","v":{"s":"⚠️ Real-world safety: "}},{"k":"inventing_tricks_here_is_creativity_in","v":{"s":"Inventing tricks here is creativity. Inventing them on a real ramp without gear is hospital math. The simulator has zero risk; the real world doesn't. Always wear a helmet, wrist guards, and pads."}},{"k":"name","v":{"s":"Name"}},{"k":"e_g_tail_dragger","v":{"s":"e.g. Tail Dragger"}},{"k":"emoji","v":{"s":"Emoji"}},{"k":"trick_emoji","v":{"s":"Trick emoji"}},{"k":"axis","v":{"s":"Axis"}},{"k":"rotation_axis","v":{"s":"Rotation axis"}},{"k":"board","v":{"s":"Board"}},{"k":"fastest_spin_1500_s_flips","v":{"s":"fastest spin (1500°/s) — flips"}},{"k":"body","v":{"s":"Body"}},{"k":"medium_spin_1000_s_full_body_rotations","v":{"s":"medium spin (1000°/s) — full-body rotations"}},{"k":"combo","v":{"s":"Combo"}},{"k":"slowest_800_s_both_axes_at_once","v":{"s":"slowest (800°/s) — both axes at once"}},{"k":"trick_physics_preview","v":{"s":"Trick physics preview"}},{"k":"min_air","v":{"s":"📐 Min air: "}},{"k":"formula","v":{"s":"💡 Formula: "}},{"k":"closest_built_in","v":{"s":"🛹 Closest built-in: "}},{"k":"save_select","v":{"s":"💾 Save & Select"}},{"k":"reset_form","v":{"s":"🔄 Reset Form"}},{"k":"new_gap","v":{"s":"🎲 New Gap"}},{"k":"wind_condition","v":{"s":"Wind condition"}},{"k":"predict_then_verify_builds_the_physics","v":{"s":"Predict, then verify. Builds the physics intuition."}},{"k":"prediction_input","v":{"s":"Prediction input"}},{"k":"avg_off","v":{"s":"⌀ avg off: "}},{"k":"best","v":{"s":"🏆 best: "}},{"k":"within_10","v":{"s":"🎯 within 10%: "}},{"k":"0_5","v":{"s":"🎬 0.5×"}},{"k":"0_25","v":{"s":"🐌 0.25×"}},{"k":"takeoff_speed","v":{"s":"⚡ Takeoff speed: "}},{"k":"air_height_above_lip","v":{"s":"📈 Air height (above lip): "}},{"k":"hang_time","v":{"s":"⏱ Hang time: "}},{"k":"rotation","v":{"s":"🌀 Rotation: "}},{"k":"predicted","v":{"s":"🔮 Predicted "}},{"k":"actual","v":{"s":" · Actual "}},{"k":"off","v":{"s":" · Off "}},{"k":"vs_best_prev","v":{"s":"👻 vs best: prev "}},{"k":"str","v":{"s":" · Δ "}},{"k":"takeoff","v":{"s":"🚀 Takeoff: "}},{"k":"range_v_sin_2_g","v":{"s":"📐 Range = v² × sin(2θ) / g = "}},{"k":"wind","v":{"s":"🌬️ Wind: "}},{"k":"peak_height","v":{"s":"⛰ Peak height: "}},{"k":"hang_time_2","v":{"s":"⏱ Hang time: "}},{"k":"clearance","v":{"s":"🎯 Clearance: "}},{"k":"predicted_2","v":{"s":"🔮 Predicted "}},{"k":"actual_2","v":{"s":" · Actual "}},{"k":"off_2","v":{"s":" · Off "}},{"k":"vs_best_prev_2","v":{"s":"👻 vs best: prev "}},{"k":"str_2","v":{"s":" · Δ "}},{"k":"coaching_suggestion","v":{"s":"Coaching suggestion"}},{"k":"dismiss_this_suggestion","v":{"s":"Dismiss this suggestion"}},{"k":"skip_2","v":{"s":"✕ Skip"}},{"k":"ai_coach","v":{"s":"🎙️ AI Coach"}},{"k":"coach_voice","v":{"s":"Coach voice"}},{"k":"gear_science_the_physics_of_not_gettin","v":{"s":"🛡️ Gear Science — the physics of not getting hurt"}},{"k":"most_skate_injuries_are_preventable","v":{"s":"Most skate injuries are preventable. "}},{"k":"each_piece_of_gear_works_because_of_ph","v":{"s":"Each piece of gear works because of physics you already know — force-over-time, stress-over-area, friction-over-distance. Here's why each one matters."}},{"k":"what_it_does","v":{"s":"🛡️ What it does: "}},{"k":"the_physics","v":{"s":"📐 The physics: "}},{"k":"why_wear_it","v":{"s":"💡 Why wear it: "}},{"k":"open_the_printable_gear_checklist","v":{"s":"Open the printable gear checklist"}},{"k":"print_gear_checklist","v":{"s":"📋 Print Gear Checklist"}},{"k":"skater_customizer_color_gear","v":{"s":"🎨 Skater Customizer — color + gear"}},{"k":"body_color","v":{"s":"Body color"}},{"k":"skater_body_color","v":{"s":"Skater body color"}},{"k":"suited_up","v":{"s":"✓ Suited up."}},{"k":"your_skater_s_ready_now_do_the_same_in","v":{"s":" Your skater's ready. Now do the same in real life."}},{"k":"lands_2","v":{"s":"Lands"}},{"k":"bails","v":{"s":"Bails"}},{"k":"best_spin","v":{"s":"Best Spin"}},{"k":"longest_gap","v":{"s":"Longest Gap"}},{"k":"personal_bests","v":{"s":"Personal bests"}},{"k":"best_halfpipe","v":{"s":"🏆 Best Halfpipe"}},{"k":"best_gap","v":{"s":"🏆 Best Gap"}},{"k":"best_air","v":{"s":"🏆 Best Air"}},{"k":"longest_streak","v":{"s":"🔥 Longest Streak"}},{"k":"reset_skatelab_stats_custom_scenarios_","v":{"s":"Reset SkateLab stats. Custom scenarios are kept."}},{"k":"clear_landings_bails_personal_bests_an","v":{"s":"Clear landings, bails, personal bests, and quest progress for SkateLab"}},{"k":"reset_stats","v":{"s":"🗑 Reset stats"}},{"k":"the_physics_behind_this","v":{"s":"📚 The physics behind this"}},{"k":"pumping_doing_work","v":{"s":"Pumping = doing work. "}},{"k":"each_time_you_push_down_at_the_bottom_","v":{"s":"Each time you push down at the bottom of the halfpipe, your legs add kinetic energy. KE = ½mv². More pumps → more KE → more speed at the lip."}},{"k":"lip_air_ke_pe","v":{"s":"Lip → air = KE → PE. "}},{"k":"above_the_lip_the_skater_s_kinetic_ene","v":{"s":"Above the lip, the skater's kinetic energy converts to gravitational potential energy. Solving ½mv² = mgh gives air height: h = v² / (2g). Doubling your speed quadruples your air."}},{"k":"spin_needs_hang_time","v":{"s":"Spin needs hang time. "}},{"k":"your_rotation_rate_deg_s_is_roughly_fi","v":{"s":"Your rotation rate (deg/s) is roughly fixed for a given trick. To complete a 720, you need air_time × rate ≥ 720°. That's why bigger spins demand more pumps."}},{"k":"range_formula","v":{"s":"Range formula: "}},{"k":"for_a_takeoff_at_speed_v_and_angle_pro","v":{"s":"For a takeoff at speed v and angle θ, projectile range = v² × sin(2θ) / g. Maximum range at θ = 45°. Steeper angle gives more height; shallower gives more distance per unit speed."}},{"k":"speed_scales_squared","v":{"s":"Speed scales squared. "}},{"k":"doubling_your_takeoff_speed_quadruples","v":{"s":"Doubling your takeoff speed quadruples your range — same as pumping in the halfpipe. That's why pros sprint hard at gaps."}},{"k":"peak_height_2","v":{"s":"Peak height: "}},{"k":"h_peak_v_sin_2g_at_30_and_15_mph_you_p","v":{"s":"h_peak = (v · sinθ)² / (2g). At 30° and 15 mph you peak ~3 ft above takeoff; at 45° you peak ~6 ft. More vertical means more time to spot the landing."}},{"k":"bmx_bigger_moment_of_inertia","v":{"s":"🚲 BMX = bigger moment of inertia. "}},{"k":"a_bmx_bike_weighs_12_kg_vs_a_skateboar","v":{"s":"A BMX bike weighs ~12 kg vs a skateboard's ~4 kg, and the wheels are much bigger. Moment of inertia I = m·r² determines how much torque you need to spin. Same arm strength → less rotation per second. That's why BMX flips and spins look more deliberate than skate spins — the rider is fighting more rotational mass for the same air time."}},{"k":"hang_time_0_3_s_manual_shove_it_territ","v":{"s":"Hang time < 0.3 s — manual / shove-it territory. No rotation room."}},{"k":"180_class_air","v":{"s":"180-class air"}},{"k":"hang_0_3_0_7_s_half_rotations_and_olli","v":{"s":"Hang ≈ 0.3–0.7 s. Half-rotations and ollies possible."}},{"k":"360_class_air","v":{"s":"360-class air"}},{"k":"hang_0_7_1_1_s_full_rotation_possible_","v":{"s":"Hang ≈ 0.7–1.1 s. Full rotation possible with average spin rate."}},{"k":"big_air_540","v":{"s":"Big-air 540"}},{"k":"hang_1_1_1_5_s_park_vert_range_540_and","v":{"s":"Hang ≈ 1.1–1.5 s. Park/vert range. 540 and 720 possible if spin rate is high."}},{"k":"pro_720","v":{"s":"Pro 720+"}},{"k":"hang_1_5_s_mega_ramp_olympic_level_900","v":{"s":"Hang > 1.5 s. Mega-ramp / Olympic-level. 900 and 1080 territory."}},{"k":"air_spin_inquiry","v":{"s":"🔬 Air / Spin Inquiry"}},{"k":"set_takeoff_speed_angle_mass_and_your_","v":{"s":"Set takeoff speed, angle, mass, and your rotation rate. Predict the biggest rotation you can land cleanly. No score, no reveal."}},{"k":"hang_time_3","v":{"s":"Hang time"}},{"k":"apex_height","v":{"s":"Apex height"}},{"k":"range","v":{"s":"Range"}},{"k":"takeoff_ke","v":{"s":"Takeoff KE"}},{"k":"takeoff_speed_2","v":{"s":"Takeoff speed"}},{"k":"takeoff_angle","v":{"s":"Takeoff angle"}},{"k":"rider_board_mass","v":{"s":"Rider + board mass"}},{"k":"rotation_rate","v":{"s":"Rotation rate"}},{"k":"log_this_physics_setup","v":{"s":"📋 Log this physics setup"}},{"k":"reset_2","v":{"s":"Reset"}},{"k":"your_hypothesis_which_slider_buys_hang","v":{"s":"Your hypothesis (which slider buys hang time fastest — angle, speed, or mass?)"}},{"k":"e_g_angle_gives_diminishing_returns_pa","v":{"s":"e.g., angle gives diminishing returns past 60° because horizontal speed vanishes..."}},{"k":"i_m_stuck_show_open_questions","v":{"s":"🤔 I'm stuck — show open questions"}},{"k":"open_questions_no_answer_key","v":{"s":"Open questions (no answer key)"}},{"k":"does_mass_appear_anywhere_in_the_air_f","v":{"s":"Does mass appear anywhere in the air formulas? Why or why not?"}},{"k":"at_what_angle_is_range_maximized_vs_ha","v":{"s":"At what angle is RANGE maximized vs HANG TIME maximized? Are they the same?"}},{"k":"why_does_the_bmx_rider_need_more_hang_","v":{"s":"Why does the BMX rider need MORE hang time for the same rotation count?"}},{"k":"how_would_you_choose_your_sliders_to_l","v":{"s":"How would you choose your sliders to land a 540 with the least KE?"}},{"k":"i_can_explain_why_this_v_m_combination","v":{"s":"I can explain why this v/θ/m combination lands at this max-rotation state."}},{"k":"explain_in_your_own_words","v":{"s":"Explain in your own words..."}},{"k":"inquiry_widget_no_score_no_reveal_no_a","v":{"s":"Inquiry widget — no score, no reveal, no answer dump. Treats takeoff as point projectile; real airs add drag, board-spin coupling, and rotation-rate-changes mid-air (tucking ↑ rate)."}},{"k":"sending_it","v":{"s":"Sending it..."}},{"k":"type_a_prediction_first","v":{"s":"Type a prediction first"}},{"k":"drop_in","v":{"s":"Drop In!"}},{"k":"send_it","v":{"s":"Send It!"}},{"k":"ready_try_chain","v":{"s":"Ready. Land it clean, then raise the difficulty or start a session."}},{"k":"need_more_air_add_pumps","v":{"s":"Need more air. Add pumps to buy hang time before the lip."}},{"k":"need_more_air_choose_smaller_trick","v":{"s":"Air budget is maxed. Try a smaller trick or a smoother surface."}},{"k":"need_more_rotation_budget","v":{"s":"The airtime is close, but the rotation budget is tight. Try skateboard mode or a smaller spin."}},{"k":"ready_to_land","v":{"s":"Ready to land"}},{"k":"needs_tuning","v":{"s":"Needs tuning"}},{"k":"air_time_short","v":{"s":"Air time"}},{"k":"trick_needs","v":{"s":"Trick needs"}},{"k":"spin_budget","v":{"s":"Spin budget"}},{"k":"landing_window_ready","v":{"s":"Landing window is lined up. Chase a cleaner clearance or a longer gap."}},{"k":"short_more_speed","v":{"s":"Short. Speed has the biggest effect because range scales with speed squared."}},{"k":"overshooting_trim_speed","v":{"s":"Overshooting. Trim speed or flatten the angle to pull the landing back."}},{"k":"landing_window","v":{"s":"Landing window"}},{"k":"recalibrate_jump","v":{"s":"Recalibrate jump"}},{"k":"range_short","v":{"s":"Range"}},{"k":"gap_short","v":{"s":"Gap"}},{"k":"peak_short","v":{"s":"Peak"}},{"k":"run_focus","v":{"s":"Run focus"}},{"k":"run_readiness","v":{"s":"Run readiness"}},{"k":"halfpipe_run_map","v":{"s":"Halfpipe run map showing drop-in, airtime, and landing"}},{"k":"gap_jump_run_map","v":{"s":"Gap jump run map showing launch, apex, and landing"}},{"k":"launch","v":{"s":"Launch"}},{"k":"clean_landing_short","v":{"s":"Clean"}},{"k":"tune_landing_short","v":{"s":"Tune"}},{"k":"live_motion","v":{"s":"Live motion"}},{"k":"energy_loop","v":{"s":"Energy loop"}},{"k":"projectile_arc","v":{"s":"Projectile arc"}},{"k":"air_spin_inquiry_summary","v":{"s":"Air / Spin Inquiry"}},{"k":"scene