anic eruptions. The planet may still have active volcanoes today!"}},{"k":"sulfuric_acid_crystal","v":{"s":"Sulfuric Acid Crystal"}},{"k":"the_atmosphere_rains_sulfuric_acid_but","v":{"s":"The atmosphere rains sulfuric acid, but it evaporates before reaching the surface due to the extreme heat."}},{"k":"pyrite_fool_s_gold","v":{"s":"Pyrite (Fool’s Gold)"}},{"k":"mountain_peaks_on_venus_may_be_coated_","v":{"s":"Mountain peaks on Venus may be coated in metallic “snow” made of lead sulfide and bismuth sulfide!"}},{"k":"pancake_dome_fragment","v":{"s":"Pancake Dome Fragment"}},{"k":"venus_has_unique_flat_topped_volcanic_","v":{"s":"Venus has unique flat-topped volcanic domes up to 65 km across, formed by extremely viscous lava."}},{"k":"iron_oxide_dust","v":{"s":"Iron Oxide Dust"}},{"k":"mars_is_red_because_its_soil_is_rich_i","v":{"s":"Mars is red because its soil is rich in iron oxide (rust). The entire planet is literally rusty!"}},{"k":"hematite_blueberry","v":{"s":"Hematite Blueberry"}},{"k":"opportunity_rover_found_tiny_hematite_","v":{"s":"Opportunity rover found tiny hematite spheres called “blueberries” — proof that water once flowed on Mars!"}},{"k":"perchlorate_salt","v":{"s":"Perchlorate Salt"}},{"k":"martian_soil_contains_toxic_perchlorat","v":{"s":"Martian soil contains toxic perchlorates — bad for humans, but bacteria on Earth can use them as fuel!"}},{"k":"olivine_crystal","v":{"s":"Olivine Crystal"}},{"k":"green_olivine_has_been_found_in_martia","v":{"s":"Green olivine has been found in Martian meteorites. On Earth, it’s a semi-precious gemstone called peridot."}},{"k":"methane_ice","v":{"s":"Methane Ice"}},{"k":"curiosity_detected_seasonal_methane_sp","v":{"s":"Curiosity detected seasonal methane spikes. Is it geological or biological? One of Mars’s biggest mysteries!"}},{"k":"nitrogen_ice_3","v":{"s":"Nitrogen Ice"}},{"k":"sputnik_planitia_is_a_vast_plain_of_ni","v":{"s":"Sputnik Planitia is a vast plain of nitrogen ice that slowly churns via convection, like a giant lava lamp!"}},{"k":"tholin_deposit","v":{"s":"Tholin Deposit"}},{"k":"tholins_are_complex_organic_molecules_","v":{"s":"Tholins are complex organic molecules made when UV light hits methane. They give Pluto its reddish color."}},{"k":"water_ice_bedrock","v":{"s":"Water Ice Bedrock"}},{"k":"pluto_s_mountains_are_made_of_water_ic","v":{"s":"Pluto’s mountains are made of water ice — at -230°C, water ice is as hard as rock!"}},{"k":"methane_frost","v":{"s":"Methane Frost"}},{"k":"methane_frosts_coat_pluto_s_peaks_like","v":{"s":"Methane frosts coat Pluto’s peaks like snow caps on Earth. When closer to the Sun, they sublimate into a thin atmosphere."}},{"k":"rock_sample","v":{"s":"Rock Sample"}},{"k":"soil_core","v":{"s":"Soil Core"}},{"k":"upper_atmosphere_6","v":{"s":"Upper Atmosphere"}},{"k":"cloud_deck_2","v":{"s":"Cloud Deck"}},{"k":"deep_troposphere","v":{"s":"Deep Troposphere"}},{"k":"metallic_hydrogen_layer","v":{"s":"Metallic Hydrogen Layer"}},{"k":"inner_core_region","v":{"s":"Inner Core Region"}},{"k":"ammonia_ice_crystal","v":{"s":"Ammonia Ice Crystal"}},{"k":"ammonia_freezes_into_ice_crystals_in_t","v":{"s":"Ammonia freezes into ice crystals in the upper atmosphere, forming the visible cloud tops."}},{"k":"hydrogen_sample","v":{"s":"Hydrogen Sample"}},{"k":"molecular_hydrogen_makes_up_90_of_the_","v":{"s":"Molecular hydrogen makes up ~90% of the atmosphere. At depth, it becomes metallic."}},{"k":"helium_droplet","v":{"s":"Helium Droplet"}},{"k":"helium_rains_out_of_the_hydrogen_at_ex","v":{"s":"Helium \"rains\" out of the hydrogen at extreme pressures, sinking toward the core."}},{"k":"water_vapor_sample","v":{"s":"Water Vapor Sample"}},{"k":"water_clouds_exist_deep_below_the_visi","v":{"s":"Water clouds exist deep below the visible surface. Jupiter may have more water than Earth."}},{"k":"methane_crystal","v":{"s":"Methane Crystal"}},{"k":"methane_gives_uranus_and_neptune_their","v":{"s":"Methane gives Uranus and Neptune their blue-green color. Under pressure, it breaks into carbon and hydrogen."}},{"k":"ammonium_hydrosulfide","v":{"s":"Ammonium Hydrosulfide"}},{"k":"this_compound_creates_the_brown_orange","v":{"s":"This compound creates the brown-orange bands visible on Jupiter and Saturn."}},{"k":"phosphine_trace","v":{"s":"Phosphine Trace"}},{"k":"phosphine_is_dredged_up_from_deep_atmo","v":{"s":"Phosphine is dredged up from deep atmosphere by convection. It’s a biosignature on rocky planets."}},{"k":"sunlight_zone_epipelagic","v":{"s":"Sunlight Zone (Epipelagic)"}},{"k":"twilight_zone_mesopelagic","v":{"s":"Twilight Zone (Mesopelagic)"}},{"k":"midnight_zone_bathypelagic","v":{"s":"Midnight Zone (Bathypelagic)"}},{"k":"abyssal_zone_abyssopelagic","v":{"s":"Abyssal Zone (Abyssopelagic)"}},{"k":"hadal_zone_trenches","v":{"s":"Hadal Zone (Trenches)"}},{"k":"giant_kelp_sample","v":{"s":"Giant Kelp Sample"}},{"k":"giant_kelp_can_grow_up_to_60cm_per_day","v":{"s":"Giant kelp can grow up to 60cm per day — the fastest growing organism on Earth!"}},{"k":"coral_fragment","v":{"s":"Coral Fragment"}},{"k":"coral_reefs_support_25_of_all_marine_s","v":{"s":"Coral reefs support 25% of all marine species despite covering less than 1% of the ocean floor."}},{"k":"bioluminescent_jellyfish","v":{"s":"Bioluminescent Jellyfish"}},{"k":"some_jellyfish_use_gfp_green_fluoresce","v":{"s":"Some jellyfish use GFP (green fluorescent protein) — the same molecule that won a Nobel Prize in chemistry!"}},{"k":"deep_sea_anglerfish","v":{"s":"Deep-Sea Anglerfish"}},{"k":"the_anglerfish_s_bioluminescent_lure_i","v":{"s":"The anglerfish’s bioluminescent lure is powered by symbiotic bacteria. Males permanently fuse to females!"}},{"k":"giant_squid_tissue","v":{"s":"Giant Squid Tissue"}},{"k":"giant_squid_have_the_largest_eyes_in_t","v":{"s":"Giant squid have the largest eyes in the animal kingdom (27 cm!) — the size of dinner plates."}},{"k":"hydrothermal_vent_microbe","v":{"s":"Hydrothermal Vent Microbe"}},{"k":"these_extremophiles_thrive_at_400_c_us","v":{"s":"These extremophiles thrive at 400°C using chemosynthesis. They may resemble the earliest life on Earth."}},{"k":"tube_worm_colony","v":{"s":"Tube Worm Colony"}},{"k":"giant_tube_worms_can_live_250_years_an","v":{"s":"Giant tube worms can live 250+ years and grow to 2.4m. They have no mouth, stomach, or eyes!"}},{"k":"mariana_snailfish","v":{"s":"Mariana Snailfish"}},{"k":"the_deepest_living_fish_ever_found_8_1","v":{"s":"The deepest-living fish ever found (8,178m). Its body has special proteins that prevent cellular collapse under pressure."}},{"k":"manganese_nodule","v":{"s":"Manganese Nodule"}},{"k":"these_potato_sized_mineral_lumps_take_","v":{"s":"These potato-sized mineral lumps take millions of years to form and contain cobalt, nickel, and rare earth metals."}},{"k":"marine_snow_sample","v":{"s":"Marine Snow Sample"}},{"k":"marine_snow_is_a_shower_of_dead_organi","v":{"s":"Marine snow is a shower of dead organisms and waste that feeds the deep sea. It can take weeks to reach the bottom."}},{"k":"one_of_the_largest_impact_craters_in_t","v":{"s":"One of the largest impact craters in the solar system (1,550 km wide)."}},{"k":"the_impact_was_so_powerful_it_created_","v":{"s":"The impact was so powerful it created chaotic terrain on the opposite side of Mercury."}},{"k":"despite_being_closest_to_the_sun_mercu","v":{"s":"Despite being closest to the Sun, Mercury has ice because some craters never see sunlight."}},{"k":"mercury_shrank_as_its_iron_core_cooled","v":{"s":"Mercury shrank as its iron core cooled, creating massive cliff-like wrinkles."}},{"k":"these_scarps_can_be_hundreds_of_km_lon","v":{"s":"These scarps can be hundreds of km long and over 1 km tall."}},{"k":"highest_mountain_on_venus_at_11_km_tal","v":{"s":"Highest mountain on Venus at 11 km — taller than Everest."}},{"k":"the_summit_is_coated_with_a_metallic_s","v":{"s":"The summit is coated with a metallic \"snow\" made from lead sulfide and bismuth sulfide."}},{"k":"flat_topped_volcanic_domes_unique_to_v","v":{"s":"Flat-topped volcanic domes unique to Venus, up to 65 km across."}},{"k":"extremely_viscous_lava_oozed_out_and_s","v":{"s":"Extremely viscous lava oozed out and spread like thick pancake batter."}},{"k":"soviet_lander_that_survived_127_minute","v":{"s":"Soviet lander that survived 127 minutes on the surface in 1982."}},{"k":"venera_13_took_the_first_color_photos_","v":{"s":"Venera 13 took the first color photos of Venus’s surface before being crushed by pressure."}},{"k":"mariana_trench","v":{"s":"Mariana Trench"}},{"k":"deepest_point_on_earth_at_11_034_m_dee","v":{"s":"Deepest point on Earth at 11,034 m — deeper than Everest is tall."}},{"k":"more_people_have_walked_on_the_moon_th","v":{"s":"More people have walked on the Moon than have been to the bottom of the Mariana Trench."}},{"k":"hydrothermal_vent_field","v":{"s":"Hydrothermal Vent Field"}},{"k":"superheated_water_erupts_at_400_c_supp","v":{"s":"Superheated water erupts at 400°C, supporting life without sunlight."}},{"k":"tube_worms_here_can_grow_to_2_4m_and_l","v":{"s":"Tube worms here can grow to 2.4m and live 250+ years using chemosynthesis — no sunlight needed!"}},{"k":"coral_reef_colony","v":{"s":"Coral Reef Colony"}},{"k":"a_living_reef_system_teeming_with_biod","v":{"s":"A living reef system teeming with biodiversity."}},{"k":"coral_reefs_support_25_of_all_marine_s_2","v":{"s":"Coral reefs support 25% of all marine species despite covering less than 1% of the ocean floor."}},{"k":"shipwreck","v":{"s":"Shipwreck"}},{"k":"a_sunken_vessel_colonized_by_marine_li","v":{"s":"A sunken vessel colonized by marine life — an artificial reef."}},{"k":"there_are_an_estimated_3_million_shipw","v":{"s":"There are an estimated 3 million shipwrecks on the ocean floor worldwide. Many become thriving ecosystems."}},{"k":"olympus_mons_is_so_wide_624_km_that_st","v":{"s":"Olympus Mons is so wide (624 km) that standing on its edge, you couldn’t see the summit — it curves beyond the horizon."}},{"k":"it_would_stretch_from_new_york_to_los_","v":{"s":"It would stretch from New York to Los Angeles and is 5x deeper than the Grand Canyon."}},{"k":"if_all_of_mars_s_polar_ice_melted_it_c","v":{"s":"If all of Mars’s polar ice melted, it could cover the entire planet in 11 meters of water."}},{"k":"jezero_crater_where_nasa_s_rover_searc","v":{"s":"Jezero Crater — where NASA’s rover searches for signs of ancient life."}},{"k":"perseverance_arrived_feb_2021_and_has_","v":{"s":"Perseverance arrived Feb 2021 and has driven 28+ km, collecting rock samples for future return to Earth."}},{"k":"an_anticyclonic_storm_raging_for_350_y","v":{"s":"An anticyclonic storm raging for 350+ years, larger than Earth."}},{"k":"wind_speeds_at_the_edge_reach_680_km_h","v":{"s":"Wind speeds at the edge reach 680 km/h — twice the speed of the strongest Earth hurricane."}},{"k":"upper_cloud_layer_made_of_frozen_ammon","v":{"s":"Upper cloud layer made of frozen ammonia crystals at -145°C."}},{"k":"below_this_layer_are_ammonium_hydrosul","v":{"s":"Below this layer are ammonium hydrosulfide clouds, and below those, water clouds. Jupiter has weather 3 layers deep."}},{"k":"zones_between_cloud_bands_where_convec","v":{"s":"Zones between cloud bands where convection drives massive lightning storms."}},{"k":"jupiter_s_lightning_is_10x_more_powerf","v":{"s":"Jupiter’s lightning is 10x more powerful than Earth’s and occurs mostly at the poles and deep clouds."}},{"k":"deep_below_the_clouds_pressure_turns_h","v":{"s":"Deep below the clouds, pressure turns hydrogen into liquid metal."}},{"k":"this_metallic_hydrogen_ocean_generates","v":{"s":"This metallic hydrogen ocean generates Jupiter’s magnetic field — 20,000x stronger than Earth’s."}},{"k":"a_persistent_hexagonal_cloud_pattern_a","v":{"s":"A persistent hexagonal cloud pattern at Saturn’s north pole."}},{"k":"each_side_of_the_hexagon_is_about_14_5","v":{"s":"Each side of the hexagon is about 14,500 km long — wider than Earth’s diameter."}},{"k":"area_where_saturn_s_rings_cast_shadows","v":{"s":"Area where Saturn’s rings cast shadows on the cloud tops."}},{"k":"saturn_s_rings_are_only_about_10_m_thi","v":{"s":"Saturn’s rings are only about 10 m thick despite being 282,000 km wide — thinner than a razor blade proportionally."}},{"k":"titan_has_lakes_of_liquid_methane_and_","v":{"s":"Titan has lakes of liquid methane and a thicker atmosphere than Earth — the only moon with a substantial atmosphere."}},{"k":"at_8_000_km_depth_extreme_pressure_cru","v":{"s":"At 8,000 km depth, extreme pressure crushes carbon into diamonds."}},{"k":"these_diamonds_may_be_as_large_as_mill","v":{"s":"These diamonds may be as large as millions of carats and rain down to form a diamond layer around the core."}},{"k":"uranus_s_magnetic_field_is_tilted_59_f","v":{"s":"Uranus’s magnetic field is tilted 59° from its rotation axis."}},{"k":"combined_with_the_98_axial_tilt_uranus","v":{"s":"Combined with the 98° axial tilt, Uranus’s magnetosphere tumbles chaotically through space."}},{"k":"faint_methane_cloud_bands_where_wind_p","v":{"s":"Faint methane cloud bands where wind patterns change direction."}},{"k":"uranus_appears_featureless_but_hubble_","v":{"s":"Uranus appears featureless but Hubble revealed complex cloud systems moving at 900 km/h."}},{"k":"a_massive_storm_system_similar_to_jupi","v":{"s":"A massive storm system similar to Jupiter’s Great Red Spot."}},{"k":"unlike_jupiter_s_spot_neptune_s_dark_s","v":{"s":"Unlike Jupiter’s spot, Neptune’s dark spots appear and disappear within years — the planet is surprisingly dynamic."}},{"k":"equatorial_winds_reaching_2_100_km_h_f","v":{"s":"Equatorial winds reaching 2,100 km/h — faster than the speed of sound."}},{"k":"neptune_generates_more_heat_than_it_re","v":{"s":"Neptune generates more heat than it receives from the Sun, driving these extreme winds from internal energy."}},{"k":"the_path_of_triton_the_only_large_moon","v":{"s":"The path of Triton — the only large moon that orbits backwards."}},{"k":"triton_is_likely_a_captured_kuiper_bel","v":{"s":"Triton is likely a captured Kuiper Belt object. Its nitrogen geysers shoot plumes 8 km high."}},{"k":"the_famous_heart_shaped_glacier_made_o","v":{"s":"The famous heart-shaped glacier made of nitrogen and carbon monoxide ice."}},{"k":"the_left_lobe_sputnik_planitia_is_a_va","v":{"s":"The left lobe (Sputnik Planitia) is a vast ice plain with convection cells that slowly churn the ice."}},{"k":"mountains_of_water_ice_rising_2_3_km_a","v":{"s":"Mountains of water ice rising 2–3 km above the nitrogen plains."}},{"k":"because_water_ice_is_less_dense_than_n","v":{"s":"Because water ice is less dense than nitrogen ice at Pluto’s temperatures, these mountains literally float."}},{"k":"tholins_are_complex_organic_molecules__2","v":{"s":"Tholins are complex organic molecules created when methane is irradiated — they give Pluto its reddish-brown color."}},{"k":"navigate_to_target_coordinates_x_60_2_","v":{"s":"Navigate to target coordinates. X = 60 × 2, Z = -80 × 2. (Grid is /10)"}},{"k":"navigate_to_target_coordinates_x_300_2","v":{"s":"Navigate to target coordinates. X = -300 ÷ 2, Z = 100 × 2. (Grid is /10)"}},{"k":"navigate_to_target_coordinates_x_125_1","v":{"s":"Navigate to target coordinates. X = 125 + 125, Z = 160 ÷ 2. (Grid is /10)"}},{"k":"navigate_to_target_coordinates_x_150_1","v":{"s":"Navigate to target coordinates. X = 150 - 150, Z = -150 × 2. (Grid is /10)"}},{"k":"navigate_to_target_coordinates_x_110_2","v":{"s":"Navigate to target coordinates. X = -110 × 2, Z = -90 × 2. (Grid is /10)"}},{"k":"a_relay_beacon_is_35m_away_at_heading_","v":{"s":"A relay beacon is 35m away at heading 045° (NE). Calculate and navigate to its position."}},{"k":"mission_control_reports_a_sample_site_","v":{"s":"Mission control reports a sample site 50m away at heading 270° (W). Navigate there."}},{"k":"beacon_alpha","v":{"s":"Beacon Alpha"}},{"k":"beacon_beta","v":{"s":"Beacon Beta"}},{"k":"beacon_gamma