"battle_menu","v":{"s":"Battle menu"}},{"k":"main_menu","v":{"s":"Main menu"}},{"k":"beginner_zone","v":{"s":"🌱 Beginner zone"}},{"k":"build_foundation_slow_accurate_beats_f","v":{"s":"Build foundation. Slow + accurate beats fast + sloppy."}},{"k":"developing","v":{"s":"🟢 Developing"}},{"k":"steady_progression_maintain_accuracy_f","v":{"s":"Steady progression. Maintain accuracy floor."}},{"k":"optimal_zone","v":{"s":"🎯 Optimal zone"}},{"k":"speed_accuracy_in_productive_band_sust","v":{"s":"Speed + accuracy in productive band. Sustainable practice."}},{"k":"proficient","v":{"s":"⚡ Proficient"}},{"k":"high_wpm_achieved_diminishing_returns_","v":{"s":"High WPM achieved. Diminishing returns from speed."}},{"k":"overreaching_accuracy_drops","v":{"s":"⚠️ Overreaching (accuracy drops)"}},{"k":"speed_exceeded_accuracy_budget_backtra","v":{"s":"Speed exceeded accuracy budget. Backtrack to slower target."}},{"k":"menu_2","v":{"s":"← Menu"}},{"k":"wpm_accuracy_tradeoff_discovery","v":{"s":"⚡ WPM-accuracy tradeoff discovery"}},{"k":"five_sliders_tune_your_practice_target","v":{"s":"Five sliders tune your practice target. Widget classifies your zone into one of 5 discrete states and renders the WPM-accuracy Pareto frontier. No score on your tuning — the inquiry is in finding sustainable practice points."}},{"k":"wpm_target","v":{"s":"WPM target →"}},{"k":"accuracy_floor","v":{"s":"Accuracy floor"}},{"k":"pareto_frontier","v":{"s":"── Pareto frontier"}},{"k":"pareto_curve_best_accuracy_achievable_","v":{"s":"Pareto curve = best accuracy achievable at each WPM. Above = unrealistic; below = room to grow."}},{"k":"log","v":{"s":"📋 Log"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"hypothesis_free_text_what_is_your_sust","v":{"s":"Hypothesis (free text): What is your sustainable target? How does accuracy floor change effective WPM?"}},{"k":"stuck_show_open_prompts","v":{"s":"🤔 Stuck — show open prompts"}},{"k":"set_wpm_80_accuracy_98_realistic_compa","v":{"s":"Set WPM=80, accuracy=98. Realistic? Compare to your zone marker."}},{"k":"drop_accuracy_floor_to_80_does_effecti","v":{"s":"Drop accuracy floor to 80%. Does effective WPM rise?"}},{"k":"pros_sustain_95_at_70_wpm_investigate_","v":{"s":"Pros sustain 95%+ at 70+ WPM. Investigate what training paths get there."}},{"k":"a_slower_target_with_high_accuracy_may","v":{"s":"A slower target with high accuracy may produce more text per session. Test."}},{"k":"i_understand_the_tradeoff_explain_in_o","v":{"s":"I understand the tradeoff — explain in own words"}},{"k":"explain_in_your_own_words_how_do_wpm_a","v":{"s":"Explain in your own words: how do WPM, accuracy, and momentum interact? What does the Pareto frontier mean for typing practice?"}},{"k":"design_note_discrete_5_zone_marker_par","v":{"s":"Design note: discrete 5-zone marker; Pareto curve shows tradeoff space; no \"correct\" target — by design."}},{"k":"maine_description","v":{"s":"Seven hand-written passages about Maine — lighthouses, lobstering, Mount Katahdin, the Penobscot River, Wabanaki history, blueberry barrens, Portland fog. One per grade band, K through high school."}},{"k":"self-advocacy_description","v":{"s":"Seven sentences a student with a disability might actually need to say to a teacher, peer, or clinician — typing practice and language rehearsal at once. Covers needing help, asking for breaks, audio learning, fidget tools, IEP testing accommodations, sensory recess needs, and medical lighting accommodations. K through high school."}},{"k":"calming_description","v":{"s":"Seven self-regulation passages a student can type — and read aloud — when feelings get big. Includes box-breathing language, the 5-4-3-2-1 grounding technique, the \"feelings are waves\" frame, the \"pause is not giving up\" reframe, and the \"anxiety lies\" CBT script. Designed by school-psych guidance; not a substitute for clinical care, but a typing-rhythm anchor a student can use in the moment."}},{"k":"growth-mindset_description","v":{"s":"Seven passages on effort, struggle, and the small word YET. Built on Carol Dweck's growth-mindset research and current brain-plasticity science. Pairs with Mind & Body Calming (regulate) and Self-Advocacy (speak up) to form a complete SEL arc — regulate, reframe, advocate. K through high school."}},{"k":"home-row_description","v":{"s":"Start here. Fingers rest on a, s, d, f · j, k, l, ;"}},{"k":"top-row_description","v":{"s":"Reach up to q w e r t y u i o p"}},{"k":"bottom-row_description","v":{"s":"Reach down to z x c v b n m"}},{"k":"common-words_description","v":{"s":"High-frequency words build real reading fluency."}},{"k":"capitalization_description","v":{"s":"Shift-key practice. Capitals at sentence starts and proper nouns."}},{"k":"number-row_description","v":{"s":"Reach up to 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 0. Same finger-color map as letters."}},{"k":"symbols_description","v":{"s":"Shift + numbers for ! @ # $ % & ( ) and other punctuation."}},{"k":"passage_description","v":{"s":"AI-generated passage for your grade level and interests. Not locked — anyone can use it."}},{"k":"custom_description","v":{"s":"Your teacher or you can enter any text — spelling lists, IEP goals, science vocab. Not scored for mastery."}},{"k":"one-hand-left_description","v":{"s":"Practice with just the left hand. Keys: q w e r t · a s d f g · z x c v b · space."}},{"k":"one-hand-right_description","v":{"s":"Practice with just the right hand. Keys: y u i o p · h j k l ; · n m , . / · space."}},{"k":"focus-errors_description","v":{"s":"Auto-generated practice for YOUR top error keys. Updates after every session based on the heatmap."}},{"k":"reduce_motion","v":{"s":"⏸ Motion"}},{"k":"non_english_passages_use_matching_keyboard","v":{"s":"This passage uses the selected language's correct accents or writing system. Choose the matching keyboard layout or input method on your device."}},{"k":"save_private_resume_draft_and_return","v":{"s":"Save a private resume draft and return to the menu"}}],"id":590}},{"k":"unitconvert","v":{"o":[{"k":"length","v":{"s":"📏 Length"}},{"k":"weight","v":{"s":"⚖️ Mass"}},{"k":"temp","v":{"s":"🌡️ Temp"}},{"k":"speed","v":{"s":"🚀 Speed"}},{"k":"volume","v":{"s":"🧪 Volume"}},{"k":"time","v":{"s":"⏰ Time"}},{"k":"area","v":{"s":"🗒️ Area"}},{"k":"pressure","v":{"s":"💨 Pressure"}},{"k":"energy","v":{"s":"⚡ Energy"}},{"k":"back","v":{"s":"Back to tools"}},{"k":"unit_converter","v":{"s":"📏 Unit Converter"}},{"k":"view_badges_b","v":{"s":"View badges (B)"}},{"k":"ai_tutor","v":{"s":"AI Tutor (?)"}},{"k":"ai","v":{"s":"🧠 AI"}},{"k":"ai_unit_tutor","v":{"s":"🧠 AI Unit Tutor"}},{"k":"ask_tutor","v":{"s":"Ask Tutor"}},{"k":"ask_again","v":{"s":"Ask Again"}},{"k":"ask_again_2","v":{"s":"🔄 Ask Again"}},{"k":"unit_converter_sections","v":{"s":"Unit Converter sections"}},{"k":"convert_the_math_behind_units","v":{"s":"Convert — the math behind units"}},{"k":"conversion_factor_ratio_equal_to_1_e_g","v":{"s":"Conversion factor = ratio equal to 1 (e.g., 1 ft = 12 in → 12 in / 1 ft). Multiplying by it changes the unit without changing the value. SI prefixes (kilo, milli) are powers of 10 — just shift the decimal."}},{"k":"all_units_reference_table","v":{"s":"All units — reference table"}},{"k":"length_mass_volume_temperature_time_en","v":{"s":"Length, mass, volume, temperature, time, energy, pressure. The single rule that matters: track units through every step. If your final answer is in m² when you wanted seconds, you made an error somewhere upstream."}},{"k":"quiz_conversion_practice","v":{"s":"Quiz — conversion practice"}},{"k":"daily_life_conversions_f_c_mph_km_h_lb","v":{"s":"Daily-life conversions (°F↔°C, mph↔km/h, lb↔kg) plus AP / SAT / lab measurements. Each question shows the conversion factor after answering so you build the muscle memory."}},{"k":"word_problem_apply_in_context","v":{"s":"Word problem — apply in context"}},{"k":"real_world_unit_conversion_scenarios_g","v":{"s":"Real-world unit-conversion scenarios: gas mileage, recipe scaling, dosage calculations, travel-distance estimates. Word problems are 80% reading comprehension + 20% conversion math."}},{"k":"magnitude_orders_of_magnitude_discover","v":{"s":"Magnitude — orders of magnitude discovery"}},{"k":"every_si_prefix_is_a_power_of_10_slide","v":{"s":"Every SI prefix is a power of 10. Slide the source and target exponents to feel how far apart scales really are — the core skill behind scientific notation and Fermi estimates."}},{"k":"value_to_convert","v":{"s":"Value to convert"}},{"k":"from_unit","v":{"s":"From unit"}},{"k":"swap_units","v":{"s":"Swap units"}},{"k":"swap_units_2","v":{"s":"Swap units"}},{"k":"to_unit","v":{"s":"To unit"}},{"k":"dimensional_analysis","v":{"s":"🔬 Dimensional Analysis"}},{"k":"save","v":{"s":"Save"}},{"k":"save_2","v":{"s":"💾 Save"}},{"k":"pin","v":{"s":"📌 Pin"}},{"k":"tutor","v":{"s":"Tutor"}},{"k":"tutor_2","v":{"s":"🧠 Tutor"}},{"k":"visual_comparison","v":{"s":"📊 Visual Comparison"}},{"k":"real_world_reference","v":{"s":"🌍 Real-World Reference"}},{"k":"fun_fact","v":{"s":"💡 Fun Fact"}},{"k":"pinned_conversions","v":{"s":"📌 Pinned Conversions"}},{"k":"history","v":{"s":"📝 History"}},{"k":"clear","v":{"s":"Clear"}},{"k":"clear_2","v":{"s":"Clear"}},{"k":"snapshot","v":{"s":"Snapshot"}},{"k":"snapshot_2","v":{"s":"📸 Snapshot"}},{"k":"change","v":{"s":"Change"}},{"k":"change_2","v":{"s":"Change →"}},{"k":"change_3","v":{"s":"Change →"}},{"k":"unit","v":{"s":"Unit"}},{"k":"value","v":{"s":"Value"}},{"k":"use","v":{"s":"Use →"}},{"k":"reference","v":{"s":"🌍 Reference"}},{"k":"next_question_n","v":{"s":"Next question (N)"}},{"k":"next_question_n_2","v":{"s":"Next question (N)"}},{"k":"test_your_unit_conversion_knowledge","v":{"s":"Test your unit conversion knowledge!"}},{"k":"22_questions_speed_bonus_streak_reward","v":{"s":"22 questions • Speed bonus • Streak rewards"}},{"k":"question","v":{"s":"🧠 Question"}},{"k":"your_answer","v":{"s":"Your answer..."}},{"k":"quiz_answer","v":{"s":"Quiz answer"}},{"k":"ask_tutor_2","v":{"s":"Ask Tutor"}},{"k":"get_a_hint_from_ai","v":{"s":"Get a hint from AI"}},{"k":"next_question","v":{"s":"Next Question"}},{"k":"next_question_2","v":{"s":"🔄 Next Question"}},{"k":"explain","v":{"s":"Explain"}},{"k":"explain_2","v":{"s":"🧠 Explain"}},{"k":"crafting_your_word_problem","v":{"s":"Crafting your word problem..."}},{"k":"click_generate_for_an_ai_crafted_word_","v":{"s":"Click Generate for an AI-crafted word problem"}},{"k":"new_problem","v":{"s":"New Problem"}},{"k":"new_problem_2","v":{"s":"🔄 New Problem"}},{"k":"save_3","v":{"s":"Save"}},{"k":"save_4","v":{"s":"💾 Save"}},{"k":"tiny_scale_change","v":{"s":"🐜 Tiny scale change"}},{"k":"2_orders_of_magnitude_close_cousins_cm","v":{"s":"<2 orders of magnitude — close cousins (cm→m)."}},{"k":"small_scale_change","v":{"s":"🟢 Small scale change"}},{"k":"2_4_oom_same_domain_g_kg","v":{"s":"2-4 OOM — same domain (g→kg)."}},{"k":"medium_scale_change","v":{"s":"🟡 Medium scale change"}},{"k":"5_8_oom_biology_to_geology_scales","v":{"s":"5-8 OOM — biology to geology scales."}},{"k":"large_scale_change","v":{"s":"🔴 Large scale change"}},{"k":"9_12_oom_micro_to_macro_span","v":{"s":"9-12 OOM — micro to macro span."}},{"k":"massive_scale_change","v":{"s":"🌌 Massive scale change"}},{"k":"13_oom_atomic_to_cosmic","v":{"s":"13+ OOM — atomic to cosmic."}},{"k":"magnitude_discovery","v":{"s":"⚙️ Magnitude discovery"}},{"k":"adjust_source_and_target_exponents_10_","v":{"s":"Adjust source and target exponents (10^N). Widget classifies magnitude change into 5 discrete bands. No score, no reveal."}},{"k":"log","v":{"s":"📋 Log"}},{"k":"reset","v":{"s":"↺ Reset"}},{"k":"hypothesis_what_real_world_examples_sp","v":{"s":"Hypothesis: What real-world examples span each magnitude band?"}},{"k":"stuck_show_open_prompts","v":{"s":"🤔 Stuck — show open prompts"}},{"k":"compare_cm_km_mm_light_year_how_many_o","v":{"s":"Compare cm→km, mm→light-year. How many OOM each?"}},{"k":"why_are_scientists_trained_in_orders_o","v":{"s":"Why are scientists trained in orders of magnitude?"}},{"k":"i_understand_explain_in_own_words","v":{"s":"I understand — explain in own words"}},{"k":"explain_why_dimensional_reasoning_acro","v":{"s":"Explain why dimensional reasoning across many OOM is hard."}},{"k":"design_note_discrete_5_state_magnitude","v":{"s":"Design note: discrete 5-state magnitude marker; no error score; no reveal — by design."}},{"k":"1_4_tabs","v":{"s":"1-4 Tabs"}},{"k":"n_next_quiz","v":{"s":"N Next Quiz"}},{"k":"b_badges","v":{"s":"B Badges"}},{"k":"ai_tutor_2","v":{"s":"? AI Tutor"}},{"k":"metric_prefixes_powers_of_10_from_atom","v":{"s":"🔬 Metric Prefixes — Powers of 10 from atoms to galaxies"}},{"k":"badge_toast","v":{"s":" Badge: "}},{"k":"badge_firstConvert","v":{"s":"First Convert"}},{"k":"badgedesc_firstConvert","v":{"s":"Make your first unit conversion"}},{"k":"badge_quizStreak5","v":{"s":"On Fire"}},{"k":"badgedesc_quizStreak5","v":{"s":"5 quiz answers in a row"}},{"k":"badge_quizStreak10","v":{"s":"Lightning"}},{"k":"badgedesc_quizStreak10","v":{"s":"10 quiz answers in a row"}},{"k":"badge_quizMaster","v":{"s":"Quiz Master"}},{"k":"badgedesc_quizMaster","v":{"s":"Answer 20 quiz questions"}},{"k":"badge_allCategories","v":{"s":"World Explorer"}},{"k":"badgedesc_allCategories","v":{"s":"Use all 9 unit categories"}},{"k":"badge_speedster","v":{"s":"Speedster"}},{"k":"badgedesc_speedster","v":{"s":"Answer a quiz in under 3 seconds"}},{"k":"badge_wordProblem","v":{"s":"Word Wizard"}},{"k":"badgedesc_wordProblem","v":{"s":"Generate an AI word problem"}},{"k":"badge_pinCollector","v":{"s":"Pin Collector"}},{"k":"badgedesc_pinCollector","v":{"s":"Pin 5 conversions"}},{"k":"badge_historian","v":{"s":"Historian"}},{"k":"badgedesc_historian","v":{"s":"Save 10 conversions to history"}},{"k":"badge_tempMaster","v":{"s":"Temp Master"}},{"k":"badgedesc_tempMaster","v":{"s":"Convert between all 3 temperature units"}},{"k":"offline_problem_ready","v":{"s":"AI is unavailable, so an offline practice problem is ready.