ilable","v":{"s":"Portrait editing is unavailable, so your portrait was not changed."}},{"k":"describe_portrait_change","v":{"s":"Describe how to change your portrait."}},{"k":"refine_portrait_title","v":{"s":"Refine character portrait"}},{"k":"refine_portrait_placeholder","v":{"s":"For example: add round glasses and a blue scarf"}},{"k":"refine_portrait_confirm","v":{"s":"Refine portrait"}},{"k":"portrait_editor_failed","v":{"s":"The portrait editor could not open, so your portrait was not changed."}},{"k":"portrait_unchanged","v":{"s":"Portrait unchanged."}},{"k":"no_portrait_changes_requested","v":{"s":"No portrait changes requested."}},{"k":"orbit_img","v":{"s":"Orbit diagram"}}],"id":600}},{"k":"alphaFold","v":{"o":[{"k":"confidence_very_high","v":{"s":"Very high"}},{"k":"confidence_very_high_detail","v":{"s":"The local backbone is predicted with very high confidence. Still compare it with experimental or biological evidence."}},{"k":"confidence_confident","v":{"s":"Confident"}},{"k":"confidence_confident_detail","v":{"s":"The local fold is generally reliable, though side chains and flexible boundaries may need closer inspection."}},{"k":"confidence_low","v":{"s":"Low"}},{"k":"confidence_low_detail","v":{"s":"Treat this region cautiously. It may be flexible, disordered, or uncertain in this prediction."}},{"k":"confidence_very_low","v":{"s":"Very low"}},{"k":"confidence_very_low_detail","v":{"s":"This region should not be interpreted as a dependable structure without supporting evidence."}},{"k":"confidence_all_sr","v":{"s":"Showing all prediction confidence bands."}},{"k":"confidence_selected_sr","v":{"s":"Showing the selected prediction confidence band:"}},{"k":"popup_blocked","v":{"s":"The AlphaFold Explorer window was blocked. Allow pop-ups for this page, then try again."}},{"k":"opened_sr","v":{"s":"Opened AlphaFold Explorer in a new window."}},{"k":"status_open","v":{"s":"Explorer connected"}},{"k":"status_opening","v":{"s":"Opening companion window"}},{"k":"status_blocked","v":{"s":"Pop-up needs permission"}},{"k":"status_ready","v":{"s":"Ready to investigate"}},{"k":"mission_label","v":{"s":"Structural biology mission"}},{"k":"title","v":{"s":"AlphaFold Explorer"}},{"k":"mission_blurb","v":{"s":"Explore a public protein prediction, inspect confidence and shape, then build a cautious claim from visible evidence."}},{"k":"confidence_preview_aria","v":{"s":"Illustrative folded protein ribbon colored by AlphaFold pLDDT confidence: deep blue and cyan are higher confidence, while yellow and orange are lower confidence. This is a teaching illustration, not a loaded protein prediction."}},{"k":"confidence_preview_label","v":{"s":"Prediction confidence preview"}},{"k":"confidence_preview_note","v":{"s":"Illustrative model | confidence is not correctness"}},{"k":"confidence_title","v":{"s":"Read the confidence colors"}},{"k":"confidence_intro","v":{"s":"pLDDT estimates local model confidence for each residue."}},{"k":"confidence_overview_detail","v":{"s":"Select a confidence band to isolate that part of the illustrative fold and learn how cautiously to interpret it."}},{"k":"confidence_caution","v":{"s":"High confidence supports the local fold. It does not prove function, binding, or biological relevance."}},{"k":"progress_label","v":{"s":"AlphaFold investigation progress"}},{"k":"metric_launches","v":{"s":"Explorer launches"}},{"k":"metric_launches_note","v":{"s":"companion-window sessions"}},{"k":"metric_structures","v":{"s":"Public structures"}},{"k":"metric_structures_note","v":{"s":"database lookups"}},{"k":"metric_prepared","v":{"s":"Inputs prepared"}},{"k":"metric_prepared_note","v":{"s":"safe classroom samples"}},{"k":"metric_guidance","v":{"s":"Reasoning checks"}},{"k":"metric_ai_on","v":{"s":"AI guidance available"}},{"k":"metric_ai_off","v":{"s":"built-in prompts active"}},{"k":"open_title","v":{"s":"Open AlphaFold Explorer in a new window"}},{"k":"refocus","v":{"s":"Return to AlphaFold Explorer"}},{"k":"open","v":{"s":"Open AlphaFold Explorer"}},{"k":"action_note","v":{"s":"Opens a companion window. Keep AlloFlow open for progress and optional guidance."}},{"k":"blocked_note","v":{"s":"Pop-up blocked - allow pop-ups for this page and try again. "}},{"k":"blocked_link","v":{"s":"Open AlphaFold Explorer directly"}},{"k":"route_title","v":{"s":"Your investigation route"}},{"k":"route_subtitle","v":{"s":"Move from model viewing to evidence-based explanation."}},{"k":"route_launch","v":{"s":"Launch safely"}},{"k":"route_launch_body","v":{"s":"Use a public, synthetic, or teacher-approved sample—never personal genetic data."}},{"k":"route_launch_state","v":{"s":"Start here"}},{"k":"route_inspect","v":{"s":"Inspect the model"}},{"k":"route_inspect_body","v":{"s":"Compare folds, domains, surfaces, pLDDT confidence, and PAE uncertainty."}},{"k":"route_inspect_state","v":{"s":"Observe next"}},{"k":"route_explain","v":{"s":"Explain cautiously"}},{"k":"route_explain_body","v":{"s":"Connect one visible feature to evidence, uncertainty, and a useful next test."}},{"k":"route_explain_state","v":{"s":"Build a claim"}},{"k":"support_label","v":{"s":"Tutorial and classroom data guidance"}},{"k":"tutorial_title","v":{"s":"How AlphaFold investigations work (4 steps)"}},{"k":"tutorial_1","v":{"s":"AlphaFold predicts a protein 3D structure from an amino acid sequence; AlphaFold DB provides public predicted structures."}},{"k":"tutorial_2","v":{"s":"Start from a classroom preset or choose a grade-level tutorial, lesson length, biology context, assignment format, and support level."}},{"k":"tutorial_3","v":{"s":"Use cautious wording: the model suggests evidence, but it is not final proof by itself."}},{"k":"tutorial_4","v":{"s":"Only prepare JSON for public, synthetic, or teacher-approved classroom samples; the explorer does not automatically submit sequences."}},{"k":"guardrail_title","v":{"s":"Classroom data boundary"}},{"k":"guardrail1","v":{"s":"Do not enter sequences from yourself, classmates, family members, patients, private genetic tests, or medical reports."}},{"k":"ai_on","v":{"s":"AI guidance receives structure metadata, learner context, and student observations or claims—not full protein sequences."}},{"k":"ai_off","v":{"s":"AI hints are off. The explorer still works with built-in inspection prompts."}},{"k":"credit","v":{"s":"Data/viewing: AlphaFold Protein Structure Database by Google DeepMind and EMBL-EBI; Mol* viewer under MIT license. AlphaFold Server opens separately for non-commercial research workflows. Internet is required for database lookup and web viewing."}},{"k":"step_label","v":{"s":"Step"}},{"k":"complete","v":{"s":"✓ Complete"}},{"k":"cross_scale_recorded_sr","v":{"s":"Cautious cross-scale conclusion recorded."}},{"k":"cross_scale_review_sr","v":{"s":"Review the evidence boundaries between RNA, protein, structure, and function."}},{"k":"record_incomplete_sr","v":{"s":"Complete the evidence-boundary check and all four evidence-record fields before saving."}},{"k":"record_saved_sr","v":{"s":"Cross-scale evidence record saved for Cell Atlas."}},{"k":"companion_verified_sr","v":{"s":"Verified AlphaFold companion evidence received for"}},{"k":"return_cell_atlas_sr","v":{"s":"Returning to the Cell Atlas evidence investigation."}},{"k":"bridge_label","v":{"s":"Cell Atlas → AlphaFold evidence bridge"}},{"k":"bridge_title","v":{"s":"One biological story, four different evidence levels"}},{"k":"bridge_intro","v":{"s":"Carry the RNA observation forward without letting one tool answer a question measured by another."}},{"k":"handoff_context_aria","v":{"s":"Cell Atlas handoff context"}},{"k":"tissue_atlas","v":{"s":"Tissue atlas"}},{"k":"selected_cell","v":{"s":"Selected cell"}},{"k":"gene_protein_arrow","v":{"s":"→"}},{"k":"rna_evidence","v":{"s":"RNA evidence"}},{"k":"atlas_observation_label","v":{"s":"Atlas observation:"}},{"k":"source_context_prefix","v":{"s":"Source context:"}},{"k":"observed_step","v":{"s":"01 Observed"}},{"k":"rna_abundance_boundary","v":{"s":"RNA abundance does not directly measure protein."}},{"k":"hypothesized_step","v":{"s":"02 Hypothesized"}},{"k":"protein_presence","v":{"s":"Protein presence"}},{"k":"protein_hypothesis","v":{"s":"The transcript supports a hypothesis that the protein may be produced. Confirm abundance and cellular localization with proteomics, immunostaining, or another protein assay."}},{"k":"predicted_step","v":{"s":"03 Predicted"}},{"k":"protein_structure","v":{"s":"Protein structure"}},{"k":"structure_prediction","v":{"s":"AlphaFold predicts a sequence-compatible 3D model. Inspect pLDDT and PAE; structural confidence is not evidence that this cell produced an active protein."}},{"k":"tested_step","v":{"s":"04 Tested"}},{"k":"function_in_context","v":{"s":"Function in context"}},{"k":"function_test","v":{"s":"Use localization, perturbation, interaction, or functional assays to test whether the protein contributes to the proposed cell role."}},{"k":"biological_hypothesis_label","v":{"s":"Biological hypothesis from the atlas:"}},{"k":"claim_question","v":{"s":"Which conclusion respects every evidence boundary?"}},{"k":"claim_choices_aria","v":{"s":"Cross-scale claim choices"}},{"k":"claim_overreach","v":{"s":"High RNA evidence plus a confident AlphaFold model proves the protein is abundant, correctly localized, and active in this cell."}},{"k":"claim_separate","v":{"s":"The atlas supports a transcript-level hypothesis, while AlphaFold supplies separate structural-model evidence; protein abundance, localization, and function still require appropriate experiments."}},{"k":"claim_expression","v":{"s":"A low-confidence AlphaFold region would show that the gene was not expressed in the atlas."}},{"k":"claim_correct","v":{"s":"Well separated: transcript, protein, structure, and function are connected hypotheses measured by different evidence."}},{"k":"claim_incorrect","v":{"s":"That claim crosses measurement levels. AlphaFold confidence describes a structural model; it cannot establish RNA expression, protein abundance, localization, or activity."}},{"k":"record_title","v":{"s":"Build a cross-scale evidence record"}},{"k":"record_intro","v":{"s":"Write only what you actually inspected. AlphaFold model evidence remains separate from the atlas RNA measurement, and no protein sequence is stored in this record."}},{"k":"record_observation_label","v":{"s":"1. Structural observation"}},{"k":"record_observation_placeholder","v":{"s":"I observed a compact region and a lower-confidence flexible segment..."}},{"k":"record_model_label","v":{"s":"2. Model evidence"}},{"k":"record_model_placeholder","v":{"s":"The pLDDT colors support local confidence in..., while PAE suggests uncertainty between..."}},{"k":"record_claim_label","v":{"s":"3. Cautious claim"}},{"k":"record_claim_placeholder","v":{"s":"Together, the atlas and model support the hypothesis that..., but they do not establish..."}},{"k":"record_next_label","v":{"s":"4. Missing evidence or next test"}},{"k":"record_next_placeholder","v":{"s":"Next I would test protein abundance, localization, or function by..."}},{"k":"record_completion_aria","v":{"s":"Evidence record completion"}},{"k":"record_separated","v":{"s":"✓ Evidence levels separated"}},{"k":"record_not_separated","v":{"s":"Evidence levels not yet separated"}},{"k":"record_observation_badge","v":{"s":"Observation"}},{"k":"record_model_badge","v":{"s":"Model evidence"}},{"k":"record_claim_badge","v":{"s":"Cautious claim"}},{"k":"record_next_badge","v":{"s":"Next test"}},{"k":"record_save_button","v":{"s":"Save cross-scale evidence record"}},{"k":"record_saved_message","v":{"s":"Evidence record saved for return to Cell Atlas. Revise any field and save again to update it."}},{"k":"inspect_prefix","v":{"s":"Inspect"}},{"k":"structure_suffix","v":{"s":"structure →"}},{"k":"return_cell_atlas_button","v":{"s":"← Return to Cell Atlas evidence"}},{"k":"open_prefilled_prefix","v":{"s":"Open"}},{"k":"open_prefilled_suffix","v":{"s":"in AlphaFold Explorer"}},{"k":"handoff_ready_prefix","v":{"s":"Cell Atlas handoff ready:"}},{"k":"public_protein","v":{"s":"public protein"}},{"k":"handoff_ready_suffix","v":{"s":"The public accession will load automatically."}},{"k":"record_downloads_aria","v":{"s":"Download evidence record"}},{"k":"record_download_md","v":{"s":"Download evidence record (.md)"}},{"k":"record_download_json","v":{"s":"Download evidence record (.json)"}},{"k":"metric_exports","v":{"s":"Evidence exports"}},{"k":"metric_exports_note","v":{"s":"saved Markdown or JSON records"}},{"k":"route_package","v":{"s":"Package the evidence"}},{"k":"route_package_body","v":{"s":"Save the completed cross-scale record as Markdown or JSON so another learner can audit the claim."}},{"k":"route_package_state","v":{"s":"Record + export"}}],"id":601}},{"k":"magnetism","v":{"o":[{"k":"a11y_station_passport_progress_of_evidence_milestone","v":{"s":"Station passport progress: {value1} of {value2} evidence milestones complete"}},{"k":"a11y_magnetic_field_lines_around_bar_magnets_draggab","v":{"s":"Magnetic field lines around {value1} bar magnets, draggable sources, component vectors, and a compass pointing along the resultant field."}},{"k":"a11y_next_action","v":{"s":"Next action: {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_center_field_versus_current_graph_for_air_and_a","v":{"s":"Center field versus current graph for air and {value1}. At {value2} amps the selected field is {value3} millitesla."}},{"k":"a11y_baseline_a","v":{"s":"Baseline A, {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_live_trial_b","v":{"s":"Live trial B, {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_unknown_ion_case_progress_of_3_evidence_steps_c","v":{"s":"Unknown-ion case progress: {value1} of 3 evidence steps complete"}},{"k":"a11y_torque_cycle_phase_current_angle_degrees_dead_s","v":{"s":"Torque cycle phase. Current angle {value1} degrees. Dead spots near 0 and 180 degrees; maximum leverage near 90 and 270 degrees; the 180 degree marker is the commutator flip."}},{"k":"a11y_torque_leverage_percent","v":{"s":"Torque leverage {value1} percent"}},{"k":"a11y_motor_model_with_a_amp_current_loop_in_field_se","v":{"s":"Motor model with a {value1} amp current loop in field setting {value2}, rotated {value3} degrees; opposite wire forces create torque"}},{"k":"a11y_linked_magnetic_flux_and_induced_voltage_graph","v":{"s":"Linked magnetic flux and induced voltage graph with {value1} samples. Current flux {value2} and voltage {value3}."}},{"k":"a11y_rotating_coil_at_degrees_and_revolutions_per_mi","v":{"s":"Rotating coil at {value1} degrees and {value2} revolutions per minute. Relative flux {value3} and induced voltage {value4}, shown on quarter-cycle-shifted graphs"}},{"k":"a11y_phase_wheel_at_degrees_flux_is_of_its_amplitude","v":{"s":"Phase wheel at {value1} degrees. Flux is {value2} of its amplitude and voltage is {value3} of its amplitude. The two signals are separated by a 90 degree phase gap."}},{"k":"a11y_prediction_for","v":{"s":"Prediction for {value1}"}},{"k":"a11y_predict_will_lift","v":{"s":"Predict {value1} will lift"}},{"k":"a11y_predict_will_show_no_pull","v":{"s":"Predict {value1} will show no pull"}},{"k":"a11y_grid_of_40_magnetic_domains_applied_field_is_si","v":{"s":"Grid of 40 magnetic domains. Applied field is {value1}; signed net magnetization is {value2} percent toward {value3}."}},{"k":"a11y_transformer_primary_coil_of_turns_and_secondary","v":{"s":"Transformer: primary coil of {value1} turns and secondary of {value2} turns on a shared iron core, output {value3} volts"}},{"k":"a11y_lamp_brightness_percent","v":{"s":"Lamp brightness {value1} percent"}},{"k":"a11y_schematic_magnetosphere_at_solar_wind_pressure","v":{"s":"Schematic magnetosphere at solar-wind pressure {value1} of 10; solar wind arrives from the left. The dayside boundary is {value2} Earth radii, the tail reaches {value3} Earth radii, and the auroral oval is near {value4} degrees magnetic latitude. A dashed outline preserves the quiet reference, and a compass shows declination {val