y","v":{"s":"Expert - audit independently"}},{"k":"historical_grounding","v":{"s":"Historical grounding"}},{"k":"at_naca_and_nasa_teams_of_women_perfor","v":{"s":"At NACA and NASA, teams of women performed and checked aerospace calculations. Katherine Johnson calculated trajectories and verified electronic-computer results. Dorothy Vaughan led the West Area Computing unit and became an expert FORTRAN programmer."}},{"k":"human_computers_organized_data_used_sh","v":{"s":"Human computers organized data, used shared tables, applied mathematical procedures, checked one another's work, and documented results."}},{"k":"as_electronic_computers_arrived_mathem","v":{"s":"As electronic computers arrived, mathematical knowledge remained essential for programming, debugging, and verification."}},{"k":"the_simulation_emphasizes_the_work_pro","v":{"s":"The simulation emphasizes the work process; it does not turn discrimination or segregation into a game mechanic."}},{"k":"this_simulation_uses_those_documented_","v":{"s":"This simulation uses those documented kinds of work as educational context; it does not recreate a copyrighted story or portray a real person as a fictional character."}},{"k":"nasa_katherine_johnson_biography","v":{"s":"NASA: Katherine Johnson biography"}},{"k":"nasa_dorothy_vaughan_biography","v":{"s":"NASA: Dorothy Vaughan biography"}},{"k":"vocabulary_desk","v":{"s":"Vocabulary desk"}},{"k":"algorithm","v":{"s":"Algorithm"}},{"k":"a_repeatable_sequence_of_steps_for_sol","v":{"s":"A repeatable sequence of steps for solving a problem."}},{"k":"human_computer","v":{"s":"Human computer"}},{"k":"a_person_employed_to_perform_and_verif","v":{"s":"A person employed to perform and verify mathematical calculations."}},{"k":"an_early_language_designed_for_scienti","v":{"s":"An early language designed for scientific and engineering computation."}},{"k":"compiler","v":{"s":"Compiler"}},{"k":"a_program_that_translates_source_instr","v":{"s":"A program that translates source instructions and reports structural errors."}},{"k":"punch_card","v":{"s":"Punch card"}},{"k":"a_physical_card_that_encoded_one_line_","v":{"s":"A physical card that encoded one line of data or program instructions."}},{"k":"batch_job","v":{"s":"Batch job"}},{"k":"a_prepared_program_submitted_for_proce","v":{"s":"A prepared program submitted for processing without an interactive screen."}},{"k":"verification","v":{"s":"Verification"}},{"k":"an_independent_check_that_a_result_agr","v":{"s":"An independent check that a result agrees with requirements and evidence."}},{"k":"teacher_guide","v":{"s":"Teacher guide"}},{"k":"suggested_time","v":{"s":"Suggested time: "}},{"k":"40_60_minutes_individually_or_in_pairs","v":{"s":"40-60 minutes individually or in pairs."}},{"k":"learning_objectives","v":{"s":"Learning objectives"}},{"k":"read_a_printed_reference_table_decompo","v":{"s":"Read a printed reference table, decompose velocity, and apply a multi-step mathematical model."}},{"k":"explain_how_variable_names_constants_f","v":{"s":"Explain how variable names, constants, functions, and statement order affect a program."}},{"k":"distinguish_compilation_execution_outp","v":{"s":"Distinguish compilation, execution, output interpretation, and independent verification."}},{"k":"connect_computing_history_to_the_docum","v":{"s":"Connect computing history to the documented labor and expertise of women mathematicians and programmers."}},{"k":"evidence_to_collect","v":{"s":"Evidence to collect: "}},{"k":"printed_trigonometry_lookup_table_prec","v":{"s":"printed trigonometry lookup, table-precision prediction, calculation ledger, repaired listing, line-printer format card, fixed-width preview confirmation, ordered deck, machine read-back, reproducibility note, audit-role record, GO/HOLD reasoning, angle-study prediction, mission-replay prediction and comparison, and the completion report."}},{"k":"debrief_prompts","v":{"s":"Debrief prompts: "}},{"k":"why_did_card_order_matter_which_