othing is shown here. This tool will not paraphrase a rule it has not fetched."}},{"k":"tap_full","v":{"s":"Open for the full text"}},{"k":"title","v":{"s":"Education Law Navigator"}},{"k":"tools","v":{"s":"Tools"}},{"k":"typeface","v":{"s":"Switch typeface"}},{"k":"verbatim","v":{"s":"Verbatim text as published"}},{"k":"verbatim_live","v":{"s":"Verbatim text, fetched live from eCFR"}}],"id":618}},{"k":"machinelab","v":{"o":[{"k":"a_bit_easier","v":{"s":"A bit easier"}},{"k":"ai_failed","v":{"s":"The tutor could not answer just now. Try again in a moment."}},{"k":"ai_hint","v":{"s":"Ask the tutor to describe what your current machine is doing with its energy."}},{"k":"ai_offline","v":{"s":"The AI tutor is not available here."}},{"k":"ai_timeout","v":{"s":"The tutor did not answer in time. Try again."}},{"k":"air_on","v":{"s":"Air resistance on"}},{"k":"air_on_k2","v":{"s":"Let the air push back"}},{"k":"all_six","v":{"s":"All six simple machines proven."}},{"k":"anatomy_aria","v":{"s":"3D machine key"}},{"k":"anatomy_arm","v":{"s":"throwing arm"}},{"k":"anatomy_beam","v":{"s":"throwing beam"}},{"k":"anatomy_focus","v":{"s":"Focus the "}},{"k":"anatomy_focus_3d","v":{"s":" in the 3D scene"}},{"k":"anatomy_focus_announce","v":{"s":"Focusing on "}},{"k":"anatomy_focus_title","v":{"s":"Focus this part in the 3D scene"}},{"k":"anatomy_hint","v":{"s":"Click a part or drag to inspect the structure."}},{"k":"anatomy_pivot","v":{"s":"pivot"}},{"k":"anatomy_spring","v":{"s":"spring bundle"}},{"k":"anatomy_stone","v":{"s":"stone"}},{"k":"anatomy_title","v":{"s":"Read the machine"}},{"k":"anatomy_weight","v":{"s":"counterweight"}},{"k":"apex_label","v":{"s":"apex "}},{"k":"apex_lbl","v":{"s":"Apex: "}},{"k":"aria_ai_level","v":{"s":"Explanation level"}},{"k":"aria_benchlist","v":{"s":"Simple machine benches"}},{"k":"aria_breach","v":{"s":"The wall is breached."}},{"k":"aria_cracked","v":{"s":" cracked, "}},{"k":"aria_explain","v":{"s":"Generate an explanation at the selected level"}},{"k":"aria_gone","v":{"s":" gone."}},{"k":"aria_intact","v":{"s":" blocks intact, "}},{"k":"aria_invalid","v":{"s":"These settings do not describe a working machine."}},{"k":"aria_level","v":{"s":"Reading level"}},{"k":"aria_ma","v":{"s":"Mechanical advantage "}},{"k":"aria_machine","v":{"s":"Choose a machine"}},{"k":"aria_machine3d","v":{"s":"Three-dimensional view of the "}},{"k":"aria_machine3d2","v":{"s":". Drag with a mouse or pen to orbit. The camera buttons and ledger provide keyboard and numeric equivalents."}},{"k":"aria_open_bench","v":{"s":"Open the bench for "}},{"k":"aria_open_machine","v":{"s":"Open the "}},{"k":"aria_predict","v":{"s":"Your predicted effort force in newtons"}},{"k":"aria_range3d","v":{"s":"Interactive three-dimensional range showing the selected machine’s launch path. Drag with a mouse or pen to orbit. The graph and controls below provide keyboard and numeric equivalents."}},{"k":"aria_range_predict","v":{"s":"Your predicted range in metres"}},{"k":"aria_shop3d","v":{"s":"Interactive three-dimensional workshop showing the selected simple machine: "}},{"k":"aria_shop3d2","v":{"s":"Amber marks the effort path and blue marks the load path. Drag with a mouse or pen to orbit. The camera buttons and panels below provide complete keyboard and numeric equivalents."}},{"k":"aria_targets","v":{"s":"Choose a target"}},{"k":"aria_topics","v":{"s":"Field manual topics"}},{"k":"aria_traj","v":{"s":"Trajectory. Range "}},{"k":"aria_traj2","v":{"s":" metres, apex "}},{"k":"aria_traj3","v":{"s":" metres, flight time "}},{"k":"aria_traj4","v":{"s":" seconds."}},{"k":"aria_views","v":{"s":"Machine Lab sections"}},{"k":"aria_wall3d","v":{"s":"Three-dimensional view of the target wall. Drag with a mouse or pen to orbit. The diagram and course table below carry the same information."}},{"k":"arm_len","v":{"s":"Arm length"}},{"k":"arm_mass","v":{"s":"Beam mass"}},{"k":"arm_mass2","v":{"s":"Arm mass"}},{"k":"bad_machine","v":{"s":"This machine cannot fire. Check the sliders."}},{"k":"bad_setup","v":{"s":"These settings do not describe a working machine. Adjust the sliders."}},{"k":"ball_g35","v":{"s":"Twisting the rope bundles stores energy, the way winding a rubber band does. More turns store more energy. Pulling the string back further stores more still."}},{"k":"ball_g68","v":{"s":"Each bundle is a torsional spring: E = one half k times the twist angle squared, and there are two of them. Stiffness k rises the more turns you wind in, so both the winding and the draw length matter. Two bundles store twice the energy, but there are also two arms to get moving, and that costs efficiency."}},{"k":"ball_g912","v":{"s":"Modelled as a linear torsional spring, E = n(1/2)k(theta)^2 with k rising linearly in the winding. Real twisted sinew is markedly nonlinear and hysteretic, loses energy internally on every shot, and changes behaviour with humidity, which is one reason surviving ancient design rules proportion the whole engine from the spring-hole diameter rather than from a stiffness figure."}},{"k":"ball_k2","v":{"s":"Two thick ropes are twisted up tight. When you let go, they untwist and snap the arms forward. It works like a very strong rubber band."}},{"k":"beam_long","v":{"s":"Long arm"}},{"k":"beam_short","v":{"s":"Short arm"}},{"k":"bench_progress_aria","v":{"s":"Simple-machine benches proven"}},{"k":"best_bound","v":{"s":"* This machine was still improving at the lightest stone the search would try, so that row is where the search stopped rather than a real best. Treat it as \"lighter than anything here\"."}},{"k":"best_caption2","v":{"s":"For each machine: the mass and diameter of its furthest-flying stone, then that stone’s range and impact energy, each followed in brackets by the figure for the stone you are currently using"}},{"k":"best_eff","v":{"s":"Worth noticing: the furthest of these is the "}},{"k":"best_eff2","v":{"s":", and its best stone takes only "}},{"k":"best_eff3","v":{"s":"% of the stored energy, against "}},{"k":"best_eff4","v":{"s":"% for the stone you are using. Throwing furthest and wasting least are pulling in opposite directions."}},{"k":"best_g35","v":{"s":"Each machine throws one size of stone furthest. Too heavy and it barely moves. Too light and the air stops it. But the stone that goes furthest is not the one that hits hardest, so look at both columns."}},{"k":"best_g68","v":{"s":"This tries many stones for each machine, keeping the rock density the same so every one of them is a real object, and reports the one that flies furthest. Furthest is not hardest: a light stone leaves fast and lands with very little energy. A siege crew wanted both, which is why they did not simply throw the furthest-flying stone."}},{"k":"best_g912","v":{"s":"The search sweeps payload mass geometrically and derives diameter from a fixed density, so mass and frontal area stay physically linked. An optimum exists because launch speed saturates at sqrt(2E/m_eff) once the payload is light against the machine inertia, while drag deceleration scales as area over mass and keeps rising as the stone shrinks. Range peaks between those limits. Impact energy does not: it falls monotonically with payload mass here, so range and delivered energy are competing objectives rather than one optimum."}},{"k":"best_k2","v":{"s":"A stone can be too heavy to throw far. It can also be too light. Press the button and each machine will try lots of stones and keep the one that goes furthest. Watch how hard it hits, though."}},{"k":"best_rho","v":{"s":"Every stone in that table is the same rock: "}},{"k":"best_rho2","v":{"s":" kg per cubic metre. Only the size changes, and the mass follows from it. Your current stone is "}},{"k":"best_rho_g35","v":{"s":"Every stone in that table is the same kind of rock. Only the size changes, and the weight follows from the size. Yours weighs "}},{"k":"best_rho_g912","v":{"s":" kg per cubic metre. Density is held fixed and diameter derived from mass, so frontal area scales as mass to the two thirds and every candidate is a physically realisable object. Your current stone is "}},{"k":"best_rho_k2","v":{"s":"Every stone in that table is made of the same rock. Only the size changes, and a smaller stone weighs less. Yours weighs "}},{"k":"best_run","v":{"s":"Find the best stone for each machine"}},{"k":"best_stale","v":{"s":"A setting has changed since this ran, so these numbers describe the old machines. Run it again to bring them up to date."}},{"k":"best_title","v":{"s":"Which stone flies furthest?"}},{"k":"blocks_down","v":{"s":" Blocks came down."}},{"k":"blow_density","v":{"s":"Concentrated into: "}},{"k":"blow_density2","v":{"s":" kJ per square metre"}},{"k":"blow_energy","v":{"s":"Energy delivered: "}},{"k":"breach_in","v":{"s":"Breached in "}},{"k":"breach_kj","v":{"s":" kJ of crank work."}},{"k":"breach_shots","v":{"s":" shots, for "}},{"k":"breached_btn","v":{"s":"Breached"}},{"k":"breached_toast","v":{"s":"Breach!"}},{"k":"budget_note","v":{"s":"Damage here is scored on total energy absorbed against a per-block budget. Those budgets are order-of-magnitude classroom values, not a prediction of how real masonry fails."}},{"k":"build_g35","v":{"s":"Lifting the counterweight stores energy. Letting it fall spends that energy on the stone. The long arm is a lever, so the stone end moves much faster than the weight end."}},{"k":"build_g68","v":{"s":"Stored energy is M g h, set entirely by the counterweight and how far it drops. The arm is a lever, so the stone travels a longer arc in the same time and therefore moves faster."}},{"k":"build_g912","v":{"s":"This is a single-degree-of-freedom energy model: E = Mgh into the system, shared between the stone and the effective mass of the arm and counterweight referred to the payload radius. A real trebuchet is a double pendulum whose sling release this model does not resolve, so treat the numbers as the right trade-off rather than a design specification."}},{"k":"build_k2","v":{"s":"A big weight falls down, and the long arm throws the stone up and away. A heavier weight falling further throws harder."}},{"k":"cam_arc","v":{"s":"Frame the full flight arc"}},{"k":"cam_arc_short","v":{"s":"Arc"}},{"k":"cam_close","v":{"s":"Show a close three-quarter view"}},{"k":"cam_close_short","v":{"s":"Close"}},{"k":"cam_down","v":{"s":"Tilt down"}},{"k":"cam_drag_hint","v":{"s":"Drag scene or use:"}},{"k":"cam_group","v":{"s":"Camera for the "}},{"k":"cam_impact","v":{"s":"Focus the impact end of the lane"}},{"k":"cam_impact_short","v":{"s":"Impact"}},{"k":"cam_in","v":{"s":"Zoom in"}},{"k":"cam_launch","v":{"s":"Focus the launch deck"}},{"k":"cam_launch_short","v":{"s":"Launch"}},{"k":"cam_left","v":{"s":"Turn left"}},{"k":"cam_out","v":{"s":"Zoom out"}},{"k":"cam_reset","v":{"s":"Reset the view"}},{"k":"cam_right","v":{"s":"Turn right"}},{"k":"cam_side","v":{"s":"Show the machine from the side"}},{"k":"cam_side_short","v":{"s":"Side"}},{"k":"cam_up","v":{"s":"Tilt up"}},{"k":"cause_arm","v":{"s":"energy left in the moving arm and counterweight"}},{"k":"cause_arm_ball","v":{"s":"energy left in the two moving arms and the string"}},{"k":"cause_arm_ball_k2","v":{"s":"energy that stayed in the two arms and the string"}},{"k":"cause_arm_k2","v":{"s":"energy that stayed in the arm and the weight"}},{"k":"cause_arm_ona","v":{"s":"energy left in the moving arm and sling"}},{"k":"cause_arm_ona_k2","v":{"s":"energy that stayed in the arm and the sling"}},{"k":"cause_drag","v":{"s":"air resistance"}},{"k":"cause_drag_k2","v":{"s":"pushing through the air"}},{"k":"cause_winch","v":{"s":"winch friction"}},{"k":"cause_winch_k2","v":{"s":"rubbing in the handle"}},{"k":"check","v":{"s":"Check"}},{"k":"cmp_arc_aria","v":{"s":"Flight comparison: "}},{"k":"cmp_arc_hint","v":{"s":"same stone · same release angle"}},{"k":"cmp_arc_title","v":{"s":"Flight shapes at a glance"}},{"k":"cmp_caption","v":{"s":"Stored energy, transfer efficiency, launch speed and range for each machine"}},{"k":"cmp_caption_k2","v":{"s":"How much energy each machine stores, how much of it reaches the stone, how fast the stone leaves and how far it goes"}},{"k":"cmp_g35","v":{"s":"Each machine stores energy a different way, then spends it on the same stone. Compare how much energy each one stores and how much of it actually reaches the stone."}},{"k":"cmp_g68","v":{"s":"Same stone, same release angle, same air. What differs is how the energy is stored and how much of the machine has to move to deliver it. Watch the efficiency column, not just the range."}},{"k":"cmp_g912","v":{"s":"The comparison is only fair in the sense that the payload and the flight conditions match. Stored energy is not equalised, because each store has its own natural scale, so read stored energy and transfer efficiency as separate axes rather than collapsing them into range."}},{"k":"cmp_k2","v":{"s":"Three different machines throw the same stone. One uses a falling weight. Two use twisted rope. See which one throws it furthest."}},{"k":"cmp_note","v":{"s":"The highlighted cells are the best in their column. The machine that throws furthest is often not the one that wastes least, because stored energy and efficiency are two different things."}},{"k":"cmp_note2","v":{"s":"One thing to be careful about: holding the stone the same is what makes this a fair test, but it is a stone of one particular size, and it suits one of these machines far better than the other two. The panel below asks a different question, which is what each machine would rather be throwing."}},{"k":"cmp_note2_g35","v":{"s":"Giving all three the same stone is what makes this a fair test. It is also one particular stone, and it suits one machine much better than the others. The next panel asks a different question: what would each machine rather throw?"}},{"k":"cmp_note2_g912","v":{"s":"A controlled comparison is only as good as its choice of what to hold constant. Fixing the payload is defensible, but it is not neutral: the fixed payload happens to sit near the trebuchet optimum and far from the torsion ones, so the ranking below is partly a statement about the stone. The panel underneath relaxes that control and optimises the payload per machine instead."}},{"k":"cmp_note2_k2","v":{"s":"All three machines are throwing the same stone, which is fair. But that stone is a good size for one of them and a bad size for the other two. The next part asks what stone each machine would like best."}},{"k":"cmp_note_g35","v":{"s":"The highlighted cells are the best in their column. Notice that the machine throwing furthest is not the one keeping the most of its energy. Storing a lot and wasting little are two separate things."}},{"k":"cmp_note_k2","v":{"s":"The green numbers are the winners in their column. The machine that throws furthest is not always the one that wastes the least. Those are two different things to be good at."}},{"k":"cmp_try","v":{"s":"Things worth trying"}},{"k":"cmp_try1","v":{"s":"Make the stone lighter, and shrink its diameter to match so it stays a real rock. Which machine copes best, and why? The button below does this for you."}},{"k":"cmp_try1_g35","v":{"s":"Make the stone lighter, and make it smaller too so it is still a real rock. Which machine copes best?"}},{"k":"cmp_try1_g912","v":{"s":"Reduce payload mass with diameter derived from a fixed density, so frontal area scales as mass to the two thirds. Which machine degrades most gracefully, and which term in m_p/(m_p + m_eff) explains it?"}},{"k":"cmp_try1_k2","v":{"s":"Make the stone smaller and lighter together, so it is still a real rock. Which machine likes that best?"}},{"k":"cmp_try2","v":{"s":"Make the onager arm heavier. Watch what happens to the share of energy that reaches the stone."}},{"k":"cmp_try2_g35","v":{"s":"Make the onager arm heavier. How much of the energy still reaches the stone?"}},{"k":"cmp_try2_g912","v":{"s":"Increase the onager arm mass. Transfer efficiency should fall even though stored energy is untouched, because m_eff is the arm inertia reduced to the payload radius."}},{"k":"cmp_try2_k2","v":{"s":"Give the onager a heavier arm. Does the stone go further or not as far?"}},{"k":"cmp_try3","v":{"s":"Lengthen the onager sling. It costs nothing and changes the efficiency. Why?"}},{"k":"cmp_try3_g35","v":{"s":"Lengthen the onager sling. It costs no energy at all, so why does the throw change?"}},{"k":"cmp_try3_g912","v":{"s":"Lengthen the onager sling. It adds no stored energy, so any change in range has to come through the effective mass. Work out which way, and why."}},{"k":"cmp_try3_k2","v":{"s":"Make the onager sling longer. Watch what changes."}},{"k":"cmp_try4","v":{"s":"Wind more turns into the bundles. Does range grow as fast as stored energy does?"}},{"k":"cmp_try4_g35","v":{"s":"Add more twists to the ropes. Does the throw grow as fast as the stored energy does?"}},{"k":"cmp_try4_g912","v":{"s":"Wind more turns into the bundles. Stored energy goes as the square of the twist angle, so predict whether range should scale linearly, and then check."}},{"k":"cmp_try4_k2","v":{"s":"Twist the ropes more times. Does the stone go much further?"}},{"k":"cmp_unbuildable","v":{"s":"not a working machine at these settings"}},{"k":"col_across","v":{"s":"Across"}},{"k":"col_beststone","v":{"s":"Best stone"}},{"k":"col_course","v":{"s":"Course"}},{"k":"col_eff","v":{"s":"Efficiency"}},{"k":"col_eff2","v":{"s":"To the stone"}},{"k":"col_hits2","v":{"s":"Lands with (yours)"}},{"k":"col_joules","v":{"s":"Joules"}},{"k":"col_launch","v":{"s":"Launch"}},{"k":"col_loss","v":{"s":"Lost to"}},{"k":"col_machine","v":{"s":"Machine"}},{"k":"col_pct","v":{"s":"% of input"}},{"k":"col_range","v":{"s":"Range"}},{"k":"col_range2","v":{"s":"Range"}},{"k":"col_range3","v":{"s":"Range (yours)"}},{"k":"col_speed","v":{"s":"Launch"}},{"k":"col_stage","v":{"s":"Stage"}},{"k":"col_stone","v":{"s":"Stone"}},{"k":"col_stone2","v":{"s":"Stone"}},{"k":"col_store","v":{"s":"Energy store"}},{"k":"col_stored","v":{"s":"Stored"}},{"k":"compare_title","v":{"s":"Three machines, one stone"}},{"k":"conditions","v":{"s":"Conditions"}},{"k":"correct_force","v":{"s":"Correct. The effort force is "}},{"k":"crank_force","v":{"s":"Crank force: "}},{"k":"crank_force_k2","v":{"s":"How hard you pull: "}},{"k":"crank_force_k2b","v":{"s":" newtons"}},{"k":"crank_turns","v":{"s":"Turns of the crank: "}},{"k":"crank_turns_k2","v":{"s":"Times you turn the handle: "}},{"k":"cw_drop","v":{"s":"Counterweight drop"}},{"k":"cw_mass","v":{"s":"Counterweight mass"}},{"k":"demo_running","v":{"s":"Running..."}},{"k":"demo_started","v":{"s":"Demonstration started for "}},{"k":"distance_times","v":{"s":"Distance ×"}},{"k":"draw","v":{"s":"Draw length"}},{"k":"drift_lbl","v":{"s":"Blown sideways: "}},{"k":"eff_tail","v":{"s":" of the stored energy reached the stone."}},{"k":"eff_tail_g35","v":{"s":"% of the energy the machine had saved up. The rest stayed behind in the moving parts."}},{"k":"eff_tail_k2","v":{"s":" out of every 100 parts went into the stone. The rest stayed in the machine."}},{"k":"effmass_a","v":{"s":"The stone is "}},{"k":"effmass_b","v":{"s":" kg, and the moving parts of the machine add another "}},{"k":"effmass_c","v":{"s":" kg of effective mass, so the stone gets "}},{"k":"effort_needed","v":{"s":"Effort needed"}},{"k":"effort_path","v":{"s":"Effort path"}},{"k":"elevation","v":{"s":"Launch height"}},{"k":"energy_ledger","v":{"s":"Energy ledger"}},{"k":"engineering_studio","v":{"s":"Interactive engineering studio"}},{"k":"enter_number","v":{"s":"Enter a number first."}},{"k":"explain","v":{"s":"Explain"}},{"k":"explain_at","v":{"s":"Explain at:"}},{"k":"fell_short","v":{"s":"Short by "}},{"k":"fell_short2","v":{"s":" m. Range the target: more stored energy, or a lighter stone, or move closer."}},{"k":"fire","v":{"s":"Fire"}},{"k":"flight_path","v":{"s":"Flight path"}},{"k":"follow_class","v":{"s":"Follow class setting"}},{"k":"force_div","v":{"s":"Force ÷"}},{"k":"fram_castle","v":{"s":"Castle"}},{"k":"fram_field","v":{"s":"Whole field"}},{"k":"fram_machine","v":{"s":"Machine"}},{"k":"framing_group","v":{"s":"Camera framing"}},{"k":"framing_label","v":{"s":"Shot:"}},{"k":"fs_aria","v":{"s":"Toggle full screen for the "}},{"k":"fs_aria2","v":{"s":". Press Escape to leave full screen."}},{"k":"fs_label","v":{"s":"Full screen"}},{"k":"fs_title","v":{"s":"Full screen (press Escape to leave)"}},{"k":"fs_toggled","v":{"s":"Full screen toggled. Press Escape to leave full screen."}},{"k":"fs_unavailable","v":{"s":"Full screen is not available here."}},{"k":"g35_q","v":{"s":"Work out the effort force, then check yourself. Effort = load divided by mechanical advantage."}},{"k":"gained_falling","v":{"s":"gained falling from the launch height"}},{"k":"gl_failed","v":{"s":"3D view unavailable. Every number below is unaffected."}},{"k":"gl_loading","v":{"s":"Loading the 3D view..."}},{"k":"hide_courses","v":{"s":"Hide courses"}},{"k":"hide_past","v":{"s":"Hide earlier shots"}},{"k":"hist_b1","v":{"s":"Two-armed torsion engines are described in surviving technical treatises by Heron of Alexandria and Philon of Byzantium, and in Book X of Vitruvius. E. W. Marsden’s Greek and Roman Artillery (1969, with a companion volume of translated technical treatises in 1971) remains the standard modern scholarly treatment. The ancient design rules proportion the entire engine from the diameter of the spring-hole, which is a strong hint that the springs were the part nobody could calculate directly."}},{"k":"hist_b2","v":{"s":"Ammianus Marcellinus, writing in the fourth century, describes a one-armed stone-thrower and reports that soldiers called it the onager, the wild ass, for the way it kicked. Earlier Roman engines were not called this, so the word is evidence about the fourth century rather than about Roman artillery in general."}},{"k":"hist_b3","v":{"s":"Ancient sources describe torsion springs made from sinew and from hair. Several authors also report cities cutting women’s hair for bowstrings or springs during a siege. That story is genuinely present in the ancient sources, and it is also exactly the kind of striking anecdote that gets repeated far more often than it is examined. Treat it as something ancient authors said, which is a different claim from something that routinely happened."}},{"k":"hist_b4","v":{"s":"Human-powered traction trebuchets are much older than counterweight ones and reached the Mediterranean world well before it. Counterweight machines appear in European sources around the late twelfth and thirteenth centuries. The precise dating, and the route by which the design travelled, are actively debated among historians, so this manual gives the century and leaves the argument open."}},{"k":"hist_b5","v":{"s":"Numbers like \"three hundred metres\" almost always come from a modern reconstruction rather than from a medieval measurement, and they get quoted as though they were historical records. If you cite a range, cite the specific reconstruction it came from. The figures this tool produces are outputs of a simplified model and are not evidence about any real machine."}},{"k":"hist_b6","v":{"s":"The popular image of a trebuchet demolishing a curtain wall overstates what these machines usually did. Historians generally give more weight to undermining, to assault, and above all to blockade and starvation. Stone-throwers were highly effective against battlements, hoardings and roofs, and for throwing incendiaries and other unpleasant things over a wall, which is a real and interesting job that is simply not the one the films show."}},{"k":"hist_t1","v":{"s":"Torsion artillery is Greek and Roman, and well documented"}},{"k":"hist_t2","v":{"s":"The onager is a late Roman name"}},{"k":"hist_t3","v":{"s":"Spring material: attested, but repeated uncritically"}},{"k":"hist_t4","v":{"s":"The counterweight trebuchet arrives later, and the details are contested"}},{"k":"hist_t5","v":{"s":"Be very careful with range figures"}},{"k":"hist_t6","v":{"s":"Siege engines rarely knocked castle walls down"}},{"k":"how_it_feels","v":{"s":"How it feels"}},{"k":"identical","v":{"s":"identical"}},{"k":"imp_big","v":{"s":"That build is too large to besiege. Try something under 400 columns."}},{"k":"imp_depth","v":{"s":" Thickness counts: a wall three deep takes three times the energy to break through."}},{"k":"imp_dropped","v":{"s":"Imp dropped"}},{"k":"imp_dropped2","v":{"s":" floating blocks were left out, since they were not standing on anything."}},{"k":"imp_empty","v":{"s":"There is no Architecture Studio build to import yet."}},{"k":"imp_float","v":{"s":"Nothing in that build is standing on the ground."}},{"k":"imp_ok","v":{"s":"Imported your build: "}},{"k":"imp_ok2","v":{"s":" columns of wall."}},{"k":"impact_lbl","v":{"s":"Impact speed: "}},{"k":"import_arch","v":{"s":"Your own build"}},{"k":"in_flight","v":{"s":"In flight…"}},{"k":"iq_aria_exp","v":{"s":"Your explanation in your own words"}},{"k":"iq_aria_hyp","v":{"s":"Your hypothesis about the three machines"}},{"k":"iq_can_explain","v":{"s":"I can explain, in my own words, why these three machines rank the way they do."}},{"k":"iq_exp_ph","v":{"s":"Explain in your own words..."}},{"k":"iq_log","v":{"s":"Log this comparison"}},{"k":"iq_log_caption","v":{"s":"Comparisons you have logged, by stone mass"}},{"k":"iq_o1","v":{"s":"Does the machine that stores the most energy also deliver the most to the stone? Should it?"}},{"k":"iq_o2","v":{"s":"The onager stores half what the ballista does. Why is its efficiency higher anyway?"}},{"k":"iq_o3","v":{"s":"Is there a stone mass at which the ordering of the three machines changes? How would you find it?"}},{"k":"iq_o4","v":{"s":"Making the arm lighter raises efficiency. What do you think stops a real engineer doing that indefinitely?"}},{"k":"iq_o5","v":{"s":"If you turned the air off, would your answer change? Try it and say why."}},{"k":"iq_open","v":{"s":"Open questions (no answer key)"}},{"k":"iq_ph","v":{"s":"Write what you expect, before you test it..."}},{"k":"iq_q","v":{"s":"Your hypothesis: which machine throws a 5 kg stone furthest, and which a 200 kg stone? What in the ledger makes you think so?"}},{"k":"iq_q_g35","v":{"s":"Your hypothesis: which machine throws a very light stone furthest, and which throws a very heavy one furthest?"}},{"k":"iq_q_g912","v":{"s":"Your hypothesis: predict the ordering of the three machines by range at 5 kg and at 200 kg, and say which term in m_p/(m_p + m_eff) decides each case."}},{"k":"iq_q_k2","v":{"s":"Which machine do you think throws best? Say why."}},{"k":"iq_sig","v":{"s":"Inquiry widget — no score, no reveal, no answer dump. Nothing here is marked, and the tool will not tell you the answer. The numbers in the table are the tool’s simplified model, not a measurement of any real machine."}},{"k":"iq_stuck","v":{"s":"I'm stuck — show open questions"}},{"k":"iq_title","v":{"s":"Build your own theory"}},{"k":"k2_trade","v":{"s":"A simple machine does not give you extra power. It lets you push less hard, but you have to push for longer."}},{"k":"last_blow","v":{"s":"The last blow"}},{"k":"last_test","v":{"s":"Last test"}},{"k":"last_test_open","v":{"s":"Open the full flight in the Test Range"}},{"k":"last_test_open_short","v":{"s":"See full flight"}},{"k":"last_test_stale","v":{"s":"Last test - settings changed"}},{"k":"last_test_stale_hint","v":{"s":"Fire again to test the new settings."}},{"k":"ledger_caption","v":{"s":"Energy ledger from crank to impact"}},{"k":"legend_cracked","v":{"s":"cracked "}},{"k":"legend_cracked2","v":{"s":"Cracked"}},{"k":"legend_gone","v":{"s":"gone "}},{"k":"legend_gone2","v":{"s":"Gone"}},{"k":"legend_intact","v":{"s":"intact "}},{"k":"legend_intact2","v":{"s":"Intact"}},{"k":"lever","v":{"o":[{"k":"copy_g35","v":{"s":"A lever turns around a point called the fulcrum. The further your push is from the fulcrum, the easier the lift becomes. Divide the effort arm by the load arm to get the number of times the lever multiplies your push."}},{"k":"copy_g68","v":{"s":"Mechanical advantage is the ratio of the arms: MA = effort arm / load arm. It does not depend on the load. Your effort force is the load divided by MA, and your hand travels MA times as far as the load rises."}},{"k":"copy_g912","v":{"s":"Taking moments about the fulcrum, F_effort x d_effort = F_load x d_load, so MA = d_effort / d_load. This is the ideal MA: it assumes a rigid massless beam and a frictionless pivot. A real lever with a heavy beam delivers less, and the gap between ideal and actual MA is the efficiency."}},{"k":"copy_k2","v":{"s":"A seesaw is a lever. If you sit far from the middle, you can lift a friend who is bigger than you. Sitting close to the middle makes it hard."}},{"k":"effort_arm","v":{"s":"Effort arm"}},{"k":"k2_a","v":{"s":"Push far from the middle"}},{"k":"k2_b","v":{"s":"Push right next to the middle"}},{"k":"k2_c","v":{"s":"It feels the same either way"}},{"k":"k2_q","v":{"s":"You want to lift something heavy with a plank over a log. Where should you push?"}},{"k":"label","v":{"s":"Lever"}},{"k":"load","v":{"s":"Load"}},{"k":"load_arm","v":{"s":"Load arm"}}],"id":620}},{"k":"lift_distance","v":{"s":"Load moves"}},{"k":"live_workshop","v":{"s":"Live workshop"}},{"k":"load","v":{"s":"Load"}},{"k":"load_moves","v":{"s":"Load moves"}},{"k":"load_path","v":{"s":"Load path"}},{"k":"loading","v":{"s":"Loading Machine Lab..."}},{"k":"log_hint","v":{"s":"Try a very light stone and a very heavy one. The light one leaves faster but wastes most of the energy on the arm. Somewhere in between throws furthest."}},{"k":"loose","v":{"s":"Loose!"}},{"k":"loosing","v":{"s":"Away!"}},{"k":"lost_to","v":{"s":"lost to "}},{"k":"lv_g2","v":{"s":"Grade 2"}},{"k":"lv_g5","v":{"s":"Grade 5"}},{"k":"lv_g8","v":{"s":"Grade 8"}},{"k":"lv_hs","v":{"s":"High school"}},{"k":"ma","v":{"s":"Mechanical advantage"}},{"k":"machine_ballista","v":{"s":"Ballista"}},{"k":"machine_onager","v":{"s":"Onager"}},{"k":"machine_switched","v":{"s":"Showing "}},{"k":"machine_switched_camera","v":{"s":". Camera reset to the overview."}},{"k":"machine_trebuchet","v":{"s":"Trebuchet"}},{"k":"machines_fired","v":{"s":"machines fired"}},{"k":"manual_e2","v":{"s":"The ledger in the Build and Test Range views shows this chain for the machine you have configured. The table view carries exactly the same numbers as the bars."}},{"k":"manual_e_g35","v":{"s":"You do work at the crank. That work gets stored, either by lifting a heavy weight or by twisting rope. When you release it, the store spends its energy on the stone. At every step a little is lost, so the stone never gets everything you put in."}},{"k":"manual_e_g68","v":{"s":"Follow the joules. Work in at the crank equals force times distance. Winch friction takes a share, so what is stored is less than what you did. At release the stored energy is shared between the stone and everything else that has to move, which is why a heavy arm is expensive. Then air resistance takes more on the way down."}},{"k":"manual_e_g912","v":{"s":"The chain is a sequence of efficiencies multiplied together. Transfer efficiency is m_p / (m_p + m_eff), where m_eff is the machine inertia reduced to the payload radius. That single expression explains why a light projectile leaves fast but wastes most of the store, and why a heavy one is efficient but slow. Range is not maximised at either end, but only once drag is present."}},{"k":"manual_e_k2","v":{"s":"Machines do not make energy. They move it around. You put energy in when you crank the handle, and the machine gives most of it back to the stone. Some always gets lost on the way."}},{"k":"manual_h_intro","v":{"s":"A note on how we know any of this. Ancient and medieval engineers left far fewer numbers than we would like, so most of what follows comes from a small number of surviving technical treatises, from archaeology, and from modern reconstructions. Where scholars disagree, this manual says so rather than picking a side."}},{"k":"manual_m1","v":{"s":"Every siege engine here is built out of the same six simple machines you met in the Machine Shop."}},{"k":"manual_m2","v":{"s":"None of them adds energy. Each one only changes the exchange rate between force and distance."}},{"k":"manual_m_lever","v":{"s":"Lever: the throwing arm itself. The pivot is the fulcrum, and the ratio of the two arms sets how much faster the payload end travels."}},{"k":"manual_m_pulley","v":{"s":"Pulley: the block and tackle on the cocking rope, multiplying the crew’s pull."}},{"k":"manual_m_ramp","v":{"s":"Inclined plane: the ramp the ammunition is rolled up, and the wedge under the frame that sets elevation."}},{"k":"manual_m_screw","v":{"s":"Screw: the tensioning gear on a torsion engine, adjusting the spring by tiny amounts against a huge load."}},{"k":"manual_m_wedge","v":{"s":"Wedge: the trigger and the pawl of the ratchet, which hold an enormous force with a small one."}},{"k":"manual_m_wheel","v":{"s":"Wheel and axle: the windlass that cocks the machine. A big handle turning a small drum."}},{"k":"manual_route_energy_action","v":{"s":"Open the 3D Test Range"}},{"k":"manual_route_energy_copy","v":{"s":"Make a prediction, fire the stone, and follow the joules from the crank to the flight."}},{"k":"manual_route_energy_title","v":{"s":"Watch the energy move"}},{"k":"manual_route_eyebrow","v":{"s":"Step back into the world"}},{"k":"manual_route_history_action","v":{"s":"Open the 3D Target Wall"}},{"k":"manual_route_history_copy","v":{"s":"Aim at a target and see what a reconstruction can show—and what history still has to tell us."}},{"k":"manual_route_history_title","v":{"s":"Put the model against a wall"}},{"k":"manual_route_machines_action","v":{"s":"Visit the Machine Shop"}},{"k":"manual_route_machines_copy","v":{"s":"Tune a bench, watch force and distance trade places, then prove your prediction."}},{"k":"manual_route_machines_title","v":{"s":"Try one simple machine"}},{"k":"manual_route_model_action","v":{"s":"Experiment in the Test Range"}},{"k":"manual_route_model_copy","v":{"s":"Change drag, gravity, angle, or wind and watch which conclusions survive."}},{"k":"manual_route_model_title","v":{"s":"Stress-test the model"}},{"k":"manual_route_record_action","v":{"s":"Open Compare"}},{"k":"manual_route_record_copy","v":{"s":"Compare the three machines side by side and record what the ledger makes you think."}},{"k":"manual_route_record_title","v":{"s":"Turn notes into a claim"}},{"k":"manual_x1","v":{"s":"This tool is a teaching model, and it is worth being precise about where it stops."}},{"k":"manual_x2","v":{"s":"What the model does get right is the shape of the trade-offs: mechanical advantage buys force by spending distance, a heavy arm steals energy from the payload, and drag is what creates a best projectile mass. Those conclusions are robust. The specific numbers are not predictions about any real machine."}},{"k":"manual_x_dens","v":{"s":"Stone mass and stone size are separate controls, so the tool will let you build an object with a density no material has, and will then simulate it perfectly happily. It tells you when you have done that, but it does not stop you. Real materials come with a density attached, and it is worth remembering that choosing a size chooses a mass too."}},{"k":"manual_x_drag","v":{"s":"Drag uses a single constant coefficient for a smooth sphere. Real projectiles tumble, and their drag changes as they do."}},{"k":"manual_x_fric","v":{"s":"One efficiency figure stands in for all the friction in the winch. A real crew would feel it vary through the pull."}},{"k":"manual_x_tors","v":{"s":"Torsion springs are modelled as linear. Real twisted sinew is strongly nonlinear, loses energy internally on every shot, and behaves differently in damp weather."}},{"k":"manual_x_treb","v":{"s":"The trebuchet is modelled with one degree of freedom. A real one is a double pendulum, and the moment the sling releases is a genuinely hard problem this model does not solve."}},{"k":"meet_note","v":{"s":"The engines are not new machines. They are these six, bolted together."}},{"k":"meet_title","v":{"s":"Where you meet this machine"}},{"k":"metres","v":{"s":"metres"}},{"k":"mismatch","v":{"s":"mismatch"}},{"k":"mission_progress","v":{"s":"Bench progress"}},{"k":"motion_active","v":{"s":"Motion active"}},{"k":"much_easier","v":{"s":"Much easier"}},{"k":"muzzle_unchanged","v":{"s":"Launch speed: "}},{"k":"nav_build","v":{"s":"Build"}},{"k":"nav_compare","v":{"s":"Compare"}},{"k":"nav_learn","v":{"s":"Field Manual"}},{"k":"nav_machines","v":{"s":"Machine Shop"}},{"k":"nav_range","v":{"s":"Test Range"}},{"k":"nav_siege","v":{"s":"Target Wall"}},{"k":"newtons","v":{"s":"newtons"}},{"k":"next_short","v":{"s":"Next: "}},{"k":"next_station","v":{"s":"Next station: "}},{"k":"next_station_open","v":{"s":"Opened the next station: "}},{"k":"no_help","v":{"s":"No help"}},{"k":"no_ledger","v":{"s":"These settings do not describe a working machine yet. Adjust the sliders."}},{"k":"no_target","v":{"s":"Nothing to hit there."}},{"k":"not_modelled","v":{"s":"in the build"}},{"k":"now_exploring","v":{"s":"Now exploring"}},{"k":"observe_lever","v":{"s":"The long effort arm travels farther while the load rises."}},{"k":"observe_pulley","v":{"s":"More supporting rope segments share the load."}},{"k":"observe_ramp","v":{"s":"A longer path reduces the force needed."}},{"k":"observe_screw","v":{"s":"Rotation becomes a small, powerful downward move."}},{"k":"observe_wedge","v":{"s":"Downward effort redirects force out to the sides."}},{"k":"observe_windlass","v":{"s":"The large wheel turns the smaller axle."}},{"k":"off_by","v":{"s":"Not yet. The effort force is "}},{"k":"ona_g35","v":{"s":"An onager has one arm instead of two. All the twisted rope pushes that single arm, and a sling on the end adds extra reach and speed."}},{"k":"ona_g68","v":{"s":"One bundle, one arm. At the same winding it stores half what a two-bundle ballista does, but it only has to accelerate one arm instead of two, so a larger share of that smaller store reaches the stone. Adding a sling lengthens the payload radius and improves the share again. Store and efficiency are two separate things, and this machine trades one for the other."}},{"k":"ona_g912","v":{"s":"Halving the store while halving the arm inertia is not a wash, because efficiency depends on the RATIO m_p/(m_p + m_eff) rather than on either quantity alone. In this model the onager typically shows a higher transfer efficiency than a ballista with the same arm mass, and a lower stored energy, so which one throws further depends on the stone. Lengthening the sling raises the payload radius and lowers the reduced arm inertia, which is the same lever argument the trebuchet makes."}},{"k":"ona_k2","v":{"s":"One arm is held by a twisted rope. It swings up fast and bangs into a padded stop, and the stone keeps going."}},{"k":"onager_sling","v":{"s":"Sling length"}},{"k":"open_bench","v":{"s":"Bench"}},{"k":"open_machine","v":{"s":"Build"}},{"k":"overlay_note","v":{"s":"Dashed arcs are earlier shots: "}},{"k":"part_arm","v":{"s":"the throwing arm"}},{"k":"part_arm_n","v":{"s":"each arm is a lever turning about its bundle, trading a short powerful twist for a long fast sweep"}},{"k":"part_arm_n_k2","v":{"s":"each arm is a lever. The rope twists it back a little way, and the arm swings the stone a long way, fast"}},{"k":"part_arms","v":{"s":"the two spring arms"}},{"k":"part_beam","v":{"s":"the throwing beam"}},{"k":"part_beam_n","v":{"s":"long arm ÷ short arm, so the stone end travels that many times further than the counterweight end"}},{"k":"part_beam_n_k2","v":{"s":"the long end of the beam moves much further than the short end does, so the stone ends up going much faster than the weight"}},{"k":"part_ramp","v":{"s":"the loading ramp"}},{"k":"part_ramp_n","v":{"s":"rolling a stone up a slope instead of lifting it, which is the only way a crew moves it at all"}},{"k":"part_ramp_n_k2","v":{"s":"rolling the stone up a slope instead of lifting it straight up, which is the only way people could move it"}},{"k":"part_screw","v":{"s":"the bundle tensioning gear"}},{"k":"part_screw_n","v":{"s":"tiny turns against a huge load, which is how the springs are tuned at all"}},{"k":"part_screw_n_k2","v":{"s":"small turns of a screw against a very big pull, which is how you tighten the ropes just right"}},{"k":"part_stop","v":{"s":"the trigger and the padded stop"}},{"k":"part_tackle","v":{"s":"the cocking tackle"}},{"k":"part_tackle_n","v":{"s":"every extra rope segment halves the pull again and doubles the rope to haul in"}},{"k":"part_tackle_n_k2","v":{"s":"each extra loop of rope makes the pull half as hard, but you have twice as much rope to pull in"}},{"k":"part_trigger","v":{"s":"the trigger and the ratchet pawl"}},{"k":"part_trigger_n","v":{"s":"a small wedge holding an enormous force, and releasing it the instant you want it gone"}},{"k":"part_trigger_n_k2","v":{"s":"a tiny wedge holds back a huge pull, and lets go the moment you want it to"}},{"k":"part_winch","v":{"s":"the winch drum and handle"}},{"k":"part_winch_n","v":{"s":"a big handle circle turning a small drum, which is why one person can cock the machine"}},{"k":"part_winch_n_k2","v":{"s":"your hand goes round a big circle and the drum only goes round a small one, so one person can pull back a machine this big"}},{"k":"parts_g35","v":{"s":"Every part of this engine is one of the six simple machines from the Machine Shop. Tap one to go and try it on its own."}},{"k":"parts_g68","v":{"s":"Nothing here is new. Every part is one of the six simple machines, and not one of them adds any energy: they only change the exchange rate between force and distance."}},{"k":"parts_g912","v":{"s":"The engine is a composition of the six machines. Each contributes a mechanical advantage to a different stage, and the ones the tool models numerically show their live value here; the rest are present in the mechanism but not in the energy model."}},{"k":"parts_k2","v":{"s":"This big machine is made of the small machines you already know."}},{"k":"parts_title","v":{"s":"Simple machines in this engine"}},{"k":"predict_body","v":{"s":"How far will this machine throw? Write a number before you pull the release."}},{"k":"predict_fire","v":{"s":"Predict, then fire"}},{"k":"proj_dia","v":{"s":"Stone diameter"}},{"k":"proj_mass","v":{"s":"Stone mass"}},{"k":"prove_it","v":{"s":"Prove it"}},{"k":"proven","v":{"s":"proven"}},{"k":"proven_short","v":{"s":"proven"}},{"k":"pulley","v":{"o":[{"k":"copy_g35","v":{"s":"Count the rope segments that actually hold the moving block up. That count is the mechanical advantage. Two segments means half the pull, but twice as much rope to haul in."}},{"k":"copy_g68","v":{"s":"MA equals the number of rope segments supporting the moving block. Effort force = load / MA, and rope pulled = height raised x MA. The rope you pull down on only counts when it runs upward from the moving block."}},{"k":"copy_g912","v":{"s":"The load is shared equally between the supporting segments because the tension in an ideal rope is uniform throughout. Real tackle loses to sheave friction and rope stiffness, typically a few percent per sheave, so a six-part tackle never delivers a true MA of 6."}},{"k":"copy_k2","v":{"s":"A pulley is a wheel with a rope over it. When more pieces of rope hold the bucket, pulling gets easier. But you have to pull a lot more rope."}},{"k":"k2_a","v":{"s":"More ropes holding it up"}},{"k":"k2_b","v":{"s":"Fewer ropes holding it up"}},{"k":"k2_c","v":{"s":"The ropes do not matter"}},{"k":"k2_q","v":{"s":"What makes it easier to pull a heavy bucket up?"}},{"k":"label","v":{"s":"Pulley"}},{"k":"load","v":{"s":"Load"}},{"k":"segments","v":{"s":"Supporting rope segments"}}],"id":621}},{"k":"ramp","v":{"o":[{"k":"copy_g35","v":{"s":"Divide the ramp length by its height. A ramp 4 m long that rises 1 m gives you 4 times the push, but you travel 4 m instead of lifting straight up 1 m."}},{"k":"copy_g68","v":{"s":"MA = length / height. The force you need along the ramp is weight x height / length. Notice the work is identical either way: weight x height, whether you lift straight up or push along the slope."}},{"k":"copy_g912","v":{"s":"Resolving the weight along the slope gives F = W sin(theta), and sin(theta) = h / L, so MA = 1 / sin(theta) = L / h. This is the frictionless ideal. Adding a coefficient of friction mu gives F = W(sin theta + mu cos theta), which is why a real ramp has a shallowest useful angle."}},{"k":"copy_k2","v":{"s":"A ramp helps you move heavy things up. A long gentle ramp is easier than a short steep one, but you have to walk a lot further."}},{"k":"height","v":{"s":"Ramp height"}},{"k":"k2_a","v":{"s":"A long, gentle ramp"}},{"k":"k2_b","v":{"s":"A short, steep ramp"}},{"k":"k2_c","v":{"s":"Both feel exactly the same"}},{"k":"k2_q","v":{"s":"You are pushing a heavy box up to a porch. Which ramp is easier?"}},{"k":"label","v":{"s":"Inclined Plane"}},{"k":"length","v":{"s":"Ramp length"}},{"k":"load","v":{"s":"Weight"}}],"id":622}},{"k":"range_fired_lane","v":{"s":"Fired result"}},{"k":"range_gl_failed","v":{"s":"3D range unavailable. The graph below carries the same path."}},{"k":"range_gl_loading","v":{"s":"Opening the 3D range lane..."}},{"k":"range_hit","v":{"s":"Within 10%. It flew "}},{"k":"range_in_flight","v":{"s":"Stone in flight"}},{"k":"range_lane","v":{"s":"3D range lane"}},{"k":"range_lbl","v":{"s":"Range: "}},{"k":"range_live_lane","v":{"s":"Live range lane"}},{"k":"range_miss","v":{"s":"It flew "}},{"k":"range_prediction_locked","v":{"s":"Prediction locked"}},{"k":"range_world_apex","v":{"s":"Apex "}},{"k":"range_world_flag","v":{"s":"Impact flag"}},{"k":"range_world_metric","v":{"s":"Landing distance"}},{"k":"range_world_path","v":{"s":"Computed path"}},{"k":"range_world_predict","v":{"s":"Predict to reveal the path"}},{"k":"range_world_prompt","v":{"s":"Make your prediction, then fire to reveal the trajectory."}},{"k":"re_explain","v":{"s":"Explain again"}},{"k":"read_aloud","v":{"s":"Read aloud"}},{"k":"reading_level","v":{"s":"Level:"}},{"k":"rebuild","v":{"s":"Rebuild the wall"}},{"k":"rec_best","v":{"s":"; furthest was "}},{"k":"rec_best2","v":{"s":" m with a "}},{"k":"rec_best_odd","v":{"s":", which was not a real rock"}},{"k":"rec_breached","v":{"s":", breached"}},{"k":"rec_copied","v":{"s":"Work record copied."}},{"k":"rec_copy","v":{"s":"Copy this record"}},{"k":"rec_copyfail","v":{"s":"Could not copy. Select the text and copy it by hand."}},{"k":"rec_exp","v":{"s":"Explanation: "}},{"k":"rec_head","v":{"s":"Machine Lab — work record"}},{"k":"rec_held","v":{"s":", wall held"}},{"k":"rec_hyp","v":{"s":"Hypothesis: "}},{"k":"rec_intro","v":{"s":"Everything you have done in this session, gathered in one place. It is a record of your work, not a mark, and nothing here is scored."}},{"k":"rec_l1","v":{"s":"Benches proven: "}},{"k":"rec_l2","v":{"s":"Best prediction streak: "}},{"k":"rec_l3","v":{"s":"Machines fired: "}},{"k":"rec_l4","v":{"s":"Shots logged: "}},{"k":"rec_l5","v":{"s":"Siege: "}},{"k":"rec_l5b","v":{"s":" shots, "}},{"k":"rec_l5c","v":{"s":" kJ of crank work"}},{"k":"rec_level","v":{"s":"Reading level: "}},{"k":"rec_none","v":{"s":"none yet"}},{"k":"rec_odd","v":{"s":"Note: "}},{"k":"rec_odd1","v":{"s":" of those shots used a stone whose weight and size do not match any real rock, so its range is not a real one."}},{"k":"rec_odd2","v":{"s":" of those shots used stones whose weight and size do not match any real rock, so those ranges are not real ones."}},{"k":"rec_sweep","v":{"s":"Best stone searched for: "}},{"k":"rec_sweep2","v":{"s":" (each machine wants a different one)"}},{"k":"release_angle","v":{"s":"Release angle"}},{"k":"right","v":{"s":"That is right. More distance, less force."}},{"k":"run_demo","v":{"s":"Run demonstration"}},{"k":"run_demo_aria","v":{"s":"Run the three-dimensional demonstration for "}},{"k":"save_design","v":{"s":"Save this design"}},{"k":"save_failed","v":{"s":"That design could not be saved."}},{"k":"save_nofire","v":{"s":"not firing"}},{"k":"save_unavailable","v":{"s":"Saving is not available here."}},{"k":"saved","v":{"s":"Design saved: "}},{"k":"screw","v":{"o":[{"k":"copy_g35","v":{"s":"Each full turn moves the screw forward by the gap between two ridges, called the pitch. Your hand travels all the way around the circle to do it, and that long trip is what makes the push so strong."}},{"k":"copy_g68","v":{"s":"MA = 2 pi R / pitch, where R is the radius of your handle or driver. Screws have the largest mechanical advantage of the six machines by a wide margin, which is why a car jack is a screw."}},{"k":"copy_g912","v":{"s":"Unwrapping one turn of the thread gives an inclined plane of base 2 pi R and rise equal to the pitch, so MA = 2 pi R / p directly. Real screw efficiency is low, often under 30 percent, because thread friction is large. That inefficiency is a feature: it is what makes a screw jack self-locking under load rather than unwinding."}},{"k":"copy_k2","v":{"s":"A screw is a ramp wrapped around a stick. Going around and around the long way is easier than pushing straight in, which is why a screw holds better than a nail you just hammer."}},{"k":"handle_r","v":{"s":"Handle radius"}},{"k":"k2_a","v":{"s":"Ridges close together"}},{"k":"k2_b","v":{"s":"Ridges far apart"}},{"k":"k2_c","v":{"s":"Ridges are just decoration"}},{"k":"k2_q","v":{"s":"A screw with which kind of ridges is easier to turn into wood?"}},{"k":"label","v":{"s":"Screw"}},{"k":"load","v":{"s":"Load"}},{"k":"pitch","v":{"s":"Thread pitch"}}],"id":623}},{"k":"shop_gl_failed","v":{"s":"3D workshop unavailable. This live diagram carries the same geometry."}},{"k":"shop_gl_loading","v":{"s":"Opening the 3D workshop..."}},{"k":"shot_log","v":{"s":"Shot log"}},{"k":"show_bars","v":{"s":"Show bars"}},{"k":"show_courses","v":{"s":"Show courses"}},{"k":"show_past","v":{"s":"Show earlier shots"}},{"k":"show_table","v":{"s":"Show table"}},{"k":"siege_stats","v":{"s":"The siege"}},{"k":"signal_aria","v":{"s":"3D yard signal lights"}},{"k":"signal_hint","v":{"s":"The lights mirror the energy story."}},{"k":"signal_ready","v":{"s":"ready"}},{"k":"signal_release","v":{"s":"release"}},{"k":"signal_stored","v":{"s":"stored energy"}},{"k":"signal_title","v":{"s":"Scene signals"}},{"k":"sling","v":{"s":"Sling length"}},{"k":"sr_breach","v":{"s":"The wall is breached."}},{"k":"sr_fired","v":{"s":"Fired. Range "}},{"k":"sr_imported","v":{"s":"Your Architecture Studio build is now the target."}},{"k":"sr_level","v":{"s":", reading level "}},{"k":"sr_ma","v":{"s":", mechanical advantage "}},{"k":"sr_metres","v":{"s":" metres, impact energy "}},{"k":"sr_saved","v":{"s":"Design saved as "}},{"k":"sr_short","v":{"s":"The shot fell short."}},{"k":"sr_summary","v":{"s":"Machine Lab, "}},{"k":"st_reach","v":{"s":"This machine reaches"}},{"k":"st_short","v":{"s":"Short by"}},{"k":"st_shots","v":{"s":"Shots loosed"}},{"k":"st_wallh","v":{"s":"Wall height"}},{"k":"st_work","v":{"s":"Total crank work"}},{"k":"stage_crank","v":{"s":"Work you do at the crank"}},{"k":"stage_crank_k2","v":{"s":"How hard you work at the handle"}},{"k":"stage_impact","v":{"s":"Kinetic energy at impact"}},{"k":"stage_impact_k2","v":{"s":"Energy the stone has when it lands"}},{"k":"stage_muzzle","v":{"s":"Kinetic energy of the stone at release"}},{"k":"stage_muzzle_k2","v":{"s":"Energy the stone has as it flies off"}},{"k":"stage_stored","v":{"s":"Stored in the raised counterweight"}},{"k":"stage_stored_ball","v":{"s":"Stored in the two twisted bundles"}},{"k":"stage_stored_ball_k2","v":{"s":"Saved up in the two twisted ropes"}},{"k":"stage_stored_k2","v":{"s":"Saved up in the lifted weight"}},{"k":"stage_stored_ona","v":{"s":"Stored in the twisted bundle"}},{"k":"stage_stored_ona_k2","v":{"s":"Saved up in the twisted rope"}},{"k":"stale_shot","v":{"s":"Current settings changed. Fire again to reveal the new result."}},{"k":"standoff","v":{"s":"Standoff from the wall"}},{"k":"station","v":{"s":"Station "}},{"k":"station_flow","v":{"s":"Station workflow: adjust, run, prove"}},{"k":"step_adjust","v":{"s":"Adjust"}},{"k":"step_prove","v":{"s":"Prove"}},{"k":"step_run","v":{"s":"Run"}},{"k":"stone_density","v":{"s":"That stone works out at "}},{"k":"stone_density2","v":{"s":" kg per cubic metre, "}},{"k":"stone_g35","v":{"s":"A rock that size would weigh about "}},{"k":"stone_g35b","v":{"s":" kg. Yours weighs "}},{"k":"stone_g35c","v":{"s":" kg, so it is "}},{"k":"stone_g912","v":{"s":". Granite is about 2700, so a rock this size would be "}},{"k":"stone_k2","v":{"s":"A real stone this big would weigh about "}},{"k":"stone_k2b","v":{"s":" kg. Yours weighs "}},{"k":"stone_odd","v":{"s":"No rock is that. Mass and size are separate sliders here, so it is easy to build something that could not exist. Air resistance depends on how big it is and inertia on how heavy, so an impossible stone will give you an impossible range."}},{"k":"stone_odd_g35","v":{"s":"No rock weighs that for its size. The two sliders move on their own, so it is easy to build a stone that could not really exist. If the stone is not real, the throw will not be real either."}},{"k":"stone_odd_g912","v":{"s":"No rock has that density. Because mass and diameter are set independently here, the two quantities drag depends on, frontal area and inertia, can be varied against each other in ways no material allows. Any range you read off an impossible object tells you about the model, not about a machine."}},{"k":"stone_odd_k2","v":{"s":"That is far too light for a stone that size. A rock that big could not float away. Try a heavier stone, or a smaller one."}},{"k":"stone_odd_k2h","v":{"s":"That is far too heavy for a stone that size. Nothing is that heavy. Try a bigger stone, or a lighter one."}},{"k":"stone_odd_short","v":{"s":"Your stone is "}},{"k":"stone_odd_short2","v":{"s":" kg and "}},{"k":"stone_odd_short2b","v":{"s":" m across"}},{"k":"stone_odd_short3","v":{"s":", which works out at "}},{"k":"stone_odd_short4","v":{"s":" kg per cubic metre. No rock is that, so treat these numbers as a story about an object that could not exist. The two sliders are in Build."}},{"k":"stone_odd_short_g35","v":{"s":". No rock weighs that for its size, so these numbers describe something that could not really exist. The two sliders are in Build."}},{"k":"stone_odd_short_g912","v":{"s":" kg per cubic metre. No rock is that, so every figure below is conditioned on an object no material could form. The two sliders are in Build."}},{"k":"stone_odd_short_k2","v":{"s":"Your stone is "}},{"k":"stone_odd_short_k2b","v":{"s":". A real stone that big would weigh about "}},{"k":"stone_odd_short_k2c","v":{"s":" kg, so this one is not really a stone. You can change it in Build."}},{"k":"store_gravity","v":{"s":"falling weight"}},{"k":"store_torsion","v":{"s":"twisted rope"}},{"k":"string_mass","v":{"s":"String mass"}},{"k":"struck","v":{"s":"Struck the "}},{"k":"struck2","v":{"s":" at course "}},{"k":"struck3","v":{"s":", delivering "}},{"k":"struck4","v":{"s":" J."}},{"k":"subtitle","v":{"s":"Six simple machines. One idea: trade distance for force."}},{"k":"sweep_done","v":{"s":"Best stone found for "}},{"k":"sweep_done2","v":{"s":" of the three machines, at the rock density you are already using."}},{"k":"sweep_none","v":{"s":"None of the three machines can throw anything at these settings."}},{"k":"sweep_nostone","v":{"s":"Set a stone mass and size first."}},{"k":"test_fire","v":{"s":"Test fire"}},{"k":"test_fire_note","v":{"s":"Watch the arm. Range and full numbers are in the Test Range."}},{"k":"the_trade","v":{"s":"The trade"}},{"k":"the_winch","v":{"s":"The winch"}},{"k":"thinking","v":{"s":"Thinking..."}},{"k":"time_lbl","v":{"s":"Flight time: "}},{"k":"title","v":{"s":"Machine Lab"}},{"k":"topic_energy","v":{"s":"Where the energy goes"}},{"k":"topic_history","v":{"s":"History and evidence"}},{"k":"topic_machines","v":{"s":"The six machines"}},{"k":"topic_model","v":{"s":"What this model is not"}},{"k":"topic_record","v":{"s":"Your work"}},{"k":"trade_body","v":{"s":"Mechanical advantage trades distance for force. It never creates energy."}},{"k":"transfer_eff","v":{"s":"Transfer efficiency: "}},{"k":"transfer_eff_g35","v":{"s":"The stone got "}},{"k":"transfer_eff_k2","v":{"s":"Out of all the energy the machine saved up, "}},{"k":"try_again","v":{"s":"Not quite. Try moving the sliders and watching what gets easier."}},{"k":"tune_station","v":{"s":"Tune this station"}},{"k":"turns","v":{"s":"Turns of twist in the bundle"}},{"k":"tut1","v":{"s":"Welcome to Machine Lab. Start in the Machine Shop: six simple machines, one idea. Mechanical advantage trades distance for force and never creates energy."}},{"k":"tut1_g35","v":{"s":"Welcome to Machine Lab! Start in the Machine Shop: six simple machines, each one trading distance for force."}},{"k":"tut1_g912","v":{"s":"Welcome to Machine Lab. The Machine Shop establishes the six ideal machines and their mechanical advantages; everything after it is those six composed into a real engine."}},{"k":"tut1_k2","v":{"s":"Welcome to Machine Lab! Start in the Machine Shop. Six simple machines, and every one of them helps you push less hard."}},{"k":"tut2","v":{"s":"Then open Build. A trebuchet, a ballista and an onager are not new machines: the panel there names every part as one of the six you just met, and takes you back to its bench."}},{"k":"tut3","v":{"s":"Watch the energy ledger beside the machine. Follow the joules from the crank to the stone, and see exactly where each one is lost."}},{"k":"tut4","v":{"s":"In the Test Range, predict the distance before you fire. Try a very light stone and a very heavy one: the fastest shot is not the furthest."}},{"k":"tut5","v":{"s":"At the Target Wall, aim flat. A high lob sails clean over a wall; walls are battered with direct fire."}},{"k":"typed_q","v":{"s":"Predict the effort force these settings need, in newtons. Do it before you read the panel above."}},{"k":"vacuum_note","v":{"s":"Turn the air off and sweep the stone mass: the range now falls steadily as mass rises, with no best value. The sweet spot you find with air on is a fact about drag, not about levers."}},{"k":"wall_caption","v":{"s":"Condition of each course, counting up from the ground"}},{"k":"wall_curtain","v":{"s":"Curtain wall"}},{"k":"wall_curtain_l","v":{"s":"A plain wall. Energy per hit against the block budget, nothing else going on."}},{"k":"wall_gatehouse","v":{"s":"Gatehouse"}},{"k":"wall_gatehouse_l","v":{"s":"The arch carries its load sideways into the stones beside the opening. Take one of those away and only that half of the arch comes down."}},{"k":"wall_gl_failed","v":{"s":"3D wall unavailable. The diagram below is the same wall."}},{"k":"wall_gl_loading","v":{"s":"Loading the 3D wall..."}},{"k":"wall_imported","v":{"s":"Your own build"}},{"k":"wall_imported_l","v":{"s":"This is the castle you built in Architecture Studio, seen face on. Depth counts as strength here: where you stacked the wall thicker, it takes proportionally more energy to break through."}},{"k":"wall_keep","v":{"s":"Keep"}},{"k":"wall_keep_l","v":{"s":"Granite, and ten courses of it. Where you aim matters more than how hard you throw."}},{"k":"wall_motte","v":{"s":"Motte and tower"}},{"k":"wall_motte_l","v":{"s":"The tower stands on an earth mound. Earth gives way far sooner than stone does, and everything above it follows."}},{"k":"wall_state","v":{"s":"Wall state"}},{"k":"watch_motion","v":{"s":"Watch the motion"}},{"k":"wedge","v":{"o":[{"k":"copy_g35","v":{"s":"Divide the wedge length by how thick it is at the back. A long slim wedge has a big number, so it pushes the log apart harder for the same hammer blow."}},{"k":"copy_g68","v":{"s":"MA = length / thickness. A wedge is an inclined plane that moves through the material instead of the load moving along it. The trade is the same: you drive it a long way in to push the halves apart a little."}},{"k":"copy_g912","v":{"s":"The ideal MA is purely geometric, but wedges are the least ideal of the six machines in practice. Friction between the faces and the material usually dominates, and is often what stops the wedge springing back out, so a splitting wedge deliberately trades efficiency for that self-holding behaviour."}},{"k":"copy_k2","v":{"s":"A wedge is a ramp that moves. An axe, a knife and your front teeth are all wedges. Long thin ones push things apart more easily than short fat ones."}},{"k":"k2_a","v":{"s":"A long, thin wedge"}},{"k":"k2_b","v":{"s":"A short, fat wedge"}},{"k":"k2_c","v":{"s":"Shape does not change anything"}},{"k":"k2_q","v":{"s":"Which wedge splits a log more easily?"}},{"k":"label","v":{"s":"Wedge"}},{"k":"length","v":{"s":"Wedge length"}},{"k":"load","v":{"s":"Splitting resistance"}},{"k":"thickness","v":{"s":"Wedge thickness"}}],"id":624}},{"k":"went_over","v":{"s":"Over the top. Lower the release angle or take some energy out."}},{"k":"went_wide","v":{"s":"Wide of the wall by "}},{"k":"went_wide_calm","v":{"s":" m."}},{"k":"went_wide_wind","v":{"s":" m. The crosswind is pushing it sideways; aim off into the wind or wait for it to drop."}},{"k":"what_to_notice","v":{"s":"What to notice"}},{"k":"winch_body","v":{"s":"Gearing the winch changes how hard you crank and how many turns it takes. Watch what it does to the shot."}},{"k":"winch_body_g35","v":{"s":"Changing the handle and the drum changes how hard you pull and how many turns it takes. See what it does to the shot, and what it does not do."}},{"k":"winch_body_k2","v":{"s":"The handle and the drum decide how hard you have to pull and how many times you have to turn. Change them and watch what happens to the throw."}},{"k":"winch_drum","v":{"s":"Winch drum radius"}},{"k":"winch_handle","v":{"s":"Crank handle radius"}},{"k":"winch_hint","v":{"s":"Change the gearing and watch: the first three numbers move, the launch speed does not."}},{"k":"winch_hint_g35","v":{"s":"Change the gearing and watch. The first three numbers move. The launch speed does not, because gearing changes how you do the work, not how much of it there is."}},{"k":"winch_hint_k2","v":{"s":"Try it: the first numbers change, but the launch speed stays the same. The winch decides how easy the work is, not how far the stone goes."}},{"k":"winch_ma2","v":{"s":"Winch mechanical advantage: "}},{"k":"winch_ma_gloss","v":{"s":"That means the winch pulls "}},{"k":"winch_ma_gloss2","v":{"s":" times harder than you do."}},{"k":"winch_pulleys","v":{"s":"Pulleys in the tackle"}},{"k":"wind","v":{"s":"Crosswind"}},{"k":"wind_g35","v":{"s":"A crosswind blows the stone off to one side. The longer it is in the air, the further it drifts."}},{"k":"wind_g68","v":{"s":"Drag acts on the stone’s speed THROUGH THE AIR, not over the ground, so a crosswind pushes it sideways for the whole flight. Slow, light stones drift most."}},{"k":"wind_g912","v":{"s":"The drag term uses velocity relative to the air mass, so a steady crosswind produces lateral acceleration until the stone matches the air sideways. Drift therefore grows with flight time and falls as the ballistic coefficient rises."}},{"k":"wind_k2","v":{"s":"Wind pushes the stone sideways while it flies."}},{"k":"windlass","v":{"o":[{"k":"copy_g35","v":{"s":"The handle sweeps a big circle while the drum winds up a small one. Divide the handle radius by the drum radius to see how many times your turn is multiplied."}},{"k":"copy_g68","v":{"s":"MA = R_handle / r_drum. One full turn moves your hand 2 pi R while the rope winds only 2 pi r, so the extra distance is exactly where the extra force comes from."}},{"k":"copy_g912","v":{"s":"This is a continuous lever: the torque balance is F_effort x R = F_load x r. Every rotation restates the same moment equation as the lever bench, which is why the two formulas look identical once you write them as ratios of radii."}},{"k":"copy_k2","v":{"s":"A big wheel turning a small one helps you lift. Think of a doorknob: the round part is wide, so it is easy to turn the skinny bit inside."}},{"k":"drum_r","v":{"s":"Drum radius"}},{"k":"handle_r","v":{"s":"Handle radius"}},{"k":"k2_a","v":{"s":"A big handle to turn"}},{"k":"k2_b","v":{"s":"A tiny handle to turn"}},{"k":"k2_c","v":{"s":"Handle size does not matter"}},{"k":"k2_q","v":{"s":"You are winding a bucket up from a well. What makes it easiest?"}},{"k":"label","v":{"s":"Wheel & Axle"}},{"k":"load","v":{"s":"Load"}}],"id":625}},{"k":"work_in","v":{"s":"Work in: "}},{"k":"work_out","v":{"s":"Work out: "}},{"k":"workshop","v":{"s":"simple-machine workshop"}},{"k":"you_move","v":{"s":"Your hand moves"}}],"id":619}},{"k":"organismid","v":{"o":[{"k":"aria_details_for","v":{"s":"Details for"}},{"k":"aria_legend","v":{"s":"Hazard tier legend"}},{"k":"aria_main","v":{"s":"Taxonomy Explorer"}},{"k":"aria_tabs","v":{"s":"Taxonomy Explorer views"}},{"k":"aria_tree","v":{"s":"Tree of life"}},{"k":"blanket_rule","v":{"s":"Blanket rule"}},{"k":"but_may_actually_be","v":{"s":"But may actually be"}},{"k":"confused_with","v":{"s":"Confused with"}},{"k":"footer","v":{"s":"Taxonomy Explorer · Ranks are conventions · No photograph makes a wild organism safe"}},{"k":"groups_intro","v":{"s":"The same organisms, sorted by what a mistake costs rather than by ancestry. A warning fires on the stakes of being wrong, never on how confident an identification feels."}},{"k":"kicker","v":{"s":"CLASSIFICATION"}},{"k":"ladder_note","v":{"s":"An honest identification narrows as it descends: confident at kingdom, hedged at species. A tool that reports the same confidence at every rank is not telling you the truth."}},{"k":"ladder_title","v":{"s":"The seven ranks, narrowing"}},{"k":"learn_intro","v":{"s":"Five things about classification that textbooks tend to state too confidently."}},{"k":"lookalikes_intro","v":{"s":"Pairs that fool people. Read the tell, then find both in the tree — several of these pairs are not even close relatives, which is the whole lesson."}},{"k":"often_taken_for","v":{"s":"Often taken for"}},{"k":"photo_pending_1","v":{"s":"Built and passing: 46 tests, offline safety fallback, EXIF and GPS scrubbing before any image leaves the device."}},{"k":"photo_pending_2","v":{"s":"Blocked on: expert sign-off for 24 deadly and 8 contact-hazard entries."}},{"k":"photo_pending_3","v":{"s":"Meanwhile: everything in this tool teaches the reasoning the photo path depends on."}},{"k":"photo_pending_body","v":{"s":"The identification engine is built and tested: a photograph goes in, and a ranked list of candidates comes back with a confidence ladder, verified GBIF and Wikipedia links, and warnings that fire on how bad a mistake would be rather than on how sure the model feels."}},{"k":"photo_pending_title","v":{"s":"Photo identification is not switched on yet"}},{"k":"photo_pending_why","v":{"s":"It stays off because its deadly-organism warnings have not been reviewed by a mycologist or naturalist. Copy that tells a child which mushroom will kill them has to be signed off by a person who knows, not shipped because the code passes its tests."}},{"k":"species_in_genus","v":{"s":"Species in this genus"}},{"k":"subtitle","v":{"s":"How biologists sort life into boxes, why the boxes keep moving, and why a lookalike can be the difference between dinner and a liver transplant."}},{"k":"title","v":{"s":"Taxonomy Explorer"}},{"k":"tree_intro","v":{"s":"Walk the ranked tree. Coloured dots mark where a hazard rule attaches — notice how often a deadly branch sits one rank away from an edible one."}},{"k":"where_it_sits","v":{"s":"Where it sits"}}],"id":626}},{"k":"paperTrail","v":{"o":[{"k":"asking","v":{"s":"What they are actually asking"}},{"k":"back_home","v":{"s":"PaperTrail"}},{"k":"choose","v":{"s":"Choose a response"}},{"k":"considered_sr","v":{"s":"Choice recorded. What follows from it is shown below."}},{"k":"disclosure_sub","v":{"s":"These are not scored. Every option below is a real choice someone might make, with a real consequence — pick the one you would actually make, then read what follows from it."}},{"k":"disclosure_title","v":{"s":"Disclosure decisions"}},{"k":"doc_foot","v":{"s":"Real versions of these documents differ by employer, landlord, and state. The questions they ask are remarkably consistent."}},{"k":"doc_sub","v":{"s":"Each row is a field on the real document. Open one to see what it is actually asking and how Sam filled it in."}},{"k":"documents","v":{"s":"Documents"}},{"k":"fields","v":{"s":"fields"}},{"k":"good_sr","v":{"s":"That is the protective choice. Explanation below."}},{"k":"intro","v":{"s":"Adult life runs on documents nobody teaches you to read. Pick one and go field by field: what each box is really asking, which ones can cost you, and what to say when someone wants you to sign right now."}},{"k":"kind_danger","v":{"s":"This one can cost you"}},{"k":"kind_normal","v":{"s":"Standard"}},{"k":"kind_watch","v":{"s":"Read carefully"}},{"k":"next","v":{"s":"Next scenario →"}},{"k":"next_case","v":{"s":"Next situation →"}},{"k":"pressure","v":{"s":"Pressure scenarios"}},{"k":"pressure_sub","v":{"s":"What to do when someone wants you to sign now."}},{"k":"read_law","v":{"s":"Read the actual text of "}},{"k":"read_law2","v":{"s":" in the Education Law Navigator — nothing there is paraphrased."}},{"k":"risky_sr","v":{"s":"That one carries risk. Explanation below."}},{"k":"safety","v":{"s":"Practice only. Every example here is filled in for a made-up person, Sam Rivera. Never type your real Social Security number, bank details, or passwords into a practice tool — including this one."}},{"k":"sam_wrote","v":{"s":"Sam wrote: "}},{"k":"scen_done","v":{"s":"All scenarios done. The pattern: the pressure to decide now is itself the warning sign, and asking for time is always allowed."}},{"k":"scripts","v":{"s":"What to say"}},{"k":"scripts_foot","v":{"s":"If someone refuses all six, that refusal is information about them, not about you."}},{"k":"scripts_intro","v":{"s":"Asking for time is a skill, not an admission that you cannot read. These six sentences work in almost every room. Say them plainly; you do not need to apologize."}},{"k":"scripts_sub","v":{"s":"Six sentences that buy you time. Asking is a skill."}},{"k":"title","v":{"s":"PaperTrail: Official Documents"}},{"k":"tools","v":{"s":"Tools"}},{"k":"work_done","v":{"s":"All four considered. The through-line: nothing is automatic after school, and asking early is usually cheaper than recovering later."}},{"k":"work_intro","v":{"s":"School protections do not follow you to work. What replaces them is request-driven, which means knowing what to ask for is the whole skill."}},{"k":"work_sub","v":{"s":"What replaces your school plan after graduation, how to ask for what you need, and whether to disclose at all."}},{"k":"work_title","v":{"s":"Work rights & disclosure"}}],"id":627}},{"k":"treelab","v":{"o":[{"k":"a11y_campaign_tree_in_3d","v":{"s":"Campaign tree in 3D"}},{"k":"a11y_campaign_camera_controls","v":{"s":"Campaign camera controls"}},{"k":"a11y_inspect_campaign_tree_parts","v":{"s":"Inspect campaign tree parts"}},{"k":"a11y_where_it_happened","v":{"s":"Where it happened"}},{"k":"a11y_earlier_runs_of_this_grove","v":{"s":"Earlier runs of this grove"}},{"k":"a11y_grove_campaign","v":{"s":"Grove campaign"}},{"k":"a11y_years_completed","v":{"s":"Years completed"}},{"k":"a11y_grove_view","v":{"s":"Grove view"}},{"k":"a11y_grove_habitat_patches","v":{"s":"Grove habitat patches"}},{"k":"a11y_selected_patch","v":{"s":"Selected patch"}},{"k":"a11y_journey_decisions","v":{"s":"Journey decisions"}},{"k":"a11y_latest_year_evidence","v":{"s":"Latest year evidence"}},{"k":"a11y_journey_timeline","v":{"s":"Journey timeline"}},{"k":"after_years","v":{"s":"after "}},{"k":"age","v":{"s":"age"}},{"k":"age_label","v":{"s":"Age"}},{"k":"all_clonal","v":{"s":"Every descendant this round is a genetic copy sharing one root system. That is reliable now and fragile against anything that beats this exact genotype."}},{"k":"all_seed","v":{"s":"Every descendant came from seed, so each one is genetically different and landed away from the parent. You paid for that in how few of them took."}},{"k":"alloc_strip_alt","v":{"s":"How the surplus divides: "}},{"k":"alt_3d","v":{"s":"Three-dimensional "}},{"k":"alt_clonal_stems","v":{"s":"clonal stems."}},{"k":"alt_dead","v":{"s":"The tree is dead and its bare frame remains visible."}},{"k":"alt_growth_rings","v":{"s":"growth rings"}},{"k":"alt_kgc_heartwood","v":{"s":"kg of carbon in dead heartwood."}},{"k":"alt_kgc_left","v":{"s":"kg C left to grow with."}},{"k":"alt_kgc_made","v":{"s":"kg C made"}},{"k":"alt_kgc_maint","v":{"s":"kg C spent on maintenance"}},{"k":"alt_kgc_reserves","v":{"s":"kg C drawn from reserves."}},{"k":"alt_limiting_now","v":{"s":"Current limiting factor: "}},{"k":"alt_mild_stress","v":{"s":"Its foliage shows mild water stress."}},{"k":"alt_rings_pre","v":{"s":"Ring width for the last "}},{"k":"alt_rings_widest","v":{"s":"Widest ring "}},{"k":"alt_tall_with","v":{"s":"metres tall, with "}},{"k":"alt_thinned","v":{"s":"Its canopy is thinned by a chronic carbon deficit."}},{"k":"alt_view_of","v":{"s":"view of "}},{"k":"alt_wilted","v":{"s":"Its leaves are visibly wilted by water stress."}},{"k":"anatomy_controls","v":{"s":"Tree anatomy"}},{"k":"banked","v":{"s":"Carbon banked"}},{"k":"banked_short","v":{"s":"banked"}},{"k":"begin_investigation","v":{"s":"Start investigation"}},{"k":"bill_body","v":{"s":"Converting sapwood to heartwood is how a tree keeps getting bigger without its maintenance cost rising forever. Dead wood still holds the tree up and costs nothing to keep."}},{"k":"budget_bar_alt","v":{"s":"Budget bar. "}},{"k":"budget_bar_credit","v":{"s":"Spent to stay alive · left to grow with"}},{"k":"budget_bar_deficit","v":{"s":"Respiration exceeds what was made; the difference is drawn from reserves."}},{"k":"budget_sub_g68","v":{"s":"Gross photosynthesis minus maintenance respiration is what is left to grow with. Everything below is spent out of that surplus."}},{"k":"budget_sub_k2","v":{"s":"Sugar made, minus sugar used just to stay alive. What is left is what the tree can grow with."}},{"k":"cancel","v":{"s":"Cancel"}},{"k":"check","v":{"s":"Knowledge check"}},{"k":"check_sub","v":{"s":"Question "}},{"k":"choose_factor","v":{"s":"Choose a factor"}},{"k":"choose_outcome","v":{"s":"Choose an outcome"}},{"k":"clear","v":{"s":"Clear"}},{"k":"clear_trial","v":{"s":"Clear trial"}},{"k":"clock_stopped","v":{"s":"The clock stopped when the tree died. Start a new seedling to run it again."}},{"k":"clonal","v":{"s":"Clonal copies"}},{"k":"close","v":{"s":"Close"}},{"k":"cm_across","v":{"s":"cm across"}},{"k":"cmp_clonal","v":{"s":"Can copy itself without seeds. "}},{"k":"cmp_life","v":{"s":"Lifespan about "}},{"k":"cmp_max","v":{"s":"tops out near "}},{"k":"cmp_seed","v":{"s":"Seed only — no clonal route. "}},{"k":"commit","v":{"s":"Commit carbon"}},{"k":"committed","v":{"s":"Committed"}},{"k":"compare","v":{"s":"Five strategies, one set of conditions"}},{"k":"compare_alt","v":{"s":"Compare alt"}},{"k":"compare_caption","v":{"s":"Trial evidence; difference is Trial B minus Trial A."}},{"k":"compare_key","v":{"s":"A cross is where a run ended. Every figure is also written out species by species below."}},{"k":"compare_note","v":{"s":"One run each, under one set of conditions. A species that loses here is not a worse tree — it is a tree built for different conditions. Change the light or the water on the Grow tab and the order can change."}},{"k":"compare_sub_g68","v":{"s":"Every species below is grown under exactly the conditions and the allocation you set on the Grow tab. Nothing else differs, so what you see is the strategy each one is built around."}},{"k":"compare_sub_k2","v":{"s":"The same weather for all five trees. They still grow differently."}},{"k":"compare_years","v":{"s":"Years to run"}},{"k":"conditions","v":{"s":"Conditions"}},{"k":"conditions_frozen","v":{"s":"The treatment is frozen. Run uses the saved starting tree even if the live tree changes later."}},{"k":"conditions_sub","v":{"s":"Change one thing at a time and watch which factor takes over as the limit."}},{"k":"controlled_pair","v":{"s":"Controlled pair: both trials began with the same species, age and height."}},{"k":"correct","v":{"s":"Correct."}},{"k":"cost","v":{"s":"Cost "}},{"k":"curve_alt_headroom","v":{"s":"At its best value this factor alone would add "}},{"k":"curves_note","v":{"s":"Curves note"}},{"k":"curves_read","v":{"s":"The flat panels are the ones where this tree already has more than it can use. The marked one is where the next improvement would actually come from."}},{"k":"curves_read_stomata","v":{"s":"Curves read stomata"}},{"k":"curves_sub_g68","v":{"s":"Each panel sweeps ONE condition across its whole range and leaves the other three where you set them. Upward on every panel is gross photosynthesis in kg of carbon a year, on one shared scale. The dot is where this tree is standing, and a curve that has gone flat under the dot is telling you that more of that input buys nothing."}},{"k":"curves_sub_k2","v":{"s":"Each picture shows what happens if you change just one thing. Higher means more sugar made. The dot is where your tree is now."}},{"k":"curves_title","v":{"s":"What happens if you change one thing"}},{"k":"dead_budget","v":{"s":"Nothing. A dead tree makes no sugar and spends none. Its stored carbon stays in the wood."}},{"k":"dead_chip","v":{"s":"This tree has died"}},{"k":"decades","v":{"s":"Decades run"}},{"k":"died_at","v":{"s":"died at "}},{"k":"diff_alloc","v":{"s":"Carbon allocation"}},{"k":"diff_drought","v":{"s":"Drought schedule"}},{"k":"difference","v":{"s":"Difference"}},{"k":"diversity","v":{"s":"Genetic diversity"}},{"k":"drought_3","v":{"s":"Drought for 3 years"}},{"k":"drought_8","v":{"s":"Drought for 8 years"}},{"k":"drought_banner","v":{"s":"Drought year. The tree has closed its stomata to save water, so it is taking in very little carbon."}},{"k":"drought_chip","v":{"s":"Drought"}},{"k":"drought_off","v":{"s":"Send a dry spell and watch what it does to the ring and to the limiting factor."}},{"k":"drought_on","v":{"s":"A drought is running. Soil water is a third of what you set, the stomata are closing, and the ring this year will show it."}},{"k":"drought_over","v":{"s":"The rains return."}},{"k":"drought_started","v":{"s":"A drought begins. It will last "}},{"k":"drought_toast","v":{"s":"Drought"}},{"k":"drought_years","v":{"s":" years."}},{"k":"edit_prediction","v":{"s":"Edit prediction"}},{"k":"empty_trial","v":{"s":"Complete an investigation, then save its evidence here."}},{"k":"end_drought","v":{"s":"End the drought"}},{"k":"established","v":{"s":"Established"}},{"k":"established_short","v":{"s":"established"}},{"k":"evidence_alt","v":{"s":"Trial evidence, year by year. Bars above the line are years the tree made more than it spent; bars below are deficit years. The strip underneath shows which factor limited each year. "}},{"k":"evidence_cap","v":{"s":"Net carbon each year (kg C), above or below zero"}},{"k":"evidence_counts_mid","v":{"s":" set it in "}},{"k":"evidence_counts_pre","v":{"s":"Limit, year by year — "}},{"k":"exact_copy","v":{"s":"Exact copy"}},{"k":"exit_full","v":{"s":"Exit full screen"}},{"k":"experiment_started","v":{"s":"Investigation started. Set the conditions, then make a prediction."}},{"k":"explanation_prompt","v":{"s":"Explain what caused the result. Use the limiting factor and carbon evidence."}},{"k":"flow_now","v":{"s":"Flow right now"}},{"k":"from_seed","v":{"s":"From seed"}},{"k":"full_deficit","v":{"s":"Spending more than it makes, and living off its reserves."}},{"k":"full_hint","v":{"s":"Drag to orbit · Escape to leave"}},{"k":"full_off","v":{"s":"Left full screen view."}},{"k":"full_on","v":{"s":"Full screen view. Press Escape to leave."}},{"k":"full_toolbar","v":{"s":"Full screen tree controls"}},{"k":"full_why_dead","v":{"s":"Nothing limits a dead tree. Start a new seedling to keep experimenting."}},{"k":"full_why_stomata","v":{"s":"Full why stomata"}},{"k":"girdling","v":{"s":"Why cutting a ring of bark kills a tree"}},{"k":"girdling_adv","v":{"s":"This is also why the cambium matters so much: it is the single living layer between the two, and it is what a ground fire has to get through. A species with thick bark is buying insulation for that one layer."}},{"k":"girdling_body","v":{"s":"Phloem sits just inside the bark; xylem is deeper in the wood. Remove a complete ring of bark and the leaves keep receiving water, so the tree looks fine for a whole season. But no sugar can reach the roots. The roots starve first, and only then does the top die."}},{"k":"girdling_sub","v":{"s":"A useful test of whether the two systems have really landed."}},{"k":"go_full","v":{"s":"Full screen"}},{"k":"goal","v":{"s":"A tree that made it"}},{"k":"goal_done","v":{"s":"Done. This tree reached full size and can seed the next generation. Open Spread to send it out."}},{"k":"goal_grown","v":{"s":"Grown to full size"}},{"k":"goal_hint","v":{"s":"Leaves earn the carbon, wood buys height, roots buy water. The split is yours."}},{"k":"goal_need_height","v":{"s":"Enough banked to reproduce. It still has growing to do."}},{"k":"goal_need_seed","v":{"s":"Full size. Move some carbon into reproduction to finish it."}},{"k":"goal_reached_say","v":{"s":"Goal reached at age "}},{"k":"goal_reached_say2","v":{"s":". This tree is full grown and can reproduce."}},{"k":"goal_seed","v":{"s":"Banked enough to reproduce"}},{"k":"goal_sub","v":{"s":"Grow to full size and bank enough carbon to make the next generation. There is no clock: reaching it late still counts."}},{"k":"goal_toast","v":{"s":"A tree that made it"}},{"k":"good_years_left","v":{"s":"Years of deficit it can still take"}},{"k":"handoff_intro","v":{"s":"Two other labs own the neighbouring scales of this same reaction, and both go deeper than this one does. Chemical Balance has the equation and its energy cost; Cell Explorer opens on the organelles, where the chloroplast is:"}},{"k":"height_change","v":{"s":"Height change"}},{"k":"height_label","v":{"s":"Height"}},{"k":"how_trees_eat","v":{"s":"How a tree feeds itself"}},{"k":"inspect_part","v":{"s":"Inspect "}},{"k":"investigation_closed","v":{"s":"Investigation closed. Ordinary playback is available again."}},{"k":"investigation_intro","v":{"s":"Start from the tree you have now. During prediction you can change the conditions and carbon allocation before locking the trial."}},{"k":"investigation_steps","v":{"s":"Investigation steps"}},{"k":"investigation_sub","v":{"s":"Freeze a starting tree, predict what will happen, run a controlled trial, and explain the evidence."}},{"k":"investigation_title","v":{"s":"Investigation studio"}},{"k":"k2_body","v":{"s":"The tree makes sugar in its leaves and uses it to grow taller, grow roots, and make seeds. The wood in a tree trunk came mostly out of the air."}},{"k":"k2_sub","v":{"s":"A tree does not eat food from the soil. It builds its own, out of air, water and sunlight."}},{"k":"leaves","v":{"s":"Leaves"}},{"k":"left","v":{"s":"Left"}},{"k":"left_short","v":{"s":"Left to grow with"}},{"k":"level","v":{"s":"Level"}},{"k":"liebig","v":{"s":"Liebig"}},{"k":"light","v":{"s":"Light"}},{"k":"limit_band","v":{"s":"What was limiting, year by year"}},{"k":"limit_band_alt","v":{"s":"Limiting factor for each of the last "}},{"k":"limit_band_alt2","v":{"s":" years. Most recent: "}},{"k":"limit_note_g35","v":{"s":"This is the one running short. Adding more of anything else will not help until you fix this one."}},{"k":"limit_note_g912","v":{"s":"The rate follows the smallest term. Raising any other input changes nothing until this one stops being the smallest."}},{"k":"limit_note_k2","v":{"s":"This is what the tree needs more of."}},{"k":"limit_word","v":{"s":"Limit"}},{"k":"limiting_badge","v":{"s":"LIMITING"}},{"k":"limiting_now","v":{"s":"Limiting right now: "}},{"k":"limiting_now_short","v":{"s":"Limiting now: "}},{"k":"limits_sub_g68","v":{"s":"Four things a tree needs. Whichever is shortest sets the speed, no matter how much of the others there is."}},{"k":"limits_sub_g912","v":{"s":"Four factors, and the rate follows the smallest of them. This is the question a living tree answers every hour, and its answer is recorded permanently in the rings."}},{"k":"litres_day","v":{"s":"litres a day"}},{"k":"lock_prediction","v":{"s":"Lock prediction"}},{"k":"m_tall","v":{"s":"m tall"}},{"k":"made_short","v":{"s":"Made"}},{"k":"make_prediction","v":{"s":"Make your prediction"}},{"k":"many_variables","v":{"s":"things changed: "}},{"k":"many_variables_note","v":{"s":"The differences below cannot be pinned on any one of them. Change one thing at a time."}},{"k":"map_alt","v":{"s":"Map alt"}},{"k":"map_capped","v":{"s":"Map capped"}},{"k":"map_leg_clone","v":{"s":"Clonal stem"}},{"k":"map_leg_failed","v":{"s":"Did not take"}},{"k":"map_leg_seed","v":{"s":"Grew from seed"}},{"k":"map_leg_wiped","v":{"s":"Killed together"}},{"k":"map_note","v":{"s":"Distances here are RELATIVE, not a scale in metres — what is real is the ordering, that a wind-carried seed can travel orders of magnitude further than a root sucker can push. The counts are exactly the ones resolved above; nothing is re-rolled to draw this."}},{"k":"map_sub_g35","v":{"s":"The same decade, seen from above. Distance is the half of this trade the numbers do not show: a clonal stem almost always takes, and it arrives next to its parent."}},{"k":"map_sub_k2","v":{"s":"Looking down at the ground around the tree. Each mark is one try."}},{"k":"map_title","v":{"s":"Where they landed"}},{"k":"mean_net","v":{"s":"Mean net carbon"}},{"k":"mean_ring","v":{"s":"Mean ring width"}},{"k":"metres","v":{"s":"metres"}},{"k":"metric","v":{"s":"Metric"}},{"k":"millimetres","v":{"s":"millimetres"}},{"k":"mixed","v":{"s":"A mixed strategy: copies close by that almost always take, plus a few genetically different seedlings further out. Most real trees hedge exactly like this."}},{"k":"model_note","v":{"s":"Qualitative teaching model, not a forest growth model or a measurement. The shapes are real (saturating light response, a smallest-factor gate, respiration that scales with living tissue) and the magnitudes are the right order for a temperate tree, but no figure here should be quoted as data."}},{"k":"negative_year","v":{"s":"The tree is spending more than it makes and is living off reserves. A few years of this is survivable. Many are not."}},{"k":"new_investigation","v":{"s":"New investigation"}},{"k":"new_mix","v":{"s":"New genetic mix"}},{"k":"new_seedling","v":{"s":"New seedling"}},{"k":"next","v":{"s":"Next"}},{"k":"no_budget","v":{"s":"No reproduction carbon banked yet. Go back to Grow, put some of the surplus into Reproduction, and run some years."}},{"k":"no_surplus","v":{"s":"Nothing to send out"}},{"k":"no_surplus_note","v":{"s":"The tree is spending more than it makes, so there is no surplus to divide. The phloem is running the other way: stored sugar is being pulled back OUT of the roots and trunk to keep the living tissue alive. Sinks become the source."}},{"k":"not_quite","v":{"s":"Not quite."}},{"k":"not_selected","v":{"s":"Not selected"}},{"k":"notebook_sub","v":{"s":"Save two trials, then compare evidence from the same starting tree under different conditions."}},{"k":"notebook_title","v":{"s":"A/B lab notebook"}},{"k":"observed_limit","v":{"s":"Observed limit"}},{"k":"observed_outcome","v":{"s":"Observed outcome"}},{"k":"observed_summary","v":{"s":"Compare predicted and observed results. A mismatch is useful evidence, not a wrong experiment."}},{"k":"of_old_age","v":{"s":"old age"}},{"k":"one_variable","v":{"s":"One variable changed: "}},{"k":"one_variable_note","v":{"s":"Whatever differs in the evidence below, this change caused it."}},{"k":"open_cell","v":{"s":"See the chloroplast in Cell Explorer →"}},{"k":"open_chembalance","v":{"s":"Balance the equation in Chemical Balance →"}},{"k":"outcome_die","v":{"s":"Die"}},{"k":"outcome_struggle","v":{"s":"Struggle"}},{"k":"outcome_thrive","v":{"s":"Grow well"}},{"k":"outcome_word","v":{"s":"Outcome"}},{"k":"overcommitted","v":{"s":"You have committed more carbon than the tree banked. Pull something back."}},{"k":"part_clones","v":{"s":"Clones"}},{"k":"part_leaves","v":{"s":"Leaves"}},{"k":"part_roots","v":{"s":"Roots"}},{"k":"part_trunk","v":{"s":"Trunk"}},{"k":"pause","v":{"s":"Pause"}},{"k":"phloem_g68","v":{"s":"Living cells carrying sugar from where it is made to where it is spent. In spring the flow reverses and runs upward."}},{"k":"phloem_g912","v":{"s":"Living cells moving sugar from any SOURCE to any SINK. Direction is not fixed: in autumn sugar runs down to the roots, and in early spring it runs back up to build leaves before there are leaves to make it."}},{"k":"phloem_k2","v":{"s":"Carries food from the leaves to the rest of the tree."}},{"k":"places","v":{"s":"Places"}},{"k":"play","v":{"s":"Play"}},{"k":"playback","v":{"s":"Run the clock"}},{"k":"playback_sub","v":{"s":"Different parts of a tree run on wildly different clocks. Seasons take months, one ring takes a year, closing a canopy takes decades."}},{"k":"playback_sub_k2","v":{"s":"Press play and watch the tree grow."}},{"k":"plus_1","v":{"s":"+1 year"}},{"k":"plus_10","v":{"s":"+10 years"}},{"k":"plus_50","v":{"s":"+50 years"}},{"k":"pm_clonal","v":{"s":"clonal"}},{"k":"pm_dbh","v":{"s":"Trunk across"}},{"k":"pm_from_seed","v":{"s":"from seed"}},{"k":"pm_genet","v":{"s":"The clonal stems share this tree’s root system and its genes, so in the sense that matters to a botanist this individual is not finished. That is how an aspen clone can outlive every stem in it by thousands of years."}},{"k":"pm_group","v":{"s":"What happened to this tree"}},{"k":"pm_height","v":{"s":"Height reached"}},{"k":"pm_kids","v":{"s":"Descendants established"}},{"k":"pm_none","v":{"s":"none"}},{"k":"pm_old_early_p","v":{"s":"Pm old early p"}},{"k":"pm_old_h","v":{"s":"Pm old h"}},{"k":"pm_old_p","v":{"s":"Pm old p"}},{"k":"pm_rings","v":{"s":"Rings laid"}},{"k":"pm_starved_h","v":{"s":"Pm starved h"}},{"k":"pm_starved_p","v":{"s":"Pm starved p"}},{"k":"pm_stressed","v":{"s":"stressed"}},{"k":"pm_try","v":{"s":"To get further next time: "}},{"k":"pm_try_body","v":{"s":"raise whatever the limiting-factor card kept naming, or spend less. Reproduction and stored reserves both come out of the same surplus as leaves and roots, and leaves are the only line on that list that earns any of it back."}},{"k":"predict_hint","v":{"s":"Set the Conditions and allocation below first. Then predict the dominant limit and the overall outcome."}},{"k":"predict_limit","v":{"s":"Which factor will limit growth most often?"}},{"k":"predict_outcome","v":{"s":"What will happen to the tree?"}},{"k":"predict_reason","v":{"s":"Why do you think so? (optional)"}},{"k":"predicted_limit","v":{"s":"Predicted limit"}},{"k":"predicted_outcome","v":{"s":"Predicted outcome"}},{"k":"prediction_editing","v":{"s":"Prediction unlocked. You can change the conditions again."}},{"k":"prediction_half","v":{"s":"You had one of the two right"}},{"k":"prediction_locked","v":{"s":"Prediction locked. Conditions are frozen and the trial is ready to run."}},{"k":"prediction_matched","v":{"s":"The evidence matched your prediction"}},{"k":"prediction_needed","v":{"s":"Choose a limiting factor and an outcome before locking the prediction."}},{"k":"prediction_surprised","v":{"s":"The evidence changed the story"}},{"k":"prepare_b","v":{"s":"Prepare Trial B from A"}},{"k":"prepare_b_note","v":{"s":"Restore Trial A’s exact starting tree, then change one condition to make a controlled Trial B."}},{"k":"prev","v":{"s":"Previous"}},{"k":"ready_title","v":{"s":"Prediction locked — ready to run"}},{"k":"record","v":{"s":"Your record so far"}},{"k":"record_clonal","v":{"s":"Your descendants are overwhelmingly clonal: reliable, close to home, and every one of them carrying the same susceptibility. One root pathogen reaches all of them."}},{"k":"record_mixed","v":{"s":"You are hedging — copies close by that almost always take, plus seedlings further out that mostly do not. Most real trees settle here too."}},{"k":"record_one_round","v":{"s":"One decade is an anecdote. Run another against a different event before drawing a conclusion."}},{"k":"record_seed","v":{"s":"Your descendants are overwhelmingly from seed: genetically varied and spread wide, and you paid for that in how few of them took."}},{"k":"record_sub","v":{"s":"Every decade you have run with this tree."}},{"k":"reproduction","v":{"s":"Reproduction"}},{"k":"reproduction_change","v":{"s":"Reproduction banked"}},{"k":"reserve_change","v":{"s":"Reserve change"}},{"k":"reserves","v":{"s":"Stored reserves"}},{"k":"reserves_left","v":{"s":"Stored sugar reserves"}},{"k":"reset_view","v":{"s":"Reset view"}},{"k":"rings","v":{"s":"Growth rings"}},{"k":"rings_laid","v":{"s":"Rings laid"}},{"k":"rings_sub_g68","v":{"s":"One bar per year, red where the tree ran a deficit. Rings usually narrow with age even in a healthy tree: the same volume of wood spread around a longer circumference is thinner."}},{"k":"rings_sub_k2","v":{"s":"One bar for each year. Taller means the tree grew a wider ring that year."}},{"k":"root_schematic","v":{"s":"Roots shown as a schematic soil cutaway"}},{"k":"roots","v":{"s":"Roots"}},{"k":"rotate_left","v":{"s":"Rotate view left"}},{"k":"rotate_right","v":{"s":"Rotate view right"}},{"k":"run_decade","v":{"s":"Run the decade"}},{"k":"run_trial","v":{"s":"Run trial"}},{"k":"save_trial","v":{"s":"Save trial"}},{"k":"saved","v":{"s":"saved"}},{"k":"say_advanced","v":{"s":"Advanced "}},{"k":"say_age","v":{"s":"Age "}},{"k":"say_dead_first","v":{"s":"This tree has died. Start a new seedling first."}},{"k":"say_died_age","v":{"s":"The tree died at age "}},{"k":"say_died_old","v":{"s":"It reached the end of its lifespan."}},{"k":"say_died_starved","v":{"s":"It spent more than it made for too long."}},{"k":"say_height","v":{"s":"height "}},{"k":"say_level_set","v":{"s":"Level set to "}},{"k":"say_opening","v":{"s":"Opening "}},{"k":"say_part_cleared","v":{"s":"Anatomy selection cleared."}},{"k":"say_part_selected","v":{"s":"selected in the three-dimensional view."}},{"k":"say_paused","v":{"s":"Paused at age "}},{"k":"say_playing","v":{"s":"Playing at "}},{"k":"say_reset_post","v":{"s":" seedling."}},{"k":"say_reset_pre","v":{"s":"Reset to a new "}},{"k":"say_speed_set","v":{"s":"Speed set to "}},{"k":"score_none","v":{"s":"Not answered yet"}},{"k":"score_right","v":{"s":"right"}},{"k":"season_driven","v":{"s":"Season (set by playback)"}},{"k":"season_honest","v":{"s":"The carbon budget on this page is a whole YEAR. Changing the season changes what you are looking at and what is described here, not a figure the model has recalculated."}},{"k":"season_label","v":{"s":"Season"}},{"k":"season_pick","v":{"s":"Season"}},{"k":"soil_water","v":{"s":"Soil water"}},{"k":"source_spring","v":{"s":"Source right now: stored reserves in the roots and trunk"}},{"k":"source_spring_note","v":{"s":"The canopy is not built yet, so sugar runs UP from store to build it. The tree is spending last year to pay for this one."}},{"k":"source_summer","v":{"s":"Source right now: the leaves"}},{"k":"species","v":{"s":"Species"}},{"k":"spend_it","v":{"s":"Where does the surplus go?"}},{"k":"spend_it_sub","v":{"s":"The tree cannot do all of these at once. More wood means fewer seeds this year."}},{"k":"spent_short","v":{"s":"Spent staying alive"}},{"k":"spread","v":{"s":"Making more trees"}},{"k":"spread_model_note","v":{"s":"The take rates below are tuned so that one decade is playable, not measured. What is real is the ORDER: a clonal shoot establishes far more reliably than a seed, and a wind-carried seed in the wild succeeds far more rarely than the figure here suggests. Compare the strategies against each other, not against the world."}},{"k":"spread_sub_g68","v":{"s":"Seeds recombine and travel, but almost none survive. Clonal routes nearly always take and cost little, but they produce genetic copies on a shared root system. Spend the reproduction carbon you banked and see what a decade throws at you."}},{"k":"spread_sub_k2","v":{"s":"Trees make new trees in more than one way. Some grow from seeds. Some grow straight out of the parent tree. Try spending your seed budget different ways."}},{"k":"start_drought","v":{"s":"Drought"}},{"k":"starved","v":{"s":"starved"}},{"k":"step_explain","v":{"s":"Explain"}},{"k":"step_predict","v":{"s":"Predict"}},{"k":"step_run","v":{"s":"Run"}},{"k":"stomata_closing","v":{"s":"Stomata closing"}},{"k":"stomata_open","v":{"s":"Stomata open"}},{"k":"stomata_open_note","v":{"s":"Wide open. Carbon is coming in and water is going out through the same pores."}},{"k":"studio_label","v":{"s":"Living systems studio"}},{"k":"subtitle","v":{"s":"What limits a tree, what it costs to stay alive, and how it makes more of itself"}},{"k":"survival","v":{"s":"Survival margin"}},{"k":"survival_bad","v":{"s":"Close to starving. The next few negative years will kill it unless something changes now."}},{"k":"survival_limit_is","v":{"s":"What is holding it back right now: "}},{"k":"survival_ok","v":{"s":"Making more than it spends. Reserves are refilling and the deficit count is back to zero."}},{"k":"survival_sub","v":{"s":"How much room this tree has left before it starves. Both bars refill on any year it makes more than it spends."}},{"k":"survival_warn","v":{"s":"Running a deficit. Give it more leaf area, easier conditions, or less to pay for, and both bars recover."}},{"k":"tab_chem","v":{"s":"Chemistry"}},{"k":"tab_compare","v":{"s":"Compare"}},{"k":"tab_grow","v":{"s":"Grow"}},{"k":"tab_quiz","v":{"s":"Check"}},{"k":"tab_spread","v":{"s":"Spread"}},{"k":"tab_transport","v":{"s":"Transport"}},{"k":"tabs_label","v":{"s":"Tree Life Lab sections"}},{"k":"takes","v":{"s":"Takes "}},{"k":"tall_short","v":{"s":"tall"}},{"k":"temperature","v":{"s":"Temperature"}},{"k":"tension_note","v":{"s":"Under drought the column is pulled harder against a drier soil. Push the tension far enough and an air bubble breaks the thread, and that segment of xylem never carries water again."}},{"k":"the_bill","v":{"s":"The respiration bill"}},{"k":"the_bill_sub","v":{"s":"The part students most often miss: a big tree does not only gain more, it SPENDS more, every hour, forever."}},{"k":"the_trade","v":{"s":"The trade the tree cannot avoid"}},{"k":"the_trade_sub","v":{"s":"The trade sub"}},{"k":"this_year","v":{"s":"This year"}},{"k":"threed_failed","v":{"s":"The 3D engine could not load, which school network filters sometimes cause. Every number and control on this page still works."}},{"k":"tile_resp","v":{"s":"Maintenance respiration"}},{"k":"tile_resp_k2","v":{"s":"Sugar used to stay alive"}},{"k":"tilt_down","v":{"s":"Tilt view down"}},{"k":"tilt_up","v":{"s":"Tilt view up"}},{"k":"title","v":{"s":"Tree Life Lab"}},{"k":"to_spend","v":{"s":"to send out this year"}},{"k":"trade_body","v":{"s":"A large tree can move well over 100 gallons of water in a day this way. Almost all of it is the unavoidable price of leaving the stomata open long enough to take carbon in."}},{"k":"trial","v":{"s":"Trial"}},{"k":"trial_b_ready","v":{"s":"Trial B starts from the same tree as Trial A. Change one condition and make a new prediction."}},{"k":"trial_complete","v":{"s":"Trial complete. Compare the observation with your prediction, then explain what happened."}},{"k":"trial_length","v":{"s":"Trial length"}},{"k":"trial_saved","v":{"s":"Trial saved in the lab notebook."}},{"k":"trial_saved_short","v":{"s":"Trial "}},{"k":"trial_showed","v":{"s":"The trial showed"}},{"k":"trial_strip_alt","v":{"s":"Limiting factor, year by year: "}},{"k":"two_pipes","v":{"s":"Two separate plumbing systems"}},{"k":"two_pipes_sub","v":{"s":"Water goes up one way. Sugar goes wherever it is needed by another. They run side by side and they are not the same tissue."}},{"k":"uncontrolled_pair","v":{"s":"These trials began from different trees. Compare cautiously, or prepare Trial B from A."}},{"k":"use_trial_run","v":{"s":"Finish or close the investigation before using ordinary year steps."}},{"k":"via_stomata","v":{"s":"Via stomata"}},{"k":"via_stomata_short","v":{"s":"(stomata closed)"}},{"k":"water","v":{"s":"Water"}},{"k":"what_limits","v":{"s":"What is limiting the rate?"}},{"k":"where_sugar","v":{"s":"Where this year’s sugar is going"}},{"k":"where_sugar_sub","v":{"s":"Straight from the allocation you set on the Grow tab. Phloem has no fixed direction: it runs from wherever sugar IS to wherever it is being spent."}},{"k":"widest","v":{"s":"Widest "}},{"k":"wood","v":{"s":"Wood (height and rings)"}},{"k":"xs_alt","v":{"s":"Cross-section of the trunk. From the outside in: bark, phloem, cambium, sapwood, heartwood. "}},{"k":"xs_bark","v":{"s":"Bark — the outer protection"}},{"k":"xs_cambium","v":{"s":"Cambium — the one living layer that makes new wood"}},{"k":"xs_heart","v":{"s":"Heartwood — dead, and free to carry"}},{"k":"xs_phloem","v":{"s":"Phloem — carries sugar, just inside the bark"}},{"k":"xs_rings_note","v":{"s":"The rings are this tree’s own record, newest at the outside. Red rings are years it spent more than it made."}},{"k":"xs_sap","v":{"s":"Sapwood — living, carries water up"}},{"k":"xs_sub_g68","v":{"s":"Cut across the trunk and the two systems are in different places: phloem in a thin band just under the bark, xylem filling the wood beneath it. The rings are this tree’s own."}},{"k":"xs_sub_k2","v":{"s":"A slice through the trunk. Each ring is one year of growing."}},{"k":"xs_title","v":{"s":"Inside the trunk"}},{"k":"xylem_g68","v":{"s":"Dead hollow cells carrying water up from the roots. Evaporation at the leaves does the pulling."}},{"k":"xylem_g912","v":{"s":"Dead, hollow cells. Water is pulled up under tension by evaporation at the leaf surface, not pushed from below. The column is under negative pressure and an air bubble can break it."}},{"k":"xylem_k2","v":{"s":"Carries water up from the roots to the leaves."}},{"k":"year","v":{"s":"Year"}},{"k":"year_many","v":{"s":"years"}},{"k":"year_one","v":{"s":"year"}},{"k":"years","v":{"s":"years"}},{"k":"you_predicted","v":{"s":"You predicted: "}},{"k":"you_reasoned","v":{"s":"Before the run you wrote: "}},{"k":"you_said","v":{"s":"You said"}},{"k":"your_explanation","v":{"s":"Your explanation"}},{"k":"your_tree","v":{"s":"your tree"}},{"k":"yr","v":{"s":"yr"}},{"k":"zero_variables","v":{"s":"Identical treatments — the two trials should match, and every difference below should be zero."}},{"k":"zoom_in","v":{"s":"Zoom in"}},{"k":"zoom_out","v":{"s":"Zoom out"}},{"k":"advanced_active_copy","v":{"s":"Advanced tools stay open while an investigation is active."}},{"k":"advanced_closed_copy","v":{"s":"Open the Investigation studio, survival diagnostics, A/B notebook, and ring evidence when you are ready."}},{"k":"advanced_hide","v":{"s":"Hide advanced tools"}},{"k":"advanced_in_use","v":{"s":"Advanced tools in use"}},{"k":"advanced_notebook","v":{"s":"A/B notebook"}},{"k":"advanced_open_copy","v":{"s":"The evidence workspace is open below. Hide it whenever you want a calmer Grow view."}},{"k":"advanced_rings","v":{"s":"Ring evidence"}},{"k":"advanced_show","v":{"s":"Go deeper"}},{"k":"advanced_survival","v":{"s":"Survival"}},{"k":"advanced_title","v":{"s":"Ready to go deeper?"}},{"k":"advanced_workspace","v":{"s":"Advanced evidence workspace"}},{"k":"all_clonal_k2","v":{"s":"The nearby shoots started this time. They stayed close to the parent tree."}},{"k":"all_seed_k2","v":{"s":"The new trees came from seed and reached farther. Many seed tries still did not grow."}},{"k":"annual_source","v":{"s":"Whole-year source: canopy photosynthesis"}},{"k":"annual_surplus_to_divide","v":{"s":"of annual surplus to divide among five destinations"}},{"k":"answer_choices","v":{"s":"Answer choices"}},{"k":"attempts_word","v":{"s":"attempts"}},{"k":"autumn_anthocyanins_copy","v":{"s":"Red and purple pigments can be produced in some leaves."}},{"k":"autumn_anthocyanins_title","v":{"s":"Anthocyanins"}},{"k":"autumn_carotenoids_copy","v":{"s":"Yellow and orange pigments already present become visible."}},{"k":"autumn_carotenoids_title","v":{"s":"Carotenoids"}},{"k":"autumn_chlorophyll_copy","v":{"s":"Green pigment breaks down and recedes."}},{"k":"autumn_chlorophyll_title","v":{"s":"Chlorophyll"}},{"k":"autumn_needle_boundary","v":{"s":"Evergreen describes overlapping foliage cohorts, not immortal needles. Older needles still fall, and their slow-decaying litter builds duff."}},{"k":"autumn_needle_lab_copy","v":{"s":"Several needle cohorts share the canopy, so shedding is staggered."}},{"k":"autumn_needle_lab_title","v":{"s":"Evergreen needle-age map"}},{"k":"autumn_needle_lab_title_k2","v":{"s":"A pine holds needles of different ages"}},{"k":"autumn_needle_middle_copy","v":{"s":"Older green needles keep working across seasons."}},{"k":"autumn_needle_middle_title","v":{"s":"Middle cohorts"}},{"k":"autumn_needle_newest_copy","v":{"s":"Newest needles stay bright and usually remain."}},{"k":"autumn_needle_newest_title","v":{"s":"Current-year needles"}},{"k":"autumn_needle_oldest_copy","v":{"s":"Some yellow or brown, detach, and join the duff."}},{"k":"autumn_needle_oldest_title","v":{"s":"Oldest cohort"}},{"k":"autumn_pigment_boundary","v":{"s":"Evidence boundary: leaf color alone cannot reconstruct one exact temperature, rainfall amount, or weather event. Species, leaf chemistry, light, sugar, and weather interact."}},{"k":"autumn_pigment_lab_copy","v":{"s":"Yellow and orange colors and red colors do not appear for exactly the same reason."}},{"k":"autumn_pigment_lab_title","v":{"s":"Autumn pigment decoder"}},{"k":"autumn_pigment_lab_title_k2","v":{"s":"Why do leaves change color?"}},{"k":"autumn_tannins_copy","v":{"s":"Brown compounds often dominate late in the season."}},{"k":"autumn_tannins_title","v":{"s":"Tannins"}},{"k":"available_to_invest","v":{"s":"available to invest"}},{"k":"back_to","v":{"s":"Back to"}},{"k":"back_to_air_k2","v":{"s":"Back to the air"}},{"k":"banked_k2","v":{"s":"Food saved"}},{"k":"bare_crown","v":{"s":"Bare crown"}},{"k":"bark_defense","v":{"s":"Bark defense"}},{"k":"before_run_explain","v":{"s":"After the run, connect the event, counts, and spatial pattern into one cautious claim."}},{"k":"before_run_explain_k2","v":{"s":"After the run, point to a number and a mark on the map when you tell why."}},{"k":"begin_investigation_k2","v":{"s":"Tell what happened"}},{"k":"bottleneck_explain","v":{"s":"The reaction can only run as fast as its scarcest usable input."}},{"k":"bottleneck_now","v":{"s":"Bottleneck right now"}},{"k":"broad_leaves","v":{"s":"Broad leaves"}},{"k":"budget_equation","v":{"s":"Carbon budget equation"}},{"k":"canopy_complete","v":{"s":"Every idea has been explored"}},{"k":"canopy_progress","v":{"s":"Canopy progress"}},{"k":"canopy_ready","v":{"s":"Ready to grow your canopy"}},{"k":"canopy_waiting","v":{"s":"ideas still waiting"}},{"k":"carbon_bank_meter","v":{"s":"Carbon bank committed"}},{"k":"carbon_bank_meter_k2","v":{"s":"Saved food used"}},{"k":"change_bottleneck","v":{"s":"Change the bottleneck first"}},{"k":"change_in_grow","v":{"s":"Change conditions in Grow"}},{"k":"chapter_chem","v":{"s":"Discover what limits growth"}},{"k":"chapter_chem_cue","v":{"s":"Look for the factor with the least headroom."}},{"k":"chapter_chem_cue_k2","v":{"s":"Find the ingredient with the smallest help bar."}},{"k":"chapter_chem_intro","v":{"s":"Read the response curves and see why adding more of everything does not always help."}},{"k":"chapter_chem_intro_k2","v":{"s":"Change light, water, air, or warmth and see which ingredient the tree needs more of."}},{"k":"chapter_chem_k2","v":{"s":"See how a tree makes food"}},{"k":"chapter_compare","v":{"s":"Compare five ways to be a tree"}},{"k":"chapter_compare_cue","v":{"s":"Same conditions. Different biology."}},{"k":"chapter_compare_intro","v":{"s":"Keep the climate fixed and reveal how each species strategy changes the outcome."}},{"k":"chapter_grow","v":{"s":"Grow a tree through time"}},{"k":"chapter_grow_cue","v":{"s":"Start here: try one change, then grow 10 years."}},{"k":"chapter_grow_intro","v":{"s":"Change one condition, advance the years, and watch the living carbon budget respond."}},{"k":"chapter_grow_intro_k2","v":{"s":"Change sunlight, water, air, or warmth. Let years pass and see how the tree responds."}},{"k":"chapter_navigation","v":{"s":"Chapter navigation"}},{"k":"chapter_position","v":{"s":"Chapter"}},{"k":"chapter_quiz","v":{"s":"Check the story you can explain"}},{"k":"chapter_quiz_cue","v":{"s":"Read the explanation after every answer."}},{"k":"chapter_quiz_cue_k2","v":{"s":"Read the clue after every answer."}},{"k":"chapter_quiz_intro","v":{"s":"Answer one idea at a time and use the feedback to strengthen your biological reasoning."}},{"k":"chapter_quiz_intro_k2","v":{"s":"Answer one idea at a time. Use each clue to make your thinking stronger."}},{"k":"chapter_quiz_k2","v":{"s":"Tell the tree's story"}},{"k":"chapter_spread","v":{"s":"Make the next generation"}},{"k":"chapter_spread_cue","v":{"s":"Try a mixed strategy, then run another decade."}},{"k":"chapter_spread_cue_k2","v":{"s":"Try seeds and shoots, then let 10 years pass."}},{"k":"chapter_spread_intro","v":{"s":"Spend stored carbon on seeds or clones and see how distance, survival, and diversity trade off."}},{"k":"chapter_spread_intro_k2","v":{"s":"Use the tree's saved food for seeds or new shoots. See which ones start growing."}},{"k":"chapter_spread_k2","v":{"s":"Help new trees begin"}},{"k":"chapter_spread_seed_cue","v":{"s":"Compare two seed routes, then run another decade."}},{"k":"chapter_spread_seed_cue_k2","v":{"s":"Try the two kinds of seed, then let 10 years pass."}},{"k":"chapter_transport","v":{"s":"Follow water and sugar"}},{"k":"chapter_transport_cue","v":{"s":"Water and sugar move through different tissues."}},{"k":"chapter_transport_intro","v":{"s":"Trace xylem upward and phloem from each carbon source to the places that need it."}},{"k":"check_k2","v":{"s":"Show what you know"}},{"k":"chem_explain_copy","v":{"s":"Use the marked response curve as evidence, then change just one condition in Grow to test the prediction."}},{"k":"chem_explain_copy_k2","v":{"s":"The sugar helps build roots, leaves, wood, flowers, and seeds."}},{"k":"chem_explain_k2","v":{"s":"Sugar becomes new tree parts"}},{"k":"chem_guess_copy_k2","v":{"s":"If one need runs low, guess that the leaf will make less sugar."}},{"k":"chem_guess_k2","v":{"s":"Less of one means less food"}},{"k":"chem_notice_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide from air meet inside the leaf."}},{"k":"chem_notice_k2","v":{"s":"A leaf gathers three things"}},{"k":"chem_observe_copy","v":{"s":"The marked input matches the smallest usable factor. This tree is making "}},{"k":"chem_predict_copy","v":{"s":"Raise "}},{"k":"chem_predict_copy_2","v":{"s":"; the dot should climb until a different factor becomes smallest."}},{"k":"chem_reasoning","v":{"s":"Turn the live reaction into a testable explanation"}},{"k":"chem_reasoning_k2","v":{"s":"Follow what a leaf does"}},{"k":"chem_story_alt","v":{"s":"Sunlight, water and carbon dioxide enter a leaf. The leaf produces sugar carbon and oxygen."}},{"k":"chem_story_alt_k2","v":{"s":"Sunlight, water and carbon dioxide from the air enter a leaf. The leaf makes sugar and releases oxygen back to the air."}},{"k":"chem_story_eyebrow","v":{"s":"Live reaction"}},{"k":"chem_story_sub","v":{"s":"Follow the live reaction: three inputs meet in the leaf, and the slowest usable input sets the pace."}},{"k":"chem_story_title","v":{"s":"From sky to sugar"}},{"k":"choose_strategy","v":{"s":"Choose a reproduction strategy"}},{"k":"choose_strategy_k2","v":{"s":"Choose how to make new trees"}},{"k":"choose_wager","v":{"s":"Choose the wager"}},{"k":"choose_wager_copy","v":{"s":"Balance reliability, distance, and genetic variety."}},{"k":"choose_wager_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Try seeds, shoots, or both. Watch how far they go and how often they grow."}},{"k":"choose_wager_k2","v":{"s":"Choose how new trees begin"}},{"k":"claim","v":{"s":"Claim"}},{"k":"claim_copy","v":{"s":"State what the tree is doing."}},{"k":"claim_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Say what you think."}},{"k":"clock_budget_copy","v":{"s":"Current settings projected across one whole model year."}},{"k":"clock_budget_stopped","v":{"s":"No carbon income"}},{"k":"clock_budget_stopped_copy","v":{"s":"The annual carbon budget stops when the living tree does."}},{"k":"clock_budget_title","v":{"s":"Carbon balance"}},{"k":"clock_budget_title_k2","v":{"s":"Food left after living"}},{"k":"clock_deficit","v":{"s":"deficit"}},{"k":"clock_exchange_closed","v":{"s":"Mostly closed"}},{"k":"clock_exchange_limit_copy","v":{"s":"The smallest current input is "}},{"k":"clock_exchange_open","v":{"s":"Open"}},{"k":"clock_exchange_partial","v":{"s":"Partly open"}},{"k":"clock_exchange_stopped","v":{"s":"No active exchange"}},{"k":"clock_exchange_stopped_copy","v":{"s":"Gas exchange has ended in this stem."}},{"k":"clock_exchange_water_copy","v":{"s":"Water stress is restricting carbon dioxide entry."}},{"k":"clock_leaf_title","v":{"s":"Leaf gas exchange"}},{"k":"clock_leaf_title_k2","v":{"s":"Tiny leaf doors"}},{"k":"clock_life_title","v":{"s":"Structure and history"}},{"k":"clock_life_title_k2","v":{"s":"The tree's life story"}},{"k":"clock_lifetime","v":{"s":"Across a lifetime"}},{"k":"clock_now","v":{"s":"Minutes to hours"}},{"k":"clock_now_k2","v":{"s":"Right now"}},{"k":"clock_stage_ended","v":{"s":"Stem ended"}},{"k":"clock_stage_ended_copy","v":{"s":"Its rings and stored wood still record the life it lived."}},{"k":"clock_stage_ended_k2","v":{"s":"This stem has died"}},{"k":"clock_stage_growing","v":{"s":"Growing tree"}},{"k":"clock_stage_growing_copy","v":{"s":"Repeated carbon surpluses are becoming height, roots, wood, and reserves."}},{"k":"clock_stage_mature","v":{"s":"Mature tree"}},{"k":"clock_stage_mature_copy","v":{"s":"The tree has reached the model's mature height and can invest more in the next generation."}},{"k":"clock_stage_mature_k2","v":{"s":"Full-grown tree"}},{"k":"clock_stage_sapling","v":{"s":"Sapling"}},{"k":"clock_stage_sapling_copy","v":{"s":"The crown is expanding while each year adds another ring."}},{"k":"clock_stage_sapling_k2","v":{"s":"Young tree"}},{"k":"clock_stage_seedling","v":{"s":"Seedling"}},{"k":"clock_stage_seedling_copy","v":{"s":"A small leaf area must earn enough carbon to establish roots and stem."}},{"k":"clock_stage_seedling_k2","v":{"s":"Baby tree"}},{"k":"clock_stage_veteran","v":{"s":"Veteran tree"}},{"k":"clock_stage_veteran_copy","v":{"s":"Growth is slower, but the long record of rings and stored carbon continues."}},{"k":"clock_stage_veteran_k2","v":{"s":"Very old tree"}},{"k":"clock_surplus","v":{"s":"surplus"}},{"k":"clock_year","v":{"s":"One whole year"}},{"k":"clocks_boundary","v":{"s":"Model boundary: current-condition snapshot → whole-year projection → stored lifetime history."}},{"k":"clocks_story","v":{"s":"leaf responses shape the yearly carbon budget; repeated years become rings, height, roots, and stored carbon."}},{"k":"clocks_story_k2","v":{"s":"leaf doors change food making; many years of food choices build the tree you see."}},{"k":"clocks_story_label","v":{"s":"Read the causal chain: "}},{"k":"clocks_story_label_k2","v":{"s":"Read the tree's story: "}},{"k":"clocks_sub","v":{"s":"Leaf responses happen quickly; carbon is balanced across a year; wood and rings accumulate across a lifetime."}},{"k":"clocks_sub_k2","v":{"s":"Look at what happens now, over one year, and across the tree's whole life."}},{"k":"clocks_title","v":{"s":"One tree, three biological clocks"}},{"k":"clocks_title_k2","v":{"s":"A tree works on three clocks"}},{"k":"co2_from_air_k2","v":{"s":"Carbon dioxide from air"}},{"k":"commit_k2","v":{"s":"Use saved food"}},{"k":"committed_k2","v":{"s":"Food used"}},{"k":"compare_chart_region","v":{"s":"Scrollable chart comparing tree height through time"}},{"k":"compare_explain_copy","v":{"s":"Use growth speed, tolerance, bark, lifespan, and height ceiling to explain why the lines separate without calling one species best everywhere."}},{"k":"compare_explain_title","v":{"s":"Same inputs make biology the explanation"}},{"k":"compare_eyebrow","v":{"s":"A controlled forest experiment"}},{"k":"compare_predict_copy","v":{"s":"Predict which tolerance or defense will matter more if only light or water changes."}},{"k":"compare_predict_title","v":{"s":"Change one condition and the order may change"}},{"k":"compare_reasoning","v":{"s":"Read a controlled comparison like a scientist"}},{"k":"continue_to","v":{"s":"Continue to"}},{"k":"control_carbon","v":{"s":"Carbon plan"}},{"k":"control_climate","v":{"s":"Climate"}},{"k":"control_time","v":{"s":"Time window"}},{"k":"controlled_comparison","v":{"s":"Controlled comparison setup"}},{"k":"current_conditions","v":{"s":"Current conditions"}},{"k":"current_limit","v":{"s":"Current limiting factor"}},{"k":"curve_key_best","v":{"s":"best result from changing only this factor"}},{"k":"curve_key_flat","v":{"s":"flat means something else is limiting"}},{"k":"curve_key_label","v":{"s":"How to read the response curves"}},{"k":"curve_key_now","v":{"s":"your tree now"}},{"k":"curve_key_up","v":{"s":"higher means more sugar made"}},{"k":"decade_reveal","v":{"s":"Decade reveal"}},{"k":"decade_reveal_k2","v":{"s":"What happened in 10 years"}},{"k":"drought_tolerance","v":{"s":"Drought tolerance"}},{"k":"effect_budget","v":{"s":"Carbon budget"}},{"k":"effect_changed","v":{"s":"You changed"}},{"k":"effect_co2_down","v":{"s":"Effect co2 down"}},{"k":"effect_co2_up","v":{"s":"Effect co2 up"}},{"k":"effect_drought_end","v":{"s":"Effect drought end"}},{"k":"effect_drought_start","v":{"s":"Effect drought start"}},{"k":"effect_from_change","v":{"s":" from this change"}},{"k":"effect_light_down","v":{"s":"Less usable light shrinks this year's carbon surplus. Run the clock and the slower growth will appear in the tree and its next ring."}},{"k":"effect_light_up","v":{"s":"More usable light raises this year's carbon surplus. Run the clock to turn that surplus into leaves, roots, wood, or seeds."}},{"k":"effect_limited_elsewhere","v":{"s":"The budget barely moved because another factor is still setting the rate. Fix the factor named above, then try this change again."}},{"k":"effect_limiting","v":{"s":"Now limiting"}},{"k":"effect_smallest","v":{"s":"The smallest input sets the rate."}},{"k":"effect_temp_closer","v":{"s":"The temperature moved closer to this species' optimum, so its carbon-making machinery can work more effectively."}},{"k":"effect_temp_farther","v":{"s":"The temperature moved away from this species' optimum, so the carbon budget tightens before the tree visibly grows."}},{"k":"effect_title","v":{"s":"Cause → effect"}},{"k":"effect_tree_response","v":{"s":"Tree response: "}},{"k":"effect_water_down","v":{"s":"Visible response: the crown wilts as water pressure falls. Closing stomata save water but also slow carbon intake."}},{"k":"effect_water_up","v":{"s":"Visible response: the crown recovers as water pressure rises. Reopening stomata can restore carbon intake."}},{"k":"established_k2","v":{"s":"Started growing"}},{"k":"establishment","v":{"s":"Establishment"}},{"k":"establishment_k2","v":{"s":"Starts growing"}},{"k":"evidence","v":{"s":"Evidence"}},{"k":"evidence_connected","v":{"s":"Evidence connected"}},{"k":"evidence_connected_k2","v":{"s":"You used the clue"}},{"k":"evidence_copy","v":{"s":"Name the observation or model output."}},{"k":"evidence_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Point to what you saw."}},{"k":"evidence_from_tree","v":{"s":"Evidence from the tree"}},{"k":"evidence_from_tree_k2","v":{"s":"Clue from the tree"}},{"k":"exact_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Same copy"}},{"k":"explain","v":{"s":"Explain"}},{"k":"explain_this_time","v":{"s":"Explain this decade, not every decade"}},{"k":"explain_this_time_k2","v":{"s":"Explain what happened this time"}},{"k":"explanation_structure","v":{"s":"Explanation structure"}},{"k":"explored","v":{"s":"explored"}},{"k":"fastest_first","v":{"s":"Fastest first"}},{"k":"finale_full_copy","v":{"s":"You can trace the tree story from resources to descendants and defend each link with evidence."}},{"k":"finale_full_copy_k2","v":{"s":"You followed the tree from sunlight and water to seeds and new shoots."}},{"k":"finale_full_title","v":{"s":"A full canopy of explanations"}},{"k":"finale_full_title_k2","v":{"s":"A full canopy of ideas"}},{"k":"finale_growing_copy","v":{"s":"This is a map of where to explore next. Revisit the looping leaves, use the explanation, and try again."}},{"k":"finale_growing_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Use the clue under each question, then try the looping leaves again."}},{"k":"finale_growing_title","v":{"s":"Your canopy is still growing"}},{"k":"finale_growing_title_k2","v":{"s":"Your ideas are still growing"}},{"k":"finale_note","v":{"s":"A score is a trail marker, not the destination. The real goal is an explanation you can defend with evidence."}},{"k":"finale_note_k2","v":{"s":"The score shows where you are today. The big goal is to tell the tree story and point to clues."}},{"k":"finale_score","v":{"s":"ideas connected on your latest attempts"}},{"k":"finale_strong_copy","v":{"s":"Most branches are strong. Revisit the looping leaves to strengthen the mechanisms that still feel uncertain."}},{"k":"finale_strong_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Most ideas are connected. Try the looping questions again to grow the last few leaves."}},{"k":"finale_strong_title","v":{"s":"Strong branches of understanding"}},{"k":"finale_strong_title_k2","v":{"s":"Your ideas have strong branches"}},{"k":"flow_evidence","v":{"s":"Turn the pattern into evidence"}},{"k":"flow_evidence_note","v":{"s":"Make a prediction, run a controlled trial, and compare what the tree actually did."}},{"k":"flow_observe","v":{"s":"Observe and grow"}},{"k":"flow_observe_note","v":{"s":"Read the living tree, move time forward, and see what its carbon budget can afford."}},{"k":"flow_shape","v":{"s":"Shape the next year"}},{"k":"flow_shape_note","v":{"s":"Change the environment and choose where the tree invests whatever carbon remains."}},{"k":"follow_food_k2","v":{"s":"Follow the food"}},{"k":"food_for_growing_k2","v":{"s":"Food for growing"}},{"k":"food_points","v":{"s":"food points"}},{"k":"forest_story","v":{"s":"The forest story you built"}},{"k":"from_seed_k2","v":{"s":"From seeds"}},{"k":"from_shoots_k2","v":{"s":"New shoots"}},{"k":"frozen_soil","v":{"s":"Frozen soil"}},{"k":"full_description","v":{"s":"Explore the tree with the controls below. Press Escape to leave full screen."}},{"k":"full_title","v":{"s":"Immersive tree viewer: "}},{"k":"genetic_variety","v":{"s":"Genetic variety"}},{"k":"genetic_variety_k2","v":{"s":"Like the parent"}},{"k":"girdle_sequence_alt","v":{"s":"What happens after a complete ring of bark is removed"}},{"k":"girdle_step_roots","v":{"s":"Roots starve first"}},{"k":"girdle_step_roots_copy","v":{"s":"The crown dies later, after the roots fail."}},{"k":"girdle_step_sugar","v":{"s":"Sugar route breaks"}},{"k":"girdle_step_sugar_copy","v":{"s":"The shallow phloem ring is removed."}},{"k":"girdle_step_water","v":{"s":"Water still rises"}},{"k":"girdle_step_water_copy","v":{"s":"The deeper xylem stays intact."}},{"k":"greatest_height","v":{"s":"Greatest height reached"}},{"k":"grew_from_k2","v":{"s":"grew from"}},{"k":"growing_parts_lower","v":{"s":"growing parts and roots"}},{"k":"growth_roots","v":{"s":"Growth + roots"}},{"k":"habitat_now","v":{"s":"Current growing conditions"}},{"k":"height_ceiling","v":{"s":"Height ceiling"}},{"k":"hold_still","v":{"s":"Hold everything else still"}},{"k":"hold_still_copy","v":{"s":"The same climate, carbon plan, and time window expose the biology."}},{"k":"idea","v":{"s":"Idea"}},{"k":"inside_leaf_k2","v":{"s":"Inside a leaf"}},{"k":"insight_prompt","v":{"s":"These are outcomes in this environment, not a universal ranking. Use each strategy signature below to explain why the lines separate."}},{"k":"journey_alt","v":{"s":"The reproduction journey: bank carbon, choose a strategy, pass through a decade of chance, and count the next generation."}},{"k":"journey_alt_k2","v":{"s":"The new-tree journey: save food, choose seeds or shoots, let ten years pass, and count what grows."}},{"k":"journey_choice","v":{"s":"Your wager"}},{"k":"journey_choice_copy","v":{"s":"Seeds, clones, or both"}},{"k":"journey_choice_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Seeds, shoots, or both"}},{"k":"journey_choice_k2","v":{"s":"Choose a way"}},{"k":"journey_decade","v":{"s":"A decade passes"}},{"k":"journey_decade_copy","v":{"s":"Chance and disturbance intervene"}},{"k":"journey_decade_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Weather and luck act"}},{"k":"journey_decade_k2","v":{"s":"Ten years pass"}},{"k":"journey_forest","v":{"s":"Next generation"}},{"k":"journey_forest_copy","v":{"s":"Survivors establish"}},{"k":"journey_forest_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Count what started growing"}},{"k":"journey_forest_k2","v":{"s":"New trees"}},{"k":"journey_parent","v":{"s":"Parent tree"}},{"k":"journey_parent_copy","v":{"s":"Banks reproduction carbon"}},{"k":"journey_parent_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Saves food"}},{"k":"journey_parent_k2","v":{"s":"Parent tree"}},{"k":"leaf_engine","v":{"s":"Leaf engine"}},{"k":"leaf_kitchen_k2","v":{"s":"Leaf kitchen"}},{"k":"leaves_lower","v":{"s":"leaves"}},{"k":"left_k2","v":{"s":"Food left"}},{"k":"life_cycle_boundary","v":{"s":"Life-cycle boundary"}},{"k":"limit_badge","v":{"s":"Limiting"}},{"k":"litres_move_daily","v":{"s":"litres move daily"}},{"k":"living_tissues","v":{"s":"Living tissues"}},{"k":"living_tissues_lower","v":{"s":"living tissues"}},{"k":"maintenance_sinks","v":{"s":"Maintenance sinks"}},{"k":"make_a_guess","v":{"s":"Make a guess"}},{"k":"make_tree_food_k2","v":{"s":"Makes tree food"}},{"k":"map_alt_k2","v":{"s":"Map alt k2"}},{"k":"map_capped_k2","v":{"s":"Map capped k2"}},{"k":"map_eyebrow","v":{"s":"Dispersal map"}},{"k":"map_eyebrow_k2","v":{"s":"New-tree map"}},{"k":"map_leg_clone_k2","v":{"s":"New shoot"}},{"k":"map_leg_failed_k2","v":{"s":"Did not grow"}},{"k":"map_leg_wiped_k2","v":{"s":"Hurt together"}},{"k":"map_note_k2","v":{"s":"This map shows near and far, not real metres. Filled marks started growing; open marks did not."}},{"k":"meet_tree_k2","v":{"s":"Meet your tree"}},{"k":"memory_causal_aperture_active","v":{"s":"Leaf gas exchange responded to the limiting input."}},{"k":"memory_causal_aperture_missing","v":{"s":"This older record did not store a stomatal opening value."}},{"k":"memory_causal_aperture_water","v":{"s":"Water stress restricted carbon dioxide entry."}},{"k":"memory_causal_carbon","v":{"s":"Carbon balance"}},{"k":"memory_causal_carbon_copy","v":{"s":"Photosynthetic income minus maintenance respiration."}},{"k":"memory_causal_carbon_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Carbon made minus carbon used to stay alive."}},{"k":"memory_causal_carbon_k2","v":{"s":"Food balance"}},{"k":"memory_causal_closed","v":{"s":"Mostly closed"}},{"k":"memory_causal_condition","v":{"s":"Limiting condition"}},{"k":"memory_causal_condition_copy","v":{"s":"The smallest model input set the rate."}},{"k":"memory_causal_condition_k2","v":{"s":"What set the pace"}},{"k":"memory_causal_condition_water","v":{"s":"Dryness triggered the leaf response."}},{"k":"memory_causal_label","v":{"s":"Causal trail from annual conditions to the growth ring"}},{"k":"memory_causal_leaf","v":{"s":"Leaf response"}},{"k":"memory_causal_leaf_k2","v":{"s":"Tiny leaf doors"}},{"k":"memory_causal_open","v":{"s":"Open"}},{"k":"memory_causal_partial","v":{"s":"Partly open"}},{"k":"memory_causal_unknown","v":{"s":"Not recorded"}},{"k":"memory_causal_wood","v":{"s":"Growth-ring record"}},{"k":"memory_causal_wood_growth","v":{"s":"A share of the surplus was allocated to stem wood."}},{"k":"memory_causal_wood_k2","v":{"s":"Wooden memory"}},{"k":"memory_causal_wood_stress","v":{"s":"A deficit marked a stress year with little carbon available for wood."}},{"k":"memory_cause_co2","v":{"s":"Carbon dioxide supply was the smallest input at the stomata, so it set the photosynthetic ceiling."}},{"k":"memory_cause_co2_k2","v":{"s":"Carbon dioxide was the ingredient in shortest supply at the leaf doors."}},{"k":"memory_cause_light","v":{"s":"Light was the smallest input, so extra carbon dioxide, water, or warmth could not raise the rate."}},{"k":"memory_cause_light_k2","v":{"s":"Light was the ingredient in shortest supply, so it set the pace."}},{"k":"memory_cause_temp","v":{"s":"Temperature held the photosynthetic machinery furthest from its working range."}},{"k":"memory_cause_temp_k2","v":{"s":"The temperature kept the leaf machinery from working at its best."}},{"k":"memory_cause_unknown","v":{"s":"The smallest model input set the photosynthetic rate for this year."}},{"k":"memory_cause_water","v":{"s":"Water stress closed the stomata, reducing carbon dioxide entry and photosynthesis."}},{"k":"memory_cause_water_k2","v":{"s":"Dry soil made the tiny leaf doors close, so less carbon dioxide could enter."}},{"k":"memory_cause_water_supply","v":{"s":"Water was the smallest input controlling the photosynthetic rate."}},{"k":"memory_claim_continuity","v":{"s":"No crossing: same side of zero"}},{"k":"memory_claim_continuity_deficit","v":{"s":"Yes. Both years stayed in carbon deficit, even though the size of the deficit may differ."}},{"k":"memory_claim_continuity_k2","v":{"s":"The balance stayed on one side"}},{"k":"memory_claim_continuity_surplus","v":{"s":"Yes. Both years stayed in carbon surplus, even though their ring widths may differ."}},{"k":"memory_claim_correct_say","v":{"s":"That claim matches the evidence."}},{"k":"memory_claim_options_label","v":{"s":"Choose a claim about the two years"}},{"k":"memory_claim_recovery","v":{"s":"Recovery: deficit to surplus"}},{"k":"memory_claim_recovery_k2","v":{"s":"The tree bounced back"}},{"k":"memory_claim_recovery_mid","v":{"s":" ended in deficit, then Year "}},{"k":"memory_claim_recovery_post","v":{"s":" returned to surplus. That is recovery in this model."}},{"k":"memory_claim_recovery_pre","v":{"s":"Yes. Year "}},{"k":"memory_claim_retry","v":{"s":"Not yet. Read the surplus or deficit label beneath each ring, then check whether the carbon balance crossed zero."}},{"k":"memory_claim_retry_k2","v":{"s":"Look again. Read the word under each ring, then see whether the tree crossed zero."}},{"k":"memory_claim_retry_say","v":{"s":"Look again at the two carbon balance labels."}},{"k":"memory_claim_setback","v":{"s":"New stress: surplus to deficit"}},{"k":"memory_claim_setback_k2","v":{"s":"The year got harder"}},{"k":"memory_claim_setback_mid","v":{"s":" ended in surplus, then Year "}},{"k":"memory_claim_setback_post","v":{"s":" fell into deficit. That is a new stress signal."}},{"k":"memory_claim_setback_pre","v":{"s":"Yes. Year "}},{"k":"memory_claim_wait","v":{"s":"Choose the claim best supported by the two surplus or deficit labels."}},{"k":"memory_claim_wait_k2","v":{"s":"Choose the story that matches the two rings."}},{"k":"memory_compare_baseline","v":{"s":"There is no earlier valid record. This year establishes the baseline for later comparisons."}},{"k":"memory_compare_baseline_k2","v":{"s":"There is no earlier ring yet. This year becomes the first comparison point."}},{"k":"memory_compare_caution","v":{"s":"Pattern-reading caution: a year-to-year change is evidence, not proof that the limiting factor alone caused the ring difference. Age and carbon allocation also matter."}},{"k":"memory_compare_caution_k2","v":{"s":"Use more than one clue: age and where the tree sends its food can change ring size too."}},{"k":"memory_compare_label","v":{"s":"Comparison with the previous recorded year"}},{"k":"memory_compare_limit_changed","v":{"s":"The limiting factor changed from "}},{"k":"memory_compare_limit_to","v":{"s":" to "}},{"k":"memory_compare_narrower","v":{"s":"The model produced a narrower ring than the year before."}},{"k":"memory_compare_recovery","v":{"s":"Net carbon returned to surplus after the previous year ended in deficit."}},{"k":"memory_compare_recovery_k2","v":{"s":"The food balance climbed back above zero after a hard year."}},{"k":"memory_compare_same_limit","v":{"s":"remained the limiting factor."}},{"k":"memory_compare_setback","v":{"s":"Net carbon crossed from surplus into deficit, signalling a new stress year."}},{"k":"memory_compare_setback_k2","v":{"s":"The food balance fell below zero after a better year."}},{"k":"memory_compare_steady","v":{"s":"Ring width stayed close to the previous year."}},{"k":"memory_compare_wider","v":{"s":"The model allocated enough carbon to wood to make a wider ring than the year before."}},{"k":"memory_compared_with","v":{"s":"Compared with Year "}},{"k":"memory_copy","v":{"s":"Each annual carbon budget leaves evidence. Choose a recent ring to connect conditions, carbon, and growth."}},{"k":"memory_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Each year leaves a ring. Choose one to discover what helped or challenged the tree."}},{"k":"memory_deficit","v":{"s":"deficit"}},{"k":"memory_detective_prompt","v":{"s":"Which claim best describes the carbon-balance change from the previous year?"}},{"k":"memory_detective_prompt_k2","v":{"s":"What story do these two rings tell?"}},{"k":"memory_detective_title","v":{"s":"Make an evidence-based claim"}},{"k":"memory_detective_title_k2","v":{"s":"Be a tree detective"}},{"k":"memory_empty_copy","v":{"s":"Advance one year to turn today's conditions and carbon budget into the first ring."}},{"k":"memory_empty_copy_k2","v":{"s":"Grow one year to help the seedling write its first wooden memory."}},{"k":"memory_empty_title","v":{"s":"A lifetime record begins with one year"}},{"k":"memory_empty_title_k2","v":{"s":"The first ring is waiting"}},{"k":"memory_field_action_button","v":{"s":"Load these conditions"}},{"k":"memory_field_action_button_k2","v":{"s":"Try these settings"}},{"k":"memory_field_action_copy","v":{"s":"Loads these values into the current controls. It does not rewind tree age or guarantee the same ring."}},{"k":"memory_field_action_copy_k2","v":{"s":"This changes the sliders, not the tree's age. An older tree may grow differently."}},{"k":"memory_field_action_title","v":{"s":"Recreate the annual inputs"}},{"k":"memory_field_action_title_k2","v":{"s":"Try this year's settings again"}},{"k":"memory_field_available","v":{"s":"available"}},{"k":"memory_field_bright","v":{"s":"bright"}},{"k":"memory_field_caution","v":{"s":"Evidence boundary: this snapshot records inputs supplied to the model for the annual step. It is not weather reconstructed from the ring."}},{"k":"memory_field_caution_k2","v":{"s":"These are the settings the model used to grow this ring."}},{"k":"memory_field_co2","v":{"s":"Atmospheric carbon dioxide"}},{"k":"memory_field_co2_ambient","v":{"s":"ambient range"}},{"k":"memory_field_co2_enriched","v":{"s":"enriched"}},{"k":"memory_field_co2_k2","v":{"s":"Carbon dioxide in air"}},{"k":"memory_field_co2_low","v":{"s":"low"}},{"k":"memory_field_cold","v":{"s":"cold"}},{"k":"memory_field_compare_caution","v":{"s":"This highlights what changed most, not what caused the ring. Check the limiting factor and leaf response before making a causal claim."}},{"k":"memory_field_compare_caution_k2","v":{"s":"This shows what changed most. Check the leaf and carbon clues before deciding why the ring changed."}},{"k":"memory_field_compare_label","v":{"s":"Annual input changes from the previous year"}},{"k":"memory_field_compare_steady","v":{"s":"The four stored inputs were unchanged. Growth can still differ because the tree became older and larger."}},{"k":"memory_field_compare_steady_k2","v":{"s":"The settings stayed the same, but the tree itself became one year older."}},{"k":"memory_field_dim","v":{"s":"dim"}},{"k":"memory_field_dry","v":{"s":"dry"}},{"k":"memory_field_hot","v":{"s":"hot"}},{"k":"memory_field_largest_shift","v":{"s":"Largest input shift: "}},{"k":"memory_field_legacy_teaser","v":{"s":"Older ring: annual input snapshot was not stored."}},{"k":"memory_field_light","v":{"s":"Relative light"}},{"k":"memory_field_light_k2","v":{"s":"Sunlight"}},{"k":"memory_field_light_short","v":{"s":"light"}},{"k":"memory_field_load_unavailable","v":{"s":"These historical conditions are not available."}},{"k":"memory_field_loaded_post","v":{"s":" conditions into the current controls. Tree age was not changed."}},{"k":"memory_field_loaded_pre","v":{"s":"Loaded Year "}},{"k":"memory_field_missing","v":{"s":"This older record predates annual condition snapshots. Its carbon, limiter, and ring evidence remain available."}},{"k":"memory_field_missing_k2","v":{"s":"This older ring still tells a growth story, but its weather settings were not saved."}},{"k":"memory_field_moderate","v":{"s":"moderate"}},{"k":"memory_field_moist","v":{"s":"moist"}},{"k":"memory_field_points","v":{"s":" points"}},{"k":"memory_field_relative","v":{"s":" percent of the displayed model range"}},{"k":"memory_field_steady","v":{"s":"The stored annual inputs held steady"}},{"k":"memory_field_temperature","v":{"s":"Temperature"}},{"k":"memory_field_title","v":{"s":"Open the annual Field Notes"}},{"k":"memory_field_title_k2","v":{"s":"Open this year's nature notes"}},{"k":"memory_field_water","v":{"s":"Soil water"}},{"k":"memory_field_water_short","v":{"s":"soil water"}},{"k":"memory_field_working","v":{"s":"working range"}},{"k":"memory_grow_first","v":{"s":"Grow first year"}},{"k":"memory_growth_year","v":{"s":"A growth year in the wood"}},{"k":"memory_key_color","v":{"s":"Top color shows the limiter"}},{"k":"memory_key_color_copy","v":{"s":"It uses the same factor colors as the Chemistry view."}},{"k":"memory_key_color_copy_k2","v":{"s":"The color names the ingredient setting the pace."}},{"k":"memory_key_color_k2","v":{"s":"Color shows what ran short"}},{"k":"memory_key_dash","v":{"s":"Dashed means carbon deficit"}},{"k":"memory_key_dash_copy","v":{"s":"Maintenance exceeded carbon income, so reserves were used."}},{"k":"memory_key_dash_copy_k2","v":{"s":"The tree used more stored food than it made."}},{"k":"memory_key_dash_k2","v":{"s":"Dashes mark a hard year"}},{"k":"memory_key_height","v":{"s":"Height shows wood growth"}},{"k":"memory_key_height_copy","v":{"s":"Taller marks represent wider modelled rings."}},{"k":"memory_key_height_copy_k2","v":{"s":"A taller mark means a wider ring."}},{"k":"memory_key_height_k2","v":{"s":"Taller means more wood"}},{"k":"memory_key_label","v":{"s":"How to read the ring yearbook"}},{"k":"memory_limited","v":{"s":"limited"}},{"k":"memory_limiting_factor","v":{"s":"Limiting factor"}},{"k":"memory_net","v":{"s":"Net carbon"}},{"k":"memory_net_change","v":{"s":"Net carbon change"}},{"k":"memory_no_previous","v":{"s":"No earlier year to compare"}},{"k":"memory_note","v":{"s":"Ring width remembers carbon sent to wood. It is not a direct weather measurement, and rings often narrow as a tree gets older."}},{"k":"memory_note_k2","v":{"s":"A ring is a clue about how much wood the tree built, not a weather report by itself."}},{"k":"memory_of","v":{"s":" of "}},{"k":"memory_replay_boundary","v":{"s":"Same annual inputs do not freeze tree age, size, maintenance costs, or carbon allocation."}},{"k":"memory_replay_changed_copy","v":{"s":"Reload the historical conditions before growing to make a same-input comparison."}},{"k":"memory_replay_changed_title","v":{"s":"Replay settings changed"}},{"k":"memory_replay_co2","v":{"s":"Carbon dioxide"}},{"k":"memory_replay_complete_copy_mid","v":{"s":" used the loaded Year "}},{"k":"memory_replay_complete_copy_post","v":{"s":" conditions."}},{"k":"memory_replay_complete_copy_pre","v":{"s":"Year "}},{"k":"memory_replay_complete_title","v":{"s":"Same inputs, a different tree"}},{"k":"memory_replay_context_age","v":{"s":"Annual record"}},{"k":"memory_replay_context_complete","v":{"s":"Inputs stayed controlled while age, size, and maintenance demands continued changing."}},{"k":"memory_replay_context_diameter","v":{"s":"Trunk diameter"}},{"k":"memory_replay_context_height","v":{"s":"Tree height"}},{"k":"memory_replay_context_label","v":{"s":"Tree context comparison"}},{"k":"memory_replay_context_ready","v":{"s":"The controls match, but the tree receiving them is now older and larger."}},{"k":"memory_replay_context_title","v":{"s":"Tree context changed"}},{"k":"memory_replay_context_title_k2","v":{"s":"The tree changed too"}},{"k":"memory_replay_context_year","v":{"s":"Year "}},{"k":"memory_replay_control_changed","v":{"s":"Changed"}},{"k":"memory_replay_control_matched","v":{"s":"Matched"}},{"k":"memory_replay_controls_count_mid","v":{"s":" of "}},{"k":"memory_replay_controls_count_post","v":{"s":" controlled inputs matched"}},{"k":"memory_replay_controls_label","v":{"s":"Controlled-input match"}},{"k":"memory_replay_controls_title","v":{"s":"Controlled inputs"}},{"k":"memory_replay_controls_title_k2","v":{"s":"Settings to keep the same"}},{"k":"memory_replay_grow","v":{"s":"Grow one test year"}},{"k":"memory_replay_grow_k2","v":{"s":"Grow and compare"}},{"k":"memory_replay_light","v":{"s":"Light"}},{"k":"memory_replay_modified_copy","v":{"s":"The new record is still useful, but it is not a same-input replay."}},{"k":"memory_replay_modified_title","v":{"s":"Replay year used different inputs"}},{"k":"memory_replay_net","v":{"s":"Net carbon change"}},{"k":"memory_replay_ready_copy_k2","v":{"s":"The old settings are on